hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was asked about such water that is in a desert and in which beasts and animals come to drink, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water is clean"," nothing defiles it.\"" One tradition has these words: \""He is not defiled.\"" There are similar words in a tradition."""
2,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about water from which animals and beasts come to drink, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the water is two-fold"," it is not impure.\"""""
3,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates to his father, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink, so he said: \When the water is two cups"," it is not impure.\"""""
4,This tradition is narrated from some other traditions.
5,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the following statement from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar radi Allahu anhuma): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a water from which animals and beasts drink. One tradition has these words: beasts and beasts. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water is two-fold"," it is not impure.\"""""
6,"The same hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: animals and beasts (meaning the word animal is transmitted first)."
7,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water is two cups"," it is not najis (the narrator doubts that perhaps these words are: not impure).\"""""
8,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When water is divided into two parts"," it is not impure.\"""""
9,This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him).
10,This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him).
11,This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him).
12,"Narrated by Abdullah bin Umar: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"," it is not impure.\"""""
13,"Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the same from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
14,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abdullah, his father (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him)."
15,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two cups"," it is not impure.\"""""
16,"Ubaidullah narrates this on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, being asked about water that is in a deserted place and animals and beasts drink from it, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two folds"," it is not impure.\"" A narrator named Ibn Arfa narrates: I heard a narrator named Hashim explaining \""Qala\"" and he says: It means two large pots."""
17,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I heard the Holy Prophet (PBUH) saying this: A person asked him about such water, which is in a deserted place, from which animals and beasts drink, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When the water is divided"," it is not impure.\"""""
18,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
19,The same tradition is narrated from another hadith.
20,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He was asked about a well into which dead bodies are put, and from which dogs and other animals drink water. The same hadith is narrated on the authority of Ubaidullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission."
21,"The same hadith along with some other traditions is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar). However, some narrators have also quoted it as a \suspended\"" tradition."""
22,"Asim bin Munzar narrates: I entered a garden with Ubaidullah bin Abdullah, in which there was a pool of water with the skin of a dead camel lying on it, so Ubaydullah bin Abdullah performed ablution on it. The skin of a dead camel is lying inside it, so he told me this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father."
23,"This hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but in this chain of transmission, the words \the narrator is in doubt"," or perhaps three forts\"" are not recorded in this chain of transmission. The same tradition is also narrated by another person in which these words are: \""When the water becomes two forts"," (the narrator doubts) perhaps these words will become three forts.\"" That's it."""
24,"Abd al-Jabar al-Makki and Musa ibn Ismail and Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Aishah narrated this chain of narration on the authority of Hamad ibn Salama and they said in it: If the water is two qala, it is not najis. They did not say \or three\""."""
25,"Asim bin Munzar narrates: We were in a garden. The narrator has doubts. These words are: He was ours or perhaps these words were Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abdullah's. Meanwhile, when it was time for prayer, Abdullah got up, and went to the tank in the garden and started performing ablution from it. Although the skin of a camel was lying in this tank, I said: You are performing ablution with it, if it has skin. He said: My father narrated this hadith to me regarding the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two cups"," it is not impure.\"""""
26,"The judge Al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us. And Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Shīrāzī narrated to us; they both said: Al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; he said: Bishr ibn al-Sarī and Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir, with this chain of transmission, similar to the statement of ʿAffān: ""When the water amounts to two qullahs, it does not become impure."""
27,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, which has these words: \When water becomes two-fold"," it is not impure.\"""""
28,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"," nothing impures it.\"""""
29,"This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"," nothing impures it.\"" In some hadiths"," these words are transmitted as \""marfu'\"" hadith", while in others," they are transmitted as \""mawfuk\"" hadith."""
30,This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is related to Mujahid from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (Radi Allahu Anhu) as a “Mowquf” Hadith.
31,"Asim says: The word \al-Qalal\"" used in the text of hadiths refers to \""big pots\""."""
32,"Yahya bin Aqeel narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When water becomes two-fold"," it is not impure and there is no harm (in using it).\"" The narrator narrates: I inquired from my teacher Yahya bin Aqeel"," what is meant by \""Hijr\""? So they replied: It means the matka of Hijr"," so I guessed: one qala is equal to two \""farq\"". Mujahid narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: \""When the water is two qalas or more"," nothing impures it.\"""""
33,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When I was raised from the seventh heaven towards the Sadrat al-Muntahi, its fruits were as large as the fruits of the Hijr, and its leaves were like the ears of an elephant. What is it? So they said: The inner rivers are in Paradise and the outer rivers are the Nile and the Euphrates.\""34""","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, went on a journey. He continued walking all night. He passed by a man who was sitting on the edge of a pond. Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu inquired: O man with a pond! Did animals drink water in this pond of yours last night? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to this person: \O owner of the pond! Do not tell him about this", this person likes caution. What these beasts drank was their air and what was left over," we got as a drink.\"""""
35,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
36,"Wakiyya says: The learned note everything, whether it is in their favor or not, and the heretics only note that which is in their favor."
37,Yahya bin Abu Zaida says: It is better to note the hadith than not to note it.
38,"Sayyiduna Jabir Ibn Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the water reaches the limit of forty Qala"," it is not impure.\"" The same hadith is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission"," but there is an illusion in its chain of transmission. Another narrator has narrated this tradition as a \""Muquf\"" tradition from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission. The same tradition is narrated from Ibn Mankadir as his own saying along with another chain of transmission"," which reads: \""Do not exceed this.\"""""
39,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the water becomes 40 galahs"," it is not impure.\"""""
40,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) says: \When the water is forty qala," then nothing impures it.\"""""
41,This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA).
42,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \When the water becomes forty qala," then nothing impures it.\"""""
43,"Muhammad bin Mankader narrates: When the water is 40 feet deep, it is not impure, or perhaps a word similar to this has been described by him."
44,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Hurairah narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him), he says: \When the water reaches the amount of forty Qala"," it is not impure.\"" This tradition has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (Radi Allahu Anhu) along with some other traditions. In some traditions"," the word \""forty large buckets\"" has been used", in some traditions," the word \""forty small buckets\"" has been used (that is"," this word has been used instead of \""Qala\"")."""
45,"Sayyiduna Thawban Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Water is a purifying thing"," except for that water whose smell or taste (impure thing) prevails.\"""""
46,"Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Nothing defiles water"," except that which changes its taste or smell.\"" The above-mentioned hadith is transmitted to Rashid bin Saad", however," Azizi has quoted this hadith on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Maama."""
47,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \Nothing defiles water"," except that which changes the smell and taste of that water.\"" This hadith has been quoted as \""marfu'\"" only from Rashid bin Sa'd and this narrator is not authentic", it is Sahih," it is narrated on the authority of Rashid bin Sa'd."""
48,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Nothing defiles water.\"""""
49,"Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Nothing defiles water except that which overpowers its smell or taste.\"" This hadith is \""musal\"" and a narrator named Abu Usama transmitted it to Rashid bin Sa'd as a \""mawquf\"" hadith."""
50,"Abu Awun Rashid bin Sa'd states: Nothing defiles water, except that which changes the smell or taste of the water."
51,"Saeed bin Musayyib says: Water is pure, nothing impures it."
52,"Dawood bin Abu Hind narrates: We asked Saeed bin Musaib about a well and a reservoir from which even dogs drink, so he said: Water has been revealed as a pure thing, nothing defiles it."
53,Dawood quotes the statement of Saeed bin Musaib: \Allah has revealed water as a pure thing," nothing can defile it.\"""""
54,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution from the \Baa'a\"" well"," although menstruating women's clothes and other dirty things are put into it. One tradition has these words: \""Dead\"" is thrown. Some narrators have quoted these words: Dog meat is put. The Prophet", peace be upon him," said: \""Water is pure"," nothing impures it.\"" These words of the hadith are in accordance with the words narrated by the narrator named Ibn Abu Aoun."""
55,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: I heard from the Prophet (PBUH), when he was asked: O Messenger of Allah! We drink water from the well of \Baa'ah\""", although the meat of dogs, the clothes of menstruating women and the filth of people are put into it (so what is the ruling on this)? The Prophet, peace be upon him," said: \""Water is pure"," nothing impures it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission"," but there is some difference in its chain of transmission."""
56,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about these reservoirs, which come at different places on the way to Makkah and Medina. He was told: Dogs and beasts drink water from these reservoirs. The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whatever they put in their stomachs is their air"," and what remains is fit for us to drink and is clean.\"""""
57,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): Water is brought for you from a well called \Baa'ah\""", which is the well of Banu Sa'idah. In this well, the clothes of menstruating women," the meat of dogs and the filth of people are put. She doesn't.\"""""
58,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
59,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution from a well called Baa'a? In which the clothes of menstruating women, the meat of dogs and dirt are put, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Water is pure and nothing impures it.\"""""
60,"This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA)."
61,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) drank the water of the \Baa'a\"" well."""
62,"Abu Sa'eed and Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrate: Once Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Amr ibn al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, passed by a reservoir, and Sayyidna Amr, may God be pleased with him, inquired: O owner of the tank! Do the beasts also come and drink water at this reservoir of yours? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: \O owner of the reservoir! Do not tell us about this (because to drink water from such a reservoir) sometimes we come after the beasts and sometimes they come after us.\"""""
63,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: When we were in Syria, I brought water to the service of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, he performed ablution with this water and then inquired: Where did you bring this water from? I have never seen any heavenly water sweeter and purer than this. Narrator narrates: I said: I have brought it from the house of an old Christian woman. When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) performed ablution, he came to her. He said: \O old woman! Accept Islam"," you will be safe. Allah Almighty has sent Sayyiduna Muhammad (PBUH) with the truth.\"" Narrator narrates: This woman removed the veil from her head and her hair was white like flowers. The old woman said: Now I am about to die"," then Sayyiduna Umar said: \""O Allah! Be a witness!\"""""
64,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: Sayyiduna Umar performed ablution at the house of a Christian, then he went to this woman, he said: \O big sister! Accept Islam", you will be safe. Allah Almighty has sent Sayyidna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace," with the truth.\"" When this woman removed the veil from her head", (her hair was white like a flower)," this old woman said: Now I am about to die. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: \""O Allah! Be a witness.\"""""
65,"Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: Once an Abyssinian fell into the well of Zamzam, i.e. he fell down and died, his body was taken out under the order of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) and about the well, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) instructed that it be cleaned. The narrator narrates: But the water of the spring did not come under the control of the people, it came from the rock (black stone). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) instructed about it: It should be completely covered with cloths, until it is completely covered, when people closed it, then water came out of it."
66,Sayyiduna Abu Tufail narrates: Once a boy fell into the well of Zam Zam and all the water was taken out of him.
67,"Ibrahim Nakhai says: Every living thing whose blood is flowing (if it falls into a well), then ablution will not be performed with the water of that well. Shuba says: I think, he also mentioned the chameleon."
68,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is purifying.\"""""
69,"Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said this about the sea: \Its water is purifying and its dead is lawful.\"""""
70,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the sea and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful.\"" These words of the hadith are narrated from a narrator named Fazl Bin Ziyad"," in another chain of transmission this tradition is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA)."""
71,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
72,"Abu Tufail narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful.\"""""
73,"On the authority of Imam Muhammad Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him) (Imam Zain al-Abidin may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of his father (Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him)) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the water of the sea, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.”"
74,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
75,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about sea water: \Its dead body is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
76,"This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas."
77,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water and he said: \Sea water is pure.\"" The narrators have narrated it in the same way"," but it is correct: this hadith is \""suspended\""."""
78,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \He who cannot be purified by the water of the sea"," may Allah not purify him.\"" The authenticity of this hadith is \""Hasan\""."""
79,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once this was mentioned to me, some people after bathing in the Sea of Khadr say: It is obligatory on us, we should also bathe with other water (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \He who is not purified by the water of the sea"," may Allah not purify him.\"""""
80,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A person asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! We people travel in the sea and take a little water with us. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
81,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about performing ablution with sea water, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
82,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water: Should it be used for ablution? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
83,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
84,"Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \O Salman! Any food or drink in which an animal (i.e. worm", spider) falls, which has no blood, and dies in the food, then it is permissible to eat and drink it," and to wash clothes and perform ablution with this water.\"""""
85,"Aslam, a freed slave of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates: Water was heated in a pot for Sayyidna Umar (RA), and he used to bathe in it. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""
86,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, while I was heating some water in the sun, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O girl! Do not do this"," because it may result in leprosy.\"" This tradition is very \""poor\"""," its narrator Khalid bin Ismail is \""obsolete\""."""
87,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing ablution with water that has been kept in the sun, or bathing with it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \It may result in rain.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Muhammad Asim. No one else has narrated this tradition from Falih"," and this hadith is not authentic regarding its transmission from Zuhri."""
88,Hasan bin Azhar narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) has said this: \Do not bathe with water heated in the sun," because it may cause cataracts.\"""""
89,Hadith 85: It is narrated about Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) that: She has declared it abominable to perform ablution with water in which bread has been soaked.
90,Zayd bin Aslam narrates: (God's guidance is:) \When you stand for prayer," wash your faces.\"" Zayd bin Aslam said: It means"," when you wake up from sleep."""
91,"Imam Malik bin Anas has quoted Zayd bin Aslam's saying about this saying of Allah Almighty: \O you who believe! When you stand for prayer.\"" Zayd bin Aslam narrates: This means: When you wake up from sleep (do ablution)."""
92,Qays narrates this about Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Bijli): He used to instruct his household to perform ablution with water in which miswak was placed.
93,"Qays narrates: Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Al-Bijli, may God be pleased with him) used to instruct his family: Do ablution with the water in which I kept the miswak. Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
94,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to use the water left over from ablution to rub his face.
95,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to use the water left over from his ablution to rub his face."
96,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever drinks something from a gold or silver vessel, or from a vessel in which gold or silver is plated," will fill his belly with Hellfire.\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
97,"Abu Burda narrated: Once I and my father (Sayyidna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: \The Holy Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him, has forbidden to drink or eat anything in a gold or silver vessel, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, It is forbidden to use mizhah," silk cloth (there are different types of silk) and to wear gold rings.”"""
98,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he said: \Why don't you use its skin?\"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it dead? The Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""It is forbidden to eat it.\"" A narrator named Aqeel has added these words in his tradition: \""Can it not be purified by water and tanning.\"" These are the words of Ibn Hani's tradition: \""Can it not be purified by water and the bark of a betel nut?\"""""
99,"This tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, the narrator named Aqeel has quoted these additional words in his tradition: \The Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," said: Can it not be purified by tanning it with water and the bark of a cucumber?\"""""
100,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he inquired: \Whose does it belong to?\"" People have said: It was given as a charity to the maidservant of Sayyida Maimunah", the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," said: \""Why did these people not benefit from it by removing its skin and tanning it?\"" People said: This is a dead body. The Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""It is forbidden to eat a dead body.\"""""
101,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the pet goat of one of his wives who had died. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Why don't you use its skin?\"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! It is carrion", the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""It is purified by tanning.\"" There is some wording difference in the tradition quoted by Ibn Sa`id (i.e. the singular pronoun is the singular masculine", instead of the feminine," the singular is absent)."""
102,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \Its meat is forbidden"," its skin can be purified by tanning.\"""""
103,"This tradition is narrated from Zuhri along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Its meat has been forbidden to you and its skin (to be used) has been permitted.\"" The chain of this hadith is \""Sahih\""."""
104,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to the owner of a dead goat: \Why did you not skin it? You used to tan it and get profit from it.\"""""
105,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the pet goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Why don't you people use its skin", tan it," because in this way it becomes pure.\"""""
106,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \The way to purify a dead body is this: it should be tanned.\"" Ibrahim Nakhai narrates: The disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) used to say: \""The way to purify wool is this: wash it.\"""""
107,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: \To tan it is to purify it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
108,"Aaliyah bint Sabi narrates, Ms. Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told her, once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by some people of Quraish, who were pulling their sheep like a (dead) donkey is pulled. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them: \If you get his skin (it will be appropriate).\"" They said: It is dead. The Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""Water and betel leaves will purify it.\"""""
109,"Sayyiduna Salama bin Muhibq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a woman for water, and she said: The water I have is in a bottle that belongs to a dead (animal). The woman said: Yes! The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \As a result of tanning"," it becomes pure.\"""""
110,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains these words: \By tanning leather"," it becomes pure.\"""""
111,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \It is its tanning that purifies it.\"""""
112,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \His tanning purifies him.\"""""
113,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every skin is purified by tanning.\"""""
114,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When the leather is tanned"," it becomes pure.\"""""
115,"We were informed by Muhammad ibn Makhlad; we were informed by Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim; Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us. And Abu Bakr al-Azraq, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Buhlul, narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ammar ibn Salam Abu Muhammad narrated to us; Zafir narrated to us; from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali; from Al-Zuhri; from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah; from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: ""Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater who eats it"" (Surah Al-An'am, verse 145). He said: ""The 'eater' (al-ta'im) is the one who eats. As for the tooth, the horn, the bone, the wool, the hair, the fur, and the sinew—there is no harm in them because they can be washed."" And Shababah said: ""Only that which is eaten of the dead animal (maytah) is forbidden, and that is the flesh. As for the skin, the tooth, the bone, the hair, and the wool—they are lawful."" Abu Bakr al-Hudhali is weak."," I do not find anything that is forbidden to the eater.\"" Explaining it in detail", Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Here Taam (eater) means the person who eats, as far as teeth, horns, bones, wool, hair, and hair are concerned, then there is no problem in it," because they are washed. A narrator named Shababa narrated this: \""That which is forbidden from the dead body", which is eaten and that which is meat, as for the skin, bone, teeth, hair, wool," then it is permissible to use them (for other purposes).\"" The narrator of this tradition", Abu Bakr Hazli," is weak."""
116,"Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates: I heard Ms. Sayyida Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrate this: She says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: \When the skin of a dead body is tanned", then there is no harm in using it, its wool, its hair, its There is no harm in using horns," as long as they are washed with water.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Yusuf bin Safar, is obsolete," and no tradition other than this tradition has been narrated from him (or only he has narrated this tradition)."""
117,This tradition is narrated by Yusuf bin Safar along with another chain of transmission.
118,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) declared the meat (eating) of a dead body to be haram, as far as its skin, hair and wool are concerned, there is nothing wrong with it. The narrator of this tradition \Abd al-Jabbar\"" is weak."""
119,"Hazeel bin Shahrabeel narrates the following regarding Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) or Sayyida Zainab (RA) or any other wife of the Prophet (PBUH): When the goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her: \Why don't you people use its skin?\"" Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! How can we use it", it is dead, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""The leather becomes pure through tanning.\"" The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated from a wife of the Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," whose words are: We had a goat that died."""
120,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, saying: (Allah the Exalted) said: \Say this! In what has been revealed to me"," I have not found anything that is forbidden for the one who eats it.\"" (The Prophet", peace be upon him," said:) \""Everything of the dead body is lawful except that which is eaten", as far as the skin, horns, hair, wool, teeth, and bones are concerned, then they are all lawful," because they are not slaughtered.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Abu Bakr Hazli," is \""obsolete\""."""
121,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The skin that is tanned becomes pure.\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
122,"Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Tanning the skin of a dead body purifies it.\"""""
123,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a goat, he inquired: \What has happened to it?\"" People said: It is dead. The Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," said: \""You tan its skin"," because its tanning purifies it.\"" Qasim", the narrator of this tradition," is \""weak\""."""
124,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: \The way to purify leather is this," it should be tanned.\"" Its chain of transmission is \""Hasan\"" and all its narrators are trustworthy."""
125,"Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: She had a goat which she used to milk. Once the Prophet (PBUH) did not see that goat, so he (PBUH) inquired: \Where is the goat?\"" So the people said: She is dead. The Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him," said: \""Why don't you profit from her skin?\"" We said: He is dead. The Holy Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him," said: \""His tanning makes it halal"," just as vinegar makes alcohol halal.\"" Faraj bin Fazala is unique in narrating this tradition and it is \""weak\""."""
126,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Use the skin of a dead animal", whether it has been tanned with clay, ashes, or salt," or (the narrator doubts these words:) or whatever makes it usable after (tanning).\"""""
127,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand in a vessel (the narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) in the water of ablution, until he washes his hands three times," because he does not know where his hand has been throughout the night?\"""""
128,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person wakes up from sleep and wants to perform ablution, he should not put his hand in the vessel until he has washed it," because he does not know where his hand has been throughout the night? And where did he keep it?\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
129,"Salim bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person wakes up from sleep", he should not put his hand in a vessel until he has washed it three times," because he does not know where his hand has been during the night or where his hand has circumambulated?\"" A person said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: What do you think? If the person wants to perform ablution from the tank (he still has to do it)? So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar threw a pebble at him and said: \""I am narrating to you a hadith about the Holy Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him, and you are saying, 'What do you think," if he had to perform ablution from a tank?'\"" This tradition is authenticated by \""Hasan\""."""
130,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \When a person wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand into a vessel until he has washed it three times," because no one knows where his hand has been throughout the night? Or where his hand has been wandering throughout the night?\"" This hadith is \""Hasan\""."""
131,"Alqamah bin Waqqas narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, narrating this. He says: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, say: It will be counted towards the Messenger, and whoever migrated for the sake of this world in order to obtain it or migrated for a woman in order to marry her, his migration will be in the direction towards which he (intentionally) migrated.”"
132,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \On the Day of Resurrection, some scriptures will be brought, which will be sealed, and they will be placed before Allah," then Allah will say to His angels: Send them away! Then the angels will say: \""By Your honor! We have seen only good in them. Allah will say this", even though He has more knowledge, all these actions were for others, today I will accept only those actions," which were done only for my pleasure."""
133,"Sayyidna Dahhak bin Qais Fahri (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allah Almighty says: \I am free from partners", so whoever associates someone with Me, then that action will be for my partner (i.e.," that person should seek his reward from him).\"" (The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O people! Purify your actions for the sake of Allah! Because Allah will only accept the action that is pure for Him", and you should not say that it is for the sake of Allah and that is because of kinship. The reason for this is: it will be in relation to kinship," it will have nothing to do with Allah and neither will you.\"" Say: It is for Allah and it is because of you", because it will be because of you," it will have nothing to do with Allah.\"""""
134,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \No one should bathe in stagnant water when he is pregnant.\"" The narrator inquired: O Sayyidna Abu Huraira! Then what should he do? So Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""Let him get water (and bathe on one side).\"" Its certificate is \""Correct\""."""
135,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I remember this very well about myself and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We used to perform ablution from the same vessel.
136,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: I remember well about myself, I used to perform ablution with the same vessel with the Holy Prophet."
137,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of Sayyidah Maimunah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I was afflicted with janabat, I took a bath with a vessel and some water was left in it, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought Tashreef. Janabat has not been established. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a bath with this vessel. In this hadith, the narrator named Samat has been disputed and only the narrator named Sharik has stated this: It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidah Maimunah."
138,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), men and women (i.e. husband and wife) used to perform ablution from the same vessel. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
139,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
140,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (R.A.). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
141,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimoona bint Harith (RA) told me this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) performed ablution with the water left over from Sayyida Maimoona’s bath. Narrator named Ramadi has narrated this: Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) performed ablution with water in the state of Janabat, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with water left over from her."
142,"Sayyidna Huqam bin Amr (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade a man to perform ablution with the water left over from a woman's ablution (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these words are:) with the water left after a woman drinks. A narrator named Shuba narrates this: Sulaiman Taymi has narrated this: Abu Hajib has narrated this with reference to a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden that a woman should perform ablution with the water left over from her ablution. The name of the narrator named Abu Hajib is Sawada bin Asim, there is a difference in this hadith regarding him, some narrators have quoted it as a “deferred” tradition as a saying of command, it has not been quoted as a “marfu’” tradition until the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him."
143,Sayyida Khula bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: (Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) says this:) Her hand and the blessed hand of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter back and forth in the same vessel.
144,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him: A polytheist mocked him and said to him: I have noted this, your master has taught you everything, even the method of defecation, so Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him, replied: \Yes! The Messenger of God", may God bless him and grant him peace, has instructed us not to turn our backs towards the Qibla and Do not perform istujah through the right hand and do not perform istujah with less than three stones," these stones should not contain any bone or manganese.”"""
145,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
146,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA): Some polytheists said to him: We have noted this, your master has taught you all kinds of things, even teaching you how to perform abstinence, then Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA) replied: “Yes! He should perform istanja through or facing the Qiblah, and you have also forbidden us to perform istanja with mengini and bone. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""
147,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said this: \When a person goes to defecate"," he should purify himself by throwing three stones. Doing so will be sufficient for him.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is \""Hasan\""."""
148,"Narrated Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to meet his needs. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) brought two stones and a ring, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the ring and said: \This is dirt"," you bring stones.\"" This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission", according to which Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once I was going somewhere with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The narrator narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him," instructed me: \""Let me bring you three stones.\"" The narrator narrates: I came to you with two stones and a ring", so the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him," put the ring aside and said: \""This is dirt"," you bring another thing (stone) to me instead.\"" In this hadith", there has been a disagreement about the narrator named Abu Ishaq," (Imam Darqutni says:) I have explained this difference at another place."""
149,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us to perform abstinence through bone, manganese or coal. The source of this tradition is Syrian and is not authentic."
150,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to perform ablution with rotten bone, manganese or coal. The narrator of this tradition, Ali bin Rabah, has not been proven to have heard it from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud."
151,"Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who was an Ansari, narrates this, he has stated this regarding the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade: \One should perform istanja through bone", mange," or skin.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is not proven. The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman Majhool."""
152,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, \to cast iron or bone.\"" You have said this: \""These two things do not purify.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is \""Sahih\""."""
153,"Abi ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the method of ablution, and he said: \Don't you find three stones? Two stones (to clean the sides of the exit) and one stone to (clean the exit).\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
154,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once Saraqa bin Malik Mudalji passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the method of ablution. He should do istanja, which does not involve any Mangani, or do it through three pieces of wood or through three lumps of clay.”"
155,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person needs to defecate," he should perform istanja through three sticks or three stones or three times by filling his fist with clay.\"" This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions and there are some differences in its traditions."""
156,"Salama bin Wahram narrates: I heard Taaws narrate this: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “When a person starts defecating, he should respect the Qibla of Allah and not turn his back towards it, then purify himself with three stones or with three pieces of wood or with a handful of clay three times. Do it and then recite: All praise is due to Allah, the Exalted, Who has removed from me that which could have tormented me and left within me that which is beneficial to me.\""157""","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is transmitted as \Mursal\"" Hadith with reference to Taus."""
158,The same tradition is narrated by Taos along with another chain of transmission.
159,"The same hadith is narrated by Taus along with another chain of transmission and it is narrated as his saying, he has not quoted this tradition as a \marfu'\"" hadith. A narrator named Ali narrates: I inquired from Sufyan: Has a narrator named Zamaa transmitted this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" hadith? So they answered: \""Yes!\"" Then I asked Salama about this", and he was not aware of this, that is," this hadith is transmitted as a \""marfu'\"" hadith."""
160,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Maswak has ten virtues: it is a cause of God's pleasure, a cause of Satan's displeasure, a cause of happiness to the angels, a cause of health and beauty of the gums, removes tooth decay, sharpens vision, creates a fragrance in the mouth, reduces phlegm," brushing is a Sunnah and increases good deeds.\"" Shaykh Abul Hasan states: The narrator of this tradition", Maali bin Maimon," is weak and obsolete."""
161,"Marwan Asfar narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, he made his camel sit facing the Qiblah and then sat down facing it and started to urinate. I said: \O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Is this not forbidden?\"" So he said: \""Yes! But it is forbidden to do this in the open air. When there is something obstructing you and the Qiblah"," there is nothing wrong with it.\"" This tradition is authentic and all its narrators are trustworthy."""
162,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, \If we pour water on our private parts (during and after defecating)"," then we should turn our backs or face towards the Qibla.\"" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: After that", I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one year before his appearance," and he was urinating facing the Qiblah. All the narrators of this hadeeth are trustworthy and a narrator named Ibn Shukar has narrated these words: \""Let us face the Qiblah or turn our backs.\"""""
163,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once it was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that some people do not like facing the Qibla while defecating and their backs, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to defecate in a place where the faeces were facing the Qibla. Imam Darqutni states: In the chain of transmission of this tradition, there is a narrator named Khalid bin Abu Salat between the narrator named Khalid and the narrator named Arak."
164,"Narrated Khalid: Those people were present with Umar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: \Since I was young"," I have never defecated facing the Qiblah.\"" Arak bin Malik was present with them. Arak said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated this: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know that some people disliked this", so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this order about his toilet," so the toilet was turned towards the Qiblah. There is another tradition similar to this."""
165,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard about some people who disliked facing the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, so by the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) their places of defecation were turned towards the direction of the Qiblah. This tradition is more authentic. This tradition has also been narrated by some other narrators."
166,"Khalid bin Abu Salat narrates: I was sitting next to Umar bin Abdul Aziz during his caliphate, and Arak bin Malik was also sitting next to him. Umar ibn Abdul Aziz said: \I have never turned my back towards the Qiblah while urinating or defecating for so long.\"" So Arak said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated this hadith to me. She says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the opinion of some people", the place of his stool was turned towards the Qiblah under the order of the Prophet (peace be upon him). The chain of transmission of this tradition is more reliable and it has the addition of a narrator named Khalid bin Abu Salat," and it is correct."""
167,"Arak bin Malik narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, she says: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded: \Turn my toilet towards the Qiblah.\"" A narrator named Yahya bin Ishaq has narrated this: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought Tashrif and people were talking about the dislike of facing the Qiblah when urinating or defecating."""
168,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: On the order of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his toilet was turned towards the Qibla, when he found out that some people disliked it."
169,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on some errand. Shaykh Abul Hasan (Imam Darqutni) says: The narrator named Isa bin Abu Isa Hanat is weak.
170,Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Do not face the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, and do not turn your back to it," but face the east or the west (according to Madinah Munawarah).\"""""
171,"Isa bin Abu 'Isa narrates: I said to Imam Sha'bi: I am very surprised at the saying of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) and the tradition narrated by Nafi' on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA). Imam Shaabi inquired: What have these two gentlemen stated? So I replied: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Do not turn your back or turn towards the Qiblah (at the time of need). While Nafi has quoted this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, he says: \I saw the Holy Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him: He went to the bathroom to defecate," which was facing the Qiblah.\"" So Imam Sha'bi said this: \""As far as the saying of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) is concerned", it is about the desert, because there are some servants of Allah who pray in the desert, so you should not turn your back or turn towards them, but as far as the toilet built in houses is concerned," there is no prohibition to turn your back or face towards the Qibla.\"""""
172,"Wasee bin Hibban narrates: I have heard Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrating this, he says: Once I climbed onto the roof of Sayyida Hafsa's (RA) house, at a time when I thought that no one would leave the house at that time. When I noticed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on two bricks facing towards the Holy House and performing his ablutions."
173,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) brought a pot of water. This tradition has also been narrated along with other sources."
174,"Talha bin Nafi narrates: Sayyidna Abu Ayyub Ansari, Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari and Sayyidna Anas bin Malik Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them) have narrated this verse regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the verse is:) “In it are those who love it: they purify themselves well, and Allah loves those who purify themselves well.” is.” The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \O group of Ansar! Allah has highly praised you for attaining purity. What is your method of attaining purity?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution for prayer"," we bathe in the state of Janabat.\"" The Prophet", peace be upon him," said: \""Do you have any other method besides this?\"" He said: \""No! But when one of us defecates", he likes it," he should defecate with water.\"" So the Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him," said: \""This will be the reason for it"," you should adopt it.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Utbah bin Abu Hakim," is not authentic."""
175,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution with the water left by animals. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ibrahim bin Abi Hiyya, who is weak. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
176,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: It was asked: \O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution with the water left by the donkeys?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Perform ablution (also) with water from the hooves of animals.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Ibn Abi Habiba", weak," his name is Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abu Habiba."""
177,This tradition is narrated from Dawud bin Husain along with another chain of transmission.
178,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The price of a dog is impure and he himself is even more impure than that.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Yusuf Samti," is weak."""
179,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the houses of some Ansaris, the houses that were before their houses (he did not visit them there), so these people were surprised by this, they said: \O Messenger of Allah! You have visited the house of so-and-so and did not visit our house?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The reason for this is: There is a dog in your house.\"" He said: \""There is a cat in their house.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The cat is among the beasts.\"" Narrator Isa bin Musayb is unique in narrating this tradition and these hadiths are reliable in narrating."""
180,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \A cat is a beast.\"" In one tradition"," the word \""alhar\"" is used for cat."""
181,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish," that person should wash it seven times.\"" This tradition is \""correct\""."""
182,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish," he should empty the dish and wash the dish seven times.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is authentic and authentic"," and all its narrators are authentic."""
183,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, this hadith was narrated about a dog: When a dog puts its mouth into a vessel, he says: \The contents of it should be washed away"," and the vessel should be washed seven times.\"" This hadith is correct and \""suspended\""."""
184,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel", the way to purify it is to wash it seven times," the first of which is to be cleaned with mud.\"""""
185,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The method of purifying a person's vessel, when a dog has put its mouth in it," is this: He should wash it seven times and clean it with mud the first time.\"" Imam Uza'i attended the service of Ibn Sirin when he was ill. Imam Uza'i has not heard hadiths from Ibn Sirin."""
186,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The way to purify a vessel, when a dog has put its mouth in it, is this: This vessel should be washed seven times, the first of which should be cleaned with mud. If a cat has put its mouth in it," it should be washed once or twice.\"" This doubt belongs to the narrator named Qara"," and this tradition is authentic."""
187,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel," wash it seven times and clean it with mud the seventh time.\"""""
188,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
189,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains the words: \The first time to be cleansed with mud.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
190,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel," wash it seven times and the first time through mud.\"" This hadith is \""correct\""."""
191,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What is the benefit of this to the people?\"" Then the Prophet (PBUH) allowed dogs to be kept to protect the hunting dogs and goats. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"," wash it seven times and rub it with mud the eighth time.\"" This hadith is \""correct\""."""
192,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish," that person should wash it seven times and one of them should clean it with sand.\"" The narrator of this tradition is the son of Jarudzid and is \""abandoned\""."""
193,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about dogs: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel," a man should wash it three times (perhaps these words are:) five times or perhaps (these words are:) seven times.\"""""
194,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \That person should wash it three times (the narrator is doubtful"," perhaps these are the words:) wash it five times or wash it seven times.\"" The narrator named Abdul Wahab is unique in quoting this tradition from a narrator named Ismail and this narrator is a \""Mutaruk Hadith\"". Other narrators have narrated this tradition with reference to a narrator named Ismail and it has these words: \""Wash it seven times.\"" And this tradition is correct."""
195,"This same tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission, in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \You should wash it seven times.\"" This tradition is more authentic."""
196,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel," you should pour out the water in it and then wash it three times.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"" and no one has narrated it in this way (as a \""suspended\"" tradition) except for a narrator named Abdul Malik."""
197,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \If a dog puts its mouth in a vessel," a man should drain the water in it and wash the vessel three times.\"""""
198,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes a cat would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would hold out a vessel to it and it would drink water from it, and then he would perform ablution with the water from the cat's paws. A narrator named Abu Bakr narrates: The narrator of this tradition is Yaqub, this is Qazi Abu Yusuf, and the narrator named Abd Rabbah is Abdullah bin Saeed Maqbri, who is weak."
199,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu has this saying about the cat's dung: \This water should be drained away and this vessel should be washed once (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) twice.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""
200,"Muhammad bin Sirin narrates this about Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, he said: \When a cat puts its mouth in a vessel"," you should drain the water in it and wash it once.\"""""
201,Muhammad bin Sireen narrates the saying of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu: He said this about cats: \If it puts its mouth into a vessel," Sayyidna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Wash it once and drain the water in it.\"""""
202,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said this about a cat: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel," a man should wash it seven times.\"" The narrator of this hadith is not Laith bin Abu Salim Hafiz and this hadith is \""suspended\""", and is not authentically transmitted by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira RA," it is more likely that it is Ata's own saying."""
203,Hasan bin Ali narrates: I heard Ata narrate this: He said this about cats: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel," a man should wash it seven times.\"""""
204,"Saeed bin Musayb says: \A man should wash it twice (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) three times.\"""""
205,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel, the way to purify it is this: it should be washed seven times, and the first time it should be cleaned with mud, and the command about the cat is this," it should be washed once or twice.\"" This doubt belongs to the narrator named Qara. Narrator Abu Bakr has narrated this: Narrator Abu Asim narrated this hadith as a “marfu’ hadith"," while other narrators narrated the command about the dog as a “marfu’ hadith and the command to muzzle the cat as a “mawafuk” hadith."""
206,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says this about a cat: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel, you wash it once (the narrator is doubtful," perhaps these words are:) wash it twice.\"" This hadith is likewise narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah as a \""suspended\"" hadith."""
207,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \The vessel will be washed when a cat puts it in its mouth," just as it is washed when a dog puts it in its mouth.\"" This hadith is \""suspended\"" and is not authentically proven from Sayyidina Abu Huraira. Anxiety is found in some traditions of the narrator named Yahya bin Ayyub."""
208,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a cat puts its mouth in it," the vessel will be washed in the same way as it is washed when a dog's mouth is put in it.\"" Shaykh (Imam Darqutni) says: This hadith is not authentic as \""marfu'\"" and it is more authentic as the saying of Sayyidina Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu"," and there is also disagreement about this."""
209,"This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another chain of transmission."""
210,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \The vessel in which the cat puts its mouth should be washed seven times.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"" and not authentically transmitted."""
211,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
212,"The sons of Taos narrate this about their father: He used to wash the pot seven times, even after a cat's mouth, like a dog's mouth. Ibn Jaraj narrates: I asked Ata: What is the ruling of the cat? So he said: \It is like a dog.\"" Or perhaps he said: \""It's worse than that.\"""""
213,"Mujahid says about putting a cat's mouth in a vessel: \Wash this vessel seven times.\"""""
214,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to perform ablution from the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water. This tradition is \correct\""."""
215,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution using the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water."
216,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \This (cat) is not impure," but it is like the (animals) living in the house.\"" This saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is about the cat."""
217,"It was narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA): Once a cat ate some of Harisa, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) later ate some of it and said: \I saw the Prophet (PBUH)"," he used to perform ablution with cat's dung (water).\"" The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission", however," it is \""suspended\"" until Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."""
218,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour the pot towards the cat and the cat would drink from it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution through the cat's hooves."
219,"Narrated Sayyidah Kabsha bint Ka'b, who was the wife of one of the sons of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah: Once Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah entered the house of Ansari, and this woman kept ablution water for him. Meanwhile, a cat came to him to drink water from it, so Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) poured the pot towards him, and the cat drank the water. That woman narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Qutada (RA) saw me looking at him with great attention, he inquired: \O my niece! Are you surprised at this?\"" The woman narrates: I answered: \""Yes!\"" So Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) said: \""The Prophet (PBUH) said this: This (cat) is not impure"," but it is one of the (pet) animals that come to you.\"""""
220,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him): Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) (or perhaps Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him) was asked about the cat's hoof, and he said: \It is among the beasts"," and there is nothing wrong with it (i.e. its hoof).\"""""
221,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) searched for water for ablution, but they did not find it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: \Is there even a little water anywhere?\"" (He was present)", he was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet. The narrator narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his blessed hand on the vessel in which there was water," then he said: \""Invoke the name of Allah and start ablution.\"" Narrator narrates: I saw springs of water coming out from between your fingers and people started performing ablution"," until all the people performed ablution. A narrator named Thabit narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Anas: \""How many were you at that time?\"" Sayyiduna Anas (RA) replied: \""(We) were about seventy people.\"""""
222,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \He who does not mention the name of Allah in the beginning, it is as if he did not perform ablution, and he who does not perform ablution, it is as if he did not pray, and he who does not love me, it is as if he did not believe in me, and he who does not love the Ansar," it is as if he does not love me.\"""""
223,"Rabi' bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \There is no ablution for a person who does not recite the name of Allah at the beginning of it (i.e. does not recite Bismillah).\"""""
224,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch (the bowl of ablution) he used to recite Bismillah first. A narrator named Abu Badr has described this (that is, these words are in the hadith): \When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up for ablution", he would recite Bismillah," then pour water from the pot on his hand.\"""""
225,"Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates his father's statement regarding his grandmother: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution", and no ablution for a person who does not begin with the name of Allah (i.e. does not recite Bismillah), and a person does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me," and a person does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar.\"""""
226,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
227,"Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \There is no prayer without ablution", and whoever does not recite the name of Allah at the beginning, he does not have ablution, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and whoever does not love the Ansar, in fact," does not believe in me.\"""""
228,"Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I heard the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam saying: \The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer", and the person who does not recite Bismillah at the beginning," that person does not have his ablution.\"""""
229,"Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, narrate this, he says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: \The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer"," and the person who does not say \""Bismillah\"" at the beginning"," does not have his ablution.\"""""
230,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
231,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (Bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \When a person starts performing ablution", he should recite Bismillah first, because this will purify his whole body. If he does not recite Bismillah before performing ablution, then only that part of him that has water will be purified. There is no god but Allah, and Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the special servant and messenger of Allah, when he recites this, the gates of heaven will be opened for him.” The narrator of this tradition, Yahya bin Hashim," is weak."""
232,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah (i.e. Bismillah), his whole body is purified, and whoever performs ablution and does not recite the name of Allah (i.e. does not recite Bismillah)," then only that part of him on which he performed ablution becomes pure.\"""""
233,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah at the beginning of ablution," his whole body becomes pure.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: \""Whoever performs ablution and does not mention the name of Allah at the beginning"," only his specific parts are purified.\"""""
234,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \For one who cannot find water," the Prophet is a means of ablution.\"" Imam Abu Muhammad narrates: This means the Prophet who is not intoxicating. The Imam has also stated this: In this tradition", the narrator named Musayb has had an illusion and this illusion is in two places, one is that he has mentioned Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and the other is that he has mentioned the Prophet (PBUH). In this tradition," there is a difference in some words regarding the disaster."""
235,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Musaib as a \suspended\"" hadith"," not as a \""marfu'\"" hadith. More authentically", this is proven: This is the saying of Ikrima," it is not a hadith \""reported\"" to the Holy Prophet"," nor is it authentic to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas. The narrator named Masib is weak."""
236,"Narrated Ikramah: \Nabeez is a means of ablution for a person who does not have anything to perform ablution other than Nabeez (i.e. he does not have water).\"""""
237,Ikramah states: \Whoever finds nothing else besides Nabeez," he can perform ablution through Nabeez.\"" Imam Uza'i states: \""If that Prophet is intoxicating"," then a person will not perform ablution through it.\"" A narrator named Abdullah narrates: My father narrated: \""Whatever cannot be called water", my favorite opinion is this: A man should not perform ablution through it," and I like it more: A man should perform tayammum instead of performing ablution through the Prophet.\"""""
238,Narrated Ikramah: \Through water, one can perform ablution," who does not have access to water.\"""""
239,"Ikramah states: \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""
240,"Isa bin Ubaid narrates: I heard Ikrima, he was asked about a person: Who does not get water. Ikramah said: \That person should perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""
241,"Ikrimah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through water.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Ibn Muharr"," \""Mitrook al-Hadith\""."""
242,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person does not get water, and if he finds Nabid," he should perform ablution through Nabid.\"" The narrator of this hadeeth is Aban"," son of Abu Ayyash and it is a \""Mutaruk Hadith\"" while the narrator Muja'ah is \""weak\"". More authentically this is proven: this is Ikrima's opinion and not a \""marfu'\"" hadith."""
243,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates this statement from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him): On the night of the meeting with the Jinn, he performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a nabid, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with it. A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is not considered authentic. There is also a saying: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) was not present with the Prophet (PBUH) on the night of the meeting with the jinn. Alqamah bin Qais has narrated it in the same way. Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah and other narrators have narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu, he says: \I was not present on the night of the meeting with the jinn.\"""""
244,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Mas’ud (RA): Once he went out with the Prophet (PBUH), it was the night when he met the jinn, and the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: “O Ibn Mas’ud! Do you have water?” Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \I have Nabeez in a vessel.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Pour it over me.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it and said: \""It is also something to drink and purification can also be achieved from it.\"" A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is unique in narrating this tradition and it is a weak narrator."""
245,"Alqamah bin Qays narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him: \When the representatives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet"," was any of you present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that night?\"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu replied: \""No!\"" This hadith is authentic regarding its transmission from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud."""
246,"Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz narrated from us, he said: Ali bin Al-Jaad narrated from us, he was informed by Shu’ba, he from Amr bin Murrah, he said: I said to Abu Ubaidah, may God be pleased with him: “Did Abdullah bin Mas’ud participate in the night of the jinn?” He said: \No.\"""""
247,"Narrated Amr bin Murrah: I asked Abu Ubaidah: \Was Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud RA the night he met the jinn?\"" So they answered: \""No!\"" It is narrated in another hadith: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: On the night of the meeting with the jinn"," the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him: \""Do you have water?\"" So they said: \""No!\"" You then inquired: \""Do you have a Prophet?\"" The narrator says: I think"," the hadith has these words: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu replied: \""Yes!\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through this prophet. Imam Darqutni states: This hadith is not proven in two contexts"," which I have already mentioned."""
248,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but its narrators have been cross-examined."
249,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired on the night of his meeting with the jinn: \Do you have any water?\"" So they said: \""No!\"" I have a prophet. The narrator narrates: Then this prophet was brought and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through him."""
250,"Abu Wail narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of his meeting with the jinn. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) asked me at some part of the night: \O Ibn Mas'ud! Do you have water?\"" I said: \""No! By Allah! O Messenger of Allah! I have only Nabeez in the vessel.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The date palm is pure and its water is purifying.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it. A narrator named Hussain bin Ubaidullah used to invent and narrate traditions on the authority of Taqqa narrators."""
251,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me. He said: \Take a vessel of water with you.\"" Then you continued walking", I also stayed with you, then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu mentioned the incident of the meeting with the jinn. Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When I poured water on you from this vessel," it was Nabeez. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah! I have made a mistake"," I have brought Nabeez.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The date palm is sweet and its water is sweet.\"" A narrator named Hasan bin Qutiba is unique in narrating this tradition"," and both Hasan bin Tasheba and a narrator named Muhammad bin Isa are weak."""
252,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the night of my meeting with the jinn, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to bring water for ablution. This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Thaqafi on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu: It is unknown. According to one view his name is Amr and according to another view his name is Abdullah bin Amr."
253,"Abu Khaldah narrates: I asked Abul Aaliyah: A person who does not have water with him, but he has Nabeez, can he perform Ghusl Janabat through this Nabeez? So Abul Alia replied: \No!\"" So I mentioned to him the hadith about the meeting with the jinn"," and he said: \""The Nabeez that is made with you is evil. What it was was raisins and water.\"""""
254,It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He did not think there was anything wrong with performing ablution through the Prophet.
255,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He said: \There is no harm in performing ablution through water.\"""""
256,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution," and there is no ablution for a person who does not recite Bismillah at the beginning.\"""""
257,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
258,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water for ablution, he performed ablution with it once, and then he said: \This is the method of ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer.\"" Then he called for water and performed ablution twice with it"," then said: \""This is the method of ablution for a person who will get a double reward for performing ablution.\"" Then he stayed for a while", then he asked for water, then he performed ablution three times. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him," said: \""This is my way of ablution and that of the Prophets before me.\"""""
259,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
260,"The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA), but some of its narrators have been declared weak."
261,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution once and said: \This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer.\"" Then he performed ablution twice", twice," and said: \""This is the way of performing ablution for a person to whom Allah will reward him twice.\"" Then he performed ablution three times and said: \""This is my method of ablution and that of the Messengers before me.\"" Narrator named Musayb bin Al-Khalya is unique in narrating this tradition from Hafs bin Maysara and this narrator named Musayb is weak."""
262,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): “Whoever performs ablution once, this is the method of ablution that is necessary, and whoever performs ablution twice, he will receive double the reward, and whoever performs ablution three times, then this is my method and that of the prophets who came before me.”"
263,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water and performed ablution with it once, and then said: \This is the method of ablution. Whoever does not perform ablution in this way"," his prayer will not be accepted.\"" Then he performed ablution twice"," then he said: \""This is the method of ablution for a person who performs ablution in this way"," Allah will give him a double reward.\"" Then he performed ablution three times"," and then he said: \""This is my way and that of the prophets who came before me.\"""""
264,"Ubaidullah bin Abu Rafi' narrated this statement of his father: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution three times, and I saw him perform ablution once."
265,"Thabit Samali narrates: I asked Imam Abu Ja'far (Imam Muhammad Baqir) this: Has Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated this hadith to you? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once, once and twice, twice and three times, then Imam Abu Ja'far (i.e. Imam Baqir) replied: \Yes!\"" The narrator of this tradition", Samali, is not authentic," and the second narrator of this tradition is Ibn Bint Sidi Taqqa."""
266,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, who was shown the way to call the call to prayer in a dream, narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and washed both feet twice. Ibn Ayaina narrated it in the same way, by the way, its narrator is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd al-Mazni, may God be pleased with him, and these are not the Companions who were taught how to give the call to prayer in a dream."
267,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, may God be pleased with him, who was shown the way to call the Adhan in a dream, narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and both feet twice, and wiped his head twice."
268,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head and washed both his feet twice.\"""""
269,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his face three times and washed both his arms twice.\"""""
270,"Amr bin Yahya narrates the statement of his father: Amr bin Abu Hasan Mazni came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu. Amr ibn Abu Hasan requested: \Can you show us this? How did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu replied: \""Yes!\"" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah called for a vessel of water", he poured water from this vessel on his right hand and washed his right hand three times, then he poured water from the vessel on both his hands and washed both hands three times, then he put both his hands in the vessel and took a chawl of water and rinsed through it and poured water into his nose, then he cleaned his nose with water in a chawl three times, then he washed his face three times, each arm up to the elbows. Washed, then took some water and anointed the head with it, they moved their hands from front to back, then from back to front," then they washed both feet up to the ankles."""
271,"Hamran narrates: One day Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani asked for water for ablution, then he performed ablution, washed both hands three times, then rinsed, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his right arm up to the elbow three times and then washed his left arm in the same way, then he wiped his head, then he washed his right foot up to the ankle three times and then his left foot in the same way. Washed, and narrated this: \I saw the Holy Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, he performed ablution in the same way as I have performed ablution, then the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: 'Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine and then gets up and performs two nafls, in which he is not lost in his thoughts," Allah Almighty will forgive his past sins.'\"" Ibn Shahab Zahri narrates: Our scholars have stated: \""This is the way to perform ablution properly for prayer.\"""""
272,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he used to pour water up to his elbows. The narrator of this tradition, Ibn Aqeel, is not authentic."
273,"A narrator named Ubaidullah has narrated this on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Rafi': When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would move his ring (while washing his hands). Both the narrator of this tradition, Muammar and his father, are weak and this tradition is not authentic."
274,"Hamran narrates: He heard Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu, Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu said: \You people come forward", I will perform ablution according to the way of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," and show you people.\"" Then Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) washed his face", washed his arms up to the elbows, until they touched the edges of his shoulders, then he wiped his head, and passed his hands over his ears and beard," and then washed both his feet."""
275,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Grinding and pouring water into the nose is an obligatory part of ablution.\"""""
276,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \This is a part of ablution"," without which ablution is not complete.\"" Narrator Issam is unique in narrating this tradition and he is delusional about it. The correct tradition is that narrated by a narrator named Ibn Jarij as a \""Mursal\"" Hadith on the authority of Salman bin Musa", the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," said: \""Whoever performs ablution"," he should rinse and pour water into his nose.\"" Imam Darqutni states: I think that the narrator named Essam narrated this hadith with reference to his memory and it got mixed up on him", and he became suspicious of the authenticity of this hadith which was narrated as the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding Sayyida Aisha," may God bless him and grant him peace."""
277,"As for the hadeeth narrated by Ibn Jarij on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, which is about ablution and putting water in the nose, then it is: Ibn Jarij narrates: Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever performs ablution"," he should rinse and pour water in the nose.\"""""
278,Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution," he should rinse and pour water into his nose.\"""""
279,Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution," he should rinse and pour water into his nose.\"""""
280,"Sulaiman ibn Musa al-Shami narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this, followed by the previous hadith."
281,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution," he should rinse and pour water into his nose.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Muhammad bin Azhar Zaeef and this tradition is incorrect"," the \""Mursal\"" tradition that was narrated before it is more authentic. The rest Allah knows best."""
282,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It is Sunnah to rinse (during ablution) and pour water into the nose. The narrator of this tradition is Ismail bin Muslim \weak\""."""
283,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA): One day he called for water for ablution and then called some of the companions of the Prophet (RA), then he poured water on his left hand through his right hand and washed it three times. He rinsed three times, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, three times, then he wiped his head, then he washed both his feet and cleaned them well, then he narrated: \I saw the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution in the same way as you have just seen me perform ablution, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Whoever performs ablution and performs ablution well", then performs two rak'ahs of prayer," then his sins are as if they were on the day when his mother gave birth to him.\"""""
284,"Basar bin Saeed narrates: Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, came to the \Maqeed\""", he asked for water for ablution, rinsed, then poured water into his nose and then washed his face three times, then washed both arms three times, then washed his feet three times," then wiped his head and said: \""I remember this about the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace," he performed ablution in the same way.\"" Then Syedna Uthman Ghani (RA) addressed the audience and said: \""O Gentlemen! Is it like this?\"" So these gentlemen answered: \""Yes!\"" This was said by some of the companions of the Holy Prophet", may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who were present there at that time. This hadith is authentic, but it is not safe to delay wiping the head. One narrator is unique in narrating it while other narrators have narrated it along with their authority. All the narrators have narrated the same thing: Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may God be pleased with him) washed all the limbs three times," then said: \""I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution in this way.\"" These narrators did not narrate anything other than this. On the contrary"," a narrator named Waqi' has narrated this with reference to Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) washed each organ three times in ablution. Some other narrators have also narrated it in the same context."""
285,"Abu Anas narrates: Once Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) performed ablution in the sitting room, while some companions (RA) were present with him. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) washed each organ three times and then inquired: \Didn't you see the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution in the same way?\"" So these gentlemen answered: \""Yes!\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
286,"Abu Wail narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, he performed ablution and washed both hands three times, then washed his face three times, then rinsed his nose three times, poured water into his nose three times, then washed both arms three times, then wiped his head and the outside and inside of both ears, and then washed both feet three times, then he crossed his fingers, and when he had washed his face, he then washed his face three times. He had also shaved his beard, then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrated this: \I saw the Prophet (PBUH)"," he performed (ablution) in the same way as you have seen me perform (ablution).\"" This hadith is narrated with the same words", but at one point in this hadith, the narrator is delusional, because it mentions the beginning of ablution by washing the face and this is before washing the face, rinsing and putting water in the nose," while the narrator named Abdul Rahman has narrated this tradition along with the same chain of transmission and it mentions the beginning of ablution by washing the face and putting water in the nose and this process is before washing the face."""
287,"Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, first he washed both hands three times, then he rinsed, he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head and then he wiped the inside and outside of both ears, he shaved his beard three times and then he washed both feet, he also washed his toes three times. and said: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform (ablution) in the same way as I have performed this (ablution).\"" The words of these two traditions are very close."""
288,"Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and after washing his arms, he wiped his head with a cotton swab."
289,"Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to visit us, and when he performed ablution, he would wipe his head with the remaining water after washing both arms and wipe in this way. After that, a narrator named Abdullah bin Dawud showed him by wiping and bringing his two hands from the back of the head to the front and then moving both hands from the front to the back of the head."
290,"A narrator named Ziyad narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) and asked him about performing ablution and said: \Should I start with the right hand or should I start with the left hand?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali reprimanded him and then he called for water and (doing ablution) washed his left hand before his right hand."""
291,"Narrated Ziyad: A man asked Sayyiduna Ali: \Can I wash my left hand before my right hand during ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali rebuked him"," then he called for water and washed his left hand before his right hand."""
292,"A narrator named Ziyad narrates: Sayyiduna Ali was asked: \Sayyidna Abu Huraira always washes the right organ first in ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali called for water and started from the left side while doing ablution."""
293,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When I perform ablution," I do not care with which organ (right or left) I have started?\"""""
294,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
295,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \I do not care about this, when I start ablution," I start with my left hand before my right hand.\"""""
296,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Abbas may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: \There is nothing wrong with that. You wash (in ablution) both your feet before your arms.\"" This tradition is \""transmitted\"" and it is not proven."""
297,"It was narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA): He was asked about a person who washes his left side first while performing ablution, then Sayyidna Abdullah (RA) said: \There is nothing wrong with that.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
298,"A narrator named Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: “He first washed his two hands while doing ablution, then rinsed them three times and poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times and then washed both feet three times, and then said: ‘Whoever likes to see the way of ablution of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, let him. Look at this way.'\ Shuaib", the narrator, has narrated these words: (Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him) said: A narrator named Abu Hanifa has narrated this hadith with reference to a narrator named Khalid, in it he has quoted these words: Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, wiped his head three times, while a group of Muhadditheen have also narrated this tradition in other contexts, and it mentions wiping his head once. Among these other muhaddiths, only the narrator named Hajjaj has been delusional at one point, he has mentioned the narrator named Amr Dhamar instead of the narrator named Abd Khair. According to our knowledge, no narrator except Imam Abu Hanifa has mentioned wiping the head three times. Imam Abu Hanifa has narrated something different from other narrators in his tradition, while on the other hand, his own opinion about the order of wiping is also different from this tradition, which he has narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, with reference to Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him," because Imam Abu Hanifa also states this: \""It is Sunnah to wipe the head once in ablution.\"" This has been narrated by Ibrahim bin Abu Yahya and Qazi Abu Yusuf along with their chain of transmission from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
299,"Abd Khair narrates: One day Sayyiduna Ali (RA) sat outside in the field after performing the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: \Bring water for ablution!\"" The servant brought water in a pot and brought a saucer with him. We were looking at Sayyiduna Ali", he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both his hands, and then he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand and washed his hands, he did this three times. A narrator named Abd Khair narrates: In each of these times, he did not put his hand inside the vessel, but poured water from the vessel and washed both hands three times. Then he put his right hand into the pot and (taking water) rinsed through it and poured water into his nose. He wiped his nose from inside with his left hand, he did this three times, then he put his right hand into the pot and washed his face three times, then he washed his right arm up to the elbow three times and his left arm up to the elbow three times, then he put his right hand into the pot until his hand was filled with water, then he raised it with the water and then turned his left hand over it and both hands He wiped his head once, then he poured water on his right foot three times with his right hand and washed that foot three times with his left hand. He poured water on his left foot three times with his right hand and washed it with his left hand. If he sees the way of ablution of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then this is the way of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some narrators have copied some of the words of this tradition more or less," but the meaning of all of them is close to each other and is authentically proven."""
300,"Abd Khair narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed all his limbs three times while performing ablution and took fresh water for his head.\"""""
301,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him: When he performed ablution, he washed his hands three times, poured water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth three times, then washed his face three times, washed each of his two arms three times, wiped his head three times, then washed his feet three times, then said: \I saw the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace," perform ablution in this way.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Ishaq Yahya," is weak."""
302,"Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, then he rinsed first, then he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, then he trimmed his beard three times, then he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head three times, he washed both feet three times, and then he narrated this matter to the Prophet, peace be upon him. I have seen him doing (ablution) like that.”"
303,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He called for water for ablution, then washed both his hands three times, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times and said: \I saw the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace," perform ablution in the same way. He also said: 'Whoever performs ablution less than that It would also be permissible to do so."""
304,"Narrated by Ibn Daraa: I entered the house of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and he heard my voice saying that I was performing ablution, so he called out: \O Muhammad!\"" I said: \""I am here!\"" He said: \""Shall I not tell you the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet?\"" I replied: \""Yes!\"" So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: \""I remember well about the Holy Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, water was brought for him, he was sitting in the courtyard at that time, he rinsed three times, poured water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his arms three times, wiped his head three times, washed his feet three times, and (then Sayyidna Uthman," may God be pleased with him) said this. Ki: \""This is how the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. I wanted to show you this.\"""""
305,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He performed ablution in a maqa'id (open space), in Madinah the maqa'id (open space) is where the funeral prayer is performed near the mosque. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani first washed his hands three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then rinsed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times. A person greeted him, he was still performing ablution, Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani did not respond to the greeting until he finished performing ablution, when he finished, he presented an excuse to him while talking to him and said: \I did not respond to the greeting because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever performs ablution in this way and does not utter a word during ablution and this (After ablution) read: \""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah", He is One God and He has no partners," Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His special servant and His special Messenger.\"""""
306,Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: \While performing ablution, he washed each organ three times and wiped his head and both ears three times and said: 'This is the way of ablution of the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him," I like to show you this.'\"""""
307,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever performs ablution and washes his hands three times, pours water into his nose three times, rinses his mouth three times, washes his face and both arms three times, wipes his head three times, washes his feet three times, then recites: ‘I testify that there is no god but Allah, and Sayyidna Muhammad. (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) is His special servant and messenger.''"
308,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him): Once he came with some of his companions and sat in a muqa'id (open space), he asked for water for ablution, then he washed both his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, poured water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, wiped his head once, then washed his two feet three times, and then said this Ki: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution in the same way. I was already in a state of ablution"," but I liked this. Let me show you how the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution.\"""""
309,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to wash each organ twice while performing ablution.
310,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) used to perform ablution twice.
311,"Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution for prayer, he would move the ring on his finger."
312,"Ghulam Safina, the slave of Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with one \Mud\"" of water and performed Ghusl with one \""Sa'\"" of water."""
313,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with about one mudd of water and performed ghusl with about one saa of water.
314,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with two \liters\"" of water and one \""Sa'\"" with eight liters of water. A narrator named Musa bin Nasr is unique in narrating this tradition and this Sahib is weak."""
315,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Ten things are part of nature: trimming the moustache, growing the beard, brushing the nose, cleaning the nose with water, clipping the nails, cleaning the armpit hair, cleaning the pubic hair," and defecating with water.\"" A narrator named Zakariya has narrated this: A narrator named Musab has narrated this: \""I have forgotten the tenth thing"," but it must be washed.\"" The narrator named Al-Khajri has quoted this with reference to the narrator named Zakariya and stated: The word \""Intaqas al-Ma'a\"" used in the hadith means to withdraw through water. A narrator named Musab bin Shaba is unique in narrating this. Narrators Abu Bashar and Sulaiman have narrated this differently", they have narrated this hadith on the authority of Talaq bin Habib, as their own words," and have not narrated this hadith as a \""marfu'\"" hadith."""
316,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Harith bin Jaz Zubaydi (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \For (some) heels and soles are the destruction of Hell.\"""""
317,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he used to rub his toes (toes) and touch his heels, and he used to say: \What do you rub between your toes", Allah will not enter the fire between them," and some heels are doomed to hell.\"""""
318,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Make a cross between your fingers, Allah will not cross between them on the Day of Resurrection with fire.”"
319,"This is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Rifa'a bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyidna Rifa'a (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Malik bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) are brothers and participated in the Battle of Badr. Sayyidna Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were sitting with the Holy Prophet (may Allah's prayers and peace be upon him). He prayed facing the Qiblah, when he finished the prayer, he came and greeted the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and also greeted the people present. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \You must go back and pray"," because you did not actually pray.\"" This person started to pray again", we kept examining his prayer carefully, we didn't understand what he did wrong? When he finished the prayer," he came and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those present. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \""It is obligatory upon you"," you go and pray again. You have not actually prayed.\"" A narrator named Hammam narrates: I do not know what is mentioned in the hadith", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him twice or instructed him three times," then the person said: \""What have I missed? I do not know which part of my prayer you are invalidating?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""No one's prayer is complete until he performs ablution well as Allah Almighty has commanded him. He should first wash his face", then wash both arms up to the elbows, then wipe his head, wash both feet up to the ankles, mention the greatness of Allah, praise Him, then recite Surah Al-Fatihah," then recite what is his destiny.\"" I said", let him recite (parts of the Qur'an) that he finds easy, then say the Takbeer and go into Ruku, and place both his hands on his knees until his joints are satisfied and wide, then he should recite 'Sami'Allah Liman Hamda' and stand up straight, until his back is straight, and every bone is in its place, then he should say the Takbeer and go into Sajdah," and keep his forehead fixed. A narrator named Hammam has sometimes quoted these words here: \""He should place his forehead on the ground", until his joints are relaxed and wide, then he should sit on his back saying the Takbeer," and keep his back straight.\"" After that", he explained the way of praying in the four rak'ahs in the same way, until he explained it completely and (the Prophet," peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""No one's prayer is complete until he does this.\"""""
320,"Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated this on the authority of Sayyida Rabi bint Mu’awz: He asked Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) about the manner of ablution of the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him), and Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) replied: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit her, she used to keep ablution water for the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him). Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Once I came to this woman, and she took out a vessel in front of me and told me: “In this vessel, I used to draw water for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to perform ablution. He washed both arms, then wiped his head from front to back and from back to front, then he washed both feet, then this woman said: \Your cousin also came to me", this woman meant Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, so I told him about this," so he said: \""I find two things in the book of God and two things to be wiped.\"" Let's do: I inquired of this lady: \""How much water was in that pot?\"" So they replied: \""As much as a 'Hashmi Madd' is"," as much as a common Madd and a quarter Madd.\"" A narrator named Abbas bin Yazid narrated this: This woman narrated the following on the authority of the Holy Prophet: The Holy Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him, washed his face before ablution and pouring water into his nose, while the people of Badr narrated this, including Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani and Sayyiduna Ali," may Allah be pleased with them. They used to do it before washing and this is also the common practice of people."""
321,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator narrated it as follows: However", this is an illusion on the part of the narrator," because the correct thing is: It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a “suspended” tradition."""
322,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator has quoted this tradition as \""Marfu'\"" tradition and it is his illusion. This is the correct thing", it is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as his own saying. The narrator of this tradition, Qasim bin Yahya," is weak."""
323,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator has quoted this tradition as a \""marfu' hadith in the same way", but this is his illusion," while other narrators have also quoted it as a \""marfu' tradition with reference to Ubayd Allah", but this is also their illusion. In addition, the narrator has also been delusional in mentioning a narrator named Thauri, however, along with another chain of transmission," this tradition is from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a \""moquf\"" tradition. It is portable."""
324,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""
325,"Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Wasti narrated that Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to him, he said that Abu Bakr told him that Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated from Ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to wipe both ears and say, \These are the two parts of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a \""suspended\"" hadith."""
326,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to wipe both ears and say: \These two are part of the head.\"""""
327,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
328,"Hilal bin Usamah narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) say: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
329,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
330,"It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Muhammad bin Fazl Muhammad bin Fazl bin Atiya"," and it is a “Mutaruk Hadith”."""
331,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
332,"The same tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions, in which the narrator is delusional at some point. The subject of this tradition also exists, but the narrator narrating it is obsolete. However, more accurately, this tradition is transmitted as a \messenger\"" tradition from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to a narrator named Sulaiman bin Musa."""
333,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
334,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \(When performing ablution) rinse and pour water into the nose and the two ears are part of the head (ie the ears will be wiped like the head).\"" The narrator of this hadith is Rabi bin Badr."""
335,"Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
336,"Sulaiman bin Musa quoted the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
337,"The same tradition is also narrated with reference to Sulaiman bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
338,"The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Solomon bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
339,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Both ears are part of the head.\"" Narrator named Ali bin Asim has been deceived in quoting this tradition", he has narrated it from the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira," the tradition that has been narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurij before him is more authentic."""
340,Sayyida Aisha Sadiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution, he should rinse and pour water into his nose, and both ears are part of the head," (meaning they will also be anointed).\"" It is quoted as such by the narrator"," but it is more authentic to be the \""Messenger\""."""
341,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person performs ablution," he should rinse and put water in his nose and both ears are part of the head.\"""""
342,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated the same thing with reference to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but in it there are these words:"
343,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Grinding and putting water in the nose is a part of ablution without which ablution is not complete," and the two ears are part of the head (i.e. they will be wiped over both of them).\"" The narrator of this hadith is Jabir Zaeef"," and there is a difference of opinion in this hadith regarding quoting from him. A narrator named Huqam bin Abdullah has narrated it as a Mursal tradition and this seems to be more accurate."""
344,A narrator named Ata has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Grinding and pouring water into the nose is one of the acts of ablution, without which ablution is not complete," and the two ears are part of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Umar bin Qays along with his chain of command as a \""suspended\"" hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."""
345,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: \In ablution," the two ears are part of the head (i.e. both ears will also be wiped) and in Ihram they are part of the face (i.e. they will not be covered).\"" The narrator of this tradition", Umar bin Qais, is weak. This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (Radi Allahu Anhu) along with another chain of transmission," but there is some disagreement in it."""
346,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \It is Sunnah to rinse and pour water into the nose," and the two ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Ismail bin Muslim weak and Qasim bin Ghassan is also weak like him. Ali bin Hashim has some differences in quoting this hadith", he narrated it along with his chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA)," but this is also not authentic."""
347,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person performs ablution," he should rinse and put water in his nose and both ears are part of the head.\"" This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission."""
348,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
349,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
350,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and one of its narrators is Muhammad bin Ziyad Matrook Hadith. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated as a \suspended\"" hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
351,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The same tradition has also been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."""
352,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rinse (while performing ablution) and pour water into the nose, both ears are part of the head. One of the narrators of this hadith, Amr Ibn Husayn, and the other narrator, Ibn Alashah, are weak."
353,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition", Ibn Muharr," is obsolete."""
354,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Bakhtari bin Ubayd Zaeef and his father is unknown."""
355,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Ali Ibn Jafar as a \""marfu'\"" hadith", but it is more correct," this hadith is \""suspended\""", the narrator of this hadith, Hasan," has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
356,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"". Some other narrators have followed suit. The same hadith is also narrated from Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
357,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" (He has also stated this:) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the corners of both eyes and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe his blessed head once. The narrator of this tradition", Shahr bin Haushab," is not authentic. A narrator named Sulaiman bin Harb has narrated this tradition as a \""suspended\"" tradition and this narrator is trustworthy and authentic."""
358,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu has quoted the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
359,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) has quoted this saying of the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words: Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" That is"," doubt is found in this tradition."""
360,"It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrators have narrated it in the same way with reference to the narrator named Hamad", however," the narrator named Sulaiman bin Harb has narrated something differently. These Sahibs are trustworthy and Hafiz."""
361,"A narrator named Shahr bin Hushab has narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA): Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) narrated the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: When the Prophet (SAW) used to perform ablution, he used to wipe the corners of his eyes with water. Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu also stated: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" Sulaiman bin Harb has stated: \""Both ears are part of the head.\"" This is the saying of Sayyidina Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu", who says something other than this (i.e. declares it as Hadith) then he has changed. Here the narrator Solomon said something else, which meant: He has made a mistake. Some other narrators have narrated something different from this, they have narrated this on the authority of Anas (RA): When the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution, he used to wash the corners of both eyes with his fingers. However," he did not mention the two ears in this tradition."""
362,"Daalaj ibn Ahmad narrates: I asked Musa ibn Haroon about this hadith, and he said: \There is no truth in it", its chain of narrators is Shahr bin Hushab, and the narrator named Shahr is weak," and there is doubt about the 'marfu' of this hadith.\"" The narrator becomes anxious in reciting the hadith."""
363,"Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This hadith is \""transmitted\"""," and this hadith is \""continuously\"" transmitted from the Prophet", may Allah bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah," but it is not authentic. The narrator of this hadith is Abu Bakr bin Maryam."""
364,"Rashid bin Saad narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
365,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Jafar bin Zubair," is obsolete."""
366,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" A narrator of this tradition", Abd Hakim," is not considered authentic."""
367,"``Urwa bin Qubaysa, on the authority of an Ansari, quoted the saying of Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father: \You people know this! The two ears are part of the head.\"""""
368,"Narrated Umrah: I asked Sayyida Aisha about the two ears, and she replied: \These two ears are part of the head.\"" Then he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the outer and inner parts of both ears while performing ablution. One of the narrators of this tradition is Yaman \""weak\""."""
369,"Abd Khair narrates: Once Sayyiduna Ali (RA) came and sat in the courtyard after offering the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: \Bring me water for ablution!\"" The servant brought water to you in a vessel", he brought a saucer with him, we were looking at Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both palms, then he held the vessel with his right hand and poured water on his left hand, then he washed both his hands, he did this three times. A narrator named Abd Khair narrates: Every time he washed his hands, he did not put his hand in the vessel, until he washed both hands three times, then he put his right hand in the vessel and rinsed (by taking water through it), poured water into his nose, wiped his nose with his left hand, he did this three times, then he washed his right arm three times up to the elbow, then he put his left hand in the vessel and filled it with water, then As much water as was in it, he raised his hand with that water and wiped it with his left hand and then he wiped his head once with both his hands. Then he poured water on his left foot three times with his right hand and washed it three times with his left foot. Whoever likes to see the way of ablution of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then this is his way.” Some narrators have reduced or increased some of his words," but their meaning is close."""
370,"Ayyub bin Abdullah narrates: I saw Hasan bin Abul Hasan, he asked for water for ablution, and a large pot of water was brought to him, then the water was poured into the bowl, he first washed both hands three times, then rinsed them three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head, then wiped both ears. And trimmed his beard, then washed both his feet up to the ankles, then narrated this: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu narrated this hadith to me."
371,"Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution. He (PBUH) wiped the front and back of his head and both ears, then he (PBUH) inserted his index fingers and wiped the outside and inside of the ear with them."
372,"Hameed narrates: Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to wipe the top and inside of his ears when performing ablution, and then he would say: \I saw the Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," do this.\"" Other narrators have narrated it on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) as his act."""
373,"Hameed narrates: I saw Sayyidna Anas bin Malik performing ablution, he wiped the inside and outside of both his ears and then said: \Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud used to order (to wipe both ears).\"""""
374,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would gently touch both his cheeks and then use his fingers to stroke his beard from below."
375,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform ablution (after that he narrated it according to the previous hadith). However, he did not quote this hadith as a \marfu'\"" hadith and that is correct."""
376,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that: When he used to wipe his head, he would lift his cap and wipe the front part of his head."
377,Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed me: \When we perform ablution for prayer," wash our feet.\"""""
378,"Abu Ammar narrates: He has had the privilege of visiting some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (He then narrated the entire incident). Sayyiduna Amr bin Absa (RA) narrated: \I said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something about ablution!\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Whoever performs ablution", he should first rinse, then put water in his nose and clean his nose, then all his sins, even from the bamboo of his nose, all the sins come out with the water. Then when he washes his face, as Allah commanded him, all the sins from his face, even from the edges of his beard, fall with the water. Then when he washes both his arms up to the elbows, all the sins of his arms, even the nails, fall with the water. fall down, then he gets up and praises Allah according to His glory, praises Him, then offers two rak'ahs of prayer, then he is (purified) from his sins," as it was on the day when his mother gave birth to him.\"""""
379,"This tradition is narrated along with another document. Its certificate is \proven\"" and \""authentic\""."""
380,"Abd al-Rahman bin Sabat narrated this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA), or perhaps on the authority of the brother of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA): Once the Prophet (PBUH) saw some people (doing ablution), the water of one of them had not reached the heel of a dirham, or perhaps the size of a nail, so the Prophet (PBUH) began to say: It's a waste.\ (The narrator narrates:) \""A man should examine this", if he sees a place where the water has not reached," then he should perform ablution again.\"""""
381,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once a person came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he had performed ablution and left a part of his foot as much as a nail (the water did not reach there), so the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Go back and perform ablution well.\"" A narrator named Jarir bin Hazim is unique in narrating this tradition from Qatadah and this narrator is reliable."""
382,"Salim, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, has quoted the statement of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, on the authority of Sayyiduna Omar, who said: \Once I was sitting with the Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him," while a man came.\"" This is narrated in another hadith", Salem has narrated this tradition from Sayyidna Abu Bakr Radi Allahu Anhu and Sayyidna Umar Radi Allahu Anhu with reference to Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar RA. The narrator narrates: Once a person came, who had performed ablution and he did not reach the part of the back of his foot, which was the size of the big toe of his foot (i.e. that part was left dry during ablution)," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Go back and complete your ablution!\"" So the man did just that."""
383,"The meaning of this hadith is close to each other, one of its narrators, Waza' bin Nafi', has been described as weak in the knowledge of hadith."
384,"Ubaid bin Umayr narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab once saw a person whose feet were partially dry and while performing ablution, water did not reach there. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered him: \Let him wash this dry place and pray again.\"""""
385,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA): Once he saw a person whose back part of his feet was dry, the water did not reach there, then Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to him: \Have you joined the prayer with this ablution?\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful! It is very cold and I have nothing to stop it.\"" Sayyiduna Umar", may Allah be pleased with him, had started to be harsh with him before, but after hearing this," he softened and said to him: \""Wash the part of your foot that you have left"," and pray again.\"" Then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) instructed him to fight."""
386,"Alaa bin Ziyad narrates the following on the authority of one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Once, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. You had bathed, but part of your body was left dry where the water did not reach. We said: \O Messenger of Allah! This part has remained dry"," water has not reached here?\"" The blessed Prophet's hair was thick"," he moistened that part with the moisture of his (wet) hair. One of the narrators of this hadith is Abd Salam bin Salih visual and not authentic. Other reliable narrators have narrated it as a \""Mursal\"" tradition", via a narrator named Ishaq," via a narrator named Alaa."""
387,"Alaa bin Ziyad narrated: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a little dry spot on his neck. This tradition is transmitted and it is correct."
388,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a special cloth with which he used to dry his limbs during ablution. The narrator of this tradition is Abu Mu'adh, Sulaiman bin Arqam and it is obsolete."
389,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, I took the water left over from his ablution and poured it into my well."
390,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father, Sayyidna Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the first revelation was revealed to him, Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and showed him how to perform ablution and pray. When he finished his ablution, he took water in a chloe and sprinkled it on his private parts."
391,"Sayyiduna Osama Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When Sayyidna Jibraeel (peace be upon him) was revealed to the Prophet (peace be upon him) (in the early days), he showed the Prophet (peace be upon him) how to perform ablution."
392,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: \Ghusl becomes wajib when the private part meets the private part.\"" When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this"," we used to bathe."""
393,"It was narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA): She was asked about a person who has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate, then Sayida Aisha (RA) said: \When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this"," we both used to take ghusl together.\"" This same tradition is transmitted as a \""marfu'\"" tradition in some other contexts"," and it is transmitted as a \""suspended\"" tradition with respect to some isnads."""
394,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Umm Kulthum (may God be pleased with him) narrated to me on the authority of Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with him), a person asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about a man who has intercourse with his wife and then (ends intercourse) before ejaculation, \Would it be necessary to perform ghusl on him?\"" So at that time", Sayyida Aisha (RA) was also sitting there," and the Holy Prophet (SAW) said: \""She and I (that is", Sayya A'isha (RA) sometimes do it like this," but then we take bath.\"")"""
395,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) offered the morning prayer. You had performed Ghusl Janabat, a verma-sized part of your blessed body was left dry where the water did not reach. It was reported: \O Messenger of Allah! The water did not reach this place.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dripped the water from his hair on that spot and turned his hand there", he did not perform the prayer again. The narrator of this hadeeth is Mutawakkil Bin Fazeel Zaeef. This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission," one of the narrators of which is a Mutrook Hadith."""
396,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a small area on his skin where the water had not reached, so he squeezed some water from his hair and applied that water to that place."
397,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person has intercourse with a woman, ghusl becomes obligatory on him," whether he has ejaculated or not.\"""""
398,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \When a man has intercourse with a woman," ghusl becomes obligatory on him.\"" A narrator quotes these words: \""Even if he has not ejaculated.\"""""
399,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Ghusl becomes necessary for four reasons: because of Janabat, on Fridays, after applying the ointment," and after giving Ghusl to the dead.\"" One of the narrators of this hadith", Musab bin Shiba," is not authentic and neither is Hafiz."""
400,Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Janabat does not affect water, it does not affect land, and it does not affect clothes (i.e., if a person who is Janabi puts his hand in water or lies down on the ground or wears any cloth," he is not impure.\"")"""
401,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) states: \There is no janabat in four things: in man, in water," in earth and in clothes.\"""""
402,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform Ghusl Janabat, first of all he would wash both his hands, then he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, then he would insert his hand into the blessed vessel and then run the water through the roots of his hair, until when he felt that he had washed his skin thoroughly, he would fill both hands with water three times. He used to pour it on his head, then wash the whole body afterwards."
403,"Jami bin Umayr narrates: Once I attended Sayyida Aisha's service with my mother and aunt, and Sayyida Aisha said: \The Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, then he would pour water on our heads three times, and we (women) would pour water on our heads five times," because our hair was tied.\"""""
404,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimunah (RA) told me this, once when the Prophet (PBUH) began to perform Ghusl Janabat, I came close to him, then he washed both his hands two or maybe three times. What, then performed ablution like the ablution of prayer, then you washed your whole body with water in both palms, then you moved away from that place a little and you washed both your feet, then I brought a handkerchief to you (so that you could wipe your body) so you did not accept it."
405,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of his aunt Sayyida Maimunah (RA), she says: \I kept water for the bath of the Holy Prophet (PBUH)"," because he (PBUH) had to perform Ghusl Janabat.\"" He poured water on his left hand through his right hand and then washed both his hands three times", then he put his right hand into the vessel and poured water on his private parts, then he touched his hand on the wall or the ground, then he rinsed, poured water into his nose, then he washed his face and arms and then he poured water over his whole body," then he The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left that place and washed both feet."""
406,Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: \My hair used to be tightly tied in the form of braids. I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: This is enough for you. You fill your head three times with both hands and pour water. (The narrator has doubts about the wording of the hadith here) If you pour water over your entire body," then you will be purified.\"""""
407,Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the Ghusl of Janabat.
408,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
409,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) made it obligatory for a Janabi person to perform ablution three times and pour water into the nose. Imam Darqutni states: This hadith is invalid. No one narrated it except a narrator named Barqa, and this narrator named Barqa used to make hadiths on his own. The correct tradition is the one narrated by a narrator named Waqiyyah, which we have previously quoted as a “Mursal” tradition on the authority of Ibn Sirin: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat."
410,Ibn Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat.
411,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) narrates: \If a person washes his face during Ghusl Janabat (and forgets to put water in his nose)," then he will wash his nose again and put water in his nose and pray from where he left off.\"" Ibn 'Arafah states: \""If a man forgets to perform ablution in Ghusl Janabat and pour water into his nose", and (he remembers during the prayer), he will leave the prayer, perform ablution, pour water into his nose," and pray afresh.\"" Imam Darqutni states: This is the only hadith transmitted by a female narrator named Aisha bint Ajard"," and the hadith transmitted by her cannot be considered authentic."""
412,Aisha bint Ajard narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will perform the prayer again in the case of forgetting to perform ablution in Janabat and putting water in the nose," but he will not do this during ablution.\"""""
413,"Aisha bint Ajard has narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will repeat the prayer only when he is on his side.\"""""
414,"Aisha bint Ajard narrated this about a Janbi person: \Whoever (while taking bath) forgets to rinse and put water in his nose.\"" That woman narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: \""He will rinse"," pour water into his nose and perform the prayer again.\"""""
415,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed us to rinse and pour water into the nose. This tradition is also transmitted along with another chain of transmission and it is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition. However"," other narrators have also narrated it as a \""Mursal\"" tradition."""
416,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, but there is some difference in its chain of transmission. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (R.A.) is not mentioned in one chain of transmission."
417,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this: \A man should bathe with the water left over from a woman's bath, or a woman should bathe with the water left over from a man's (bath)," but both of them can bathe together.\"" A narrator named Shuba has narrated the opposite tradition."""
418,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Sarjis Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \A woman can perform ablution or ghusl with the water left over from a man's bath or ablution," but a man cannot perform ablution through the water left over from a woman's bath or ablution.\"" This hadith is more authentic in terms of \""mafuk\"" and it is more correct."""
419,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Menstruating women and menstruating women should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""
420,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
421,The same hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has been narrated along with another chain of transmission and it has also been followed.
422,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
423,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \A foreigner should not read the Qur'an at all.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
424,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \A pregnant person and a menstruating woman should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""
425,"Abu Zarif Hamdani narrates: Once we were with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) in an open field, Sayyidna Ali (RA) went to the edge of this field. By Allah! I don't know, did they urinate or defecate, they called for a vessel of water, then they washed both their hands and then joined them both and recited the first part of the Qur'an and then said: \You can recite the Qur'an until a person is afflicted with Janabat", if he is afflicted with Janabat," then he cannot recite a single word of it.\"" This hadith has been authentically narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
426,"According to a hadith, it was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). According to the second chain of transmission, this is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrates: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \O Ali! I am pleased with you with what I am pleased with myself", and I dislike for you with what I dislike with myself. Do not recite the Qur'an when you are in the state of Janabat, nor do it when you are in the state of Ruku, nor do it when you are Be in a state of prostration, and do not pray while your hair is tied," and do not bow down (in the state of bowing during the prayer) as a donkey bows its head.\"""""
427,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Ghafqi narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate something and then he said: \Tonic the veil for me so that I may take a bath!\"" I inquired of you: \""Are you in a state of janabat?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Yes!\"" Later", I told Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) about this," so he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: \""He has told that"," the Prophet (PBUH) ate and drank something in the state of Janabat.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: \""Yes! When I perform ablution", I can eat and drink," but I cannot recite Qur'aat until I perform ablution.\"""""
428,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Malik Ghafqi narrates: He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this from Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: \When I perform ablution in the state of Janabat", I can eat and drink," but I do not offer prayers or recite the Qur'an until I have performed ghusl.\"""""
429,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was nothing that prevented the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from reciting the Qur’an, except when he was in a state of janabat. A narrator named Sufyan narrates: Shu'ba said to me: \I have not narrated a better hadith than him.\"""""
430,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"" The evidence of this tradition is excellent. Some other narrators did not mention Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas in his chain of transmission."""
431,"It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has prohibited us from saying: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""
432,"Ikramah narrates: Once Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha was sleeping by the side of his wife, he got up and went to his maidservant who was at the edge of the house and started having intercourse with her. His wife was frightened in a dream. When she went out, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (RA) had finished with the company and was coming back. He was confronted by his wife who was holding a knife, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha (RA) said: \What happened?\"" So his wife replied: \""What is the matter", if I had found you in the state in which I saw you before," I would have put this knife between your two shoulders.\"" Ibn Rawaha inquired: \""Where did you see me?\"" So the wife replied: \""I have seen you consorting with maidens.\"" So Ibn Rawaha said: \""You did not see me.\"" Then Sayyiduna Ibn Rawaha said: \""The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade anyone from reciting the Qur'an in the state of Janabat.\"" So the wife said: \""Then you recite.\"" So Sayyiduna Ibn Rawahha recited these verses: \""There came to us the Messenger of Allah reciting His Book", which is more famous and brighter than the bright and bright morning, He brought us guidance, after our hearts had become blind, it was guidance that was reassuring and what he said came to pass. He used to spend the night in such a position that his side was separated from the bed," when the bed of the polytheists was their weight.\"" were burdened by So the woman said: \""I believe in Allah and deny what I have seen with my eyes.\"" Then the next day", Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawaha (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about this," and the Prophet (PBUH) smiled. Narrator narrates: Until I saw your side teeth."""
433,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah entered the house (after that he narrated the entire incident, in which these words are:) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah narrated that: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""
434,Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu states: \A menstruating woman," a pregnant woman and a postpartum woman will not recite the Qur'an.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Yahya"," this is Ibn Abi Anisa and it is weak."""
435,"Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrates this statement of his father: The letter that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, also contained the following: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are ablution.\"" This hadith is \""Mussal\"" and its narrator is \""Thiqa\""."""
436,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates: The letter that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm (RA), when he sent him to Najran, contained the following:"
437,"Salim narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
438,"Abdullah ibn Abu Bakr and Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr narrate this on the authority of their father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter to him, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
439,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wrote this letter to the people of Yemen, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
440,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are in the state of ablution.\"""""
441,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: Sayyidna Umar came out with a sword hanging around his neck and was told: \Your brother-in-law and your sister have become ungodly (i.e. they have accepted Islam).\"" So Sayyiduna Umar (R.A.) came to them both", and there was an emigrant person sitting next to them, whose name was Habab. These people were reciting Surah Al-Fatiha," then Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""Give me this book that you have"," so that I may read it.\"" Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wanted to read this book"," but his sister told him: \""You are impure", only the pure can touch it," and bathe it or perform ablution.\"" So Sayyiduna Umar rose up", he performed ablution, then he took this writing and recited Surah Fatiha. The narrator of this tradition, Qasim bin Uthman," is not authentic."""
442,"Alqamah narrates: Once we were on a journey with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him. So Sayyiduna Salman Farsi Radiyallahu Anhu said: \You ask me"," I have not touched the Qur'an.\"" Then they recited before us the verse that we wanted and at that time there was no water between us and them. All the narrators of this hadeeth are authentic and one party has disagreed with it."""
443,"Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were with Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, and when he came, I said: \O Abu Abdullah! It would be appropriate if you perform ablution"," so that we may inquire of you about some verses.\"" So Sayyiduna Salman Farsi Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""I am not touching the Qur'an"," it can only be touched by ablution people.\"" (The narrator narrates:) Then Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA) recited to us the verses that we wanted. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."""
444,"Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were traveling with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, then when he came, I said: \O Abu Abdullah! Perform ablution so that we may inquire from you about some verses of the Qur'an.\"" So he said: \""You ask me", I am not touching it," it can only be touched by ablution people.\"" Then we asked Sayyiduna Salman Farsi", may Allah be pleased with him, and he recited some verses to us before performing ablution. The text of this hadith is close," and all the evidence is authentically transmitted."""
445,This tradition along with some other isnads is narrated on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid about Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him).
446,"Regarding Alqamah and Aswad, it has been narrated about Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He recited a verse of the Qur'an while he was performing ablution. All these credentials are authentic."
447,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about semen on clothes, and he said: \It is like mucus and saliva. That will be enough for you. Clean it with a piece of cloth or grass.\"" Only the narrator Ishaq has narrated this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" tradition."""
448,It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about semen on clothes: He said: \It is like phlegm and saliva," you clean it with grass.\"""""
449,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I used to scrape semen from the clothes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it was dry, and if it was wet, I would wash it off."
450,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: If I saw a stain (of semen) on the clothes of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to wash them. This tradition is authentic."
451,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When semen got on the Prophet's clothes, he would wash them and go to pray, while she used to see the traces of washing on his clothes."
452,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to think: \Clothes do not have Janabat, the land does not have Janabat," and no one does not give Janabat to another person.\"" This tradition is not proven", the narrator of this tradition, a woman named Umm Qalus," is not recognized as authentic."""
453,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Janabat and he intended to sleep, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, but if he intended to eat something in that state, he would wash both his palms and eat. This tradition is authentic."
454,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of janabat, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something (in the state of janabat), he would wash both hands and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
455,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of Janabat, he would perform ablution before going to sleep, like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something while he was in the state of Janabat, he would wash both his hands and rinse them and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
456,Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) narrated to me: \Some people say: Ghusl is required due to ejaculation (although in reality) it was a leave given by the Prophet (PBUH) in the early days of Islam," after which he (PBUH) ordered us to bathe.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
457,"Al-Zuhri narrates: I asked Urwa about a man who has intercourse, but does not ejaculate, and Urwa replied: \The opinion of the people is this", they adopt the last commandment of the Prophet," may God's prayers and peace be upon him.\"" Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) told me: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same thing and not perform ghusl", but this was before the conquest of Makkah. After that," he started performing ghusl and instructed people to perform ghusl (in such a situation).\"""""
458,"Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to me. I was drawing water from a bucket by the side of a well at that time. He said: \O Ammar! What are you doing?\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed to you! I want to wash off the phlegm on my clothes.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""O Ammar! Clothes are washed for five reasons: feces", urine, vomit, blood or semen. O Ammar! Your phlegm," your tears and the water in your bladder are the same.\"" This hadith has only been narrated by Thabit ibn Hamad and it is very weak. The two narrators of this tradition", Ibrahim and Thabit," are weak."""
459,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Beware of urine," because the punishment in the grave is usually due to it.\"" This tradition is more secure as being \""transcendent\""."""
460,"Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no harm in the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"" The narrator of this tradition is weak."""
461,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \There is nothing wrong with the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"" This tradition is not authentically proven. Some of its narrators are weak and one narrator is obsolete. According to a saying", this thing was narrated from the Prophet," peace and blessings be upon him: \""There is nothing wrong with the fat of the animal whose meat is eaten.\"""""
462,"Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is nothing wrong with the fat of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"""""
463,"Abdullah bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father: \There is no harm in the sight of the animal whose flesh is eaten.\"""""
464,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Beware of urine," because the punishment in the grave is usually due to it.\"" More accurately"," tradition is \""transmitted\""."""
465,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Often the punishment of the grave is due to urine.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
466,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this as a \Marfu'\"" tradition: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \""The punishment of the grave is due to urine"," so you people should avoid urine.\"" There is no problem in the authenticity of this tradition."""
467,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) urinated on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I picked him up hard. In one hadith are the words: He said: \Leave it alone! For it does not eat"," nor does it urinate.\"""""
468,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about the urine of a milk-drinking child: \Water should be poured over the child's urine," and the girl's urine should be washed.\"" A narrator named Qatadah has made this clear: \""It is until the two of them do not eat", if they start eating," both of them will be washed.\"""""
469,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Water will be sprinkled on the urine of a boy and the urine of a girl will be washed.\"""""
470,Narrated Qatadah: \It is when they are not eating, if they start eating," the urine of both of them will be washed away.\"""""
471,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the urine of a minor child got on the blessed body of the Prophet (PBUH) or on his skin, he sprinkled water on the place where the urine had got on."
472,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says this about the child's urine: \Water should be sprinkled on the part on which it is applied.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) did the same thing when Imam Hussain bin Ali (RA) got urine. The narrator of this tradition is Ibrahim", the son of Abu Yahya," and it is weak."""
473,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to come to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and go to sleep. This tradition is authentic.
474,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates: I saw the Companions of the Holy Prophet (SAW) who used to get up to pray, and sometimes I even heard one of them snoring, but they would get up and pray again and not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mubarak has stated this: \For us"," this order is when these people used to sleep while sitting.\"" This hadith is authentic."""
475,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) used to wait for the call to prayer until Isha, until their heads were bowed down (i.e. they fell asleep), then they would get up and perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. This tradition is authentically transmitted."
476,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Some people from the ``Arina tribe came to Madinah to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The climate there did not suit them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \If you people want"," go to the charity camels and drink their milk and urine there.\"" They did so and they recovered", then they went to the herdsman of those camels and killed him and took the camels of the Prophet with them and left Islam and became apostates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent people after him. When they were caught," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off their hands and feet and put stitches in their eyes and then threw them on the rocky ground until they died in that state."""
477,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once a villager came, he urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the place be dug up, and then a bucket of water be poured over it. The villager said: \O Messenger of Allah! A person loves some people"," although he does not act like their actions.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""He will be with whomever he loves.\"" A narrator of this tradition is Samaan Majhool."""
478,"Sayyiduna Abdullah narrates: Once a villager attended the Prophet's service, he was an old man, he said: \O Sayyidna Muhammad! When will the Hour come?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""What have you prepared for this?\"" He replied: \""By Him Who sent you with the truth", I have not prepared for him any more prayers or fasts," but I love Allah and His Messenger.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""You will be with the one you love.\"" The narrator narrates: Then that old man went and wanted to urinate in the mosque", some people passed by him and stopped him," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Let him do it! Maybe"," it will be Paradise.\"" Then they poured water on his urine."""
479,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Muaqal (RA) narrates: Once a villager stood on the edge of the mosque, he removed his apron and urinated there, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Take out the dirt from the place where he urinated and throw water on that place.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Muaqal al-Tabi and this hadith is \""Mursal\""."""
480,Sayyidna Safwan bin Asal narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission for a traveler to wipe his socks for three days. However, the order of Janabat is different (so this order is only about) defecating," urinating or defecating (i.e. after that a person can wipe his socks during ablution).\"" There is only one tradition in which there is a command to expel the wind."""
481,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who sees tari but does not remember Ihtlam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who remembers this. Sayyidah Umm Salim Radiyallahu Anha said: \If a woman sees this thing? Will this ruling be required for her as well?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Yes! Women are the aspect of men.\"""""
482,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) saying: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Ghusl is required in five cases: after Janabat, Ghusl on Friday, after bathing the dead," after bathing in the water of Hammam.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Musab bin Shuba"," weak."""
483,"Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: Once he was sitting with the Prophet (PBUH), while a man came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he said: \O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about such a person? Who approaches a woman who is not lawful for him and what men do to women", he does to her everything," but he does not have intercourse with her.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Perform ablution well"," then get up and pray.\"" The narrator narrates: So Allah revealed this verse: \""Establish prayer in both parts of the day and also in part of the night.\"" Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) inquired: \""Is this ruling specific to this person or is it specific to all Muslims?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""This is common to all Muslims.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
484,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: \A prayer will not be repeated because of kissing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. In the proof of this tradition"," the narrator named Mansoor bin Dazan has narrated something like this."""
485,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet of Allah used to kiss me, then he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) would go to pray and not perform ablution again."
486,"This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions, in one of which there are these words: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss while fasting. Imam Malik has quoted this saying of Imam Zuhri: \After kissing"," ablution becomes obligatory.\"" So if the hadith narrated from Sayyida Aisha (RA) regarding Zuhri is accepted as correct", then Zuhri should not have issued a fatwa against him," Allah knows best!"""
487,"Imam Malik narrates this statement of Ibn Shihab Zuhri, who says: \If a husband kisses his wife"," it is obligatory to perform ablution on her.\"""""
488,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah used to kiss one of his wives, then he (may God bless him and grant him peace) would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. (After narrating this) Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while he was fasting."
489,"It has been narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa: She came to know a saying of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, that ablution is necessary after kissing, so Sayida Aisha said: \The Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him, used to kiss while fasting," and he did not perform ablution again.\"""""
490,"There are these words in a hadith: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"""""
491,"Urwa bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A gentleman has narrated this: Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) was asked about a person who kisses his wife after performing ablution, so Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her) said: \The Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," used to kiss one of his wives and not perform ablution again.\"" He says: I said to Sayyida Aisha: \""If that is the case"," then that wife will be you.\"" The narrator narrates: So Sayyida Aisha remained silent."""
492,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me and then pray and not perform ablution again. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ghalib ibn Ubaidullah, and it is obsolete."
493,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and then pray and not perform ablution again.
494,"Ata states: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is correct."""
495,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then go to pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Urwa narrates: I said to Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may God be pleased with her: \Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then pray and not perform ablution again. (The narrator says:) So I said: \""Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""
496,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast and perform ablution before praying, then if any of his wives came in front of him, he would kiss her and then perform the prayer (i.e. he would not perform ablution again). Narrated Urwa: I said to him: \Who else can she be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""
497,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, then kiss his wife, and then pray and would not perform ablution again. Both of them have the same word."
498,"This tradition is also narrated along with another document. Sufyan Al-Thawri, who has the most knowledge about this, says: The narrator named Habib has not heard hadiths from Urwa."
499,"Narrated ``Urwah: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) used to pray, even though drops of blood were falling on the mat. Similarly, with regard to kissing, the narrator named Yahya has described: \Describe it from me.\"" The status of both of them is the same"," as if there is nothing wrong with them."""
500,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution and after performing ablution he would kiss (his wife) and then pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Waqiyyah has stated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mahdi has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her (his wife) and not perform ablution again. Narrated Abu Asim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) and then pray and not perform ablution again. The same hadith has been narrated along with some other traditions, but there is some difference in its traditions. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and not perform ablution again, Allah knows best!"
501,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and would not perform ablution again. (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) You used to pray."
502,It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and then pray.
503,"Ms. Sayyida Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to perform ablution for prayer and then kiss (his wife) and not perform ablution again."
504,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss her while he was fasting. Uthman bin Abu Sha'ba has narrated in the same way.
505,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of Sayyidah Zaynab: He asked Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) about a person who kisses his wife and touches her. So Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) replied: \Sometimes the Prophet (PBUH) would perform ablution and then kiss me and then go back and pray and would not perform ablution again.\"" The narrator of this tradition is an anonymous narrator named Zainab and such a tradition cannot be presented as evidence."""
506,"Amr Ibn Shuaib narrates this on the authority of Sayyidah Zaynab: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) used to kiss her and then pray and not perform ablution again. According to Ata, kissing does not require ablution."
507,This tradition is also narrated along with another document.
508,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss one of his wives and then not perform ablution again. Here the narrator's statement that this hadith is narrated from Abdullah bin Ghalib is an illusion. What they meant was: It was narrated from Ghalib bin Ubaidullah, and this narrator is obsolete."
509,"Ata is convinced: \Kissing does not require ablution.\"""""
510,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) while he was fasting, then after that he would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. It is flawed in several respects."
511,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): According to him, kissing does not make ablution necessary."
512,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
513,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with him), she says: Once at night I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the bed. I am, only You can be helped in Your presence and I cannot praise You and I cannot describe Your praise, Your praise is the same as You yourself have described Your own praise. There are some differences in the authenticity of this tradition."
514,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat (in the cold season) and I had not yet done Ghusl Janabat.
515,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on my bed, so I got up. I thought that he had gone to visit his maidservant Maria. They were praying in the state of: \O Allah! I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment", I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure, and I seek Your refuge in Your presence. I cannot express Your praise," so it is as if You yourself have expressed Your praise.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition is Faraj bin Fazala"," weak. Some other narrators have disagreed with its transmission and narrate this tradition as a \""Mursal\"" hadith."""
516,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: \Whoever kisses his wife while she is in a state of ablution," then he should perform ablution again.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
517,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \Kissing is part of touching (which is mentioned in the Qur'an)," so do ablution after it.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
518,"Salim narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): He said this about a man kissing and touching his wife with his hand: \This is part of malamast", so if a person kisses his wife and touches her with his hand," ablution becomes obligatory on him.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
519,Salim narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He used to think: \Kissing is part of Lams (touching," which is mentioned in the Qur'an).\"" And Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered to perform ablution in this regard."""
520,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said this about kissing: \It makes ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
521,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: \Kissing is a part of 'touching'.\"""""
522,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
523,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of touch and it becomes necessary to perform ablution on it.\"" Ibn 'Arafah and the narrator Ma'ali have added this: \""Touch is something other than intercourse.\"" And this is authentic."""
524,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""
525,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""
526,The same hadith has been narrated in the same way along with some other traditions.
527,"Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: \When a person touches his private parts"," he should not pray until he performs ablution.\"" The narrator narrates: Urwa denied this", so he inquired from Basra about it, and Basra confirmed what he had said. This is authentic. Some other narrators have adapted it," in which it is also mentioned: Arwa says: \""I asked Basra about this: so he confirmed it.\"""""
528,"Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution like the ablution of prayer.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
529,"Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: \When a person touches his private parts"," he should perform ablution in the form of prayer.\"""""
530,"Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution again.\"""""
531,"Nafi', narrates the saying of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever touches his private parts"," he should perform ablution like the ablution of prayer.\"""""
532,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person moves his hand towards his private area, even if there is no hijab (cloth) between his hand and his private area," then that person performs ablution like the ablution of prayer (i.e. it becomes necessary to perform ablution on him).\"""""
533,"Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When a man touches his private parts", he should perform ablution, and when a woman touches her private parts," she should perform ablution.\"""""
534,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: \Whoever touches his private parts", he should perform ablution, and whoever touches her private parts," he should perform ablution.\"""""
535,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is ruin for those who touch their private parts and offer prayers without performing ablution.\"" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""May my parents be sacrificed to you! This ruling is for men"," what is your opinion about women?\"" So the Prophet", peace be upon him," said: \""When a woman touches her private parts"," she should perform ablution for prayer.\"" The pure narrator of this tradition is Abd al-Rahman Umari"," weak."""
536,"Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever touches his private parts or touches his testicles and touches his pubic area should perform ablution.\"" This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions", however, the narrator is delusional in mentioning the testicles and the smelly place," because this thing is not mentioned in the tradition narrated from Sayyidah Basrah. More secure is this: This is the saying of Arwa and it is transmitted as a \""marfu'\"" hadith"," the authentic narrators have narrated it in the same way."""
537,Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Whoever touches his private parts," he should perform ablution.\"" The narrators narrate: Arwah narrates: \""Whoever touches his genital area or his testicles or touches his private parts should perform ablution.\"" These words are narrated by a narrator named Abu Ash-Sha'at"," and this tradition is \""authentic\""."""
538,Hisham bin Arwah narrates: My father used to say: \When a person touches his private parts or his testicles or his private parts," he should not pray until he performs ablution.\"" All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."""
539,"Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the honor of being the companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person touches his private parts or his testicles"," he should not pray until he performs ablution.\"""""
540,"Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this statement of his father: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). At that time, people were busy building the mosque of Medina. Narrator narrates: People were moving stones at that time. The narrator narrates: I said, \O Messenger of Allah! Shall I not do the same as these people are moving (stones)?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""No! Rather", you turn them into slurry, O people of Yamama!," because you are expert in this.\"" The narrator narrates: I made them and they began to carry them away."""
541,"Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement from his father: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he asked him about touching the private parts. A narrator named Ibn Abi Hatim narrates: I asked my father (Abu Hatim) and Sayyiduna Abu Shaykh Zarrah Razi about this tradition narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Jabir, and they both replied: \The narrator named Qays bin Talaq is not one to be accepted as authentic.\"" So these two gentlemen showed this narrator to be weak and did not declare him as authentic."""
542,"Abu Uthman Nahdi narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) narrated this. It is narrated in a hadith: A narrator named Asma bin Malik Hatami, who was a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated this: A person said: \O Messenger of Allah! I got an itch during the prayer. When I itched"," my hand touched my private part.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""(Sometimes) I also do this.\"""""
543,"Qays bin Talaq narrates the statement of his father Sayyiduna Talq bin Ali (RA): We set out in a delegation to attend the presence of the Prophet (PBUH), when we entered his presence, we pledged allegiance to him and prayed in his lead. Have an opinion?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \He is a piece of your body.\"" (The narrator doubts"," perhaps these are the words:) \""There is a piece of meat.\"""""
544,"Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this on the authority of his father: We asked the Prophet (PBUH) about touching the private parts, and he (PBUH) said: “It is a part of your body.” The narrator of this tradition is Ayyub, unknown."
545,"A Muhaddith named Raja bin Marji narrates: Once we gathered in the mosque of Khaif, among whom were Ahmad bin Hanbal, Ali bin Madini and Yahya bin Mu'in, and a discussion broke out between them about touching the private parts, and Yahya said: \After this"," ablution will be performed.\"" Ali bin Madini expressed his opinion according to the opinion of the people of Kufa and imitated their opinion. Yahya bin Mu'in quoted the hadith of Basrah bint Safwan in support of his position"," while Ali bin Madini quoted the hadith of Qays bin Talq in support of his position. He said to Yahya: \""How can you follow the authority of Basra? While Marwan (who was the governor of Madinah)", he sent a soldier," until that soldier came to Marwan with the woman's answer.\"" So Yahya said: \""Many people have criticized Qays bin Talaq and have not declared his tradition to be authentic.\"" So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said: \""What you both described"," the incident is like this.\"" Yahya al-Mahdi", on the authority of Imam Malik, narrates the following about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him," says: \""It is not necessary to perform ablution after this"," it is a part of your body.\"" So Yahya inquired: \""Who has copied this?\"" So he replied: \""This is what Sufyan narrated on the authority of Abu Qais on the authority of Hazeel"," on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him).\"" So whenever the opinions of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masood (RA) and Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) differ on a matter", then Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masood is more deserving of being followed. So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said to them," \""It is so.\"" But the narration of the narrator Abu Qais cannot be presented as an argument. So he said: \""Abu Na'im has narrated this statement of Sayyidina Ammar bin Yasir", may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Mu'mar," regarding Umayr.\"" He says: \""I do not care whether I touch it (the private part) or touch my nose.\"" So Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said: \""Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) are both of the same generation"," so whoever wants to adopt their opinion and whoever wants to adopt their opinion.\"""""
546,"Shaqiq narrates: Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: \I do not care if I touch my private parts or touch my nose while I am in the state of prayer.\"""""
547,"Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \I do not care whether I touch my private part or touch my ear during prayer.\"""""
548,"Ubaidullah narrates: Sayyiduna Umar was asked about touching the armpit, and he said: \Wudhu will be performed after that.\"""""
549,"It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""
550,"It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""
551,Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu says: \When a person touches his armpit," he should perform ablution.\"""""
552,"Hammad bin Zayd has stated this: When Ayub was mentioned about touching the armpits, he said: \Some armpits are like that"," one should perform ghusl after touching them.\"""""
553,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Wudhu must be performed on what comes out," but what enters inside does not need to be performed.\"""""
554,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his back on and prayed and did not perform ablution again, he only washed the part where he put his back on. Ibn Abu Ashreen narrates this tradition as a \marfu'\"" hadith"," while a narrator named Abu Mughira narrates it as \""suspended\"" on the authority of Uza'i"," and this is correct."""
555,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution (washing his face), he would touch his cheeks and stroke his beard downwards with his fingers."
556,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): When he performed ablution, he would touch his two cheeks and sometimes stroke his beard with his fingers, and sometimes leave it off. This tradition is \suspended\"" and rightly so."""
557,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he gently touched his cheeks and stroked his beard with his fingers."
558,"Qatadah and Yazid al-Raqashi have narrated this: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
559,"Ismail bin Muhammad al-Safar narrated to us that Ibrahim bin Hani narrated to us, he said that Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, he said that Uza’i narrated to us, he said that Abdul Wahid bin Qays narrated to us, he said that Yazid al-Raqashi narrated this hadith from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if this hadith is “Mursal” (meaning the middle narrator is missing), then it is also authentic."
560,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \When a person has a hemorrhage during his prayer, he should go back," wash off the blood and perform ablution again and pray anew.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Arqam"," obsolete."""
561,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \The water of the sea is the ablution water of the angels. When they descend, they perform ablution with it, and when they ascend," they perform ablution with it.\"""""
562,Sayyiduna Ali bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person passes out during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution again," and pray again.\"""""
563,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person vomits or belches bitterly during prayer, he should go back, perform ablution," and start reciting more than what he had already prayed. This is when he has not said anything in between.\"" A narrator named Ibn Juraj has narrated this"," \""If he speaks"," he will pray anew.\"""""
564,"Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When a person vomits or belches sourly during prayer", he should go back, perform ablution, and perform his prayer from the same place (from where he left it)," this is when he has not spoken.\"" Ibn Jaraj narrates."""
565,This hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa.
566,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
567,Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever belches or vomits or has a hemorrhage (and this happens during prayer), then he should go back, perform ablution again," and complete his prayer.\"""""
568,This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa.
569,"This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) along with another chain of transmission. The same tradition is also transmitted as \Mursal\"" along with another document."""
570,"Ibn Juraj narrates this on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person bleeds or vomits during prayer", he should go back, perform ablution, and return and continue the prayer from where he left it," (this ruling is until) he has finished speaking.\"""""
571,"Ibn Jaraj has narrated a similar tradition on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikah, on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha, and on the authority of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
572,"Ibn Jurayj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \When a person vomits during prayer", or belches sourly, or passes wind, then he should go back, perform ablution, and return and start his prayer from the place (from where he left it)," this is when he has not uttered a word.\"" A narrator named Abu Bakr has stated this: It is correct to transmit it from Ibn Jaraj as a \""Mursal\"" tradition", however, a narrator Ismail bin Ayyash has narrated it on the authority of Ibn Jarij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikah on the authority of Sayyida Aisha," there is no truth to it."""
573,"Ibn Jaraj, in reference to his father, quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: \Whoever has a hemorrhage", vomits, or belches, then he should perform ablution and perform ablution as much as he had prayed, then complete the remaining prayer," and he should refrain from speaking to anyone.\"""""
574,"Imam Zayd bin Ali narrates this statement of his grandfather, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Sour belching or (vomiting) breaks ablution.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Sawar", it is obsolete," and no one else has narrated this tradition with reference to Sayyiduna Zayd."""
575,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \When a person feels a rumbling in his stomach, vomits, or has a hemorrhage, he should go back (perform ablution) and return to pray from where he left," this is when he has not spoken to anyone.\"""""
576,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \When a person is leading the people in prayer and feels a rumbling in his stomach or he has a hemorrhage or vomits," he should put a cloth over his nose and hold the hand of one of the people present and lead him forward.\"""""
577,"Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet saw me, blood was flowing from my nose, so he said: \Perform ablution again.\"" A narrator named Mahamali has made this clear: \""It means you perform ablution"," because ablution has been broken.\"""""
578,"This same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: \His haemorrhage broke out"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should perform ablution again because of this.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Amr Qureshi", Amr bin Khalid, Abu Khalid Wasti," which is a lost hadith. Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and Yahya bin Mu'in have stated this: \""Abu Khalid Wasti is a liar.\"""""
579,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: If the Prophet (PBUH) had a haemorrhage during the prayer, he (PBUH) would perform ablution and perform the remaining prayer. The narrator of this tradition is ``Amr bin Riyah, obsolete."
580,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed the prayer after ablution and did not perform ablution again. The Prophet (PBUH) only washed the place where he had put his heels.
581,"Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Wudhu becomes necessary after every bleeding.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Sayyidna Umar bin Abdul Aziz, did not listen to the hadiths from Tamim Dari and did not visit them, while the two narrators of this tradition, Yazid bin Khalid, Yazid bin Muhammad," are both unknown."""
582,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \It is not necessary to perform ablution if one or two drops of blood appear"," but it is necessary every time the blood flows.\"""""
583,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \A drop or two drops of blood does not make ablution obligatory," until the blood starts to flow (it is not obligatory until then).\"" The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Fazl bin Utbah", weak," and Sufyan bin Zia and Hajjaj bin ??? are also weak."""
584,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever has a hemorrhage during prayer," he should perform ablution and (perform the prayer from where he left it).\"" The narrator of this tradition is Abu Bakr Dahiri", Abdullah bin Hakim," the abandoned hadith."""
585,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever breaks his ablution, if he is in the state of prayer, he should put his hand over his nose and go back," so that it is evident that his hemorrhage has broken out.\"""""
586,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person breaks his ablution during prayer, he should hold his nose," then go back.\"""""
587,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: \When a person breaks his ablution during prayer," then he should hold his nose and then go back.\"""""
588,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has permitted the blood of boils and abscesses (it does not require ablution).
589,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever breaks his ablution during prayer should hold his nose and then go back and perform ablution.\"""""
590,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) ended his fast by saying this. The narrator narrates: Later, I met Sayyidna Thawban (RA) in the Jamia Masjid of Damascus, I mentioned this to him, and he said (Abu Dardaa said the truth) that I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH)."
591,"A narrator named Saad narrated: Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrated this hadith to him, then he narrated a similar hadith from the Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (RA) and on the authority of Sayyidna Thawban (RA)."
592,"Ma'dan bin Abu Talha narrates this: Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) told him, after that he mentioned the previous hadeeth, in which it is mentioned: (Sayyidna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \I performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).\"""""
593,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which there are these words: Sayyidna Thawban (RA) said: \He has said the truth"," I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH).\"""""
594,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said: \O Messenger of Allah! Whenever I perform ablution (blood) starts flowing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When you perform ablution", if it continues to flow from your top to your feet," then it is not necessary to perform ablution on you.\"" Ramwi named Abdullah bin Malik", this is weak," this tradition is not authentic."""
595,"Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting. It was something other than Ramadan. He suffered something that tormented him, which caused him to vomit. Then he vomited. Then he called me for ablution and performed ablution and ended the fast. I said: \O Messenger of Allah! Is it obligatory to perform ablution after vomiting?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""If this was a duty"," you would have received its command.\"" The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had fasted the next day"," so I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \""This is the judgment of my breaking the fast of the previous day.\"" This hadith has been narrated only by Atiya bin Sakin with reference to Uza'i"," a person who rejects the hadith."""
596,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) fell asleep, he was in a state of prostration at that time, until he started snoring, then he stood up and prayed. I said: \O Messenger of Allah! You were asleep.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Wudhu is obligatory on a person who sleeps lying down", because when he sleeps lying down," his joints become loose.\"" A narrator named Abu Khalid is unique in quoting this tradition with reference to Abu Qatada. This tradition is not reliable."""
597,Sayyiduna Mu'awiya bin Abu Sufyan (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The eye is the closure of the anus, so when the eye falls asleep," this closure is broken.\"""""
598,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
599,"Sayyidna Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Whoever sleeps while sitting", it is not necessary to perform ablution on him, but whoever puts his side (on the ground)," it is necessary to perform ablution on him.\"""""
600,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \The eye is a blockage of the anus. Whoever sleeps," he should perform ablution well.\"""""
601,"Abu Malih narrates this on the authority of his father: Once we were praying in the company of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and a man who was blind came, and we laughed when he fell into the pit, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered us to perform complete ablution again and pray anew. The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which both Hasan bin Dinar and Hasan bin Amara are weak narrators, they have made a mistake in its chain of transmission. Hasan al-Basri has narrated this tradition on the authority of Hafsa bint Salman, on the authority of Abul Aaliya. Hasan often cites the \Messenger\"" tradition with reference to the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him). Even Hasan bin Amara has related this tradition", he has narrated this with reference to Khalid with reference to Abu Walid, with reference to his father, so this is a very ugly illusion. This tradition was narrated by Khalid on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin and Abul Aaliya from the Prophet. Sufyan al-Thawri, Hamad bin Salamah and other narrators have also narrated it in the same way. A narrator named Ibn Ishaq has quoted in his tradition with difficulty regarding transmission from Hasan bin Dinar, sometimes quoting him on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Abul Malih, on the authority of his father. Qatadah has quoted this tradition from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a “Messenger” tradition with reference to Abul Aaliyah. It has been narrated on the authority of Saad bin Abu Arooba, Muammar, Abu Awanah, Saad bin Bashir, and other narrators have narrated it on the authority of them," after that we will mention the hadith of these gentlemen."""
602,"Abul Malih narrates on the authority of his father: We were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while a blind man came and fell into the pit, that is, the well in the mosque, so some people behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, laughed. The narrator of this hadith is Hasan bin Dinar, the abandoned hadith. This tradition has also been narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Amr, this narrator is also an abandoned hadith, he has narrated this tradition on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abul Aaliya, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of a narrator named Salam."
603,"Narrated Anas bin Malik: A blind person fell into a well, some people behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah has narrated this: It was narrated on the authority of Anas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was leading the people in prayer, while a blind man entered the mosque, he fell into a well, some people laughed behind the Prophet (PBUH). A narrator named Ibn Mukhlid and Sayyiduna Anas (may God be pleased with him) narrated this on the authority of Abul Aaliyah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer. There was a well in the middle of the mosque. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah narrates: This hadith is rejected. Shaykh Abul Hasan says: This hadith has been narrated from a narrator named Salam by a narrator named Abd al-Rahman, this person is a muratuk who compiles hadiths. This tradition has been narrated by Dawud bin Muhibr, this person is also obsolete, who compiles hadiths, he has narrated this tradition from Ayyub's father, who is weak, he has narrated it from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Qatadah."
604,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading us in prayer, while a blind man came, he fell into a pit and started crying. This is the correct statement of the person who narrated it as a \Mursal\"" hadith on the authority of Qatadah"," on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."""
605,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: A blind man fell into a well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer. Some of those who were praying under the guidance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at this, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again."
606,"Abul Aaliyah narrates this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer, while a man fell into the well, some of the people present laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed again to perform ablution and pray."
607,This hadith has been narrated on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah.
608,"This hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abul Aliya along with another chain of transmission."
609,This tradition is narrated from Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission.
610,
611,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \When a person laughs (during the prayer)," he should perform ablution again and perform the prayer again.\"""""
612,Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Whoever laughs during the prayer," then he should perform ablution again and perform the prayer.\"" A narrator named Hasan has stated this: \""Whoever laughs"," he will repeat ablution and pray.\"" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Sufyan"," who is weak and his status in the knowledge of hadith is very bad. This tradition along with another chain of transmission is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas bin Malik."""
613,"Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us—and the most favorable assessment of Sufyan ibn Muhammad is that he erred in this hadith—on the authority of Ibn Wahb, if he did not deliberately fabricate it in his statement ""from al-Hasan, from Anas."" For others have narrated it from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan, as a mursal (interrupted chain) from the Prophet ﷺ. Among them: Khalid ibn Khidash al-Muhallabi, Mawhib ibn Yazid, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb. And others did not mention Anas ibn Malik in their hadith from Ibn Wahb in the chain, nor did they mention Sulayman ibn Arqam between al-Zuhri and al-Hasan, even though he was al-Zuhri's nephew. And Ibn Abi Atiq narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ. These are four opinions from al-Hasan, all of them invalid; because al-Hasan only heard this hadith from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ."
614,"Sayyiduna Hasan Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a man with weak eyesight came, (the narrator suspects) that he was blind, he fell into the well, some people laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution. The narrator narrates: I mentioned this tradition to Hafs bin Salman, so he said: \I narrated this tradition to Hasan al-Basri with reference to Hafsa (daughter of Sirin)", and it is correct," this tradition is transmitted from Hasan al-Basri as a \""Mursal\"" tradition.\"""""
615,"Abu Ali Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us (L12530), Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi (L12383) narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini (L5792) narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi (L4493) said to me: ""This hadith revolves around Abu al-Aliyah."" So I said: ""Al-Hasan has narrated it mursalan (without mentioning the Companion)."" He said: ""Hammad ibn Zayd (L2491) narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, he said: 'I narrated it to Al-Hasan, from Hafsah, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Then Ibrahim has narrated it mursalan."" Abd al-Rahman said: ""Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Hashim, he said: 'I narrated it to Ibrahim, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Al-Zuhri has narrated it mursalan."" He said: ""I read it in the book of Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Al-Hasan."""
616,Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to repeat the prayer and perform ablution again.
617,"Hasan narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a person came and fell into a well."
618,"Hasan al-Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a person came and fell into the well."
619,Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to perform ablution again and perform the prayer again.
620,"Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, after that, according to the previous hadith."
621,"Zahri said: Laughing or laughing (during the prayer) does not break Wudhu. What Zahri has quoted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Hasan, if it was correct according to Zahri, he would not have issued a fatwa against it and contrary to it, Allah knows best!"
622,"Ma'bad narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a blind man came, who fell into the pit, and some people laughed, until they laughed. When he finished the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever among you laughed"," let him perform ablution and perform the prayer again.\"""""
623,"Al-Mabadi Jahani narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the morning prayer, while a blind man came, near the place of the Prophet’s prayer, there was a well, on which a bucket was placed. It has been fixed, he should perform ablution (again) and perform the prayer again."
624,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying. A man with poor eyesight came, passed by a well (pit) with a log lying on it, and fell into the pit. Some of those who were praying behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer and said: \He who laughed among you should perform ablution again and perform the prayer.\"" These words are from a narrator named Ziyad bin Ayyub."""
625,"Ibn Sirin narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the Companions in prayer, after that the hadith was narrated as before, but he narrated these words: When that person fell into the pit, some people laughed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave this order, after that the hadith was narrated as before. This tradition is authentic, which is narrated on the authority of Khalid on the authority of Hafsa on the authority of Abul Aaliyah. A muhaddith called Hasan says: It is narrated on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abul Malih, on the authority of his father, this is a very clear mistake. The same tradition has been narrated by some other narrators on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
626,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, while a person came who had poor eyesight and fell into a pit. The people laughed at him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered: Those who laughed should perform ablution again and pray."
627,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
628,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer, while a man came, he placed his foot on the basket, which was placed at the head of the well, and fell into the well. Then the people behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered some of those who laughed: They should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
629,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer. There was a blind person among those present, who fell into the well. Some of the companions laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered the prayer and ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
630,"This same hadith is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
631,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his Companions in prayer. Meanwhile, a man with weak eyesight passed by a pit, on which something was placed, and he fell into the pit. The same tradition is narrated from another hadith."
632,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person came who fell into the pit, and some of the people present laughed. This tradition is transmitted along with other evidences."
633,"Abul Aaliyah narrates on the authority of an Ansari: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person with poor eyesight came and fell into the pit."
634,Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution.
635,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person came who had weak eyesight, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he fell into the pit that was in the mosque, so some people laughed."
636,This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission.
637,This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission.
638,Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed.
639,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in the Fajr prayer or in the evening prayer. There was a pit in the mosque. A person with poor eyesight fell into the pit and some people laughed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and asked the people the reason for laughing, and they told him the reason."
640,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: Some of those who were praying in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) laughed, so the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: The person who laughed should perform ablution and pray again."
641,Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed.
642,"Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, there was a hole in the mosque, a person who was blind came and some people laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, those who laughed should perform ablution again and perform the prayer."
643,"Ibrahim narrates: A blind man came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at that time, he slipped and fell into the pit, so the people laughed."
644,"This hadith has been narrated as a \Mursal\"" tradition with reference to Ibrahim", while in another chain of transmission, it has been chained with reference to Ibrahim, in reference to Abul Alia, while the same chain of transmission has been chained with reference to some other chain of traditions. Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who was more familiar with Abul Aaliyah and Hasan al-Basri," used to say: Do not accept the \""Mursal\"" tradition narrated by Abul Aaliyah"," because both of them do not care from whom they have taken it."""
645,"Asim narrates: Ibn Sirin said to me: Recite the hadith you have to recite! But do not narrate any hadith to me regarding two men from Basra: Abul Aaliyah and Hasan, because these two do not care who they get their hadith from."
646,"Muhammad bin Sirin says: There are four people who authenticate everyone who narrates their hadith and they do not care from whom they have taken the hadith. Hasan Basri, Abul Aliya, Hameed bin Hilal, Dawood bin Abu Hind. This tradition is narrated by Jabir on the authority of Amish, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, he has mentioned this hadith and also mentioned its cause."
647,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us: He who laughs during the prayer should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. Shaykh Abu Bakr Neshapuri says: This Hadith is rejected and not authentic. It is authentically narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir to the contrary.
648,Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary.
649,Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary.
650,"Sufyan narrates: Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a person who laughs during the prayer, (so he said:) He will perform the prayer again, but ablution will not be required for him."
651,"Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, he will perform the prayer again, but ablution is not required on him."
652,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If a person laughs during the prayer, he should repeat the prayer, but it is not necessary to perform ablution on him."
653,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He was asked about laughing during the prayer, and he said: That person will perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary for him to perform ablution."
654,"A narrator named Abu Sufyan has narrated this, Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu has said this about the one who laughs during the prayer, that person should perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary to perform ablution again. This tradition is narrated from Sha'bi along with another chain of transmission."
655,A narrator named Abu Sufyan narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: A person who laughs during prayer does not require ablution. This tradition is narrated along with another document.
656,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary.
657,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary (i.e. does not break ablution).
658,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “Laughter breaks the prayer, but it does not break the ablution.”"
659,"There is another hadith to the contrary, narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Talking (during prayer) breaks the prayer"," but does not break the ablution.\"""""
660,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that, according to him, laughing during prayer does not make ablution necessary."
661,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Smiling does not break the prayer," unless a person laughs (the prayer does not break).\"" This same hadith has been transmitted as a \""marfu'\"" hadith along with another chain of transmission."""
662,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, it is necessary to perform the prayer again."
663,"Hameed bin Hilal says: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) left with a delegation, in this delegation there was a blind man from the tribe of Abdul Qays. Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) was leading the prayer. Narrated Ahnaf: When I heard his voice saying that he had fallen into the well, everyone in the audience laughed except me and Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari. Sayyiduna Abu Musa completed the prayer and inquired: What happened to these people? These people said: So-and-so had fallen into the pit, so Sayyiduna Abu Musa ordered him to pray again."
664,"Hameed bin Hilal narrates: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) was teaching his companions to pray, those companions saw something that made them laugh, so Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, after finishing the prayer, said: Whoever among you laughed should perform the prayer again."
665,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (RA): He was leading the people in prayer, and the people saw something at which some people laughed at the example of Sayyidna Abu Musa. After completing the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: \Whoever laughed among you should perform the prayer again.\"""""
666,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching the Asr prayer to his companions. He smiled during the prayer. Have you smiled during prayer? The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Mikael passed by me," there was dust on his wings. He smiled at me and I smiled at him. He was returning after chasing a people (of the enemy).\"""""
667,"Sahl bin Mu'adh narrates on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \The one who laughs"," looks around and snaps his fingers during the prayer has the same status.\"""""
668,Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: A person who laughs during the prayer does not need to perform ablution on him. This order was for those who were performing the prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him).
669,Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The entire surface of the earth has been made a place for us to pray, and its soil has been made a source of purification for us," and our ranks have been made like the ranks of the angels.\"""""
670,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, which reads: \All the earth has been made for us a place of prayer and a means of purification when we cannot find water.\"""""
671,"Umayr, who was the slave of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Once, I and Abdullah bin Yasar, who is the slave of Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, both of us attended the service of Sayyidna Abu Jaham bin Harith Ansari, and Sayyidna Abu Jaham, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was coming from the well of Jamal. Aya, he greeted you, the Prophet did not respond to the greeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approached the wall, wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) and then greeted it."
672,Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. He met a man who was coming from the front.
673,"Sayyiduna Abu Jaham bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. A person greeted him from the front, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to the greeting, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his blessed hand on the wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he said: “Peace be upon you too.”"
674,"Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was coming to the well of the camel, perhaps after defecating or urinating. I greeted you, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to my greeting, then the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hand on the blessed wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to my greeting."
675,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Jaham (RA) about the Holy Prophet (PBUH).
676,"Narrated by Nafi: Once, I attended the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, in connection with some work of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visiting after defecating or urinating. This person greeted him, the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not respond to him, until the person was about to leave the street, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hands on the blessed wall and wiped his face, then turned again and wiped both his arms (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to his greeting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \I did not respond to you because I was not in a state of ablution.\"""""
677,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: Once the Prophet (PBUH) was coming home after defecating. A man came to him near the well of Jamal, he greeted him, the Prophet did not return his greeting until he came to the wall and wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) then returned the man's greeting."
678,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said this about Allah's commandment: \If you are sick or on a journey.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \""When a person gets a wound in the way of Allah", or has an abscess or scabies, then has Janabat or fears that he may die because of taking ghusl," such a person will perform Tayammum.\"""""
679,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \It is permissible for a sick person to perform tayammum through clay.\"""""
680,"Ata narrated this tradition as a marfu', hadith, up to the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, while other narrators narrated it as a muwaqf tradition."
681,"Sayyiduna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Once I had a fever in a winter night, it was a matter of Ghazwa Zaat-ul-Salsil, I was afraid that if I bathed, I would be killed, so I performed Tayammum and led the morning prayer to my companions. Later, when this was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he inquired: \O Amr! Did you lead your companions in prayer while you were in Janabat?\"" So I told you about the reason that prevented me from taking bath. I said: I heard Allah saying: \""Do not kill yourselves"," surely Allah is the Most Merciful to you.\"" So the Prophet (PBUH) smiled. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say anything to me."""
682,"Abu Qais, who is the slave of Sayyidna Amr bin As, narrates: Once Sayyidna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, went to a house. During this time they had to pack for the cold, it had never been so cold before. When he started to go for the morning prayer, he said: \By Allah! I had a cold last night. Such cold"," by Allah! I have never seen it.\"" Then he washed his legs (where there was a sign of Ithlam)", performed ablution for the prayer and led his companions in prayer. When he attended the Prophet's service," the Prophet asked his companions: \""How did you find Amr"," how was his company?\"" So he greatly praised Sayyiduna Amr (and also said): \""O Messenger of Allah! Once he taught us the prayer in the state of Janabat.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyidna Amr"," Sayyidna Amr told him about this situation and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace! Allah said: 'Do not kill yourself.' So the Holy Prophet (PBUH) smiled at Sayyiduna Amr's words."""
683,Rabi bin Badr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyiduna Asla said: \You show me how the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," taught you how to perform tayammum.\"" So they put their two palms together on the ground", then blew on them, then wiped their faces with them, even wiped their beards, then put both hands on the ground, wiped the ground with them, one of them joined the other. He wiped the outside and inside of his palm. In a hadith these words are: The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) taught me how to anoint? The narrator narrates: Then he placed both his palms on the ground, then raised them towards his face, then made a second stroke," then wiped the outer and inner parts of both hands until he wiped the elbows with his hands."""
684,Shaqiq narrates: Once I was sitting with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud and Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with them). Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: \O Abu Abd al-Rahman! What do you think if a person who becomes janib does not get water for a month," he will continue to perform tayammum during that time?\"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah said: \""He will not perform Tayammum"," even if he does not get water for a month.\"" So Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari said: \""Then what will you say about this verse? Which is present in Surah Al-Maida (God's guidance) 'then you do not find water"," then perform tayammum through pure soil'.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""If people are given permission in this regard", a time will soon come when they will find the water cold," so they will start doing tayammum with pure mud.\"" The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Musa asked him: \""You dislike him for this reason?\"" He replied: \""Yes.\"" So Sayyidna Abu Musa said to him: \""Didn't you hear what Ammar said to Sayyidna Umar?\"" (He narrated): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on some errand. I got sidetracked", I didn't get water. I collapsed into the mud like an animal. Then I attended the service of the Holy Prophet. When I mentioned this to him," the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""It was enough for you that you would wipe both hands on the ground with one of them and then wipe your face with both of them.\"" So Sayyidna Abdullah replied: \""You did not think about Sayyidna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu"," Sayyidna Umar was not satisfied with the statement of Sayyidna Ammar Radi Allahu Anhu.\"" The words of a narrator named Yusuf are: \""You wipe both your hands on the ground"," then wipe your face and both arms with them.\"" Sayyidna Abdullah said: \""Have you not seen this? Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not content himself with the statement of Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him).\"""""
685,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He (may God bless him and grant him peace) said: \There are two strokes in Tayammum. One stroke is for the face and one stroke is for both arms up to the elbows.\"" A narrator named Ali bin Zabayan has narrated it as a marfu' tradition which other men have narrated as muwaqf and this is correct."""
686,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \There are two strokes in Tayammum. One stroke is for the face and one stroke is for both arms up to the elbows (for wiping).\"""""
687,Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to perform Tayammum up to his elbows.
688,"Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): We performed tayammum with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his time in al-Aqdas. We used to strike our hands on clean clay and then we would wipe our hands and then wipe our face with it."
689,"Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): We performed tayammum with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e. in his time). It consists of two multiplications. One stroke was for the face and both palms, while one stroke was for both arms up to the elbows. The two narrators of this tradition are Sulaiman bin Arqam and Sulaiman bin Abu Dawud."
690,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tayammum: \There will be two strokes. One stroke will be for the face," and the other stroke will be for the hands up to the elbows.\"""""
691,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \One stroke in tayammum is for the face and one stroke is for the wrists to the elbows.\"" All its narrators are reliable"," but the truth is that this tradition is suspended."""
692,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that a person came and said: \Janabat has come upon me. I have become spoiled in the mud.\"" So he said: \""Strike (your hands) on the ground.\"" So he struck his hand on the ground and wiped his face with both hands"," then he struck his other hand on the ground and wiped his hands up to the elbows with it."""
693,"A narrator named Aban narrates: Qatadah was asked about tayammum during the journey, and he replied, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) used to say that it would be done up to the elbows. Hasan al-Basri and Ibrahim Nakhai say: Up to the elbows (will be wiped). Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrated this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Tayammum will be performed up to the elbows.\"" A narrator named Abu Ishaq narrates: I mentioned this tradition to Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and he liked this tradition very much. He said: \""What a wonderful tradition.\"""""
694,"Salim narrates this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: When he performed tayammum, he used to strike both hands on the ground. Through them, they used to wipe their hands up to both elbows. They did not sweep the soil with their hands."
695,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \(In tayammum) there will be two strokes. One stroke will be for the face and one stroke will be for both arms.\"""""
696,Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to perform Tayammum on his face and both arms.
697,"Sayyiduna Ammar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Tayammum is the name of striking (i.e. wiping over) the face and both arms.\"""""
698,"It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) that a person came and said: \I have been afflicted with janabat and I have become spoiled in the dust.\"" So they said: \""Strike your hands on the ground.\"" He struck his hand on the ground and then wiped his face with it and then again struck his hand on the ground and then wiped both his arms up to the elbows with these two hands."""
699,Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is only one stroke in Tayammum," which is for the face and both arms.\"" A narrator named Ramadi narrates: A narrator named Yazid narrates: Whoever adopts this hadith"," there is nothing wrong with it."""
700,"Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \That much is enough for you.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand on the blessed earth"," then he blew on it and wiped his face and both arms with it."""
701,"Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: Once he got sidetracked during a journey and fell into the mud. When he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about it, the Prophet (PBUH) said: \O Ammar! It would have been enough for you to strike your two hands on the dirt", then blow on them," then rub your hands with them up to your face and wrists.\"" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Ibrahim as a superior tradition", while other narrators have narrated it as a fixed tradition, and its narrator Abu Malik is considered to have hadiths from Sayyidna Ammar, because other narrators have narrated it from Sayyidna Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him," regarding this Abu Malik."""
702,"A narrator named Abu Malik narrates: I heard Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir giving a sermon in Kufa, and he mentioned Tayammum and said: \In it one will strike one's hand on the ground and wipe one's face and both arms with it.\"""""
703,"Abu Malik narrates this about Sayyidna Ammar: He struck his palms on the clay and blew on it and spread it on his face and wiped both arms up to the joints, then Sayyidna Ammar said: \Tayammum is done like this.\"" This same tradition is narrated as a hadith along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
704,Imam al-Shaabi states: It is necessary to perform tayammum on the part which is ordered to be washed. The organ which is not ordered to be washed will be abandoned in Tayammum.
705,Imam Sha'bi states: We have been ordered to perform tayammum on those parts of ourselves which have been ordered to be washed (in ablution).
706,Qatadah narrates: Sayyiduna Amr bin As used to perform tayammum for every prayer. Qatadah himself used to issue fatwas accordingly.
707,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \Tayammum will be performed for every prayer.\"""""
708,"Sayyiduna Amr bin As says: \Tayammum will be performed for every prayer.\"""""
709,Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to perform tayammum for every prayer.
710,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \This is a Sunnah," a person should pray only one prayer with Tayammum and then perform Tayammum (again) for the second prayer.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Hasan bin Amara."""
711,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \It is a Sunnah that a man should not offer more than one prayer with one Tayammum.\"""""
712,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Only one prayer will be performed through Tayammum.\"""""
713,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A person who performs tayammum should not lead those who perform ablution.\"" Its evidence is weak."""
714,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \A bound person should not lead the absolute people and a person performing tayammum should not lead those who perform ablution.\"""""
715,The same tradition about Tayammum is narrated along with another chain of transmission.
716,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing tayammum at a place called Murbad-ul-Naam," while he (peace be upon him) was observing the houses of Madinah from this place.\"""""
717,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform tayammum at Murbad al-Naam, which is three miles away from Madinah Munawwarah."
718,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
719,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed tayammum at a distance of one or two miles from Madinah and offered Asr prayer, then he came to (the city) and the sun was still high. He did not pray again."
720,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \When a person is on a journey, he should calculate the time between himself and the last time of prayer. If he cannot find water," he should perform tayammum.\"""""
721,Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Pure soil is a means of ablution for a Muslim," even if he does not get water for ten years.\"""""
722,"Abu Qalaba narrates this regarding a person from Banu Amir: I was told about Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, so I attended his service. I asked him: \Are you Sayyidna Abu Dharr?\"" He replied: \""That's what my family calls me.\"" Then Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari Radiyallahu Anhu said: Once I said: \""O Messenger of Allah! I have become a victim of death.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""What has caused you to perish?\"" I said: \""I was in a place where no water could be found. I had my wife with me. I got janabat.\"" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Pure soil is a means of attaining purity until a man finds water", even if ten years pass. When you find water," pour it on your body.\"""""
723,Mahlab narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari Radiyallahu Anhu: He said: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet PBUH and the Prophet PBUH said: \O Abu Dharr! Indeed, mud is a means of purification for a person who does not get water, even if he does not get it for ten years. When you find water," pour it on your body.\"""""
724,Amr bin Bajdan narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari quoting the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wa sallam saying: \Indeed, pure soil is a means of purification for a Muslim if it lasts for ten years. When a man drinks water," he should pour water over his body. It will be better for him.\"""""
725,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari, may Allah be pleased with him, but it contains these words: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: \This is a means of attaining purity.\"""""
726,Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Pure soil is a means of attaining purity, even if a person does not get water for ten years. When you drink water," pour it over your skin.\"" A narrator named Raja bin Aamir has narrated it in this way", but it is true that it is related to a person belonging to Banu Amir," as Ibn Alayhi narrated it from a narrator named Ibn Ayyub."""
727,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once two men set out on a journey. It was time for prayer in front of both of them. They didn't have water, they both performed tayammum through pure clay then during this prayer time they both got water. One of them performed ablution and offered the prayer again, while the other person did not offer the prayer again. Then these two came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned this to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the person who had not repeated the prayer: \You have done well"," your prayer has been correct.\"" To the other person who performed ablution and prayed again"," he said: \""You will have a double reward.\"" In narrating this tradition through a narrator named Layth"," the narrator named Abdullah ibn Nafi is unique. Ibn Mubarak and other Muhadditheen have narrated a tradition to the contrary."""
728,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Mubarak, Ata bin Yasar narrates: Both of these men were given janabat. Both of them performed Tayammum, Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) is not mentioned in this hadith."
729,"Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once we set out on a journey. One of us was hit by a stone which injured his head and then he got concussion. He inquired of his companions: \Do you think I need to perform tayammum?\"" The Companions replied: \""When you are able to use water"," there is no leave for you with us.\"" The person took a bath and died. We came to the service of the Holy Prophet. When you were told about it"," the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""These people killed him. May Allah destroy them. Why did they not inquire when they did not know"," the healing of a sick person in questioning. It was enough for that person that he would perform tayammum (bandage) and (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words) bandage his wound and anoint it and wash the rest of his body.\"" The narrator named Musa is in doubt here. Shaykh Abu Bakr states: The people of Makkah are unique in narrating this tradition and the people of Al-Jazira transmitted it. He has not narrated it from Sayyidina Jabir regarding Ata. This tradition is only narrated by a narrator named Zubair and is not authentic. Imam Uza'i has narrated a hadith to the contrary", which is narrated from Sayyidna Abdullah regarding Ata. There is also a difference of opinion in quoting from Imam Uza'i. According to one tradition, it was narrated from Ata, and according to another tradition," it was narrated from him: \""I have come to know this regarding Ata.\"" And Imam Uza'i has quoted the last part of it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Ata as a transmitted tradition", and this is correct. Ibn Abi Hatim narrates: I asked my father and a narrator named Shaykh Abi Zariyah about it, and they both replied: This hadith was narrated by Ibn al-Ashireen, on the authority of Uza'i, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas," may God be pleased with him. These gentlemen have quoted it as an authentic tradition."""
730,"Ata narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated this: A person was wounded during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He was embarrassed. When he discovered the problem, he was told that he had to take a ghusl, which he did and died. When the Prophet (PBUH) was informed about this, he (PBUH) said: \These people have killed him. May Allah destroy them. Isn't the healing of a sick person in questioning?\"""""
731,"A narrator named Ata narrates that he came to know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about this, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if the person had washed his body and left the head where the wound was, it would have been permissible for him to do so. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
732,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA).
733,"Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrating that during the time of the Holy Prophet, a man was injured, then he developed a fever, so he was asked to take a bath. He took bath and died. When this was reported to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said that those people killed him. May Allah destroy these people, isn't the healing of a sick person in questioning? A narrator named Ata narrates that we came to know that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if the person had washed his body and left the part of his head where the wound was, it would have been correct."
734,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him).
735,This same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
736,"The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission, while other narrators have also followed it."
737,"Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, then he (PBUH) wiped his forehead, turban and both socks."
738,"The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate on the authority of their father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anointed both his socks, the front of his head and his turban."
739,"The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrated the same thing from the Prophet (PBUH) regarding his father. A narrator has narrated these words in his hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the front of his head, the front of his forehead, his two socks and his cloak."
740,"The sons of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrate on the authority of their father that the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution. You wiped your forehead, wiped both socks and wiped your turban. A narrator named Bakr has narrated that I heard this hadith from the son of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba."
741,"A narrator named Hammam narrates that Sayyiduna Jarir (may God be pleased with him) urinated, then wiped his socks while performing ablution. So they were asked why you have done this, you have already urinated? He replied, \I saw the Holy Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, first he urinated," then after that he performed ablution and wiped both socks.\"" A narrator named Amish narrates that Ibrahim says that these people liked this hadeeth very much", the reason being that Sayyiduna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed. A narrator named Isa bin Yunus narrated in his tradition that he was asked," \""O Abu Amr! You are doing this"," have you urinated before?\"" So he replied that what would prevent me from doing that when I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. The disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) liked this tradition very much because Sayyidna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after the revelation of Surah Maida."""
742,"Hammam bin Harith narrates that I saw Sayyiduna Jarir, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution with the ablution vessel and then wiped his socks. He was asked if you are wiping your socks? So he replied that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. This tradition was very liked by the students of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). He used to say that Sayyiduna Jarir (RA) accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed."
743,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
744,Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah Bijli (RA) narrates that I came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) after the revelation of Surah al-Maidah. I saw you wipe your socks.
745,Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping his socks. People inquired whether you saw this after Surah al-Maida was revealed. He said that I accepted Islam after Surah Maida was revealed.
746,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that after Surah Maida was revealed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to wipe his socks until he appeared in the presence of Allah."
747,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of his father that he allowed a traveler to wipe his feet for three days and three nights, while a resident for one day and one night. If a man wears socks after performing ablution, he can wipe the socks during that time. A narrator named Abu Ash'ath states that a traveler can wipe it for three days and three nights while a resident can wipe it for one day and one night."
748,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
749,"Urwa bin Mughirah narrates on the authority of his father that I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace! Are you wiping your socks?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wore both of them in such a state that they were both clean."""
750,"Sayyiduna Hasan Basri states that the upper part of the socks will be wiped, like lines will be made with the fingers."
751,This tradition is also narrated along with a document.
752,"Sayyiduna Al-Mughira (RA) says: I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, so he wiped the upper part and the lower part of the socks."
753,"The same hadith is transmitted as Mursal Hadith along with another chain of transmission, in which Sayyiduna Mughirah (RA) was not mentioned."
754,Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates that I saw the Prophet (PBUH) wiping the top of his socks.
755,"Salim narrates on the authority of his father Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that Sayyidna Sa’d (RA) inquired from Sayyidna Umar (RA) about wiping the socks, and he said, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) commanding to wipe the upper part of the socks, which is three days and three nights for a traveler and one day and one night for a resident."
756,"Mufadl bin Fazalah narrates that I asked Yazid bin Abu Habib about wiping over the socks, and he said that Abdullah bin Huqam has quoted this statement of Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may God be pleased with him) with reference to Ali bin Rabah. Sayyiduna Uqbah told him that once he joined a delegation and attended the service of Sayyiduna Umar. Uqba says that at that time I was wearing thick socks and that day was Friday. So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to them that you have acted according to the Sunnah. One hadith has the words that you have done right, but the word \Sunnah\"" is not mentioned in it."""
757,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I left Syria on Friday to go to Madinah and reached Madinah on Friday. I attended the service of Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu, and he asked, \How long have you been wearing socks on your feet?\"" I replied that last Friday. They inquired whether you had taken them off. I replied that no! So he said that you have acted according to the Sunnah. Sheikh Abu Bakr says that this hadith is poor. Sheikh Abul Hasan says that its chain of transmission is authentic."""
758,Nafi' narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not set a time limit for wiping over the socks.
759,"Nafi', narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he says that there is no time limit for wiping the socks, you wipe them until you take them off."
760,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the traveler used to wipe his socks until he took them off.
761,"Zar bin Habish narrates that I attended the service of Sayyidna Safwan bin Asal. He asked why you came? I replied that I have come to acquire knowledge. So he said, \I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever leaves his home to seek knowledge"," the angels are pleased with his action and rest on him.\"" Zar said"," \""I have come to inquire about wiping on the socks.\"" So he replied that I was among the army that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent on a campaign and instructed us that you can wipe your socks for three days during the journey and for one day and one night during the stay", while we have worn them in a state of ablution and we will not take them off while urinating, defecating or getting up after sleeping, we will only take them off in a state of Janabat. Sayyiduna Safwan (RA) also said that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that there is a door in the West that is open for repentance," the width of which is the distance of seventy years. It will not close until the sun rises from its side."""
762,"Ali bin Ibrahim narrates that I heard Shaykh Abu Bakr bin Khuzima saying that I mentioned the tradition of Abdul Razzaq to Imam Muzni, so he said to me that our companions have also narrated this tradition, because Imam Shafi'i has no other authentic argument than this. The author says that these words of the hadeeth that when we entered them in the state of ablution."
763,"``Urwa bin Mughirah narrates the statement of his father that I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him! Can any of us wipe his socks?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when this person has entered them both in a state of ablution."""
764,"Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik Ashjajai (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us to anoint the soles of the feet on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, for a traveler for three days and three nights and for a resident for one day and one night."
765,"Ubada bin Nasa'i, on the authority of Abi, who is Ibn Amara, narrates that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in the house of Sayyidina Amara facing both Qiblas. He said, \O Messenger of Allah"," may I wipe my socks?\"" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah! For one day?\"" The Prophet said"," \""Yes"," you can.\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace! For two days?\"" The Prophet said"," \""Yes"," you can.\"" And even for three days. He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace! Even for three days?\"" They even asked for seven days. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""As much as you see fit.\"" Its certificate is not proven. There is a difference of opinion in narrating a tradition from a narrator named Yahya bin Ayyub", which I have mentioned elsewhere. The narrators of this tradition, Abd al-Rahman, Muhammad bin Yazid, and Ayyub bin Qahtan," are all unknown. Allah knows best."""
766,"Sayyidna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) narrates that he attended the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA) on the occasion of the conquest of Damascus. He says that I was wearing socks. Sayyiduna Umar asked, \O Uqbah! How many days have you not removed your socks?\"" So I remembered what I wore from last Friday to this Friday. I said"," \""For eight days.\"" So he said that you have done right and according to the Sunnah."""
767,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains the words that you have acted according to the Sunnah. There is no mention of anyone else in the chain of transmission between Yazid and the narrator named Ali."
768,"Umar bin Ishaq narrates that I read in the book of Ata bin Yasar, which was with Ata bin Yasar. He says: I asked Sayyida Maimunah (RA), who was the wife of the Prophet (PBUH), about wiping over the socks. So he said that I said, \O Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace! Can a man always wipe his socks without removing them?\"" The Prophet said"," \""Yes.\"""""
769,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that if the rules of the religion of Allah were in accordance with opinion, the lower part of the socks would have more right to be wiped than the upper part, but I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping the upper part. The words of the tradition are from a narrator named Ibn Mukhlid."
770,"Abd Khair narrates that Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said to me that I believe that the lower part of the socks is more righteous than the upper part, but I saw the Prophet (PBUH) wiping the upper part."
771,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that once we were traveling with the Prophet (PBUH) until morning approached. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to camp. When the people caught their eye, they fell asleep, until the sun rose. The first to wake up was Sayyiduna Abu Bakr. No one would wake up the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from sleep until he himself woke up. When Sayyiduna Umar woke up, he saw that the sun had risen. So he sat on the head of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to say Takbeer in a loud voice, until the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up. When you woke up, you saw that the sun had risen. So you left. You traveled a bit, until the sun shone brightly. So you stopped and led us in prayer. One of the attendees stayed away. He did not pray with us. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he inquired, \What has prevented you from praying with us?\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah! I have received Janabat.\"" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to perform tayammum with clay and perform the prayer. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me ahead with some horsemen to find water", for we were very thirsty. While we were travelling, we saw a woman with two muskets. We asked him," \""Where is the water?\"" \""There is no water here","\"" he said. We inquired"," \""How far is it between us and the water?\"" He replied"," \""One day and one night.\"" We said"," \""Go to the Messenger of Allah.\"" He said"," \""Where are the Messengers of Allah?\"" So we took it to the service of the Holy Prophet. She told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same thing that she told us", but she added that she was the mother of orphans. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered about his muskets, whose mouths were opened from the bottom side. So we forty thirsty people drank water from it until we were full. We filled every pot and bowl we had. We gave water to our companion for bathing, but we did not water our camels. Then the Prophet (PBUH) ordered," \""Bring whatever you have.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) collected pieces of bread", dates, etc. for him and tied a bundle to him and said," \""You go and feed it to your family"," and know that We have not reduced your water in any way.\"" When she went to her house", she said," \""I have met the greatest magician", or rather he is a prophet," as people have described.\"" The narrator says that because of this woman", Allah blessed her tribe with guidance. That woman also became a Muslim and her clan members also became Muslims. Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, has narrated this tradition on the authority of Abu Waleed along with this chain of transmission, while Imam Muslim, may God have mercy on him," has narrated this tradition on the authority of Ahmad bin Saeed al-Darmi."""
772,
773,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that we were on a journey with the Prophet (PBUH). We walked all night. When the last part of the night happened, we fell asleep. There is nothing more enjoyable than sleeping at this time. The heat of the sun woke us up. He has quoted the previous hadith. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, \O such and such a person! Did you not pray with us?\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah! I was afflicted with Janabat and there is no water.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You use clay"," it will be better for you.\"" There are also words in this tradition that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel", poured water into the vessel through the mouths of the musketeers, then he rinsed it, put the water in the vessel again, then he again poured that water into the muskets and closed their mouths from the top and opened them from the bottom. Then he announced to the people," \""Let them drink water themselves and water their animals.\"" He who wanted to drink himself drank", and he who fed the animals also fed them. In the end, water was given to the person who was afflicted with Janabat. He gave him a pot of water and said," \""Pour it over your body.\"" The woman stood and watched what was happening to her water. The narrator says that by Allah! When their mouths were closed"," it seemed as if the muskets were even fuller than they had been in the beginning. He has narrated the rest of the hadith like this."""
774,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says about such a person who is traveling, if he has Janabat and does not have water with him, due to which he is afraid of being thirsty."
775,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that once the funeral was brought, he was not in the state of ablution at that time. He performed Tayammum and offered the funeral prayer."
776,Al-Khajri bin Zayd narrates that Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) had the disease of dropping urine and he used to pray while the drops were coming out.
777,"Sayyidna Al-Khajri bin Zayd narrates that Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) said Takbeer, then drops of his urine started coming out. They tried to hold back as much as they could, but when he overcame them, they performed ablution and prayed."
778,"Saeed bin Musayyib says that if it is flowing on my knees, then I will not finish the prayer. A narrator named Sufyan states that it refers to urine, i.e. when a person is suffering from an illness."
779,"Zubayd bin Salat narrates that I heard Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that when a person performs ablution and wears socks, he can pray over them by wiping them. If he wants, he should not take them off, but the ruling is different in the case of Janabat."
780,"This same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Anas, along with another chain of transmission. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id states that according to my knowledge this hadith has been narrated only by Asad bin Musa."
781,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said that when a person performs ablution and wears his socks, he can pray in them. He should anoint them, then if he wishes, he should not take them off, but in the case of Janabat, the ruling is different."
782,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the traveler to stay for three days and three nights, and the resident for one day and one night. When he performs ablution and wears socks, the permission is that he can wipe both socks between ablutions. This tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions."
783,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if the rules of religion were related to opinion, the lower part of the sock would be more righteous than the upper part, but I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping the upper part."
784,"Imam Zayd narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father, his grandfather, that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed me to anoint the socks."
785,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to wipe his bandage. This hadeeth is not authentic. Its narrator, Abu Amara, is very weak."
786,"Ibrahim narrates on the authority of Nakhai, Alqamah and Aswad that about a person who performs ablution and wipes his socks, then takes them off, they both said: \He will wash his feet.\"""""
787,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Fatimah bint Abu Habish asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \O Messenger of Allah! I am not pure," should I give up prayer?\"" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \""This is blood from a vein", it is not menstruation. When you have menstruation, you should stop praying. When its period is over," you should wash the blood from your body and pray.\"""""
788,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Fatimah bint Abu Habish came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah! I am a woman suffering from istihazah. I am not pure. Shall I give up prayer?\"" He said: \""No", it is blood from another vein, not menstruation. When menstruation occurs, stop praying. When it ends," take a bath and start praying.\"" A narrator named Yahya has narrated this: \""When he leaves"," wash the blood from your body and pray.\"" In one narration these words are added: Hisham narrates: My father narrated this: \""Then perform ablution for every prayer"," until that time comes.\"""""
789,Sayyidna Fatima bint Abu Habish (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she was suffering from istihazah. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \When the menstrual blood comes, it will be more. When such a situation occurs, you should give up praying. But when there is another situation, you should perform ablution and perform the prayer," because it is blood from someone else's vein.\"""""
790,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: Fatima bint Abu Habish was suffering from istihazah. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Menstrual blood is black which is recognizable. When it is, you should abandon the prayer, and when it is of a different color," perform ablution and perform the prayer.\"""""
791,Urwah narrates the statement of Sayyidah Fatimah bint Abu Habish (may God be pleased with her): She became afflicted with istihazah. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \When there is menstrual blood, it will be black blood that will be recognized. When it is blood, you should refrain from praying, and when there is blood of another color, you should perform ablution and perform the prayer," because it is blood from another vein.\"" In a hadith", it is narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha. Fatimah bint Abu Habish narrated a hadeeth after that. In this tradition," the words of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are quoted: \""When the blood is of another type"," perform ablution and pray.\"""""
792,"Urwa narrates this statement about Sayyida Fatimah bint Abu Habish (RA): When she suffered from Istihazah, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her: \The menstrual blood will be black and it will be recognized", so stop praying. When it is different, perform ablution and pray," because it is blood from another vein.\"""""
793,"Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) who is the wife of the Prophet (PBUH) narrates: Fatimah bint Abu Habish was a victim of Istihaha during the time of the Prophet (PBUH). Sayyida Umm Salma asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this issue, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \She should count the number of days she used to menstruate in the first months and give up the prayer during that time. When that time has passed"," she should perform ghusl and perform ablution and put on a cloth and perform the prayer.\"""""
794,"Salman bin Yasar narrates: Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the issue of Fatima bint Abu Habish, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: “She will abstain during the specified period of menstruation and after that she will perform ghusl and pray.” The same hadith is narrated from Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) along with another chain of transmission, but it contains the words of the Prophet (PBUH): \She will wait for the days of her menses and abandon the prayer.\"""""
795,"Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: Sayyida Fatimah bint Abu Habish (may Allah be pleased with her) complained of istihazah, until a large vessel was kept for her in which the blood would bleed. The narrator narrates: Then he said to Sayyidah Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her: \Ask the matter from the Holy Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""She will give up prayer during the days of her menstruation"," then she will perform the prayer after taking a ghusl and wearing a cloth.\"""""
796,"Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: Sayyida Fatimah bint Abu Habish (RA) complained of istihazah, so she inquired from the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator doubts that these are the words: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the issue for her, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed: “She should give up prayer during the specific days of her menstruation, and in addition, she should perform ghusl and perform the prayer after tying a cloth.” A narrator named Sulaiman was asked: \Did her husband have intercourse with her?\"" So they replied: \""We will narrate what we have heard.\"""""
797,"Ata states: \The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"""""
798,"Ata states: \The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"""""
799,"Ata states: \The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"""""
800,"Ata states: \The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"" Abu Ibrahim narrates: Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal adopted these two traditions and presented them as arguments."""
801,Ata bin Abi Rabah states: The minimum period of menstruation is one day.
802,The participant narrates that we had a woman who used to menstruate for fifteen days every month and that menstruation was perfect and normal.
803,Uza'i narrates that we had a woman who used to menstruate in the morning and became pure in the evening.
804,Hasan bin Saleh states that the maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.
805,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: Menstruation can last for (at least) three days or it can last for four or five or six or seven or eight or nine or ten days. This hadith has not been narrated by anyone except Haroon bin Ziyad along with this chain of authority, and this narrator is weak, and since it was transmitted from Amish, this tradition has no origin for the people of Kufa, and Allah knows best."
806,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Menstruation may last for three days, or for four days, or for five days, or for six days, or for seven days, or for eight days, or for nine days, or for ten days."
807,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that menstruation can last three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten days."
808,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: The period of menstruation can be at least three days and at most ten days.
809,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: Menstruation cannot last more than ten days.
810,Sufyan Thauri says: The minimum period of menstruation is three days and the maximum is ten days.
811,"Sayyiduna Anas says that a woman will be considered menstruating until the period lasts for ten days, if it lasts more than that, then she will be considered mustahad."
812,"Shaykh Abu Zareah Damaschi says: I saw Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal, he did not accept this tradition of Jald bin Ayyub."
813,"Hammad bin Zayd narrates that I and Jarir bin Hazim went to Jalad bin Ayyub and he narrated this tradition about a mustahadha woman, a mustahadha woman will wait for three days, five days or seven days or ten days, (that is, she will consider these days as menstruation), so we went and we tried to forbid them, but they did not differentiate between menstruation and istahadha."
814,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu used to say: A menstruating woman will wait for three, four, five, ten days, if the bleeding lasts more than ten days, then she will be Mustahadha, and she will take a bath and start praying."
815,"Uthman bin Abul-Aas narrates: A woman will not count as mustahadhah because of one or two or three days, until she reaches ten days."
816,"Uthman bin Abul As-Thaqafi states that a menstruating woman who continues to bleed after ten days, then she will be regarded as Mustahadha, she will perform ghusl and pray."
817,Saeed bin Jubayr says: The maximum duration of menstruation is thirteen days.
818,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Fatima bint Abu Habish came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman suffering from istihadah.” The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is blood from someone else’s vein. A narrator named Ammar is unique in narrating this tradition, it is weak, while according to the Muhadditheen, this tradition is suspended as it was narrated from Ismail (it contains these words) A woman suffering from istihaza will count the days of her menstruation, after which she will bathe and perform ablution for each prayer."
819,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Fatima bint Abu Habish came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am suffering from Istihazah, so how can I be pure?” It is portable. Some narrators have narrated it as a marfu' tradition, while some narrators have narrated it as a suspended tradition, and these traditions are also authentic."
820,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that an Ansari woman came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said, \O Messenger of Allah", I am suffering from istihazah. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed her not to pray during the specific days of her menstruation, then take a bath and perform ablution at the time of each prayer," even though drops of blood are falling on the mat."""
821,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Fatima bint Abu Habish came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “It is blood from another vein."
822,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Fatima bint Abu Habish attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “You should abandon the prayer during the days of your menstruation, then take a ghusl and start praying even if drops of blood fall on the mat. There are these words in a hadith: Do you perform ablution for every prayer?"
823,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: take a bath again, then perform ablution for each prayer, and perform the prayer, even though drops of blood are falling on the mat."
824,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that Fatimah bint Abu Habish came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
825,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A musthahaza woman will pray even though drops of blood are falling on the mat.
826,"Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr narrates: We got up from Abdullah bin Dawud and came to Yahya bin Saeed, and he asked, \Where did you come from?\"" He replied"," \""He is coming from Abdullah bin Dawud.\"" He asked"," \""Did he tell you the hadith?\"" So we replied", he narrated the hadith of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqah regarding Amish, regarding Habib, regarding Urwa," then Yahya said: Sufyan Thawri has the most knowledge about this."""
827,"Imam Abu Dawud says that the hadith transmitted from Amish indicates that it is weak, that is, the narrator named Hafs narrated it from Amish as a fixed tradition and denied this. And there are these words in it that woman used to bathe before every prayer. All this statement is from Imam Abu Dawood."
828,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A mustahadhah woman will pray even if her blood drops are falling on the mat. The narrator named Hafs did not narrate this hadith as a valid tradition, while the narrator named Usama followed it."
829,It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa that she was asked about a musthahaza woman and she said that she will not give up prayer even if drops of blood are falling on the mat.
830,"It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she was asked about a musthahaza woman, and she said, \She will not abandon the prayer"," even though drops of blood are falling on the mat.\"" A narrator named Waqi' has narrated it as a marfu' hadith by Ali Ibn Hashim and a narrator named Hafs has narrated it as a muqaf tradition."""
831,"Yahya bin Moin says that a narrator named Habib bin Thabit has narrated two hadiths regarding Arwa, but both of them have no status."
832,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Fatimah bint Abu Habish came and said: I have a complaint of istihaza, I am not pure. The woman said, \I am suffering from istihazah. My blood does not stop. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said", 'This is the blood of another vein. It is not the blood of menstruation. When menstruation comes, you should give up prayer, and when it ends," take ablution and start praying."""
833,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: Recitation means purity.
834,"Sayyida Hamna bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I was suffering from severe istihadah, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to find out about it. This thing has stopped me from praying, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Put a piece of cloth, the bleeding will stop.” The woman said, “It is more.” The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, “Tie a bandage.” He said, “It is more than that. If you have the power of both, then you know better. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \This is Satan's trick. According to the knowledge of God", your period is six or seven days. After that, you take a bath. Then you see that you are now purified," so clean the place. Then you should pray and fast for twenty-four days or twenty-three days. It is permissible for you to do this. Do it in the same way every month.\"" In general", women live for the specific period of their menstruation and tahr, and if you have the strength to do so, then delay the Zuhr prayer and perform the Asr prayer early, then perform ghusl and perform the Zuhr and Asr together, then delay the Maghrib and perform the Isha prayer early, and perform the two prayers at the same time. Pay, fast if you have the strength to do so, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""I like this.\"""""
835,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
836,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
837,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
838,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
839,"Sayyida Asma bint Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, I said, O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah bint Abu Habish has been complaining of istihaza for so long. It is from the devil, she should sit in a large pot. When the woman sat on it, the yellowness of her period prevailed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \She should perform a ghusl once for Zuhr and Asr", and perform a ghusl once for Maghrib and Isha," then perform a separate ghusl for Fajr and perform ablution in between.\"""""
840,"Sayyida Asma bint Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, “I said, O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah bint Abu Habish has not prayed for such a long time. He should hasten Isha and pray for both of them after performing ghusl once."
841,"Ibn Abi Malika narrates: Sayyida Fatimah bint Abi Habish (may Allah be pleased with her) complained of Istihaza. She did not pray for such a long time. She came to the service of Sayya Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: O Umm al-Mu'minin, I am afraid that I may not end up in hell and have no part in Islam. It has been a long time since I did not pray. I am bleeding Istihaza. said: You stay when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to inquire from him in the way that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned to me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Tell Fatimah that she should give up prayer during the specific days of her menstruation in every month. When those specific days are over, she should take a bath once and put cotton on her private parts and tie a wide bandage around it so that (the blood does not come out) then perform ablution for each prayer and perform the prayer. There is a disease that he has contracted. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
842,"Ibn Abi Malika narrates that my aunt, Sayyida Fatimah bint Abu Habish, may Allah be pleased with her, came to the service of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa and said: I am afraid that I will not go to Hell, because I have not prayed for two years (the narrator doubts that these words are the words), Sayyida Ayesha said, \You wait when the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, brings Tashrif," then (inquire from him).\"" The Messenger of God came and Aisha told her that it was Fatimah", and the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to her," \""Abandon prayer during the specific days of menstruation", then take a bath once a day, then perform ablution for each name, and cover your private parts, because it is an illness that has been contracted, or it is a stroke of the devil," or a vein that has been severed.\"""""
843,Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates that a woman asked the Prophet (PBUH) \I am suffering from impurity, I am not pure," should I stop praying?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No", rather, you should give up praying on those specific days in which you used to menstruate," then after that you should bathe and tie a cloth and pray."""
844,"Sayyida Umm Salma narrates that a woman's blood was flowing profusely and it would not stop. Sayyida Umm Salma asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \That woman will examine the specific days in which she used to menstruate. She will give up prayer for that number of days", then when it is time for prayer," she will perform ablution and pray with a cloth.\"""""
845,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “A young girl and a woman who is disappointed with menstruation will not menstruate for less than three days, and it will not last more than ten days. Menstrual blood is black and thick, in which redness prevails, while the blood of Istihaza is yellow and thin. This tradition is not proven. Its two narrators, Abdul Malik and Alaa, are both weak, while the narrator named Makhool is not proven."
846,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this, the amount of menstruation of a virgin girl, Yathiba, is at least three days and the maximum is ten days. If the blood comes out profusely during the prayer, then he should put a cotton cloth, if the blood is still coming out, then put another cloth or a bandage. The narrator of this tradition is Abdul Malik Majhool, while the narrator named Alaa is Alaa bin Kathir and it is weak in hadith, while the narrator named Makhool has not heard any hadith from Sayyidna Abu Umamah."
847,Sayyidna Wathila Bin Asqaa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the minimum period of menstruation is three days and the maximum period is ten days. The narrator of this hadith is Hamad bin Minhal unknown while Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Anas is weak.
848,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Fatimah bin Qays asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the issue of istihaza woman, what should she do? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \She should count the specific days of her menstruation", then when she becomes pure," she should take a bath and perform the prayer.\"" A narrator named Jafar bin Sulaiman is unique in narrating this tradition. The narration narrated by Ibn Jaraj regarding Abu Zubayr is not correct"," the narrator is delusional because the name of this lady was Fatima bint Abu Habish."""
849,"Ata narrates that when a pregnant woman sees blood, Sayyida Aisha said that she cannot menstruate, so she will perform ghusl and pray."
850,"Sayyidah Umm Atiya (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that we women did not care about the discharge that was visible after initiation, which was yellowish or yellowish in color."
851,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa likes that a woman suffering from Istihazah should have intercourse with her husband.
852,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about nifas (the maximum period is forty days, but if the woman observes tahr before that (then the ruling will be different). This hadith was narrated by a narrator named Hameed only by a narrator named Salam. This salam is long and it is weak in the hadith."
853,Sayyidna Uthman bin Abul-Aas (RA) said to his wives: You used to not adorn yourself in front of me before forty days have passed. Do not exceed forty days.
854,"Sayyidna Uthman bin Abul As, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that when she was purified from nifas, she adorned herself, then Sayyidna Uthman bin Abul As said, \Didn't I tell you?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us to stay away from pregnant women for forty days. A narrator named Umar bin Haroon has narrated it as a valid tradition while a narrator named Wakiy has narrated it contrary to it."""
855,"Sayyidna Uthman bin Abul As said to his wives: When a woman among you was in labor, she would not come near me for forty days. Similarly, this hadith has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may God be pleased with him) and others as their own sayings."
856,Sayyiduna Uthman bin Abul-Aas (RA) says that the Prophet (PBUH) has fixed the period of forty days for pregnant women.
857,"The same hadith has been narrated by the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa. One of the narrators of this hadith is Abu Bilal Al-Ash'ari, while the other narrator is Ata bin Ajlan, the hadeeth is obsolete."
858,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said that a woman who has given birth will wait for forty days. The narrators of this hadith are Amr bin Husain and Ibn Alashah, both weak and outdated."
859,"It is narrated about ``Aiz bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that his wife suffered from nifas. After twenty days, she was purified and came to his bed. He said: What is your problem? He said: I have become pure, so he struck the woman with his foot and said: Get away from me, you are not something that can separate me from my religion until forty days have passed (you cannot come near me). In a hadith, these words are Sayyidna Ayaz bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him: he is the person who pledged allegiance to the hand of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, under the tree. This hadith has been narrated only by a narrator named Muawiya with reference to Jalad bin Ayyub and this narrator is weak."
860,Sayyiduna Umar (RA) says that a woman in childbirth will sit for forty days.
861,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) when seven days have passed for a postpartum woman and then she observes tahr, then she should perform ghusl and start praying. Its narrator Saleem narrates: Later, I met Ali bin Ali Muhaddith, he narrated the same tradition with reference to Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Aswad, Ubadah, and Abd al-Rahman. The black narrator of this tradition is Ibn Thaalba the Syrian."
862,"Sayyida Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pregnant women used to sit for forty days."
863,The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission in it is al-Faat. She used to sit after her nifas.
864,"Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz narrates that Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal was asked, I was listening to this, he was asked about the women who have given birth, if they see blood, how long should they sit, and he replied: For forty days, after that she will perform ghusl."
865,"Abdullah bin Abu Malikah narrates that Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa was asked about the women who are pregnant, and she said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about it, and he said that she would stay for forty days, then she would perform ghusl and purify herself and start offering prayers. The narrator of this tradition is Ata, a obsolete hadith."
866,"Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) narrates this about the Prophet (PBUH): She asked the Prophet (PBUH) how long a woman would sit after giving birth to a child. So the Prophet said, \Such a woman will remain seated for forty days. If she observes tahr before that"," (her ruling will be different)."""
867,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a postpartum woman observes tahr, it is not permissible for her to abandon prayer."
868,"Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanum narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, about a menstruating woman who becomes pure a little before sunset, and he said: \She will perform Asr prayer.\"" I asked: \""She will perform Maghrib prayer before sunset.\"" He said"," \""She will perform the Isha prayer. I inquired about who is purified before the sun rises. He said"," \""She will perform the morning prayer. This is what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us to do. This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Saeed."""
869,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Battle of Zaat al-Raqqa. (The judge quoted these words) When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encamped at a place, he said, “Who will guard us tonight?” Then an Ansari and a Muhajir went forward. When they reached the end of the gorge, the Ansari man said to the Muhajir: In which part of the night do you dislike (the first part or the last part)? He said: In the first part, the narrator narrates that the emigrant fell asleep and the Ansari stood up and prayed. The same person (polytheist) came and when he saw the face of a person, he knew that it was for the protection of the people, so he shot that Ansari with an arrow that hit him. The person shot the third arrow which hit the Ansari, so the Ansari put it away, then the Ansari bowed, then went into prostration, then he lifted his companion (and said to him) get up because I am bleeding profusely. He had shot you earlier. Why did you not tell me then? This Ansari said: I was reciting such a surah and it did not please me to leave it in the middle before I finished it, but when this person kept shooting at me, then I went into Ruku (after finishing the prayer), then I woke you up. By Allah, what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had instructed me to protect, if I was about to waste it, (I had this desire) before finishing it. dying"
870,Sayyidna Masoor bin Mukharama (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Umar (RA) continued to pray while his wound was bleeding.
871,The same hadith is also related to Sayyidna Masoor bin Mukharama along with another chain of transmission about Sayyidna Umar (RA).
872,Syedna Jarhad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him. He was in the mosque at that time. He was wearing a cloak in which his thigh was visible.
873,This tradition is also narrated along with a document.
874,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said to me that you should wear a veil over your thighs, because the thighs are part of a veil."
875,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said to me: Do not uncover your thighs and do not look at the thighs of any living or dead person.
876,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrated: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the bandage that is tied on a wound, etc. How can such a person perform ablution? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Such a person will be anointed with water in the state of janabat.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will wipe his whole body"," then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: \""Do not kill yourselves. Verily", Allah is Most Merciful to you (so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""If such a person is afraid"," he should perform tayammum.\"""""
877,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA).
878,"Imam Zaidi, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib regarding his father (Imam Zain al-Abidin) and his grandfather (Imam Hussain, may Allah be pleased with him). I have broken a joint."
879,This tradition is narrated by Amr bin Khalid Wasti along with another chain of transmission.
880,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a place where filth etc. is thrown.
881,"Narrated by Nafi, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was asked about a place where dirt is thrown, can one perform prayer there? So he said, \When you water it three times"," then you should pray there.\"""""
882,"Sayyida Asma Bint Abu Bakr said this to Hajjaj Bin Yusuf: Once the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) applied to his back, he gave his blood to my son, and my son drank it. So he said, \I don't like it that I should shed your blood.\"" The Prophet said"," \""Hell will never touch you.\"" Then the Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him, put his hand on his head and said," \""Woe to those who (commit a crime", i.e., martyr you) regarding you. Woe to those who (commit a crime, i.e.," martyr you) regarding you.\"""""
883,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Every noble work that does not begin with the praise of Allah is incomplete. The narrator named Qara is unique in narrating this hadith with reference to Zuhri. The narrator narrates. Other narrators have described it as a transmitted tradition with reference to Zuhri"," and the narrator named Qara is not authentic in this hadith. This hadith has been narrated by other narrators on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b on the authority of his father on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this hadith is not authentic."""
884,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) said: Every important work that does not begin with the mention of Allah (SWT) is incomplete.
885,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how many prayers Allah has made obligatory on His servants. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five prayers, he inquired: Have you performed any fard before and after them? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has made five prayers obligatory on His servants, so this person swore by Allah that He will not add anything to them, and He will not decrease anything from them."
886,"Abd al-Malik bin Rabi narrates this as a hadith on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When your children reach the age of seven, separate their beds; when they reach the age of ten, beat them for (skipping) prayer."
887,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Command your children to pray at the age of seven, and when they reach the age of ten, beat them for this reason (i.e. for abandoning the prayer) and separate their beds. Seventy to the knees."
888,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said this: Command your children to pray at the age of seven and beat them at the age of ten and separate their beds."
889,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The knee is a part of seventy. The narrator of this hadith is Abul-Junub: Weak.
890,Sayyidna Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The part above the knees is seventy and the part below the navel is seventy.
891,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command them to pray at the age of seven and beat them at the age of thirteen for (skipping the prayer).
892,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: I have been commanded to fight with people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad (PBUH) is the Messenger of Allah, and that they establish prayer and give Zakat, then their blood and wealth become forbidden to me, and they will be accountable to Allah. The same hadith is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) with another chain of transmission, while it is also narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (RA) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) on the authority of the Prophet (PBUH)."
893,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight with the polytheists until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. If we eat the slaughtered animals, their property and blood will become forbidden to us, but their right will remain intact: they will get everything that a Muslim gets, everything that is required of a Muslim will be required of them."
894,The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission.
895,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas bin Malik.
896,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas bin Malik.
897,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
898,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have been ordered to fight with the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and they establish prayer and pay zakat."
899,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
900,Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: I have been ordered to fight the people until they establish prayer and pay Zakat and bear witness.
901,"Abdullah Bin Mahreez narrates: This Sahib was under the care of Sayyidna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu, when he was sent to Syria, he used to say: I said to Sayyidna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu: Uncle, I am going to go to Syria, I am afraid that I will not be able to ask you about your call to prayer. I went out with some people. We were on the way to Hunain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was returning from Hunain. Lia: You sent someone to take us until we were brought and stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). All the people pointed towards me: they said rightly: So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them all and stopped me. I got up at that time and there was nothing more distasteful to me than what the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given me. I stood in front of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Ashdaan, Laala illa Allah, Ashhad in Laala illa Allah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasool Allah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasool Allah. Then he said to me: Read it again! And spread your voice then you said to me: Now read this: Ashdaan Lailaha illa Allah Ashhad in Lailaha illa Allah Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah Hai Ali Salat Hai Ali Salat Hai Ali Falah Hai Ali Falah Allah Akbar Allah Akbar La ilaha but Allah. When I finished the call to prayer, the Prophet (peace be upon him) called me and gave me a bag containing some silver. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his blessed hand on the forehead of Sayyidina Abu Mahzoora, then moved his hand on his face, then moved it on his chest, then moved it on his liver until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved his blessed hand to the navel of Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora, then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: May he bless you and shower blessings on you. I allow you to do this. At that time, whatever dislike I had for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disappeared and it was all transformed into love for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I went to Sayyiduna Uttab bin Asaid, who was the governor appointed by the Prophet (peace be upon him), and I started giving the call to prayer under the order of the Prophet (peace be upon him). A narrator named Ibn Juraj has narrated this: I heard this hadith from a man from the descendants of Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu, in the same way that Ibn Muhairiz narrated this hadith to me."
902,Rabi' states: Imam Shafi'i has said this: I found Ibrahim bin Abdul Aziz and he gave Azad in the same way as Ibn Muhairiz narrated. I think that he has described this Iqamah as the same tradition as he has described the incident of Azan.
903,"Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Hunain. I followed him with ten men from Mecca. The person gave the adhan separately, I gave the adhan last, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You come forward! Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made me sit in front of him, then he put his hand on my forehead and prayed for me three times, then he said: Go and call the Adhan to the House of Allah. I said: How is that? Ya Rasulullah! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the way of calling the call to prayer, the way the call to prayer is given today (the words of the calling to call to prayer were): Allah is great, Allah is great, Allah is great. These words are used in the first call to prayer in the morning. \Salaat khair min sleep Salat khair min sleep\"". Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me how to say the words of Iqamah twice (his words are: \""The height of the prayer", the height of the prayer, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar," Lailaha illa Allah\""."""
904,"Sayyidna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I went to Hunain along with ten young people with the Prophet PBUH. At that time, the Prophet PBUH was the most disliked person to us. When these people gave the call to prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! This is the person from whom I heard the call to prayer. You go and call the call to prayer for the people of Makkah and you say to Atab that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given this order: I call the call to prayer for the people of Makkah. Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar. These words are two times, Ashhad in laala illa Allah, you should read this twice, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasool Allah, Hai ali Salat, twice Hay Ali al Falah, twice Allah akbar, Allah akbar la ilaha illa Allah, when you give the first call to prayer in the morning, say: Salat khair min al-Num. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (RA) did not cut the hair of his forehead and did not make alms there because the Prophet (PBUH) touched him."
905,"Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) taught these words for the call to prayer: Allah is great, Allah is great, Allah is great."
906,"Ammar bin Saad narrates the statement of his father Sayyidna Saad Saad al-Qurz: This is the call to prayer of Sayyidna Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu, which was ordered by the Holy Prophet. Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Ashhadan Lailaha illa Allah, Ashhad in Lailaha illa Allah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah, then he returns and says Ashhad in Lailaha illa Allah, Ashhad in Lailaha illa Allah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah, Hai Ali Salat, Hai Ali Salat Hai Ali Al Falah, Hai Ali Falah Allah Akbar, Allah Akbar, La ilaha but Allah. His words of Iqamah are: The words of Iqamah became one by one, similarly this sentence was also said once: Sayyidna Saad Radiyallahu Anhu says: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Saad! When you do not see Bilal with me, then give the adhan. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his blessed hand over his head and said: O Saad! May Allah bless you! When you do not see Bilal with me, give the call to prayer. The narrator used to say: When Syedna Bilal asked (the Caliph at that time) Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) for permission to go to Jihad, then Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked him: O Bilal, to whom should I entrust the call to prayer? He replied: Sa'd's, because he gave the call to prayer for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Quba'. Sayyiduna Umar called Sa'd and said: The task of giving the call to prayer is entrusted to you and it will be entrusted to your children after you. Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) used to take it and walk it in front of the Prophet (PBUH) and bury it in the Eid Gah, so Sayyidna Sa'd did the same."
907,"Ibrahim bin Abdulaziz used to say: I have found my grandfather Amjad, my father and other relatives saying: He used to recite Iqamah in these words. Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar Ashhad in ilaaha illa Allah Ashhad in Muhammad Rasool Allah Hai Ali Salat Hai Ali Al-Falah Qud Qad Salawat Allahu Akbar la ilaha ila Allah."
908,"Ibrahim bin Abu Mahzourah narrates the following saying of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Sayyiduna Abu Mahzourah and taught him how to give the Adhan and instructed him to give the Adhan in Makkah, in which Allah the Great twice and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him to recite the words of Iqamah once."
909,"Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) taught him the nineteen words of Iqamah. The words of the Adhan are: Allah is great, Allah is great, Allah is great. Similarly, the words of Iqamah will be recited twice and will not be repeated."
910,"Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When I was a young boy, I gave the Fajr call to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
911,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When the Muslims came to Madinah, they used to gather together at the time of prayer. They were not called (regularly) for it. One day they discussed about this, and someone said: You guys should ring the bell like the bells of the Christians, and some of you should play the trumpets like the Jews. Sayyidna Umar (RA) said, \Why don't you send some people?\"" So that they would announce for the prayer", then the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O Bilal," get up and give the adhan."""
912,"Abdul Malik narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O Abu Mahzura, recite the words twice in the call to prayer for every prayer and say in the call to prayer in the morning: Prayer is better than sleep."
913,Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) taught me the nineteen words of the Adhan.
914,Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers.
915,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed us to make the Adhan (call to prayer) stand still and say the words of Iqamah quickly.
916,"Abu Zubair, the muezzin of Bayt al-Maqdis, narrated: Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) came to us and said, \When you give the call to prayer", stand still, and when you say Iqamah," say it loudly.\"""""
917,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) had a muezzin who used to give the Adhan quickly, so the Prophet (PBUH) said: The Adhan is the path of gentleness and ease."
918,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abu Mahzoura (RA) was instructed: He should recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers, and turn to the right and left while saying Iqamah."
919,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the words of Adhan were used twice and the words of Iqamah were used once."
920,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the words of the Adhaan were recited twice and the words of the Iqamah once, however, when the muezzin recited Qad Qat-e-Salah, he recited it twice."
921,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyiduna Bilal was given this order: He should recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers.
922,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Sayyiduna Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu used to recite the words of Adhan twice and the words of Iqamah once, except for the height of salat."
923,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was ordered: He should recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers.
924,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal: He should recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers.
925,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
926,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal to recite the words of Adhan in even numbers and the words of Iqamah in odd numbers.
927,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Sayyiduna Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu used to recite the words of Adhan twice and the words of Iqamah once, but he used to recite the words of Qad Qawat Salat twice."
928,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal: He should recite the words of Adhan twice and the words of Iqamah once.
929,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever continues to give the Adhan for twelve years, Jannah will become obligatory for him, and sixty good deeds will be written for each Adhan, and thirty good deeds will be written for each Iqamah."
930,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever continues to give the Adhan for twelve years, Jannah will become obligatory for him, and because of his giving the Adhan, sixty good deeds will be written in return for the Adhan and thirty good deeds will be written in lieu of standing."
931,Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the words of Adhan were used twice and the words of Iqamah were used once.
932,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he could not pray in congregation, he would give the call to prayer (to pray by himself) and say Iqamah (he would say the words of Iqamah twice)."
933,"Imam Muhammad bin Ali narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ali (RA): Sayyidna Jibraeel had revealed the words of Iqamah separately, and the Prophet (PBUH) declared it permissible to recite the words twice in the Adhan."
934,Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I heard Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) give the Adhan in front of the Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace).
935,"Muhammad bin Abdullah narrates: My father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the bell (for prayer), I saw in a dream a man who came to me and taught me this. He recited the words of Adhan twice and the words of Iqamah once. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If Allah wills, this dream will come true. Stand with Bilal and teach Bilal what you have seen, because his voice is louder than yours. When Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, heard this, he said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, I have also seen a dream similar to what he saw. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: Then by Allah Praise in every way is specific (which has enabled us)."
936,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), the words Adhan and Iqamah were paired. The narrator of this tradition is Ibn Abi Laili, Qazi Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, who was considered weak in the knowledge of hadith, because his memory was weak. Similarly, it is not proven that Ibn Abi Laili heard the hadith from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar."
937,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laili narrates: Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrated this: An Ansari man Abdullah bin Zayd (RA) came to the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I saw in a dream that a person came down from the sky, he was covered with two cloaks, he landed on a wall of Medina, he said the words of Adhan twice, then he sat down, then he stood up, then he said those words twice. A narrator named Abu Bakr bin Ayyash has narrated this. It is similar to the way in which the call to prayer is given today. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \Teach this to Bilal.\"" Then Sayyiduna Umar", may God be pleased with him, said: I have also seen a dream similar to what he saw," but it has overtaken me."""
938,"Aoun bin Abu Juhaifa narrates the statement of his father: Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the adhan before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in which he said the words twice and then said the Iqamah in the same way."
939,Aun bin Abu Huhaifa narrates this on the authority of his father: Sayyiduna Bilal gave the call to prayer before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose words were two times and the words of Iqamah were also two times. A narrator named Abu Aoun has narrated these words: The words of the call to prayer were two times Iqamah as well.
940,Ibrahim Nakhai narrates this statement of Aswad: Sayyiduna Bilal used to recite the words of Adhan twice and recited the words of Iqamah twice.
941,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Bilal (RA): His call to prayer and his Iqamah used to be repeated twice.
942,This tradition is narrated along with another document. Ramadi says: Sufyan did not listen to him.
943,"Abdullah bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd) on the authority of his father: When he saw in a dream the method of the call to prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyidna Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer."
944,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Sunnah is that when the muezzin gives the Fajr call to prayer, he should say: Hai Ali al-Falah, followed by salat khair min num, twice, and then say: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Lailaha illa Allaha."
945,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Taswaib will be in the morning prayer when the muezzin says in the Fajr call to prayer, Hai Ali al-Salawat, and Hai Ali al-Falah, then salat khair min num, he will say."
946,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this about Sayyidna Umar (RA): He said to his Muzan: When you reach the Azan of Fajr, Hayy Ali As-Salat, then say: As-Salat Khair Min-Num, As-Salt Khair Min-Num."
947,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laili narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed me: I should say Tasweeb in the Fajr call to prayer, but he forbade me to say Tasweeb in the Isha call to prayer."
948,"Malik bin Dinar narrates: When the sons of Sayyiduna Mahzura finished giving the call to prayer, I followed them to Masjid Haram (the minaret) and I said to them: Tell me about the call to prayer that your father gave in front of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. \Ashhad in Laala ila Allah", Ashhad in Muhammad Rasoolullah, Hai Ali Salwa," Hai Ali Falah\"" read this once and then read these words again: \""Ashhad in Laala ila Allah","\"" Ashhad in Laala ila Allah", Ashhad in Muhammad Rasoolullah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasoolullah," until at the end of the Adhan recite these words: \""Allah Akbar Allah Akbar Laala Ala Allah\"" Narrator Dawood is unique in narrating this tradition."""
949,Sayyiduna Abu Mahzoora (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) taught him these words of the Adhan. \Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar Ashhad in laala ila Allah," \""Ashhad in Laala ila Allah", Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah, Ashhad in Muhammad Rasulullah," \"". Then he said it again: Ashhad in laala ila Allah: these words were two times: Ashhad in Muhammad Rasoolullah: these words were also twice", Hai Ali al-Salaw, these words were also two kinds," Hai Ali al Falah."""
950,"Aswad narrates that Syedna Bilal's call to prayer used to end with these words: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Laala illa Allah."
951,Aswad narrates: The last words of Sayyiduna Bilal's Adhan were: Laala ila Allah.
952,"Aswad narrated this about Sayyiduna Bilal: At the end of Sayyiduna Bilal's Adhan, these words were used: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar laalaala illa Allah."
953,Aswad narrates: Sayyiduna Bilal used to say these words at the end of the adhan: Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar Laala ila Allah.
954,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: Once Sayyiduna Bilal gave the call to prayer before dawn, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him: He should go back and announce three times: Beware, the servant has slept (i.e., he has made a mistake). He went back and said in a loud voice: Beware, the servant had slept. Another narrator has followed him, but this narrator is weak."
955,"Narrated by Nafi': Sayyiduna Umar's muezzin, whose name was Masruh, gave the call to prayer in the morning before he became righteous, then Sayyiduna Umar ordered him."
956,Ayyub narrates: Once Sayyiduna Bilal gave the call to prayer at night. This tradition is transmitted.
957,"Hameed bin Hilal narrates: Once Sayyiduna Bilal gave the call to prayer at night, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him: He should go back to his place and proclaim loudly: Beware! Surely the servant had fallen asleep (i.e. he made a mistake) so he went back, Sayyiduna Bilal Radiyallahu Anhu said: I wish Bilal's mother had not given birth to him."
958,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Once Sayyidna Bilal (RA) gave the call to prayer before dawn, and the Prophet (PBUH) got angry and ordered him to say: Verily, the servant had fallen asleep, and Bilal (RA) felt very sorry for him. In this hadith, the narrator named Aamir is delusional. The correct tradition is the one that has passed before him. It is narrated by the narrator named Ibn Harb on the authority of Nafi regarding the muezzin of Sayyiduna Umar."
959,"Sayyidna Anas (RA) narrates: Once Sayyidna Bilal (RA) gave the call to prayer before dawn, and the Prophet (PBUH) ordered him: Go back and announce: Verily, the servant was asleep. Narrator Abu Yusuf is unique in narrating this tradition."
960,"Qatadah narrates: Once Sayyiduna Bilal gave the call to prayer, his chain of transmission does not mention Sayyiduna Anas Radi Allahu Anhu."
961,"Hasan al-Basri narrates the statement of Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA): Once Sayyidna Bilal (RA) gave the call to prayer, then the Prophet (PBUH) ordered him to repeat it again, then Sayyidna Bilal (RA) climbed the minaret and he was saying, “I wish Bilal’s Maan would cry for him and his forehead became sweaty. He repeated, then when the morning dawned, he gave the call to prayer. The narrator of this tradition, Muhammad bin Qasim Asadi, is very weak."
962,"Muhammad bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his uncle Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to adopt different forms, but he had not yet adopted any of them. Bilal gave the call to prayer, Sayyiduna Abdullah narrates, I was looking at him, I wanted to give it myself, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You say Iqamah.\"""""
963,The same hadith is narrated from Sayyidina Abdullah bin Zayd on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad along with another chain of transmission.
964,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are two days in which you should not fast and two hours in which you should not pray, because Christians and Jews seek (worship) at that time. is)."
965,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After the dawn (in Nawafil) only Durkaat (i.e. Fajr prayers) will be performed.
966,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates: We attended the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa before the morning prayer. One day we attended her service and she was performing the prayer at that time. We asked her: Which prayer is this? So they replied, I had slept at night, and could not pay some Nawafal, so I did not want to abandon them."
967,"Amr Shaibani narrates: The owner of this house told us this while pointing to the house of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, but he did not mention his name: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, which deed is more virtuous. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To perform the prayer at its initial time. I asked, then which one? You said, Jihad in the way of Allah, I inquired: Then which one? You said to treat parents well. (Sayyidna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says) If I had asked you more, you would have given me more answers."
968,Abu Amr Shaybani narrates this from a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked which deed is more virtuous. So you said that the most virtuous deed is to perform the prayer at its time. A hadith has these words: The prayer is to be offered at its earliest time.
969,"Abu Amr Shaibani narrates: The owner of this house narrated this hadith to me. He means Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud. He said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
970,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best deed is to perform the prayer at its earliest time.
971,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked which deed is more virtuous. So he said: To perform the prayer at its initial time. A group of Muhadditheen have narrated contrary to it.
972,Sayyida Umm Farah (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: The most excellent deed in the sight of Allah is to perform the prayer at its earliest time.
973,Sayyidah Umm Farooah narrates: I asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deed is more virtuous? So he said: To perform the prayer at its initial time.
974,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it also mentions this: Sayyidah Umm Farah (may God be pleased with her) is one of the women who pledged allegiance to the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under a tree."
975,Sayyida Umm Farah (may Allah be pleased with her) is one of the young women who accepted Islam at the behest of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She narrates: One day I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning the deeds.
976,Sayyidah Umm Farah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked. I was listening to this.
977,Sayyidah Umm Farah (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: The most beloved deed to Allah is to perform the prayer at its earliest time. These words of the tradition are from a narrator named Umari.
978,Qasim bin Ghannam narrates this regarding the woman who accepted Islam on the hand of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked which deed is more virtuous/so he said: Faith in Allah. You said to perform the prayer at its time.
979,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person who performs the prayer within its time but does not perform it in its early time (the person who performed the prayer) is better for that person than his family and wealth.
980,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never offered the last prayer during his life until he passed away, only twice."
981,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never offered the last prayer until he passed away.
982,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa narrates: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing any prayer at the last hour until he passed away.
983,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Performing the prayer at the beginning of the prayer is a cause of obtaining the pleasure of Allah, and performing the prayer at the last time is a cause of forgiveness from Allah."
984,Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first time of the prayer is the cause of Allah's approval and the last time is the cause of Allah's forgiveness.
985,"Ibrahim bin Abd al-Malik narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first time (of prayer) is the pleasure of God, the middle time is the mercy of God, and the last time is the forgiveness of God."
986,"Ibn Shihab narrates: Once Umar bin Abdulaziz was sitting on the pulpit (i.e. giving a sermon) and he delayed the Asr prayer a little. Tawrah bin Zubair said: Sayyidna Jibraeel told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of prayer. Umar bin Abdulaziz said to him: Try to understand what you are saying. Yes, they say: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrating this. He said this. I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Once Gabriel (PBUH) came down and told me about the time of prayer. I prayed with him, then I prayed (the next prayer) with him. (Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates:) I remember this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to perform the Zuhr prayer when the sun was setting, but when it was hot, he used to postpone this prayer. Then he could reach Dhu al-Halifa before sunset. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set. He used to offer the Isha prayer when the horizon darkened. (The narrator says: There are these words in a hadith) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the morning prayer sometimes in the dark and sometimes in the light, but after that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started performing it in the dark and this was the norm until the death of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
987,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: When he prayed Asr, the sun was bright and high. If a person walked, after finishing the prayer, he could reach Dhul-Hulaifah, which was six miles away, and he could reach there before sunset. In this tradition, there are also these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the morning prayer in the dark, then one day the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform it in the light as well (but after that he adopted the habit of performing it in the dark) again. He never performed this prayer in the light and this was his routine until the death of the Prophet (PBUH)."
988,"Dashim bin Abdullah Nakhai narrated: We were sitting with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) in the Grand Mosque, Kufa was special in those days, the muezzin came to him and said: Amir al-Mu’minin: It is time for Asr prayer. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, “Sit down.” He sat down. After finishing, they came back and sat in the same place, where they were sitting earlier, then we got up on our knees and tried to check that the sun had not set. The narrator of this hadith, Ziyad bin Abdullah Nakhai, is unknown, only a narrator named Abbas has narrated the hadith regarding him."
989,"Abdul Wahid bin Nafi narrates, I entered the mosque of Madinah Munawwarah and the muezzin gave the Asr call. The narrator narrates that there was an old man sitting there. He reprimanded the muezzin and said: My father told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to instruct me to perform this prayer with delay. He is the son of Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij). Imam Darqutni (may Allah have mercy on him) said: These sons of Sayyidna Rafi are not strong. A narrator named Musa bin Ismail, narrating this hadith, has stated this: His surname was Abur Mah, similarly there is a difference of opinion about his name."
990,"It is narrated about Abd al-Rahman bin Rafi: Once the muezzin gave the adhan for Asr, he gave the adhan a little early, so Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Rafi reprimanded him and said: May you be in trouble! My father (who was a Sahabi Rasool) has told me this: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has ordered the people to delay the Asr prayer. This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads, while the opposite is narrated from some other Companions, it proves that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed to perform the Asr prayer early."
991,"Abu Najashi narrates: Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) narrated this hadith to me. He says: We used to perform Asr prayer with the Prophet (PBUH) and then a camel would be sacrificed, its meat would be cut into ten parts and then not cooked, and before sunset we would eat the roasted meat. The name of the narrator named Abu Najashi is Atta bin Suhaib, he is trustworthy and famous, he was in the service of Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij for six years, Ikramah bin Ammar, Imam Uza'i, Ayyub and others have narrated hadiths regarding him. The tradition narrated by this narrator, which is narrated by Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij, is better than the tradition, which is narrated by a narrator named Abdul Wahid, regarding the son of Sayyidna Rafi', and Allah knows best."
992,"Narrated ``Urwa: I heard Sayyidna Bashir bin Abu Mas'ud narrating: Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Asr prayer, the sun was bright and high."
993,"Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) narrates, The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Should I not tell you about the prayer of a hypocrite, he keeps postponing Asr prayer until he performs it like a cow's face is slaughtered?"
994,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer the Asr prayer when the sun was still high and bright, and a person would go to a nearby area of Madinah and reach there, and the sun was still high. This tradition has been narrated by Sayyiduna Anas with reference to some other narrators."
995,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Asr prayer, then a person would go to the Quba."
996,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I offered Asr prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the sun was still bright, then I came to my family and they were sitting there. I said: Why are you people sitting?"
997,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) taught us the Asr prayer while the sun was still bright and shining, then I came to my family, they were sitting on the edge of Madinah, they had not prayed yet, I said: Why are you sitting?"
998,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The most distant from the Ansar was the house of Sayyidna Abul Baba, who was in Quba and the house of Abu Umays, who was in the neighborhood of Banu Haritha. These two men used to pray in the lead of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then they reached their respective places."
999,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the hypocrite, he keeps looking at the sun, until when the sun turns yellow and reaches between the two horns of Satan, that person gets up and bows four times, and he mentions Allah very little in this prayer."
1000,This same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him).
1001,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Asr prayer while the sun was still in my room and the shadow was not falling.
1002,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I performed the Asr prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (SAW). I have a camel and I want to sacrifice it. I want you to be there, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed from there and we also walked. Then the camel was sacrificed and then it was prepared for us, so we ate its meat before the sun set. used to"
1003,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Asr prayer. When we had finished praying, a man belonging to Banusalma came to his service and said: O Messenger of Allah, we want to sacrifice a camel. That the camel was not yet sacrificed, it was sacrificed again, then its meat was prepared and cooked again, so we ate it before sunset."
1004,Abu Qalaba says: Asr is named because it is squeezed.
1005,"Khalid al-Thuqa narrated: Hasan al-Basri, Ibn Sirin and Abu Qalaba used to perform Asr late."
1006,Muhammad bin Hanafiyah says: Asr is named because it is squeezed.
1007,"Once Taus performed the Asr prayer late, and when he was asked about it, he said: Asr is named because it is squeezed."
1008,Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah used to perform Asr prayer late.
1009,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Gabriel (Peace be upon him) came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) when the sun had set and said: O Muhammad (Peace be upon him): Get up and offer the Zuhr prayer. Then some time passed so that when a person's shadow became as big as his own, he came to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the time of Asr and said: O Sayyidna Muhammad, get up and offer the Asr prayer. He performed this prayer when the sun had completely set, then some time passed until the twilight left, then Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Get up and offer the Isha prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) got up and he offered this prayer. Sayyidna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got up and prayed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got up and offered the morning prayer. The next day, Sayyidna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at noon when the shadow of the man had become as large as him, and said: O Sayyidna Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Get up and offer the Zuhr prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got up and offered the Zuhr prayer, then Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to him when the shadow of a man had doubled and said: O Muhammad, get up and offer the Asr prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) got up and offered the Asr prayer. It was the same time (there was no delay in it). He said: Get up and offer the Maghrib prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Maghrib prayer. Then Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) for the Isha prayer when a third of the night had passed and he said: Get up and offer the Isha prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) offered this prayer, then the Prophet He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the morning prayer when the light had spread well, and said: Get up and offer the morning prayer."
1010,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
1011,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Gabriel (PBUH) came to the Prophet (PBUH) to tell him about the prayer. He came to him when the sun had set. (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to you when the shadow of a man became equal to his height. Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) went ahead. The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood behind him and the people stood behind him. They stood behind him and the people stood behind the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they offered Maghrib prayer. After that, he mentioned the rest of the hadith, but it contains these words: The next day, Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun had set, that was the same time. At the end of this tradition is this: Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) said: There is a time (shari'a of prayers) between these two prayers. Peace be upon him said: Where is the person who inquires about prayer? Between these two (times) is the time for prayer."
1012,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Gabriel led me in prayer twice in Makkah, after which he mentioned the hadith, in which his words are: And performed the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, and performed the Maghrib prayer the next day at the same time as the previous day."
1013,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person came and asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the times of prayers. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered prayers at both times, one day at this time and one day at that time. Between these two times is (the specific time of prayers)."
1014,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Gabriel led me to prayer twice at the House of Allah, after which he mentioned the entire hadith in which he narrated the following about the second day: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said) He taught me the Maghrib prayer at the time when the fasting person breaks his fast. This was the same time."
1015,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Jibraeel (peace be upon him) attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and offered all the prayers in two times, except for the Maghrib prayer (reading at the same time)."
1016,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him."
1017,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated this: Jibreel (peace be upon him) led me in prayer twice in Makkah. The first time he came to me, then he mentioned the times of prayer (following this in the hadith are these words): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He came to me when the sun had set."
1018,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me when the morning had dawned (after that the narrator mentioned the entire hadith). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about Maghrib prayer: Then he came to me when the sun had set and said: Get up and offer the Maghrib prayer, so I offered three rakats of the Maghrib prayer. The narrator has mentioned this tradition as a long hadith."
1019,Sayyidna Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir may Allah have mercy on him) that he did not delay the Maghrib prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with food or any other busyness.
1020,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him). I asked Sayyidna Jabir about delaying Maghrib prayer because of dinner. Sayyidna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not delay the Maghrib prayer because of eating or doing anything else."
1021,Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Pray Maghrib before the stars rise.
1022,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah when the sun had set. The narrators narrated that he offered four rak'ahs of prayer in which he did not recite aloud. The people continued to follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and continued to pray following the example of Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace be upon him). followed the prayer of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and continued to pray following the example of Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace be upon him), then some time passed until the sun set, so he led the people in three rak'ahs, of which he recited aloud in the first two rak'ahs and did not recite aloud in the third rak'ah. He recited aloud and did not recite aloud in the last two rak'ahs, then some time passed until dawn dawned, so he led the people to pray two rak'ahs and they recited aloud in those two rak'ahs."
1023,This tradition is transmitted as a Mursal tradition along with another Sanad.
1024,"Sayyiduna Majma bin Jariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the timings of the prayers, so he first offered the prayers at the beginning time, then he offered the prayers at the last time, and said: There is a time for the prayers between these two."
1025,"The sons of Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud (RA) narrate this on the authority of their father: Sayyidna Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) when the sun had set. Then Sayyiduna Gabriel (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun had set, and said: Get up and offer the prayer."
1026,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It was Gabriel (PBUH) who came to teach you about your religion, then he prayed. After that, the narrator has mentioned a tradition related to the times of the prayers, in which the words are: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set."
1027,"This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the next day and offered him the Maghrib prayer at the same time when the sun had set and when it becomes permissible for a fasting person to break his fast."
1028,"Muhammad bin Ammar has narrated this about Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA), he mentioned that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) told him: Sayyidna Gabriel (PBUH) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and offered all the prayers at different times, except for Maghrib (prayer at the same time). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He came to me at Maghrib and prayed for me when the sun had set, then he came to me (i.e. the narrator says: the next day)."
1029,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: When the prayer became obligatory, Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and led him the Zuhr prayer. After that, the narrator mentioned the times of the prayers, in which these words are said: Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) led the Prophet (peace be upon him) in Maghrib prayer when the sun had set. He led the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Maghrib prayer when the sun had set."
1030,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is a beginning time for prayer and a final time. The beginning time of Zuhr is when the sun sets and the last time is when Asr begins. The beginning time of Asr is when it begins and the last time is when the sun turns yellow. The first time of Isha is when the twilight disappears and the last time is when half of the night has passed. This tradition is not authentic as a Musnad, other narrators have quoted it as a Mursal tradition regarding Mujahid."
1031,Mujahid narrates: It has been stated: There is a beginning time for prayer and a final time.Then he mentioned this hadith.
1032,"The same hadith is narrated by Mujahid along with another chain of transmission from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but it has these words: The early time of Asr is when the sun is shining until the time of Maghrib comes."
1033,"Sulaiman Bin Burida narrates this statement of his father: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the time of prayer. Then he commanded them, they said Iqamah for Asr while the sun was still high and bright, then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded them, so they said Iqamah for Maghrib when the sun had set, then under the command of the Prophet, they said Iqamah for the Isha prayer when the twilight had set, then under the command of the Prophet, they said Iqamah for the Fajr prayer when the morning had risen. was When the second day came, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to perform the Zuhr prayer at a cool time, so they performed it at a cool time, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon them) instructed them to perform Iqamah for Asr while the sun was still high, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed this prayer a little later than on the previous day. At that time, when the twilight had not yet set, then under the command of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said Iqamah for Fajr, when the light had spread, then the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, inquired: Where is the person who asks about the time of prayer? So the person answered him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your prayer times are between the two that you have seen."
1034,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1035,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1036,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to stand for the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, and then ordered them to stand for the Maghrib prayer the next day when the twilight had not yet set."
1037,"Abu Bakr bin Musa narrates this incident of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father: A man came to his service and asked him about the times of the prayers. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him. According to him, he said Iqamah for Zuhr prayer when the sun had set, and a person used to guess whether it was noon or not, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more knowledge about it. According to the order of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said Iqamah for the Isha prayer at the time when the twilight had set. Then the next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Fajr prayer. When he finished the prayer, a person could say that the sun had risen or was about to rise. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Maghrib prayer until it was a little before sunset, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer until a third of the night had passed."
1038,"Abu Bakr bin Abu Musa narrates the following statement from his father, Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash’ari (RA): A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked him about the prayers, but he did not give him any answer. According to him, he said Iqamah for Zuhr prayer at the time when a person thinks that the sun has set or has not yet set, by the way, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has more knowledge about it. Iqamah was said for Isha prayer at the time when the twilight had set. The narrator narrates: The next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Fajr prayer at a time when people thought that the sun had risen or had not yet risen. Well, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew more about this. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Zuhr prayer at the time when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Asr prayer on the first day. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Maghrib prayer shortly before the sunset, then he offered the Isha prayer after a third of the night had passed, then he inquired, \Where is the questioner?\"" Between these two times is the time (of prayers)."""
1039,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Musa, on the authority of his father. \So he said Iqamah for the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set","\"" says the narrator. Then the next day"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Maghrib prayer until the twilight was about to set. A narrator named Qazi has similarly narrated it as a short tradition."""
1040,"Abdullah bin Burida narrates the statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In addition to the Maghrib prayer, two rak'ahs (Nafl Yasunat) will be performed between Harazan and Iqamah."
1041,"Hayan bin Ubaidullah Adwi narrates: Once we were sitting with Hazrat Abdullah bin Burida, may Allah be pleased with him, and the muezzin gave the adhan for the Zuhr prayer. The Rak'ats will be performed. Abdullah Bin Burida says: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar performing these two Rak'ats even at Maghrib. He would not abandon them under any circumstances. The narrator narrates: We got up and we prayed two rak'ahs before Iqamah, then we waited until the Imam came, then we performed the obligatory prayer following him. Husain Mualim, Saeed Jariri, Kahams bin Hasan, have narrated traditions contrary to him, all these narrators are reliable, while the narrator named Hayan bin Ubaidullah is not very authentic; the rest is known to Allah."
1042,"Abdullah bin Burida narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah Muzni. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: perform two rak'ahs of Nawafil before the Maghrib duties. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him) says: This hadith is more authentic than the previous one."
1043,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, “The Nafl prayer will be offered between the Azan and the Iqamah,” (he repeated this sentence twice) and then he said, “This order is for him who does not want to gamble.”"
1044,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever wants to perform the Nafl prayer between the Adhan and Iqamah.
1045,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Burida (RA) narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (PBUH) said that the Nafl prayer should be performed between the Azan and the Iqamah.
1046,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said that two rak'ahs (Sunnah Yanfal) should be performed before every obligatory prayer. These words are from a narrator named Ibn Dawud: A narrator named Ismail has quoted the word, mafuruzat, instead of the word, maktuba."
1047,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sometimes a stranger would enter the mosque of Madinah and people were praying there at Maghrib, so it was felt that the people had already prayed (in congregation), because there were so many people who prayed two rak'ahs before the Maghrib prayer."
1048,"Abd al-Aziz Lebanese narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik narrating that it was the custom of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that when the muezzin gave the Maghrib call to prayer, they would rush to the pillars to pray two rak'ahs before Maghrib."
1049,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Companions heard the Maghrib call to prayer, they would get up and perform Nawafil as if it were obligatory."
1050,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to perform Dunaafal before Maghrib. The narrator narrates: We asked Sayyiduna Anas: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see you people performing this prayer? So Sayyiduna Anas said: The Prophet has seen us perform this prayer, but he did not order us to perform it, nor did he ever forbid it."
1051,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may God be pleased with him) narrates: It was our custom in Madinah when the Maghrib call to prayer was given, we people would quickly move towards the pillars and pray two rak'ahs (as Nawafil before the obligatory prayer) until a stranger would enter the mosque and he would feel that perhaps the prayer had been offered, because there were a large number of those who offered these two rak'ahs."
1052,"Shaykh Abul Khair narrates: Shaykh Abu Tamim Jaishani got up and started offering two rak'ahs before Maghrib prayer, so I said to Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir: Pay attention to them: Which prayer are they praying? Sayyiduna Uqbah turned to him and said: This is the prayer we used to perform during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
1053,"Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are two types of righteous morning, one is the righteous morning which spreads (in the width direction) like the tail of a snake. is) and forbids eating for the person who breaks the fast (i.e., the time for the fast ends at that time)."
1054,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) and Sayyidna Shaddad Bin Aws (RA) said: There are two types of twilight, red and white. When the reddish twilight sets, it is time for prayer, and in the same way, morning dawn is of two types, one with length and one with width. When the width ends, then the time for prayer begins."
1055,Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Shafaq is called red.
1056,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this, \Shafaq\"" means red", when Shafaq sets, the prayer becomes obligatory (i.e.," its time begins)."""
1057,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Shafaq refers to redness.
1058,"Sayyiduna Numan bin Basheer (RA) narrates: I have the most knowledge about the Isha prayer at this time, the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform it when the moon sets on the third night."
1059,"The same hadith has been narrated about the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: (The narrator is in doubt) The moon of the third night or the moon of the fourth night (used to set). Some other narrators have also narrated it on the authority of Sayyiduna Nu'man (RA), and they have quoted in it the words, the moon of the third night:"
1060,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (according to Madinah Munawarah): The place between the east and the west is the Qiblah.
1061,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (according to Madinah Munawarah): The place between the east and the west is the Qiblah.
1062,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) sent out an expedition. I was also present in it. Once, in extreme darkness, we could not figure out the direction of the Qibla. So many of us said: \We have guessed the Qibla"," it is like this.\"" What was it", they drew a line in this direction. When the morning came and the sun rose, those two lines were not in the direction of Qiblah. When we returned from our journey and we inquired about it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent," so Allah revealed this verse. \""The East and the West belong to Allah", wherever you turn," Allah's presence will be there.\"" It means that wherever you are."""
1063,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this verse was specifically revealed about the Nafl prayer, that is, whichever way your riding is, you can pray facing that way."
1064,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: We were on a journey with the Prophet (PBUH) and during that time it became dark, we were very worried and there was a disagreement between us about the Qiblah. Each of us prayed facing our favorite direction and some people also marked a mark in front of us so that we would remember our place. Diya, you said this, your prayer has been correct. It is narrated in the same way on the authority of a narrator named Muhammad bin Salim, while some other narrators have narrated it from another chain of transmission and both of these narrators are weak."
1065,Abdullah bin Aamir narrates this statement of his father: Once during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we prayed on a very dark night during a journey. We did not know which direction the Qibla was facing. \Wherever you are," God's presence will be there.\"""""
1066,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Each of us prayed facing the stones in front of us. When morning came, our direction was not towards the Qiblah."
1067,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1068,"Sayyiduna Malik bin Hawairat (RA) narrates: We came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), we were young people, our ages were close to each other, and we stayed in his service for twenty days. People, now go back to your homes, and stay there, educate these people, treat them well, just as you saw me praying, continue to pray in the same way, when it is time for prayer, one of you should give the call to prayer, and the one who is older among you should lead you."
1069,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Malik bin Haweerith along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \You people should pray in the same way as you have seen me praying.\"""""
1070,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when three men are together, one of them should lead them, (i.e. they should perform the prayer in congregation) and the one who can recite the Qur’aat well (or memorizes the most verses) will be more entitled to lead the prayer."
1071,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once some people were performing the morning prayer in the Kaaba, while a person came to them and said: Last night, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received the order of the Qur’an. You should also turn towards it (the narrator says) At that time, these people were facing towards Syria (i.e. Bayt al-Maqdis), so they turned around and started facing the Kaaba (praying) at that time."
1072,"Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: After the arrival of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, for about sixteen months, we people followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by turning towards Bait-ul-Maqdis and praying. \We see your face rising towards the sky", we will turn you towards the Qiblah which you are satisfied with," so you turn your face towards Masjid Haram\"". So Allah commanded the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Turn your face towards the Kaaba (the narrator says:) A man passed by us"," we were facing towards the Holy Place and praying."""
1073,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: A person announced on behalf of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the Kaaba has been made the Qiblah (the narrator says).
1074,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'idi (may God be pleased with him) narrates: When the Kaaba was made the Qiblah, a person passed by the people living in the Kaabah, who were praying at that time."
1075,Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) used to perform the Isha prayer following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) and then he would go back to his neighborhood and lead those people in prayer.
1076,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) used to perform the Isha prayer following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), and then he would go back to his neighborhood and lead those people in prayer."
1077,"Abd al-Malik bin Rabi', on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the prayer in the pen of camels, but he permitted the prayer in the pen of the goats. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id has said these words: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has commanded us: We should pray in the sheepfolds, and you have forbidden us in this regard, we should pray in the camel folds."
1078,"Abd al-Malik bin Rabi', on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in the sheep pen, do not pray in the camel pen."
1079,Abd al-Malik Ibn Rabi' narrated his grandfather's statement on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying in the pen of camels.
1080,"Sayyidina Yazid bin Aamir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to me: When you (come to the mosque) for prayer and find people praying, pray with them."
1081,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person came. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished praying at that time. He got up and began to pray alone. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will cooperate with him? He should perform this prayer with him (again).
1082,"Sayyiduna Asma bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was sitting in the mosque after performing the Zuhr prayer, while a person came in and began to pray. The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Would anyone get up and do good to him so that he could pray with him?\"""""
1083,"Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When there are two people, they should stand together and pray, and if there are three, then one of them should go ahead."
1084,"Sayyidah Umm Waraqah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave them this permission, that the Adhan should be given for them and Iqamah should be called for them, and that they should lead the women (i.e. lead them in congregational prayer)."
1085,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam of the people should be the one who migrated first. Don't lead him and don't sit in his designated place, but he can sit with his permission. (The narrator narrates): At the beginning of the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our shoulders."
1086,"Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The person who knows the Qur'an more should lead the people."
1087,Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Two or more people are a congregation.
1088,Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men and more people are a congregation (i.e. they should pray in congregation).
1089,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: No villager, no foreigner, and no minor boy should stand in the first row."
1090,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The rules of the Sunnah include that when the Imam returns the salam, he should not stand and offer Nawafl at the same place where a person has performed the obligatory prayer, but rather move away from there to one side or perform Nawafl by talking in between."
1091,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A person stood up and asked, O Messenger of Allah: Can a person pray in one piece of cloth? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \All of you people have two clothes?\"" The narrator narrates: During the time of Sayyiduna Umar", a person stood in front of him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, can a person pray wearing a piece of cloth? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: When Allah has given you room, you should also give yourself room. Narrator narrates: After that, that person used to pray by wearing an apron and covering it with a chador, wearing a yaqmeez and wearing an apron, wearing a quba over the yashalwar and wearing a yashalwar over the chador and wearing a yashalwar and wearing a yaqba over the shirt. The narrator has doubts: perhaps these words are: He used to pray wearing a pajama and a shirt, or wearing a pajama and wrapping a chador over it," or wearing a pajama and wearing a Qabaa on top."""
1092,"Urwa bin Mughirah narrated this statement of his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Prophet died until a person from his people led him. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him, says this) A narrator of this hadith, Ibn Abu Umayyah, is not authentic."
1093,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) turned to the people and said: Straighten your ranks. The Prophet (PBUH) said this three times. (Says the narrator) So I saw every person next to him shin with his shin, his knee with his shoulder, his shoulder with his shoulder (i.e. trying to make the row perfectly straight)."
1094,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to hold his left hand with his right hand during prayer.
1095,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: There are three things (in the routines of Prophethood): breaking the fast early, making the Suhoor late, and placing the right hand over the left during prayer."
1096,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: We (i.e.) the Prophets have been commanded: We should break the fast early, make the suhoor late, and place our right hands over our left hands during prayer."
1097,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): We Prophets have been commanded to delay Suhoor and break fast and keep our right hands over our left hands during prayer.
1098,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says that it is Sunnah to place one hand over the other during prayer.
1099,Sayyidna Ali (RA) says: (Allah is the guide) So pray for your Lord and sacrifice.
1100,Qabaisa bin Halab narrates this statement of his father: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right hand on his left hand during prayer.
1101,Alqamah bin Wail Hazrami narrates the statement of his father: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right hand on his left hand during prayer.
1102,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is Sunnah to place one hand on the other hand below the navel during prayer.
1103,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Among the sunnahs of prayer, this is also included, placing the right hand on the left hand below the navel."
1104,"Alqamah bin Wail narrated this statement from his father: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stood up to pray, and he held (the wrist) of his left hand with his right hand."
1105,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me. I was placing my left hand on my right hand during prayer, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) took my right hand and placed it on my left."
1106,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a gentleman who had his left hand on his right hand (after this is according to the previous hadith).
1107,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him. He was praying at that time. He was placing his left hand on his right hand.
1108,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for prayer, he would say this and that about the right and the left, and then he would say: Keep (the row) straight and be equal."
1109,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up for prayer, he would say Takbeer and raise both hands up to his shoulders. When he finished his recitation and started bowing, he would do the same. When he rose from Bowing, he would do the same again. After that, he would not bow during the prayer. When he was sitting, when he would stand up after performing two Rak'ahs, then he would bow and say Takbeer in the same way. would say"
1110,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would raise both his hands until they were at the level of his shoulders, then he would say Takbeer, then when he started to bow down, he would do it, then when he raised his head from bowing, he would do it."
1111,"Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would stand for prayer, he would raise both of his hands until they both came against his shoulders, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say Takbeer with him, then when he started to bow, he would raise them both until they both came against his shoulders, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go into bowing. When he got up, he would raise both of them until they were facing his shoulders, then he would recite, Sama'Allah Liman Hamda, then the Prophet (PBUH) would go into prostration."
1112,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) stand up to pray, then he raised both his hands until they both came to his shoulders, then he said Takbeer, and he did the same when he raised his blessed head from Ruku, then he recited, ``Sama'Allah Liman Hamda'', but when he raised his head from Sajdah, the Prophet (PBUH) did not do so at that time."
1113,"The same hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) is present along with another chain of transmission, it has these words: He performed Rifa Yaddin and then said Takbeer."
1114,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to pray, he would raise both his hands until they reached the level of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shoulders and he would say Takbeer (after that, according to the previous hadith)."
1115,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise both his hands until they were equal to or close to his shoulders (after that he narrated according to the previous hadith).
1116,"The same hadith is narrated from Zahri along with another chain of transmission, in which there are these words: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Takbeer at the beginning of the prayer, he would raise both hands while he was saying Takbeer, until those two hands came to the level of his shoulders (after that, according to the previous hadith)."
1117,"Salim narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for prayer, he would raise both his hands up to his shoulders and say Takbeer, then when he started to bow, he would raise his hands to his shoulders and say Takbeer. Laiya who narrated his praise) then you would go into prostration, you would not perform Rifa Yadeen between Prostrations, you would perform Rifa Yadeen while saying Takbeer in every rak'at when you would say Takbeer before going into Ruku until your prayer was complete (ie you used to do this during the whole prayer)."
1118,"Narrated by Nafi': When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) saw a person who bowed down while praying and did not make rifa'idin, he used to pick him up to hit him with pebbles until that person started making rifa'idin."
1119,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bow down while bowing at the beginning of the prayer. This hadith has been narrated only by Abd al-Wahhab as an authentic hadith on the authority of Hameed.
1120,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of the prayer, he bowed his hands until both of his hands were at the level of his shoulders, then when he started to bow (he did so), then when he raised his head (he did it at that time), he (while sitting) placed his right hand on his right knee and his left hand on his left knee. (of the right hand) made a circle and pointed thus, the narrator named Sufyan said by pointing with his index finger. The narrator narrates: I attended the service of these gentlemen (i.e. the Companions) and I found them in such a state that they used to pray in the cold season even with a cloak over them."
1121,"Hussain bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: We attended the service of Ibrahim Nakhai, and Amr bin Marwah told him this. So Ibrahim Nakhai said: I understand that your father must have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing this for only one day, and he would have remembered this, so did Sayyidna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) not remember this? After that, Ibrahim Nakhai said: Rifa Yaddin will be done only at the beginning of the prayer."
1122,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) going into Ruku at the beginning of the prayer, and when he recited Samaa Allah Liman Hamda (i.e. getting up from Ruku) he raised both his hands to his ears (i.e. raised his hands)."
1123,"Sayyidna Malik bin Hawairat (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform Rifa Yadeen at the beginning of the prayer, while going into Ruku, and when he raised his head from Ruku. A narrator named Ibn Mubashir narrated these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bow at the beginning of the prayer, then when he started bowing, when he raised his head from bowing (even then he bowed). A narrator named Abu Awana has narrated this: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the Takbeer, he raised his hands up to his shoulders, when he went into the bow, when he raised his head from the bow, and when he recited, Sama'Allah Liman Hamda."
1124,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said, \Shall I show you the way of prayer of the Prophet (PBUH)?\"" Then he said Takbeer and raised both hands", then said Takbeer and raised both hands before going into Ruku, then recited Sama'Allah Liman Hamda, then raised both hands (after finishing the prayer) He said," \""You people do the same.\"" (The narrator says:) He did not perform rifa-yedeen between the two prostrations."""
1125,"This same hadith has been narrated in another chain of transmission from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him). The Al-Durawis have narrated it as a marfu' hadith on the authority of Hamad, while the rest of the narrators besides these two have narrated it as a muqaf tradition. I have heard Qazi Abu Ja'far saying: At first I had the same position as the people of Iraq, but then I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a dream."
1126,"Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) used to raise both his hands while saying Takbeer, we used to see that both thumbs of the Prophet (PBUH) came close to his ears."
1127,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laili narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Bara' (RA) narrating this hadith in that gathering, in which Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) was present."
1128,"Abdullah bin Mubarak says: According to me, this tradition narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, is not authentic. According to me, the hadith in which it is mentioned is authentic: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Rif Yaddin while going into Ruku and raising his head from Ruku. Abdullah bin Mubarak has narrated this: Ubaidullah Umari, Imam Malik, Muammar, Sufyan, Yunus, Muhammad bin Abu Hafsa have narrated this tradition from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Zuhri, on the authority of Salem on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar)."
1129,Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) making ablution at the beginning of the prayer.
1130,": This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, along with another chain of transmission."
1131,"Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stood up for prayer, and he said Takbeer and said, ``Refu Yadin.'' A narrator named Yazid was exhorted in his last years to recite these words: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do so, so he accepted this exhortation, the words of this tradition were confused for him."
1132,"Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet (SAW) when he stood up to pray, he (SAW) raised both hands up to his ears while saying Takbeer. Narrated Ali bin Asim: When I came to Kufa, I was told that a narrator named Yazid was alive. I went to his service and he narrated this hadith to me. I said to him: I have been told this tradition by Ibn Abi Layli, who has also quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not make ablution later, so he replied: I do not remember these words."
1133,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates: I have performed prayers following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA). A narrator named Ishaq has stated this: We will adopt this tradition about the way of praying. The narrator Muhammad bin Jabir is unique in narrating this tradition and this Sahib is weak. Muhammad bin Jabir narrated it from Ibrahim Nakhai with reference to a narrator named Hamad, while other narrators besides Hamad narrated it from Ibrahim Nakhai as a messenger tradition from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu as his own action. But he did not copy, which is related to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this tradition is correct."
1134,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) to see for myself how the Prophet (SAW) prayed. When he raised his head, he raised both hands as much. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration, he placed his two hands against the same part of his head."
1135,"This tradition is narrated from Wail bin Hajar along with another chain of transmission, but it does not mention prostration."
1136,"This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: At the beginning of the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise both hands up to his shoulders, when he (may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him) went into ruku’, and when he raised his head from ruku’, he would raise his hands in the same way."
1137,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to start the prayer, after saying the Takbeer, he would recite this dua: \I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth properly", and I am not a polytheist. My prayer, my sacrifice, my life, my death are for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds who has no partner. I have been commanded to do this and I am the first Muslim, O Allah! You are the king, there is no other god but you, so you are my Lord, I am your servant, I have wronged myself, I confess my sin, then forgive me all my sins, no one can forgive sins except you, I am present, in your presence, goodness and happiness are all in your hand, and evil cannot come to you, yes, I can do everything with your help, I turn to you, your self is blessed, you are high and superior," I ask you for forgiveness. I do and I repent before you.\"" When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into Ruku", he used to recite: O Allah! I bowed to You, I believed in You, I bowed before You, my hearing, my sight, my brain, my bones, my muscles (bowed before You). When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing," he used to recite this dua: \""Whoever recites the praise of Allah", Allah listens to his praise. O our Lord, every kind of praise is reserved for You, such that it fills the heavens and the earth, and fills the space between them," and also fills the portion that is due to you.\"" When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration"," he used to recite: \""O Allah", I prostrated before You, I accepted Islam because I believe in You, my head is bowed to the One who created it, gave it form and gave it a good form, blessed it with hearing and sight. Blessed is God," the best creator.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say this dua when he returned salam after praying: O Allah: What I have done before", what I will do later, what I will do in secret, what I have done openly, what I have done extravagantly, about which You know more than I do, so forgive me for all of these. Imam Darqutni (may God have mercy on him) narrates: This has been revealed by reference to Nazr bin Shamail," who is one of the experts in lexicography."""
1138,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite the following at the beginning of the obligatory prayer: \I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth. I have turned (toward Allah) as a Muslim, and I am not a polytheist. My prayer, my sacrifice, my life, my death are for Allah, who is the Lord of all the worlds, with whom there is no partner. I have been commanded to do this and I am a Muslim, O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, there is no god but You, You are pure, Praise is reserved for You, You are my Lord, I am Your servant, I have wronged myself, I confess my sin, so forgive me for all my sins, no one can forgive my sins except You, only You can guide me to good conduct, and remove your good conduct from me, only You can remove bad conduct from me, I am present, goodness and happiness are yours. The hand is in the power, that person is guided, whom You grant guidance, I do everything with Your help, I turn to You, You are the Blessed, the Most High," I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. The narrator has quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go into prostration in the obligatory prayer."""
1139,Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite the following when he started the prayer: \Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my life, my death is for Allah, the Lord of the worlds, with whom there is no partner. I have been commanded to do this, and I am the first Muslim, O Allah! By guiding me towards good morals and good deeds, only You can guide me towards good morals and good deeds, save me from bad morals and bad deeds, only You can save me from them. Narrated Shuaib: Muhammad bin Munkadir and other jurists said to me: It would be better if you read these words too," and I am a Muslim. These words of tradition are from a narrator named Abdul Kareem."""
1140,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) used to stand up at night to offer Nawafil, after saying Takbeer at the beginning of the prayer, he used to recite: \So pure", O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, blessed is Your name, Exalted is You," there is no god but You. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite these words three times: \""I seek refuge in Allah", the All-Hearing and All-Knowing, from the rejected Satan," his whispers and tricks."""
1141,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this at the beginning of the prayer: \So pure, O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed, Your honor is high and superior, There is no god but You. And Imam Abu Dawud has stated this, this hadith has been narrated only by Talaq bin Ghannam with reference to a narrator named Abdul Salam," and this hadith is not authentic."""
1142,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab: When the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to say Takbeer for prayer, he would recite: \So pure", O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed," Your majesty is exalted and superior and there is no god but You when you used to recite Tawz. \""I seek refuge in Allah from Satan his whispers and his tricks: This saint has narrated this tradition from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Nafi", on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), but the more secure tradition is this, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) as his own saying, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah and Aswad, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Yahya bin Ayyub has quoted in his chain of transmission as the saying of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)," this is correct."""
1143,"Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: When Sayyiduna Umar said Takbeer for prayer, he used to recite this dua: You are pure, O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed, Your majesty is high and superior, and there is no god but You."
1144,"Aswad narrates this about Sayyiduna Umar: When he started the prayer, he used to recite: Glory be to You, O Allah, praise be to You, Your name is blessed, Your majesty is exalted and exalted, and there is no god but You."
1145,"Alqamah narrates, he attended the service of Sayyidna Umar ibn al-Khattab and when he saw Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, start the prayer, he recited: You are holy, O Allah."
1146,"Al-Aswad narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he started the prayer, he recited this after saying Takbeer."
1147,"The same tradition is narrated along with another document, however, these words are added to the names, after that they used to read ta'awz."
1148,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: At the beginning of the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise both his hands until his thumbs reached the level of his ears after saying the Takbeer."
1149,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this at the beginning of the prayer: So pure O Allah! Praise be to You, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, there is no god but You."
1150,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, in which these words are added: \You used to raise both your hands up to your shoulders and then read: To Paq Hai O Allah!\"""""
1151,"Al-Qamah and Aswad narrate: Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to recite the Takbeer. \So pure", O Allah! Praise be to You, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty," there is no god but You. (Sayyidna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu used to recite these words in such a loud voice) that a person standing near him could hear them."""
1152,"Ata narrates: Ubaid bin Umayr and I attended the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa. We asked her about the beginning of the Prophet's prayer, so she said: When the Prophet said the Takbeer, he used to recite: \Glory be to Allah", praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed, Your majesty is high and superior," and there is no god but You.\"""""
1153,"Aswad narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to recite: \Glory be to Allah", praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed, Your majesty is high and superior," and there is no god but You.\"" (The narrator says) Sayyiduna Umar used to recite these words aloud so that you would teach us them."""
1154,Abu Wail narrates: Syedna Uthman Ghani used to recite this dua at the beginning of the prayer: \So pure, O Allah! Praise is reserved for You, Your name is blessed," Your majesty is high and superior and there is no god but You. Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite these words to us (i.e. used to recite these words aloud)."""
1155,"Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ali Ibn Abu Talib (RA) that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful in prayer."
1156,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) used to recite Bismillah-e-Rahman-e-Raheem in a loud voice along with both surahs.
1157,"Imam Abu Ja'far Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father (Imam Baqir) regarding his father Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding his father Imam Hussain, he says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you stand up for prayer, how do you show respect? I said, I am reciting Alhamdulillah, Lord of the worlds."
1158,Sayyidna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ammar (RA) say that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Bismillah Al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice during obligatory prayers.
1159,Both Sayyidna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ammar (RA) narrated that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Bismillah Al-Rahman Al-Rahim in a loud voice.
1160,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Bismillah-e-Rahman-e-Raheem in a loud voice in prayer.
1161,"Ahmad bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father, Amirul Momineen Mahdi led us to Maghrib prayer, he recited Bismillah Rahman Al Rahim in a loud voice. The narrator says: I said: Amirul Momineen, what is this way? So he said, \My father has narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas", may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather. The narrator says," I inquired whether we can narrate it with reference to you. He replied yes."""
1162,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice at the beginning of the prayer.
1163,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) used to recite Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem, together with the two Surahs in a loud voice until he passed away."
1164,It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice and it was mentioned that the Prophet also used to recite it loudly.
1165,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Bismillah Rahman Raheem at the beginning of prayer. A narrator named Nishapuri used to recite these words.
1166,Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates that I performed prayers following the example of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA).
1167,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \When Gabriel came to me with the revelation", he first recited in front of me in the name of Allah," the Merciful.\"""""
1168,"Naeem bin Abdullah narrates: I prayed following the example of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him. He recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim, then he recited Surah Al-Fatiha until he reached this verse, Ghir al-Maghdhub alihim wala al-Dhaaleen, then he said Amen. He said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my life"," I pray better than all of you according to the way of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him). (Imam Dar Qutni says) This hadith is authentic and all its narrators are trustworthy."""
1169,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
1170,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
1171,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (SAW) used to recite recitations while teaching the people to pray, he used to start the recitation with the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated: This is a verse from the Book of Allah. If you wish, you can recite it at the beginning of the Qur’an. A narrator named Farsi narrated these words: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead the people, he used to recite Bismillah, Rahman al-Rahim, and he did not quote any other words."
1172,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Jibraeel told me the way of prayer, he got up, he said Takbeer in front of us, then he recited Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem, in this prayer, which is recited aloud, and he did not do this in every rak'ah."
1173,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this.
1174,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem in a loud voice. The correct one is Abu Mushar."
1175,"Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the same way: Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem, Al-Hamdulillah, Rabb, Al-Amin, Rahman, Raheem, Ta Wala, Al-Dhaaleen. He used to recite these verses one by one."
1176,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father (Imam Baqir), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked how you recite when you stand for prayer."
1177,"Qatadah narrates: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) was asked how the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qaraat. He replied, “It was by stretching the Qaraat."
1178,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) reciting Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem in a loud voice."
1179,"Muhammad bin Mutawakkil narrates: I have performed Fajr and Maghrib prayers so many times following the example of Mu'tamar bin Sulaiman: I cannot count them. I used to read Bismillah Rahman Raheem. I heard Mu'tamar say: I will always follow my father's way of praying, my father has narrated this."
1180,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem in a loud voice."
1181,Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Sayyidna Jibraeel led me in prayer near the Ka'ba, so he recited loudly in the name of Allah, Most Merciful," Most Merciful.\"""""
1182,"Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the sukta twice (while reciting) one sukta when he recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim and one sukta when he finished reciting. Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) did not accept this, so people wrote a letter to Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) about this, and he wrote in reply: Samra has stated correctly."
1183,"Ibn Burida narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Before leaving the mosque, I will teach you a verse (maybe the narrator doubts this word), a surah, which was revealed to me alone among the prophets who came after Sulaiman (peace be upon him). The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got up and walked, so I also followed him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the door of the mosque, he took one foot out from the door of the mosque and the other foot was still inside the mosque. What do you start with? The narrator says: I said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the same, this is the same, then you visited."
1184,"Abdullah bin Buraidah narrates this statement of his father Sayyiduna Buraidah (RA) I heard the Prophet (PBUH) reciting Bismillah Al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice. Narrated by Abdullah bin Burida: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite it aloud, likewise Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Muhammad bin Hanafyah (may Allah be pleased with him) also used to recite it aloud."
1185,Sayyiduna Haqma bin Umayr (may Allah be pleased with him) who is a Badri (companion) narrates that I prayed in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
1186,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice.
1187,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Mu'awiya (RA) prayed in Madinah, he recited it aloud, but he did not recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud, nor did he recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim before Surah Fatiha, nor did he recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim before the last Surah. His voice could reach the Muhajirin and the Ansar, who prayed and greeted them, and addressed them in a loud voice and said: O Sayyidna Muawiya, have you shortened the prayer or have you forgotten? The narrator narrates that after that he recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice in every prayer he performed, before Surah Al-Fatiha and before the Surah after Al-Fatiha (recited aloud Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim) and also recited Takbeer while prostrating. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
1188,"Ismail bin Ubaid narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Muawiya bin Abu Sufyan (RA) came to Madinah to perform Hajj or Umrah. He did not recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim (in a loud voice) at the beginning of the recitation while leading the people and started reciting Surah Fatiha. You have intentionally omitted or forgot to recite Bismillah Rahman Raheem. (The narrator narrates: When Sayyiduna Muawiya (RA) led these people in the next prayer, he recited Bismillah, Rahman, Raheem in a loud voice). Imam Dar Qutni, may God have mercy on him, narrates: In addition to the traditions that we have quoted about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim out loud, some other companions and pure wives have also narrated this. But those traditions have also been quoted which make it clear which of the Companions of the Holy Prophet and the scholars who came after them used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice."
1189,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who does not recite Surah Al-Fatiha while praying, his prayer is not complete. The narrator narrates: I said: O Sayyidna Abu Huraira! Sometimes I follow the example of the Imam, he pinched (something) on my shin and said: Then recite it in your heart, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Ta'ala says: I have divided the prayer (reciting) into two parts between myself and my servants, and half of it is for him. My servant mentioned my greatness then he says, Ayak Nabad Wayak Nasta'in, so this verse will be divided into two parts between me and my servant, the last part of the surah is for my servant and what my servant asked for he will get. The narrator named Ibn Simaan is Abdullah bin Simaan and this person is a abandoned hadeeth. A group of reliable narrators have narrated this hadith on the authority of Alaa bin Abd al-Rahman. These narrators include Imam Malik bin Anas, Shaykh Ibn Jarij, Shaykh Ruh bin Qasim, Shaykh Ibn Aayynah, Ibn Ajlan, Hasan bin Hur, Abu Wais and others. These men have quoted differences in the authenticity of this hadith, but they agree on the text. So it will be considered correct to quote all these gentlemen unanimously against the narration narrated by Ibn Samaan, Allah knows best."
1190,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you recite Alhamdulillah, Lord of the Worlds, recite Bismillah, Rahman, Rahim, because it is Umm Al-Qur’an, Umm Al-Katab, and Sabaa Mastani, and Bismillah, Rahman Al-Rahim is one of its verses."
1191,"Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qur’aat, he used to recite each verse separately. Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Umar ibn Harun narrated it on the authority of Ibn Jarij and added some additional words."
1192,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Alhamdulillah, Lord of the worlds, at the beginning of the prayer, and then he would remain silent for a while. This hadith has been narrated by the narrator named Abu Dawood only as a superior hadith with respect to Shu'ba, while other narrators have narrated it as a muwaqf tradition as the work of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."
1193,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) praying wearing shoes and wearing socks.
1194,"Abd Khair narrates that Sayyiduna Ali was asked about the seven bladders, and he said, Alhamdulillah. He said to him: Yes, these are six verses."
1195,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abu Awfi (RA) narrates: A man came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and mentioned that he could not memorize the Qur'an. A narrator named Ibn Uyaynah narrated these words: He said, O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will replace the Qur'an for me, because I cannot recite it. \Glory be to Allah. All praise is reserved for Allah and there is no god but Allah. Allah is the Greatest and nothing can happen without Allah's help.\"" The narrator narrates: He closed his fingers (remembered these words) and then said: This is for the praise of my Lord. What will happen to me (as a supplication)? Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You should make this supplication.\"" \""O Allah! So forgive me", then have mercy on me, keep me firm on the guidance, then grant me sustenance," and grant me prosperity (says the narrator)."""
1196,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abu Awfi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, \O Messenger of Allah", I cannot learn the Qur'an," so what will be sufficient for me to recite in prayer?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Read this: \""Allah's Self is pure. All praises are reserved for Allah. Nothing can happen without Allah's help. Allah is the Greatest and there is no god but Allah.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Read this. \""O Allah! So forgive me! So have mercy on me! So give me sustenance", then keep me firm on the guidance, then bless me with health. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," This person has filled both his hands with goodness (says the narrator)."""
1197,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abu Awfi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I cannot learn the Qur’an. \In the name of Allah (I begin my work receiving blessings) All praises are reserved for Allah. There is no god but Allah. Allah is the Greatest.\"""""
1198,"Ibn Abi Malikah narrates: I heard Sayyidah Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, when she was asked about a verse of the Qur'an, and she recited: I begin by seeking blessings in the name of Allah, the Most Merciful and the Most Merciful. \Those who follow what is similar to it in order to seek temptation and seek its interpretation", although its interpretation is known only to Allah, and those who have influence in knowledge say," 'We believe in it.'\"" Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when you see such people", they are the same people whom Allah has mentioned," so avoid them."""
1199,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I prayed following the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, and Sayyidna Uthman RA."
1200,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman (may God be pleased with him). The same tradition is also reported in some other isnads, but there are some word differences in it."
1201,"Sayyidna Anas (RA) narrates: I prayed following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, and Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
1202,"This tradition has also been narrated along with some other isnads, but there is some wording difference in it. This tradition has also been followed."
1203,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I prayed following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, and Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
1204,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice. Narrated by Allah Anhu.
1205,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin the recitation with Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with them) (in a loud voice during the prayer) with Alhamdulillah, Lord of the worlds."
1206,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I have prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with them)."
1207,"Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We have prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Usman Ghani."
1208,"Saeed bin Yazid Azdi narrates: I asked Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to start the recitation (in a loud voice) with Alhamdulillah, Lord of the Worlds or Bismillah, Rahman al-Raheem. (The narrator says) I inquired: Did the Prophet pray wearing shoes."
1209,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever prays with the Imam should recite Surah Al-Fatihah during the Imam's sukkah, and whoever recites the entire Surah, then it is sufficient for him to do so. A narrator named Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubayd is weak."
1210,"Yazid bin Sharik narrates: He asked Sayyiduna Umar (RA) about the issue of reciting in the imitation of the Imam, so he said, \You should recite Surah Fatiha.\"" (The narrator says) I inquired: Although (Imam) you? So he said", Although I (the Imam) am (the narrator says) I inquired, although you are reciting loudly? So he replied," Even though I am reciting loudly (still recite Surah Fatiha). All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."""
1211,"Yazid bin Sharik narrates: I inquired from Sayyiduna Umar (RA) about the issue of reciting in the imitation of the Imam, so he instructed me to recite it. The narrator says: I said: Even if you are the imam (I will recite the recitation), he replied: Even if I am the imam (then you also recite the recitation). (says the narrator) I asked, although you are reciting aloud? He replied, \Even though I am reciting it aloud"," its authority is authentic.\"""""
1212,Abdullah bin Huzail narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) should I recite the Qur'aat behind the Imam? He replied yes.
1213,"Sayyidna Mahmud bin Rabi Ansari, who was staying in Ilya, narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the morning prayer. Do it because whoever does not recite it, his prayer is not (perfect). This document is \Hasan\""."""
1214,"This same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads in the same way, but it has these words: (It seems) as if you are reciting behind me."
1215,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
1216,"This same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads, but it contains these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I think you people are reciting behind your Imam when he is reciting loudly. We said", 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah," we will recite it quickly.''"""
1217,"Sayyidna Nafi bin Mahmud narrates: Once Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived late for the morning prayer. Sayyiduna Ubadah also started reciting Surah Fatiha. (The narrator says) When he finished the prayer, I said to Sayyiduna Ubadah (RA): You have done an act about which I could not understand whether it is a Sunnah. Or did you do it by mistake? Sayyiduna Obada inquired which one he is? The narrator says, I heard you reciting Surah Al-Fatihah while Abu Na'im was reciting loudly, then Hazrat Ubada (RA) said, \That is the case. The Prophet (PBUH) led us a prayer in which it was recited loudly", so during that time he had difficulty in reciting it. When the Prophet (PBUH) finished reciting the prayer, he turned towards us and said, 'When I was reciting loudly, were you also reciting it?' So some of us said: We have done this," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do it. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."""
1218,"Abu Nu'im narrates that Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) has quoted the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) Do you people recite Qur'aat with me while praying? We said yes. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Do it. Yes", of course," read Surah Al-Fatihah.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
1219,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) asked us, do you people recite with me while I am praying? We said, \We recite Qur'at"," but we recite it quickly.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Do not recite Surah Al-Fatiha"," but recite Surah Fatiha and recite it in your heart.\"""""
1220,"Nafi bin Mahmud narrates that he heard Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting Surah Al-Fatiha (in congregational prayer), Abu Naeem (Imam Sahib) was reciting loudly. Nafee said: I heard you reciting Surah Al-Fatiha, although the Imam was reciting loudly, then Sayyiduna Ubadah said: Yes, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us a prayer in which he recited aloud. We said, \Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said," \""I was also wondering if I was being challenged in the Qur'an. None of you should recite any part of the Qur'an while I am reciting aloud"," but read Surah Fatiha.\"" The chain of transmission of this hadith is Hasan and all its narrators are trustworthy."""
1221,"Nafee bin Mahmud narrates: I attended the service of Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) and he mentioned this hadith regarding the Prophet (PBUH) (followed by the previous hadith), however, it contains these words (the Prophet (PBUH) said). \None of you should ever recite Qur'at", but recite Surat Al-Fatihah, because whoever does not recite it," his prayer is not complete.\"""""
1222,"Sayyidna Mahmud bin Rabi' Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) came and stood with me and started reciting following the lead of the Imam, although the Imam was also reciting when he finished praying, I said to him: Abu Waleed! He also started reciting even though he was listening to the imam reciting loudly, then Sayyiduna Ubada bin Samit said, \Yes", once we recited in the same way in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had difficulty in reciting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Subhan Allah: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished reciting the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us," \""Was anyone reciting with me?\"" We said yes. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""I was also wondering who is competing with me in the Qur'an. When the imam is reciting", do not recite with him, but recite Surah Fatiha," because the person who does not recite it does not pray.\"" Muawiya and the narrator named Ishaq bin Abu Farah are weak."""
1223,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather in reference to his father. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that whoever is performing the obligatory prayer, he should recite Surah Al-Fatihah in it and recite one surah along with it. If he does not do this, his prayer will be incomplete and will not be fulfilled. A narrator named Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubayd bin Umayr is weak."
1224,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to go and announce among the people that prayer does not begin until Surah Fatiha is recited and no more is recited.
1225,Muhammad bin Rabi' narrated that Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the person who does not recite Surah Al-Fatihah does not pray. A narrator named Ziyad has quoted these words: the prayer of a person who does not recite Surah Fatiha in it is not valid.
1226,"Sayyidna Mahmud bin Rabi', Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no prayer for a person who does not recite Fatiha while sleeping.\"" (This tradition is also authentic) The same tradition has been narrated by some other narrators."""
1227,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, “The Imam is the guarantor of what he does, so you also do it.” Sheikh Abu Hatim has stated this. This tradition corrects the position of those who are convinced that recitation will be recited under the guidance of the Imam."
1228,"Mahmood bin Rabi', quoting Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit, quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Surah Fatiha is a substitute for all other surahs, but no other surah can replace it. A narrator named Muhammad bin Khalad is unique in narrating this tradition."
1229,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give this instruction (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these are the words) He used to say, following the example of the Imam, recite Surah Fatiha and any surah along with it in the first two rak'ahs, and recite only Surah Fatiha in the last two rak'ahs."
1230,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to order (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words) He liked that in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and Asr, Surah Fatiha and a surah along with it should be recited, and in the last two rak'ats, only Surah Fatiha should be recited, when a person is praying under the guidance of the Imam. The evidence of this tradition is authentic."
1231,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1232,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and Asr, recite Surah Al-Fatiha and any surah along with it in the lead of the imam."
1233,Imam Abu Hanifa (may Allah have mercy on him) quotes this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his chain of transmission. This hadith has been narrated from a narrator named Musa only by Imam Abu Hanifah and a narrator named Hasan and both of them are weak.
1234,"Imam Abu Hanifah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) with regard to his chain of transmission: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer. Argument broke out between the two of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whoever is praying in the lead of the Imam"," only the recitations of the Imam count as the recitations of that person.\"" This tradition has been narrated by Imam Layth bin Saad on the authority of Imam Abu Yusuf from Imam Abu Hanifa."""
1235,"Layth bin Saad narrates on the authority of Imam Abu Yusuf and Imam Abu Hanifah, Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A man started reciting Surah Al-Ala following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), when the Prophet (PBUH) finished praying, he asked who among you had recited Surah Al-Ala. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I realized that one of you is causing trouble for me.\"""""
1236,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A man recited the Zuhr and Asr prayers following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), another person stopped him with a gesture, and when he finished the prayer, the first person said: Are you preventing me from reciting the prayer following the Prophet (PBUH)? He said, \Whoever is praying in the lead of the Imam"," then the recitation of the Imam is counted as the recitation of that person.\"" A narrator named Abulwaleed is unknown in his chain of transmission"," only Imam Abu Hanifa has mentioned it in his chain of transmission from Sayyidna Jabir (RA)."""
1237,"The same hadith has been narrated with reference to Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission. This tradition is also transmitted along with some other isnads. In some isnads, this tradition is transmitted as Mursal Hadith and this is correct."
1238,"Salim bin Abdullah narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar), whoever is the imam (i.e. performing the prayer in congregation) then the imam’s recitation will count as that person’s recitation. The narrator of this tradition is Muhammad bin Fazl."
1239,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu narrated about this verse here: \And when the Qur'an is recited," be silent and listen attentively so that you may be shown mercy.\"" Sayedna Abu Huraira (RA) says that it was revealed about raising a voice. These words of the hadith are from the narrator named Ibn Abu Dawud. The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Amir weak."""
1240,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching the people to pray. These words of the tradition have been narrated by the narrator named Hajjaj, other students of Qatadah namely Shuba, Saeed, and others have narrated the tradition on the contrary, they have not narrated these words in their tradition. \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to recite it.\"" Hajj?? The named narrator is not authentic."""
1241,"Sayyiduna Jabir Ibn Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) has said that the prayer in which Surah Al-Fatiha is not recited is defective, except for the prayer which is led by the Imam. The narrator named Yahya bin Salam is weak. It is true that this hadith is suspended."
1242,This hadith has been transmitted as a suspended tradition along with another Sunad.
1243,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: The Imam has been appointed so that he is followed.
1244,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Imam has been appointed so that he may be followed. Imam Abu Abd al-Rahman has stated this, Mukhrami says, this person is Taqqa, that is, the narrator named Muhammad bin Saad (Taqaq)."
1245,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH): The Imam has been appointed so that he may be followed. Do not disagree with him. When he says Takbeer, you also say Takbeer. And when he recites, you remain silent. All of you should also sit and pray. The narrator of this hadith is Ismail bin Aban Zaeef."
1246,"This hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA). The narrator of this tradition, Abu Saad al-Saghani, is weak."
1247,Imam Sha'bi narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that recitation will not be recited following the example of the Imam. This tradition is transmitted.
1248,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked, \Should I recite the Qur'aat following the lead of the Imam"," or should I remain silent?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be silent: this will be enough for you. A narrator named Ghassan is unique in narrating this tradition and this Sahib is weak"," while the other narrators of this tradition are Qais and Muhammad bin Salim."""
1249,"Hattan bin Abdullah al-Raqashi narrates that once Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) taught us the prayer. Sayyiduna Abu Musa told us: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the prayer, he (may God bless him and grant him peace) used to teach us. Shaykh Abu Hamid has spelled out this tradition in a similar way to us, the narrator of this tradition, Salim bin Nuh, is not authentic."
1250,"Hattan bin Abdullah al-Raqashi narrates: We performed the Isha prayer following the example of Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may God be pleased with him), after which he mentioned a long hadith in which these words are: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a sermon, he taught us how to pray and explained his Sunnah before us. The same hadith has been narrated with reference to some other isnads, but some narrators have quoted these words in it: \And when he recites"," you people be silent.\"""""
1251,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When Imam Ghair al-Maghzoob Alaihim Wala Al-Dhaaleen recites, you should remain silent."
1252,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The narrator of this tradition, Asim, is not authentic: quoting this tradition as a marfu' hadith is delusional."
1253,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever has an imam (i.e., one who is praying in congregation), the recitation of the imam will count as the recitation of that person."
1254,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1255,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever recites after the imam has violated the Sunnah.
1256,"This tradition is also narrated along with another document, but its document is not authentic."
1257,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person who recites following the lead of the Imam has violated the Sunnah.
1258,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person who recites following the lead of the Imam has violated the Sunnah.
1259,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who does not follow the Sunnah will recite in the example of the Imam.
1260,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Reciting the Imam's recitation is sufficient for you.
1261,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him).
1262,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked: Will recitation be recited in every prayer? He said: Yes! So one of the Ansar said: So it became obligatory (says the narrator). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed me and said, because I was sitting closest to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among those present. The narrator has narrated it in the same way, but the narrator of Zaydnam is delusional in it (the correct form of the previous tradition is this)."
1263,"The same hadith is quoted with reference to another chain of transmission in which these words are said: Sayyiduna Abu Darda said, O Kathir: I think that reciting the Imam's recitation will be sufficient for all of them."
1264,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has said this: The recitation of the imam will count as the recitation of the person who has an imam. Both Abu Yahya Taymi and Muhammad bin Ubadiya are weak.
1265,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered a prayer and when he finished it, he asked if any of you had recited the Qur’an with me. One of the people present said: I, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I was also thinking who is competing with me in recitation. When I am reciting in a low voice", you should also recite with me, and when I am reciting in a loud voice," no one should recite with me.\"" A narrator named Zakariya is unique in narrating this tradition and this person is a Mankar-ul-Hadith and obsolete."""
1266,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): It is sufficient for you to recite the Imam's recitation, whether he recites in a low voice or in a loud voice. A narrator named Abu Musa narrates, I asked Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal about this hadeeth about the Qur'aat transmitted from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, and he said, \This hadeeth is denied.\"""""
1267,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) say this: When the Imam recites \Ghira al-Maghdoob 'Alihim Wala Al-Dhaaleen\"" he should say Amen and draw the voice in it. Narrator Abu Bakr-Nami states that this is a Sunnah. The people of Kufa are unique in quoting this tradition. This tradition is authentic and the tradition after it is also authentic."""
1268,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: He heard the Prophet (PBUH) say Amen loudly when he recited \Ghira al-Maghdoob (Alaihi Hum Wala Al-Dhaaleen)\""."""
1269,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I recited the curse of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of the narrators of this tradition, Abd al-Rahman, says: What is more serious about this is that a person (another narrator of this tradition) inquired about it from Sufyan, so I think that Sufyan spoke about some part of it and this person spoke about another part."
1270,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: I prayed following the example of the Holy Prophet (SAW). A narrator named Shuba has narrated these words: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Amen to the earth."
1271,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) narrates: I prayed following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) when the Prophet (PBUH) recited Wala al-Dhaaleen, the Prophet (PBUH) said Amen: and the Prophet (PBUH) raised his voice in it. This hadith is authentic."
1272,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Wala al-Zaaleen, he would say Amen and say it loudly."
1273,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira. The narrator of the previous tradition, Bahr, is weak in trust."
1274,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) finished reciting Surah Al-Fatiha, he used to say Amen in a loud voice."
1275,"Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I remember this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to be silent twice during the prayer, one when the imam had said Takbeer and was about to start the recitation, and the second was when he finished reciting Surah Fatiha. Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) did not accept this, so these people wrote a letter about it to Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) in Madinah, and he confirmed the statement of Sayyidna Samura (RA). Hasan al-Basri heard a hadith from Sayyiduna Samrah (may God be pleased with him) that has been disputed."
1276,"Hasan al-Basri narrates: When Sayyiduna Samrah (RA) used to start the prayer, he would remain silent for a while, then when he finished reciting Wala al-Dhaaleen, he would remain silent for a while."
1277,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the Takbir at the beginning of the prayer, he would remain silent for a while. I said: O Messenger of Allah: May my parents be sacrificed to you. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I read this: O Allah! So create a distance between me and my sins as much as You have placed a distance between the East and the West and O Allah cleanse me from my sins as a white cloth is cleansed from dirt."
1278,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: We estimated the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) in the Zuhr and Asr prayers, so we estimated that the time of the Prophet (PBUH) in the Zuhr Prayer is as long as thirty verses can be recited in a while, i.e. the length of Surah Sajdah. In the same way, we estimated his stay in the first rak'at of Asr, and it was equal to the last two rak'ats of Zuhr, and we estimated his stay in the last two rak'ats of Asr, and it was half of that. This tradition is proven and correct."
1279,"Qais bin Abu Hazim narrates: I prayed in Basra following Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, he recited Surah Fatiha in the first rak'ah and recited the first verse of Surah Baqarah, then he stood up for the second rak'ah and recited Surah Fatihah and recited the second verse of Surah Baqarah. He said: \Recite as much of it as you can easily read.\"" The authenticity of this hadeeth is good"," in it there is an argument for those who are convinced that: \""Recite this commandment of Allah"," you should recite what can be easily recited.\"""""
1280,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: A person stood up and asked: O Messenger of Allah: Will it be recited in every rak'ah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, one of the people present said: It has become necessary. (The narrator of this hadith) Sayyiduna Abu Darda said (to his disciple) O Katheer: (Many say: I was by his side at that time) I think that the recitation of the Imam when he was leading the people in prayer would be sufficient for those people. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: I think that reciting the Imam's recitation will be sufficient for these people. The narrator is delusional in this hadith. The truth is: These words are from Sayyiduna Abu Darda' as narrated by a narrator named Ibn Wahhib, Allah knows best."
1281,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us how to pray. The narrator says) When Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) found out about this tradition, he said: My brother (Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud (RA) said correctly: Yes, we used to do this before, but then we were ordered to do it this way, then Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) placed both hands on the knees (this means: ordered to do this while bowing)."
1282,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: He said Takbeer, raised both hands, then when he went into Ruku, he put both hands together and placed them between both knees. When Sayyidna Saad (RA) came to know about this, he said: My brother said right: Yes, we used to do it like this before, but then we were ordered to place both palms on both knees. This certificate is proven and correct."
1283,"Alqamah bin Wail narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Wail bin Hajar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spread his fingers when he bowed, and when he went into prostration, he used to bring all five fingers together. This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads."
1284,"Abdullah bin Burida narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Burida! When you bow down, recite this: \Hear Allah", Praise be to Allah, Lord, Praise be to the fullness of the heavens and the fullness of the earth," and the fullness of all things.\"" Allah heard the person who praised him", O Allah, our Lord! Praise is reserved for You, which is enough to fill the heavens and the earth, and besides them," to fill whatever you want."""
1285,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When we used to pray in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to recite, Sama’ullah al-ulman Hamda, and the person behind the Prophet (peace be upon him) also used to recite, Sama’Allah al-man Hamda."
1286,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When the imam recites Sama'Allah Al-Man Hamdah, the person behind him should recite, 'Allahum Rabbanalik Walik Al-Hamdah.'"
1287,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) led us in prayer, then he turned towards us and said: Do you people recite after the imam? We said: There is a gentleman among us who recited this."
1288,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led his companions in prayer. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished praying, he turned to them and said: Were you reciting while the Imam was reciting? The people remained silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this three times, and a gentleman said: A few gentlemen have stated this: We have done the same. These words belong to a narrator named Farsi."
1289,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1290,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to those present who were reciting aloud (following the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)): You have made it difficult for me to recite. (Sayyidna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates:) Earlier we (used to reply to salams) in prayer, then we were told: Prayer is a distraction (therefore no conversation or speech should be made between prayers)."
1291,"Saeed bin Musayyib used to say here: When you find some people in the state of ruku, say Takbeer and go into Ruku, then that one Takbeer will be sufficient for you as Takbeer Tahreema and Takbeer going into Ruku. This has also been narrated from Saeed bin Musaib: He says: Whoever forgets to say Takbeer Tahreema at the beginning of the prayer, then he says Takbeer to go into Ruku, then doing so will be sufficient for him."
1292,"Sayyiduna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Subhan Rabi al-Azeem wa Bhamdah three times while bowing and while prostrating, he used to recite Subhan Rabi al-Ala: three times."
1293,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: This is a Sunnah: a person should read Subhan Rabi al-Azeem wa Bhamda while bowing, and Subhan Rabi al-Ala wa Bhamda while prostrating."
1294,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) went into prostration in the obligatory prayer, he used to recite the following: \O Allah", I prostrated to You, I believed in You and I accepted Islam for You. You are my Lord. My face is in the presence of the One who created it, gave it shape and form, gave it hearing and sight, then Allah is the Blessed One," the Greatest Creator.\"" When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into Ruku", he used to recite: O Allah, I bowed down for You, I believed in You, I accepted Islam for You, You are my Lord, my hearing, my sight, my brain, my bones, my whole being bowed before Allah, the Lord of all the worlds. When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing in obligatory prayer," he used to recite: \""O Allah"," our Lord! All praise is reserved for You that fills the heavens and fills the earth and also fills whatever you want.” The authenticity of this hadith is Sahih Hasan."""
1295,"It has been narrated in another chain of transmission, which has these words: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bow down, it specifically mentions bowing and does not mention other things."
1296,"Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Muta'im (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) went into Ruku, he would recite Subhan Rabi Al-Azeem three times."
1297,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this statement from his father: I remember this about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to recite Subhan Rabi al-Azeem three times while bowing."
1298,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a person bows, he should recite the Tasbeeh three times, because he will be reciting the Tasbeeh with his body, and with him three hundred and thirty-three bones and three hundred and thirty-three veins are reciting the Tasbeeh of Allah."
1299,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When a person recites Subhan Rabi al-Azeem three times while bowing, then his bowing will be complete."
1300,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite this dua while bowing:
1301,"The narrator says: I inquired from Sulaiman bin Harb: Shu'ba narrated this: Hisham narrated this tradition to me, he said: He narrated this."
1302,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration, his fingers would point towards the Qiblah."
1303,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration, he would place both hands on his knees."
1304,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a person goes into prostration, he should place both his hands before his legs and he should not sit like a camel."
1305,"It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a person goes into prostration, he should place his hands in front of his knees and should not sit like a camel."
1306,"There is this addition in another hadith: When the imam says Sama'Allah Al-Man Hamdah, the person behind him should read: Sama'Allah Liman Hamdah Al-Hum Rabnalik Al-HamdAllah Ta'ala heard the praise of the person who recited his praise, O Allah! O our Lord! All praise is reserved for You."
1307,"Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration, he would place both his knees in front of his hands, and when he stood up, he would raise both hands before his knees. Narrator Yazid is unique in narrating this tradition, he narrated it from a participant and this narrator is not authentic."
1308,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates: I remember this about the Holy Prophet (SAW): The Prophet (SAW) said the Takbeer until he raised both his thumbs to his ears, then he bowed until every joint of the Prophet’s (SAW) body stayed in its place, then he raised his blessed head until every joint of his body stayed in its place, then he bowed while saying the Takbeer, then he bowed both his knees. Put the hands on the ground first. Al-Ala bin Ismail is also unique in quoting this hadith, Allah knows best."
1309,"Abu Qalaba narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Sulaiman Malik bin Hawairat (RA) came to our mosque, he said: By Allah! I pray you, I do not intend to pray at this time, but I want to show you how I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying. The narrator narrates that when he got up after performing the second prostration in the first rak'at, he sat down first (then stood up)."
1310,"Sayyiduna Malik bin Hawairat Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I remember this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He (peace be upon him) was praying, when he was in the first and third rak'ahs, he did not get up until he first went straight. This hadith is authentic."
1311,"Sayyiduna Malik bin Hawairat (RA) narrates: Those people came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) along with one of his companions. The Prophet (PBUH) said to both of them: When the time for prayer comes, both of you should call the Adhaan, both of you should say Iqamah, and let the one of you who is older than the two of you lead the prayer, and you should pray in the same way as you have seen me praying. This tradition is authentic."
1312,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If you want your prayer to be pure, you should lead your righteous people, (i.e. make them Imams)."
1313,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who observes one rak'at of prayer has observed this prayer, that is, he finds it before the imam has raised his back (from the bowing of the last rak'at)."
1314,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When you come for prayer and we are in the state of prostration, you should also go into prostration, but do not count it as a rak'ah."
1315,Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The person who does not keep his back straight in bowing and prostrating does not pray. The chain of this hadith is proven and correct.
1316,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: \The prayer of a person who does not keep his back upright in prayer is not performed.\"""""
1317,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) saw one of his wives who was praying, she was not putting her nose on the ground. The Prophet (PBUH) said: O woman! You should put your nose on the ground. The person who does not put his nose and forehead on the ground during the prayer does not pray. The narrator of this hadith is weak, and this tradition is not authentic regarding Muqatil's narration regarding Arwa."
1318,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \There is no prayer for a person who does not put his nose on the ground.\"" Other narrators have narrated it as Mursal Hadith."""
1319,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) saw a person praying who was not placing his nose on the ground. This hadith has been transmitted as a messenger along with another sanad.
1320,"Abdul Aziz narrates I said to Wahib: O Abu Na'im! Why don't you keep your forehead and nose on the ground during prayer? So he said: I heard Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah narrating this: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating on the upper part of the forehead, i.e. where the hair begins. Narrator Abdul Aziz is unique in narrating this tradition and it is not authentic."
1321,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Sunnah way (of sitting) in prayer is to put the left foot down and keep the right foot standing.
1322,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The way (to sit) in prayer is to spread the left foot and raise the right foot.
1323,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah way (of sitting) in prayer is that you should put your left foot down and raise your right foot. All these hadiths are authentic, but they have been narrated only by a narrator named Thaqafi."
1324,"On the authority of Amir bin Abdullah, his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair, may God be pleased with him) narrated this statement: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray (during the prayer), he used to pray (says the narrator) that is, he used to pray in tashahhud. He used to hold his left knee with his blessed hand."
1325,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to teach us the words of tashahhud in the same way that the Prophet (PBUH) used to teach us the Qur’an. \All verbal and physical blessed pure worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! May peace be upon you and may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon us," may peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. The authenticity of this hadeeth is Sahih."""
1326,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to teach us this tashahhud (in these words): \All blessed and pure worship is for Allah," O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon us. Peace be upon us and upon all the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His special servant and the Messenger of Allah."""
1327,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Before tashahhud became obligatory, we used to recite: Peace be upon Allah, Gabriel and Michael. All physical and verbal acts of worship are pure acts of worship reserved for Allah, O Prophet! Peace be upon you, may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon us, may peace be upon us, the righteous servants of Allah. Its certificate is authentic."
1328,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us tashahhud in these words: All worship is for Allah (after this the narrator mentioned the previous hadith).
1329,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to recite the following in Tashahhud: All verbal and physical acts of worship are reserved for Allah, O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may the blessings of Allah be upon you. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have added these words to it: And may His blessings also descend (these are the words of the martyrdom of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) May peace be upon us and all the righteous servants of Allah. These are the words of tashahhud) I bear witness that Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him) is his servant and his messenger."
1330,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach tashahhud in these words. \All pure worship is reserved for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon us. Peace be upon us and upon all the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is none worthy of worship but Allah, He is One, He has no partner, and Sayyiduna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace," is His servant and His Messenger.\"" (The narrator says) Then he used to send blessings on the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). These words of the hadith are from the narrator named Ibn Abu Uthman."""
1331,"A narrator named Yaqoob bin Ashjaja narrates: Aun bin Abdullah wrote down the words of tashahud narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, then he held my hand and told: Sayyiduna Umar once held his hand and said this. \Salutations to Allah", Salutations and Blessings to Allah, all verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah. This hadith is authentic, hasan, and its narrator, Ibn Lahiyyah," is not authentic."""
1332,"Hattan bin Abdullah al-Raqashi narrates: These people prayed following the example of Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari said: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) explained to us the way to pray before us while giving a sermon, and he taught us the Sunnah. After this, the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith, which also contains these words: When a person sits in Qa'dah, recite these words: All verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon you, may peace be upon us and upon all the righteous servants of Allah. The disciples of the narrator named Qatadah have added these words to the names: He is One and He has no partner, while other narrators have narrated the opposite regarding Qatadah."
1333,"A narrator named Qasim narrates: Once Al-Qamah held my hand and said: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah held my hand and told me that: Once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, held my hand and taught me the words of tashahhud during prayer (these are the words). All verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may the blessings and mercy of Allah be upon us and peace be upon us and all the righteous servants of Allah. Other narrators have followed in narrating it."
1334,The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of narrators. Some narrators have quoted additional words at the end of it. \When you read this (the narrator doubts maybe these are the words) you will do so, then you have completed your prayer, now if you want to get up, get up, if you want to sit down," then sit down.\"" Some narrators", quoting this tradition with reference to Zuhair, have recorded these words in the hadith and combined them with the words of the Holy Prophet, while the narrator named Shababa has narrated it separately with reference to Zuhair, and has quoted these words as the words of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, and these words are more suitable to be the words of Sayyidna Abdullah than to be recorded in the hadith of the Prophet," may God bless him and grant him peace."""
1335,"A narrator named Qasim narrates: Al-Qamah held my hand and said: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud held my hand and said: Once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, held my hand and taught me the words of tashahhud (these are the words): All verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! May peace be upon you and may the blessings and mercy of Allah be upon us and may peace be upon us and all the righteous servants of Allah. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud says: When you read this, you have performed the obligatory prayer. Now if you want to get up, get up. If you want to sit, sit down. The narrator of this tradition here is Shababa Thaqa. He has mentioned this separately at the end of the tradition. Some other narrators have also narrated it in the same way as the words of Sayyiduna Abdullah, they have not narrated (the additional words) as a marfu' hadith."
1336,"A narrator named Qasim narrates: Once Alqamah held my hand and told him. All verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! May peace be upon you and may the blessings and mercy of Allah be upon us and may peace be upon us and all the righteous servants of Allah. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud said: When you have completed this (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words), when you have done this, you have performed your prayer."
1337,"The same tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads in which there are these words: A narrator named Qasim narrates: Alqamah held my hand and (there are also these words in the narration) Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) held the hand of Alqamah and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held the hand of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) and taught him the words of tashahhud (which are these). All verbal and physical worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! May peace be upon you and may the blessings and mercy of Allah be upon us and may peace be upon us and all the righteous servants of Allah. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said this: When you are finished with this, you will finish the prayer."
1338,"Mujahid narrates: Ibn Abi Layli (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) Abu Muammar has narrated this, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu taught me the words of tashahhud and narrated that these words were taught to me by the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) in the same way that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) used to teach us a chapter of the Qur’an (these are the words): All pure and physical and verbal worship is reserved for Allah, O Prophet! Peace be upon you and may the blessings and mercy of Allah be upon us and may peace be upon us and all the good servants of Allah. So send blessings on Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and on his family, just as You sent blessings on Sayyiduna Ibrahim, indeed, to the Lord of praise and greatness, O Allah, send blessings on us along with them. May the blessings of the people of faith be upon Sayyidna Muhammad (peace be upon him), who is a prophet, and may peace be upon him, may the mercy and blessings of Allah be upon him. Mujahid says that when a person uses these words while sending greetings, and greetings are sent to all the righteous servants of Allah, then he has sent greetings to all the people living in the heavens and the earth. A narrator named Abdul Wahab bin Mujahid is weak."
1339,"A narrator named Ibn Ishaq narrated this: He narrated to me this hadith about sending blessings on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer: When a Muslim person sends blessings on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during prayer. (There are these words in a hadith) Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates: A person came and sat in front of the Holy Prophet (SAW). We were around him at that time. This person said, O Messenger of Allah, we have become familiar with the way of sending salutations on you while we are praying, so how do we send salutations on you while we are praying? The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until we wished that this person had not asked him this question, but then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you wish to send blessings upon me, recite this: \O Allah! So send blessings upon Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)", who is the mother, and upon the family of Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him), just as you sent blessings upon Sayyiduna Ibrahim and Sayyiduna Ibrahim’s family, and upon Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him), who is the mother of the Prophet, and upon the family of Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him)," just as you blessed Sayyiduna Ibrahim and Sayyiduna Ibrahim’s family. \"" The authenticity of this tradition is authentic."""
1340,"Abdullah bin Burida narrated this statement of his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Burida! When you sit in the tashahhud in prayer, never give up the words of tashahhud and sending blessings on me, because this is the zakat of prayer, and also send greetings to all the prophets and messengers of Allah, and send greetings to all the righteous servants of Allah."
1341,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Prayer is not accepted without performing ablution and sending blessings upon me. Amr bin Shamar and Jabir Jafi are both weak narrators.
1342,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not send blessings on his Prophet.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition", Abd al-Muhaiman Abbas," is not authentic."""
1343,"Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever prays and does not send blessings on me and my family in it, his prayer will not be accepted. One of the narrators of this hadith is Jabir Zaeef, and it has been disputed in narrating the hadith from him."
1344,"Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: If I do not send blessings on the family of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while praying, then I consider that my prayer has not been completed."
1345,"Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the prayer during which I do not send blessings upon Sayyidna Muhammad (peace be upon him), I think that my prayer has not been completed."
1346,Amir bin Sa'd on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He used to salute the right until the whiteness of his blessed face was visible and he used to salute the left until the whiteness of his blessed face was seen. The evidence of this tradition is authentic.
1347,"Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to greet the right side, the whiteness of his right cheek would be seen, and when he greeted him to the left, the whiteness of his left cheek would be seen."
1348,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say salam to the right, he used to say Salam alaikum wa rahmatullah, until the whiteness of his face was visible, and when he used to say salam to the left (the same thing happened). Narrator Abu Ishaq has been disputed in narrating this tradition, the second chain of this tradition is better."
1349,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I remember this very well about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to say Takbeer every time he stood up, bowed, stood up, and sat down, and he used to say Salaam alaikum wa rahmatullah, salam alaikum wa rahmatullah, until the whiteness of his blessed face could be seen. (Sayyidna Abdullah says) I have seen Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar also do the same."
1350,Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to greet him twice (i.e. on both sides).
1351,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I may forget whatever I want, but I will not forget the way the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say salam during prayer. After that, Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu said this: The sight of the whiteness of both the faces of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, seems to be in my eyes even today."
1352,Sayyida Aisha Sadiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make a salam in prayer and he would also turn towards the front and say (the words of salutation): He used to lean slightly to the right.
1353,"Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to say salam once while facing the front in prayer, but when he turned his salam to the right, he also turned to the side of repentance."
1354,Abd al-Muhaiman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make a salam to the right in prayer.
1355,"Abd al-Muhaiman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say one salam, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say any more salams."
1356,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The key to prayer is ablution. A narrator has copied the word tahoor instead of the word ablution.
1357,Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: We should send greetings to our rulers and send greetings to each other.
1358,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When Najm is sitting in the amount of tashahhud, his prayer is complete."
1359,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is ablution.
1360,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Wudu is performed before prayer, it begins with Takbeer and ends with salutation."
1361,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to pray, and when he said the Takbeer, he turned back from there. I was in a state of janabat and I did not remember to take bath."
1362,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) started the prayer, he (PBUH) said the Takbeer, following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), we also recited the Takbeer, then the Prophet (PBUH) signaled to those present that you should remain in the state you are in. The drops were dripping. A narrator named Abdul Wahab has narrated the opposite tradition."
1363,"Sayyidna Bakr bin Abdullah Muzni (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started the prayer, he said the Takbeer and the people behind him also said the Takbeer, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke the prayer and signaled to his Companions to remain in the same state as they were, so they remained in the state of standing, until when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, drops of water were dripping from his head. A narrator named Abdul Wahab narrates: We also issue a fatwa accordingly."
1364,"Sayyiduna Wabsa narrates: He stood alone at the back of the row and prayed, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to pray again."
1365,"Sayyiduna Wabsa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man prayed standing alone at the back of the row, and the Prophet ordered him to pray again."
1366,Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) led the people in prayer. He was not in the state of ablution at that time. The prayer of the people was completed and the Prophet (PBUH) repeated this prayer.
1367,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words of yours: When the imam leads the prayer to the people who are in a state of ablution due to forgetfulness, then the prayer of the people will be valid and the imam will perform this prayer again."
1368,"Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): If an imam forgets to lead people in a state of janabat, their prayer will be valid, then this imam should perform ablution and repeat his prayer. A narrator named Isa bin Ibrahim narrated these same words."
1369,Saeed bin Musaib narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in the state of Janabat (forgetfulness). The Prophet (peace be upon him) also repeated his prayer and the people also repeated their prayer. This tradition is transmitted and the narrator named Abu Jabar is an obsolete hadith.
1370,"Asim bin Zamra narrates this about Sayyidna Ali: Once he led the people in prayer in the state of Janabat (forgetfulness), then Sayyidna Ali repeated the prayer and instructed the people to repeat the prayer. The narrator of this tradition is Amr bin Khalid, this person is Abu Khalid Wasti (who has quoted the Musnad of Imam Zayd regarding Imam Zayd)."
1371,"Shareed Thaqafi narrates: Once Sayyiduna Umar (R.A.) taught the prayer to the people. They were in a state of janabat. They repeated that prayer, but he did not order the people to repeat that prayer."
1372,"Muhammad Bin Amr narrates: Once Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) led the people in prayer, he was in a state of janabat at that time, and later when he saw a mark of ihtilam on his clothes, he said: I am old, by Allah, I think I have contracted janabat, but I did not know about it, then Hazrat Uthman repeated the prayer, and of course he did not order the people to perform that prayer again. A narrator named Abd al-Rahman narrates: It is agreed that a person with Janabat will repeat this prayer, but people will not repeat this prayer. As far as I know, there is no disagreement about this."
1373,"Salim narrates the saying of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) about a person who leads people in the state of ablution."
1374,"Narrated by Nafi: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed to his companions, later he remembered that he had touched his private parts (due to which his ablution was broken), so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) performed ablution again (and prayed again), but he did not instruct those people to perform that prayer again. Ibn Mahdi narrates: I inquired from Sufyan: Are you aware of this, that a narrator has also narrated this? These people also prayed again? He replied no, only a narrator named Hamad has narrated this."
1375,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We performed an obligatory prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rubbed his hands together during the prayer. I felt the coolness of his tongue on my hands, By Allah, if my brother Sulaiman (peace be upon him) had not prayed this before me, I would have tied this devil to a pillar of this mosque and the children of Madinah would have circled around him (and mocked him)."
1376,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Once he prayed (after finishing his prayer) he said, “Satan came before me to spoil my prayer, so Allah overpowered me. Dua remembered: \O my Lord: grant me a kingdom that no one else will get after me.\"" (The Holy Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him) says," So Allah humiliated this devil and sent him back."""
1377,"Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Wudu is the key to prayer. Imam Abu Hanifah, may God have mercy on him, says: This means reciting tashahhud (i.e. recite tashahhud after every two rak'ahs)."
1378,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us the Zuhr prayer or perhaps the Asr prayer. Yes, the prayer has been shortened, Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar were also present, but they did not have the courage to address the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Neither have I forgotten"," nor has the prayer been shortened.\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," perhaps you have forgotten.\"" So the people indicated yes: The Prophet returned to his place and after offering the remaining two rak'ats", he returned the salam, then he prostrated like the normal prostrations or a little longer than that while saying the Takbeer, then he raised his head and said the Takbeer. A narrator named Muhammad was asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greet before prostrating himself? So he replied," \""I do not remember these words regarding Sayyidna Abu Huraira", but I have been told this: Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated this: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace," greeted him."""
1379,"This tradition is narrated along with some other isnads, but it does not contain these words: So people pointed out, these words were narrated only by the narrator named Hamad bin Zayd."
1380,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer, some donkeys passed in front of him, and Ayyash bin Abu Rabiyyah, one of those who were praying in the lead of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), began to say Subhan Allah. He said, O Messenger of Allah, I said: Yes, because I have heard that if a donkey passes in front, the prayer breaks."
1381,"Salem bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar RA): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar RA said: Nothing breaks the prayer of a Muslim, but you try to stop him as much as possible (so that he does not pass in front of you during the prayer)."
1382,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Nothing breaks the prayer (i.e. it does not break the prayer by passing in front of it).
1383,Sayyidina Abu Umamah narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Nothing breaks the prayer.
1384,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: It is said: Nothing breaks a Muslim's prayer (i.e., prayer is not broken due to the passage of anything in front of it)."
1385,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A dog, a woman, or a donkey does not break a man's prayer (by passing in front of him), but prevent them from passing in front of you as much as you can."
1386,"Sayyidna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to meet Sayyidna Abbas (RA) in his neighborhood, where the Prophet (PBUH) offered the Asr prayer, a small dog and a donkey passed in front of him, but they were not rebuked and they were not reprimanded."
1387,Sayyidna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to meet Sayyidna Abbas (RA).
1388,"Sayyiduna Fazl bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to us and we were in our residence. The Prophet (PBUH) led us in the Asr prayer. A small dog and a donkey passed in front of him, which were our (pets), but we did not stop them and did not return them."
1389,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once I was discussing with Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) about a problem of prayer. At the same time, Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA) also came to us and said, “Shall I narrate to you the hadith that I heard from the Prophet (PBUH)?” We said: “Yes.” If there is a doubt about it, he should pray so much that the doubt becomes about the increase."
1390,"Makhool narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When a person is in doubt about his prayer and he does not know whether he has prayed more (rak'ats) or less, then if the doubt is about one rak'at or two rak'ats, he should consider it as one, if it is about two or three, then two, if it is three or four, then consider it as three until he becomes delusional. be about This same tradition is narrated from Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission."
1391,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him): Whoever doubts whether a prayer should be three or four rak'ahs should complete the prayer (i.e. perform one more rak'ah) because an increase in it is better than a decrease in it.
1392,"Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Bazaz, Abu Bakr narrated to us, he narrated to us from Ja’far ibn Muhammad ibn Fudhil, he narrated from Ammar ibn Matar al-Anbari (who used to come in spirit), he narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, he narrated from his father, he from Makhool, he narrated from Karib (slave of Ibn Abbas), he narrated from Ibn Abbas, he narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God said: Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If a person neglects three or four (rak'ahs) in prayer", he should complete the prayer," because doing more is better than doing less.\"""""
1393,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: When a person makes a mistake about two or one rak'ah, he should consider it as one, and when he is in doubt about two rak'ahs, he should consider them two, and when he is in doubt about three or four, he should consider them as three, and then complete the remaining prayer, until he becomes more delusional. Be it not about lack, then when he is sitting (i.e. reciting tashahhud) he should perform two prostrations (i.e. perform prostration)."
1394,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): On the day Sayyiduna Dhuwalideen came to him (i.e. the day he told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prostrating himself in prayer), on that day the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed two prostrations of prostration after returning the salutation. The word of these two traditions is the same."
1395,Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) prostrated after saluting on the day of Sayyidna Dhu-Walideen (the Day of Attention).
1396,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a person does not know how many rak'ahs he has performed, he should pray three or four rak'ahs, add one more rak'ah, and then perform two sajdahs of Sahu while he is sitting (i.e. reciting tashahhud). If he pays, these two will disgrace the devil."
1397,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): When a person doubts during prayer whether he has performed three rak'ahs or four rak'ahs, then he should perform one more rak'ah until he is sure that the doubt is greater, then he should prostrate before returning the salam. If so, both of these will be a source of humiliation for Satan."
1398,"Sayyidina Abu Saeed al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person has a doubt during the prayer and does not know how many rak'ahs he has performed, three or four, he should put the doubt aside and base it on what he believes in. Both of these (sajdahs) will be disgraceful to Shaytaan if the rakats are performed."
1399,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: When a person has a doubt about his prayer, he should put the doubt aside and base it on faith. Through this, his prayer will be completed and the two prostrations of Sahu will dust the nose of Satan."
1400,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): When a person is in doubt about his prayer and does not know how many rak'ahs he has performed: four yatin? So he should put his doubt aside and base it on faith, then stand up and pray one rak'at, then when he is sitting (i.e. reciting the tashahhud) he should perform prostration twice before turning the salam. Both prostrations will make Satan's nose dusty."
1401,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When a person is in doubt about his prayer, if he is sure that he has performed three rak'ahs, then he should perform one more rak'ah and perform two prostrations. He had performed three rak'ahs, now the rak'ah he has performed will become the fourth rak'ah, and the two prostrations of Sajdah Sahu will dust the nose of the devil, and he had previously performed four rak'ahs, so now with what he has performed, it will become the fifth, and these two sajdahs will make the fifth rak'ah equal."
1402,"Abd al-Muhaiman narrates the statement of his grandfather Munzeer bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding his father: These companions are among the Naqba of Banus Sa’idah."
1403,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us, \When a person is praying and he does not know whether he has performed more Rak'ats or less?\"" So he should prostrate twice while he is sitting (i.e. do it during tashahhud)"," then after that he should return the salam."""
1404,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When the muezzin gives the call to prayer, the devil leaves the mosque, his air is emitted. creates various thoughts in the mind, after which he does not remember whether he has increased or decreased the prayer. When a person is faced with this situation, when he is sitting (i.e. while reciting the tashahhud), he should perform Sajdah twice."
1405,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever is in doubt about his prayer and is not sure whether he has performed three rak'ahs or four rak'ahs? So he should get up and perform another rak'ah and then after that, when he is sitting, he should prostrate twice before returning the salam."
1406,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said that when a person prays and does not know whether he has performed three rak'ahs or four, then he should complete it until he is sure that he has performed the complete prayer, then after that he should prostrate twice before turning the salutation. If already married, these prostrations will become a disgrace to Satan."
1407,"Muhammad bin Yusuf narrates: Me?? He heard his father narrate that once Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah led these people in prayer, they prayed two rak'ahs and then stood up even though they were required to sit. The people said SubhanAllah upon that, but they did not sit until they sat down to return the salutation (in the final tashahhud) and they prostrated twice. These are the words of a narrator named Neshapuri: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing the same."
1408,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered a prayer. The narrator of this tradition, Ibrahim, narrates: I do not know whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned any increase or decrease in this prayer. (Sayyidna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates:) When the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) greeted him, he was asked: O Messenger of Allah, has there been any new order regarding prayer? The Prophet (PBUH) said no, why what happened? The people said, \You have prayed like this.\"" The Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him, straightened his legs, turned his face towards the Qibla, and prostrated himself twice. If he is in doubt about his prayer, he should try to find the correct form, then complete the prayer according to the same calculation," then offer salutations and after that do Sajdah twice."""
1409,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person is in doubt about his prayer, he should try to adopt the correct posture and then perform Sajdah twice."
1410,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a human being and I forget, just like you people forget. If a person is in doubt about his prayer, he should examine which form of prayer is closest to the correctness of the prayer, then complete the prayer according to the same calculation and then perform Sajdah twice."
1411,"Al-Qamah narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) prostrated twice after returning the salam, and he said: The Prophet (PBUH) also performed these two prostrations after returning the salam."
1412,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Bahina (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Zuhr prayer. He stood up after praying two rak'ahs.
1413,"Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The person who follows the Imam (due to some mistake of his own), it is not necessary to perform prostration on him, but if a mistake is made by the Imam, it is necessary to perform prostration on the Imam, and it is also necessary for those who lead the prayer. But if there is a mistake on the part of the person performing the prayer following the lead of the imam, then prostration is not required on him, rather the imam is sufficient for him."
1414,"Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: Prostration on any mistake is obligatory only when a person stands instead of sitting or sits instead of standing."
1415,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once Sayyidna Umar (RA) was discussing with me about increasing in prayer, while Sayyidna (RA) Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA) came to us and stayed with us."
1416,"Narrated Ubaidullah bin Abdullah (this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once I was with Sayyiduna Umar, we were discussing about prayer. Meanwhile, Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came and said, “Should I not tell you the hadith that I heard from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that when you are in doubt about a lack during the prayer, continue to pray until the doubt becomes about an increase."
1417,"Abu Ubaydah bin Abdullah narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him) that when you are in the state of prayer and you are in doubt about three or four rak'ahs, and you think that four have been recited, then after reciting the tashahhud, prostrate twice, do this while you are sitting and before turning the salam, then recite the tashahud again and then the salam. turn Some other narrators have narrated it, but they have not narrated it as a marfu' hadeeth."
1418,"Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When the imam stands up (instead of sitting) after performing two rak'ahs, and remembers this before standing up, he should sit down. Other narrators have narrated it in the same way."
1419,"Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person has a doubt and he stands up (instead of sitting) after praying the rakat, if he stands fully, he should continue praying in the same way and then perform Sajdah twice."
1420,Some narrators of this tradition have been criticized.
1421,Muhammad bin Hanafiyah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that ablution is the key to prayer. A narrator named Ubaidullah has quoted some words differently.
1422,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When the imam is sitting in tashahhud after reciting the last rak'at, and following his example, someone breaks his ablution before the imam turns his salutations, then that person's prayer will be counted as complete. The narrator of this hadith is Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad Zaeef, it has not been recognized as authentic."
1423,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When the imam finishes the prayer and he is sitting while he is sitting, if his ablution is broken before making the salam, then his prayer will be complete and the person who is following him will complete his prayer."
1424,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the imam breaks his ablution after rising from the last prostration and sitting upright, his prayer will be counted as complete, and the prayer of the person who followed him from the beginning of the prayer will also be counted as complete."
1425,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I had a complaint of piles and I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it.
1426,The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) with reference to some other isnads.
1427,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: I had a complaint about Nasur. I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the prayer, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \Pray while standing. If you cannot do this", then sit down. If you cannot do this," then pay the Pahlavi.\"""""
1428,"The same tradition is narrated along with another tradition, however, the name of the disease, basoor, is quoted in it."
1429,"Sayyidna Ya'li bin Umayyah narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we reached a place that was narrow, the sky was above us and the valley below us. It was time for prayer. While living, he prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
1430,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktoum Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: He said, O Messenger of Allah, there is no one to accompany me, who stays with me all the time, while there are also drains and trees between me and the mosque, so is there room for me to pray in my house?"
1431,Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (PBUH) and he slept until the sun came up. The Prophet (PBUH) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (RA).
1432,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person has performed one rak'at of the morning prayer, he should perform the second rak'at while the sun rises."
1433,"A narrator named Hammam narrates: Qatadah was asked about a person who had performed one rakat of the morning prayer and then the sun came out, then Qatadah said: This saying of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace."
1434,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: He who has performed one rak'ah of morning prayer and then the sun rises during that time, he should complete his prayer."
1435,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A person who has performed one rak'ah of the Fajr prayer and the sun rises during that time, then that person should perform the Fajr prayer."
1436,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Whoever has not performed the two Rak'ats of Fajr until the sun rises"," he should perform them both.\"""""
1437,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and all the people fell asleep at the time of the Fajr prayer. They woke up due to the heat of the sun. When the sun rose a little and became bright, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the muezzin. Wasallam performed the Fajr prayer (as a judgment)."
1438,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
1439,"Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: Once he came (to the mosque) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the Fajr prayer. He said, I did not pay them before Fajr (i.e. these are the two sunnahs of Fajr), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent and did not say anything."
1440,Sayyiduna Qays bin Amr (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) saw a man who was offering two rak'ahs after the Fajr prayer. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired whether the morning prayer is offered twice. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent.
1441,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to participate in an expedition (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these words are:) to Syria. When the last part of the night came, we camped (and slept). We could not wake up until the heat of the sun woke us up. We traveled for a while until the sun rose a little, then the people did their needs, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal to give the Adhan: Then we prayed two rak'ats, then he said Iqamah under the command of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the morning prayer. We said: O Prophet of Allah! Shall we not make up for it tomorrow in its time? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people: Will Allah forbid you people from usury, and accept it from you?"
1442,Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a sermon (after which the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith) in which these words are: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no extravagance in sleeping for the person who does not perform the prayer until the time of the next prayer arrives.
1443,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If there is any worldly work of yours, it is your business, and if there is a religious matter, it will come to me. (after) pay or pay on time the next day."
1444,"Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about people falling asleep during the prayer, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no Tafreet in falling asleep, the Tafreet is in waking up. The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) heard me narrating this hadith and said to me: O young man, remember the hadith you are narrating because I too have heard this hadith from the mouth of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
1445,"The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission, in which there is a similar story, but it contains these words: We said: Shall we not pay it tomorrow? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you from usury and will accept it himself."
1446,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: (After that, he narrated a tradition similar to this, which contains these words): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you from usury and He will accept it from you."
1447,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people of Makkah! Do not shorten the prayer by less than four barads (travelling a distance) equal to the distance from Makkah to Isfan."
1448,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once we traveled with the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) stayed for seventeen days, during which time the Prophet (PBUH) continued to offer short prayers. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas says: When we are travelers and stay for thirteen days, we shorten the prayer; if we stay longer than that, we offer the full prayer."
1449,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We stayed with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for seventeen days in one place during a journey, during which time we continued to offer short prayers. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We will offer short prayers for seventeen days; if we have to stay longer than that, we will offer complete prayers."
1450,"Kareeb narrates: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Shall I tell you about the way the Prophet (PBUH) prayed during a journey? We answered: Yes! So he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in his residence and the sun was setting (i.e. it was noon), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers together before leaving for the journey, and when the sun had not set when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present (in the house) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to leave, he would leave. Then when it was Asr time, at that time he would stop his journey and perform Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time. Likewise, if it was Maghrib time in the residence of the Prophet (peace be upon him), he would perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time, and if it was not Maghrib time, he would leave and perform these two prayers together at the time of Isha prayer. The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
1451,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was the custom of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when the sun went down, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and when he left before the sun set, he would postpone these two prayers and even the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform these two prayers at the time of the Asr prayer."
1452,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was encamped somewhere and the sun had already set, he would not leave until he had performed the Asr prayer, and if he had left before sunset, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would offer both prayers at the time of the Asr prayer."
1453,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to leave after the sun had set, he (may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him) would offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and if he had to leave before that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would postpone the Zuhr prayer until Asr time."
1454,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers together during a journey, he used to postpone the Zuhr prayer until the early Asr time came (so he used to perform both prayers together at that time)."
1455,"Ibn Shihab narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to set out on a journey before the sun set, he would set out until Asr time began, then he would halt and offer these two prayers together."
1456,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, so he would postpone the Zuhr prayer until the early time of Asr began, and then he would perform these two prayers together."
1457,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar came to Makkah and he was informed of the illness of his wife Safiyya bint Abu Ubaid, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar accelerated his journey. When the sun set, one of his companions said: It is time for prayer, but Sayyidna Abdullah remained silent. Ibn Umm (may God be pleased with him) continued walking until dusk fell, so he halted and called for prayer. Here the Nishapuri narrator has quoted a different word, the following words are agreed upon by the narrators who say: Sayyiduna Abdullah stood up and offered Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time. They used to perform their prayers regardless of the direction of the Suri. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) told these people: What the Prophet (PBUH) used to do in the same way."
1458,"Salim narrates: When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) was informed of his (wife) Safiyya's illness, he began to travel quickly, then he narrated a tradition similar to this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in which these words are: \Shortly after sunset\"". A narrator named Ibn Wahib followed him."""
1459,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would set out for a journey, he would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and when he started to leave before that, he would postpone the Zuhr prayer and perform the Asr prayer early and perform these two prayers together."
1460,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) had to travel fast, he used to perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time. A narrator has also quoted the words of, till the fourth night."
1461,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
1462,"Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk (this was the practice of the Holy Prophet) when the sun had set before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, he would perform the Zuhr and Asr prayers at the same time, and if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left before the sun set, he would delay the Zuhr prayer until he stopped for the Asr prayer. If the sun set before leaving, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform Maghrib and Isha prayers at the same time, and if he left before sunset, he would postpone the Maghrib prayer, then stop for Isha and perform these two prayers together."
1463,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but its chain of transmission is somewhat different."
1464,"Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was the custom of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk (from encampment during the journey) when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left before the sun set, he would postpone the Zuhr prayer until the time of Asr when he offered both of them together, and when he left after the sun had set, he would offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers together and then leave. In the same way, when he left before Maghrib, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to postpone the Maghrib prayer, until he offered it together with the Isha prayer, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left after the sunset, he would quickly offer the Isha prayer and perform it with the Maghrib prayer. Imam Abu Dawud has stated this: This hadith has been narrated only by a narrator named Qatadah."
1465,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1466,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was informed of the illness of his wife Safiyyah. He was traveling at that time. He accelerated his speed when the sun set and asked him to pray. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had to do something, he used to do it in the same way."
1467,"Nafee narrates a similar hadith on the authority of Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), but it contains these words: He encamped before twilight and offered the Maghrib prayer, and then he waited until twilight fell, then he offered the Isha prayer."
1468,"Narrated Nafi: I set out with Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, he was on his way to his land. He stopped at a place on the way. A man came to him and told him (his wife) Safia bint Abu Ubaid is in a critical condition and I think you will not be able to reach her (before her death). We were traveling until the sun set. I was closely related to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He used to pray with great regularity. I said: It is time for prayer. He did not pay attention to me and continued walking as he had been going before until when it was the end of twilight, he stopped and offered Maghrib prayer. Fascinated, he told us that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had to hurry in a matter, he used to do the same."
1469,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
1470,"Nafee narrated: Once we were coming from Makkah with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, until on the way he was told about the serious illness of his wife Safiyyah, so he sped up the journey. It was his custom to get down and offer the Maghrib prayer at the same time as the sun set, but that night it did not happen. He offered the prayer, then when the twilight had set, he stood up and offered the Isha prayer, then he turned towards us and told us, what we used to do with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
1471,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1472,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Jaafar (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray standing up, except in the case of fear of drowning. Imam Dar Qutni narrates: What is meant is that they should pray while standing in the Kushi."
1473,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Ja'far bin Abu Talib to Abyssinia, he said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we pray in a boat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Pray standing in it"," unless you are afraid of drowning.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition", Husain bin Alwan," is obsolete."""
1474,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about praying in a boat, and he said: “It is to be prayed standing up, but if you are afraid of drowning (the ruling is different)."
1475,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Whoever performs two prayers at the same time without any excuse will be guilty of a major sin. Shaykh says: The narrator named Hansh is Abu Ali Rahbi and it is abandoned.
1476,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was traveling and he had to perform the Nafl prayer, he used to turn his camel towards the Qiblah and then say Takbeer."
1477,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was on a journey and had to perform the Nafl prayer, he used to face the Qiblah and then say Takbeer."
1478,"Sayyidina Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was on a journey and had to perform the Nafl prayer, he (PBUH) would turn his camel towards the Qiblah, then say Takbeer and then start performing the prayer, regardless of the direction in which his stirrups were facing."
1479,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) sent me on some errand, and when I returned, you were on your horse. I greeted you, but you did not answer me. Then I saw you bowing and prostrating with gestures, so I stood aside. Then he said to me, \What did you do with your errand?\"" I said that I have done such and such. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not respond to you because I was praying."""
1480,Mahmood bin Labaid narrates: Sayyidna Asayd bin Hudair complained of ``Irq al-Nisa''. He was our Imam.
1481,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this as a hadeeth: One who prays while sitting gets half the reward of one who prays while standing, except for the person who sits cross-legged."
1482,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) sitting and praying.
1483,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a problem, he ordered Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to lead the people in prayer, then the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace) felt better, so he came and sat by Sayyidna Abu Bakr’s side. study"
1484,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this about Sayyidna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt better, so he walked (into the mosque) supported by two men. Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) came and sat by Sayyidna Abu Bakr's side. He started reciting from the place where Sayyidna Abu Bakr left off."
1485,Imam Shaabi narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that no one should lead while sitting.
1486,"Sayyiduna Salama bin Akwa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about praying with a bow, so he said, \Take off the horn and pray while wearing a bow.\"""""
1487,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates: \At the time of every prayer," take adornment\"". He says: This means praying with shoes on. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing shoes", then he took them off, so the people also took off their shoes. The people said," \""We saw you take off your shoes"," so we took them off.\"""""
1488,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to give food to our Imam during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
1489,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whoever gives a morsel to the Imam, he has spoken, (meaning his prayer will be broken). The narrator of this hadith is Muhammad bin Salem."
1490,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This is the word (says the narrator) that is, giving food to the Imam."
1491,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the Imam asks you for something to eat, feed him (i.e. give him a bite if he forgets)."
1492,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching us the prayer, he started reciting a surah, he left out a verse from it. When he finished the prayer, I said, \O Messenger of Allah", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," has such and such a verse been abrogated?\"""""
1493,Sayyidina Anas (RA) narrates: The Companions of the Prophet (PBUH) used to give each other morsels during prayer.
1494,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If one dirham of blood is applied, that prayer will be repeated. Some other narrators have not disagreed in narrating it."
1495,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when there is blood on the cloth as much as one dirham, then the cloth will be washed and the prayer will be performed again."
1496,The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and one of its narrators is obsolete.
1497,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the Imam returns the salam, you return the salam to the right and to the left, and after that you do not turn to any part of your prayer."
1498,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The prayer that you lead with the Imam will be your first prayer, and you should perform the recitation that has been completed before. Saeed bin Musayb also has the same opinion as Sayedna Ali."
1499,"Muhammad bin Shuaib narrates: I asked Imam Uza'i and Saeed bin Abdul Aziz about this, and they both said: Consider the part of the Imam's prayer that you have found to be the first part of your prayer."
1500,"Hasan al-Basri narrates: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill for ten days, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) led the people in prayer."
1501,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever prays in the lead of the Imam, the recitations of the Imam will be counted as his recitations. This tradition is rejected, its narrator Sahl bin Abbas is obsolete."
1502,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever is praying in the lead of the Imam, the recitation of the Imam will count as his recitation. A narrator named Abul Hasan has narrated it as a rejected hadith and it is an illusion."
1503,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says about reciting the Imam's recitation: It is enough for you to recite the Imam's recitation.
1504,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever has an Imam present, the recitations of the Imam will count as his recitations. This hadith is not authentic, Muhammad bin Abdarazi narrator is unique in narrating it and it is weak."
1505,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether recitation will be performed in every prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Yes, a person belonging to the Ansar said: It has become obligatory. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Darda turned to me and said: Because I was sitting closest to him among those present."
1506,"Sayyidah Umm Waraqa, may Allah be pleased with her, used to lead the Imamate (of women)."
1507,"Rita Hanafia narrates: Sayyida Aisha used to lead us, she used to stand among the women in the obligatory prayer."
1508,"Hujairah bint Hussain narrates: Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) led us in Asr prayer, and she stood between us. The same hadith has been narrated in some other contexts, but there is some illusion in its authenticity, and some have opposed it."
1509,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer. A person recited in his lead. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished praying, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Who is trying to interrupt these surahs?” Imam Darqutani (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: These words of the tradition, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade people from reciting in the lead of the Imam."
1510,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) recited Surah Al-Ala while performing the Zuhr prayer. (After finishing the prayer), the Prophet (PBUH) inquired which of you was reciting. A narrator named Shuba narrates, I asked Qatadah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapprove of this, he replied that if you had disapproved of it, you would have forbidden it."
1511,Sayyidna Masoor Bin Mukharama (RA) narrates: I saw Sayyidna Umar (RA) praying even though his wound was bleeding.
1512,"Sa'sa' bin Suhan narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said Takbeer five times, four times, and seven times in Iraq (in the funeral prayer). He has stated this: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said Takbeer (in the funeral prayer) eleven times, nine times, seven times, six times, five times, four times."
1513,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in Surah The narrator narrates: It is narrated only by a narrator named Hafs.
1514,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite this in the Sajdah recitation. \My face is bowed before the One who created it," gave it hearing and sight by His help and power.\"""""
1515,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Dawud (peace be upon him) prostrated here because of repentance, and we prostrate because of gratitude."
1516,"This hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, which is about this prostration which is in the hundredth chapter of Prophet Dawud (peace be upon him) who performed this prostration as a repentance, and we perform this prostration as a sign of gratitude."
1517,Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: He heard Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrating this.
1518,Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Syedna Uthman Ghani (RA) recited 100 verses on the pulpit and then got down and recited Sajdah.
1519,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: One day the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was delivering a sermon to us. There is an event of repentance and I see that you people are ready to prostrate, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down from the pulpit and he prostrated, so we also prostrated."
1520,"Sayyiduna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, taught him fifteen places in the Holy Qur'an where prostration is performed, three of them are in detailed surahs, and two are prostrations in the Hundred-Rah Hajj."
1521,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I asked: O Messenger of Allah, are there two prostrations in Hajj? He said yes, if you do not pay them then do not recite this surah."
1522,"Abdullah bin Tha'albah narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, he performed two prostrations in Surah Hajj. The narrator narrates: I inquired whether in the morning prayer? He answered yes, in the morning prayer."
1523,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (and with him) the jinn, humans and trees prostrated in the last verse of Surah Najam."
1524,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated while reciting Surah Najm, and the Muslims and polytheists also prostrated (with him)."
1525,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) recited this Surah, Al-Najm, and he prostrated in it."
1526,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I have recited Sajdah in Surah Al-Anshaqaq and Surah Al-Alak following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
1527,"Al-Khari bin Zayd narrates the statement of his father Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit Ansari: I recited Surah Najm in front of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and none of us prostrated. A narrator named Abu Sakhr narrates: I followed Umar bin Abdul Aziz and Abu Bakr bin Hazm (performed the prayer in which they recited this Surah), but they both did not recite Sajdah."
1528,"Abu Ja'afar narrates: The Holy Prophet saw a person who was imperfect, so he went into prostration."
1529,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates: Whenever the Prophet (PBUH) was happy, he (PBUH) would go into prostration to thank Allah."
1530,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates: Whenever the Prophet (PBUH) was in a happy situation or he (PBUH) was happy about something, he used to go into Sajdah."
1531,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This completes the prayer.
1532,"Jabir bin Yazid narrates the following statement from his father: I joined the Holy Prophet in his Hajj, I performed the morning prayer in the mosque of Khaif following him. When they went, both of them were trembling. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired why you two did not pray with us. They said, O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our residence. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do the Yesanah, when you have prayed in your residence, then you come to the mosque where the prayer is being offered with the congregation, then offer the prayer with the people, it will become a nafl prayer for you."
1533,"This tradition has been narrated along with some other isnads, but these words are added in it: One of them said: O Messenger of Allah! If you pray for forgiveness for us, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Allah has forgiven you.\"""""
1534,"Jabir bin Yazid narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the Fajr prayer in Mina. When he finished the prayer, he saw two men behind the people. He called both of them. They were both trembling. He inquired why you did not offer the prayer with the people. They both said: We had already offered the prayer in our residence. He said: \You should do Asana when a person has offered the prayer in his residence and then he is the imam.\"" If he performs congregational prayer along with the Imam"," then it will become nafl for him."""
1535,"The same hadith is narrated along with some other isnads, but it contains these words: \So you people should pray with him and declare it as a Nafl prayer.\"" Some other narrators have narrated a tradition contrary to it."""
1536,"Jabir bin Yazid narrates the statement of his father: I prayed in the footsteps of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. When he finished the prayer, he saw two men behind the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do this. When a person has prayed in his home and then he comes to the Imam, he should offer the prayer with the Imam and the prayer he prayed in his home should be considered as Nafl."
1537,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a tradition similar to this regarding the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): However, it contains these words: \It will become a Nafl for both of you and what you performed in your residence will be an obligatory prayer.\"" This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."""
1538,This tradition along with some other isnads is narrated by Jabir bin Yazid from his father.
1539,This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid.
1540,The same hadith is related to Jabir bin Yazid in the same manner as the hadith of Shu'ba.
1541,"Basr bin Muhjan narrates this statement of his father: Once he was sitting with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and offered the prayer. When he came back, Sayyiduna Muhjan was sitting in his place. Aren't you a Muslim? He said yes! O Messenger of Allah, but I had prayed in my house, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, when you come, pray with the people, even if you have already prayed. These words of the hadith are from Imam Malik, and its meaning is close."
1542,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not perform the (same) obligatory prayer twice in a day.
1543,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1544,"Ghulam Sulaiman, the slave of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) narrates: One day, I attended the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA), he was sitting in the court and the people were performing Asr prayer at that time. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman! People are praying? He said: I have performed the prayer (now I am not performing this prayer with the people) because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: An obligatory prayer will not be performed twice in a day."
1545,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform eleven rak'ahs between the time he finished the Isha prayer and the time when the morning prayer came. In them, he would say salam after every two rak'ahs and he would make them stand by one rak'ah. If so, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up and perform two short rak'ahs, then he would lie down on his right side until the muezzin came to call him for prayer, and he would accompany him. Various narrators have narrated this incident with a lack of words."
1546,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The nawafl of the night and the day shall be paid by dudu.
1547,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Nawafs of the night and the day will be paid in two.
1548,"Sayyidna Matal Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Nafl) Prayer will be performed two by two. After praying two rakats, you will sit in Tashahhud, show humility and raise your hands and say Ya Allah, Ya Allah. Whoever does not do this (his prayer) will be incomplete. The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidna Fazl bin Abbas with reference to another chain of transmission."
1549,"Yasar narrates: Once, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) saw me praying (Nafal) in the morning after becoming righteous, and while hitting me with pebbles, he said, \O Jesus! How many rakaat have you performed? I replied"," \""I don't remember.\"" He said: \""You don't understand. Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and we were performing the Nawafil prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed his great displeasure at us and said: Let all those present convey this to those who are not present: After being righteous in the morning"," only two rak'ahs (Sunnah) can be offered."""
1550,"Yasar narrates: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) saw me reciting Nawafil after I became righteous in the morning, and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: O Yasar! Once, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and we were performing this Nawafil prayer at that time, so he said: All people should convey this to those who are not present."
1551,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: After the morning prayer, no prayer can be offered except two rak'ahs of the Sunnah."
1552,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) found some people absent during the prayer (in congregation) and inquired: Why did those people not participate in the prayer? So the people told him that he had some work to do, so he said: A person who lives in the neighborhood of the mosque prays only in the mosque. These words of the tradition are from the narrator named Ibn Mukhlid: while the narrator named Abu Hamid has quoted these words: A person who hears the call to prayer and does not come (to the mosque) does not pray, but if there is an excuse, then (the ruling is different)."
1553,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the person who lives in the neighborhood of the mosque prays only in the mosque.
1554,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whoever lives in the neighborhood of the mosque and hears the muezzin giving the call to prayer and does not come (to the mosque to offer prayers) without an excuse, then his prayer is not performed."
1555,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever hears the call to prayer and does not respond to it (i.e. does not come to the mosque to pray in congregation), his prayer is not performed, but if there is an excuse, then (the ruling is different)."
1556,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, while some narrators have quoted it as a marfu' hadith."
1557,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who listens to the call to prayer and does not have an excuse to obey him (i.e. going to pray in congregation), people asked what is meant by an excuse? He said: Fear or illness (the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then Allah will not accept the prayer that this person has offered (in his home)."
1558,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a person forgets a prayer and then remembers that prayer while he is performing another prayer, he should first perform his current prayer, when he is finished with it, then perform the prayer that he forgot."
1559,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: When a person forgets a prayer and then remembers that prayer when he is in the lead of the Imam, he should perform the prayer followed by the Imam."
1560,"Some narrators have narrated it as a marfu' hadith, but these narrators are delusional about it."
1561,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Praying while sitting has half the reward of praying while standing, and praying while lying down has half the reward of praying while sitting."
1562,"Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) was riding a horse in Madinah, and he was injured by a palm trunk, as a result of which his foot was injured. He stayed in the house of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa. When we came to your service (the next time), you were performing the obligatory prayer at that time. We stood behind you, so you indicated to us that we should sit down. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Follow the Imam."
1563,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the word, Nafl, is not mentioned in it."
1564,"Ibrahim bin Ubaid narrates: I attended the service of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, and I found his companions sitting and leading the prayer. When they had finished praying, I asked them about it. Pray standing and when he prays sitting, you should also pray sitting."
1565,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever forgets to pray, the time to perform it will be when he remembers it.”"
1566,"Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Mut'am Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Banu Abd Manaf, if you become the supervisor of this task, then you should never prevent anyone from circumambulating the House of Allah and offering prayers, regardless of the time of day or night."
1567,"Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut’im (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): O Banu Abd Manaf (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words) O children of Qusay: Do not prevent anyone from circumambulating the House of Allah and offering prayers here, whatever part of the day or night."
1568,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: O Banu Abd Manaf: Be careful not to prevent anyone from praying at this House of Allah, no matter what time of the day or night."
1569,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Banu Abdul Munaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House of Allah, whatever the time of the day or night."
1570,"Nafi bin Jubayr narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in reference to his father: O Banu Abd Manaf, do not forbid anyone who is praying near this House of Allah, whatever the time of the day or night."
1571,"Mujahid narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Zar Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, came to Makkah, he held the door frame of the Kaaba and said: Whoever knows me knows me, but whoever does not know me (let him know) I am Jandab (and my surname is Abu Dhar). And no (Nafal) prayer can be performed from the time of the Asr prayer until the sunset, although the ruling of Makkah is different."
1572,"Sayyiduna Jubayr bin Mut'ayim (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, O Banu Abdul Muttalib! You should not prevent anyone from praying at this House of Allah, no matter what time of the day or night."
1573,"Nafi bin Jubayr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this, O Banu Abd Manaf! O Banu Hashim, if this matter were in Your power, I would never prevent a person circumambulating this house (and anyone praying near it) from (circumcising or offering prayers) at any time of the night or day."
1574,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words. \You shall not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House of Allah at any time of the day or night."""
1575,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) O Banu Abd Manaf, do not stop anyone who is performing Tawaf of this House of Allah (or near it), because the morning prayer is not a prayer until the sun rises, and after the Asr prayer, there is no prayer until the sun sets. However, the order near this house in Mecca is different. (Here) people can circumambulate (at these times) and pray."
1576,": Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, it is obligatory for him to perform the Friday prayer on Friday. He will take care of this person, and Allah is Careless and Praiseworthy."
1577,"-: Tariq bin Shahab narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: It is obligatory for all people to read Fridays, not only for the four: a slave, a (minor) child, a sick person and a woman."
1578,": Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: (We are the ones who will come later and the Day of Resurrection will be the ones ahead). The reason for this is: Those people were given the Book before us and we were given the Book after them. So this is the Day that Allah made obligatory on these people and then Allah guided us about it, so people are our followers in this regard. The Jewish day is tomorrow (Saturday) and the Christian day is the day after (Saturday)."
1579,"-: Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu: This method is being used: When three people are present, one of them will be the imam, and where there are forty people or more, there will be Friday prayer, Eid al-Zuha prayer, and Eid al-Fitr prayer. The reason for this is: these people are considered as one congregation."
1580,"- Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (in a village) there are fifty people, Jumu'ah will be obligatory on them, and it will not be obligatory on less than that."
1581,: 1563 Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this: It is obligatory to pray Jumu'ah for fifty people.
1582,: 1564 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is not necessary for a traveler to read Friday.
1583,": 1565 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A certain Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to us on Friday. At the same time, a caravan came with grain and that caravan stopped in an open field. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) revealed this verse: And when they saw the thing of trade and interest, they went towards it and left you in a state of stay."
1584,": 1566 Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon while standing on Friday. Meanwhile, a caravan came (After that, the narrator has narrated the entire hadith, after which these words follow):"
1585,"Muhammad bin Abu Umamah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b (may God be pleased with him) regarding his father: I used to take my father with me when his sight was gone. Once I took him to perform the Friday prayer. After hearing the call to prayer, he prayed for mercy and asked for forgiveness for Sayyiduna Abu Umamah. asked them: O Abajan! Every time you hear the call to prayer on Friday, you pray for forgiveness for Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu. What is the reason for this? So he replied: O my son! He (Sayyidna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him) was the first person who started Jumu'ah in the low ground of the stone yellow plain of Banu Bayadah in Madinah, the name of this place is \Naqi' al-Khuzmat\"". So they replied: There were forty persons."""
1586,: 1568 This hadith is narrated along with another document.
1587,": 1569 The same tradition is also transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but it also contains these words: In the low part of the rocky land of Banubayzah where plants grow and which is called \Naqee Al-Khuzmat\"" the rest of the tradition is the same as the previous tradition."""
1588,": 1570 Amro bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather: Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the voice (of the muezzin)."
1589,": 1571 Amro bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: \Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the voice of wisdom.\"""""
1590,: 1572 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the call to prayer on Friday.
1591,": 1573 The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the word \Tazeen\"" is used here."""
1592,": 1574 Sayyidah Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Friday is obligatory for those who live in every settlement, even if only four people remain in that settlement."
1593,": 1575 Sayyidah Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It is obligatory to read the Friday prayer for those living in a Haras settlement, in which the Imam is present, even though there are only four people present in this settlement."
1594,": 1576 Sayyida Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: It is obligatory for the residents of every town to read Friday, even if only three people remain there and the fourth is their imam."
1595,": 1577 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday, he should add another rak'ah to it."
1596,: 1578 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday should perform another rak'ah along with it.
1597,": 1579 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should offer the second rak'ah along with it, and if he finds the people in a gathering during the Friday prayer, then he should offer four rak'ahs."
1598,": 1580: Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday, let him perform another rak'ah along with it."
1599,": 1581 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Whoever finds one rak'ah of the Friday prayer, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it."
1600,": 1582 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and if he finds people in a state of burning, then he should perform four rak'ahs."
1601,": 1583 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and whoever misses two rak'ahs, then he should perform four rak'ahs (Zhuhr)."
1602,": 1584 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person observes two rak'ahs of Friday, he has observed the Friday prayer. The words are equivalent."
1603,": 1585 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: He who prays the second rak'ah on Friday should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and whoever does not perform the rak'ah of the second rak'ah should perform the four rak'ahs of Zuhr."
1604,": 1586 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet (SAW) saying: When you perform the second rak'at of Friday, perform another rak'at along with it, and if the second rak'at is also missed, then perform four rak'ats of Zuhr."
1605,": 1587 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) said this: Whoever finds the Imam in a state of assembly, 'He did not return the salam', then he performed this prayer."
1606,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever performs one rak’at of the Friday prayer or any other prayer, then he adds a second rak’at to it, then his prayer will be complete. is:"
1607,": 1589 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever observes one rak'ah of Friday, he should add another rak'ah to it."
1608,: 1590 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever observes one rak'ah in Friday (Friday prayer) has observed this prayer and adds another rak'ah to it.
1609,": 1591 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) said this: When one of you observes one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform another rak'ah along with it."
1610,": 1592 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) came, the Prophet (PBUH) was delivering the sermon on Friday. If you are giving a sermon, then that person should perform two rak'ahs and perform them briefly."
1611,": 1593 Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) came. The Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to the people at that time. He sat down. The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a person comes on Friday and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time, that person should perform two short rak'ahs and then sit down."
1612,": 1594 Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) narrated this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When someone from among you comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon, he should perform two short rak'ahs and perform them quickly."
1613,": 1595 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this during the sermon: When a person from among you comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon at that time, the narrator has this doubt."
1614,": 1596 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): When a person comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon at that time, then that person performs two rak'ahs. So he replied: Yes!"
1615,": 1597 Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this while giving a sermon: When a person comes and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time, and that person should perform two rak'ahs."
1616,": 1598 Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this while giving a sermon: \When a person comes and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time"," that person should perform two rak'ahs.\"""""
1617,": 1599 Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was giving a sermon on Friday, while a person came in and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray two rak'ahs."
1618,": 1600 Narrated Anas: A man from the tribe of Qays entered (the mosque). The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon at that time. It is correct: this Mu'tamarnami has been transmitted as a messenger tradition with reference to the narrator's father, but Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal has narrated it in the same way."
1619,: 1601 Mu'tamar narrates this statement of his father: A person came (inside the mosque) while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was giving a sermon. Have you prayed? He said: No! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So you should pray. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept waiting for him until he prayed.
1620,": 1602 Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radi Allahu Anhu narrates: On Friday, Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (Radi Allahu Anhu) entered (inside the mosque) and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Pray two rak'ats and do not do it again."
1621,": 1603 Muhammad bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray two rak'ahs, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped the sermon until he had finished two rak'ahs, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued his sermon."
1622,": 1604 Muhammad bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray this prayer, he stopped his sermon until he had finished praying."
1623,": 1605 Abdullah bin Saidan Salmi narrates: I performed the Friday prayer following the example of Sayyidna Abu Bakr, his prayer and his sermon used to be before noon."
1624,: 1606 Iyas bin Salamah narrates this statement of his father: We used to perform the Friday prayer with our father following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then when we came back we did not find any shade under which we should come.
1625,: 1607 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: We used to do qilaulah after Friday and eat food.
1626,: 1608 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: We used to do qilaula after Friday and eat food.
1627,: 1609 The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad (RA).
1628,: 1610 Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to perform the Friday prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then there would be Qailula after that.
1629,": 1611 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) narrates: We used to leave early to perform the Friday prayer following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), then when we came back, we would eat lunch and do Qilaula."
1630,: 1612 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to deliver two sermons.
1631,": 1613 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: There are three things that are obligatory on me and for you they are nafl: performing the sacrifice, performing the Witr prayer, and performing two rak'ahs of the Fajr Sunnah."
1632,: 1614 Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been ordered to perform Witr prayer and sacrifice and I have not been obliged to do so.
1633,": 1615 Saeed bin Yasarbayan says: I was traveling on the way to Makkah with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyid narrates: When I had this apprehension that the dawn was about to dawn, I got off the horse and offered the Witr prayer. Then I came to meet Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, asked me: Where did you stay? I said: I was afraid of being honest in the morning, so I got down from the horse and went to pray. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar asked: Is it not enough for you to follow the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
1634,": 1616 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (PBUH): He (PBUH) used to perform nawafl on top of his horse, no matter which direction it was facing."
1635,": 1617 It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that he used to perform the Witr prayer on top of his horse, and he has mentioned this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (that is, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same)."
1636,": 1618 Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to perform the Nafl prayer on top of his horse, and when he had to perform Witrād, he would get off the horse and perform the Witrah."
1637,": 1619 Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps without performing Witr or forgets to perform Witr, he should perform it in the morning or when he remembers."
1638,": 1620 Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked: If one of us prays in the morning and he has not yet performed Witrah, the Prophet (Peace be upon him) said: He should perform Witrah in the morning."
1639,: 1621 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever commits ablution at night," he should make up for it the next day.\"""""
1640,": 1622 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Witrhaq is right and obligatory. Whoever wants to perform three Witradas should perform three, and whoever wants to perform one Rakat, then he should perform one Rakat and Witrada. Be of"
1641,: 1623 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever wants to pray five rak'ahs, whoever wants to pray three rak'ahs," and whoever wants to pray one rak'ah.\"""""
1642,": 1624 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: There are twenty-five, three or one."
1643,": 1625 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is right for whoever wants to pray seven rak'ahs in the morning, whoever wants to pray five rak'ahs, whoever wants to pray three witr's and whoever wants to pray one witr."
1644,": 1626 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: You should perform five rak'ahs and witr's. If you cannot afford it, perform three."
1645,: 1627 The same tradition is narrated along with another document.
1646,": 1628 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: It is permissible for anyone who wishes to pray five rak'ahs, whoever wishes to pray three rak'ahs, and whoever wishes to pray one rak'ah, and whoever is able to only point, let him point."
1647,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1648,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I said, O Messenger of Allah! How much do I have? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I asked, O Prophet of Allah! I have more power than that. Then the Holy Prophet said three. Then he said five. Then he said seven. At that time, I would have accepted the leave given by the Prophet."
1649,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the two rakats of Witr in the later rakats, and in these two rakats he would recite Surah Al-Aali and Surah Al-Kafrun, while in the second rakat he would recite Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq and Surah Al-Nas."
1650,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: perform three rak'ahs and divide them into five or seven rak'ahs and do not compare it to Maghrib prayer.
1651,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform three rak'ahs and alternate them with five rak'ahs or seven rak'ahs. Do not compare it to Maghrib prayer."
1652,"Qays bin Abu Hazim narrates: I saw Sayyidna Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, perform one rak'ah after Isha, so I inquired which prayer it was. So he replied, I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing one rak'ah and witrada."
1653,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There are three Witrs of the night, just as there are three rak’ahs of the Witr of the day (i.e. the evening prayer)."
1654,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates what the Prophet (PBUH) used to do while riding his horse.
1655,Saeed bin Yasar Bayan says: \I got off the horse and said, 'Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me," 'Isn't the good deeds of the Messenger of Allah sufficient for you? I said yes! So he said: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do while riding?"""
1656,"Sayyiduna Al-Khazaifah bin Hudhafa (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) came to us, he (PBUH) said, “Allah has given you one more prayer, which is better for you than red camels.” It is the Witr prayer."
1657,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us, and the blessed face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, showed a state of happiness and contentment. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Allah, the Most High, has given you one more prayer, and that prayer is the Witr prayer."
1658,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather, \A long time passed that we did not pray any more than five prayers.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us and we gathered together. The narrator (i.e. Ubaidullah) Muhammad bin Ubaidullah Azim is weak."""
1659,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform three rak'ahs of Witrada, in which he used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun and Surah Al-Ikhlas. used to do"
1660,"Sayyiduna Abi Ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun, Surah Al-Ikhlas in the three rak'ats of Witr, and before going into Ruku, he recited the Qunoot Dua."
1661,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Ala, Surah Al-Kafrun and Surah Al-Ikhlas during the Witr prayer."
1662,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates that one night I stayed with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in order to find out when the Qunut prayer is recited in the Witr prayer. How do I pray Qunut? So my mother came and told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Qunut before bowing.
1663,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Qunut before bowing in the Witr prayer.
1664,"Sayyidna Suwayd bin Ghafla (RA) narrates, I have heard Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Uthman, Sayyidna Ali (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qunut at the end of Witr. These Companions also used to do the same."
1665,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to not return salam after performing two rak'ahs of witr.
1666,"Muhammad bin Sirin narrates that I asked Sayyidna Anas bin Malik about the Dua of Qunut, and he replied that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Dua of Qunut after bowing."
1667,"Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Anas, may the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite the Qunut supplication in the morning prayer. He answered yes! (It has been read) Narrator narrates, then it was asked whether the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qunoot supplication in the Fajr prayer. So they answered yes! It is recited a little after Ruku."
1668,Abu Uthman narrates that Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (RA) used to recite Qunut after Ruku in the morning prayer.
1669,"Qays bin Abu Hazim narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Sa'd (RA) performing one rak'ah after the Isha prayer, so I asked him which prayer it was. So he said, I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing one rakat and witrada."
1670,"Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman narrates that Sayyidna Saad bin Abi Waqqas (RA) offered the Isha prayer, then performed one rak'ah and then a person asked him, O Abu Ishaq! Didn't I see you performing one rak'ah and witrada? So they inquired, then Sayyidna Saad said, O blind! Will you teach me my religion?"
1671,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \Will you teach me the method of my prayer?\"""""
1672,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform one rak'ah and witrada.
1673,"Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman narrates that once I thought that tonight no place would be able to separate me from Ibrahim. A man came and placed his hand between my shoulders. You performed one rak'ah, so they replied that it was my witr."
1674,"Ibn Abi Malikah narrates that a person said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him: \Do you not wonder about Sayyidna Mu'awiya", may God be pleased with him," who prays one rak'ah and Witrada?\"" Then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas", may God be pleased with him, said," \""Yes"," he is a jurist.\"""""
1675,"Syed Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the first rak'ah of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was the second rak'ah of Witr, in which he used to recite Surah Al-Ala and Surah Al-Kafrun and then in the witr rak'at he recited Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq and Surah Al-Nas."
1676,Syed Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform three rak'ahs of witrada.
1677,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Witr.
1678,"The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, along with another chain of transmission."
1679,"Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Anfal on his ride, regardless of the direction it was facing, he used to perform the Witr on him, but he did not perform the obligatory prayer while riding."
1680,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform the Witr prayer on his horse.
1681,"The freed slave of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that once we were on a journey with the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
1682,Sayyida Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform a short rak'at after Witr.
1683,"The freed slave of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: We were on a journey with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: \Travel causes trouble and fatigue", so when a person performs Witrah, then he should perform two rak'ahs after that. If he wakes up, then it is fine," otherwise these two rak'ahs will be enough for him.\"""""
1684,Sayyidna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Qunut in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers. The narrator Abu Bakr Naami has narrated this.
1685,Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Qunut in the morning and evening prayers.
1686,Muhammad bin Sirin narrated this hadith to me by the person who had performed the Fajr prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head after the second rak'ah and stood for a while (i.e. during which he recited the Qunut prayer).
1687,Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to recite Qunut in whatever duty he performed.
1688,"Abdullah bin Nafi' narrated this statement of Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) regarding his father. The narrators of this hadith, Muhammad bin Yala, Anbasa, Abdullah bin Nafi, are all weak, and it is not proven that another narrator, Nafi, heard the hadith from Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA)."
1689,"This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is related to Safia bint Abu Ubayd from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but this woman named Safia was not blessed with the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
1690,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) went into Ruku during the prayer, then he raised his head and said this dua. O Allah! Save Ayyash bin Rabia! O Allah! Save Salma bin Hisham! O Allah! Give salvation to Waleed bin Waleed! O Allah! Save the weak Muslims! O Allah! Send down your harshness harmful (on the members of the tribe)! O Allah! In the time of Syedna Yusuf (peace be upon him), impose a famine on them! (O Allah!) Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went into prostration."
1691,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, \I pray in a better way than all of you according to the way of the Prophet (PBUH).\"" The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) in the last rak'ah of the Zuhr 'Isha prayer"," \""after reading Sama'Allah Liman Hamda"," he used to recite Qunut and pray for the believers and curse the disbelievers.\"""""
1692,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) continued to recite Qunut in the Fajr prayer until he (PBUH) left this world.
1693,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Qunut for a month, in which he prayed for harm for them (infidels), then he abandoned it."
1694,"Rabi bin Anas narrates that once I was sitting with Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Qunut for a month."
1695,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that I have prayed following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) 'The Prophet (PBUH) kept reciting the Qunut after bowing in the morning prayer until I separated from him. (i.e. he left the world).
1696,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I recited Dua Qunut following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) until I separated from them (i.e. they left this world).
1697,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman (the narrator says 'I think' he also mentioned the fourth Caliph) recited the Dua of Qunut, 'until I separated from them."
1698,Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyidna Anas (RA) said to me that I recited Dua Qunut following the example of the Prophet (PBUH) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) until I became separated from both of them.
1699,Abu Tufail narrates this about Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with them) that both of them prayed following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qunut supplication in the morning prayer.
1700,"Sayyidna Hasan Basri says, \Whoever forgets to recite Qunut in the morning prayer"," it is necessary to perform Sajdah on him.\"""""
1701,"Saeed bin Abdulaziz says about this person, \Whoever forgets to recite the Qunoot prayer in the morning prayer"," it is necessary to perform prostration on him.\"""""
1702,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform two rak'ahs after Witr, and he used to perform this rak'ah sitting down. Narrator Abu Bakr-Nami has stated that this is the method which the people of Basra are unique in imitating and the people of Syria have preserved it."
1703,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) kept reciting Qunut prayers until he left this world.
1704,"Saeed bin Jubayr (RA) narrates, “I bear witness that I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) saying, ‘Reciting Qunut in the morning prayer is an innovation."
1705,"Abu Qalaba says: I met Sayyidna Amr, and he told me this hadith: We used to live in a place where there was water and it was a passage for people. Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I kept remembering that word and it became firm in my heart. The common Arabs suspended their acceptance of Islam with the conquest of Makkah. They used to say that this Prophet and his people should be justified. If he prevails over his people, then he will be a true prophet. When we received the news of the conquest of Makkah, every nation hurried to accept Islam. He stayed with the Holy Prophet for some time. When he returned from serving the Holy Prophet, we went to meet him. When he saw us, he swore by Allah! I am coming to you from the true Messenger of Allah. He has ordered you to do this. He has said that this is how you should pray at this time. This is how you should pray at this time. This is how you should pray at this time. I was made to stand in front 'I was 6 or 7 years old at that time' 'I had a cloak which was small' I used to go to Sajdah and it was removed, so a woman of the tribe said: Why don't you people cover the back part of your Qari? Then the tribesmen gave me a shirt which was made of Bahraini cloth."
1706,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) quotes his father (Imam Baqir) on Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) on the authority of Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If the sick person is able to pray standing, then he should pray standing, otherwise he should pray sitting. He should pray and both his feet should be in the direction of Qiblah."
1707,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates that a sick person should pray with his feet facing the Qibla while lying on the mat.
1708,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person is praying and he vomits, he should put his hand over his mouth and ask someone who is the best among those present to lead him. If it has not been done, then he will pray anew."
1709,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Sunnah is that a person should not go out (to pray the Eid prayer) until he has taken some food and paid Sadaqah al-Fitr.
1710,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that (a person) should not go out on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he has taken some food and given Sadaqah al-Fitr.
1711,"Hanash bin Mu'tamarbayan narrates, \I saw Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of Eid-ul-Adha. He kept reciting Takbeer until he reached the Eidgah.\"""""
1712,It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to leave the mosque to pray the Eid prayer and would continue to recite the Takbeer until he reached the Eidgah and would continue to recite the Takbeer until the Imam came.
1713,"Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that in earlier times, people used to recite Takbeer on Eid-ul-Fitr with greater intensity (i.e. louder) than on Eid-ul-Adha."
1714,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to leave his house on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr and start reciting Takbeer until he (PBUH) used to come to the Eidgah.
1715,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Buraidah (RA) narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (PBUH) did not go out (to pray) on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he had eaten something, and he (PBUH) did not eat anything on the day of Eid-ul-Adha until he returned (after performing the Eid prayer) then he used to eat the meat of the sacrifice. Abdul Samadnami the narrator has quoted these words until he used to sacrifice."
1716,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that 'when he would leave on the day of Eid al-Ladha or the day of Eid al-Fitr, he would recite the takbeer continuously until he reached the place of Eid."
1717,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he ate some dates.
1718,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go out (to pray) on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr until he had eaten some dates.
1719,Ubaydullah bin Abdullah narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) asked Sayyidna Abu Waqid Laithi (RA) which surah the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite in the Eid-ul-Fitr prayer and in the Eid-ul-Zhaha prayer. So he replied: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Surah Q and Surah Uqtarbat.
1720,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited twelve takbeers in addition to the initial takbeer in the prayers of both Eids.
1721,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say seven takbirs in the first rak'at of the Eid prayer and five takbirs in the second rak'at.
1722,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) about the Holy Prophet (PBUH).
1723,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said, 'Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar (RA) used to perform the Eid prayer before giving the sermon."
1724,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, “On the day of Eid, I participated in the prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
1725,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform any prayer before this prayer and after this prayer (the narrator narrates), i.e. the Eid prayer."
1726,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say seven and five takbeers in the prayers of Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Zuha. These words are from the narration of Abu Tahirnami narrator.
1727,"Abdullah bin Muhammad narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say seven takbirs in the first rakat of the Eid prayer, and in the second rakat, he said five takbirs: He used to pray before giving the sermon."
1728,"Amro bin Shoaib, regarding his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said twelve takbirs in the prayer of both Eids, that is, in the prayer of Eid al-Zuha and in the prayer of Eid al-Fitr: He used to say seven takbirs in the first rakat and five takbirs in the second rakat."
1729,"Along with another chain of transmission, it has been narrated about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that seven takbirs will be recited in the first rakat and five takbirs will be recited in the second rakat and the recitation in both rakats will be after these takbirs."
1730,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement on the authority of his father, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited seven takbirs in the first rak'at on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr and five takbirs in the second rak'at.\"" These were in addition to the takbirs of the prayer."""
1731,"Kathir bin Abdullah narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say takbirs in the Eid prayer: He used to say seven takbirs in the first rak'at and five takbirs in the second rak'at. Bukhari quoted these words additionally in his tradition. Before reciting (used to say takbirs)."
1732,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Takbirs will be recited during the Eids.
1733,"Abu Tufail, Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib and Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir, may Allah be pleased with them, narrate this that they cursed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to recite Bismillah along with Surah Al-Fatiha in the obligatory prayer, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the dua of Qunut in the Fajr prayer and in the Witr prayer, and he used to recite the Dua of Qunut in the Fajr prayer and in the Witr prayer, and during the days of Tashreeq, from the beginning of the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah to the days of Tashreeq. On the last day till Asr prayer, on which day people leave in large numbers, they recite Takbeer after every fard prayer."
1734,Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim in a loud voice in the obligatory prayer.
1735,Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Takbeer after the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah and continued to recite it until the Asr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq.
1736,Imam Muhammad Al-Bas Qar (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to say Takbeer on the day of Arafah and he used to finish this act on the last day of ``Tashreeq''.
1737,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) offered the morning prayer on the day of Arafah, he (PBUH) turned to his companions and said, “Stay in your place.” Then he (PBUH) started reciting this. \Allah is the greatest", Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, There is no god but Allah, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest," All praise is for Allah.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to start reciting this takbeer in the morning on the day of Arafah and continued reciting it (after every prayer) until Asr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."""
1738,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sa'ib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was participating in the Eid prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said, \Now we will give the sermon to whoever wants to sit down (the narrator narrates means to sit down to listen to the sermon) and whoever wants to go"," let him go.\"""""
1739,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the takbeer of the days of Tashreeq will begin after noon on the day of sacrifice and it will be recited for the last time in the morning prayer on the last day of the days of Tashreeq.
1740,The previous hadith has been narrated from two different sources.
1741,"Narrated by Abdul Malik bin Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Farah (Abu Marwan), on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farah, on the authority of Abu Salama Al-Hazrami, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
1742,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): People (i.e. the Companions) used to say Takbeer after Zuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice and they used to say Takbeer until Zuhr prayer on the last day of Tashreeq.
1743,"A narrator named Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father, when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) was confined, he started saying Takbeer in front of us on the Day of Sacrifice from the Zuhr prayer, and he recited the Takbeer until the Zuhr prayer on the last day of ``Tashreeq'' (the last day of ``Tashreeq'')."
1744,"A narrator named Abdullah narrates this about Sayyidna Umar and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with them. Both of them used to perform Zuhr prayer in Dadi Mohsab on the day of their return and did not say Takbeer after that."
1745,It has been narrated about Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say Takbeer after all prayers during the days of Tashreeq: He used to recite Allahu Akbar three times.
1746,The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
1747,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went inside the Kaaba, then he came outside. Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was behind him. He answered no! The narrator narrates that the next day, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again went inside the Kaaba. He answered yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed two rak'ats. He turned towards the trunk of the tree and placed the second pillar on his right."
1748,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) entered the Kaaba, and Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) was also with him."
1749,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went inside the Ka’ba, and he prayed two rak’ahs among his friends. He asked the people and came outside (this time the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not pray inside the Kaaba)."
1750,"Sayyidna Masurabin Mukharama (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah Ibn Abbas (RA) came to the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA) when he was wounded. He said, Ameerul-Mu'minin, it is time for prayer. Sayyidna Umar (RA) said, \There is no place in Islam for such a person to offer prayer.\"" Then Sayyidna Umar (RA) performed the prayer"," although blood was flowing from his wound at that time."""
1751,Abdullah bin Burida narrates this statement of his father: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the main difference between us and them (infidels) is to perform the prayer.
1752,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated by Abdullah bin Baridah from his father.
1753,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: “The main difference between a servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer.”
1754,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Kufr (the narrator has doubts, perhaps this is the word) between polytheism and faith (the main difference) is abandoning prayer."
1755,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The (main difference) between a servant and a disbeliever is abandoning prayer.\"""""
1756,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there was a person whose worship and austerity we liked very much. We mentioned this person to the Prophet (peace be upon him). At the same time, that person came forward. We said, 'This is that person.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You are telling me about a person who has the mark of Satan on his face.' There is no one more virtuous than me and no better than me.' The person replied, 'Allah knows.' I asked Sayyidna Abub! Sayyidna Abu Bakr (peace be upon him) went to him and he was praying. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (peace be upon him) thought this. Shall I kill such a person who is offering Salat?', although the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing those who pray.'"
1757,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Umar Bin Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to kill those who pray.
1758,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had henna on both his hands and feet. People said, O Messenger of Allah! It resembles women, so it was ordered that it should be taken out of Madinah and sent to a place called Naqi'. It was said, O Messenger of Allah! Shouldn't we kill him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am forbidden to kill the worshipers. In one tradition these words are: A eunuch was brought who had henna applied to both his hands and feet."
1759,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “After me, there will be some rulers over you. A righteous person will be your ruler along with his good deeds and a sinner will be along with his sins. You will get your reward, they will get their sin."
1760,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that there are four characteristics that I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I did not tell you about them. Today I will tell you about them. Do not make takfir because of the sin of one of my people of the Qiblah, even if he commits a great sin, and offer prayer following the example of every imam, and wage jihad with Haramir (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words), fight, and the fourth thing is Abu Bakr Sadiq, Umar, Uthman and Ali, and say only good things and say this. \This Ummah has passed away", they will get the reward for the good deeds they did," and you will get the reward for the good deeds you do.\"""""
1761,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Every person who believes that there is no god but Allah," perform his funeral prayer and pray behind every person who believes that there is no god but Allah.\"""""
1762,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: perform the funeral prayer for each person, believing in God alone, and pray behind each person, believing in God alone."
1763,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
1764,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this. It is obligatory on you to pray in the lead of every Muslim, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins, and it is obligatory on you to fight with Haramir, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins, and it is obligatory on you to offer the funeral prayer for every Muslim who dies, whether he is righteous or sinful, even if he commits major sins."
1765,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this. Among the basic teachings of the religion, this is included: \Prayer will be offered behind every good person and sinner"," and Jihad will be fought with Haramir.\"""""
1766,"Sayyiduna Wathila Bin Asqaa (RA) narrates, \The Prophet (PBUH) said: Do not make takfir of your people of the Qiblah", even if they commit major sins, and pray in the lead of every Imam, and participate in Jihad along with Haramir," and perform the funeral prayer for every deceased.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Abu Saeed," is unknown."""
1767,"Sayyidna Wathila bin Asqaa (RA) narrates the same in reference to the Prophet (PBUH), but in it there are these words: \Perform the funeral prayer for every deceased among the people of the Qibla.\"""""
1768,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Pray behind every righteous person and sinner, perform the funeral prayer of every righteous person and sinner, participate in Jihad with every righteous person and sinner. The narrator named Makhool has not heard the hadiths from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) and other than that the narrator is trustworthy."
1769,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three things are Sunnah: forming a row behind every imam (praying in congregation), you will get the reward of your prayer, and the burden of his sin will be on him, and taking part in Haramirah Murah Jihad, you will get the reward of your bravery, and his evil will be on him, and performing the funeral prayer for every deceased among the people of Tawheed, even if he committed suicide. The narrator Umar bin Subh is obsolete."
1770,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that prayer is not performed in fear.
1771,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, and the people stood up following his example. When they stood up for the second rak'at, those people who had prostrated with him moved back and they began to protect their brothers. Then another group came and they performed one rak'at with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Everyone was saying Takbeer in the prayer, but they were also protecting each other."
1772,The same hadith is related to Zahri along with another chain of transmission.
1773,This tradition is also transmitted along with another document.
1774,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to perform the prayer of fear. She was close to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the other people stood in their place and protected their brothers. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prostrating, the back row went into prostration. The row that was near the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) went into prostration, and the others stood up, protecting their brothers."
1775,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led one group of two groups in the prayer of fear, one group, and the other group stood facing the enemy, then those people retreated and stood facing the enemy instead of their companions, and the other people came forward. Rakaat has been performed."
1776,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the prayer of fear during a war, and one group stood behind him and another group stood between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the enemy. The Prophet (PBUH) greeted all of them, then both groups performed one rak'ah later."
1777,"Sayyiduna Abu Ayyash Zarqi narrates that we were with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the place of Isfaan. is more beloved than their children and their own lives, then Sayyiduna Gabriel appeared with this verse in the time between Zuhr and Asr. \And when you are among them"," do not pray.\"" When it was time for prayer", the people took up their weapons under the command of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When those in the first row prostrated and then stood up, the people in the back row went into prostration, then those in the back row took the place of those in the front row, and those in the front moved in the place of those behind, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, and all the people bowed with him, then he raised his head, and all the people raised their heads. When they sat down, those in the second row prostrated, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted all of them. The narrator says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in this way twice," once in Isfan and once in the area of Banusalim."""
1778,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1779,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged Banu Muhareb at the place of Nakhl, then it was announced among the people that the prayer had begun, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the Muslims into two groups. Also perform four rak'ats of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and each group performed four rak'ats."
1780,"Saleh bin Khawat narrates the statement of the Companion who, following the example of the Prophet, offered the prayer of fear in the Battle of Zaat al-Raqqa (the Companions narrate) One group formed a line with the Prophet, and the other group remained in front of the enemy. Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lead them the remaining rak'ah of his prayer, then they remained seated and the group completed their prayer, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon them) greeted them all. Ibn Mahdi says that Imam Malik has issued a fatwa according to this tradition. Ibn Wahhib says that Imam Malik first said to me: I like this tradition the most, but then he changed his position and said: The most favorite thing for me is that those people complete their prayers after returning the salam."
1781,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) led his companions in fear prayer, he prayed two rak'ahs to some of the companions, and they returned the salam."
1782,"Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) recited durqaat to them in the prayer of fear, then he recited durqaat to other people and greeted them."
1783,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in Maghrib prayer three rak'ahs, then he finished the prayer, then other people came and he also led them three rak'ahs."
1784,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the prayer of fear. After completing the prayer, they returned the salam, then these people went and stood in the place of the first people, facing the enemy."
1785,"Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates that she asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether a woman can pray only in a shirt and a chador while wearing an apron. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If his shirt is so long that it covers both his feet (then it is permissible to do so). The same hadith is also transmitted along with some other isnaads, however, along with these isnaads, it is transmitted as the saying of Sayyida Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her."
1786,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that once the sun was eclipsed, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered a person to announce that the prayer would be performed in congregation. A narrator named Ibn Abi Dawud says that this is a Sunnah and the people of Madinah are unique in quoting it. A narrator named Abd al-Rahman has narrated this regarding Zuhri: \The eclipse prayer should be announced.\"""""
1787,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1788,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once in the blessed life of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the sun was eclipsed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the mosque. He recited Sama’Allah Laman Hamdah Rabbanna Wilk Al-Hamd and then he stood up and started reciting ‘but it was less than the previous recitation’ then after that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a long bow saying Takbeer ‘but it was less than the first Ruk’ah’ then after that he recited Sama’Allah Laman Hamdah Rabbanna Wilk Al-Hamd’ then he did the same in the second Rak’at and he did it four times in these two Rak’ats. Bowed and prostrated four times. The sun had risen before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer.
1789,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the solar eclipse prayer. This hadith is narrated in the same way as it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sayyida Aisha that she bowed twice in each rak'at.
1790,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited long (in the solar eclipse prayer). A narrator named Ibn Abu Dawud narrates that the people of Madinah are unique in imitating reciting aloud.
1791,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed eight times in four rak'ats in the lunar eclipse and solar eclipse prayers, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in each rak'at."
1792,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed four times (in two rak'ahs) and prostrated himself four times during the solar eclipse and lunar eclipse prayers.
1793,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakra (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the sun was eclipsed during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). There is also this in this hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said that when Allah Ta’ala manifests on something from His creation, it (bows) before Him with humility and humility."
1794,"Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that when Allah Ta'ala manifests for something from among His creatures, it bows before Him. The same tradition is narrated with another document."
1795,"Muhammad bin Ali (may he refer to Imam Muhammad al-Baqir, may Allah be pleased with him) says that there are two signs of our Mahdi that have never occurred after the creation of the heavens and the earth: the eclipse of the moon on the first night of Ramadan and the eclipse of the sun on the fifteenth day of the month when Allah created the heavens and the earth."
1796,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the sun and the moon are the signs of Allah Almighty.
1797,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, ‘Once a Prophet went out with the people to perform the Istiqa prayer."
1798,Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad Al-Baqir (RA)): The Prophet (PBUH) used to fold his cloak while praying for rain so that the famine would end.
1799,"Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the Eidgah to pray the Istiqah prayer. A narrator named Sufyan says that while turning the cloak upside down, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned its right side to the left and the left side to the right."
1800,A narrator named Talha narrates that Marwan sent me to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) so that I could inquire from him about the Sunnah method of performing the Istiqa prayer. Sayyidna Abdullah bin RA said: \Istiqa (i.e.," to pray for rain) is the Sunnah to perform the Istiqa prayer in the Eidgah.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the Takbeer seven times in the first rak'ah and recited Surah Al-Ala while in the second rak'ah he recited the Surah Al-Gashiya."""
1801,Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the people to pray for rain.
1802,Ibad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the people to pray for rain. He came to the Eidgah and prayed for rain.
1803,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to recite aloud during Eid and Istiqa prayers.
1804,Ubad bin Tamim narrates this statement of his uncle Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to pray for rain. He gave a sermon to the people.
1805,This same hadith along with some other isnads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd.
1806,"Ishaq bin Abdullah narrates that Waleed bin Utbah, the governor of Madinah, sent him to Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: O my nephew! You should inquire from them what the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did in relation to praying for rain. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited with a state of humility and humility. The narrator has disagreed in quoting a single word here."
1807,"Hisham bin Ishaq narrates this statement of his father. An emir sent me to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) to ask him about the Istiqa prayer. Narrators named Harun and Yusuf narrated these words. So that I may inquire from him about the prayer to be recited in connection with the prayer for rain.' So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said, 'Why did he not inquire from me himself?' Prophet Muhammad did not give a sermon like you people."
1808,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only raised his hands while praying for rain. These words are narrated along with another chain of transmission: Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never raised his hands while praying. He only raised his hands while praying for rain.
1809,"Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in front of Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
1810,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1811,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Do not declare your dead to be impure, because a Muslim is not impure in life or death.”"
1812,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Gabriel (A.S.) performed the funeral prayer for Sayyidna Adam (A.S.), he recited the takbirs for Sayyidna Adam. A tombstone was installed. The narrator of this tradition, Abd al-Rahman bin Malik, is obsolete."
1813,Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the angels had performed the funeral prayer of Sayyidna Adam (peace be upon him) and they had recited takbeers over him. They said: O children of Adam! This is your way (of performing the funeral prayer).
1814,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is reported as a \suspended\"" hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Abi (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
1815,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b (RA).
1816,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the angels said praises to Sayyidna Adam (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Abu Bakr said praises to the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said praises to Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) said praises to Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may God bless him and grant him peace) said praises to Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyidna Imam Hussain said four takbeers on Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA)."
1817,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) offered a funeral prayer.
1818,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) recited four takbeers in the funeral prayer for the last time. Sayyiduna Imam Hussain (RA) recited four Takbirs in the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Imam Hussain (RA) and the angels recited four Takbirs in the funeral prayer of Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him). The narrator of this hadith is Firat bin Sa'ib, this is an obsolete hadith."
1819,Talha bin Abdullah narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) led a funeral prayer and he recited Surah Fatiha in it.
1820,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we give ghusl to the dead, one of us performs ghusl and the other does not (i.e. it is not necessary to perform ghusl after giving ghusl to the deceased)."
1821,"Ayyub bin Nu'man narrates that I performed a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyidna Zaid bin Arqam, and he recited five takbeers during it. The narrator quoted this hadith as a marfu' hadith."
1822,") Hadith (1844 Ayyub bin Saeed narrates that I offered a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam, and he recited five takbeers. Then he narrated that I offered a funeral prayer following the example of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he also recited five takbeers. Therefore, we will not abandon them because of any person."
1823,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said six takbirs on the people of Badr, five takbirs on the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and four takbirs on all other people."
1824,"Narrator named Marqa narrates that I performed a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, and he recited Takbeer five times during it."
1825,"Isa, the slave of Sayyidna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I performed a funeral prayer under the guidance of my master (Sayyidna Huzaifa bin Yaman, may God be pleased with him), who was a good man, and he recited the takbeer five times. was"
1826,"Ubaid bin Saaq narrates that once Sayyiduna Sahl bin Haneef (RA) led us in the funeral prayer, when he said the first takbeer, then he recited Surah Fatiha until his voice reached the people behind him. The narrator narrates, then he continued to say Takbeer until there was only one Takbeer left, so he recited the words of Tashahhud for the prayer, then he said Takbeer and ended the prayer."
1827,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back after attending the funeral of a person in the field of Baqi', I was feeling a severe pain in my head. (The literal translation of this would be: Oh! I died.) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Oh, my head! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If you die before me", you will not suffer any harm because I will give you a shroud, I will perform your funeral prayer," and I will bury you.\"" When you do that", you will come back to my house and spend the night here with your new wife.' The Prophet smiled. After that, the suffering of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began," in which he passed away."""
1828,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \So I will give you a bath and I will give you a shroud.\"""""
1829,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission and it has these words \So I will bathe you.\"""""
1830,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed a funeral prayer, then he (PBUH) placed his blessed right hand on his blessed left hand."
1831,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the funeral prayer for a person, he (peace be upon him) would raise both hands in the first takbeer and then place his blessed right hand on his blessed left hand."
1832,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise both hands in the first takbeer of the funeral prayer, and after that he did not raise his hands while saying the takbeer in the funeral prayer."
1833,"According to Umarubian, a Christian woman died who had a Muslim child in her womb, so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) ordered that this woman should be buried in the Muslim cemetery because of the child."
1834,"Abu Salman narrates that once Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, led the funeral prayer of a person, and he recited Takbeer five times. So they said it was done on purpose, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pay it in the same way."
1835,"Abdullah Bin Ka'b narrates this statement of his father, Sayyidna Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said that his mother, who was a Christian, had passed away and he wanted to attend the funeral of his mother. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him) narrates this hadith is not proven. One of the narrators of this hadith is weak."
1836,"Abdullah bin Aamir narrates this statement of his father. I remember this very well about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he buried Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoon, may Allah be pleased with him. They were standing on the side."
1837,"Masrooq narrates that Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, led the funeral prayer of a wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I heard him say, \I will offer the funeral prayer for this woman in the same way that the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace," led the funeral prayer for the last time.\"""""
1838,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) did not raise both hands while praying, he used to raise both hands so much that the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
1839,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you bathe the dead, it is not necessary for you to bathe because your dead body is not najis. That is sufficient for you. Wash your hands."
1840,"Imam Shaabi narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave whose owner had been buried some time ago. The narrator narrates: I asked Imam Shaabi: Who narrated this hadith to you? He replied that it was narrated by a reliable person, who was present on this occasion, that is Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."
1841,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave that was isolated, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Takbeer four times over it (while performing the funeral prayer). The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads and all these narrators have narrated the same thing."
1842,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led a funeral prayer for a person.
1843,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man used to clean the mosque (of the Prophet) 'He passed away and was buried at night'. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and others with him visited the grave of that person. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “These graves are filled with darkness for their people (i.e. men), and Allah, the Exalted, illuminates their graves for them because of my offering the funeral prayer of these people.” These words of tradition are from a narrator named Ali bin Muslim."
1844,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) visited the grave of a person after he was buried. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed (the funeral prayer) on the grave of a woman.
1845,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a newly built grave and asked why you did not tell me about it. The people said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleeping at that time. We did not like to wake him up. Some narrators have quoted some additional words and meanings in it, but the meaning is the same."
1846,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered his funeral prayer three days after the death of a person.
1847,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the funeral prayer at the grave of a person one month after his burial. The narrator named Bishrban Adam is unique in quoting from the narrator named Abu Asim.
1848,"Sayyiduna Abu Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the nine men who participated in the Battle of Uhud were brought, and with them was the tenth Sayyidna Hamzah (may God be pleased with them). Then these nine people were buried and Sayyidna Hamza (RA) was not buried (meaning the Prophet (PBUH) performed the funeral prayer of Sayyidna Hamza (RA)."
1849,Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the funeral prayers of those who were martyred in the Battle of Uhud after eight years.
1850,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (RA) narrates that when the news of the death of Sayyidna Ja'far Tayyar (RA) came, the Prophet (PBUH) said, \Prepare food for Ja'far's family"," as a situation has befallen them which has preoccupied them (the narrator is in doubt about a word here)."""
1851,"Sayyidah Asma bint Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) willed that her husband Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with her) and Asma (daughter of Umays) would bathe her, so they both gave her ghusl."
1852,"Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) led the funeral prayer for seven people together, including men and women. The narrator narrates that Sayyida Umm Kulthum, the wife of Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) and the daughter of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and her daughter-in-law were buried. His son's name was Zaid bin Umar. In those days, Sayyidna Saeed bin Al-Aas was the governor and among those present were Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, Abu Hurairah, Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri and Sayyidna Qatadah. I wonder what the method is? He said it is Sunnah."
1853,"Sayyiduna Utban bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered Nawafil in his house at the time of Chasht. Chapter: It is permissible to act a little during the prayer, and which prayer must be made up for the person who faints."
1854,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, 'If someone knocked on the door during that time, if the door was in front of him or on the right or left side of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Prophet (peace be upon him) would open the door."
1855,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and the door would be closed. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned that the door was in the direction of Qiblah.
1856,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I used to ask to open the door, even though the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing Nawafil standing at that time."
1857,"Asim bin Zamra narrates: We said to Sayyiduna Ali (RA): Tell us a hadith about the Nawafil of the Prophet (PBUH)' So he said: 'Who can keep his strength'? The narrator says: 'We asked you to tell us about it as far as we have power, and we will perform it.' It would rise as much in the direction as Asr (rises in the direction of the west) then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform two rak'ats, and you would send salutations on the angels, the prophets and their followers, the believers and the Muslims in between them, then you would wait until at the time of Chasht, it would be so high that it would be as high as it was in the direction of the east at the time of Zuhr. If it was late, you would pray four rak'ahs and in them you would greet the angels, the prophets and their followers, the believers and the Muslims. After that, you would pray two rak'ahs (Sunnah) after the Zuhr prayer, and then you would pray four rak'ahs (Sunnah) before you, and you would also pray between them in the same way."
1858,"Asim Ibn Zamra narrated, 'We asked Sayyiduna Ali (RA) about the prayer of the Prophet (PBUH), and he said, 'Who has the power to do it?' That the sun would be as far away from the point of sunrise as it would be away from the point of sunset (i.e. it would be the time of sunset). At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform four rak'ahs of Sunnah before the Zuhr prayer after sunset, then he would perform two rak'ahs of Sunnah after Zuhr, and then he would perform the first four rak'ahs again."
1859,"Yazid, the slave of Sayyidna Ammar (RA) narrates that once Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) fell into a stupor, which lasted until the time of Zuhr Asr (Maghrib) and Isha."
1860,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a person who faints and leaves the prayer. If he comes, that person will perform this prayer. The words of both the narrators of this tradition are the same, but there is some difference in the chain of transmission."
1861,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, that once he was unconscious for a day and a night, and he did not make up the prayers during that time."
1862,"According to another chain of transmission, it has been narrated that once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was unconscious for more than two days, so he did not make up the prayers (during that time)."
1863,"Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was once unconscious for three days and three nights, so he did not make up (the obligatory prayers) during that time."
1864,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to look left and right while praying, but he did not turn his neck and look at his back. A narrator named Fazl bin Musa is unique in narrating this tradition as a connected tradition. Other rabbis have quoted it as a mursal tradition."
1865,Abdullah bin Saeed narrates this in his chain of transmission: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to look here and there during the prayer without bending his neck.
1866,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (in order to attract the Imam): The command to say Subhan Allah is for men and the command to clap is for women.
1867,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever makes a gesture during the prayer that is understood, then that person will perform his prayer again. One of the narrators of this hadith is unknown, and the last part of the hadith is an addition to the hadith. It may be. These are the words of the narrator. It is authentically proven from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to point during prayer. This hadith has been narrated by Sayyidna Anas, Sayyidna Jabir (RA) and other Companions of the Prophet (RA) with reference to the Prophet (PBUH)."
1868,Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make gestures while praying.
1869,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make gestures while praying.
1870,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever performs one prostration of the morning prayer before the sun rises, he performs this prayer, or if he performs the prostration (of the Asr prayer) before the sun sets, he performs this prayer."
1871,"Bakir bin Ashaj states that there were nine mosques in Madinah along with the blessed mosque of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the people living near these mosques used to listen to the adhan of Sayyiduna Bilal (may God be pleased with them), but they used to pray in these mosques. There was a mosque of Banu Salama, a mosque of Banurataj, which belonged to Banu Abd al-Ashhal, a mosque of Banuzareq, a mosque of Banughafar, a mosque of Islam and a mosque of Jahina, the narrator has doubts about the ninth mosque. Chapter - A person who prays facing another person who is looking in front of him in the direction of the Qibla, must pray again."
1872,"Muhammad bin Hanafiya narrated that the Holy Prophet saw a person who was praying towards another person, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that person to pray again. I have performed the complete prayer for you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You have performed the prayer in such a state that you were looking at another person in the direction of the Qiblah.\"""""
1873,"Sayyidna Abbas Jashmi narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said that some imams are people who drive away. Qatadah, the narrator of this tradition, says, \According to my knowledge"," those who drive away here are those who recite for a long time during Ma'mat until people leave them and go away.\"""""
1874,"Ibn Sabat narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the morning prayer, he recited seven verses in it, then he heard the sound of a child crying, so he went into ruku', then he stood up (in the second rak'at), then he recited two verses and went into ruku'."
1875,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes hear the cry of a child with its mother.
1876,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to me that you should not expose your breasts in front of anyone and do not look at the breasts of any living or deceased person (because the breasts are a hundredfold).
1877,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a muezzin who used to give adhan in the manner of Tarbiyah.
1878,"Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs four rak'ats after the Isha prayer, recites them, bows and prostrates well in them, then that person will get the same reward for this prayer as the reward for performing those rak'ats in Shab al-Qadr."
1879,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that menstruating and puerperal women should not recite any part of the Qur'an.
1880,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrates that a blind person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, \O Messenger of Allah! I hear the call to prayer", but sometimes there is no one to accompany me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""When you hear the call to prayer", accept the invitation of the person calling you to Allah (i.e.," come to the mosque to pray in congregation)."""
1881,"Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade the imam standing on top of something and the people behind him are called narrators, that is, those standing below him on the ground."
1882,"Sayyidna Abu Murshad Ghanwi, may Allah be pleased with him, who had the honor of participating in the Battle of Badr, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if you want your prayer to be accepted, let your best people lead you because they are the representatives between you and your Lord. The authenticity of this tradition is not proven. The narrator of this tradition, Abdullah bin Musa, is weak."
1883,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this when those people bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Sayyidna Muhammad (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) is the Messenger of Allah, and those people establish prayer, and pay Zakat, then they will secure their lives and their wealth from me. It will be the responsibility (then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said) By Allah! If those people refuse to pay me a rope that they used to pay to the Holy Prophet, then I will fight with them on that too."
1884,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I have been commanded to do three things. I have been commanded to fight with the people until they confess that there is no god but Allah. It will be the responsibility of Allah.
1885,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight with people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, to establish prayer, and to pay Zakat."
1886,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: I have been ordered to fight with the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The right will remain intact and the account of these people will be held by Allah Ta'ala.
1887,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on a person's wealth until a year has passed. Other narrators have narrated it as a suspended tradition.
1888,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on the benefited property until one year has passed on it.
1889,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat on wealth is not required until one year has passed. The narrators have differed in quoting some words here.
1890,This tradition is also narrated along with another document.
1891,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not required on wealth until one year has passed.
1892,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on wealth until one year has passed on it.
1893,This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) along with another chain of transmission.
1894,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on property until it remains with its owner for one year.
1895,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Radiyallahu Anhu says that when a person acquires wealth, Zakat on it is not halal (i.e. not obligatory) until one year has passed."
1896,Abdullah bin Waqid narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) used to receive half a dinar out of every twenty dinars and one dinar out of every forty dinars (i.e. two and a half percent of zakat).
1897,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that no payment is required for 190 dirhams.
1898,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take a quarter of a tenth of every forty dirhams (i.e. two and a half percent).
1899,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, that zakat is not required on wheat and dates until they reach the amount of five wasqs, and on silver, zakat is not required until it reaches five ounces, and on camels, zakat is not required until they reach five camels."
1900,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that zakat is not required on silver less than five ounces, zakat is not required on less than five camels, and zakat is not required on dates less than five wasq."
1901,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on less than five ounces of silver, Zakat is not required on less than five camels, and Zakat is not required on dates that are less than five vasaqs."
1902,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: Zakat is not required for less than five camels, no payment is required for less than forty goats, no payment is required for less than thirty cows, no payment is required for less than twenty shekels of gold, no payment is required for less than two dirhams (of silver), no payment is required for less than five Wasq (of grain), while usher dates are not required. ``Grapes'' ``Wheat'' which will be collected from that which is irrigated naturally will require payment of usher and that which is irrigated (artificially) by means of dol will require payment of half of usher."
1903,"Sayyiduna Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he instructed him not to accept anything from a piece (of gold or silver) 'When the silver reaches two dirhams, to accept five dirhams from it,' not to accept anything more than that until it reaches forty dirhams,' when it reaches forty dirhams, then to accept one dirham from it (i.e. for every forty dirhams). receiving one). One of the narrators of this hadith is Humanhal bin Jarrah, whose surname is Abu Atuf, while his name is Jarrah bin Minhal. A narrator named Ibn Ishaq has copied his name in reverse."
1904,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) to Yemen and asked him: What have you been ordered to do? He said, \I have been ordered to receive one Tabi Tabi'a from every thirty cows and one Masna from every forty cows.\"" He was asked: \""Have you been given any orders about opportunities?\"" He replied"," \""No!\"" I will ask the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this. (ie no payment will be required). The narrator describes; It means an animal that is between two years old and the words mean that nothing will be taken from it."""
1905,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his father. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro was asked about gems, pearls, precious stones, small pearls (or Abyssinian pearls) and plants that grow in the ground such as pearls, jewels, silk, vegetables that grow from the ground, pickled cucumbers, etc. He said that Zakat is not required on any stone and no Zakat is required on vegetables either. Wasallam only prescribed the payment (of Ushar) in wheat, barley, dates and grapes."
1906,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) both state that the payment of zakat on dates and date-palm trees is not required until they reach five Wasaqs.
1907,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this with reference to Sayyidna Ali Bin Abu Talib (RA) The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables, Zakat will not be required on “Araya” (Zakat will not be required on grains less than five wasaqs), Zakat will not be required on factors, and Zakat will not be required on the forehead. A narrator named Saqr bin Habib narrates that Pashani means horse, mule and slave."
1908,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that vegetables that grow from the ground do not require Zakat."
1909,"Sayyidna Muhammad bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When he sent Sayyidna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) to Yemen, he instructed him to collect one dinar out of every forty dinars, collect five dirhams out of every two dirhams, and zakat is not required on less than five wasaqs, zakat is not required on less than five camels, and zakat is not required on vegetables."
1910,Musa bin Talha narrates this statement of his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables.
1911,"Musa bin Talha narrates this on the authority of his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables."
1912,"Musa bin Talha narrates this from Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Zakat will not be required on vegetables. The narrator of this tradition, Marwan Sanjari, is weak."
1913,"Musa bin Talhah narrates this about Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him."
1914,"Musa bin Talha narrates that we have a letter of Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (Radi Allahu Anhu) in which it is written that the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) received zakat from wheat, raisins and dates."
1915,"Musa bin Talha narrated this in reference to the martyrs of Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him: the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that the land on which the sky is Baal (a palm tree planted near water so that the tree itself gets watered by underground water) and watered by flowing water (i.e. canal, etc.) will be required to pay usher, and the land that is watered by sprinkling (i.e. artificially) I will have to pay half-usher. Payment of Zakat will be required on dates, wheat, grains, but it is waived on cucumbers, watermelons, apples, kasab and other vegetables."
1916,Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on vegetables.
1917,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with regard to the martyrs of Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him).
1918,This same tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to Sayyidna Mu'adhbin Jabal (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
1919,Musa bin Talha narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade collecting zakat from vegetables.
1920,The same hadith has been narrated by Sayyiduna Mu'adhbin Jabal (RA) on the authority of Musa bin Talha along with another chain of transmission.
1921,"Abu Burda' narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Musa Ash'ari (RA) and Sayyidna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) when the Prophet (PBUH) sent these two men to Yemen, and they both taught the people about the religious rules, (and he said) You people should only receive Zakat from these four things which are 'wheat', raisins and dates."
1922,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this: Zakat is not required on any field (agricultural produce) until it reaches five wasqs. When it reaches five wasqs, then payment of zakat will be required on it, and one wasq is sixty sa’s. It is equal to a dirham."
1923,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that Zakat should not be collected from a field (i.e. agricultural produce) until its yield is five Wasaq.
1924,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: I have forgiven you the zakat of your slaves and horses, but you should bring your silver, agricultural produce and animal zakat."
1925,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this as a hadith transmitted to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that zakat will not be required for less than five wasaqs, and one wasaq is equal to sixty Makhtums."
1926,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on less than five Wasaqs and one Wasaq is sixty Sa'ahs.
1927,"Taus narrates that a calf was brought to the service of Sayyidna Mu'adh Radiyallahu Anhu, and he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) did not give me any order about it. The narrator narrates that their number was less than 30."
1928,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu’adh (RA) to Yemen, he ordered him to receive one tabi’ or one tabiyyah from every thirty cows and receive one masna from every forty cows. So he said, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give me any order about this. When I go to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"," I will inquire from him.\"" Then when Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him about the calf", the Prophet (peace be upon him) said that no payment will be required for it. A narrator named Mas'udi narrates that when their number is less than thirty, when the number of cows is from forty to sixty, two tabi'ahs will be required, when they reach seventy, one masna will be paid, and when they reach eighty, then two masna will be required, and when they reach ninety," three tabi's will be required. Masoudi says that the word \""Awq\"" is written with \""s\""."""
1929,"Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent him to Yemen, he said, \You receive grain (in zakat) from grain", from goats you receive goats from camels zakat, from camels zakat you receive camels," and from cows you receive zakat from cows.\"""""
1930,Sayyiduna Mu'adhbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the people of Yemen: \You bring to me on Thursdays and twenty-one," and I will collect Zakat from you.\"" Amrunami narrator has quoted these words"," you bring me wide clothes. This hadith is transmitted because the narrator named Taus has not found the time of Sayyidna Mu'adh."""
1931,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Muqathis were not among the things that Sayyiduna Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) brought.
1932,"Malik bin Aws narrates that once we were sitting near Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him. Meanwhile, Sayyidna Abu Zar Ghafari, may God be pleased with him, came to him and greeted him. He replied, \I am fine.\"" Then he went to a pillar and stood. People also got up and went towards him and surrounded him. \""I was also among those who surrounded him.\"" People said: O Abu Dharr! If you tell us a hadith about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)", he said: I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Zakat is required on camels, Zakat is required on goats, Zakat is required on cows," and Zakat is required on linen (silk). The narrator says he mentioned this word with \""z\""."""
1933,"Malik bin Awf narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Dharghafari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Zakat is required on camels, Zakat is required on goats, Zakat is required on cows, and on silk, Zakat is obligatory. If kept, it will be counted as a treasure through which it will be tarnished on the Day of Resurrection."
1934,"Malik bin Aws narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Zakat is given on camels, Zakat is given on goats, Zakat is given on cows, and Zakat is given on sheep.”"
1935,"Sayyiduna Mu'adbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to Yemen and instructed them to collect one tabi' or one tabi'ah from every thirty camels, and one masna from every forty cows, and from every adult person to collect a dinar equal to it."
1936,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the narrators have disagreed about one of its words."
1937,Sayyiduna Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to Yemen and instructed them to collect one tabi or one tabiyya from every thirty cows and one masna from every forty cows and to collect one dinar from every adult person for it.
1938,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Zakat is not required on domestic camels."
1939,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on cows for domestic use, but one Tabi' is required for every thirty cows and one Masna for every forty cows."
1940,"Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that nothing is necessary in a cow for domestic use. In another tradition, the words are slightly different."
1941,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on cows for domestic use.
1942,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a cow used for farming does not require zakat.
1943,"Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates, \I was staying with Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas"," may God be pleased with him.\"" After that", he mentioned a word. Then he also said that one day he heard Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said that (in order to avoid the collection of zakat, one should not separate the collected property and not collect the separate property). It will go and there will be two groups of people who will share about the tank," the shepherd and the animal to be given for marriage."""
1944,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat will not be required in Mushirah (that is, it is used for driving cows)."
1945,"Ibn Juraj narrates, I asked Ata about such people who have shares with each other, if they have 40 goats, then one goat will be required to be paid for all of them. So he said that one goat will be required to be paid for both of them."
1946,Hameed bin Hilal narrates that a person brought a scripture to Hasan Basri in which various problems were written. He asked him about this scripture. He did not find any mistakes in these problems.
1947,"Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghaflah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person who received zakat from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. I sat by his side. A man brought a camel with a high hump and said: You accept it. He refused to accept it."
1948,Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghaflah (RA) narrates that a person who received Zakat from the Prophet (PBUH) came to us. I sat next to him. I asked him what is written in your handwriting. He told him not to separate the wealth and not to collect the separate wealth (says the narrator) Then a man came to him with a camel with a high hump and he refused to accept it.
1949,"Sayyiduna Suwayd bin Ghafla (RA) narrates that a person came to us to receive Zakat from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The narrator narrates that I read in his writings that separate wealth should not be collected and that separate wealth should not be separated to avoid zakat (payment or collection). Refused to accept the camel. He said: If I received it from the wealth of a Muslim, then what would I do in the presence of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but there is some difference in it."
1950,"Ata narrates that Sayyidah Umm Salamah (RA) was wearing a gold necklace. She asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \When you pay his Zakat"," it will not be counted; its meaning is the same.\"""""
1951,"Abdullah bin Shaddad narrates: We came to the service of Sayyida Ayesha, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me, and he saw silver bracelets in my hand. Where did they come from? I said, I have made them so that I can wear them and come in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired whether you have paid his zakat. I did not submit! (or whatever Allah willed) then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \These are enough for you in Hell.\"" A narrator named Muhammad bin Ata is unknown."""
1952,"Imam Shaabi narrates: I heard Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (RA) narrating that I brought a chain in the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that contained seventy pounds of gold. I said, O Messenger of Allah! You collect zakat from it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) collected one mithaqal and three-fourths of a mithqal from it."
1953,"This hadith has been narrated along with another document, however, these words are extra in it. I said, O Messenger of Allah! Is there any right in wealth apart from zakat? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! Then he recited the verse \And he gives of his wealth of his own choice.\"""""
1954,Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays Radiyallahu Anha narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam).
1955,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) says that there is no Zakat on jewelry, the narrator of this tradition, Abu Hamza, his name is Maymun, and this is a weak hadeeth."
1956,Sayyid Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that there is no harm in wearing ornaments when their Zakat is paid.
1957,"Amro bin Shoaib cites this statement of his grandfather regarding his father, he wrote this letter to his secretary Salim asking him to pay zakat every year on the ornaments of his daughters."
1958,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Masood) narrates that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “I have some jewels and my husband is a poor man. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! This tradition is an illusion. It is correct. This tradition is related to Ibrahim."
1959,"Alqamah narrates that the wife of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) asked her about her jewels, and he said, \If they are worth two hundred dirhams"," zakat must be paid on them.\"" She said"," \""My nephews are under my care. Shall I spend it on them?\"" So Syedna Abdullah replied yes! This tradition is \""suspended\""."""
1960,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not obligatory on the property of a slave until he is freed.
1961,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, \Two women from Yemen came to the service of the Holy Prophet"," may God bless him and grant him peace.\"" They were wearing gold bracelets. He answered no! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then both of you should fulfill his right. There are these words in a hadith", they were both wearing gold bracelets. It also has these words (the Prophet," peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then both of you pay the right for it. It is obligatory on you (the narrator says)."""
1962,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates, “I asked the Prophet (PBUH) that my wife has twenty shekels worth of jewellery. One of the narrators of this tradition, Yahya bin Abu Anisa, is obsolete, and this tradition is illusory. It is true that this tradition is transmitted and suspended."
1963,Ibrahim Nakhai narrates that the wife of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) asked her about a necklace of hers which was twenty shekels and was made of gold. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) answered yes! How much did this woman ask? So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) replied five dirhams. This lady inquired whether I should pay this to such and such a person. This lady inquired about her nephew who was an orphan and was being raised by this lady.
1964,"Ibrahim Nakhai narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud's wife had jewelry. This woman asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may I pay her zakat. He answered yes! The woman asked if I should give this to my orphaned nephew. He said yes!"
1965,"Ali bin Salim narrates that I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik about jewelry, and he said that Zakat is not obligatory on it."
1966,"According to Nafi, one of the daughters of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was given 1,000 dirhams. This woman made jewelry for her, which amounted to four hundred dinars."
1967,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that Zakat is not required on jewelry.
1968,"Nafee narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) made jewelry worth four dinars for his daughters, but Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) did not pay their zakat."
1969,It has been narrated about Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) that she made gold ornaments for her daughters and did not pay their Zakat. The value of these ornaments was around fifty thousand.
1970,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up to give a sermon to the people."
1971,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Protect the property of orphans, do not deprive them of Zakat."
1972,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that Zakat will be required on the property of an orphan."
1973,Saeed bin Musaib narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said this: Take care of the wealth of the orphans and do not deprive them of Zakat.
1974,"Ibn Abu Rafi' narrated that the wealth of these people was with Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. When Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, returned the property to them, these people found some deficiency in it. Then, when they calculated it with the Zakat, they found it complete. Those people came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with them. Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with them, said, \Did you people think that I would have wealth and I would not pay Zakat on it?\"""""
1975,"The sons of Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) gave some land to Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) as a landholder. took possession of this wealth, so they counted their wealth and found it less. They came to Sayyidna Ali (RA) and told him about it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) inquired whether you have calculated his Zakat. The narrator narrates that these people calculated his zakat and found it fulfilled, then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said, \You people thought that I would have some wealth and I would not pay its zakat.\"""""
1976,"Narrated by Nafee, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) had the property of an orphan."
1977,Ubaid bin Umayr narrates that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said this: Take care of the property of the orphans and do not deprive them of Zakat.
1978,Nafi narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to pay Zakat on the property of an orphan.
1979,"Mujahid narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) gave some land to his slave Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) and he could not take care of it. That when the children of Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (RA) grew up, Sayyidna 'Ali (RA) found the wealth less. He replied, Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, calculate his Zakat. When he calculated it, he found it."
1980,Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated that Sayyiduna Ali (RA) paid zakat on the property of the children of Sayyidna Abu Rafa’ (RA).
1981,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that Zakat is not required on the property of a minor. The narrator of this tradition, Ibn Lahiyyah, is not considered authentic."
1982,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather about his father: A woman from Yemen came to the Prophet's service with her daughter. In her hands were two rings made of gold. The Prophet asked, \Have you paid her zakat?\"" He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Would you like it if Allah", the Exalted," clothed you with two bracelets of fire?”"""
1983,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, we have found this in the writings of Sayyiduna Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this about the zakat of camels. For five camels, one goat must be paid; for ten camels, two goats must be paid; for fifteen camels, three goats must be paid; for twenty, four goats must be paid; for twenty-five goats, payment must be made; then when they are more, then the payment of a daughter will be required among them. The payment of Lubun will be required, then if it is even more than one, it will be necessary to pay one Haqq for them. If there is more than one of them, one jazaa must be paid for every forty, and one haqqa must be paid for every fifty."
1984,"Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, among others; and al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā and al-Faḍl ibn Sahl narrated to us, they said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbdillāh, from Anas, that when Abū Bakr was appointed as khalīfah, he dispatched Anas ibn Mālik to al-Baḥrayn and wrote for him this document: \This is the obligatory charity (ṣadaqah) that the Messenger of Allah", peace and blessings be upon him, imposed upon the Muslims, which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever among the believers is asked for it in its proper form, let him give it; and whoever is asked for more than that, let him not give it. For twenty-four camels or fewer, the obligation falls upon sheep: for every five, one sheep. When they reach twenty-five up to thirty-five, the due is a bint makhāḍ (a female camel in its second year). When they reach thirty-six up to forty-five, the due is a bint labūn (a female camel in its third year). When they reach forty-six up to sixty, the due is a ḥiqqah (a female camel in its fourth year, capable of being mounted). When they reach sixty-one up to seventy-five, the due is a jadhaʿah (a female camel in its fifth year). When they reach seventy-six up to ninety, the due are two bint labūn. When they reach ninety-one up to one hundred and twenty, the due are two ḥiqqah capable of being mounted. When they exceed one hundred and twenty, for every forty, a bint labūn is due, and for every fifty, a ḥiqqah. If the ages of the camels differ regarding the obligatory charity dues, then for one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a jadhaʿah but he does not have a jadhaʿah and has a ḥiqqah, the ḥiqqah shall be accepted from him, and he shall add with it two sheep if they are readily available to him, or twenty dirhams. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he does not have a ḥiqqah and has a jadhaʿah, the jadhaʿah shall be accepted from him, and the collector (muṣaddiq) shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he has only a bint labūn, the bint labūn shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have a bint labūn and has a ḥiqqah, the ḥiqqah shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have one and has a bint makhāḍ, the bint makhāḍ shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it twenty dirhams or two sheep. For one upon whom the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he does not have one and has a bint labūn, the bint labūn shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him twenty dirhams or two sheep. If he does not have a bint makhāḍ in its proper form but has an ibn labūn (a male camel in its third year), it shall be accepted from him and nothing additional shall be required with it. Whoever has only four camels, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. When the camels reach five, one sheep is due. The ṣadaqah on freely grazing sheep: when they are forty up to one hundred and twenty, one sheep is due. When they exceed one hundred and twenty up to two hundred, two sheep are due. When they exceed two hundred up to three hundred, three sheep are due. When they exceed three hundred, for every hundred, one sheep is due. No decrepit animal, no defective animal, and no male goat shall be taken as ṣadaqah unless the collector so chooses. Separate flocks shall not be combined, nor shall a combined flock be separated, out of fear of the ṣadaqah. Whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle between them on an equal basis. If a man's freely grazing sheep fall short of forty by one, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. On silver (riqqah), the rate is one-quarter of one-tenth (2.5%). If one's wealth amounts to only one hundred and ninety dirhams," there is no ṣadaqah upon it unless the owner volunteers.\"" Yūsuf said in his narration: \""Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq wrote for him this document when he dispatched him to al-Baḥrayn: 'In the name of Allah", the Most Gracious," the Most Merciful. This is the obligatory charity.'\"" Al-Faḍl ibn Sahl said: \""When Abū Bakr was appointed khalīfah", he dispatched Anas ibn Mālik to al-Baḥrayn and wrote for him this document, and sealed it with the seal of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The inscription on the seal of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was: 'Muḥammad' on one line, 'Rasūl' on one line, and 'Allāh' on one line. This is the obligatory charity that Allah imposed upon the Muslims, which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him," commanded.\"""""
1985,"Dalaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Shīrawayh narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh informed us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: \We took this document from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Anas", who narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: 'These are the obligatory charities of the Muslims which Allah commanded His Messenger. Whoever among the believers is asked for it, let him give it in its proper form; and whoever is asked for it in an improper form, let him not give it. For every twenty-four camels or fewer, the obligation falls upon sheep: for every five, one sheep. For twenty-five up to thirty-five, a bint makhāḍ is due; if no bint makhāḍ is available, then an ibn labūn (male) is given. For thirty-six up to forty-five, a bint labūn is due. For forty-six up to sixty, a ḥiqqah is due. For sixty-one up to seventy-five, a jadhaʿah is due. For seventy-six up to ninety, two bint labūn are due. For ninety-one up to one hundred and twenty, two ḥiqqah are due. For one hundred and twenty-one onward, for every forty, a bint labūn is due, and for every fifty, a ḥiqqah. If the ages of the camels differ, and the ṣadaqah due upon him is a jadhaʿah but he does not have a jadhaʿah and has a ḥiqqah, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall add with it two sheep if they are readily available, or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a ḥiqqah but he does not have one and has a jadhaʿah, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due upon him is a ḥiqqah but he has only a bint labūn, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have a bint labūn and has a ḥiqqah, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint labūn but he does not have one and has a bint makhāḍ, it shall be accepted from him, and he shall be given with it two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he has only a bint labūn, it shall be accepted from him, and the collector shall give him two sheep or twenty dirhams. If the ṣadaqah due is a bint makhāḍ but he does not have one and has an ibn labūn (male), it shall be taken from him and nothing additional shall be required. Whoever has only four camels, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. When the camels reach five, one sheep is due. On freely grazing sheep: when they are forty up to one hundred and twenty, one sheep is due. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one up to two hundred, two sheep are due. When they exceed by one up to three hundred, for every hundred, one sheep is due. No decrepit animal, no defective animal, and no male goat shall be taken as ṣadaqah unless the collector so chooses. Separate flocks shall not be combined, nor shall a combined flock be separated, out of fear of the ṣadaqah. Whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle between them on an equal basis. If the freely grazing sheep fall short of forty by one, there is no ṣadaqah upon them unless their owner volunteers. On silver, the rate is one-quarter of one-tenth. If one's wealth amounts to only one hundred and ninety dirhams," there is no ṣadaqah upon it unless the owner volunteers.\"" This chain of narration is sound (ṣaḥīḥ)"," and all its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt)."""
1986,"Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: \This is a copy of the document of the Messenger of Allah", peace and blessings be upon him, which he wrote regarding charity," and it was in the possession of the family of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar read it to me", and I memorized it as it was. It is the same copy that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz transcribed from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar and Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh when he was appointed governor of al-Madīnah. He instructed his officials to act according to it and wrote with it to al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, and al-Walīd instructed his officials to act according to it. Thereafter, the caliphs continued to command accordingly. Then Hishām ibn Hānīʾ ordered it to be copied and sent to every Muslim official," commanding them to act by it and not to transgress it.\"" This is the document explaining its contents: \""No charity is taken from camels until they reach five. When they reach five", one sheep is due, up to ten. When they reach ten, two sheep are due, up to fifteen. When they reach fifteen, three sheep are due, up to twenty. When they reach twenty, four sheep are due, up to twenty-five. When they reach twenty-five, the obligation is established: a bint makhāḍ is due. If no bint makhāḍ is found, an ibn labūn (male) is given, up to thirty-five. When they reach thirty-six, a bint labūn is due, up to forty-five. When they reach forty-six, a ḥiqqah capable of being mounted is due, up to sixty. When they reach sixty-one, a jadhaʿah is due, up to seventy-five. When they reach seventy-six, two bint labūn are due, up to ninety. When they reach ninety-one, two ḥiqqah capable of being mounted are due, up to one hundred and twenty. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one, three bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and twenty-nine. When they reach one hundred and thirty, a ḥiqqah and two bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and thirty-nine. When they reach one hundred and forty, two ḥiqqah and a bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and forty-nine. When they reach one hundred and fifty, three ḥiqqah are due, up to one hundred and fifty-nine. When they reach one hundred and sixty, four bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and sixty-nine. When they reach one hundred and seventy, a ḥiqqah and three bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and seventy-nine. When they reach one hundred and eighty, two ḥiqqah and two bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and eighty-nine. When they reach one hundred and ninety, three ḥiqqah and a bint labūn are due, up to one hundred and ninety-nine. When they reach two hundred, four ḥiqqah or five bint labūn are due—whichever ages are found shall be taken according to the enumeration we have written in this document. Thereafter, everything regarding camels shall be taken according to what we have written in this document. No charity is taken from sheep until they reach forty. When they reach forty, one sheep is due, up to one hundred and twenty. When they reach one hundred and twenty-one, two sheep are due, up to two hundred. When they reach two hundred and one, three sheep are due, up to three hundred. When they exceed three hundred by one sheep, only three sheep are due until they reach four hundred. When they reach four hundred, four sheep are due, up to five hundred. When they reach five hundred, five sheep are due, up to six hundred. When they reach six hundred, six sheep are due, up to seven hundred. When they reach seven hundred, seven sheep are due, up to eight hundred. When they reach eight hundred, eight sheep are due, up to nine hundred. When they reach nine hundred, nine sheep are due, up to one thousand. When they reach one thousand, ten sheep are due. Thereafter, for every additional hundred," one sheep is due.\"""""
1987,"Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman narrates that when Sayyiduna Umar bin Abdul Aziz was appointed as the caliph, he sent a message to Madinah asking them to look for a ruling on Zakat related to the time of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam). Similarly, the family of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) found the letter of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he wrote to his officials about Zakat and it was in accordance with what is written in the letter of the Prophet (PBUH) that the Prophet (PBUH) sent to Sayyidna Umar Bin Hazm (RA). Umar bin Abdul Aziz ordered his officials about Zakat to receive it in the light of these two letters. About the Zakat of camels, the same thing was written in both of them that if their number exceeds ninety one, it will be necessary to pay two Haqq among them. This ruling is up to twenty-one."
1988,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Saeed narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri, may God be pleased with him): My mother sent me to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. \He who asks for something from another even though he has one ounce (of silver) with him", then he has transgressed (Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him) I thought that my camel or Qoota was worth more than an ounce, so I came back," \""I did not ask you for anything.\"""""
1989,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a prosperous person and a person of high status.
1990,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a person who is prosperous and a companion.
1991,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1992,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, but there is a difference of one word in it."
1993,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that zakat (wealth) came in the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and people came to serve him.
1994,"Ubaidullah bin Adi narrates that two people told me this: \Both of them came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the farewell Hajj and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for some of the Zakat money that he had.\"" I give it to both of you. It is not permissible to give it to a wealthy person and a person who has the ability to earn."""
1995,"Sayyidna Qubaysa bin Makhariq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him for help for Hamala. And then he asks from someone, 'When he makes this payment, then he does not take anything.' A person whose (production) suffers a calamity and he wastes his property.' Belonging to 'They should bear witness that it is now begging for this person (so only these people can beg) besides it, begging will be haram.'"
1996,"Sayyidna Qubaysa bin Makhariq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I had to make a payment. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to seek his help in this matter. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We will make the payment on your behalf and remove it from the charity camels. Begging is forbidden 'Only three people can beg' 'A person who has to pay something, it becomes permissible to beg for him until he pays the payment and then stops after that' A person who is in dire need and hunger until three wise men of his nation testify to this (here the narrator is doubtful 'maybe this is such a word)' state that it is permissible for him to beg in such need and need even For him to be able to meet his needs and for a person who befalls a calamity and wastes his wealth, it is permissible for such a person to beg until he is able to meet his needs, then he stops after that."
1997,Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is not permissible for a wealthy person to ask for anything from anyone. Only five people have a different ruling. Seen as a gift.
1998,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
1999,"Sayyiduna Ali (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever asks for something even though he is prosperous, he increases the punishment of Hell through this act. He said, O Messenger of Allah! What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The dinner should be available. The narrator named Umar bin Khalid is obsolete."
2000,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who, even though he is prosperous, begs from people, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his face will have a stain (the narrator has doubts about a single word here). What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fifty dirhams or as much gold as their value. A narrator named Ibn Aslam is weak."
2001,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that it is not permissible to take Zakat for a person who has fifty dirhams in his possession. The name of the narrator Abu Shiba is Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq and it is weak.
2002,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever, despite being prosperous, asks the people, “When he comes on the Day of Resurrection, there will be a scar on his face.” What is prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whether it is a dirham or as much gold as their value.\"""""
2003,"According to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA), this raiyat is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains the words fifty dirhams. Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him, narrates that in the first hadith, the narrator is delusional, he has quoted it with reference to Abu Ishaq, this is Sahib Hakeem bin Jubeer, and he is weak."
2004,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who asks someone for something even though he is prosperous, when he comes on the Day of Resurrection, his face will be stained (the narrator has doubts about a word here). What does prosperity mean? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fifty dirhams or as much gold as its value (to be present)."
2005,"Hasan bin Saad narrates this statement of his father, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah (bin Masoud), may Allah be pleased with them, say that it is not permissible for a person to ask for anything from anyone who has fifty dirhams or gold equivalent to their value."
2006,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the payment of zakat. He was told by Ibn Jameel, Khalid bin Waleed and Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib refused to pay the zakat. My armor and all my equipment is devoted to the cause of Allah Ta'ala. As far as Mr. Abbas is concerned, this payment is my responsibility and I will also pay him the same amount."
2007,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect Zakat, but Ibn Jameel, Khalid bin Waleed and Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) refused to pay Zakat (when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told about this), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn Jameel did this because he was poor, then Allah made him prosperous as far as Khalid is concerned. So you have abused him because he has already dedicated his armor and equipment in the way of Allah. As for Sayyiduna Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah. His payment will be on me and the same amount will be paid with him."
2008,Sayyiduna Ali (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abbas (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether he could pay Zakat on his wealth before the specified time had passed. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed them to do so.
2009,It is narrated along with another document that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: We had received the Zakat of this year from Sayyiduna Abbas (may God be pleased with him) last year.
2010,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that we had received his Zakat from Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) last year.
2011,"Sayyiduna Talha (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O Umar! Do you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father? We were in need of some property at that time, so we had already received Zakat on the property of Sayyiduna Abbas two years ago. The authenticity of this tradition has been contradicted by the narrator named Hakam. It is Sahih."
2012,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (SAW) sent Sayyiduna Umar (RA) to collect Zakat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) had already given us the Zakat for this year and the next year."
2013,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Umar (RA) to collect Zakat. When he returned, he complained about Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) and said that he did not pay his Zakat to me. Do you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father? Sayyiduna Abbas (RA) had already paid two years of Zakat together. The narrator has quoted the name of another narrator as Ubaidullah bin Umar, but what he meant was that this hadith was narrated from Muhammad bin Ubaidullah, \Allah knows the rest.\"""""
2014,"Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyidna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to collect Zakat and during this he had some disagreement with Sayyidna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, \Don't you know that a man's uncle takes the place of his father?\"" Sayyidna Abbas had already given us this year's Zakat last year."""
2015,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Try to escape Hellfire by means of a piece of date-palm, because it acts as a barrier for a hungry person as it does for a well-watered person."
2016,"Sayyida Fatima bin Qays (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that there is a right to wealth in addition to zakat. Then the Prophet (PBUH) recited this verse: \Goodness is not only this. Turn your faces away.\"" This verse is valid till the end."""
2017,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2018,"Abu Amrub bin Hamas narrates this statement of his father: I used to sell curry and quiver. Once, Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, passed by me and he said to me, pay zakat on your wealth. I said: O Commander of the Faithful! It is in the sally, so he said, you estimate its value, then pay its zakat."
2019,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him). The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this about a horse."
2020,"Haritha bin Muzarab narrates that some people from Egypt came to the service of Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them. They told us that we have received some land and some slaves. We want them to pay their zakat. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, said, \What my two masters before me did not do"," I will not do that until I consult about it.\"" So they all declared it right. Sayyidna Ali remained silent. Sayyidna Umar said", O Abul Hasan! Why are you not talking? So Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: What these men have advised you is right, but it is important that it is not a tax that they will have to pay even after you. Sayyidna Umar (RA) collected 10 dirhams from a slave and ordered him to provide two acres of wheat as food per month. 5 dirhams were received from the mule and 5 jirabs were required to be given as monthly food. A narrator named Abu Ishaq says that during the time of Hajj," it was collected from us but our share was not paid."""
2021,"A narrator named Haritha narrates that some people from Syria came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar, they told us that we have acquired some property, which are horses and slaves. Sayyiduna Ali (RA) was also included in it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, \It is fine if it is not considered as a tribute that will continue to be collected from him even after him.\"""""
2022,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have forgiven you the zakat of horses and slaves, and no zakat will be required for less than two hundred (dirhams)."
2023,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat will not be required on a horse and a slave.
2024,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no obligation to give charity to a slave."""
2025,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that a man's horse and his slave will not be required to pay any kind of charity (i.e. Zakat).
2026,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that Zakat is not required on a Muslim man's mare, his slave and his maidservant. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
2027,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed this Sunnah regarding the dowry of women that it should be twelve ounces and one ounce is worth forty dirhams, so it will be four hundred and eighty dirhams in total, and the Prophet of Allah has also set this limit. has also established this Sunnah which is produced from the land i.e. Wheat, Barley, Raisins, Dates. When these are five wasaqs, one wasaq is of sixty Sa'as, then it will be three Saas in total which will be according to this Sa'as which are related to the Sunnah. This hadith has been narrated only by Saleh bin Musa with regard to Mansoor and this person is weak in hadeeth."
2028,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has established this Sunnah: \Zakat will not be required on grains less than five wasaqs.\"""""
2029,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Zakat is not required on five ounces (of silver), Zakat is not required on less than five camels, and Zakat is not required on grains less than five Wasq. (The narrator narrates) A wasaq is sixty sa's."
2030,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if (the land) is found in Baal, it is necessary to pay a tenth of it (translated)."
2031,"Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) about the land irrigated by the sky (i.e. rain) through canals and springs, and the land irrigated (i.e. naturally irrigated), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed ushar (i.e. the payment of one-tenth of the produce) and on that which is irrigated (artificially) he has prescribed half-ushar (i.e. the payment of one-twentieth)."
2032,"Salim bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has prescribed the payment of one-tenth (of the produce of the land) that is irrigated through the Baal (underground irrigation of a tree near water), sky, canal, spring, and that which is artificially irrigated will require the payment of half-usher."
2033,"Sayyiduna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed one-tenth of the land that does not need irrigation and the land that is irrigated by rain, canals and springs, and one-twentieth of the land that is irrigated with water from wells."
2034,"Narrator Abu Bakr-Nami has narrated this. Shaykh Rabi' has narrated this. I have heard Imam Shafi'i saying, 'The word \Al-Baal\"" used in tradition means the one whose roots reach the water."""
2035,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that the land that is irrigated by rain or spring will be required to pay usher, and that which is irrigated through a dole (i.e. by artificial means), it will be required to pay half usher."
2036,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a letter to the people of Yemen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote this letter to Harith Abdul Kalal and his other companions living in Yemen, who belonged to Maafir and Hamdan. of the produce) shall be required to pay one-twentieth."
2037,"Abu Zubayr says: He heard Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “The land that is irrigated by a spring will require the payment of one-tenth, and the land that is irrigated by the Saniya will require the payment of half-tithe."
2038,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave an order about Zakat, and a man brought raw dates. (Narrated by the narrators) Whoever brought anything, that thing was attributed to the person who brought it, so this verse was revealed about it, \And do not intend to spend it on something worthless.\"" The narrator states that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that 'Jarur and Lon al-Muhabiq should be received in Zakat."""
2039,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2040,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two types of dates (to receive as Zakat) Jaar War and Lon Ahabiq. The narrator narrates that some people used to deliberately take their bad fruits and pay them in zakat, so they were forbidden to pay these two kinds of dates. This is why this verse was revealed: \And do not intend to spend it on something worthless.\"" This tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions."""
2041,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that some people used to pay the bad fruits of their fruits as Zakat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking or paying two kinds of dates as Zakat. Some narrators have also copied this tradition as a Mursal tradition."
2042,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this verse in which Allah Ta'ala has said, \And do not intend to spend it on something worthless.\"""""
2043,Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to estimate the grape trees of the Thaqif tribe by how much fruit is on them. This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2044,Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharma (may God be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Atab bin Usayd (may God be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the grape trees of the Thaqif tribe should be assessed in the same way as date trees (fruits on them) are assessed.
2045,"The same hadith is narrated from Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd along with another chain of transmission. Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered grapes to be valued as dates are valued and their zakat was collected in the form of minqi, just as the zakat of palm trees is collected in the form of dates. Some other narrators have followed in narrating it."
2046,"Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about the zakat of grapes: it will be assessed in the same way as a date tree (fallen dates) is assessed, and then its zakat will be paid in the form of raisins (yaminqi), just as the zakat of a date tree is paid in the form of dates. Follow up."
2047,"Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this about the zakat of grapes, then after that he narrated according to the previous hadith."
2048,Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send a person to these people to estimate the production of grapes and fruits of the youth (and Zakat was collected based on this calculation).
2049,"Sayyiduna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that Zakat be collected in the form of grapes by calculating the yield of a grape tree, just as dates are estimated (or dates are collected by estimation)."
2050,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when Allah gave the land of Khyber to His Messenger as wealth, His Messenger allowed them (Jews) to stay there and made an agreement that the produce there would be (divided equally) between those Jews and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). You are the most disliked of Allah's creations to me. You copied the Prophets of Allah. You attributed falsehood to Allah. But my dislike of you will not induce me to do anything wrong with you. So they said: Because of this (justice and justice) the heavens and the earth are established. We collect from this account. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Radiyallahu Anhu said, \Take out (i.e."," pay) me this production.\"""""
2051,"Sayyiduna Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) ordered that Zakat be collected in the form of grapes by calculating the yield of a grape tree, just as dates are estimated (or dates are collected by estimation)."
2052,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) was once mentioning about Khyber. She said that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Rawaha (RA) to the Jews. When the fruit was ready, he estimated the yield of the palm trees. Then he gave the Jews the option to collect according to this estimate or pay them according to this estimate. The Prophet (PBUH) ordered to estimate. Zakat should be calculated before the fruit is ready and separated. This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira along with another chain of transmission."
2053,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission regarding Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa.
2054,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Hatmah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to make an estimate. Abu Hathmah has imposed more payment on us while estimating. So the Prophet called him and said: Your cousin has to say, \You have made more payment on him in estimating\"" (says the narrator). I said", O Messenger of Allah! I have left so many more dates for him, so that he can feed his family and the poor, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Your cousin has given you more and has acted justly.\"""""
2055,"Sayyiduna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him to guide me to an action that would bring me closer to Paradise and keep me away from Hell! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “If you shorten the speech, avoid asking, ‘Free the slave,’ free the neck (free the slave or the slave girl).” He said, O Messenger of Allah! Aren't these two the same? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! Freeing the soul means that you free it and freeing the neck means that you help it to pay its price 'Give the high-yielding (camel or goat) free of charge and keep the relationship with the abusive relative' If you cannot do this, speak only good things with your tongue."
2056,"Abu Ahmad Zubair says that Sufyan Al-Thawri came and asked him about this hadith. I was there at that time. The narrator has a doubt, 'Perhaps these are the words. Sufyan al-Thawri came to me and asked me about this hadith."
2057,"This same tradition is narrated along with another document, but these words are added in it: feed the hungry, feed the thirsty, enjoin good and forbid evil."
2058,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Mu’adh (RA) to Yemen and said, “When you go to the People of the Book, invite them to bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah.” Tell them that Allah has made zakat obligatory on them in their wealth, which will be given from the wealthy to the poor. If they accept your words about this, then avoid accepting the good wealth of the people and avoid the curse of the oppressed, because there is no veil between him (and Allah)."
2059,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyiduna Mu'adh (RA) to Yemen, he said to him, \Are you going to the People of the Book?\"" The first thing you should invite them to do is to 'confess the oneness of Allah Ta'ala. When they come to know this", you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made five daily prayers obligatory on them. When they know this, you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made five daily prayers obligatory on them, and you should tell them that Allah Ta'ala has made Zakat of their wealth obligatory on them. It will be given from the wealthy people to their poor people. If they acknowledge this," then you will receive it and avoid receiving people's (especially) good wealth."""
2060,Aun bin Abu Huhaifa narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person who collected zakat to us. He collected zakat from our prosperous people and then distributed it among our poor people.
2061,"Aun bin Abu Huhaifah narrates this statement of his father, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his servants to us, in which he collected zakat from our wealthy people and gave it to our poor people. I was an orphan (adult) boy at that time."
2062,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says that Zakat money will not be transferred from one city to another, but it can be done to give a loan to relatives. This tradition is discontinued."
2063,"Sayyidna Ziyad bin Harith al-Sadai (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), ‘He (PBUH) was about to send an army to my people at that time.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! Stop your army. I guarantee you that those people will accept Islam and obey. I write a letter to my people, they will come accepting Islam and obey. The narrator says, \I didn't ask for the people who believe in him!\"" Rather", Allah Ta'ala has favored these people and has blessed them with guidance. Narrator narrates: Then a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) and asked the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) for the amount of Zakat. The Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said to him: Allah, the Exalted," is not satisfied with the decision of any Prophet or any other person regarding Zakat until that person divides this Zakat into eight parts."""
2064,"Sayyidna Haritha bin Muzarab (RA) narrates that some people from Syria came to the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA) and they told us that they had left some property and got slaves. A narrator named Ishaq has quoted these words: \I will do what has been done by those before me.\"" Then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) consulted the people about it. \""Among the people who consulted"," Sayyidna Ali (RA) was included.\"" A narrator named Isaac quotes these words if it is not placed in the order that the wallaby receives it after you (so that's fine). (The narrator says) So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) made the payment of one dinar obligatory for a horse."""
2065,"Asim bin Zamra narrates that some people from Syria brought horses and slaves. They said to Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them: You should collect their Zakat. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, said, \According to my knowledge"," no one has done this before me. I will inquire about it.\"""""
2066,"Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa Radiyallahu Anhu narrates, \He has narrated this matter as a hadeeth\"" (that is", the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said)," \""Whatever Allah has made lawful in His book", is lawful, and what He has made forbidden, is forbidden," and what He has not mentioned is a health.\"" The matter is not forgotten (does not forget). Then he recited this verse. \""And your Lord is not forgetful.\"""""
2067,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sadaqah al-Fitr is a means of purification for the fasting person, and it is given to a poor person as food. No one is hurt in the words of this tradition."
2068,"Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) quotes this statement of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father (Sayyidna Imam Hussain, peace be upon him). So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is obligatory on every small, big, free, slave, and Muslim.”"
2069,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered every Muslim, whether he is free or slave, minor or adult, to pay one saa of dates or one saa of jujube."
2070,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but the word \Muslims\"" is added in it."""
2071,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ordered every Muslim, whether he is a slave or free, male or female, minor or adult, to pay one Saa of dates or one Saa of dates as Sadaqah Fitr after Ramadan."
2072,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has made it obligatory to give one Sa'a of dates or one Sa'a of dates, which is to be paid as Sadaqah Fitr to every slave or free, male and female, minor and adult Muslim."
2073,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has ordered that every Muslim, whether he is young or old, should pay one saa of dates or one saa of barley in the charity of Fitr."
2074,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every free and slave Muslim, which is a saa of dates or a saa of jujube."
2075,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has made it obligatory for every Muslim to pay one Saa of dates as Sadaqah Fitr, after which the narrator mentioned the entire hadith."
2076,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) made obligatory on every Muslim, free or slave, male or female, one saa of dates or one saa of dates as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
2077,"Imam Ali Raza (may Allah be pleased with him) and Imam Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to his father (Imam Jafar Sadiq may God bless him and grant him peace) and his grandfather (Imam Muhammad Baqir may God bless him and grant him peace) with reference to his forefathers and forefathers (i.e. Imam Zain al-Abidin, Imam Hussain and Sayyiduna Ali may God bless him and grant him peace) narrate this saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made it obligatory to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr on every young and old woman who is under his protection."
2078,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has ordered to give Sadaqah-e-Fitrada on behalf of every young and old, free and slave, who are under your care. A narrator named Qasim has narrated it as a marfu' hadith, 'this narrator is not strong and it is true that this hadith is suspended."
2079,"Nafi' narrated this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he used to give Sadaqah Fitrada on behalf of all his family members, including all the people who were dependent on him, he also used to give Sadaqah Fitrada on behalf of his slaves and the slaves of his wives."
2080,Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace be upon him) sent a person to announce this announcement in the streets of Mecca.
2081,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person who announced in a loud voice in the valley of Makkah, “Remember to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr (it is obligatory).” After that, the narrator narrated the previous hadith, “however, these words are extra in it. It is obligatory for every citizen and villager.”"
2082,Amro bin Shuaib narrates that I have come to know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a person who made this announcement to every Muslim (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith).
2083,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a person to announce that Sadaqah al-Fitr is Haqq and that every man, woman, freed slave, citizen, villager, Muslim must give it from a prah, which will be half a day of wheat and a day of date palm."
2084,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered a person to make this announcement in a valley in the valley of Makkah. However, in this tradition, these words are added, remember that children belong to the bed and the adulterer gets deprivation."
2085,Ata states that there will be two days of wheat and one day of dates and one sa' of dates.
2086,"Kathir bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory for every Muslim to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr, which is a Saa of dates, or a Saa of raisins, or a Saa of cheese, or a Saa of jaggery."
2087,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the Prophet (SAW) ordered every citizen and inhabitant, small and large, free and slave, to give a saa of dates, a saa of barley or a maund of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
2088,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that Sadaqah al-Fitr will be one saa of dates or two maads of wheat and it will be paid by every free slave.
2089,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has made Ramadan charity obligatory for every male, female, free and slave, which will be a saa of dates or a saa of grain."
2090,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encouraged everyone to give charity in Ramadan (i.e. Sadaqah al-Fitr) which is a saa of dates or a saa of wheat or a saa of wheat. A narrator of this tradition is not Bakrban Asudaqvi.
2091,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we have been commanded that we should pay Ramadan charity (i.e. Sadaqah al-Fitr) from every free slave, one Saa of grain. will be done Narrator states, I think, 'There are also these words in the hadith, the person who will pay the dough will be accepted by him and the person who will do satvadaka will be accepted by him."
2092,"Kathir bin Abdullah narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has made it obligatory for every man, woman, slave or free to pay Sadaqah al-Fitr."
2093,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) prescribed a saa of dates and a saa of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr. The narrator has also quoted these words. It is obligatory on every free and slave, male and female Muslim."
2094,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm to receive half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates.
2095,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), people used to give a saa of wheat or a saa of dates or a saa of raisins as Sadaqah al-Fitr. When the time of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) came, wheat became abundant, so he set half a sa' of wheat in place of all these things."
2096,"This tradition has been narrated along with some other evidences. In one tradition, these words are mentioned. People mentioned before him the charity of Fitr. He said: I will give the same charity of Fitr that I used to pay during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It will be a saa of dates or raisins, a saa of wheat or a saa of barley or a saa of cheese. Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri said no! This is the price set by Sayyiduna Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) 'I will not accept it nor will I follow it."
2097,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says: “We used to give Sadaqah-e-Fitr on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr, which was one Sa’a of grain or one Sa’a of dates or one Sa’a of barley or one Sa’a of raisins or one Sa’a of raisins. He gave a sermon to the people on the pulpit of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and while mentioning Sadaqah al-Fitr, he explained that I believe that a handful of wheat in the evening is equal to one saa of dates. Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that at that time people first mentioned Domad."
2098,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it these words are a saa of grain."
2099,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to pay one saa of flour or one saa of dates or one saa of wheat or one saa of raisins or one saa of barley or one saa of cheese."
2100,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to him about Sadaqah al-Fitr: It will be a saa of raisins or a saa of dates or a saa of cheese or a saa of flour.
2101,"Malik bin Aws narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give one Saa of grain in Sadaqah al-Fitr. Narrator states that in those days, our grains were wheat, dates, sorghum and cheese."
2102,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2103,"Abdullah bin Thaalbah narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Sadaqa al-Fitr, one Sa'a of dates, one Sa'a of wheat, and half a Sa'a of wheat, should be paid by men and women, free and slave."
2104,"Abdullah bin Thaalbah narrates this statement of his father. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “From every human being, give a sa’a of wheat from every person, small and large, male and female, from the prosperous and the poor."
2105,"Tha'albah bin Abu Sa'eer narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: He paid a sa'a of wheat (the narrator has doubts about a word here) Pay from every small and big, male and female, free and slave, prosperous and poor. Allah will give him more than that."
2106,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \As far as the poor are concerned"," Allah will make him prosperous\""."""
2107,"Al-Zuhri narrates this statement of his father regarding Ibn Abu Saair: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Give a Saa of wheat as Sadaqah al-Fitr from every person, whether he is young or old, free or slave, male or female."
2108,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
2109,"Al-Zuhri narrates this statement of his father with reference to Abdullah bin Thaalbah: Once, while giving a sermon, the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered that every young and old, free and slave, should pay one saa of dates or one saa of barley as Sadaqah al-Fitr."
2110,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: Giving Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every wealthy and poor person.
2111,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Thaalba (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon a day or two before Eid, he (PBUH) said, \Every person will pay a sah of wheat in Sadaqah al-Fitr"," or a sah of any kind of grain in addition to that.\"""""
2112,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) ordered the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr. He said, \It will be one Sa'a of dates", or one Sa'a of wheat," or one Sa'a of wheat.\"""""
2113,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about Sadaqah al-Fitr: “It shall be paid by every small and great, free and slave” which is half a saa of wheat or a saa of dates. The narrator has narrated it as a marfu' hadith in the same way."
2114,This same hadith has been transmitted as a muqaf tradition along with another chain of transmission and it is correct.
2115,"Asma bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sadaqah al-Fitr: it will consist of two saa of wheat, or one saa of barley, or one saa of dates, or one saa of raisins."
2116,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) states that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr is obligatory on every free and slave, male and female, young and old, poor and rich. The narrator narrates that Zahri has narrated this tradition as a marfu' hadith."
2117,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon and said to us, “Whoever has this, he should give half a Sa’a of wheat or a Sa’a of dates or a Sa’a of barley or a Sa’a of flour or a Sa’a of wheat or a Sa’a of wheat (as Sadaqah Fitr). These words have been narrated by a narrator named Salman bin Arqam and this person is a dead hadith."
2118,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Thaalbah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a sermon to the people one day before Eid-ul-Fitr and said, \One Sa'a of wheat should be performed by two men (here", the narrator has doubts about the wording of the hadith) or one Sa'a of date palm or one Sa'a of jujube should be performed by each free and slave," young and old.\"""""
2119,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sadaqa al-Fitr will be paid by every young and old, male and female, Jew and Christian (slave) free and slave, which is half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates or one saa of barley."
2120,"It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to pay sadaqah on behalf of everyone, young and old, male and female, free and slave, unbeliever and Muslim, and he even used to pay sadaqah al-fitr on behalf of his second-class slaves. One of the narrators of this tradition is Uthman."
2121,"Ata bin Abi Rabah says that a man will also give charity on behalf of his slave, even if that slave is a Magian."
2122,"Imam Abu Hanifa says that if you give alms (this is a special tree of India) in Sadaqah al-Fitr, it will also be permissible."
2123,"Bishr ibn Umar narrates, I requested Imam Malik to give me the Mad (specific measure) of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imam Malik asked for it. A slave brought it and he gave it to him. I showed it to Imam Malik and asked: Is this him? He answered yes! This is the measure of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said, “This is not the specific measure of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he himself used.” Rather, it is a measure according to his measurements (says the narrator). We pay according to this.' I said: A person wants to give Sadaqah al-Fitr or a kind of expiation according to Mud (whichever is greater, will it be paid)? He said: No! He should pay according to that amount, then after that he should pay as much as he wants."
2124,"Ishaq bin Salman narrates: I asked Imam Malik: O Abu Abdullah! What was the weight of the Prophet's Sa'a? So he replied, five pounds and one-third of a pound according to the Iraqi pound. I have measured it. I said: O Abu Abdullah! You have issued a fatwa against the elders of your time. They asked who they are. I said: Imam Abu Hanifa! Because they say that it is eight pounds, Imam Malik got angry and said: May Allah destroy them! What courage has he shown regarding Allah Ta'ala? Then he said to one of the people sitting there: O so-and-so! You come with your old majesty, oh so and so! You bring your uncle's saa, oh so-and-so! You bring your grandmother's saa. A narrator named Ishaq narrates that there various people gathered together, Imam Malik said; On what account do you preserve it? So he said that my father has narrated this matter regarding his father, he had paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this saa. The second gentleman said that my father has narrated this with reference to his brother, he had paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this saa. The third said: My father told me this. He narrated this from his mother. He paid the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) according to this Saa. The narrator says: I said: O Abu Abdullah! I will tell you something even more surprising about him (i.e. Imam Abu Hanifa) 'He says that half a Sa'a will be paid in Sadaqah al-Fitr and one Sa'a is worth eight pounds', so Imam Malik said that this is even more surprising than before. We have heard the scholars of our city (Madinah) saying this in full."
2125,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) states that the payment of Sadaqah al-Fitr will be obligatory on every Muslim, big or small, on a “free slave” who will buy two half of wheat or one saa of wheat."
2126,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it will be two maunds of wheat or one saa of wheat.
2127,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that your expenses will be calculated according to the calculation, it will be half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates."
2128,Abu Qalaba says that he has told me that those who paid Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) paid half a sa' of wheat.
2129,Abu Qalaba narrates that a person told me that he had paid one Saa of wheat to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) on behalf of two men (i.e. half a Saa is required to be paid to one person).
2130,"Hasan al-Basri narrates that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was the governor of Basra, he said at the end of Ramadan, Pay Zakat (Zakat al-Fitr) for your fasts. The narrator narrates that the people started looking at each other and Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) inquired who are the people here who belong to the people of Madinah? Those people stand up! And tell your companions about it, because these people do not know that this is the payment that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made obligatory on every male and female, free and slave, which is a saa of barley or a saa of dates or half a saa of wheat."
2131,"Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, while giving a sermon to the people at the end of Ramadan, said, O people of Basra! Pay the zakat of your fasts (i.e. give charity at Fitr) the narrator says. People started looking at each other and Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) said, \All the people who are here from Madinah should stand up and teach this to their companions"," because these people do not know that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered half a Saa of wheat or a Saa of barley or a Saa of dates for every free and slave\"" Mandatory on women. Hasan Basri narrates that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when Allah gives you prosperity"," you should pay one Sa'a of wheat."""
2132,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that before the people go to perform the Eid prayer, Sadaqah al-Fitr should be given (narrated by the narrator)."
2133,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) made it obligatory to pay Zakat al-Fitr.
2134,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this order: \A person should give Sadaqah al-Fitr before going to pray.\"""""
2135,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this instruction about it: \It should be performed before the people go for the Eid prayer.\"""""
2136,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that this is a Sunnah: \A person should not go to perform the Eid prayer until he has taken some food and given Sadaqah al-Fitr.\"""""
2137,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that this is a Sunnah: \Ghusl Janabat should be performed with one Sa'a of water," and ablution and one liter of water should be performed.\"" One Sa'a is eight Ritals. Regarding the narrator named Mansoor"," this hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Salih and this person is weak."""
2138,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with a bucket of water.
2139,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with one mud (water) and one sa' (eight liters) of water.
2140,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the husband of Sayyida Barira (RA) was a slave, his name was Mugheeth, that scene is also in my eyes, that man was crying behind this woman, his tears were flowing on his beard. Don't you wonder how much Mughees loves Breera and how much Breera dislikes Mughees. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to this woman that you should maintain your marriage with him, because he is the father of your children. This woman said, O Messenger of Allah! Are you ordering me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I am interceding.\"" The woman said"," \""There is no need for me to have intercourse with her.\"""""
2141,"Majlid narrates that I was the secretary of Jaz bin Muawiya, who is the uncle of Sayyidna Ahnaf bin Qays. We received a letter from Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, a year before his death. (The narrator says) We killed three sorcerers. We made every man to marry a wife whose marriage has been forbidden by Allah. Then they prepared a lot of food and invited the magicians. They placed their swords on their shoulders. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not receive jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received jizya from the Magi who belonged to the Hijra."
2142,"Abu Muawiya narrates that I was the secretary of Sayyidna Jaz bin Muawiya, “We received a letter from Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (which contained this text) Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, collected jizya from the Magi who belonged to the Hijra, so you should also collect jizya from the Magi of your region. The narrator of this hadith is not authentic."
2143,"A narrator named Bajla narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not receive jizya from the Magi before, even Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) testified that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, received jizya from these magi. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated that once I was sitting at the door of the Prophet (PBUH) two men came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). So both of them said (they have given this decision) Either we accept Islam or we are killed, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated, then the people adopted the statement of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman Bin Awf (RA) and abandoned my tradition."
2144,"Bajla Tamimi narrates that Sayyiduna Umar did not want to accept jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to collect jizya from the Magi who belonged to the \Hijr\""."""
2145,"Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that if I had not seen my companions receiving jizya from the Magi, I would not have received it from them. Then he recited this verse (i.e., I would not have received it by the command of this verse) \And fight those who do not believe in Allah and the Last Day"," and do not consider that which is forbidden by Allah and His Messenger to be haram.\"" Act while they are disrespectful."""
2146,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the people went out to see the moon. I told the Prophet (PBUH) that I had also seen the moon. So the Prophet (PBUH) himself fasted and ordered the people to fast too. Regarding quoting from Ibn Wahib, this tradition has been narrated by Marwan ibn Muhammad, who is unique and this narrator is reliable."
2147,This tradition is also narrated along with an Usand.
2148,"Taus narrates: I was in Madinah, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas were also there. A man came to the governor there and testified that he had seen the moon (i.e., when he saw the moon of Ramadan). The Messenger of Allah accepted the testimony of one person about seeing the moon of Ramadan. These two men also stated that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to accept the testimony of only two men about the moon of Eid al-Fitr. The narrator named Abu Ismail Hafs is unique in narrating this tradition and it is weak."
2149,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe the moon of Sha'ban, then he would observe the moon and observe the fast."
2150,"Saying salah, we were present with Sayyidna Ammar, may Allah be pleased with him, and a goat was roasted for him, and he asked to eat it: so a man withdrew."
2151,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting for six days (the day of which there is doubt), the day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of Eid al-Adha, the days of Tashriq among the narrators of this hadith, other narrators are more authentic than Waqidi."
2152,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that there was a dispute among the people about the moon of Ramadan. Some said: It will be seen today. Some said: It will be seen tomorrow. So he answered yes! So the Prophet (PBUH) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (RA) to proclaim among the people that they should fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast by looking at it (the moon) and end the fast by looking at it. If a cloud overshadows you, complete the count of thirty days, start fasting and do not fast the day before. Some narrators have also quoted this tradition as a Mursal tradition."
2153,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \A man came to the Messenger of Allah", may God bless him and grant him peace," and said: I have seen the moon.\"" He answered yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," “O Bilal! Announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow."""
2154,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated that a villager came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have seen the moon. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O Bilal! Announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow. The meaning of this hadith is close to the meaning (of the previous tradition)."
2155,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2156,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a villager came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “I have seen the first moon.” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (PBUH) is the Messenger of Allah?” He said: Yes! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced that people should fast."
2157,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came on a moonlit night of Ramadan and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have seen the moon.' The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah? He said yes! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced that you people should fast. This tradition has been narrated by a narrator named Shuba as a transmitted tradition from Thori."
2158,"Ikrimah narrates that a villager testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah? He said yes! So the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the people to celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr."
2159,"Ikrima narrates that the people had doubts about the moon of Ramadan. They decided that they would not fast the next day and not perform Taraweeh that night. A villager came to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) from the rocky land. He testified that he had seen the moon. There is no god but I am the messenger of Allah? He said yes! But he testified that he had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal to tell the people to recite Taraweeh on that day (and fast the next day)."
2160,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Before the moon of Ramadan is visible (do not fast as a precaution), however (if a person has a habit of fasting and it is a day, then he can fast) fast by looking at the moon and end the fast by looking at it. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
2161,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this one or two days before Ramadan (do not start fasting as a precaution), then complete the count of thirty and finish fasting."
2162,This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission (stop fasting).
2163,This hadeeth was narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) and all these chain of chains are authentic.
2164,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you see the first moon, start fasting, and when you see it, stop fasting, and if it is cloudy, then fast for thirty days."
2165,"Sayyiduna Rabi narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast it (on seeing the first moon) and perform Eid-ul-Fitr upon seeing it, and if it is cloudy, complete the thirty days of Sha’ban, then start fasting. (Look at the moon) This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions."
2166,"Rabi' has narrated it from a Sahabi, the month (do not start fasting before it begins) until you see the first moon."
2167,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Do not start fasting until you see the first moon, and do not end it until you see the first moon. If it is cloudy, fast for thirty days. This hadith has been narrated in Mota on the authority of Nafi on the authority of Ibn Dinar on the authority of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in which there are these words: complete the count."
2168,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (the month) is sometimes twenty-nine days long. Narrated by Nafi) When the twenty-nine days of Sha'ban passed, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) would say to someone who was permitted to see the moon, 'If it was visible, then it would be fine.' The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to finish fasting with the people."
2169,Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Beware! Before the month (of Ramadan) (do not fast as a precaution) until you see the moon (complete the number of thirty days) and do not fast until you see the moon (or complete the number). All the narrators of this tradition are authentic.
2170,"Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of one of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this. \Do not fast (as a precaution) before the month of Ramadan. Do not start fasting until you see the moon and complete the number of Leviathan. Then start fasting and do not stop fasting until you see (the moon of Shawwal) or complete the number of thirty.\"""""
2171,This tradition is also narrated along with another document which is similar to it.
2172,"Abu Bakhtari narrates that we saw the Eid moon at the place of Zaat Shaquq. We doubted whether it was the first moon or the second or third date. So we sent a person to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah has related this order to seeing the moon. This hadith is authentic regarding its transmission from Shu'ba. Other narrators have narrated it on the authority of Amro bin Murrah."
2173,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (The narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words). The hadith is authentic regarding transmission from Shuba. Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, has quoted this hadith from Shuba regarding Adam, and it contains these words: \You complete the number of thirty days of the month of Sha'ban.\"" In this hadith"," the word \""means\"" is not quoted."""
2174,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Count the moon of the first of Sha’ban for Ramadan and do not combine Sha’ban with Ramadan.
2175,"Sayyidna Qays bin Talaq narrates from his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \Allah has placed the first moon to count the days for people. When you see it", start fasting, and when you see it, stop fasting, and if there is a cloud over you, complete the number of thirty. Muhammad bin Jabarrawi narrates that I heard this tradition from him. In addition, I heard more narrations from Muhammad bin Jabernami narrators are not authentic," they are weak."""
2176,"Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take care of the number of Sha’ban for Ramadan.” Do not fast before the month of Ramadan begins. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his thumb inwards."
2177,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the month is sometimes twenty-nine days long, so do not start fasting until you see the moon, and do not fast until you see it, and if there are clouds, complete the number of thirty. Mina is the place of all sacrifices and Makkah is the place of all sacrifices. Hamad bin Zayd has narrated this tradition with reference to Ayub and has narrated it as a tradition that has been passed down to the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
2178,"This tradition is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, it mentions that it was transmitted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while there is also a continuation of the same tradition."
2179,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) \Start fasting by looking at the moon.\"" Then he has narrated the previous hadith according to it"," but he did not mention that \""the month is sometimes twenty-nine days long. The narrator of this hadith is Rooh Bin Qasim Al-Thaqa.\"""""
2180,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that your fast will be on the same day when all the people will fast and your Eid will be on the same day when everyone will be celebrating the Eid.
2181,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Fasting will be on the same day when you all fast, and Eid-ul-Fitr will be on the same day when you all celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr, and the Great Eid will be when you all offer Eid-ul-Fitr. The narrator of this tradition is weak."
2182,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when a person hears the call to prayer and has a vessel in his hand, he should not put it down until he fulfills his need. Imam Abu Dawud states that the authenticity of this hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Rooh bin Ubadah in the same way as described by Abdul A'la."
2183,"Abd al-Rahman bin Aish, who was a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, says that Fajr is of two types, one that spreads in the sky in the direction of length, it does not interfere with a person's Suhoor prayer, it is not permissible to perform the Fajr prayer at this time, but when it spreads in the direction of width, then the food (of Suhoor) becomes Ihram at that time, and at that time you can perform the Fajr prayer. This tradition is authentic."
2184,"Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman narrates that I have come to know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Fajr is of two types, one is like the tail of a wolf, it does not make anything halal or haraam, but the one that spreads in the direction of width, it becomes halal to pray and the (eating) of Suhoor becomes haraam."
2185,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Fajr is of two types. One is that in which it is not permissible to pray (Fajr) prayer. Faryabi and other Muhadditheen have narrated it as a Muqoof tradition, while the students of Ibn Jaraj have narrated it as a Muqoof tradition with regard to him."
2186,"Salim bin Abu Ubaid narrates that I was under the tutelage of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq, may Allah be pleased with him, one night he prayed for as long as Allah permitted. Salim narrates, I came out and came back and told him that the whiteness in the sky is moving upwards (in the direction of length). I came again and came and replied that the red has spread in the direction of the width in the sky, so he said yes! Now it's time, bring my breakfast."
2187,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \I said: The direction of the width is light and it is red"," so Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: Now bring me something to drink. Narrators narrate these words in a tradition. One day Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: \""Stand at the door (between me and Fajr) and tell me when (Fajr breaks) this tradition is authentic."""
2188,"Abdullah bin Nu'man narrates that once in the last part of the night in the month of Ramadan, Sayyidna Qais bin Talaq (RA) came to me. At that time, the Suhoor meal had been stopped due to the fear of dawn. He asked me for curry. I said: O uncle! If there is still some part of the night left, I will give you food and drink. Then they came inside, so I gave them meat and nabeez in front of them (Tharir). They ate and drank them and forced me too. So I also ate and drank and I was afraid of dawn. Then Sayyiduna Talaq has narrated this thing regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As long as the head does not spread in front of you in the direction of width, the narrator indicated this with his hand. His narrator, Qais bin Talaq, is not authentic."
2189,"Sayyiduna Samura bin Jund b, may Allah be pleased with him, said this while giving a sermon: \Do not let Bilal's call to prayer stop you from starting Suhoor"," and do not let the light that spreads across the horizon (in the direction of length) stop you as long as it spreads in the direction of width (you may eat Suhoor). This tradition is authentic."""
2190,Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Do not misunderstand Bilal's call to prayer and this whiteness.
2191,"Hussain bin Harith narrates the polemical narration: The Governor of Makkah while giving a sermon to us gave this oath to the people and inquired who saw the moon on \so-and-so first\"" then he told us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us (to sacrifice on the day of Eid al-Adha) if we do not see the moon ourselves and two righteous witnesses testify to this", then we should offer the sacrifice (i.e. Eid al-Adha) on the testimony of both of them. Asked who the governor was, he replied, I don't know. After that, I met him. He said that he was Sahib Harith bin Hatib," who was the brother of Sayyidna Muhammad bin Hatib. His chain of transmission is connected and this hadith is authentic."""
2192,"Hussain bin Harith narrates, the governor of Makkah said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had instructed us to (sacrifice after seeing the moon), that is, to celebrate Eid-ul-Adha, and if we do not see the moon ourselves and two righteous people bear witness to it, then we should sacrifice on the basis of the testimony of both of them. So he replied that he was Harith bin Hatib, who was the brother of Muhammad bin Hatib. This governor also said that there is a person among you who has the most knowledge in the (rules) of Allah and His Messenger. Then this governor pointed to a person who was there. The narrator describes who he was? So he replied - He was Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA). Abu Bakr Nishapuri narrates that I inquired about this tradition from Ibrahim Harbi. He said that Saeed bin Sulaiman narrated this tradition to us. After that, Ibrahim narrated that he was Sahib Harith bin Hatib bin Harith bin Muammar bin Khabib bin Wahib bin Huzaifah bin Juma, who had the privilege of migrating to Abyssinia."
2193,"Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that we have the privilege of being in the company of the Companions of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. \Start fasting after seeing it (the first moon) and stop fasting when you see it", and if it is cloudy, complete the number of thirty. If two righteous people testify," then start fasting (on the basis of their testimony). Perform Eid-ul-Fitr or sacrifice (i.e. celebrate Eid-ul-Adha)."""
2194,Rabi narrates this with reference to a Sahabi: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting and it was the thirtieth day of Ramadhan. Dodihati came and they testified that there is no god but Allah and they said that they had seen the moon last night.
2195,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates that Sayyiduna Umar accepted the testimony of a person regarding the sighting of the moon on Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha. The narrator named Eid al-Ala has quoted Ibn Abi Laila in the same way, but the narrator named Abd al-Ala is weak. Similarly, the narrator named Ibn Abi Laila has not found the age of Sayyiduna Umar. Abu Wail Shaqiq bin Salama has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated this on the authority of Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, has said this: \You people should not fast until two men bear witness (that they have seen the moon).\"" This tradition has been narrated by Amish and Mansoor on his authority."""
2196,"Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates that we received a letter from Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. We were in Khanaqin at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \When you see the moon of the first day in the early part of the day"," then do not celebrate Eid until the third hour until two people testify that they saw the moon the previous night. This tradition is more authentic than the tradition of Ibn Abi Laila.\"""""
2197,"Abu Wail narrates that a letter came to us (at the place of Khanaqin) from Sayyiduna Umar (in which it was written): The first moon is sometimes small and large, so when you see the moon in the early part of the day, do not celebrate Eid until two men testify that they saw the moon the previous night."
2198,"Ibn Abi Laila narrates, \I was with Sayyidna Umar (RA) and a rider came to him and said that he had seen the first moon. So Sayyidna Umar (RA) instructed the people to celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr.\"" Muhammad bin Ali narrates: I asked Abu Na'im whether Ibn Abi Laila narrated the hadith from Sayyiduna Umar", so he replied," \""I don't know.\"" Muhammad bin Ali narrates", I inquired from Yahya bin Mu'in whether Ibn Laila had heard the hadith from Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him), so he did not declare it to be correct. The tradition of Abu Wail is more authentic in terms of chain of transmission," which is narrated by Amish and Mansoor with reference to Abu Wail."""
2199,"Abu Wail narrated that a letter from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us, and we were at the place of Khanaqin at that time (it contained this text) The first moon is sometimes small and big, so when you see the moon in the early part of the day, do not celebrate Eid until two righteous men testify that they saw the moon last night. Who is"
2200,"Abu Wail narrates that a letter came to us from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that we were in Khanaqin at that time (it contained this text) The first moon is sometimes small and large, so when you see the moon during the day, break your fast until evening, until two Muslims testify that they saw the moon last night (then you break your fast and celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr)."
2201,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2202,"Rabi bin Harash narrates on the authority of a Sahabi, there was a dispute between the people about the last day of Ramadan, 'the villagers came and they swore in the name of Allah in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and testified that they both had seen the moon last night. A narrator named Khalaf narrated this additionally: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed) People to come to the Eidgah (for the Eid prayer)."
2203,"Abu Umar bin Anas narrates this on the authority of his uncle. It was witnessed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the people had seen the moon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the people (to break their fast and go for the Eid prayer the next morning). This tradition is good and the tradition after it is also good."
2204,"Abu Bashir narrates, I heard Abu Umayr bin Anas narrate on the authority of some of his uncles, Abu Nafar narrates on the authority of his Ansari uncles, they were present with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the latter part of the day, some riders came there and testified that they had seen the moon last night, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed the people that they should (break their fast and go to the Eidgah the next day) to perform the Eid prayer. go"
2205,"Fatima bint Hussain narrates that a person testified to Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) about seeing the moon of Ramadan, then Sayyidna Ali Bin Abu Talib (RA) fasted. The narrator narrates that he also ordered the people to fast and said, \I should fast on the day of Sha'baan"," this is better for me than that I should not fast on the day of Ramadan.\"" Imam Shafi'i says"," \""If the common people have not seen the moon of Ramadan and a righteous person sees it", then I will accept his testimony because it is also transmitted by influence and caution is also in it, but after that Imam Shafi'i issued this fatwa. The testimony of at least two people is a condition for Ramadan. Imam Shafi'i and some of our companions have stated this. This is Ruqiyas," this is the order of witnessing about every missing thing."""
2206,"Imam Shafi'i says that whoever sees the moon of Ramadan alone, then he should fast on that day, and whoever sees the moon of Shawwal, he should not fast on that day and keep it a secret (but on the testimony of this banana, other people will not fast or not fast)."
2207,"Imam Malik states that whoever sees the moon of Ramadan alone, then he should fast because it is not right for him to fast now, because he knows that this day is part of Ramadan. Then he should state this when the moon appears in front of the people and they should say that we have seen the moon."
2208,"Abu Bakhtari narrates: We saw the moon of Dhu al-Hajj, and it seemed large to us. The person who described it as less, said it was the moon of the second night: And the one who was describing it more, he called it the moon of the third night. He said, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has conditioned (the beginning of the month) with the sighting of the moon.\"" This tradition and the following tradition are authentic."""
2209,"Abu Bahtari narrates: We set out to perform Umrah. When we camped in Batin Nakhla, we saw the moon. Some said: This is the moon of the second night, and some said: This is the moon of the third. At night, he said, \This is the same night in which you saw it"," because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his command conditional on seeing it. This hadith is authentic.\"""""
2210,"Abu Bakhtari narrates that we saw the moon of Ramadan. We were present in ``Urq. We sent a person to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) to inquire about it. He said: The Prophet (PBUH) said this. Verily, Allah spreads it out in front of you so that you can see it."
2211,"Kareeb narrates that Sayyida Umm al-Fazl bint Harith (RA) sent him to the service of Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) and he says, “I came to Syria to complete the work of Sayyid Umm Fazl.” At the same time, the moon of Ramadan was seen. I was in Syria. “I saw the moon on Friday night. When did you see the moon? So I replied, I saw it on Friday night. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) asked: Did you see it from God? I said: Yes! And the people had also seen it. I had also fasted. Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) had also fasted. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We saw it on Saturday night and we will fast continuously. He answered no! This is what the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has instructed us. This tradition is authentic."
2212,"Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the morning of the thirtieth day of Ramadan, Dudihati came and testified before the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw the moon last night. Chapter To make the intention (of fasting) at night."
2213,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH). \The person who does not intend to fast before dawn is not fasting," he does not fast.\"" Abdullah bin Ibadanami is unique in quoting this hadith from Mufadl"," but all his narrators are reliable."""
2214,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Hafsa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “There is no fasting for a person who does not make it obligatory before he is righteous in the morning.”"
2215,"This is narrated along with another chain of transmission. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever does not make it necessary at night\"" this tradition is also chained together with other chain of chains."""
2216,Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Whoever does not make it obligatory before dawn, his fast is not fasted. Some narrators have narrated it as a valid tradition, some have narrated it as the saying of Sayyidna Hafsa, may Allah be pleased with them, and some have narrated it as the saying of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, while some narrators have related it to Salem," Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Narrated by Hafsah Radiyallahu Anhu."""
2217,"Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a person who does not intend to fast in the morning before becoming righteous, does not fast."
2218,"Saida Maimoona bint Saad (RA) narrates that I heard the Holy Prophet (SAW) saying, \Whoever intends to fast at night", let him fast, and whoever comes in the morning and does not intend to fast," let him not fast.\"""""
2219,"Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Qais says that I heard the wife of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), Mrs. Aisha Siddiqa (R.A.), saying that once on the thirtieth day, the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) woke up in the morning while fasting."
2220,"Salim narrates this about his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): Once he saw the Shawwal moon during the day, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is not lawful for you to break the fast until you see the first moon, when it is visible (ie at night)."
2221,"Mu'adhbin Muhammad narrates, I asked Zuhri about the moon of Shawwal when it is seen in the morning, and he said, I heard Saeed bin Musayyib say that if the moon of Shawwal rises in the morning until Asr (maybe these words are up to Maghrib), the moon of that night that follows will be counted. Imam Abu Abdullah says that everyone agrees on this."
2222,"Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her. A vessel was brought to him, so he drank from it. Then he extended the vessel to me. I said, I am fasting. Eat it."
2223,"The son of Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) narrates that he heard Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) saying, \A drink was brought to the Prophet (PBUH).\"" He drank it"," and then extended it to me. \""Then I said"," \""O Prophet of God! I was fasting",' then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Did you fast? They did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," then there is no harm to you. The wording of this hadith has been disputed in narrating from a narrator named Sumak."""
2224,"Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a drink was brought before the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He drank it and gave it to me to drink, so I also drank it. I said, O Messenger of Allah! I was fasting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A person who observes post-post-fasting is (Amin) about his will (the narrator doubts that he may say these words) is amir (i.e. he owns his will) i.e. he can keep the fast if he wants to and break it if he wants to.” Shuba narrates, I inquired, have you heard this hadith from Sayyida Umm Hani? So he said: No! This hadith has been narrated by our family and Abu Salih, a narrator named Shuba narrates."
2225,The same hadith is narrated from Sayyida Umm Hani (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
2226,"Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank a drink and gave his remaining drink to Sayyida Umm Hani (may God be pleased with him), so Sayyida Umm Hani also drank it. There are such words in a tradition narrated by a narrator named Abu Awana. \The narrator's saying that this hadith is narrated from Yahya bin Ja'd is an illusion of a narrator named Waleed and this narrator is weak.\"""""
2227,"Harun narrates this from his grandmother (Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with him) I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I was fasting. If it was a fast of expiation, then you should fast one day instead of it, and if it was a fast of post-post-mortem, then if you want to make up for it, then if you want, do not make up for it. This hadith has been narrated by Hatim bin Abu Saghira on the authority of Samak on the authority of Abu Salih on the authority of Sayyidah Umm Hani."
2228,"Sayyida Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the one who fasts post-natally has the right to keep the fast if he wishes."
2229,"Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A person who fasts after fasting is Amin (the narrator has doubts) about himself, Ameer (i.e. he is the owner of his own will) whether he keeps the fast or breaks it if he wants. Sumak has heard this hadith from the son of Sayyida Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with him) 'Allah knows the rest."
2230,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) that he did not think there was any problem in breaking the post-natal fast.
2231,Sayyidah Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes intend to fast in the morning. Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes! But there is nothing wrong with me breaking the fast while it is Nazr Kana or Ramadan Kana. The narrator named Muhammad Bin Ubaidullah is Arzmi and this narrator is weak.
2232,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to like one food. I did not submit! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then I will fast.\"""""
2233,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and asked, “Do you have anything (to eat)?” I did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then I fast.\"" Then one day", the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to me and asked," \""Do you have anything to eat?\"" I said yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Then I will eat.\"""""
2234,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a person fasts after fasting, he can break it whenever he wants."
2235,"Aoun bin Abu Huhaifa narrates this with reference to his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made Sayyiduna Sulaiman Farsi and Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with them) each other's mouths. He replied, \Your brother recites Bharnaful all night long. He fasts during the day. He has no need of the world and his wife. Then Sayyidna Abu Darda came. He welcomed Sayyidna Sulaiman. He gave food in front of him. Sayyiduna Sulaiman said to him: Eat too.\"" The Prophet (may Allah be pleased with him) also said: I will not eat until you eat. Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) ate with him. Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him at night. When it was night", Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) wanted them to start performing Nawafil. So Sayyiduna Salman stopped them and said to them: Your body has a right over you and your Lord has a right over you. You also have the right to observe the post-post-fasting and even leave it for a day. Abu Darda came to the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) to tell him about what Sayyiduna Salman (Radi Allahu Anhu) said to him: So the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said to him," O Abu Darda! Your body also has a right over you. He said the same thing that Sayyidna Salman said. These words of tradition are from a narrator named Abu Talib."""
2236,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that sometimes the Holy Prophet (PBUH) would come to us and ask, \Do you have anything to eat?\"" If we answer yes! So you would eat it and if we ask", yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: I fast. Once you came to us, we were sent a gift (Hays). I said, O Messenger of Allah! We have been given the gift of ``what I have kept for you.'' So he said, ``I intended to fast in the morning,"'' but then you ate it. This hadith is authentic."""
2237,"Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to me and said: I have intended to fast. Then Hays was brought to your service. In these words, this hadith has been quoted only by Bahli, 'no one else has copied it and no one has followed it', i.e. these words, \I will fast again in its place. Perhaps this matter has become suspicious for them", 'Allah knows best'," because other narrators have disagreed with Ibn Uyaynah in copying these words."""
2238,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask for something to eat and if he did not get anything on that day, he would fast on that day. Abdullah, the narrator of this tradition, is not known."
2239,"Ibrahim bin Ubaid narrates that once Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) prepared food and invited the Prophet (PBUH) and some of his companions, one of the people present said: I have stopped fasting. The Prophet (PBUH) said: Your brother has prepared food for you. Your brother has arranged for you."
2240,Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever forgetfully eats something in the month of Ramadan," then it will not be necessary to make up for it. Allah will have fed and watered him.\"""""
2241,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that one of the companions of the Prophet (PBUH) prepared food. He invited the Prophet (PBUH) and his companions. 'The food was brought.' Then one of those people retreated. 'The Prophet (PBUH) asked him what happened to you?' He said, \I have fasted.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him"," \""Your brother has arranged and prepared it for you", and now you are saying," \""I have fasted.\"" Eat it and instead of this fast"," fast another day.\"""""
2242,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that if a fasting person forgets to eat something, then this is the sustenance that Allah has given him. Its chain of transmission is correct and all its narrators are trustworthy."
2243,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that if someone forgetfully eats something in the month of Ramadan (while fasting), then no expiation will be required for him and no disbeliever will be required for him. A narrator named Muhammad bin Marzooq is unique in narrating this tradition and it is reliable that he is the one who narrated this tradition from Muhammad bin Abdullah Ansari."
2244,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If one of you eats something forgetfully or drinks something forgetfully (in the month of Ramadan), it will not be necessary to make up for it."
2245,The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission.
2246,Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever eats or drinks something while forgetting (the duty of fasting), then he should maintain his fast, and it will not be necessary to make up for it. The narrator of this hadith is Narrator Nazrbin Tarif," Abu Juzi is weak.\"""""
2247,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever forgets to eat or drink something in Ramadan (while fasting) then completes his fast, and it will not be necessary to make up for it. The narrator named Yasin is weak and the narrator named Abdullah bin Saeed is also like him (weak)."
2248,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever forgets to eat or drink something (while fasting), then this is the sustenance that Allah has given him. Both the narrators of this tradition, Mandal and Abdullah bin Saeed, are weak."
2249,"Waleed bin Abdul Rahman narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) mentioning that he had forgotten to eat something on the first day of Ramadan, he said, “I mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH).” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Complete your fast.” Indeed, ALLAH has fed and watered you, and there is no obligation on you."
2250,"This tradition is also narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, along with another chain of transmission."
2251,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever forgets to eat or drink something, then he should not break the fast because this is the sustenance that Allah has given him."
2252,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a person who forgot to eat something and he is fasting.
2253,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “After this, there is a hadith according to the previous one, its chain of transmission is authentic.”"
2254,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (while fasting in the month of Ramadan). Abu Bakr Nahishli has narrated the same words following him and this narrator is reliable.
2255,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her during the month of Ramadan.
2256,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss him while he was fasting in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to have the most control over himself."
2257,"Dawood bin Abu Asim narrates that he heard Saeed bin Musaib narrating that once Sayyiduna (R.A.) came to his companions and inquired, \What are the people's opinions about what I have done today?\"" In the morning", I had fasted, then a maid passed by me, I liked her, so I had intercourse with her, people felt this act of hers was very wrong, while Sayyidna Ali remained silent, Sayyidna Umar inquired, what do you say? He said," \""You have committed a halal deed", and instead of this day," you should fast on another day.\"" Then Sayyiduna Umar", may Allah be pleased with him, said," \""You have given the best fatwa of all of them.\"""""
2258,"Sayyiduna Abu Darda (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) vomited, so he broke it. The narrator narrates that later I met Sayyidna Thawban, a freed slave of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) in the Jama Masjid of Damascus. The name of a narrator of this hadith according to one view is Ma'dan bin Abu Talha and according to another view it is Ma'dan bin Talha."
2259,"Sayyidna Fazala bin Ubaid narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting, he vomited, so he broke his fast."
2260,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, \I used to not consider it abhorrent for a fasting person to touch his back.\"" Once Sayyidna Ja'far bin Abu Talib (may God be pleased with him) was fasting and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him. It is narrated that Sayyiduna Anas used to pray while fasting. All the narrators of this tradition are reliable and I do not know of any reason for it."""
2261,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it is permissible to make a fasting person sit on his back. The narrator of this hadith is Abdul Aziz.
2262,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the fasting person to make his back. All the narrators of this hadith are trustworthy.
2263,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that kissing and kissing a fasting person is permitted.
2264,"Ayyub bin Muhammad Ajli, on the authority of the son of Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, narrates this on the authority of his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast on the 17th day of Ramadan, although he had previously said that the fast of one who fasts and fasts is broken. There has been a dispute regarding the transmission of this tradition from a narrator named Yasin and this narrator is weak."
2265,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fasten his legs while he was fasting.
2266,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fast on the 17th day of Ramadan, although he had previously said that the fast of both the one who drives and the one who drives is broken."
2267,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to fasten his heels, although he had previously said that the fast of the one who puts on his heels and the one who is doing them is broken."
2268,Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission for a fasting person to kiss and touch each other.
2269,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that three things do not break the fast: vomiting, belching, and defecation."
2270,Sayyiduna Maimuna bint Saad (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who kisses his wife even though both of them have fasted.
2271,"This tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, this is not proven."
2272,"Sayyidna Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was fasting. This is not the fasting of Ramadan. He had a problem that was painful for him. Then he vomited. Then he asked for water for ablution. Is it obligatory to perform ablution after vomiting? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If this was obligatory"," you would have mentioned it in the Qur'an.\"" The narrator narrates that after that", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted the next day, so I heard him saying," \""This is in return for my breaking the fast of the previous day.\"""""
2273,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever vomits on purpose, Qadaa will be obligatory on him, and whoever vomits, Qadaa will not be obligatory on him. All the narrators of this hadith are trustworthy."
2274,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2275,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH) \When a fasting person vomits with his mouth full," it is not necessary for him to break his fast and then it is not necessary to make up for it.\"" If he intentionally vomits"," then it is necessary to make up for it."""
2276,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever vomits with his mouth full, he must complete his fast, and he will have to make up for it, and whoever vomits on purpose," he must make up for it.\"""""
2277,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would break his fast, he would eat a few dates or a few chawhars, and if he did not have that, he would drink a few sips of water."
2278,Thabit Banani narrates that he heard Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) used to break his fast after eating a few dates.
2279,"Marwan narrates that I saw Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, that he was holding his beard in his fist and was cutting off the part that was more than a fist."
2280,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates what the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the time of breaking the fast: \O Allah! We have fasted for You and we have broken the fast from the sustenance that You have given us.\"" So accept it from us."""
2281,"Urwa quoted Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA), while Salim quoted it on Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA), both of them said that fasting on these days is only for the person who has a sacrificial animal."
2282,This hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and its chain of transmission is correct.
2283,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that the Prophet (PBUH) permitted a person performing Hajj to fast during the days of Tashreeq if he does not have an animal for sacrifice.
2284,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the permission to fast during the days of Tashreeq is only for those performing Hajj who have a sacrificial animal with them. This hadith is authentic.
2285,"Urwa Bin Zubair has narrated this. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa and Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) have both narrated this. The Prophet (PBUH) also did not allow a person to fast during the days of Tashreek, except for a person who performs Hajj (and has an animal with him) and a person who is besieged. This person is Abu Maryam Al-Kufi and he is weak."
2286,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that whoever has a sacrificial animal with him should fast three days before the sacrifice, and whoever could not fast during those three days should fast during the days of Tashreeq (i.e. the days of menstruation). The narrator of this hadith is weak."
2287,Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyidna Abdullah bin Hudhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) to go round Mina (to announce) that you should not fast during these days! Because these are the days of eating and drinking and the days of remembering Allah.
2288,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him).
2289,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa Sahmi (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) instructed a few people, including him, that on the occasion of Hajj Al-Wadaa, they should go around in the manna on the day of sacrifice and announce that these are the days of eating and drinking and remembering Allah."
2290,"Masoud bin Huqam narrates this on the authority of one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) that the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) instructed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa (R.A.) to announce during the days of Tashreeq, beware! These are the days of Eid and the days of eating, drinking and dhikr, so only the person who is performing Hajj and has a sacrificial animal with him should fast on those days, and the person who has not fasted continuously during the days of Hajj can fast on those days. The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Abu Dawood weak. This hadith has been quoted by Zubaid on the authority of Zuhri, which he has quoted on the authority of Masood bin Haqam on the authority of one of the Prophet’s Companions. The narrator of this hadith is Sulaiman bin Abu Dawud is weak. This hadith has been quoted by Zubaydi on the authority of Zuhari, which he has quoted on the authority of Masood bin Haqam, on the authority of a companion of the Prophet, peace be upon him."
2291,"Muhammad bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, \I attended the service of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in the month of Ramadan. He was about to set out on a journey. His horse was ready and he had put on his clothes for the journey. The sun was about to set. He ordered food and ate it. Then he mounted. I said to him: Is this Sunnah?\"" He said: Yes!"""
2292,"Narrated Amro bin Amir, may Allah be pleased with him: I heard Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say: Sayyidna Abu Musa said to me: I have been told that when you leave (on a journey), you leave fasting, and when you enter a city, you are in a state of fasting. (i) entered into a state without fasting."
2293,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Umrah in the month of Ramadan. The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not fast. I was fasting. My parents are sacrificed for you! You did not fast and I fasted. You offered a short prayer. I offered a full prayer. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Aisha! You have done well."
2294,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Umrah, 'I was with him,' the Prophet (PBUH) offered a short prayer, 'I offered the full prayer,' 'He did not fast and I fasted,' when I reached Makkah, I said, O Messenger of Allah! My parents are sacrificed for you! You offered a short prayer, I offered a complete prayer, you did not fast, I fasted, then the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said, Aisha! You have done well. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not object to me in this regard. A narrator named Abd al-Rahman has found the time of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, when she was near puberty, she was with her father at that time."
2295,"Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates that I went to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her. She had a gentleman with her. She said, O mother! What makes Ghusl obligatory? Tawseedah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the private parts are found, then Ghusl becomes obligatory."
2296,"Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates that my father used to send me to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her. I used to ask her when the year came in which I had a heart attack. Have you made this move? Then they pulled down the curtain between me and themselves."
2297,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed all of these actions, he performed both full and short prayers, he fasted and did not fast during the journey, and the narrator of this hadith is weak."
2298,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray both short and full prayers while traveling.
2299,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in full while traveling, and sometimes he would offer short prayers. The narrator of this narration is not authentic."
2300,Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) both fasting and not fasting during the journey.
2301,"Sayyidna Hamza bin Umar Wasalmi (RA) narrates that he said, O Messenger of Allah! I find the strength to fast during the journey. Will there be any sin on me (if I fast)? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is a leave from Allah, whoever accepts it, he will do good.” And whoever wants to fast, there is no sin on him. The chain of transmission of this tradition is authentic. He narrated it from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) with reference to her father. Sayyidna Hamza bin Amro asked that there is a possibility that both these traditions are correct. Allah knows best."
2302,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) traveled in the month of Ramadan and he fasted. Once he traveled in the month of Ramadan, he did not fast."
2303,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have become a victim of death, you discovered your potential! what happened He said, \I have intercourse with my wife during the day in Ramadan.\"" The narrator narrates that the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, said," \""Free a slave.\"" He said"," \""I do not have that.\"" Then a sack of dates came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which contained fifteen saa of dates. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Give it as charity to the poor.\"" He asked"," \""Should I give charity to people poorer than my own house?\"" There is no one more needy than my family between the two sides of Madinah Munawarah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled until his wisdom teeth were visible. Seek forgiveness from Allah and feed this to your family. Its chain of transmission is authentic."""
2304,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace. A sack was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there were 15 saa of dates. And feed sixty poor people on your behalf."
2305,"The same hadith is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) on the authority of the Prophet (PBUH), but it contains these words: A sack was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), which contained fifteen sa’a of dates. In this tradition, the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Eat it and let your family eat it.” Fast for one day and seek forgiveness from Allah."
2306,Mujahid narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the person who broke his fast during the day in the month of Ramadan to pay Zaharka Kaffarah.
2307,"Along with another hadith, this has been narrated from Mujahid as a messenger, and in one hadith regarding Mujahid, it has been narrated from Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) the narrator of this hadith is not authentic."
2308,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person ate (i.e. broke his fast) in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to free a slave or to fast for two months or to feed sixty poor people."
2309,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (PBUH), he (PBUH) said, “Whoever breaks his fast for one day in the month of Ramadan while he is present, then he should sacrifice an animal."
2310,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever breaks one fast of Ramadan (or does not keep it) without an excuse, then he must fast for thirty days, and whoever breaks two fasts, he must fast sixty, and whoever breaks three fasts, he must fast ninety."
2311,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever does not fast for one day of Ramadan without any excuse," he will be required to fast for a month. The narrator of this hadith is weak.\"""""
2312,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that after half of Sha’ban has passed, one should not fast until Ramadan comes."
2313,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) “Whoever is required to fast in Ramadan, he should continue it and keep the fast (and not leave it in between)."
2314,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has given this advice about the Qadaa of Ramadan: \A person should continue it and do not make any difference in it.\"""""
2315,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated that this verse was revealed, \so it will be counted in other consecutive days"," after which the word \""consecutive\"" was omitted."""
2316,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that this verse was revealed, \So it will be counted in other days which will be tarohogi\"" then after that the word \""Lagatar\"" was dropped."""
2317,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about making up for Ramadan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “He will make up the fast of this fast, if he makes a difference in the middle, it will be permissible for him to do so.”"
2318,"Abu Aamir Huzni narrates that I cursed Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he was asked about the Qada of Ramadan. He said, \Surely Allah has not given you this leave. You do not fast"," nor does He want you to suffer hardship in regard to its Qada.\"""""
2319,"Abu Amir Hozni narrates that I cursed Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about performing Ramadan separately, so he said, count the number and fast as you wish."
2320,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) has narrated this about the Qadaa of Ramadan (he says): Take it as you wish.
2321,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) have said that there is no problem in keeping the Qada of Ramadan differently.
2322,Sayyidna Rafi Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) says that you should keep count and fast as you wish.
2323,Abdullah bin Abu Malikah narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) does not see any problem in making up the Qada of Ramadan regularly.
2324,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that according to him, there is no problem in performing the qada of Ramadan separately."
2325,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) say that you can keep them separately and complete the number.
2326,"Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the qaza of Ramadan, so he said, \You count the count and fast as much as you want.\"""""
2327,"Sayyiduna Mu'azbin Jabal (RA) says, \You can make a difference in the Qadaa of Ramadan"," but count the count."""
2328,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) says, \You should keep count and do it whenever you want (i.e. do Qadaa)."""
2329,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this about the Qadaa of Ramadan: If a person wants, he can keep it separately, and if he wants, he can keep it continuously."
2330,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Harah Ubaid bin Umayr in another chain of transmission.
2331,"/ 1 The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, with reference to Harah Ata of another chain of transmission."
2332,"Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) says that you can keep the Qadaa of Ramadan separately, because Allah has said this, then it will be counted in other days."
2333,"Muhammad bin Munkadar narrates that I have come to know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about keeping the fasts of Ramadan separate. He said, \It is your will. What do you think?\"" Apart from Abu Bakr", other narrators have narrated it as a received tradition, however, they have narrated it on the authority of Musa bin Uqbah," on the authority of Abu Zubair on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir (RA) and this tradition is also not confirmed."""
2334,"Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about keeping the fasts of Ramadan separately. He said, \What do you think? If a person owes a debt and pays it in dirhams", even if he pays it all in the same way," will it be necessary for him to pay the debt or will he be considered as a blasphemer?\"" The people said yes! Ya Rasulullah! This hadith is narrated on the authority of Abu Zubair on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
2335,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \If a person dies and there are some fasts on him," then his wali fasts on his behalf is authentic\""."""
2336,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever dies and some fasts are due to him," his guardian (heir) should fast on his behalf.\"""""
2337,This tradition along with some other isnads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA).
2338,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “My sister has passed away.” The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, “If she had a debt, would you have paid it?” He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \So Allah is more entitled to this (that his right be paid)."""
2339,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words. This woman had submitted that she (the deceased) was required to fast for two consecutive months, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Allah's debt (has the right\"" to be paid)."""
2340,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and said, 'My mother has passed away and she was required to fast for a month.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your mother had a debt, would you have paid it on her behalf? He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The debt of Allah", the Exalted," is more entitled to be paid.\"""""
2341,"Yunus narrates Saeed bin Zayd (the narrator named Anbsa narrated this, he is the brother of Yunus) asked Nafi, who is the slave of Abdullah bin Umar, about a person who falls ill and his illness lasts for a long time. If he is unable to fast in the month of Ramadan, if he gives a piece of wheat to a poor person in exchange for each fast, then it will not be necessary for him to make up for it."
2342,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever is blessed with the time of Ramadan (and is able to fast for some reason) and is required to pay for a part of Ramadan (i.e. some of his fasts), then he should give a piece of wheat to a poor person for each fast."
2343,"Ata narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu said about a person who fell ill in Ramadan and later recovered, “He did not fast (in the first part) until he got the opportunity to fast in the last part. And when he is done with it, then he will fast the day that he neglected to do so."
2344,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says about the person who neglects to make up Ramadan until he reaches the last part of Ramadan. He says that person will fast with the people and then he will also fast on the day he neglected and he will feed a poor person for each day.
2345,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about a person who cannot fast in the month of Ramadan due to illness, then he recovers and does not fast until the next Ramadan comes. He did not keep and in exchange for each day he will feed one resident."
2346,"Ata narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) saying: He says about a person who falls ill in the month of Ramadan and does not fast, then he recovers, or a person who fasts until he is blessed with the next Ramadan. Will feed. His tradition is authentic."
2347,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that whoever neglects the fasts of Ramadan until the next Ramadan comes, then that person will fast that Ramadan."
2348,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a person is not healthy in the middle of Ramadan, he will fast the current Ramadan (i.e. fasts to make up for it) and eat food from the previous Ramadan, and it will not be necessary for him to make up (for the fasts of the previous Ramadan), but whoever is healthy and does not fast until the next Ramadan comes, he will fast the current Ramadan. will feed him and when his fasts of this month are over, then he will make up for the fasts of the previous Ramadan."
2349,"Ziyad bin Jabir narrates, I remember a person came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and asked him a question, and that person said: He had vowed that he would fast every Wednesday. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said, \Allah has ordered the fulfillment of the vow and the Prophet (PBUH) has forbidden us to fast on the day of sacrifice. This is an authentic document.\"""""
2350,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we have kept twenty-nine fasts more than the number of thirty times we kept with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e., in his holy time) (ie, the month of Ramadan is sometimes twenty-nine days long)."
2351,"This is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her: She was asked, O Mother of the Believers! Can the month of Ramadan be twenty-nine days? He replied, \I have fasted twenty-nine times more than I have fasted thirty times with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (i.e. in his time of the Holy Prophet)\"". Its chain of transmission is authentic and the tradition before it is not proven"," because its narrator is Abd al-Ala bin Abul Mus and is obsolete."""
2352,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that we have fasted thirty times with the Holy Prophet (SAW) more than twenty-nine fasts.
2353,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) Sayyidna Umar (RA) made a vow during the Jahiliyyah era that he would perform one-night Itikaaf in Masjid Haram.
2354,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, made a vow during the time of Jahiliyya that he would perform one night of I’tikaf in Masjid al-Haram."
2355,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Fasting is not obligatory on a person who performs I'tikaaf. However, if he makes it obligatory on himself (also to fast), the ruling (will be different). The Sheikh has narrated this hadith as a valid hadith," while other narrators have not transmitted it as a valid hadith."""
2356,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \I'tikaaf is valid only with fasting.\"" Swedish narrators are unique in quoting this."""
2357,"Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, \Every mosque in which there is a muezzin and an imam can perform I'tikaf.\"" The narrator of this tradition", Zahaq," has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Huzaifah."""
2358,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs itikaaf can attend the Friday prayer, attend a funeral and visit the sick."
2359,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who does itikaaf can visit the sick, attend a funeral, go for Friday, go to his home (but cannot stay with them for long)."
2360,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) narrates this about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) He asked the Prophet (PBUH) about I'tikaf, it was obligatory for a young man, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to perform I'tikaf and also fast."
2361,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) has narrated this saying, 'Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to the Prophet (PBUH) that I had made a vow that I would perform I'tikaf for one day,' then the Prophet (PBUH) said, 'You should perform I'tikaf and fast as well.' I have heard Shaykh Abu Bakr Nishapuri saying, “He says that this hadeeth has been rejected because the authentic disciples of Amro bin Dinar did not narrate it, including Ibn Jarij, Ibn Uyaynah, Hamad bin Salamah, Hamad bin Zayd and others, while its narrator Ibn Badil is weak.”"
2362,Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates; The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I'tikaf in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan.
2363,"Urwa bin Zubair and Saeed bin Musaib narrated this. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) told them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I’tikaaf in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan until Allah passed away. He will not participate in the funeral, he will not go to visit the sick, he will not touch a woman and he will not have intercourse with her, and I'tikaf can only be in the mosque where congregational prayers are held, and the person who performs I'tikaf will be ordered to fast. Narrator) is the word of Zuhri, who has recorded it in the hadith, due to which this illusion has occurred, Allah knows best, but the narrator Hisham bin Sulaiman has not mentioned it"
2364,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform I’tikaaf in the last ten days of Ramadan until Allah passed away. I'tikaaf will only be in the place where congregational prayers are offered, and the Sunnah for the person performing I'tikaf is to fast."
2365,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Umar, may God be pleased with him, had vowed during the time of polytheism that he would do itikaf and fast. After he accepted Islam, he reported to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \You fulfill your vow"," its chain of transmission is good.\"" The narrator named Saeed bin Basheer is unique in quoting it in these words."""
2366,"Abu Ishaq Khwarazmi narrates: I asked Asim Ahol, can a fasting person perform maswak? He answered yes! I discovered that both wet and dry maswak can be used. He answered yes! I have a question, can I do both in the beginning, the end or the end of the day? He answered yes! I inquired from whom is this said? So he replied that it was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the narrator of this tradition, Abu Ishaq Khwarazmi, is weak."
2367,Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi narrates this on the authority of his father: I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rubbing his mouth while fasting. Other narrators are more authentic than Asim bin Ubaidullah.
2368,Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi narrates on the authority of his parents: I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing maswak while fasting.
2369,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
2370,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that you are allowed to brush your teeth until Asr prayer, when you pray Asr, then put it aside."
2371,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \The best thing for a fasting person is to brush his teeth.\"" In one hadith"," these words are \""One of the best things for a fasting person to do is to brush his teeth.\"""""
2372,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when you fast, brush your teeth in the morning and don't brush your teeth in the evening. The reason for this is that the lips of a fasting person will be dry in the evening."
2373,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Khabab (RA) along with another chain of transmission. A narrator named Abu Umar Kaisan is not authentic and there are no narrators known between him and Sayyiduna Ali.
2374,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when an old person is unable to fast, then he should take one medicine for each fast."
2375,"Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA) narrates that in the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), we broke the fast one day in the month of Ramadan when it was overcast, but later the sun came out (it turned out that it was not time to break the fast). So he replied that it was necessary to do so. Its certificate is valid and proven."
2376,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2377,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has said this about the saying of Allah, \And for those who do not have the power", their ransom is to feed a poor person. He means a poor person. Allah says," \""Let the one who does good be generous. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if he feeds another poor person", if it remains too much, he says that this order is not abrogated, but this leave has been given to the old man who cannot afford to fast," and this order to feed is for the person who knows that he will no longer have the strength to fast."""
2378,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (God is the guide) the redemption of those who have the power is to feed a poor person. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says that those who do not have the power to do so, they are bound to feed one poor person, and whoever wants to do good in the afterlife, should feed one more poor person. So it is better if in this case the leave is given only to the old man who does not have the strength to fast and it is given to the sick person who knows that he will never be cured again, his certificate is correct."
2379,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says (may Allah guide him) that the ransom for those who do not have the strength to do so is to feed a poor person (may Allah guide him) “Whoever should do good after his death” means that he should feed one more poor person (may Allah guide him) “then it will be better for him. There is more for you. (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that this leave is given only to the old man who does not have the strength to fast, and to the sick person who knows that he will not be cured."
2380,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this leave is for the old man, he should stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day, and no qaza will be required for him. His certificate is correct."
2381,Ata narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) reciting this: \And those who do not have the strength to do so," their ransom is to feed the poor.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that this order is not abrogated. It means an old man or a woman. The answer is that they will never be able to fast. So they should feed one poor person for each day. This tradition is correct."""
2382,"Saeed bin Jabirbayan says that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said to his mother, who was pregnant and was nursing a child, (she said:) You are among those people who do not have the strength to fast."
2383,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that a tuberculosis patient who is disappointed that he will be cured and will never be able to fast, such a person will not fast and will feed one poor person for every day."
2384,"Saeed bin Jubeer narrated this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him. He had a maidservant who was nursing a child. She fell ill, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, instructed her that you should not fast, and give food (as fidya) and keep qazana. This hadith is authentic."
2385,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) or perhaps Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has said that a pregnant woman who breastfeeds will not fast, and she will not make up for it later (rather, she will feed the poor). This tradition and the following tradition are authentic."
2386,"According to Mujahidbayan, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, recited this verse: \For those who do not have the strength"," it is obligatory to feed a poor person as a ransom.\"" Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas", may Allah be pleased with him," says that this means an old man who cannot afford to fast."""
2387,"Ikramah narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to recite this verse, \And those who do not have the power to do it"," it is obligatory on them.\"" Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say that this verse was abrogated."""
2388,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that his wife asked him, \She was pregnant.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar", may Allah be pleased with him, said," \""You should stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day.\"""""
2389,"Narrated by Nafi, a daughter of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with her, she was the wife of a Qureshi, when she became pregnant, she felt very thirsty, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with her, instructed her to stop fasting and feed a poor person for one day."
2390,Ayyub narrates that one year Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) could not fast due to his weakness.
2391,"Qatadah narrates that Sayyiduna Anas (may God be pleased with him) became weak before his death, so he did not fast, he instructed his wife to feed one poor person for every day."
2392,"Mujahid narrates: I heard Qays ibn Sa'ib narrating that the ransom of the month of Ramadan will be given by a man who feeds one poor person for every day, so feed two poor people on my behalf."
2393,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says, \If a person becomes old and is unable to fast"," then it is obligatory on him to pay a full amount of wheat for each day.\"""""
2394,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “If a person owes a debt, if it is paid by him, then it is paid by him.” The Prophet (PBUH) said similar things about Hajj and fasting."
2395,"Muhammad bin Hasan, regarding his father (Hasan), his father (Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God bless him and grant him peace), his grandfather (Imam Hussain, may God bless him and grant him peace), narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib, may God bless him and grant him peace, a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said, O Messenger of God! I have become a victim of death. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked what has caused you to become a victim of death. He said, \I have had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired"," \""Do you have any slaves or concubines?\"" He did not answer this request! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed that he should be given fifteen sa’s. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said", “You feed these sixty poor people.” He said," “By the One who has sent you with the truth! Has been paid."""
2396,"Amir bin Saad narrates the statement of his father (Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
2397,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates, A person broke his fast in the month of Ramadan, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to free a slave as an atonement, or to fast for two months, or to feed sixty poor people. Give charity, he said, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know of anyone who needs it more than me, then the Prophet smiled until his side teeth were visible, then he said, \Eat it.\"" Some narrators have narrated in this tradition that this person had broken the fast of Ramadan and he was given the option to make expiation (to choose one of the above three cases)", but most of the narrators have narrated that this person had broken his fast by having intercourse, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) first ordered him to expiate by freeing a slave. When he could not afford it," he ordered him to feed sixty poor people."""
2398,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have perished (perhaps these are the words) I have perished (myself). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast for two consecutive months. Feed it to your family.
2399,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) gave this instruction to a person who breaks the fast in Ramadan (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith), but these words are superfluous in the names, you should eat it and fast for one day."
2400,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “I have had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan (fasting). I can't even do that. The narrator narrates, a basket of fifteen Sa'a dates was brought to the Prophet, and he said, \Take it and feed it yourself.\"" He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," we need it the most in the whole city.\"" These words are from a narrator named Bakr and narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Abu Hafsa."""
2401,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: A sack was brought and there was a measure in which there were fifteen sa's, 'It is also', there were fifteen sa's of dates."
2402,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was told that he had intercourse with his wife during Ramadan (while fasting). I do not have that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast for two consecutive months. He said: I cannot afford it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Feed sixty poor people. He said, \Are you more needy than yourself and your family?\"" He said"," \""I have no one more needy than myself and my family.\"""""
2403,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: “Whoever does not fast one month of Ramadan, he will be required to fast for a month, his chain of transmission is not proven."
2404,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever does not fast one day of Ramadan without any illness or leave, even fasting forever will not be a reward for him."
2405,"Rabi'ah bin Abdul Rahman says that whoever does not fast one day of Ramadan, he will fast for twelve days. This is because Allah has preferred fasting one month to twelve months."
2406,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has said that if a person does not fast in Ramadan without leave or illness, even fasting all the time will not make up for him."
2407,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Hudhafa Sahmi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on my camel in the days of Mina to announce, O people, these are the days of eating, drinking and companionship. The narrator of this tradition is weak."
2408,"Sayyidna Hamza Aslami narrates: He saw a man who was going to the residences of the people during the days of Tashriq in Mina, he was riding a camel and he was saying: Be careful not to fast during these days because these are the days of eating and drinking and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is among you. Not done."
2409,"Qatadah narrates the statement of Anas, the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade fasting on five days of the year, the day of Eid al-Fitr, the day of Eid al-Adha and the three days of the days of Tashreeq. A narrator named Uthman narrates, We have narrated the same hadith regarding Muhammad bin Khalid."
2410,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed Sayyidna Umar bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him) about Sadaqah al-Fitr, that it should be half a saa of wheat or one saa of dates."
2411,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when there is milk in the udder, do it with milk, and when there is no wool (on the animal's back), then do it with milk."
2412,"Masoud bin Haqm Zarqi' narrates this with reference to one of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hudhafa, may God be pleased with him, announced this during the days of Tashreeq, under the command of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace! These are the days of Eid, these are the days of eating, drinking and remembering, so only a person who is a pilgrim or a pilgrim who does not have a sacrificial animal with him, or who has not fasted continuously during the days of Hajj should fast on these days."
2413,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates when this verse was revealed, \And it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah"," and it is obligatory upon the person who has the power to reach it.\"" So a person stood up", he said," O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by \""sibyl\"" here? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ``Zad travel and ride.''"""
2414,"Amro bin Shoaib quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, in reference to his father, \In reference to his grandfather"," \""The way to reach the house of Allah is the journey of Adsafar Adar."""
2415,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! What makes Hajj obligatory? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zadrah and ride (to be available)."
2416,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Zad Safar and Sawari\""."""
2417,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) (Allah the Exalted said) \It is obligatory upon people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah," whoever has the means to reach it.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I said"," O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Zad Safar and Sawari\""."""
2418,"This same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Anas, along with another chain of transmission."
2419,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him).
2420,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa.
2421,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (SAW) was asked about the saying of Allah, “And the Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah is obligatory on those who have a way to reach it.” The sages have discovered who is more virtuous? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \In which the Talbiyyah is recited aloud"," the blood of the sacrificial animal has been shed.\"""""
2422,This same tradition and chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the route to Hajj.
2423,"Muhammad bin Ubad narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, came to us and told us that a person said, O Messenger of God! What is meant by Hajj? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
2424,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission with reference to Sayyidna Hasan al-Basri. \And for the sake of Allah, it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah," whoever has the means to reach it.\"" The people said"," O Messenger of Allah! What does sable mean? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."""
2425,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah! Is performing Hajj every year (obligatory?) The Prophet (PBUH) said no! Rather, a Hajj (obligatory) is offered, what is meant by the way up to it? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
2426,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah! Means how to reach it? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaad Safar and Sawari (to be available)."
2427,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has quoted the saying of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) 'Sabil means to be able to travel and ride.
2428,"Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, narrates from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, that, “By Allah, the Hajj of the House is the right of Allah upon the people, that whoever is able to reach his house, should perform the Hajj.” He was asked about this verse. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \It means that you have the back of the ride.\"""""
2429,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Sayyida Zubayah (may Allah be pleased with her) who was ill. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then make up your mind for Hajj and make a condition with it and say: O Allah! Where I am not able to go further"," I will give Ihram Kol."""
2430,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) visited Sayyida Zaba’ah bint Zubair (RA) and he said, “O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, when putting on Ihram, make a condition that where I am not able to go further, I will open Ihram, then you will have the right to do so."
2431,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyid al-Zabaa'ah that you intend to perform Hajj and make a condition that I will open Ihram where I am no longer able to go further.
2432,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) took a bath, then he put on his clothes, then when he came to Dhul-Halifa, he offered two rak'ahs there, then he sat on his camel, when his ride stopped, from there he put on the Ihram for Hajj (i.e., he intended to do it)."
2433,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that this is a Sunnah: When a person begins to put on Ihram, he should perform ghusl when he begins to enter Makkah (he should also perform ghusl at that time)."
2434,"Al-Khahir ibn Zayd narrated this on the authority of his father (Zayd ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him) that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took a ghusl before putting on Ihram. Ibn Sa’id states that this hadith is weak."
2435,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2436,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) took a ghusl at the place of \Fasq\"" before entering Makkah."""
2437,"Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhaifa narrates that a gentleman has narrated this. I used to ask people about the hadith of Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim (RA) 'He was by my side', but I did not ask him if I then came to him. When I came to serve him, he said to me, ``Adi bin Hatim! Accept Islam and you will be safe. After that, he mentioned the entire hadith, which contains these words: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to me, “Soon a woman will depart from “Hira” (a place called) and she will circumambulate the House of Allah without being sheltered by anyone."
2438,"Sayyidna Adi bin Hatim (RA) came and stayed with the Holy Prophet (SAW) and the Prophet (SAW) said to him, “Soon a time will come when a woman will leave Hira (a place called) without seeking the shelter of a person until she performs Hajj to the House of Allah, and a time will soon come when the wealth will be so much that a man will wish to find someone to receive this charity. Anhu narrates: I saw a woman who left without seeking shelter from anyone, until she performed Hajj to the House of Allah. This tradition is short."
2439,"Muhammad bin Huzaifah narrates that we used to recite the hadith of Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim (RA) to each other. He used to live in a village on the outskirts of Kufa. I thought that it would be appropriate if I went to him and heard this hadith from him. So I attended his service. ``Adi said, \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent", I escaped and went to a distant part of the Islamic kingdom. Then I thought that I should be present in his service. If he is truthful, I will accept his word. When I (in his service) the Ayatullah stood for me. The narrator narrates (after that he narrated to me the entire hadith in which this statement is made) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, “Have you gone to Hira? I did not submit! But I know its place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""The time will soon come when a woman will leave there without taking shelter from anyone.\"" Sayyiduna Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Then I saw a woman who set out from Hira and circumambulated the House of Kaaba (arrived at Makkah). This tradition is short."""
2440,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to Madinah, 'The Prophet (PBUH) opened the gate, where are you staying? He said to such and such a woman, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Has he closed the door of your children? A woman should perform Hajj only when there is a dear Muharram with her.\"""""
2441,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated this saying about the Prophet (PBUH): “The Prophet (PBUH) did not allow a woman to perform Hajj whose husband was present, even though she had wealth."
2442,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying, \No woman should travel for three days or go for Hajj unless her husband is with her.\"""""
2443,"Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The day of 'Arafah is the day in which people recognize each other.\"""""
2444,"Ya'qub bin Zayd quoted the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: \Arafah is the day in which people recognize each other.\"""""
2445,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that your Eid-ul-Fitr day is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr and the day of Eid-ul-Adha is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Adha.
2446,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \The day of your Eid-ul-Fitr is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Fitr," and the day of Eid-ul-Adha is when you celebrate Eid-ul-Adha.\"""""
2447,Muhammad bin Mankader has quoted on the authority of Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a narrator named Abu Hisham narrates this.
2448,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the words \I am here\"" were included in the Talbiyah of the Holy Prophet (SAW)."""
2449,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I took the words of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastily while he was reciting them. \O Allah! I am present! O Allah! I am present! I am present! You have no partner, I am present! Verily, all praise and praise is reserved for You," and the kingdom also has no partner.\"""""
2450,"This same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, in which these words of his are mentioned. The talbiya of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, 'After that, he has narrated as per the previous hadith' in which these words have been quoted additionally. The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) was repeating these words."
2451,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to put on Ihram, he used to wash his holy head with khatmi and ashnan and apply olive oil on it. This happened many times."
2452,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the months of Hajj are Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'dah and the first ten days of Dhul-Hijj."
2453,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the months of Hajj are Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'd and Dhul-Hijj."
2454,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zubair (RA) narrates that the month of Hajj is Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa’da and the first ten days of Dhu Hajj."
2455,"Abu Shaykh narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) about the months of Hajj, and he replied that Shawwal is the ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and Dhul-Hijj."
2456,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says, \The months of Hajj are fixed.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this Shawwal is the ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and Dhul-Hijj."""
2457,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him).
2458,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him).
2459,"Abdul Aziz bin Rabi narrates this from his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon in the middle of the days of Tashriq (the narrator narrates), this means on the day of the first departure."
2460,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates about the saying of Allah (Glory be to the Almighty) “So whoever makes Hajj obligatory among them” Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says, what this means is that he should make the intention of Ihram."
2461,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) says that making Hajj obligatory means putting on Ihram.
2462,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that making Hajj obligatory means putting on Ihram (i.e. intending to do it).
2463,"Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) said to me, “Soon a woman will depart from Hira until she circumambulates this house and she will fear only Allah (there will be no fear of anyone else besides Him).”"
2464,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) while giving a sermon in Arafat saying, \Whoever does not have shoes should wear socks and whoever does not have an apron should wear trousers.\"""""
2465,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2466,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this about Muharram. \When he does not have shoes, he should wear socks and when he does not have an apron," he should wear shalwar.\"""""
2467,"Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \He who does not have shoes should wear socks", and if he does not have an apron," he should wear shalwar.\"""""
2468,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person who cannot find shoes should wear socks and a person who cannot find an apron should wear shalwar.
2469,Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \He who does not find shoes should wear socks," but cut them below the ankles.\"" A narrator named Abbas narrates that if Muharram does not find shoes", he should wear socks," but he should cut them both in such a way that they reach below both ankles."""
2470,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying while delivering a sermon, \Whoever does not have shoes should wear socks and whoever does not have an apron should wear pants.\"""""
2471,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \Whoever does not have an apron should wear shalwar", and whoever does not have shoes," should wear socks.\"" (Imam Darqutni", may God have mercy on him) narrates that this refers to Madinah before wearing Ihram. While other narrators have narrated the hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, it mentions that, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Prophet saying that while giving a sermon, so this hadith will be after the hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar," may Allah be pleased with him."""
2472,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) \Whoever does not get shoes, he should wear socks," but he should cut them from the bottom up to the ankles.\"""""
2473,"Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): A person asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, what clothes should a person in the state of Ihram wear? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not wear a shirt, he will not wear a turban, he will not wear shalwar, he will not wear a hat, and he will not wear a cloth that has varus or saffron on it, he will not wear socks. A narrator named Yusuf has quoted these words: \Cut the ants so that they reach below the ankles.\"""""
2474,"Safwan bin Ya'ila narrates this statement of his father: I wanted to see the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such a state that he was receiving revelation. Once when we were in Jarana and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also there. A person came who was wearing a Jabba and tied the Ihram of Umrah and he also applied perfume. He said, O Messenger of Allah! You say about such a person who has made the intention of Haram in his life. At the same time, the revelation began to be revealed to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he started snoring. After that, this state of his ended. So you inquired where is the person who had just asked me a question? This person was brought. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “As for the modesty, take it off, and as for the fragrance, wash it and put on Ihram again.” Abu Abd al-Rahman (Imam al-Nasa'i, may God have mercy on him) narrated this. To the best of my knowledge, no one has narrated this saying, 'The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed this person to put on Ihram again."
2475,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \A person in the state of Ihram can kill rats", scorpions, mad dogs," and crows.\"""""
2476,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a person in the state of Ihram can kill a wolf, a crow, an eagle, and a mouse."
2477,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar.
2478,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing a shirt and wearing socks (in the state of Ihram).
2479,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) who said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to smell the best perfume while putting on Ihram.
2480,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person in the state of Ihram can smell a basil (scented) flower, he can enter the bath, he can pull out a tooth, he can tear open an abscess, and when his nail breaks, he can remove the pain from you."
2481,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that there is no harm in using a belt and a ring for a person in the state of Ihram.
2482,It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that a person in the state of Ihram is allowed to wear a ring and tie a waist belt.
2483,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) states that there is no problem in wearing a ring for a person in the state of Ihram.
2484,"This same hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, it does not mention that it was transmitted from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas."
2485,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we used to travel with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to say Takbeer when he walked on high ground, and when he descended to low ground, he used to say Subhan Allah."
2486,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this, and the Sunnah of Hajj includes this: \A man who performs Hajj in the month of Ihram has been followed by some other narrators.\"" His narrator is Abul Qasim"," who is the imam of Abdullah bin Harith's Azad."""
2487,It is narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said this about a person who puts on the Ihram for Hajj before the months of Hajj. He said that this is not a Sunnah.
2488,Abu Zubayr narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) whether it is permissible to wear Ihram before the beginning of the month of Hajj. He answered no!
2489,"Ata narrates that Allah Ta'ala has said this: \The months of Hajj are fixed\"" and the reason for this is that a person should not wear the Ihram of Hajj before that."""
2490,"Salim narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to refuse to set conditions for Hajj and said, \Isn't the Sunnah of your Prophet sufficient for you?\"""""
2491,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission. However, it contains these words (he said) The Sunnah of your Prophet is sufficient. He did not set any conditions."
2492,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) went to Sayyida Zaba’ah Bint Zubair (RA) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj, but I am sick. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Make up your mind and make a condition that I will open Ihram where I am not able to go further.\"""""
2493,"Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma Sayyidah Dabba'ah Bint Zubayr Radiyallahu Anhu came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Put on Ihram and make it a condition that I will open Ihram where I am not able to go further.\"" The narrator says that he had performed Hajj."""
2494,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2495,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2496,Sayyid Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed the Zubayah (to wear Ihram).
2497,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Zaat-e-Irq as a miqat for the people of Iraq.
2498,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2499,Amro bin Shuaib narrates on the authority of his father and grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Zaat-i-Irq as the Miqat for the people of Iraq.
2500,The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission in which these words are said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the entire hadith and said: It is) appointed Zaat-e-Irq as Miqat for the people of Iraq.
2501,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet appointed Dhul-Halifa for the people of Madinah, Yallam for the people of Yemen, Hajfah for the people of Egypt, and Zaat-Irq for the people of Iraq."
2502,"Sayyiduna Harith bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was in Mina at that time (after that he mentioned the entire hadith in which he stated that) he appointed Yallam as a miqat for the people of Yemen, that they would put on Ihram from there, and Zaat-Irq (assigned a miqat) for the people of Iraq."
2503,"Abu Zubair narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) and inquired from him about putting on Ihram, and he narrated this with reference to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The place for the people of Madinah to put on Ihram is Dhul-Halifa, while the other way is Hajfah."
2504,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, it has been narrated as a hadith that the Prophet appointed Dhu’l-Halifa for the people of Medina, Hajfah for the people of Syria, Qarn for the people of Najd (the word Qarn Al-Mazil) for the people of Yemen, and Yalmalum for the people of Yemen. (There are these words in one tradition) He will put on Ihram from his house, (And in one tradition there are these words) He will put on Ihram from wherever he wants. Even the people of Makkah will put on Ihram in Makkah."
2505,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2506,Khalid Ibn Sa'ib narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel came to me and he said to me: I should instruct my companions to recite Talbiyyah in a loud voice.
2507,"Amara bin Khuzamah narrates this statement of his father: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished reciting Talbiyah, he prayed to Allah for His forgiveness and approval and sought refuge in His mercy from Hell."
2508,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj.
2509,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that we had put on Ihram for the Hajj people with the Prophet (PBUH).
2510,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) first appointed Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may God be pleased with him) as Ameer al-Hajj, so he performed the Hajj, then in 9 Hijra he appointed Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) as Ameer al-Hajj, and he also performed the Hajj in 10 Hijri. Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also performed Hajj in person, then he also performed Hajj in person, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) passed away, then Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) became the caliph. Umar (RA) passed away and Sayyidna Uthman (RA) became the caliph, so he also performed Hajj."
2511,Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates this statement of his father: I performed Hajj with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) He performed Hajj I performed Hajj with Sayyidna Umar (RA) He performed Hajj I performed Hajj with Sayyidna Uthman (RA) He performed Hajj.
2512,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make his back in a state of haraam.
2513,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was walking between Makkah and Madinah (i.e. during the journey) 'The Prophet (PBUH) was both fasting and in the state of Ihram at that time.
2514,"Narrated by Sayyidna Urwah bin Mudhars (RA) I came to the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and asked him what had happened while he was staying in Muzdalifah. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah! I am present at your service from the two mountains of Behar. I have tired my rider and I have also tired myself. By Allah! I have camped near every mountain, then my Hajj will be done, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever performed the morning prayer with us in Muzdalifah and who reached Arafat before that at night or during the day, he has fulfilled his vow and his Hajj is complete."
2515,"Sayyidna Urwa bin Mudras (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and he was in Muzdalifah at that time.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Did I have Hajj? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever performs this prayer with us and stays with us until we leave, or whoever leaves Arafat at night or before it during the day, his Hajj will be completed and he has fulfilled his vow."
2516,Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Yamar Deli narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He was encamped in Arafa at that time. What is Hajj? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Hajj Arafa (the name of the person standing) is one who reaches Arafa before dawn on the day of sacrifice.
2517,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2518,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said, “Whoever stands at Arafat during the night, he has performed Hajj, and whoever does not stand at Arafat during the night, his Hajj will be completed, so he wears Ihram for Umrah, and it will be necessary for him to perform Hajj the next year.” The narrator named Rahmat bin Musab is weak."
2519,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said that whoever reaches Arafat and stops there and also reaches Muzdalifah, his Hajj will be completed, and whoever cannot reach Arafat, he cannot perform Hajj, he should put on Ihram for Umrah."
2520,Ibrahim Taymi quotes this statement of Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) regarding his father. By Allah! The order of Hajj Tamattu was reserved only for us or for the person who was besieged.
2521,"Harith bin Bilal narrates this statement of his father: I said, O Messenger of Allah! The order to cancel Hajj is only for us or for those after us? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! It is only for us."
2522,Ibrahim Taymi narrates that his father narrated this about Sayyiduna Abu'd Radiyallahu Anhu. It is reserved only for us i.e. the Companions of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It is not for the rest of the people.
2523,"Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) says that no one has the right to enjoy Hajj, he should only put on Ihram for Hajj and cancel it again through Umrah, except for those riders who were with the Prophet (PBUH)."
2524,Sayyiduna Abu Zar Ghaffari (RA) says that no one has the right to do this after us. He should first put on Ihram for Hajj and then cancel it and change it to Umrah before performing Hajj.
2525,Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) says that no one has the right to cancel Hajj by performing Umrah after putting on Ihram.
2526,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates about Sayyida Aisha, she came (for Hajj) with two sacrificial animals. Both of them were lost, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair, may Allah be pleased with them, sent two more animals to the service of Sayyida Aisha. He slaughtered them and said that this is the Sunnah about sacrificial animals."
2527,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: “Whoever takes a sacrificial animal and then loses it, it is not obligatory on him to replace it."
2528,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who sent a sacrificial animal and then that animal (lost or died), then if that person wants, he can replace it with another animal."
2529,Both Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharama (RA) and Marwan Bin Huqm (R.A.) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed seventy camels on behalf of seven hundred men at Hudaybiyyah.
2530,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that on the occasion of Eid al-Adha, one camel will be sacrificed by ten men."
2531,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, one of its narrators is Ayyub Abu Jamal Zaeef and only he has narrated this tradition regarding Ata."
2532,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has prescribed this Sunnah: Cows and camels will be sacrificed by seven men.
2533,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that we sacrificed seventy camels on the occasion of the Peace of Hudaybiyyah. One camel belonged to seven men. On that day, the Prophet (PBUH) said that a few people should sacrifice one animal together."
2534,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever forgets or abandons any of the rituals of Hajj, he will have to make a sacrifice."
2535,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2536,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if a person abandons any of his rituals, he will make a sacrifice."
2537,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Asim Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon in the mud on the middle of Eid al-Adha (says the narrator), that is, the day after the sacrifice."
2538,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that expiation is given on purpose.
2539,"Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
2540,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates: We asked Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) about the cave, and he said, \It is necessary to make a hole in it.\"" I asked"," \""Is this necessary?\"" He replied yes"," he said that it is necessary."""
2541,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “The wound is a victim (says the narrator) and the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) has prescribed the payment of expiation for the scaly in it."
2542,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates this about Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: He says, \I found out that it is possible to eat the goh?\"" He answered yes! I wonder if it is hunting? He answered yes! I inquired"," have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"""
2543,"Ibn Abu Ammar narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) about the cave. He answered yes! I asked: Can it be eaten? He said yes! I inquired, have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"
2544,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates that he inquired from Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) about Goh. He inquired whether it can be eaten. Sayyiduna Jabir answered yes! I wonder if it is hunting? You answered yes! I inquired, have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"
2545,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the cave, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \It is hunting.\"" (The narrator says) If a person in the state of Ihram kills him"," then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed the sacrifice of a drumstick."""
2546,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “If a person in the state of Ihram kills it, he must pay for it, and about the deer, he said: “A goat must be sacrificed. It is an animal that walks."
2547,It has been narrated about Sayyidna Jabir (R.A.) that he had given a decision to sacrifice a bullock in the hunting of a cave.
2548,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this ruling regarding the pigeon of the sanctuary: \The expiation for killing a pigeon in the sanctuary will be a goat; the expiation for damaging an egg will be one dirham; for killing an ostrich, a camel must be sacrificed; for killing a cow, a cow must be sacrificed; and for killing a cow," a cow must be sacrificed.\"""""
2549,Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had given this decision about the deer: 'A goat must be sacrificed'. He said that the child who has been weaned and can walk.
2550,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) gave this decision regarding an ostrich egg: \If a person in the state of Ihram harms it," he must pay a ransom according to its value.\"""""
2551,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, but there is some wording difference in it."
2552,"Muawiya bin Qura narrated this from an Ansari elder: A man was riding his horse in the state of Ihram, he came to an ostrich's nest and picked up an egg that fell from his hand, then Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (R.A.) decreed about him that he would buy the daughters of Mukhaz, give them to Jafti, then the children she would give birth to would be donated to the House of Allah, and Even if these camels did not give birth to a child, the expiation of that person will be paid, because sometimes a child comes out of an egg and sometimes a child does not come out. Yes, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, in exchange for each egg, one should feed a poor person or fast for one day (expiation)."
2553,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA).
2554,This tradition is narrated from an Ansari companion along with another chain of transmission.
2555,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated this about Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Once a man put an ostrich's nest under the feet of his camel. He came to the service of the Prophet and mentioned this to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, Ali has said what he had to say about this, but why do you not come to leave? You will be required to fast one day or eat one day for each one."
2556,"Mu'awiya bin Qura narrated that a man built an ostrich's nest under the feet of his camel. He asked Sayyidna Ali (RA) about it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, \In exchange for each egg"," you have to give one camel as a mate or pay for the baby in the camel's belly.\"" Anhu said to him: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have heard what he said. Why don't you come to leave? For one egg you have to fast for a day and feed a poor person."""
2557,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that in exchange for an ostrich egg, one should fast for one day or feed a poor person."
2558,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2559,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about an egg which was broken by a man in the state of Ihram (the decision of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that one day of fasting should be observed in exchange for one egg).
2560,"It was narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In the ransom of this egg of the camel; A narrator named Abu Khalid narrates that if a person in the state of Ihram breaks an ostrich egg, he will fast for one day."
2561,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision regarding an ostrich egg (this egg was broken by a person in the state of Ihram, that person will fast for one egg)."
2562,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It has been said about the egg, if a person in the state of Ihram breaks it, he will pay for it."
2563,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that once some people killed a caveman and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that all these people will be required to sacrifice one piece of meat, which they will perform together."
2564,"Narrator of Amarnami states that some slaves of Ibn Zubair were in the state of Ihram. \Once a woman passed by them. They killed her with sticks. Then they were confused about this. They came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and mentioned this to him. Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) said: \""You will be required to sacrifice a stick.\"" Will it be necessary? So Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""You are doing too much for yourselves. You will all have to sacrifice one piece of meat.\"" The lexicographers said: These words of the hadith are meant by lamazirbakum"," in this case you will abuse yourself."""
2565,"Sayyiduna Usama bin Sharik (RA) narrates, “I went to perform Hajj with the Holy Prophet (PBUH)” People came to serve him “Someone was saying this, O Messenger of Allah! I have tried before performing Tawaf, or I have postponed a thing, or I have taken one of the members first, then this is what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying, there is no harm, except for the person who harms the honor of a Muslim and he is a transgressor, this person will suffer embarrassment and will be killed."
2566,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “I have performed ablution before performing the sacrifice! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You take the sacrifice now. There is no problem. Another person said: I have done the sacrifice before hitting the pebbles!\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You now throw pebbles!\"" There is no problem."""
2567,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that on the day of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped on his horse. People started asking him questions. One of them said, O Messenger of Allah! I didn't know that 'pebbles must be thrown before the sacrifice'. I have already sacrificed before throwing the pebbles. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Now throw the pebbles"," there is no harm.\"" The other person said", O Messenger of Allah! I did not know that the sacrifice will be done before shaving the head. It was done before. The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him," \""Do it now. There is no problem.\"""""
2568,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2569,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates, “I remember this saying about the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ‘He (PBUH) was sitting on his camel in Mina. I used to think that 'one goes to the head before making the sacrifice, so I went to the head before the sacrifice.' The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'There is no harm in doing the sacrifice now. There is no harm in it.' I used to think that ``one should clean one's head before throwing pebbles'', so I cleaned one's head before throwing pebbles.'' The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it these words are added: \Departed before hitting the pebbles.\"" This narrator has not been followed in these words and I think the narrator is delusional in quoting these words."""
2570,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I cursed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice, a person attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was staying near Jamrah. I have shaved my head before throwing pebbles. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now throw the pebbles, there is no harm.” Then another person came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him. He said, “I have sacrificed before throwing the pebbles.” \I have performed Tawaf before throwing pebbles.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You now throw pebbles. There is no harm.\"" The narrator narrates that on that day", I saw you and said that whatever question was asked of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that you should do it now," there is no harm."""
2571,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who slaughtered his head with his head before stoning, or sacrificed, or was asked about doing something similar first or later."
2572,"Ata and other narrators have narrated these three things regarding the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: About a person who shaved his head before throwing pebbles. Sacrifice was done. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now throw pebbles. Sacrifice is part of throwing pebbles and throwing pebbles is like making a sacrifice.” The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads, but in them are these words: \Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to us on the day of sacrifice.\"" After that", the narrator mentioned the previous hadith, which contains these words (the person said), I understood that such and such work precedes such and such (the narrator quoted these words about three works).” So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said," “There is nothing wrong with that.”"""
2573,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon. A person stood in front of him. He said, \I used to think that such and such work precedes such and such work.\"" Then another person stood up and said", O Messenger of God! I used to think that such and such a task is before these three tasks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Do it now. There is no problem.\"" (The narrator says) On that day", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about anything, he said the same thing, do it now," there is no harm."""
2574,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about any work that a person had done before another work, or if one work had been done before another."
2575,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, and he (peace be upon him) used to say that there is no problem."
2576,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have performed Tawaf before playing rummy. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You now throw pebbles. There is no harm.\"" A person said", O Messenger of Allah! I have shaved my head before playing rummy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""There is no problem if you play rummy.\"" One person said"," \""I have sacrificed before playing rummy.\"""""
2577,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, quotes this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father (Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him) with reference to Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace."
2578,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2579,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father (Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him). When the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came near Mount Safa, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: \Verily"," Safa and Marwa are the signs of Allah.\"" Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) started from Safa."""
2580,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may Allah have mercy on him) Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this. looked at"
2581,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received the black stone and the Yamani stone."
2582,"As soon as Mansoor bin Abdul Rahman quoted this statement of his mother Safiyya, some women belonging to Banu Abdul Dar have said that 'those who were blessed with the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him', they told us! Entering the house of Ibn Abi Hussain, we peeped through the door and saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running towards the place of sacrifice until he reached Zakaq Banuflan. This is a place which is called the place of sacrifice. Try because it is obligatory upon you to try."
2583,"Sayyidna Burah bint Abu Tijarrat (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, “I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ‘When he reached the end of the place of Sa’i, the Prophet (Sallallahu ‘Alaihi Wasallam) said, ‘You people, make Sa’i, because Allah has made it obligatory for you to perform Sa’i (she narrates). Waslam's legs were visible."
2584,"Sayyida Habiba bint Abu Tijarrat (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, “I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing Sa’i between Safa and Marwah."
2585,"A woman named Safiyyah narrates this statement of the daughter of Abu Tujarat: I entered the house of Abu Hussain with some women of the Quraish. I saw the shins. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You people, strive because Allah has made it necessary for you to strive."
2586,"A woman belonging to Safiyyah bint Shiba Banu Abddar, who is the daughter of Abu Tjarat, narrates this with reference to her, “She narrates, I entered the house of Aal Abu Hussain with some women of the Quraish, and we saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after this, this woman has mentioned according to the previous hadith)."
2587,"Safiyyah Bint Sheebah narrates, I was standing in my window, I saw the Holy Prophet between Safa and Marwah, I saw the Holy Prophet running when he came to the valley."
2588,"Nafee narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, about a bald person, his head will go away."
2589,"Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said this about a bald person, his head will be covered with shavings. A narrator named Abdul Kareem has narrated this in my writing, 'Once the narrator has narrated it as a marfu' hadith and once he has not quoted it as a marfu' hadith."
2590,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).
2591,"It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that once he put on Ihram for Umrah, when he reached Dhu al-Halifa, he said, “The case of both of them is one and the same."
2592,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever wears Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time, it will be sufficient for him to perform Tawaf once and perform Sa’i once, and he will not become halal because of either of them, but he will become halal from both of them."
2593,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this: Whoever wears Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time, it will be enough for him to perform Tawaf once, then after that he will not open the Haram until he completes his Hajj, then he will open Ihram for both of them at the same time."
2594,Nafi' narrated this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he once performed Hajj and Umrah together and performed the same effort for both of them and stated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also did the same.
2595,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a single Tawaf for the Hajj of the Qur’an, and after doing it, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not open his Ihram."
2596,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) entered Makkah wearing Ihram for the Hajj of the Qur’an and entered Makkah.
2597,"According to Mujahid Bayan, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to say that when he used to perform Hajj and Umrah at the same time, they both have the same route. This hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Hasan bin Amara with reference to the narrator named Hakam, and this person is a lost hadeeth."
2598,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) have narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions circled between Safa and Marwah only once, that was for their Umrah and Hajj."
2599,"This has been narrated about Taus, the narrator narrates, I asked him about Hajj Tamattu, and he said: Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this hadith to me."
2600,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once for both of them and performed Sa’i once for Hajj and Umrah.
2601,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform Tawaf more than once (ie for both Hajj and Umrah).
2602,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time.
2603,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions did not perform Tawaf more than once (i.e. they used to perform Tawaf once for both Hajj and Umrah).
2604,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj to the Qur’an, and he performed Tawaf once, both he and his companions. A narrator named Ibn Mubashir has narrated these words, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once and performed Sa'i once (the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also did the same)."
2605,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the same Tawaf for Hajj and Umrah.
2606,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj, but some of his companions did not."
2607,"Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that when a person performs Hajj on behalf of his parents, he will be accepted by that person and by his parents, and the souls of both of them (i.e. parents) will be given this good news in heaven, and that person will be recorded as \good\"" in the presence of Allah."""
2608,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents or performs the duty on their behalf, he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with the righteous people."
2609,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, \My parents have passed away. It was obligatory for them to perform Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on their behalf?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""What do you think? If your father had a debt"," would you have paid it on his behalf?\"" He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You should also perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\"""""
2610,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his father and mother, then he has fulfilled the obligation of Hajj on their behalf, and this person will receive the reward of performing Hajj ten times."
2611,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) that my father had passed away. He had not performed the Hajj. If your father had a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would he accept it? He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You should also perform Hajj on his behalf.\"""""
2612,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) about performing Hajj on his father's behalf. He said, 'You should perform Hajj on his behalf.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more entitled to this (that his debt be paid)."
2613,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed the Hajj of the Qur’an, it was the occasion of the Farewell Hajj."
2614,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2615,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah and performed Sa’i only once.
2616,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) regarding his father (Imam Muhammad Al-Baqir (RA)): The Prophet (PBUH) combined Hajj and Umrah (i.e. performed Hajj of the Qur’an), so he performed Tawaf for both of them once."
2617,Abdullah Bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions performed Tawaf once for their Hajj and Umrah.
2618,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time.
2619,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah.
2620,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah, and he did not perform Tawaf again after that."
2621,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah.
2622,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, explains: No! By Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf only once for both of them."
2623,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this is enough for you, 'You perform Tawaf once for both of them after Maghrib."
2624,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2625,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to her that performing Tawaf between As-Safa and Marwah is sufficient for both your Hajj and Umrah.
2626,"According to Mujahid Bayan, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) had menstruation at the place of \Saraf\"" and she was purified from it on the day of 'Arafah", then the Prophet (PBUH) said to her," \""Performing tawaf between Safa and Marwah will be sufficient for you for both Hajj and Umrah.\"" The words of the tradition are from a narrator named Abu Na'im."""
2627,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with him) that the first circumambulation between Safa and Marwah will be sufficient for you for Hajj and Umrah. Narrator Ibn Makhlid has quoted these words: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that your first circumambulation will be sufficient for both your Hajj and Umrah.
2628,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates that Sayyiduna Ali once performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time, then he performed Tawaf once for both of them, but he performed Sa'i twice for both of them. Hafs bin Abu Dawudnami is a weak narrator while Abdul Rahman bin Abu Laila has a bad memory and his illusions are high."
2629,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates this about Sayyiduna Ali, he performed Tawaf twice for both Hajj and Umrah, and performed Sa'i twice for both, and said, \I have seen the Holy Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," do the same.\"" Hasan bin Amara is an obsolete hadith."""
2630,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj to the Qur’an, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf twice and performed Sa’i twice."
2631,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf twice for his Umrah and Hajj and performed Sa'i twice. (The narrator narrates) Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) also did the same. The narrator named Abu Baruh is Amro bin Yazid and this person is also weak."
2632,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf twice and attempted Sa’i twice. Some narrators differ in narrating this hadith. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time. There is no mention of doing Tawaf and Sa'i in this tradition. The narrator named Muhammad bin Yahya has narrated this correct tradition many times and it has also been stated that he had turned away from mentioning Tawaf and Sa'i and started narrating the correct tradition.
2633,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj to the Qur'an.
2634,"Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us; Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Malik ibn al-Harith—or Mansur, from Malik ibn al-Harith—from Abu Nasr, who said:I met 'Ali when I had entered ihram for Hajj, and he had entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah combined. I said: ""Can I do as you did?"" He said: ""That would have been if you had started the 'Umrah first."" I said: ""How do I do it if I want that?"" He said: ""You take a vessel of water and pour it over yourself, then you enter ihram for both together, then you perform two tawafs for them and two sa'ys for them, and your ihram does not become permissible until the Day of Sacrifice.""Mansur said: I mentioned that to Mujahid, and he said: ""We used to give fatwa only for a single tawaf, but as for now, we do not do that.""", may God be pleased with him, 'I had put on Ihram for Hajj, while he had put on Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time. I asked if I could do it as you have done.' He said, 'It can be done if you perform Umrah first.' He said: Take a pot of water and pour it over you and then put on Ihram for both of them together. Then it will not be permissible for both of them to perform Tawaf twice and perform Sa'i once and for you to open Ihram before the Day of Sacrifice. A narrator named Mansoor narrates that I mentioned this tradition to Mujahid, so he said," \""We are giving this fatwa. Tawaf will be performed once"," but now we will not do it.\"""""
2635,Imam Shafi'i says this: I adopt people and it is better to have fun. We do not call it makruh.
2636,"Mujahid narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Dharghafari (RA) came, he held the door frame of the Kaaba and then said: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that a person should pray after the morning prayer until the sun rises and after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."
2637,"Sayyidna Jubir ibn al-Mu'tam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Banu Abdul Muttalib! You should not prevent anyone from circumambulating this house and not preventing anyone from offering prayers, whether it is any part of the day or night."
2638,"Sayyidna Jubir ibn al-Mu'tam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd Manaf! This matter is now up to us, so I do not know that you have prevented any person from praying near this house, whether it is any part of the day or night."
2639,"Nafi bin Jubayr quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father, O Banu Abd Manaf! You should not prevent anyone from offering prayers near this house at any part of the day or night."
2640,"Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that a person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself, he can marry someone. Imam Shafi'i has quoted these words additionally and he cannot even give the message of marriage to anyone."
2641,"Nabiyyah bin Wahhib narrates that Umar bin Ubaidullah sent a message to Aban bin Uthman, 'Iban was the Commander of Hajj in those days, both of them were in the state of Ihram (the message was sent) I want to marry Talha bin Umar with the daughter of Shaiba bin Jubayr, and I want you to be a part of it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said that a person in the state of Ihram is neither self-respecting, nor can he send a message of marriage to anyone, nor can he marry anyone."
2642,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person who was reciting talbiyah by a person named Shabarmah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He did not submit! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \First", perform Hajj on your own behalf," then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""
2643,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired"," \""Have you performed Hajj?\"" He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then this is from you and later you will perform Hajj from Shabarmah."""
2644,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person reciting talbiya on behalf of another person, so he said to him: O you who recite talbiya on behalf of such and such a person! If you have performed the obligatory Hajj, then recite Talbiyah from Shabarmah, otherwise recite Talbiyah from yourself."
2645,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed a person who was reciting talbiyah on behalf of a person named Nabisha. This is from Nabeesha, you must first perform Hajj on your own behalf. The narrator named Hasan bin Amara is unique in narrating this hadith and this person is an abandoned hadith."
2646,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) passed by a man who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of Nabisha. It will be from Nabisha, you should perform Hajj from your side."
2647,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) heard a person who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of Nabeesha. Have you done Hajj? He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then it will be done by Nabishah. You perform Hajj on your own behalf.\"""""
2648,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) cursed a person who was saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, “Who is Shabarmah?” He replied, 'My brother.' So he did not submit! The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said, \Perform Hajj on your own behalf"," then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"" This hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas", may Allah be pleased with him," is correct. It has been stated that the hadith narrated before it is an illusion. It has been stated that a narrator named Hasan bin Amara narrated it and then turned to him."""
2649,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) asked, “Have you performed Hajj before?” He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then it will be done on your behalf. Later"," you will perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""
2650,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2651,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Have you performed Hajj on your behalf? He did not submit! He said to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then recite Talbiyah on your behalf."
2652,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2653,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a person who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of another person. If you have not performed the fard, then recite Talbiyah on your own behalf."
2654,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He heard a person reciting Talbiyah on behalf of another person, so he said to him, \If you have performed Hajj on your behalf", then recite Talbiyah on his behalf," otherwise perform Hajj on your behalf.\"""""
2655,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then perform Hajj on your own, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah."
2656,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person reciting talbiyah by Shabarma, so he inquired who is Shabarma? This person mentioned his relationship with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you performed Hajj yourself? Narrator states that this person answered no! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then first you perform Hajj on your behalf, then you perform Hajj on behalf of Shubarmah."
2657,Another chain of transmission is similar to the (past hadith) of Ibn Abi Laila.
2658,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked who is Shabarmah? He replied that he is my brother (the narrator doubts that maybe these are the words) He mentioned his relationship. So he said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then do it on your behalf and later perform Hajj on behalf of Shubarmah.\"""""
2659,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \You should do it on your own side"," then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""
2660,This tradition is narrated as a marfu' hadith along with another chain of transmission.
2661,"Along with another chain of transmission, it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah” (following this is according to the previous hadith)."
2662,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person reciting talbiyah by Shabarmah and inquired who is Shabarmah? He replied that he is my brother, or I am related to him. He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said, \Do it on your behalf\"" then he would perform Hajj on his behalf."""
2663,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying Talbiyah by Shabarmah and asked him, \Have you performed Hajj?\"" He submitted! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Then recite the talbiyah on your own behalf.\"""""
2664,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he saw a person reciting talbiya from Shabarmah."
2665,This tradition has been narrated as a muquf tradition from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission.
2666,"Safiyyah Bint Sheeba narrates Umm Uthman Bint Abu Sufyan has narrated this, Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this. The Prophet (PBUH) said, “It is not obligatory on women to shave their heads. Women will only cut their hair short."
2667,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that shaving the head is not for women.
2668,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhu says this about a woman in the state of Ihram, she will cut as much hair as her index finger."
2669,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says this: The sunnah is that on the night of putting on Ihram, a woman will put some henna on her head, then wash her head and put it on her head."
2670,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave permission to women to wear socks in the state of Ihram. Salim narrates that earlier Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to call it makruh, until a woman named Safiyyah narrated this hadith regarding Sayyida Aisha (RA) (so he issued a fatwa according to it)."
2671,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to give this fatwa that women should cut off their socks, until Safiyyah told him that Sayyida Aisha (RA) had instructed women not to cut them off. This tradition is suspended."
2672,"Ata narrates that once a man had intercourse with his wife before circumambulating Baitullah on the Day of Sacrifice, then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said that they will both sacrifice a camel, but now it will not be obligatory for them to perform Hajj again next year."
2673,"Ibrahim bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharama had a disagreement about whether a person in the state of Ihram can shed his head or not. So these gentlemen sent me to the service of Ayyub Ansari (RA) so that I could find out from whom they had seen the Prophet (PBUH) 'The Prophet (PBUH) used to wash himself in his state of Ihram (or not)', then Sayyidna Ayub Ansari (RA) poured water on his head, 'moved his hand to the front and brought it back from the back."
2674,"Sayyidna Mu'awiya bin Khadij (RA) narrates that he was present at the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and his mother Kabsha bint Maadi Karb was present with him. Her mother said, O Messenger of Allah! I have made this vow, 'I will circumambulate the house of Sirin', so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Walk on your feet and perform circumambulation' seven times with both hands and seven times with both feet."
2675,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Do not throw pebbles at Jamrat until the sun rises.
2676,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed his wives to leave Muzdalifah at night and throw pebbles at Jamrat, then return to their place of residence in the morning, so those women continued to do so until they died (i.e. they continued to do so for the rest of their lives). Ata states that we will continue to do the same."
2677,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) completed his Hajj, I perfumed the Prophet (PBUH) before performing his circumambulation."
2678,Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I perfumed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my two hands when he shaved his head after slaughtering an animal.
2679,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I perfumed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he put on his Ihram and before performing Tawaf when he took off his Ihram (perfumed him).
2680,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that on the last day of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back. He offered the Zuhr prayer, then he went back and spent the nights of Tashreek in the moon. He also stopped and stood there for a long time praying (with Griya Waziri) then did not stop there at the time of pelting pebbles on the third Jamrah."
2681,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) went on foot to throw stones and returned on foot. During this time, he did not ride a horse. Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar also used to do the same."
2682,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates, “I remember this saying about the Holy Prophet (SAW) ‘He (SAW) threw pebbles at Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice at Chasht, and then after that he (SAW) threw pebbles at it at the time of sunset. Ibn Abu Shaybah narrates that stones will be thrown at the time of chasht on the day of sacrifice at Jamrah al-Uqbah, and the next day when the sun sets."
2683,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2684,"Zahri narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw pebbles at the Jamra which is near the Mina Mosque, he hit it with seven pebbles. While throwing each pebble, he said Takbeer. Then he came in front of the Jamra and stood facing the House of Allah. Throwing each pebble, he said Takbeer, then he moved a little to the left, which is Wadi Wal-Hisa, then he stood there facing the House of Allah, he raised both his hands and began to pray. Come, then you did not stand next to him. Al-Zuhri has narrated this. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to do the same thing."
2685,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates from his father, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission to herdsmen to throw pebbles at night\"" or at any time during the day."""
2686,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when a man throws pebbles, shaves his head, and speaks with his mouth, then he becomes lawful for everything, but he cannot have intercourse with his wife."
2687,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When you throw pebbles and make sacrifices, you will become lawful for everything (but you cannot have intercourse with women)."
2688,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when you throw pebbles, make sacrifices, you become lawful for everything, but you cannot have intercourse with a woman. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
2689,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that on the night of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a message to Umm Salama."
2690,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when a person starts going back, he should circumambulate the Bayt Allah last, but this is not an order for menstruating women, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given them this permission (they can go back without circumambulating the House of Allah for the last time). A narrator named Abu Ammar has stated that a person who performs Hajj to Bait Allah should perform Tawaf of Bait Allah at the end, however, the order for menstruating women is different, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given them permission (that they may go back without performing Tawaf)."
2691,"Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id and Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Mubashshir narrated to us; they said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; from Ayyub; from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah; from Tawus, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar when he was asked about that — meaning the menstruating woman departing (before the farewell circumambulation). He said: ""She must remain until her last act is at the House (the Ka'bah)."" Tawus said: So I do not know whether Ibn Umar forgot it or had not heard what his companions heard. Then, after a year or two, I witnessed him being asked about it, and he said: ""I have been informed that a concession was granted to them.""", may Allah be pleased with him. He was asked about this, that is, about the return of a menstruating woman. He said, 'She will stay there until she performs Tawaf of the House of Allah for the last time.' Yadusal was present with him later, and he was asked about it, and he said," \""It has been explained to me that these women are allowed to do so (they can go back without performing Tawaf)."""
2692,Sayyiduna Hajjaj bin Amr Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who becomes injured or disabled will take off his ihram and it will be obligatory for him to perform Hajj the following year.
2693,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has said that whoever performs Hajj and comes to visit my grave after I leave, it is said that he came to visit me during my lifetime."
2694,"Sayyiduna Hatib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever came to visit me after my death, it is said that he came to visit me during my lifetime, and whoever dies in one of Makkah or Madinah will be resurrected with the believers on the Day of Resurrection."
2695,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that whoever visits my grave, my intercession will be obligatory for him."
2696,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah regarding his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him)."
2697,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that Iqra bin Habs asked the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, whether it is obligatory to perform Hajj every year. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, it is obligatory to perform Hajj once, and whoever performs Hajj after that, it will be Nafil for him."
2698,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people! If Hajj was made obligatory on you, then Iqra bin Habs (RA) said, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? The Prophet (PBUH) remained silent, then he said, No, but it is obligatory to perform Hajj only once. After that, whoever performs Hajj will have Nafl for him."
2699,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Iqra bin Habs (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hajj every year.
2700,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2701,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2702,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ordered to perform Hajj, Iqra Bin Habis (RA) asked: Is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? Ya Rasulullah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I had said yes, then it would have become obligatory."
2703,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates when this verse was revealed. \And it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah," whoever has the means to reach it.\"" People asked", O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. The people said: Is it obligatory every year? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, if I had said yes," it would have become necessary. Then Allah revealed this verse. \""O believers! Do not discover things which", if revealed to you, would make you feel bad. There are these words in a tradition, people asked what every year? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, then the people asked," \""What about every year?\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:"""
2704,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) in a loud voice whether it is obligatory to perform Hajj every year. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, then he said no! On the contrary, it is obligatory for a Muslim to perform Hajj once every year. If I had said it every year, it would have become obligatory every year. Another person stood up and asked, \Can I perform Hajj on behalf of my father because he is an elderly man?\"""""
2705,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon and the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people! Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon you. Then a man stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? He asked this question three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give him any answer. When I command you to do something, do it as much as you can, and when I forbid you to do something, refrain from it."
2706,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) stood among us to deliver a sermon and said: O people! Allah Ta'ala has made it obligatory upon you to perform Hajj.
2707,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) said this: O people, performing Hajj has been made obligatory upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give him any answer, he repeated the question, he asked, O Messenger of Allah, what every year? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Who is the one who said this? The people said that there is such and such a person. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \By the One in Whose Power is my life. If I had said yes", it would have become obligatory. If it had become obligatory, you would not have been able to pay it, and if you were not able to do it," then you would have committed disbelief. So Allah revealed this verse. \""O believers! Do not inquire about such things which", if they were revealed to you," would lead you astray."""
2708,"Yahya bin Ya'Umar narrates: I said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, some people say that there is no reality of fate. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \If you meet him"," convey this message to me that Abdullah bin Umar requests in the presence of Allah to be indifferent to you and you have nothing to do with him.\"" (Then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated this hadith. I heard Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab narrating that he said that one day we were sitting with the Prophet (PBUH) in the presence of some people", while a man came there, he had no sign of travel and he was not a resident of the city. He placed his hand on the knees of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Sayyidna Muhammad, what is Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, and establish prayer, and pay Zakat, and perform Hajj, and perform Umrah, and perform ablution, and perform ablution, and observe the fast of Ramadan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes. After that, he narrated the rest of the hadith. At the end of this hadith, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Block this person to me.\"" (says the narrator) We went out in search of him", but we could not find him. Sometimes I had a hard time recognizing them and I recognized them when they left. The chain of transmission of this hadith is proven and correct," Imam Muslim has narrated it with the same chain of transmission."""
2709,"Sayyiduna Saraqa bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is the order of Umrah specific to us this year or is it for forever? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No, it is forever, Umrah has entered Hajj until the Day of Judgment (meaning both of them can be performed together). All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
2710,"Sayyidna Aburzain (RA) narrates that he asked the Prophet (PBUH) this question. He said, \My father has become old. He has become a Muslim", but now he cannot perform Umrah and travel. The Prophet (PBUH) said," 'You should perform both Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father.'"""
2711,"Sayyida Umm Salma narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever wears the Ihram of Hajj and Umrah to go from Masjid Al-Aqsa to Masjid Haram, all past and future sins of that person will be forgiven, and Paradise will be obligatory for him."
2712,"Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever puts on the Ihram for Hajj or Umrah from Bait al-Maqdis, he will become from his sins as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."
2713,"Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever wears Ihram for Hajj or Umrah from Bait-ul-Maqdis, his past sins will be forgiven."
2714,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that whoever performs Hajj or Umrah and does not commit any filth or immorality during it, when he returns, he will be as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."
2715,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether it is necessary to wage Jihad on women.
2716,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory for women to wage Jihad?"
2717,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that Hajj and Umrah are compulsory for all people, only the people of Makkah have a different ruling, since their Umrah must be circumambulated. When the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) entered Makkah, he was wearing Ihram for Hajj or Ihram for Umrah."
2718,Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Hajj and Umrah are both obligatory.
2719,"It is narrated that Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about performing Umrah before Hajj, and he said that these are two prayers."
2720,"Narrated by Nafi, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to say that Hajj and Umrah are obligatory on all of God's creation, that is, on those who have the means to go there, and if a person does more after that, then it is good and a posthumous act of worship. The narrator narrates, I heard him say something about the people of Makkah."
2721,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that performing Umrah is obligatory like Hajj and it is a short Hajj.
2722,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the major Hajj is on the day of sacrifice and the minor Hajj is Umrah.
2723,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. \Umrah is a short Hajj and the Qur'an can only be touched by an ablution person\""."""
2724,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of Zakat and Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Yes.” It is portable."
2725,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but if you perform Umrah, it is better for you."
2726,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2727,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Umrah and is it obligatory like Hajj? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, but if you perform Umrah, it is better for you."
2728,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) told her about her Umrah, i.e. the Umrah performed by Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, that the reward for your Umrah will be based on what you have spent."
2729,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked her about her Umrah.
2730,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs Umrah will continue to read Talbiyah until he starts Tawaf.
2731,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the person who performs Hajj by combining Umrah with Hajj.
2732,"Saeed Ibn Musaib narrates that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Uthman (RA) both came for Hajj. On the way, Sayyidna Uthman (RA) forbade Umrah to be added to Hajj as a ritual. But Sayyidna Uthman did not forbid these gentlemen, Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, \I know that you have forbidden them to perform Umrah together as a form of Tamattu.\"" He replied"," \""Yes!\"" So Sayyiduna Ali said to him"," \""Haven't you heard this"," then you have enjoyed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?\"" So they answered yes."""
2733,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that on the way to Hajj, Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) was told to Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) that Sayyidna 'Uthman had forbidden his companions from combining Umrah with Hajj, that is, from performing Hajj, so Sayyidna 'Ali said to his companions: When Sayyidna 'Uthman departs, you will also depart. The narrator narrates that then Sayyiduna Ali and his companions put on Ihram for Umrah, Sayyiduna Uthman did not say anything to them: Sayyiduna Ali said to Sayyiduna Uthman: I have been told this about you: You have forbidden your companions from combining Umrah with Hajj, i.e. performing Hajj Tamattu. So Syedna Usman replied yes. Saeed narrates, I do not know what Syedna Usman replied to him."
2734,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) read this. \I am here to perform Hajj and Umrah together.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
2735,"Abdullah bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah, knowing that he would not perform Hajj after that."
2736,"Abdullah bin Abu Malikah narrates that a person came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas asked him where you came from. He replied, \I am drinking Zam Zam water.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas asked him"," \""Did you drink it as it should have been drunk?\"" He asked"," \""O Sayyidna Ibn Abbas"," how is it (drinking)?\"" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas said"," \""When you drink it", turn towards the Qiblah and recite the name of Allah, and then drink it in three breaths and drink it in large quantities when you drink it," because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites the praises of Allah.\"" Peace be upon him has said that the main difference between us and the hypocrites is that they (hypocrites) do not drink zam-zam in large quantities."""
2737,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2738,Ikrama narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say this dua when he drank Zam Zam water. \O Allah! I ask You for knowledge that gives benefit, I ask for sustenance that is vast," and I ask for healing from every disease."""
2739,"Mujahid narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink the water of Zam-Zam, if you drink it because you will be healed by it, then Allah will bless you with healing. The result is and through this Allah watered Sayyidna Ismail."
2740,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching his blessed face and his chest with that of Multzam.
2741,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) placed his forehead on the Black Stone.
2742,"Ata narrates that I saw Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri, Abu Huraira, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, and Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu, these gentlemen used to kiss their hands when receiving the Black Stone. The narrator narrates, I inquired if you have seen Sayyidna Ibn Abbas doing this too, so he replied, I have seen Sayyidna Ibn Abbas doing this many times."
2743,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss the Yamani man and he would place his blessed face on it.
2744,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah has quoted this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that it is lawful for you to hunt dry land while you are in the state of Ihram, when you have not hunted it yourself, and it has not been hunted by you."
2745,This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir along with another chain of transmission.
2746,This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
2747,This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him).
2748,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
2749,"Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah narrates this statement from his father (Sayyidna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of Hudaybiyyah, I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (to perform Umrah), my companions put on Ihram, but I did not put on Ihram, I saw a blue cow and attacked it and hunted it, then I narrated this incident to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioning that I was not wearing Ihram at that time and I have hunted it for you, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his companions to eat that meat, but the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not eat it because I had told you that I had hunted it for you. These are the words of the hadith, I have hunted for you and these words the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not eat, it was mentioned only by a narrator named Muammar. All Muslims agree on this. Believers! Do not kill the victim when you are in the state of Ihram."
2750,"Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father. He performed Umrah with Sayyidna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, along with a few others. They offered a bird to Sayyidna Uthman, so Sayyidna Uthman said to the others: Let them eat it, and he refused to eat it. So Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied that my position regarding him is not like yours, he has been hunted for me."
2751,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: I rent things like this, now they say that your Hajj has not been done? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said, “A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and he (PBUH) inquired about the matter about which you asked me: Yes, the Prophet (PBUH) remained silent until this verse was revealed. \There is no sin on you when you seek the grace of your Lord.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Your Hajj has been completed.\"""""
2752,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar: I give (riding animals) (to the pilgrims) on rent. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated a tradition similar to this regarding the Prophet (PBUH) and he said, \You are a Haji.\"""""
2753,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA).
2754,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who had been slaughtered before sacrificing his head, but before offering sacrifice, the Prophet (PBUH) kept saying that there is no harm in it, there is no harm in it."
2755,Alaa bin Musayb narrates this with reference to a person belonging to Banutim.
2756,"Abu Umamah Taymi narrates: I said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): If we rent (animals to pilgrims), will our Hajj be performed? So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said, \Don't you people circumambulate the House of Allah", don't you go to Arafat field, don't you throw pebbles at Jamrat," and don't you shave your head?\"" We replied yes! So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said", “A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked him about the same thing that he had asked me," but the Prophet (PBUH) did not answer him until Gabriel came down with this verse. \""There is no sin on you if you seek the grace of your Lord.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""You people are pilgrims.\"""""
2757,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (Radi Allahu Anhu) (the narrator says) has narrated this as a hadeeth, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one should ever say that I will remain single."
2758,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade a Muslim called a single (monk) to go.
2759,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I cursed the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that at that time he was giving the sermon of Hajj Al-Wada to the people on his camel. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Obey your Lord", perform the five prayers, pay Zakat on your wealth, observe the fasts of your appointed month," obey your rulers and enter the Paradise of your Lord.\"" Narrator narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abu Umamah", may God be pleased with him, how many years ago did you hear this hadith? He replied," I was thirty years old at that time."""
2760,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a woman should keep her face uncovered in Ihram.
2761,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that a woman will cover her face in Ihram and a man will cover his head in Ihram.
2762,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We (women) set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were in the state of Ihram.
2763,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were in the state of Ihram. When we encountered a rider, we would put the cloth on our heads in front of our faces and when he passed by, we would remove it."
2764,Sayyidah Umm Salma (RA) narrates: We were with the Prophet (PBUH) and we were in the state of Ihram.
2765,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person fell from his camel, he was in the state of Ihram, he passed away, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered about him that he will be shrouded in these two clothes, he will be bathed but his face should not be covered, he will be perfumed, and he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection while reciting Talbiyah."
2766,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says that it is not necessary for women to perform the Tawaf of Baytullah and the Sa'i of Safa and Marwah.
2767,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a woman will not climb directly above Safa and Marwah, and she will not raise her voice while reciting Talbiyah. In one tradition, only these words are said: A woman will not climb over Safawmruh."
2768,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that it is not obligatory for women to run between Baitullah (during Tawaf) and Safa and Marwah.
2769,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person fell off his horse in the morning of the day of Arafah and he was in the state of Ihram. He died. This was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, \Ghusl him with water and berry leaves", and shroud him in the same two clothes, and do not cover his face," because he will be alive on the Day of Resurrection reciting Talbiyah.\"""""
2770,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words and it is not Sarkodhanpana."
2771,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet (PBUH) and a man fell from his camel and died. He was in the state of Ihram.
2772,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this about a person who dies in the state of Ihram, you should cover him and do not resemble the Jews."
2773,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2774,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person was accompanying the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the state of Ihram and he fell from his camel, his neck bone was broken and he died. A narrator named Ibn Jaraj narrates, I asked my teacher, did Saeed bin Jubayr tell you about the place where that person fell? So he answered no!"
2775,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
2776,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover the faces of your men and do not resemble the Jews.
2777,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) A person was following the Prophet (PBUH) in the state of Ihram, he fell from his camel, his neck bone was broken, and he died."
2778,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2779,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever performs Hajj or Umrah dies in this state (i.e. the state of Ihram), then he will not appear and will not be counted from him, and said to him: You will enter Paradise."
2780,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw that his lice were falling on his face. This is about the location of Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, \Are your lice bothering you?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be leaders", even though they were at Hudaybiyyah at that time and the Prophet had not yet announced to the people that he would open Ihram here, because the people wanted him to enter Makkah. Then Allah revealed the order of redemption. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to divide one, the difference," among six poor people or sacrifice a goat or fast for three days."""
2781,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him, he was lighting a fire under his hand. Narrator named Sufyan narrates (about this event) this verse was revealed: \So whoever among you is sick or has a headache"," let him give an offering.\"""""
2782,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw that his lice were falling on his face. This is about the location of Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, \Are your lice bothering you?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to be leaders", even though they were at the place of Hudaybiyyah at that time and the Prophet had not yet announced to the people that he would open Ihram here because the people wanted him to enter Makkah. Then Allah sent down the order of redemption, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to divide one, the difference," among six poor people or sacrifice an animal or fast for three days."""
2783,Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him and he was lighting a fire under his hand. This is about Hudaybiyah. The Prophet (PBUH) asked him if your lice were bothering you. (The narrator narrates) So this verse was revealed: \So whoever among you is sick or has a headache," he should fast as a ransom or give charity or sacrifice.\"" The order of fasting is to fast for three days. Sadaqah means that six poor people should be given one", a difference," and Qurbani means that a goat should be sacrificed."""
2784,"Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by him, his hair was big at the roots of his hair and there were lice in the upper part of his hair. He said no! The Prophet said: Then if you wish, fast for three days, feed three sa's of dates (to the poor) and give one sa' to each poor person."
2785,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about a person in the state of Ihram who trims his nails, he will feed a sa'a of grain from each palm."
2786,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that people used to go back to wherever they were going from Mina. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to perform Tawaf of the House of Allah at the end (and go home from there).
2787,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this as a hadeeth: He who eats the rent of houses in Makkah eats fire.
2788,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the method of throwing pebbles is to say Takbeer along with it.
2789,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: We said, O Messenger of Allah, we believe that the number of pebbles that are thrown at the Jamrats every year will be exhausted. The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Those that are accepted will be picked up. If it is possible"," you will see (heaps of pebbles) here like mountains.\"""""
2790,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person completes his Hajj, he should return to his home as soon as possible because his reward is high."
2791,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \When a man returns from a journey and brings a gift for his wife", he should give her a gift," even if it is a stone.\"""""
2792,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Allah frees many people on the day of Arafah, and on no other day does He free more people from hell."
2793,"Umar ibn Uthman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There are four people whom I, Hal, and the Haram will not give safety to in any place: Hawairat ibn Naqeed, Muqais, Hilal ibn Khatl, and Abdullah ibn Abu Sarh. (The narrator narrates) Hawarith was killed by Sayyidna Ali (RA), Muqis was killed by his cousin, Laha, Hilal bin Khatl was killed by Sayyidna Zubair (RA) As for Abdullah bin Sarh, Sayyidna Uthman (RA) asked for protection for him, he was his foster brother. One was killed and the other survived. He later accepted Islam."
2794,Umar ibn Uthman narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \You are Saeed. Who is greater among us (the two of us)," me or you?\"" So they said", I (was born) before you, may God bless you, and you are older than me, and you, may God bless you," are better than me."""
2795,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: You should perform Hajj before you cannot perform Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The villagers will sit on the edges of their own areas and no one will be able to reach (Mecca) to perform Hajj.\"""""
2796,"Sayyiduna Fazla bin Ubaid (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the Battle of Khyber, a necklace was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) which was plated with gold and had precious stones attached to it. You return it until both of them (i.e. stone and gold) are separated."
2797,"A necklace was brought to the service of Sayyidna Fazla bin Ubaid, may God bless him and grant him peace, which was covered with gold and stones, and the gold and stones were taken off under his orders, and he said, \Sell the gold and gold in exchange for equal weight.\"""""
2798,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, people used to sell fruits for sale. A narrator named Ibn Mahdi has quoted these words. People used to pledge allegiance for twenty-two years, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Make salaf in exchange for the prescribed measure and weight.\"""""
2799,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to sell Salaf for a year and a half, so he said, \Whoever wants to sell Salaf (loan) should trade for a specified period of time in exchange for a specified measure and a specified weight.\"" These words of the tradition are from a narrator named Neshapuri"," Mohali has quoted these words."""
2800,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to borrow and trade dates for two or three years."
2801,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to trade on loan for a year or two."
2802,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to trade fruits on loan for two or three years."
2803,"Makhool narrates this hadith as a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever buys something that he has not seen, he has the right to accept it when he sees it, and if he wants to, he can leave it. Abu al-Hasan (i.e. Darqutni) says that this hadith is transmitted and its narrator Abu Bakr Maryam is weak."
2804,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words, Ibn Sirin states that even if the thing is not according to the time that the person mentioned to the buyer, this deal will be binding."
2805,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person buys something that he has not seen, when he sees it, he will have the right (if he wishes to cancel the deal). This hadith along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while some narrators have quoted it as a muqaf tradition up to Ibn Sirin, i.e. as his own words."
2806,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate this on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, “Whoever buys something, it will be obligatory for him to take it, and he will have the right to terminate the transaction until his partner separates from him."
2807,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when two men make a deal, each of them will have the right until they separate from each other and live together or one of them gives the other the right."
2808,"The same hadith has been narrated in the same way along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him), however, it is about two parties and the narrator named Ibn Wahib is unique in narrating it."
2809,"Sheikh Abu Wasi narrates: We were participating in a war campaign, while a man came and his horse was with him. One of us said: Will you sell this horse in exchange for this slave? He said: Yes! Then he sold it, then he stayed with us that night, and when morning came, he went to his horse, and our companion said to him: What is your relationship with this horse? Have you not sold it to me? So the man said: I do not need this deal. So our companion said: Now you have nothing to do with it. You have sold it to me. When the people came to them, Sayyidna Abu Barzah said to them both: Are you satisfied with the decision of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
2810,"Shaykh Abu Wasi narrates: We were engaged in a battle, we camped at a place, a man from the army came to us and he was riding his horse, he traded his horse with one of our companions. After that, the narrator has narrated a similar hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Burzah."
2811,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we used to make a deal with each other, each of the parties would have authority until the two parties to the deal separated from each other. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once me and Sayyidna Uthman made a deal, I sold my land that was in the valley to his land that was in Khyber."
2812,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A true and trustworthy merchant will be with the martyrs. A narrator named Fazl has quoted these words: On the Day of Resurrection, the Prophets will be with the Siddiqeen and the Martyrs."
2813,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a true and trustworthy merchant will be with the righteous prophets and martyrs on the Day of Resurrection.
2814,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this hadith: the price of alcohol is forbidden, the earnings of a prostitute is forbidden, the price of a dog is forbidden, if the owner of a dog comes to you and asks for the price of his dog, fill both his hands with mud, and if the owner of the dog comes to you and asks for the price of his dog, fill both his hands with mud."
2815,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when Allah Ta'ala declares something haram (this is what it means), He also makes the price of that thing haram."
2816,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Verily, Allah has forbidden wine and its price, and He has forbidden carrion and its price, and He has forbidden pigs and its price."
2817,"Sayyiduna Tamim Dari quotes the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that it is not permissible to take the price of anything that is not permissible to eat."
2818,"Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna 'Uthman, \When you buy something", measure it with what you buy, and when you sell it," measure it with what you sell.\"""""
2819,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah forbade the sale of grain until it is measured on both sides by the seller and by the buyer.
2820,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates that he asked the Messenger of Allah, \O Messenger of Allah", if I buy and sell," which of the stocks is halal for me and which of the stocks is forbidden for me?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""My nephew"," buy something and do not sell it until you take possession of it yourself.\"""""
2821,"The same hadith is narrated by another Companion, when you do not sell anything to Tulawas until you have measured it."
2822,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Buy something and do not sell it until you measure it."
2823,"Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah gave him one dinar one day and said, \Buy a sacrificial animal from it.\"" He bought a sacrificial animal for one dinar", when he sold it for two dinars," then he bought a sacrificial animal for one dinar."""
2824,"Narrated Urwa bin Abul Ja'd: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the merchants' caravan, he gave one dinar to a companion and ordered him to buy a goat for me. So he went and bought two goats for one dinar. When they came with a goat, the Prophet said, May Allah bless your deal. The narrator says (it used to be the case that) I used to stand in a bazaar of Kufa and perform Kamaliya for forty thousand."
2825,"Narrated by Sayyidna Urwa bin Abul Jaid, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the caravan of merchants, so he gave me one dinar. He said, O Urwa, go to those merchants and get a goat from them for one dinar. The narrator says: I went to these merchants and bought two goats for one dinar. Then I brought one goat and one dinar and came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your goat and this is your dinar. Then the Prophet inquired, what have you done? So I narrated the entire incident to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said, \O Allah"," bless his deal.\"" The narrator says"," I remember this very well about myself."""
2826,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade bidding.
2827,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates, I heard a man narrating, his name was Shahr, he was a merchant. He asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, about the auction, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, inquired that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a person to take usury on his brother's bargain (he cannot do this until someone else leaves it), except for the order of booty and inheritance. is different."
2828,This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar.
2829,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: I bought olive oil in the market, and a man came to me and asked me to give him a higher profit. They do not take it home, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it to be done in this way."
2830,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2831,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I bought olive oil from the market, when I was making a deal, a man met me and he offered me a higher profit. If the bargain is to be sold at the same place from where it was bought, this cannot be done until the person who trades takes it to his place."
2832,Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of the fruit of a tree until it is ready for use.
2833,"Yunus narrates, I inquired from Shaykh Abu Nad about the traditions mentioned about selling the fruit before it is ripe. Arwah bin Zubair, Sayyidna Sahl bin Hatmah, Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) quoted this statement. Earlier, people used to trade fruit before it was ripe. When such cases appeared in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in abundance, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised those people and said, \Do not sell the fruit until it is ripe.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said this because there were many disputes and cases These words of the hadith are from the narrator named Aburdad", Sheikh Abu Dawud, may God have mercy on him," says these words that the fruit has become diseased."""
2834,"Sayyidna Saeed bin Musaib narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that usury is only in gold, silver, measured, weighed, eaten and drunk things. Imam Darqutni (may Allah have mercy on him) says that this hadith is transmitted and a narrator named Shaykh Mubarak has narrated it as a hadith transmitted to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Imam Malik."
2835,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of fruit until it is ready for consumption.
2836,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to sell fruits before they are ripe, unless it is clear whether the fruit will be white or red. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling the milk in the udder and also the wool (on the back of the animal)."
2837,"Sayyidina Abdullah bin Abbas narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit until it is ready to eat, and he also forbade the sale of the wool on the animal's back, the milk in the udder, and the ghee in the milk. A narrator named Waqiyyah has quoted it according to a Mursal tradition with reference to a narrator named Umar Bin Farrukh."
2838,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Do not sell the milk in the udder and do not sell the wool on the back of the animal. This tradition is discontinued.
2839,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade the sale of what is in the wombs of animals until they give birth, and he forbade the sale of booty until it is divided, and he forbade the sale of charity until it is divided, and he forbade the sale of what comes out after diving."
2840,Sayyiduna Ikrima narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the milk in the udder to be sold for the ghee in the udder.
2841,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade giving allegiance. A narrator named Ayyub has described this. A narrator named Yahya has explained Baighar. He says that Baighar includes trading what the diver brings out after diving. Baighar includes trading a runaway slave or a runaway camel or trading what is in the stomach of animals or trading what comes out of minerals. Or what is in the udders of animals should be traded.
2842,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of gharar and pebbles.
2843,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hanzala (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that one dirham of usury that a person eats and eats intentionally is more serious (i.e. worse) for him than committing adultery thirty-six times. This tradition is also transmitted along with a chain of transmission, but it is not transmitted as a hadith."
2844,"Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that if I commit adultery thirty times, that is more pleasing to me than if I eat a dirham of usury, of which, may Allah know that I ate it, I took it, it was usury. Imam Darqutni (may Allah have mercy on him) says that this hadith is more authentic than the mentioned hadith."
2845,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Hanzalah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that one dirham of usury is a greater sin in the sight of Allah than committing fornication thirty-six times by mistake.
2846,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sold a free man who was bankrupt.
2847,"Abd al-Rahman bin Mut'am narrates that my partner bought some dirhams in half, so I said: This is not right, so the man said: I have sold them in the market and no one objected to it. There is nothing wrong with borrowing that will not be fine. You should inquire with Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, for he is the most knowledgeable of all of us about the issues of trade."
2848,"Shaykh Abu Minhal, Sayyidna Bara and Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam narrate this matter. (That is, dirhams or dinars are being paid on both sides)."
2849,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Sayyidna Sawad bin Ghaziyya, who belonged to Bani Adi. He did not say, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have bought good dates for two Sa's and two Sa's for three Sa's. Imam Dar al-Qatni, may God bless him and grant him peace, says that every type of date palm that does not have a specific name is called a collection: It is like there is a collection (of different types of dates) in the land of so-and-so."
2850,This hadith is narrated by Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad bin Abdul Majeed bin Suhail along with another chain of transmission.
2851,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri.
2852,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah and Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA).
2853,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the thing that is weighed should be equal when both of them have the same oath, and when something is found, it should be the same, but when the oaths on both sides are different, then there is nothing wrong with that. The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) with regard to other isnads."
2854,"Shaykh Abu Ash'ath narrates that he was present at the sermon of Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit, may God be pleased with him. He narrates that I heard him narrate that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates that gold should be sold for gold, but it can be done with an equal weight, and silver can be exchanged for silver, but it can be done with an equal weight. He ordered to sell dates for wheat and dates, and salt for salt, and then explained that there is no problem in trading barley for wheat as long as it is hand-to-hand and whatever is more in it, but this transaction should be hand-to-hand, except in cases where the more he gives or takes, it will act as usury. A narrator named Abdullah narrates: I narrated this hadith to my father, and he considered it to be good."
2855,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when there is a dispute between the seller and the buyer, and both of them do not have any evidence, the seller will be sworn in, then the buyer has the choice whether to sell it or not."
2856,"Abdul Malik bin Ubaydah narrates: I was with Abu Ubaydah bin Abdullah two men came to him and they traded one thing and they said: I have bought this thing for so much. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed about the seller, that an oath should be taken from him, after which the buyer will have the right to acquire the item according to the seller's statement and to abandon it if he wishes."
2857,"Abdul Malik bin Jubeer narrates: I was with Abu Ubaidah, the son of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, and two men came to him. They had traded something. One of them said: I have bought this thing for so much. The other said: I have sold this thing for so much. I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when such a case was brought before him, and he ordered that the seller should take an oath, and then the buyer would be given this option whether he took it from him or left it. This tradition is also present along with another document."
2858,"Abd al-Rahman bin Qays narrates this message from his grandfather regarding his father. Sayyidna Ash'ath bin Qais bought a slave from Khums for twenty thousand dirhams from Sayyidna Abdullah. Sayyidna Abdullah gave this message about its price. He said: I have bought it for ten thousand dirhams. Abdullah said: Name someone who can decide between you and me. Sayyidna Ash'at said: You will decide between me and you. It has been heard that when there is a dispute between the parties to the deal and there is no proof between them, then the statement of the owner of the goods will be valid or both of them should abandon the deal."
2859,This tradition is transmitted as a muqaf hadith along with another chain of transmission.
2860,"Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud sold a government slave for twenty thousand, that is, he brought ten thousand to Sayyidna Ash'ath bin Qays, then Sayyidna Abdullah said: I sold it to you for twenty two thousand, then Ash'at said: I did it for ten thousand. I am narrating to you a hadith narrated on the authority of the Messenger of Allah."
2861,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when there is a difference between the two parties to the transaction, the seller's statement will be valid, but if the item has been lost, then the buyer's statement will be valid. The narrator of this tradition, Hasan bin Amara, is obsolete."
2862,"Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him) when there is a dispute between the two parties about the transaction and the goods are in the same state and have not perished, then the seller's statement will be valid or else both of them will terminate the transaction."
2863,The same tradition is also narrated in another document.
2864,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2865,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when there is a dispute between the two men who have traded and the goods sold have been lost, then the seller's statement will be valid. He has narrated this tradition as a marfu' hadith."
2866,"Qasim bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud sold a government slave to Ash’ath. They had a dispute about the price. Sayyidna Abdullah said: I sold it to you for twenty thousand. Sayyidna Ash’at said: I bought it from you for ten thousand. Sayyidna Ash'ath said: Sayyidna Abdullah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that when there is a dispute between two parties to a transaction and the goods sold are in their original condition and both parties do not have any evidence, then the seller's statement will be valid, or both of them will terminate the transaction. Sayyidna Ash'at said: finish"
2867,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bundle of leaves from a villager. When a deal was made, the Prophet said to him, “You have the power (that if you wish, you can terminate it).” The man said to the Prophet (peace be upon him): May Allah bless your deal. In one hadith, these words are said: The villager said to the Holy Prophet: May Allah settle your business. All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
2868,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) bought something from a villager. I think he was related to Banu Umar bin Sa’sa’ah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bunch of leaves from him. When the deal was made, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “You can take it if you want.” The villager said: I have not seen such a deal till today, may God Almighty Keep your deals settled! Which tribe do you belong to? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is from Quraysh."
2869,"Taus narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a bunch of leaves from a villager, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the villager the right to terminate the deal if he wished. The narrator has quoted as per previous tradition."
2870,"A narrator named Amr has narrated this. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was riding a camel that did not enter Q Abu. It was owned by his father. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar could not pass Q Abu on it. That camel went ahead of the Prophet's camel. Later, he reprimanded him, but that camel did not enter Q Abu. The Prophet (PBUH) said, \O Umar! Sell me. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought it. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and said"," \""This is yours. Now treat him as you wish.\"" These words of tradition are from a narrator named Ibn Ibad."""
2871,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Barira entered into a contract of writing for herself in exchange for paying Nawaqiyya every year. She came to Sayya Ayesha Siddiqa to help her in this matter. Tusaida Ayesha said, \No", if you want, I will pay the whole thing at once," but I will have the right to your walaa.\"" He said: That the right of Wala will remain with them. She came to Sayyida Aisha. Meanwhile", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. Tubira told Sayyida Aisha in a low voice all the things that she had said to her owners (and the answer they had given). This is what Tusayda Aisha said: No, and I will have the right of Wala, (so I am ready for this matter). Aisha said," \""O Messenger of Allah", Barirah came to me to seek my help regarding her contract of writing. I said: If the owners want," I will pay them all together and the right of ownership will remain with me.\"" He attains that which liberates. Sayyida Aisha narrates) So I bought him and set him free. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up while giving a sermon to the people", praising Allah and saying: What has happened to the people? The condition that Allah has allowed will be stronger. What has happened to the people, they say that you free so-and-so and the right of ownership will remain with me. The right of ownership belongs to the person who frees. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Berira's husband was a slave," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Berira authority."""
2872,"Abdul Wahid bin Ayman narrates this statement of his father: I came to the service of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, I said to her: O Umm al-Mu'minin, I was with Utbah bin Abulhab, (i.e. I was his slave). So he said, \O my son", I came to Berira. He had made a contract for writing. He said: You buy me. I said: OK. He said: My owners will not sell me until they impose the condition of my walaa. So I said: Then I have no need for you. When the Prophet heard this or it was reported to him, he inquired what Barira was saying. I told you about it. He said," \""You buy him and set him free", and let these people remain as they are," and impose whatever conditions they wish.\"" (Sayyida Aisha) So I bought him and set him free", then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""The right of the freedman belongs to the one who frees him"," even if (the people of the other side) impose such conditions.\"""""
2873,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Basheer Saghir had a special place where he used to sit next to the Prophet (PBUH) regularly. Once, the Prophet (PBUH) did not visit him for three days (after three days). I have not seen you for the last three days, so they said, \My parents are sacrificed to you. I bought a camel from such and such a person. He stayed with me", and after that he became rebellious and ran away. I went after him, (caught him) and handed him over to his owner," so he took him from me.\"" He said"," \""Don't you know that rebellious animals are returned on the same basis?\"""""
2874,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a tradition similar to this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The rebellious camel is returned.
2875,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I used to trade camels in Baqi, sometimes I would sell them for dinars, and I would receive dirhams instead of dinars, and sometimes I would sell them for dirhams and receive dinars instead of dirhams, which would take its place, and he used to give it away. I said, O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you a question. I trade camels for profit. Sometimes I sell them for dinars but receive dirhams. Sometimes I sell them for dirhams and receive dinars. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \There is nothing wrong with it if you continue to take it according to the price of that day until the two of you separate or there is no agreement between you.\"" There is some difference in wording in one tradition."""
2876,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt can only be sold hand-to-hand. be)."
2877,"Muammar bin Abdullah narrates that he sent his slave with a saa of wheat and said: Sell him a saa and bring what he bought through it. The slave went and received a saa and a little more than a saa when he came and told them about it. Umar said: Why did you do this? Go and return it and give only equal religion, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Grain for grain. What they meant was that it can only be taken equally, which was our food in those days. The slave said: These are not like it. Toumamar said: I am afraid that they are equal to it."
2878,"It is narrated about Muammar bin Abdullah that he sent his slave with a saa of wheat and said: Sell him a saa and bring what he bought with it. The slave went and received a saa and a little more than a saa when he came and told him about it. Umar said: Why did you interfere with it? Go and return it and give only equal religion, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that grain can only be exchanged for grain. The narrator says that our diet used to be in those days, he said to Muammar: He said that they are not like him, so he said, I think that they are like him."
2879,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the one who takes usury and the one who gives it are equal (sinners).
2880,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the dinar will be exchanged for the dinar, and the dirham will be exchanged for the dirham for an additional payment."
2881,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said on the occasion of the Farewell Hajj that a Muslim is the brother of another Muslim, for him the blood of his brother or anything from his property is not halal, except what he gives to him according to his choice. Beware! Have I preached? The people said: Yes, the Prophet said, O Allah, be a witness."
2882,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that no one should become a companion to his brother until he gives it to him of his own free will.
2883,"Sayyidna Amr bin Yathirbi narrates that I was present with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the farewell Hajj in Mina. The narrator says) I said at that time, O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about this if I find my cousin's goats in front of me and take one of them and slaughter it, will there be any sin on me in this regard? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If you come across a goat and at that time you have a knife in your hand and something to bind your hands and feet"," do not touch that goat.\"""""
2884,"Sayyidna Amr bin Yathirbi narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while giving a sermon to us, said, \Beware that the wealth of his brother is not lawful for any Muslim"," except that which he himself chooses to give.\"" That goat is found in Virana) and at that time you picked up the knife and the equipment for tying the goat", but you could not touch it. Imam Darqutni (may God have mercy on him) says that it has been stated that (Khubat al-Hamish) is a place between Makkah and its suburbs," it is a place where there is no population."""
2885,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that it is permissible for any Muslim to take wealth only by his will.
2886,Sayyiduna Abu Hira al-Raqashi narrates the statement of his uncle that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the wealth of any Muslim can be taken only by his will.
2887,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
2888,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the wealth of a believer is as respectable as his life.
2889,"Abdullah Bin Ka'b narrates this statement of his father, once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and he was confused with one of his debtors. He said, O Messenger of Allah, this is my debt. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired if you do not do this, that is, you should receive half from him. He said this through his blessed hand, and I said yes! O Messenger of Allah, he received half of the share, and left half of the share (the narrator doubts that perhaps the word half has been transferred instead of Shatar in the hadith)."
2890,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the Muslims will act according to the terms of each other and peace between Muslims is permissible. These words of tradition are from a narrator named Yunus, while other narrators have quoted the word, between people."
2891,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that reconciliation between Muslims is permissible.
2892,Kathir bin Abdullah narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather: The conditions prescribed by the Muslims (will be fulfilled) except for a condition that makes a lawful thing haram or makes a haram thing lawful.
2893,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa cites this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2894,Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the conditions of the Muslims will be obeyed as long as they are in accordance with the truth.
2895,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charity of a deer is what a man spends on his life on his wife. be done or spent in any sinful act. The narrator says, I inquired from Muhammad bin Mankader, what is meant by this, that a man should protect his honor through it? So he said that he should pay a poet or a foul-mouthed man (so that he would not be rude to him)."
2896,Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a person who finds his property with a person should take it and the other person will demand it from the person from whom he bought it.
2897,"Sayyidna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if a person finds his property with a certain person, he will be more entitled to that property and the other person will go to the person from whom he bought it."
2898,"Sayyidna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the person who is found to have property in a certain way, he will be more entitled to that property and the person who bought it will go to the person who sold it."
2899,"Sayyiduna Samrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if a person finds his property in possession of a particular person, he is more entitled to that property, and the person who had that property will go after the person from whom he bought the property."
2900,"Umar Ibn Khaldah Ansari narrates that we came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Huraira about one of our companions who had been declared bankrupt due to illness. Sayyidna Abu Huraira said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had given this decision about a person who had passed away and was bankrupt. which forms part of this partner)."
2901,"Ibn Khaldah Zarqi, who was a judge of Madinah Munawarah, narrates that we came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, about one of our companions who had become bankrupt, so Sayyidna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that this is a matter about which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has given a ruling that a person who dies or is declared bankrupt, and then the owner of a certain property finds his property with him, he will be more entitled to that property."
2902,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) who sells an item, then his partner is declared bankrupt, and the first person finds his item in his possession, and the first person did not receive anything from the price of the item, then the item will be given to that person, but if he had received some of the price, then he will be considered like other creditors."
2903,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a person who sells an item and then goes to a particular person who has been declared bankrupt, and the seller has not received any of its value, then the item will be given to that person, but if he has received some of its value, he will be counted as the other creditors. A narrator named Yaman bin Adi has quoted these words, if this person has paid some of its price, then that other person will be counted like the rest of the debtors."
2904,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same with regard to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but these words are added. \A person who dies having the property of another person", whether that person has received any money from his compensation or not," he will be counted like other creditors\"". A narrator named Yaman bin Adi has disputed its authenticity."""
2905,This tradition is narrated along with another document. A narrator named Yaman bin Adi is weak in hadith.
2906,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \When a person becomes bankrupt and a seller finds the property in his possession"," he will have more rights to the property than other creditors.\"""""
2907,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever finds his wealth in the possession of a person who has been declared bankrupt, then he will be more entitled to this wealth than others.” The meaning is the same."
2908,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you sell a fruit to your brother and some calamity befalls that fruit, then it is not permissible for you to take the wealth of your brother without any right."
2909,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If you sell some fruit to your brother and some calamity befalls him, then it is not permissible for you to receive any compensation for it. The narrator narrates that I inquired from my teacher Abu Zubair that there are these words in the hadeeth which Aih? So they did not answer."
2910,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, it also has the same words. So he said: No."
2911,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever buys (or sells) fruit and a heavenly calamity befalls him, then he does not take anything from it, on what basis will you receive your brother’s property without any right?”"
2912,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a reduction in compensation for the loss caused by a calamity, and he forbade bargaining for a later payment of several years."
2913,"Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says about a person who pledges something and then it is lost. Sayyidna Umar (RA) says: If it is less than what he was pledged, he will return his full right, and if it is more than that, he will be a trustee."
2914,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned something (regarding a reduction in compensation) due to calamity. Sufyan says I don't know how much reduction you ordered.
2915,"Saeed bin Musaib narrates that the slave of Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA) was declared bankrupt, and he was brought to Sayyidna Uthman (RA), then Sayyidna Uthman (RA) gave this decision about him: The person who received some of his right before he became bankrupt became his, and the person who found his property with him will be more entitled to this property."
2916,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the pledged thing is fully (considered as pledge).
2917,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \The pledge is considered as a pledge in its entirety.\"""""
2918,"Sayyiduna Anas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pledged thing is with whatever is in it. The narrator of Ismail used to fabricate this hadith, and the narration of this hadith by Qatadah and Hamad bin Salamah is invalid, and God knows best."
2919,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the mortgage is not closed (to the one with whom it is placed), he will receive its benefits and the ransom will also be the responsibility of that person."
2920,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2921,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the mortgage is not closed for the person with whom it is kept, he will get the benefit of it and his ransom will be his responsibility."
2922,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) that the mortgage is not foreclosed, but the person will take the benefit of it and you will have to pay for it."
2923,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a mortgage is not closed, a person takes advantage of it and the ransom is his responsibility."
2924,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same with regard to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
2925,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A mortgage is not closed, you will get the benefit of it and you will be responsible for paying for it."
2926,"Saeed bin Musaib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the mortgage is not closed, the person takes the benefit and the ransom is his responsibility."
2927,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the mortgage is not closed, the mortgage is with the person with whom it is placed, that person takes advantage of it and the ransom is also his responsibility."
2928,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when a horse is pawned, a person can ride on it by paying the expenses, similarly when an animal is pawned, he can milk it."
2929,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when an animal is pledged, the person with whom it is pledged will be responsible for its fodder."
2930,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that one can ride on a mortgaged animal and milk it.
2931,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that the pledged thing is considered as a pledge in its entirety.
2932,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave me a shield jointly with Ammar and Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. He made us sharers in the things we had taken from the booty of the idolaters.
2933,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Allah says, “I am with two partners until one of them betrays the other, then when he betrays, I leave between them (i.e., My mercy does not remain with them)."
2934,"Abu Hiyaan Taymi narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Allah's grace is upon two partners as long as one of them does not betray his partner."
2935,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, \Whoever has entrusted you with a trust", return it to him, and whoever has betrayed you," do not betray him.\"""""
2936,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: To the person who has entrusted you, repay the trust to the person who has betrayed you, do not betray him."
2937,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever entrusts you with a trust, pay back the trust and whoever betrays you," do not betray him.\"""""
2938,"Arwa narrated that there was a dispute between two men belonging to the Ansar about a piece of land. One of them had planted a palm tree there and the land was the property of the other. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision that the land would be given to its owner. Nothing can be (forced) on the land of The narrator says that the person who narrated this tradition to me said that he had seen this palm tree which was very tall and whose roots had been cut by an axe. These words of the hadith are not for an oppressor, it means that you go into someone else's land and start farming there (ie do it without his consent)."
2939,"Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade muhaqla and muzabnah. He (PBUH) said: “There are three types of farming: One is when a person owns land and he cultivates it, a person who is given land as a gift and cultivates it, and a person who rents land in exchange for gold and silver (then he can cultivate it)."
2940,"Hanzalah bin Qais Zarqi narrates that he asked Sayyidna Rafi bin Khadij about renting land, and he said, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting land.\"" So he said"," there is no problem in giving it in exchange for gold and silver."""
2941,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade giving land on rent, except in exchange for gold and silver (land can be given on rent)."
2942,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa that once the Prophet (PBUH) was going on a journey and he saw a field that was flourishing. Calculate what you have spent in that land and then take it from the owner of the land and hand over that person's land and his field to him.
2943,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber and the palm groves there to the Jews so that they (the Muslims) would pay half of it.
2944,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khaybar to the people living there on the condition that they would pay half (to the Muslims) of the produce there, be it fruit or agriculture."
2945,"There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed with the people of Khyber that whatever produce there would be, be it fruit or agriculture (they would pay half of it to the Muslims)."
2946,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), people used to buy and sell fruits. When it was time to harvest, the debt collector would come and the one who had to pay would say that this time the produce has suffered such and such a disaster. Cultivate till the fruit is ripe and ready. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this as an advice because there was a lot of disagreement among the people about it."
2947,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) agreed with the people of Khyber that they would pay half of the production of dates and crops produced there to the Muslims. The narrators have disagreed about one word of the tradition.
2948,It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar that he narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the Jews living in Khaybar to work on the lands there on the condition that they would pay half of the produce (to the Muslims) and these portions were fixed.
2949,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber and the palm groves there (to the Jews) on the condition of paying half of the produce. In a tradition, these words were given to the Jews by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
2950,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the land of Khyber (to the Jews) on the condition that they would pay a half share of dates, agriculture, produce and all other (kinds of produce)."
2951,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) temporarily took some armor and weapons from Safwan bin Umayyah on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It is taken temporarily"," which will be returned.\"""""
2952,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) borrowed some weapons from Safwan bin Umayyah, and Safwan asked if it will be returned, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
2953,"Safwan bin Ya'ali narrates the statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when my messenger comes to you, give him this thing. The narrator says, I think he mentioned thirty thousand and thirty camels. Sayyidna Ya'ali bin Umayyah says that I asked, are you taking a loan that will be returned? So the Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
2954,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another document, in which there are these words: I asked, O Messenger of Allah, should you temporarily take those whose ransom will be paid? Or are they taking it temporarily so that they will be returned? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, they will be returned."
2955,"Umayyah bin Safwan narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him to borrow some armor on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, so he said, “O Sayyidna Muhammad! What are usurping? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said no, but they are taking them temporarily for which a ransom will also be paid. The narrator narrates that some of his armors were damaged, so the Prophet offered him to take their ransom, so he said that now I have been attracted to Islam and I am more interested in it."
2956,"Umayya bin Safwan narrates that his father narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed some iron armor from me, so I asked, O Messenger of Allah, are they guaranteed? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \These are collaterals. Some of them were lost", so the Prophet said to them, 'If you want," I will give you its ransom.'\"""""
2957,"Ata has narrated with reference to some people belonging to the family of Abdullah bin Safwan that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Safwan, do you have any weapons? He said, are you taking it temporarily or will you usurp it? After this, the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith."
2958,"A narrator named Abdul Aziz has narrated on the authority of Ata with reference to some people belonging to the family of Sayyiduna Safwan that the Prophet (peace be upon him) temporarily took (some weapons). After that, the narrator mentioned the previous hadith."
2959,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \What is temporarily taken will be returned"," and what is given as a donation (for temporary use) will be returned.\"" So a person said: Is this the decision of the Messenger of Allah? So he said"," \""This is the decision of Allah"," who has the right to fulfill it.\"""""
2960,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) say this during his sermon on the occasion of Hajj Al-Wadaa: Allah has determined the right of every possessor, therefore a will cannot be made for an heir. Allah Ta'ala will continue to be cursed by His angels and all humans until the Day of Resurrection. A woman should not spend anything from her husband's house without his permission. It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, not even grain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It is our most important wealth.\"" Then he said"," \""What is given for temporary use will be returned", and what is given as a gift for temporary use will also be returned, the duty will be paid," and the person in charge will be obliged to pay the ransom.\"""""
2961,Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who is entrusted with a trust will not be required to pay a ransom.
2962,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to his father, \Don't make me a witness about adultery.\"""""
2963,"Sayyidna Nu'man (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that his mother said to his father Sayyidna Bashir: That he should give his son Nu'man a garden of dates, so Sayyidna Bashir did so, then he asked who should I make a witness about this? So this woman said: To the Holy Prophet, Sayyiduna Nu'man's father came to the Prophet's service and mentioned this to him. The Holy Prophet said, \Do you have any other children besides him?\"" He said yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""Have you given it to everyone else in the same way as you have given it to him?\"" He said no! So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""A person like me cannot be a witness to such a thing. Allah", the Exalted, likes that you act justly towards your children," just as He likes that you act justly among yourselves.\"""""
2964,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that my father gave me a slave as a gift and my mother instructed me to go with him to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so that I could make him a witness on this matter. They said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then take it back.\"""""
2965,This hadith is also narrated along with another document.
2966,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) that a person called him and wanted to make him a witness regarding his will, so he preferred some of his children over other children in the will, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) has forbidden us to be witnesses in an act of transgression. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (R.A.) walked quickly."
2967,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) both narrate this as a valid hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is not permissible for any Muslim to take something back after making a donation, but he can take back what he gives to his children. It is like one who licks his own vomit again after vomiting."
2968,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: No one can take back what he has given to him, only the father can take back (what was given to him) from his children. The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but there is some wording difference in it. And this hadith is narrated as Mursal Hadith along with a chain of transmission which has these words: A father can take back his Hiba (from his children)."
2969,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) who does something wrong, then he is more entitled to that thing as long as he does not take any retribution for it. This hadith is not authentically proved to be authentic, but it is true that it is transmitted as a suspended tradition from Sayyiduna Umar on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar."
2970,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a man is more entitled to his reward until he takes any revenge for it.
2971,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the one who gives a bribe is more entitled to his bribe as long as he does not take any retribution for it.
2972,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2973,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says, \A man is more entitled to his reward until he receives any reward for it.\"""""
2974,"Sayyidna Samrah narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that when a man gives a gift to a relative, he should not take it back. The narrator named Abdullah bin Jafar is unique in narrating this tradition."
2975,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who gives something and then wants to take it back, then he will be more entitled to that thing as long as he does not take any revenge for it, but his example will be like a dog that licks its own vomit."
2976,"Sayyidna Tariq bin Abdullah Moharibi (RA) narrates that I visited the Prophet (PBUH) twice. Once I saw him in the market of Dhul Majaz. I was there with my goods which I had kept there for sale. Similarly, when the Prophet (PBUH) passed by, he was wearing a red halwa and he was saying in a loud voice, O people! A man was walking behind you holding a stone, the person who had seriously injured you was saying, O people, do not listen to them because they are lying, so I asked who is this sir? So people said that this is a young man from the descendants of Abdul Muttalib. People said that it was his uncle Abd al-Azi (says the narrator) it was Abul Hab. Then when Islam prevailed and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, we came with some horsemen from Rabdah and the southern areas of Rabdah, and we camped near Madinah. There was a woman with us. We replied from Rabdah and the narrator from the southern areas of Rabdah says that we had red camels with us. They inquired whether you will sell your camels. So we answered yes, they inquired, for how much? We said: In exchange for so many sa's of dates, they did not ask us to make any reduction. Then they took hold of the camel's head and went inside the city and disappeared from our sight. We began to blame each other. I have seen a thing (which proves it) that they will not disgrace you. I have not seen the face of any person like that. You look more like the fourteenth moon than a young one. Then when it was time for Isha, a person came to us and said, \Peace be upon you. I am the messenger of Allah's Messenger who has come to you. He has instructed you to eat your fill of these dates and measure them completely.\"" The next day we entered the city of Madinah", and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing on the pulpit and giving a sermon to the people. He was saying: The giving hand is the upper hand and you start the spending on the person who is under your care, your mother, your father, your sister, your brother and your closest loved one. Then an Ansari stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah, this Banu Taalba," who killed such and such a person in the time of Jahiliyyah. He will not pay ransom on behalf of his children."""
2977,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever makes a cash transaction for something, he should not make any change (in the thing given) as payment. Ibrahim bin Saeed says that means he should receive the same thing for which he made a cash deal or pay the same compensation on the condition of which he made a cash deal."
2978,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says (the narrator says: I think this is the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW)) When you buy a Salaf, do not sell it further until you measure it completely."
2979,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that the person who pledges allegiance to Salaf should not impose the condition of paying anything other than the agreed payment.
2980,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Banunazir to leave Madinah, some of his people came to serve him and said: We have some duties that have not yet been returned."
2981,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
2982,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that when the Prophet (PBUH) ordered Banun Nazir to be exiled, he said, O Sayyidna Muhammad! We want to take some loans from people, so he said, forgive them and leave here quickly."
2983,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says that when the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended to evict Banunazir (from Medina), he said, \O Messenger of God", you have ordered us to evacuate," while we are about to take loans from people that have not yet been received.\"""""
2984,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a funeral was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he did not ask about his deeds, but only asked about his debt. When you stood up, you asked your companions whether your companion has any debt. The people asked for two dinars, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from there. He said, \You should perform the funeral prayer for your companion.\"" Sayyiduna Ali", may God be pleased with him, said," \""O Messenger of God"," it is my responsibility to pay for both of them. This person is free from both of them.\"" Just as you have removed the trouble of your brother", whoever dies and owes him a debt, then he is pledged in exchange for that debt, and whoever removes the trouble of the debt of a dead person, Allah will remove the trouble of that person on the Day of Resurrection. So someone asked, is this a special order for Sayyiduna Ali or for all Muslims? He said," \""Rather"," it is for all Muslims.\"""""
2985,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (hire) Nirjanur for a couple.
2986,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that grapes should not be sold until they are ripe, and grapes should not be sold until their seeds are ready."
2987,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabnah and forbade that fresh dates should be measured and sold in exchange for dry dates.
2988,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (selling) fresh dates instead of dry dates.
2989,Salim narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of dry dates for fresh dates.
2990,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Muhakla, Muzabnah, Mukhabara, and forbade Sunya, but if there is knowledge about it (then the ruling will be different)."
2991,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade trading in an unknown thing until one is aware of it.
2992,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade fruits until they are ripe and ready, and do not trade fruits for dates. A"
2993,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade the likes of him.
2994,Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the lending of dry dates in exchange for dry dates. There is some disagreement about the wording of this tradition.
2995,"Abdullah bin Yazid narrates that Shaykh Abu Ayyash asked Sayyidna Sa'd about two types of wheat (whether they can be traded with each other), then Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) declared it abominable. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about it that when it dries up, it decreases."
2996,"Abdullah bin Zayd narrates that Sheikh Abu Ayyash Zayd told him that he once asked Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) about two types of wheat: Sayyidna Sa'd asked him which of the two types is better. So they replied white ones, then Sayyidna Sa'd (RA) forbade them from doing so. Sayyidna Sa'd said that I asked the Prophet (PBUH) to curse him. People answered yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
2997,"Sheikh Abu Ayyash narrates that during the time of Sayyidna Sa'd, men made a deal about two types of barley. Sayyidna Sa'd said that in the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), two men made a deal of dry and fresh dates. The people replied yes, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Then it is not true)."
2998,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever buys and sells with another, each of them will have the right (to terminate the transaction) until they separate from their place, except in the case where the authority has been given in the transaction, and it is not permissible for a person to separate from his partner under the fear that he will terminate the transaction. will"
2999,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
3000,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement from his father: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and asked him about a person in the state of Ihram who has intercourse with his wife. He pointed to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and said, \Go to him and ask him.\"" The man asked if I should sit down now. He said: No", you go with the people, people who work, you should do the same. Next year, you should come and perform Hajj and bring the sacrificial animal with you. The man came back to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and told him about it. Sayyidna Abdullah said to him," \""You go to Sayyidna Abbas", may God be pleased with him," and ask him.\"" So Sayyidna Abbas also answered in the same way that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had answered him. That person came back to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr and told him about what Sayyidna Abbas had answered. Then the person inquired what do you say about it? So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar said"," I also give the same answer as what he has described."""
3001,"Muhammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naqqāsh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Tamīm narrated to us; he said: I said to Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī: ""Shuʿayb, the father of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, did he hear from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said to him: ""Then ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather — people criticize this?"" He said: ""I saw ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, al-Ḥumaydī, and Isḥāq ibn Rāhwayh citing it as evidence."" I said: ""Then what do those who criticize it say?"" He said: ""They say: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated excessively, or words to that effect."""
3002,"Yunus bin Ishaq narrates this statement of his mother Aaliyah, I and Umm Qahba Khatoon went to Makkah. We replied, \We belong to Kufa. Now Aaliyah is narrating. It is as if Ayesha did not pay attention to us", and Qahbah said to her: O Umm al-Mu'minin, I have a slave girl. I bought her from Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam Ansari for eight hundred dirhams until he was paid. Then when he decided to sell this slave girl, I bought her for six hundred dirhams in cash. Narrator Khatun narrates that Sayyida Aisha turned to us and said," \""You have done a great deal. You should go and tell Zayd that he has ruined the Jihad he had done with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). However", if he repents," the order will be different. So this lady said to Sayida Aisha: What do you think if I receive my original money from him?\"" \""Whoever comes to an admonition from his Lord and turns away before it has already happened"," it will be his.\"" Shaykh states that the women named Qahba and Aaliyah are unknown and their tradition cannot be presented as evidence."""
3003,"Shaykh Abu Ishaq Subi'i narrates the statement of his wife. She came to the service of Sayyida Aisha. She was accompanied by the mother of Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam Ansari, and there was another woman. Tusideh Aisha said, \You have made a very bad deal. What happened to him (sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam) with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is nullified until he repents (then the ruling will be different)."""
3004,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) prescribed tribute according to time.
3005,"Sayyidna Mukhlid bin Khafaf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a slave was jointly owned by some people and they sold him. One of the partners was absent. When he came and he refused to accept the deal, those people brought their case to Hisham bin Ismail. He gave a decision that the deal would be declared null and void and those people would deal according to the rate of that day and tribute would be collected. Two slaves were sold for this slave. I went to the service of Urwa bin Zubayr and mentioned this to him, and he said, Sayyida Aisha narrated this hadith to me."
3006,"Hamza bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father, whatever is alive and accumulated at the time of the transaction will be considered as part of the property of the buyer."
3007,"It is narrated about Talha bin Yazid that he discussed some deals with Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I have not found anything for you that is more comprehensive than what the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave to Hibban bin Munqar. His eyesight was weak, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him permission to cancel the deal for three days. He will keep it and if he likes it, he will take it, if he doesn't like it, he will abandon it."
3008,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyidna Safwan bin Munqar was an old man who had an injury on his head. Because of this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him the authority to terminate the deal for three days. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I heard him saying that he used to say Khadaba instead of Khalaba."
3009,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a person who used to buy and sell, and his mental state was found to be defective. Once his family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Prophet of Allah, stop such and such a person from taking possession because he makes a deal, but there is some weakness in his mental state. He said, \I cannot make a living without buying and selling.\"" The Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him, said," \""If you must buy and sell"," do it.\"""""
3010,"The first hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you must buy and sell, then he said: Do it as it is in exchange for him and there will be no deception. A narrator named Abdul Wahab says that means people will not suffer any loss for him."
3011,"Nafi narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) told him that an Ansari had a stutter in his tongue and he always made a loss in dealings with him. It is narrated about Sayyidna Munqar bin Amr that he had an injury on his head which affected his language, and his mental state also changed somewhat. He used to trade and he always lost money in trade. You will have authority for three days, if after three days you agree, then keep it and if you don't like it, return it to the owner. The life of these Companions was very long. They lived for thirty-two years during the time of Sayyidna Uthman, when people spread everywhere and the number of people also increased, and there used to be a good deal in the market. At that time, they used to buy and sell in the market."
3012,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that the power lasts for three days.
3013,"Hibban bin Waseet narrates this statement of his father regarding his father, when Sayyiduna Umar was appointed as the caliph, he said: O people, I have examined this matter and I have found that the thing that is most similar to your deals in the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the authority, which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave to Hibban bin Munqidh for three days, and this incident happened regarding a slave."
3014,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that Makkah is Haram, it is forbidden to sell the land here and it is forbidden to rent the houses here."
3015,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Allah has appointed Makkah as a Haram. Selling the land here and its price is eating Ihram.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said that whoever eats anything from the rent of houses in Makkah will eat fire. Imam Abu Hanifah", may God have mercy on him, has narrated this tradition as a suspended tradition, but he has had an illusion in it. The second illusion he has had is that he has narrated the name of the narrator as Ubaidullah bin Abu Zayed," although he is Ibn Abi Ziyad."""
3016,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever eats the rent of the houses of Makkah puts fire in his stomach (this hadith is suspended).
3017,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says, “Whoever eats the rent of the houses of Makkah (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
3018,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Makkah, Manakh, the land here cannot be sold and the houses cannot be rented. The narrator named Ismail bin Ibrahim is weak, and no one else narrated this hadith except him."
3019,"Sayyidna Alqamah bin Nadla (RA) says that during the time of the Prophet (PBUH) and Sayyidna Umar (RA), whoever was in need would stay there, and whoever did not need it, he would let someone else stay there."
3020,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but this is added in it, it used to be the same during the era of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3021,"Sayyidna Alqamah bin Nadla (may God be pleased with him) Kanani narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet, Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar (may God be pleased with him), the houses of Makkah were given away to people and they were not sold."
3022,"Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him) when Makkah was conquered, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave safety to all except four men and two women. Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad bin Abu Sarh."
3023,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, when the Prophet (PBUH) left for Makkah, he said to Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA), call the Ansar and bring them! So they announced, O Ansar! Attend the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Ansar came as they had come under a pre-arranged meeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Go along this path. Whoever tries to come in front of you", kill him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed. Allah blessed him with victory. Then he went up to Safa and addressed the people. At that time (the Ansar) were in the lower part of the hill, one of them said to his companion: Now the love of his people has been highlighted in his heart and he has become attached to his town. The people of the Ansar told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this through revelation, and he said, O Ansar! You said this: Now the love of the nation has been highlighted in the heart of this gentleman and he has developed an attachment to his village. Then you said who am I? By Allah, I am indeed a servant of Allah and I am His Messenger. My life and my death are with you. The Ansar said, O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, we said this only out of fear that you, may God bless you," would not separate from us."""
3024,"Abdullah bin Rabah narrates that we went as a delegation to Sayyiduna Muawiyah (RA) and with us was Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) one of us would prepare the food and then invite his companions. On the occasion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with the army on the right side and on the left. When I called them, they came walking fast. Tomorrow, when these obscene people of Quraysh come before you, you have to grind them. We will meet you on Safa (hill). The narrator narrates that he signaled with his hand, the next day the person who tried to come for the contest was killed by Mard or the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was granted victory. If the Quraysh continue to be killed in this way, after today there will be no sign of the Quraysh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, whoever closes the door of his house is safe. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the Ansar said: Now the love of his people has become evident in his heart, and he has developed an attachment to his town, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) revealed several revelations about this. I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. I migrated to Allah and to you. My life and my death are with you."
3025,Sarq says: I had to give some property of a person (the narrator doubts that these are the words) I had to give a loan to a person. That person took me to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The two sons of Zayd bin Aslam have narrated it differently.
3026,"Abd al-Rahman and Abdullah, the sons of Zayd bin Aslam, narrate this on the authority of their father. They participated in a battle. They heard a person calling another person in a loud voice, O thief, O thief. So he told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me this name. I bought a camel from a villager, then I hid from him. I lost the value of the camel. The villager was looking for me, and people said to him: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and tell him about this. I bought a camel and then he hid from me. I could not find him. The Prophet said, \Look for him. The narrator narrates that this man found me and took me to the service of the Prophet. He said", O Messenger of Allah, this is the person who bought the camel from me and hid from me. The Prophet said, 'You pay the price.' It has been lost. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""You are a thief!\"" Then he said to the villager", you go and sell it in the market and get the price of your camel, so this villager made me stand in the market and the price I was charged, he asked the buyer, what are you going to do with it? He said I will free him," so this villager freed me."""
3027,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates: I saw an old man in Alexandria whose name was Sarq. I inquired what this name was. So they told me that this name was given to me by the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I will not give it up. So he said, I came to Madinah and I told the people that my wealth is coming. Those people made some deals with me. I had to pay them. That wealth was lost from me. Those people took me to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said, \You are a thief!\"" Then you sold me for four camels", these creditors asked the buyer what will you do with it? He told that I will free him, so these people said: We also need reward as much as you, so these people together freed me," but my name remained."""
3028,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked before entering Makkah, O Messenger of Allah, where will you stay or in your house? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has Aqeel (bin Abu Talib) left us any house (because) a disbeliever does not inherit a Muslim and a Muslim does not inherit a disbeliever."
3029,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, where will you camp tomorrow? If Allah willed (the narrators narrate) this is the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has Aqeel left anything for us as an inheritance (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
3030,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates, He said, O Messenger of Allah, will you stay in your house in Makkah? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Has Aqeel left us any desired place?\"" (The narrator narrates) Mr. Aqeel was the heir of Mr. Abu Talib. Ibn Shihab explains that the scholars take this meaning from this statement of Allah: \""Those who believed and migrated", Jihad is this verse up to this point," there is nothing in their Wilayat.\"""""
3031,"The same hadith is narrated from Zuhri, however, these words are added in it (the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), said: We will camp in Khaif Bani Kinana, where the Quraysh had taken an oath to remain steadfast in disbelief."
3032,"Abdullah bin Zayd narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father. Abdullah and Ubaidullah, the two sons of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) passed by Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) who was in Iraq (performing the duties of the governor). These two gentlemen were coming from the land of Iran. I wish I had something (the narrator doubts that maybe these are the words) I wish I had power over something (that I could give you) Yes, I have accumulated this wealth, take it, buy goods with it, when you go to Sayyidna Umar, then sell it, the profit is yours and pay the original amount to you Sayyidna Umar. The narrator narrates that when these two gentlemen appeared in the service of Amirul Momineen, he asked them if Abu Musa had treated the children of all the emigrants in the same way. They both answered no! So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, Ameerul Momineen will not declare it as valid, he gave it as a loan."
3033,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Companions of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when he gave something to a person, used to impose on him the condition that you will not give my property to any living being, do not take it on a sea voyage, do not take it and camp in a waterway."
3034,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) permitted us thirty horsemen to go on an expedition. We encamped near an Arab tribe (settlement). The narrator narrates that the chief of the tribe was bitten (by a poisonous animal). They came to us and inquired whether any of you can survive the bite of a scorpion. The narrator narrates I replied yes I can, but I will not do so until you people pay us (his compensation). He said: We will give you thirty goats (as compensation for him). He came to the service of Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) and mentioned this to him, so he asked, \How did you know that it also has a tail?\"" (I replied"," you have told me) So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Divide them and keep my share with you."""
3035,"The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however the narrator named Shuba has narrated something different in it."
3036,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to an Arab tribe and they did not show hospitality to them. So these people fixed a herd of goats as a compensation, so they started reciting the Fatiha while they were sleeping. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said, \How do you know that there is breath through it?\"" You use them and keep my share in them."""
3037,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition led by Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and he passed by a town whose chief was bitten by a poisonous animal. When a person wants to die, our leader is dying, Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri said: I came to him and I recited Surah Fatiha and breathed on him, and he recovered. Those people sent food to us and sent goats. How did you know that it also has a tail? I said, O Messenger of Allah, this matter came to my mind, so the Prophet said, \Eat (the meat of) these goats and feed us from it as well.\"""""
3038,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates that once some companions were going somewhere, a man came to them and said: The chief of this tribe has been bitten by a poisonous animal. Those companions said: Have you received the reward of the Book of Allah? These companions did not take anything from what they had received as compensation. When these people came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they told him, O Messenger of Allah, that he has received compensation for the Book of Allah. They also told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what they had done (i.e. recited Surah Al-Fatiha). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you know that it also has a tail? That is, of Surah Al-Fatihah, then he said, \Of all things that you receive compensation for"," the most entitled is the Book of Allah.\"" This hadith has been narrated in Sahih."""
3039,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by an Arab tribe whose member had been bitten (by a poisonous animal). Those companions said: Have you received the reward of the Book of Allah? These companions did not take anything from what they had received as compensation. When these people came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), they told him, O Messenger of Allah, that he had received compensation for the Book of Allah, so they also told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, O Messenger of Allah. We passed by an Arab tribe whose member had been bitten (by a poisonous animal). If he recited the book of Allah and breathed on it on the condition, then he was cured. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The book of Allah is the most entitled of all things that you receive compensation for. This hadith is authentic and has been narrated by Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, on the authority of Saydan bin Mudarib, from Abu Mushar."
3040,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that some prisoners were brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered me to sell two of them. I sold them and separated them (i.e. sold them to two separate men).
3041,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me two slaves who were both brothers. I sold one of them. I said, I have sold one of them, so you said, take it back."
3042,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that he separated a woman and her son while selling, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to cancel the deal. A narrator named Uthman narrated that he had made a separation between a slave girl and her son, and the Prophet forbade him to do so, so he annulled the deal."
3043,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when prisoners were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to give the whole house to them (someone), just like those people used to be, and he did not separate them."
3044,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that the person who separates is cursed. Narrator Abu Bakr narrates that these words are ambiguous, for us it means to separate a prisoner from his offspring."
3045,Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making a distinction between brothers or parents and children (while selling slaves or concubines).
3046,Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the person who (by selling slaves and maidservants) makes a distinction between a mother and her children or brothers.
3047,"Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever separates a mother from her children (by selling slaves and maidservants), Allah will separate that person and his friends on the Day of Resurrection."
3048,Harith bin Salim narrates this statement of his father: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a person who discriminates between fathers and children among prisoners.
3049,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the separation between the mother and her children (while selling slaves and maidservants). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said until the boy becomes an adult and the girl does not menstruate. There is, indeed, a narrator named Abdullah, and it is weak, Ali bin Madani has accused him of being a liar, and none other than him has narrated the hadiths regarding Saeed bin Abdul Aziz."
3050,"Aban narrates that Amir al-Shaabi narrated this hadith to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever takes an animal whose owners cannot feed it and leaves it open to graze, then he takes the animal and gives it life (i.e. provides food), then it will be his property. There are also these words in Aban's narration, Ubaidullah says, I inquired about whom he narrated this hadith. So he replied, with reference to several Companions (this hadith has been narrated), this tradition narrated by Hamad is more clear and complete."
3051,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the occasion of the conquest of Khyber, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that booty should be sold before it was distributed, and that pregnant women should not have sex before they give birth to their children. (On this occasion, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domesticated donkeys and the meat of wild animals."
3052,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr bin As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to provide supplies for the army. He bought a camel, on the condition that when the person receiving the charity came, the cost of the ride would be paid."
3053,"Amr bin Harish narrates I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr, we live in a place where dinars and dirhams are not customary. So he said, \You have asked a person who knows about this. Once", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave camels from the camels of Sadaqat for war until the camels were exhausted, but some people were left who did not have animals to ride. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You buy for us some camels, which will be in exchange for the young camels that will be received as Sadaqah, and when the Sadaqah comes, we will pay those people.' The narrator says) So I bought a camel in exchange for twenty-two young camels, until I was exhausted," then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid for it from the camels of Sadaqah."""
3054,Amr ibn Harish narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to provide equipment for an army and the camels ran out.
3055,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to provide supplies for the army. When the camels became scarce, he instructed us to get one camel in exchange for two camels from the charity camels."
3056,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling meat in exchange for an animal. Yazid bin Marwan is unique in quoting this tradition from Imam Malik, along with this chain of command, and he has not been followed."
3057,Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animals in exchange for meat. Ibn Musayyib narrates that it is forbidden to sell animals in exchange for meat.
3058,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade selling an animal on loan in exchange for an animal.
3059,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of an animal (in exchange for an animal).
3060,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making a loan in return for a loan.
3061,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this tradition about the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that he (PBUH) forbade the trading of wood for wood. Ahl lexicographers have explained this, it means making a loan deal in exchange for a loan."
3062,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade using the price of cats and dogs.
3063,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the use of the price of a cat.
3064,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that three things are forbidden, the income of a stalker, the income of a prostitute, and a dog's prey. One of the narrators of this hadith) Walid bin Ubaidullah, is weak."
3065,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog and a cat, but the order for a trained dog (i.e. a hunting dog) is different. A narrator of this tradition) Hasan bin Abu Ja'far is weak."
3066,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that three things are forbidden: the income of a stalker, the compensation of a woman who commits adultery is forbidden, and the price of a dog is forbidden. One of the narrators of this hadith (Musthini, is weak."
3067,"Abu Zubair, quoting Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) says, I think he must have mentioned this with reference to the Prophet (PBUH), he forbade the price of dogs and cats, but the ruling on hunting dogs is different."
3068,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (use) the price of a dog and a cat, but the ruling on a hunting dog is different."
3069,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it is forbidden to (use) the price of a dog and a cat, but the ruling on a hunting dog is different. Hammad did not mention that this hadith was transmitted from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and this hadith is more authentic than the previous one."
3070,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever buys an animal in Misrata will have the right for three days.
3071,The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA).
3072,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) have narrated this as a valid hadith (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) said, “A citizen should not bargain for a villager, do not buy goods on the way (before the caravan reaches the market), do not make artificial bids, do not place a price against that of your brother, and do not send a message in comparison with your brother’s message of marriage until that other person Do not marry or destroy this message. No woman should demand the divorce of her sister (Sukan) in order to obtain the benefits of her (Sukan) share through her, because that woman will get what is due to her. Can be done."
3073,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (in the same deal) salaf and sale are two conditions in one deal. Dealing with something that is not in one's possession, the profit of which one is not responsible for the guarantee (all these things) are not permissible."
3074,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that an urban person should not make a bargain for a villager. I give a saa of dates, not of wheat."
3075,"Kathir bin Abdullah narrated this statement of his grandfather regarding his father. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no status of ``Jalab, Junab, Objection.'' saw Asim bin Ubaidullah has followed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of Salem, in narrating it about Misrat. Hasan bin Amara has narrated from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layli, on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali. A narrator named Abu Shiba has narrated it from Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA). A narrator named Shuba has narrated it on the authority of a Companion (whose name is not mentioned)."
3076,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade Muhakla, Mukhazara, Malamsa, Manabza and Muzabna. A narrator named `Umar (bin Yunus) narrated this. My father explained it as follows. Mukhadra means that a buyer will not buy a field or an orchard of date palms until they are red or yellow (i.e. the produce is ripe). Manabaza means that the buyer will throw the cloth to the seller and the seller will throw the cloth to the buyer and say that it is yours in exchange for it. The relationship is that the buyer will buy the goods even though he has not even seen the goods. Mohakla refers to land on rent."
3077,"Thabit bin Saeed narrates this statement of his grandfather Sayyidna Abayd bin Hamal regarding his father. He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for that piece of land, which he said: \I used to go and it was Marib.\"" The Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him that piece of land. I went to a place called Malh, in the age of Jahiliyyah, that is a place where?? There is no salt, whoever reaches there can get it. Its example is that of flowing water which does not stop flowing. Then Iqra asked Abayd about the piece of land of salt, then Sayyiduna Abayd said: I am making it with you on the condition that you will use it as charity on my behalf. Of the water flowing from the fountain, whoever reaches it will use it. The narrator narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him some land and a date garden at the place of Jarf," meaning Jarf. Narrator named Faraj bin Saeed has narrated this. It was also the case that whoever reaches it will get it."""
3078,"Mujahid narrates that a few people decided to work jointly in an agricultural land, one of them had the land, another person was to provide agricultural implements, a third person was to work in the field, and a fourth person was to provide seeds. ordered to be done, fixed the wages for the person who had to labor in the field, and declared the man who supplied you to be the owner of all the produce. The narrator narrates that I narrated this hadith to Makhool, so he said, \I would not have been happy if I had received Wasif in exchange for this hadith.\"" This Hadith is transmitted by Messenger and is authentic. The narrator of this tradition is weak."""
3079,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said (in Islam) there is no harm or harm to a person who tries to cause harm, Allah will afflict him with harm, and whoever tries to cause hardship, Allah will afflict him with hardship."
3080,Abu Hab narrates that Sayyidna Faid bin Khalid said to me: Shall I read to you the text that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had written for me? (These are his words). \This (the text is about) Faid bin Khalid bought from the Messenger of Allah, Sayyiduna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, a slave (maybe the narrator doubts) a maidservant, in whom there is no disease, no deceit, no defect. This is a transaction of one Muslim with another Muslim. There are these words in a tradition," then he brought out this writing in front of me. \""This (the text is about) Faid bin Khalid bought from the Messenger of Allah", Sayyidna Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, a slave (maybe the narrator doubts) a maidservant (here the narrator named Ibad is doubtful) in whom there is no disease, no deceit," no defect. This is a transaction of one Muslim with another Muslim."""
3081,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: When Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him, gave a person his property as Mudarabat, he stipulated that he would not travel with it on the sea, that he would not camp with it in any (valley) place, that he would not buy any living thing with it, and if he did so, he would pay the guarantee (compensation) for it. When I mentioned it in front of the Prophet (peace be upon him), he declared it correct."
3082,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: I attended a funeral prayer in which the Prophet (PBUH) was also present. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started to leave there. He said, \You people", perform the funeral prayer for your companion. When Sayyiduna saw you going back, he said, 'O Messenger of God," this person is free from his debt. I am his guarantor for the payment he is responsible for.'\"" May Allah give you a good reward", just as you have taken responsibility for the payment of your Muslim brother, so may Allah take responsibility for your payments on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever pays his brother's debt on the Day of Resurrection," Allah will be responsible for the payments of that person on the Day of Resurrection."""
3083,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended a funeral. When he was placed, he was told that he was responsible for a debt. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew. Sayyidna Ali said: O Prophet of Allah, I am his guarantor. In giving a loan, the Prophet said: O Ali, may Allah meet your needs in the same way as you have met the needs of your fellow Muslim brother. Is it common for faith? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is common to all believers."
3084,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a gentleman passed away, we bathed him, shrouded him, perfumed him and placed him near the place of Sayyidna Gabriel (peace be upon him), where funerals were kept. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) started turning back, one of us, whose name was Abu Qatada, asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to serve him, O Messenger of Allah, the payment of these two (dinars) is my responsibility. Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) performed the funeral prayer for this person. After that, whenever the Prophet (peace be upon him) met Sayyiduna Abu Qatada, the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him what he did with these two dinars. Finally, when Sayyiduna Qatadah told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that both of them had been fulfilled in the Messenger of Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now this person has been blessed with coolness."
3085,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) quotes this statement of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the worship of Allah, the most excellent thing to do is to gain understanding in the religion. One jurist is more of a source of trouble for Satan than a thousand worshipers. There is a pillar of everything, the pillar of this religion is Fiqh. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I should sit for an hour and gain knowledge of religion, this is more beloved to me than that I spend the whole night performing Nawafil."
3086,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prophets are leaders, jurisprudents are chiefs, their companionship leads to increase (in knowledge and reward)."
3087,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is permissible to kill any Muslim in three cases: a married adulterer who will be stoned to death, a person who kills someone intentionally and will be killed in return, a person who leaves Islam and opposes Allah and His Messenger, then he will be killed, or crucified, or exiled."
3088,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3089,"The same tradition is also narrated in some other isnads, however, some words have been said about some of its narrators."
3090,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): By the one who has no god but a Muslim who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, shedding his blood is permissible only in three cases: when he abandons Islam and separates from the community (of Muslims), or a married adulterer and (i.e., a murderer) life for life."
3091,This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) along with another chain of transmission.
3092,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not permissible to shed the blood of any Muslim (after this, according to the previous hadith). Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the same as the previous tradition regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
3093,"Amish says: I narrated this hadith to Ibrahim, so he said: Aswad narrated this hadith to me regarding Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her)."
3094,"A Muhaddith named Abd al-Rahman narrates: The narrator has combined these two traditions, that is, the tradition narrated by Masrooq from Sayyidna Abdullah and the tradition narrated by Ibrahim Aswad (from Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her)."
3095,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that any Muslim belonging to this Ummah can be killed for one of three reasons: A person who kills someone will be killed in retaliation, a married adulterer, a person who leaves the Jamaat (the narrator is doubtful, perhaps these are the words)."
3096,This tradition is narrated from Sayyedah Aisha along with another chain of transmission. This tradition is suspended.
3097,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Allah Ta’ala narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep boundaries away from Muslims as much as you can.
3098,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: (Try to keep the boundaries).
3099,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA), Sayyidna Uqbah Bin Amir Jahni (RA) said: When the hadd (matter of proof) becomes doubtful before you, keep it as far away from you as possible."
3100,"Sayyiduna Salamah bin Muhibq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A case was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who had committed adultery with his wife's maidservant, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not issue a ban on him."
3101,"Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade taking revenge in the mosque, establishing boundaries in it, and reciting poetry in it."
3102,Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade taking qisas in the mosque or establishing limits in it.
3103,Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Limits should not be established in mosques and Qisas should not be taken in them.
3104,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) says: Among the children of Israel there was an order of retribution, but there was no order of death among them, so Allah said this to this Ummah (which is mentioned in the Qur'an in these words:). \Retribution has been made obligatory upon you for the slain.\"" So whoever is forgiven by his brother. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas", may Allah be pleased with him," says: This forgiveness will be in such a way that the other party agrees to accept the debt in the act of murder. \""This is a relief and a mercy from your Lord.\"" This tradition is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) regarding Mujahid."""
3105,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a fugitive steals a slave, his hand will not be cut off, and the hand of a dhimmi will not be cut off either. This hadith has been narrated as marfu' hadith only by Fahdnami narrator, it is true that this hadith is muquf."
3106,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, was convinced that if a fugitive slave steals, his hand will not be cut off."
3107,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, is convinced that the limit will not be extended to a slave, nor will the limit be extended to a person living in a Jewish or Christian land."
3108,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: There will be no limitation on the slave and the People of the Book. What is narrated before it as tradition, muquf, hadith is more authentic than this, the rest, Allah knows best."
3109,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Retribution can only be taken by the sword. Its narrator is Sulaiman Bin Arqam, Mutrook."
3110,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Retribution can only be taken with an iron (weapon), life or other than (an organ) can be taken only with an iron (weapon)."
3111,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Retribution can only be taken by the sword.
3112,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Retribution can only be taken with weapons.
3113,"This tradition is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). There is a narrator named Abu Mu'adh Sulaiman ibn Arqam, obsolete."
3114,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement on the authority of his father: A man struck another man in the knee, and that man came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, give me retribution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) punished him, then that person came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have become lame (so punish the other party more).” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I forbade you, you disobeyed me. (The narrator narrates:) After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that revenge should be taken on the injured person before he recovers."
3115,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person was injured and he intended to take revenge, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking revenge on the person who injured him, until the injured person recovers."
3116,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but there is some wording difference in it."
3117,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person struck another person in the knee, and that person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to present Qisas (the case of taking revenge) and he said to him: You should get well first. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, \You will not get anything"," you have disobeyed.\"" A narrator named Sheikh Abu Ahmad bin Abdus says: This hadith was narrated only by Abu Bakr and Uthman (both of them are the sons of Abu Shaybah). Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal and other muhaddiths have narrated this hadith from Amr (bin Dinar) on the authority of Ibn ‘Alaihi", on the authority of Ayyub. Amr ibn Dinar's disciples narrated it in the same way on his authority, and it is safe to have this tradition," Mursal."""
3118,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha along with another chain of transmission.
3119,"Muhammad bin Talha narrated: A person shot an arrow in the leg of another, so the other person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, give me retribution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him retribution, then he (the person who took retribution) did not recover, so he came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Give me my right."
3120,This tradition is narrated from Muhammad bin Talha along with another chain of transmission.
3121,Amr bin Shu'ayb narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then forbade taking revenge for an injured person before his recovery.
3122,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \One should wait for one year to take revenge for a wound.\"" There is a weak and obsolete narrator named Yazid bin Ayyad."""
3123,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Abul Qasim said: Whoever falsely accuses his slave of adultery, he will be punished on the Day of Judgment."
3124,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, Imam Bukhari (may God have mercy on him) narrated it along with his chain of transmission, all its narrators are trustworthy and hafiz."
3125,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Abul Qasim (may God bless him and grant him peace) say: Whoever accuses his slave of adultery (falsely) and then does not repent, that person will be punished on the Day of Resurrection."
3126,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abul Qasim (PBUH) said to me, “When a person falsely accuses his slave of adultery and the slave is acquitted of what he has (accused), then that person will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection."
3127,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall, and, Arj, I will not be retaliated against."
3128,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman's diet will be equal to a man's diet, until it reaches one-third of a woman's diet."
3129,"Ḥamzah ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us, ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; and Muḥammad ibn Nūḥ al-Jundaysābūrī narrated to us; and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mālik al-Askāfī narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿlā ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muḥāribī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: \Māʿiz ibn Mālik came to the Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Woe to you! Go back, seek forgiveness from Allah, and repent to Him.' He said: He went back a short distance, then came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said the same to him. This continued until the fourth time, when the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'From what shall I purify you?' He said: 'From zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse).' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: 'Is he afflicted with insanity?' He was informed that he was not insane. He asked: 'Has he consumed wine?' A man stood up and smelled him but found no smell of wine on him. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Are you a thayyib (one who has previously engaged in lawful sexual relations)?' He said: 'Yes.' He was then ordered to be stoned. The people were divided into two groups regarding him. One group said: 'Māʿiz has perished upon the worst of his deeds; his sin has encompassed him.' The other group said: 'Is there any repentance better than the repentance of Māʿiz? A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, placed his hand in his hand," and said: \""Kill me with stones.\""' They remained in that state for two or three days. Then the Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him, came to them while they were sitting. He greeted them, then sat down, and said: 'Seek forgiveness for Māʿiz ibn Mālik.' They said: 'May Allah forgive Māʿiz ibn Mālik.' The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'He has repented a repentance that, if it were distributed among an entire nation, it would suffice them.' Then a woman from Ghāmid, of the Azd, came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, purify me.' He said: 'Woe to you! Go back, seek forgiveness from Allah, and repent to Him.' She said: 'Do you intend to turn me back as you turned back Māʿiz ibn Mālik?' He said: 'What is that?' She said: 'She is pregnant from zinā.' He said: 'Are you a thayyib?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then we shall not stone you until you deliver what is in your womb.' A man from the Anṣār took responsibility for her until she gave birth. He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'The Ghāmidī woman has given birth.' He said: 'Then we shall not stone her and leave her infant small, with no one to nurse him.' A man from the Anṣār stood up and said: 'I shall take responsibility for his nursing," O Prophet of Allah.' So he stoned her.\"""""
3130,"Abdul Jabbar bin Wail has narrated this statement of his father: In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if a woman was forced to commit adultery with him, he did not issue a limit to that woman, but he did issue a limit to the one who violated her. The narrator narrates: It is mentioned in it that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeathed this woman."
3131,Taus narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed (the following words are in the next hadith).
3132,"Ta'aws narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is killed by mistake, or (unknowingly) killed by an arrow, it will be considered as a wrongful killing, and the death of the Prophet will be the death of a wrongful killing, and the person who was killed as a noble killing will have to be avenged."
3133,"Ta'aws narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever is killed by mistake, or is killed by a stone, or is killed by a staff, then his death will be the death of culpable homicide, and the death of a person who is killed intentionally will be retribution. Angels and all humans will be cursed, no duty or filial worship of such a person will be accepted."
3134,"Taus, quoting Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever is killed by mistake, or is hit with a stone or a stick, (and he dies), then this killing will be a mistake, and his death will be the death of the wrongful killing. A narrator named Hussain has quoted these words in excess: Allah will not accept any of his obligatory or posthumous worship."
3135,"A similar hadith has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, the narrator did not mention Hamza in his chain of transmission. Some narrators have quoted it from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, with reference to Taus."
3136,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Deliberate killing will be punished", but if the guardian of the deceased wishes," he can forgive it.\"""""
3137,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The death of a person who is killed by hitting a stone, stick, or stick without knowing it will be the death of a guilty person. This is similar to the statement of Hamad bin Zayd."
3138,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be retribution for killing on purpose, and for killing by mistake, there will be no retribution. Whoever is killed by mistake with a stone or stick will have retribution, which will be in the form of camels of different ages."
3139,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The person who is accidentally killed by hitting a stone (the narrator doubts that these are the words) or a stick will be killed by mistake, and the person who is killed intentionally will be punished."
3140,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates as a hadeeth: (The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said) Whoever is killed by mistake or is killed by hitting him with a stone or a stick, his death will be the death of a wrongful killing, and the person who is killed intentionally will be punished. Yanaful worship will not be accepted."
3141,"Ta'aws narrates: A person who is killed by a stick, a stick, or a stone during a fight will be paid his dowry, but he will not be killed in return, because it is not known who is his killer. I say this: Have you not seen the decision of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the case of two women belonging to the Huzail tribe, one of them had killed the other with a stick. This hadith has been narrated by the son of Taus on the authority of his father."
3142,": The sons of Taos narrate this about their father: My father had a book, which contained various types of almsgiving orders, which were revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through revelation. The act of committing murder shall be the act of culpable homicide, such as by means of a stone, a cane, or a lathi (a murder is committed) while the murderer has not raised a weapon."
3143,"The sons of Taos narrate this statement of their father: A person who is accidentally killed by a stone, a lathi, his death will be miserable."
3144,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, the day of suspected murder is like the day of murder, except that the killer will not be killed."
3145,"Sayyiduna Abu Shureeh Kaabi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared Makkah Haram. No one who believes in Allah and the Last Day should shed blood in it and cut down its trees. Daya, for me it was also declared halal for a short time, then it will remain Haram until the Day of Judgment is established, O people of Khuza'ah tribe, you killed a person from Huzail tribe, I will give him death."
3146,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: O people of Khuza'ah tribe, you killed a person of Huzail Qila, I will pay his dowry. Whoever is killed after that, the deceased's survivors will have one of two options: if they like, they will kill (the murderer as revenge) and if they like, they will receive dowdy."
3147,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “Whoever is killed or is afflicted with khabl, (says the narrator) khabl means ‘arj (i.e. becoming lame), then he will have the option of one of three things. If he takes one of these forms and then commits adultery after that, he will go to hell where he will remain forever."
3148,"Sayyiduna Abu Shareeh Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most disliked of His creatures in the sight of Allah is the person who kills someone unjustly, and the person who demands the blood of the age of ignorance, and the person who shows his eyes in sleep what they did not see (i.e. narrates a false dream)."
3149,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) conquered Makkah, he stood in front of the people to give a sermon. After praising Allah, he said: \Indeed", Allah Almighty did not allow elephants to enter Makkah, but He gave dominion over it to His Messenger and the believers. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it was declared lawful for me in a certain part of the day, and it will not be lawful for anyone after me. The game here will not be chased away, the tree here will not be cut, the fallen object here will not be picked up, but it can be picked up to make an announcement, to someone who is dear to him. If he is killed, he will have the option of one of two things, either he should be paid a dowry or he should be killed (as revenge), then Sayyiduna Abbas stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah: Allow us to cut the grass called Azhar, because we use it in our houses and graves. A gentleman named Abu Shah, who belonged to Yemen, said: O Messenger of Allah! Write it to me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," write it to Abu Shah. A narrator named Walid narrates: I asked Imam Uza'i: What is meant by this sentence (of Sayyidna Abu Shah)? Write it to me! So he said: That is the sermon that he heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
3150,This tradition is narrated from Imam Uza'i along with another chain of transmission.
3151,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The people of Khuza'ah tribe killed a member of the tribe in revenge for one of their slain in the year of the conquest of Makkah. \Allah did not allow elephants to enter Makkah, but He gave His Messenger and the believers dominion over it. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it will not be lawful for anyone after me. Remember! It became lawful for me also up to a certain part of the day, now at this time it is Haram, the thorn here cannot be broken, the tree here cannot be cut, the fallen object here cannot be picked up, but it can be picked up to announce, if a person's loved one is killed, then he will have the option of one of two things either to kill the killer (in Qisas) or to pay the dowry to the relatives of the slain. (The narrator narrates) A man from Yemen came and said: O Messenger of Allah, write it down for me, so the Prophet said: Write it down to Abu So-and-So. A man from Quraysh said: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to cut the azhar," because we use it in our houses and graves."""
3152,"Malik Ishtar narrates: I attended the service of Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him. I said: O Commander of the Faithful! When we got up from you, we heard some things, did the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give you anything other than the Qur'an? Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: No, it is only this scripture that is in the hilt of my sword. Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) called the maidservant and she brought this scripture (it had this writing: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Surely Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah Haram", and I declare Madinah Haram, between the rocky land on both sides (Madinah Munawarah) is Haram. The thorn here cannot be broken, the prey here cannot be chased away. Whoever invents any heresy or harbors any heresy, Allah will curse him with his angels and all the people. Compared to others, all believers are like a hand, their blood is of equal importance. If they are pregnant," the shelter given by an ordinary person will be recognized and no Muslim can be killed in revenge of an infidel."""
3153,"Abu Huhaifa has narrated the same on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali, his words are slightly different, but the meaning is the same."
3154,Musa bin Ali narrates: I have cursed my father during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of Hajj (reciting these verses) in a loud voice. \O people! A wrong situation came before me that a blind person would pay the death of a sighted person, when they both fell together and both were injured. It happened that a blind person was accompanying the blind man, they both fell into a well, and the blind man fell on top of the blind man, as a result of which the blind man died, so Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave this decision," the blind man will pay the death of the blind man."""
3155,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has committed adultery with such and such a woman. He also mentioned the woman’s name. (i.e.) did not punish him)."
3156,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a girl became pregnant as a result of adultery. He was asked: Who made you pregnant? He said: I have been impregnated by Al-Muqaad (namely Sahib). When he was asked about this, he confessed his crime. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not be able to bear the whip. So, under the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he took 100 twigs and gave him a single blow. The narrator has described it in the same way, but it is true that it is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA)."
3157,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA): A man named Anjat lived near the house of Sayyidna Sa’d (RA), he committed adultery with a woman. Imam Dar Qutni says: (In this hadith, the word Ikhtal is used), but the correct word is Ishkal, (i.e. palm branches)."
3158,Sayyidna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this statement of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri Radiyallahu Anhu: The stomach of a Sahib called Anus was slightly enlarged. He lived near the house of Umm Saad. A girl became pregnant.
3159,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah bin Sahl (RA) narrates the statement of his father: A maidservant of Banus Sa'ida became pregnant as a result of adultery, and when she gave birth to a child, he asked her: \Whose child is your child?\"" He replied: So", he (the accused) was a thin and weak person, his skin was like that of a snake due to weakness. Lo, which has a hundred branches, and he struck it once," so did the people."""
3160,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had become pregnant as a result of adultery. The clothes were tied well and then she was stoned. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed her funeral prayer. It was submitted to him that he first stoned her to death and then performed her funeral prayer. Who sacrifices himself (in obedience to Allah's command).
3161,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: You have stoned him, (and now offered the funeral prayer). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If all the people of Madinah did this repentance, it would be enough for them all."
3162,Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman from the tribe of Jahaina came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
3163,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had stolen a cloak. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, he has stolen. The thief said: O Messenger of Allah, yes, the Prophet said, take him and cut off his hand, then apply a scar (so that the blood will flow) and then bring him to me. Accepted."
3164,Muhammad Bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) who had stolen a cloak. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Have you really stolen? He said yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: cut off his hand and put a scar on it. The people cut off his hand and then put a scar on it.
3165,Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman has narrated a similar tradition from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him).
3166,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a person steals, his right hand should be cut off. If he steals again, his left foot should be cut off. If he steals again, I will imprison him and keep him in prison until he recovers. having no feet by which to walk."
3167,"Maysara narrated: A man and his mother came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali, the woman said: This son of mine has killed my husband. Tubita said: (The murdered) was my slave, who committed adultery with my mother. Hazrat Ali said, \You are both disgraced and lost. (O woman) If you are truthful", your son will be killed, and if your son is truthful," we will stone you.\"" When Sayyiduna Ali went to pray", the boy said to his mother: What do you think they will kill me or stone you? The narrator says: Then both of them left. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) finished praying," he inquired about them and was told that they had both left."""
3168,"Uqbah bin Aws narrates this statement of a Companion: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, he said: \There is no god but Allah", He is the One God. He fulfilled His promise, He helped His servant, He drove back the armies (of enemies). Remember, everything that is considered great and excellent (in society) and counted (every) blood (retribution) and wealth (i.e. payment) is under these two feet of mine (i.e. I give it to him). I consider it forbidden) except for the service of Baitullah and the service of giving water to the pilgrims (because these will be the standard of virtue) Remembering that murder is suspected of intentional, if someone is killed with a stick or staff, his death is a hundred camels," of which forty will be pregnant she-camels."""
3169,This tradition along with some other isnaads has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr.
3170,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no god but Allah, He is the One God, He fulfilled His promise, He helped His servant, He drove back the armies (of the enemies) Remember, everything that is considered great (and virtue) and is counted (in society).” Every) blood (retribution) and property (i.e. payment) of Jahiliyyah is under these two feet of mine (i.e. I declare it forbidden) except the service of the House of Allah and the service of giving water to the pilgrims (because these will be the standard of virtue). Dit is a hundred camels."
3171,Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aws narrates this on the authority of a Sahabi: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah (after that he narrated the hadith as mentioned above).
3172,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House of Ka'b while standing on the steps. \All praise is due to Allah who fulfilled His promise", helped His servants, drove back the armies (of the disbelievers) Remember, the victim of wrongdoing is the one who is killed by a stick or a staff, his body will be a hundred camels," in which forty camels will be pregnant. is below (i.e. I abrogate them) except (two things) the service of the Ka'ba and the service of giving water to the pilgrims."""
3173,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying this while standing on the steps of the Kaaba (after that he mentioned the above hadith).
3174,Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that retribution can only be done with the sword.
3175,"Hasan al-Basri narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that revenge can only be taken by the sword. A narrator named Yunus narrates: I asked Hassan Basri: From whom did you hear this hadith? So he replied, I have heard Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA) mentioning this."
3176,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Everything (killing by means of a sword) is considered as a wrongful killing, and in wrongful killings (death) is required. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
3177,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Everything (killing by means of a sword) is considered as a wrongful killing, and in wrongful killings (death) is required."
3178,Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Anything (killed by means of) other than iron (weapon) will be considered as wrongful killing," and for wrongful killings (death) will be required.\"""""
3179,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA).
3180,Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Anything (killed by means of) other than iron (weapon) will be considered as wrongful killing," and for wrongful killings (death) will be required.\"""""
3181,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Qisas will be taken only when a person is killed by the sword, and in the case of wrongful killing (payment of dowry) will be imposed on the family of the murderer. It is narrated in the same way on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA)."
3182,"Ikrimah narrates: Sayyidna Ali (RA) burned some people who were apostates. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas was informed about this, so he said: I do not burn those people in the fire, because the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Do not punish anyone (i.e. by burning them in fire) in the same way that Allah punishes them. (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him) said, \I would have killed those people because the Prophet", may God's prayers and peace be upon him," said this: \""Whoever changes his religion (i.e. Islam)"," kill him.\"" The narrator narrates: When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) was informed about this", he said," May Ibn Abbas (RA) be satyanas. This tradition is proven and correct."""
3183,"Bashir bin Yasar narrates about Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (RA) and Hazrat Muhaisah Bin Mas’ud (RA): These two men went to Khabeer. In those days, peace (of Muslims and Jews) was going on. These two men separated from each other in relation to their work. Sayyidna Muhaisah (RA) reached his other companion, Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Sahl, who was covered in blood and had been killed. Muhaisa buried him later when they came to Madinah, Abdul Rahman bin Sahl, Hawaisah bin Masood and Muhaisah bin Masud attended the Prophet’s service. Abdul Rahman bin Sahl started talking. Willing to take the blood of his partner (in exchange, the narrator suspects, perhaps these are the words) to become worthy of the blood of his murderer? He said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we take an oath? While we were not there, we did not see (the killings)? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Fifty of the Jews will be acquitted after taking an oath.\"" The narrator narrates: So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid these people on his behalf."""
3184,"Bashir bin Yasar, the freed slave of Banu Haritha, who was an elderly and wise man, and he also visited some of the Companions belonging to his (master's) family of Banu Haritha, including Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah, may God be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Suwayd bin Nu'man may Allah be pleased with him. About the Banu Haritha, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sahl, a member of the Ansar, was killed in Khyber. Bashir mentioned this: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Sahl (RA) and Sayyidna Muhaisa Bin Mas’ud (RA) belonged to Banu Haritha. These two men visited Khyber during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). In those days, there was peace (between Muslims and Jews), only Jews lived in Khyber. After that, he has narrated the hadith as mentioned above) but it contains these words: How can we accept the oaths of the people of the infidels?"
3185,"Basheer bin Yasar narrates this on the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (RA) and Hadhrat Rafi’ bin Khadij (RA): Both of them have narrated this: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Sahl (RA) and Sayyidna Muhaisah (RA) went to Khyber after that, according to the previous hadith."
3186,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Muhaisah bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Hawaisa bin Masoud (RA), Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman RA (Bin Sahl) and Sayyidna Abdullah Sahl (RA) went to Khyber. When told about this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, “You can make fifty people take an oath as a measure of mercy and punish your murderer, so these gentlemen did not like it. O Messenger of Allah, should we accept the oaths of the infidels? (The narrator narrates) Then the wealth of Zakat came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself paid the death of (the deceased)."
3187,"Bashir bin Yasar narrates: A companion from the Ansar, whose name was Sayyidna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this, he went to Khaibar along with some members of his tribe, there they were separated from each other, then they found one of their members killed. So those people said: We did not kill, nor do we know about the murderer. Then these gentlemen came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said, O Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace! When we went to Khyber, we found one of our people killed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Give the elder a chance first.\"" They said: We do not have any evidence. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then (those Jews) take an oath (and they will be acquitted). They said: We will not agree to the Jews taking an oath. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not like that the blood of the deceased should go in vain"," so he himself paid one hundred camels from the Zakat camels as a dowry."""
3188,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3189,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Abu Hatmah (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Some of the members of the Ansar went to Khaibar and one of them was killed. This matter came before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: \Where are your proofs?\"" He said: \""We do not have any proof.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said", “Then take an oath.” He said," “We were not there."""
3190,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is necessary for the claimant to present evidence and for the one who denies it, it is necessary to take an oath, but the ruling of Qasamat is different."
3191,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father and his grandfather, It is necessary for the claimant to present evidence and for the one who denies it, it is necessary to take an oath, but the ruling of Qasamat is different."
3192,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, Abdul Razzaq, on the contrary, has quoted it as a Mursal tradition."
3193,"Abd al-Malik bin Umayr narrates: I was present with Sayyidna Ali, a man from Banu Ajl was brought to him, Mastward bin Qubaysa, who had left Islam and became a Christian. Sayyidna Ali asked him what I have been told about you. What have you been told about me, he asked? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I have been told about you that you have become a Christian. He said: I am steadfast in the religion of Sayyiduna Masih (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Ali (may peace be upon him) said to him: I am also steadfast in the religion of Sayyiduna Masih (peace be upon him). So I did not understand what the man answered. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered: Kill him, he was killed (says the narrator)."
3194,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was a woman who had two sons who were like pearls. She used to be rude in honor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The man forbade her, but she did not stop. took it and stabbed that woman in the stomach (by which the woman died when this case came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Be a witness"," the blood of this woman was wasted.\"" These words are from a narrator named Ibn Karamat."""
3195,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: A blind man whose mother used to insult the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the evening, that person forbade the woman but she did not stop. The blind man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am the owner of this woman. She was insolent in honor of you. I stopped her but she did not stop. He said, you people be witnesses, the blood of this woman was wasted."
3196,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep the limits (of information) to your limit, when it reaches me, it will be necessary (to issue it)."
3197,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, but it contains these words: \When (the case of limitation) is brought before me"," it will be necessary (to issue it).\"" Muslim and Ibn Ayyash agree in narrating this tradition as", received, while Abd al-Razzaq narrated it as, mursal, tradition," followed by Ibn 'Alaihi."""
3198,Amr bin Shuaib narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (After this there is a similar hadith).
3199,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forgive each other before bringing the limits to me, for the limit (of the case) that reaches me will be necessary to release (the limit). (This hadith is transmitted)."
3200,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Kill the person who changes his religion (Islam).
3201,Ikramah has narrated the same from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA).
3202,"Saeed bin Abdul Aziz narrates: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) killed a woman named Umm Qarfa Fazaria as an apostate because of her apostasy. Sayyida Umm Waraqa Ansariyyah, who was named Shaheedah by the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was killed by the slave and maidservant of this woman during the caliphate of Sayyidna Umar, so Sayyidna Umar killed them both by crucifixion."
3203,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Umar.
3204,"Sayyiduna Jundab al-Khair (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \The punishment for a sorcerer is to be killed by the sword.\"""""
3205,"Jundab narrated about lightning: He killed a sorcerer who was with Walid bin Uqbah, then he recited this verse: Atatun al-Sahar waantum al-Taramin."
3206,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed the payment of a slave or a horse or a mule for the loss of a child in the womb. One of the parties against whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given judgment said: Shall I pay his dowry? He who has neither eaten nor drunk nor uttered a sound nor wept, such blood flows into the blood, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \He is speaking like poets"," a slave or a horse or a mule must be paid as a ransom.\"""""
3207,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, inquired from the people: What was the decision of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the (disposal) of the child in the womb? As for the child in the womb, he decreed that a Yakinese slave should be paid as ransom, and the woman (slayer) should be killed in exchange for the woman. There are these words in a hadith: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) asked the people: What was the decision of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the (disposal) of the child in the womb? So Sayyidna Hamal bin Malik bin Nabagha Ansari stood up and killed my two wives. One of them hit the other with a piece of wood. He hit her on the head with that piece of wood, as a result of which the other woman and the child in her womb died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed about the child in the womb that a slave would be paid as a ransom, and the woman (killer) would be killed in exchange for the woman. A narrator named Ibn Junayd has narrated these words: Atarb bin Malik Yashayd Hamal bin Malik stood up (i.e. the narrator is in doubt about his name)."
3208,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He was present when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision about this. Hamal bin Nabagha Ansari came and told that there was a fight between two women. The narrator (Ibn Juraj) narrates: I inquired from Amr (bin Dinar), the son of Taus did not tell me this about his father, so Amr bin Dinar said: You have made me doubt."
3209,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Umar (RA) stood on the pulpit and said: I give the intercessor of Allah to the person who has heard the decision of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) regarding the killing of the child in the womb. I was between two women, one of them hit the other with a stick and killed the other woman and the child in her womb. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided to pay the dowry of the child in the womb to a slave or a woman. Sayyiduna Umar said: Allahu Akbar, if we had not heard this hadith, we would have given a different decision."
3210,"The sons of Taus narrate this on the authority of their father: Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) asked for advice (followed by a previous hadith containing these words), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the payment of a woman's dowry, and ordered the payment of a slave or a horse as a ransom for a child in the womb."
3211,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a woman becomes an apostate, she should not be killed. The narrator of this tradition is Abdullah bin Isa, a liar, he has quoted false traditions regarding Affan and other narrators, and there is no valid tradition related to this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3212,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) used to say about an apostate woman, she will be imprisoned, she will not be killed."
3213,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who apostates from Islam will be imprisoned, she will not be killed."
3214,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Uhud, a woman became apostate, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to repent."
3215,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman named Umm Marwan apostatized from Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that Islam be offered to her if she accepted Islam again, otherwise she would be killed."
3216,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3217,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a woman who left Islam and became an apostate: She should be slaughtered.
3218,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A woman apostatized from Islam, then the Prophet (PBUH) ordered people to accept Islam before her."
3219,"Zahri says about a woman who disbelieves after accepting Islam: She was told to repent: she will go, if she repents then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3220,"Ibrahim Nakhai says this about the apostate woman: She was told to repent: Go, if she repents then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3221,"Ibrahim Nakhai says: If that woman accepts Islam then it is fine, otherwise she will be killed."
3222,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every apostate who does not accept Islam again will be killed, whether he is a man or a woman."
3223,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni may Allah be pleased with him say: When the matter of the hadd (to be established) becomes doubtful before you, you should fulfill the hadd as far as possible (i.e., avoid issuing it)."
3224,"Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this statement of his grandfather: On the occasion of the Battle of Khyber, the roasted meat of a goat was offered to the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, which was mixed with poison. This meat was presented as a gift by a Jewish woman. Allah's Messenger passed away, when he passed away, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this Jewish woman. He replied, I have fed you with poison. I thought that if you really became the Prophet, it would not harm you, because Allah would fulfill His decision regarding you, (i.e., you will live until Islam prevails) and if you did not become the Prophet, then I wished to save the people from you, so he was crucified under the order of the Prophet."
3225,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ma'adh (RA) May you touch it? He said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'You have committed adultery.' He said, 'Yes.'"
3226,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says, when Sayyidna Ma'ez bin Malik (RA) appeared before the Prophet (PBUH) and confessed adultery before him, the Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ma'az, \Perhaps you only kissed"," or only touched?\"" They said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""So it is like that (that is"," you have committed adultery).\"" A narrator named Ibn Sinan quoted these words: Perhaps you have kissed", you have touched, remember? He did not ask. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him," \""Did you do this (i.e. adultery)?\"" (The narrator narrates) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not use any sarcasm"," so he said yes."""
3227,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person from the tribe of Islam who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had committed adultery, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, “Perhaps you have only kissed, or only touched, or only seen."
3228,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A woman came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said: I have committed adultery, you should issue a ban on me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Bring someone who can be a sponsor for your child.\"" A person stood up and said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," may I become a sponsor for his child?\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) stoned this woman to death."""
3229,"Sha'bi narrated: A married adulterer was brought before Sayyidna Ali (RA), and Sayyidna Ali (RA) flogged her on Thursday, and stoned her on Friday."
3230,"Sha'bi narrated: The maidservant of Saeed bin Qays was brought to the service of Sayyidna Ali, who had committed adultery. Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged her and then stoned her."
3231,"Sha'bi narrated: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) flogged him on Thursday and stoned him to death on Friday. So he said, I have flogged him according to the order of the Book of Allah and stoned him according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."
3232,"Sha'bi narrated: The maidservant of Saeed bin Qays was brought to the service of Sayyidna Ali, who had committed adultery. Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, flogged her and then stoned her."
3233,"Narrated Sha'bi: A woman called Sharaha Hamdaniyyah was brought before Sayyiduna Ali, (a woman) who had committed adultery, so Sayyidna Ali sent her back to give birth to the first child. He stoned her and said, \I have flogged her according to the order of the Book of Allah"," and I have stoned her according to the order of the Sunnah.\"" Hazrat Ali said"," \""If a woman gives birth to an illegitimate child or confesses to it", the Imam will stone her first, then others will stone her, but the woman whose crime is proven by witnesses will be stoned first by the witnesses," then others will stone her.\"""""
3234,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When you find someone doing the deeds of the people of Lut, then kill both the person doing the deed and the one with whom the deed was done."
3235,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about such a virgin who is caught doing the deeds of the people of Lot: He will be stoned."
3236,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a person says to another person, O eunuch, beat (the person who said) twenty sticks. kill"
3237,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that whoever misbehaves with an animal, kill him and kill that animal as well. The narrator says: We said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: What is the animal's fault? So he said, \I did not hear these words from the Prophet", may God bless him and grant him peace, but I think that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, disapproved of eating the meat of the animal on which this act was performed," or gaining any profit from it.\"""""
3238,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: A woman from the tribe of Jahaina came to the service of the Prophet (SAW) and she confessed to adultery. He said to (this woman) you go and breastfeed the child. This woman did so, then she came to the service of the Holy Prophet, upon the order of the Holy Prophet, the clothes were tied tightly on her body, then under his order, she was stoned. Peace be upon him said: This woman has repented like this, if it is distributed among seventy people of Madinah, it will be enough for all of them."
3239,"Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same thing: However, it contains these words."
3240,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A member of the tribe of Islam came to the Prophet (PBUH) and confessed to adultery. The Prophet (PBUH) turned away from him. He confessed, and the Prophet (PBUH) reprimanded him. He testified about himself four times (that he had committed adultery). The Prophet said, \Are you mad?\"" He said"," \""No"," Prophet.\"" Allah's Messenger inquired if you are married", he said yes," then he was stoned to death in Eid Gah under the order of the Holy Prophet (SAW)."""
3241,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, prescribed one-third of the death penalty for removing the eye of a blind person from its designated place, and one-third of the death penalty for amputating the hand of a person with a paralyzed hand."
3242,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed a dowry of one hundred camels. Narrator narrates: He fixed the price of Haravant at eighty dirhams, so the total amount of the diet was eight thousand dirhams, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the diet of the People of the Book as half of the diet of a Muslim. During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) and during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, this was the same amount. During the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar, camels became expensive, so Sayyiduna Omar fixed their price at twenty-two dirhams (per camel), so the amount of diyat increased to 12,000 dirhams."
3243,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to a Dhimmi by paying the same amount of money as a Muslim.
3244,"Ibn Shahab narrates: Both Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) set the same rate of diet for a Jewish Christian person as that of a free Muslim person, provided that person is a covenant (i.e. Dhimmi), while Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani and Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) did not give diet to a polytheist Muslim."
3245,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had decided to pay twelve thousand dirhams in the Dayat. A narrator named Muhammad bin Maimon narrates: Our teacher narrated it to us once on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), however, most of the times he has quoted this tradition as a (messenger) tradition from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Ikrimah."
3246,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, a person killed another person, so the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, set his death penalty at twelve thousand dirhams. \Except in the case that Allah and His Messenger make them rich with His grace\"" means those people will be rich by receiving money."""
3247,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The diet of a Jew and a Christian will be 4,4,000 dirhams, while the diet of a Magian will be 800 dirhams."
3248,Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams.
3249,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: These two things were found in the possession of the sword of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The most disobedient person on earth is the one who kills someone other than his killer (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words), who kills someone other than his killer, and the person who attributes himself to someone else instead of his master. Obligatory worship will not be accepted. (The second thing is this): The lives of the believers are of equal status and the protection given to them by the common person will be respected, no Muslim will be killed in exchange for an unbeliever, and no covenant (dhimmi) will be killed, and people belonging to two religions will not inherit Ekad Wasra (this tradition is short)."
3250,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade his companions to be gentle with the Khawarij. They passed by Abdullah bin Khabab, so they seized him and took him and left. They passed by a date that had fallen from a tree. Abdullah bin Khabab said: Shall I not guide you to something that is more honorable for you? The people said: Yes. Abdullah bin Khabab said: I am he. Then these people killed Abdullah bin Khabab. Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was informed of this, so he sent a message to the people: Pay us the death of Abdullah bin Khabab. What is killing? Sayyiduna Ali said, Have you all killed him? They replied, Yes, then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said Allahu Akbar: Then he ordered, (your companions) to attack these people vigorously. The narrator narrates: So Sayyidna Ali (RA) killed all these people, Sayyidna Ali (RA) ordered to find the one with protruding flesh among them. After that, the narrator has mentioned the whole incident."
3251,"Abu Huws narrates: On the day of the battle of Nahrwan, we were with Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) on one side of the canal, while foreigners came and camped on the other side of the canal. If you heard, Abdullah bin Khabab said, My father narrated this hadith to me. He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Such a trial will come. A sitting person will be better than a standing one"," and a standing person will be better than a running one.\"" So they said: Allah said: Call them loudly and tell them to send the killer of Abdullah bin Khabab to us. In response"," these people said three times: We have all killed them. Then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said to his companions: Now attack them. The narrator narrates: After that Sayyiduna Ali and his companions killed those people. The narrator narrates."""
3252,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A free person will not be killed in exchange for a slave.
3253,"Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) say: When a free person kills a slave as a premeditated murder, then qisas will not be taken, but the dowry shall be paid. (Imam Darqutni (may God have mercy on him) says:) This hadith cannot be presented as evidence, because it, the Messenger, is."
3254,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah (injunction) is: A Muslim should not be killed in exchange for an infidel, the Sunnah (injunction) is that a free person should not be killed in exchange for a slave."
3255,Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar did not kill a free man (as revenge) for killing a slave.
3256,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3257,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah (ruling) is this: A Muslim shall not be killed in exchange for a contract (i.e. a non-Muslim), and a free person shall not be killed in exchange for a slave."
3258,Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said about the killing of a slave of a free person: In it the price (as dowry) will be paid.
3259,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a Muslim killed in return for an agreement (Dhimmi). This hadith has been narrated only by Ibrahim bin Abu Yahya as a Musnad. This person is an abandoned hadith. It is true that this tradition has been narrated by Ibn Belmani as a transmitted tradition.
3260,"Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani, quoted, has narrated this as a hadith: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a Muslim killed in Qisas, that Muslim had killed a Jew. Ramadi has quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a Muslim in exchange for a dhimmi."
3261,"Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a person belonging to the people of Qiblah in exchange for a dhimmi. He said, \I have the most right to fulfill my duty.\"""""
3262,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3263,Sayyiduna Anas bin Amlak (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put stitches in the eyes of those (the apostates) because they put stitches in the eyes of the shepherd (of the camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)). Ibn Sa'eed says that by these (the apostates) are meant the people of the ``Arina'' tribe.
3264,"Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Khurash bin Umayyah (a non-Muslim) was killed, although the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already forbidden killing a non-Muslim. (The narrator narrates) This happened when Khurash bin Umayyah killed a man from the Hazail tribe on the occasion of the conquest of Makkah."
3265,"Sayyiduna Asma Bin Malik (RA) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW), a slave stole something. His case was presented to the Prophet (SAWS) and the Prophet (SAWS) forgave him. Then his case was presented to the Prophet (SAWS) a second time that he had stolen, and the Prophet (SAWS) forgave it again. Then for the fourth time, the case was presented to you that he had stolen? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forgave him again, then when he was accused of stealing for the fifth time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off one of his hands. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It is four (times of forgiveness) instead of four (times of forgiveness)."""
3266,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: This verse, warriors?? Revealed about: \Indeed"," those who fight Allah and His Messenger: this is their punishment.\"" When those people commit the crime of robbing and killing people and taking property", they will be crucified. If they kill people but do not take property," they will be killed."""
3267,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Sayyidna Ali Radiyallahu Anhu passed away from a mad woman of the so-and-so tribe who had committed adultery and Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu ordered her to be stoned. \The pen has been lifted from three types of people, a madman whose intellect has been overwhelmed," a person who sleeps until he wakes up and a child until he becomes an adult.\"" So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: You; He said correctly: Yes"," then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) left this woman."""
3268,"Saeed bin Musaib narrates: Two men were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, one of whom had killed and the other had held (the slain), so the Holy Prophet had the murderer killed (as a punishment), and the one who held (the slain) was imprisoned."
3269,"Ismail Ibn Umayyah, Marfu', narrates as a hadith: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The one who kills will be killed and the one who holds the slain will be imprisoned."
3270,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \When a person is holding someone and another kills him", the person who killed him will be killed," and the person holding him will be imprisoned.\"""""
3271,"Ismail Ibn Umayyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision in a case in which one person held another captive, and the third person killed him."
3272,Amir (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) also made the same decision
3273,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Qatadah bin Abdullah: If I had not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The revenge of the children will not be taken from the father, then I would have killed you (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) I would have blown your neck."
3274,Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that a father will not be retaliated against his son.
3275,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No limit will be established in the mosque and no father will be killed in exchange for the son.
3276,Narrated Umar: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the father will not be killed in exchange for the son.
3277,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The father will not be killed in exchange for the son"," even if (the father killed the son) intentionally.\"""""
3278,"Sayyidna Saraqa bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We will take revenge from the son for the father, but we will not take revenge for the son from his father."
3279,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No boundary shall be established in the mosque and no father shall be killed in exchange for the son.
3280,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, these words are added in it: father will not be avenged by son."
3281,"Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \The son will not be retaliated against by the father.\"""""
3282,"Amr bin Shu'ayb, on the authority of his father, narrates the following statement of his grandfather: A man killed his slave as premeditated murder, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him and exiled him for a year."
3283,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who killed his slave as a premeditated murder, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him and exiled him for a year."
3284,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3285,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3286,"Amr Bin Shuaib narrates: For a Muslim who kills a person of the Book, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made it necessary to pay four thousand dirhams (as a ransom)."
3287,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, the Dhimmi's diet will be equal to the Muslim's diet. This hadith has not been narrated by anyone other than Abukarz regarding Nafi, and this person is abandoned, his name is Abdullah bin Abd al-Malik Fahri."
3288,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has declared the contract (Dhimmi) to be equal to the Muslim's. Uthman is a narrator, waqasi, and obsolete hadith."
3289,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Muslim killed a dhimmi as a premeditated murder. This case was brought before Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), so he did not kill him (the murderer as retribution), and he (the murdered person) was sentenced to death, which was the same as the death of a Muslim."
3290,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at 4,000 dirhams, while a Magian set it at 800 dirhams. Shuba says: I asked my teacher, have you heard this hadith from Saeed himself? He answered no! By the way, if I wanted, I could have listened to it in his own words. This hadith was narrated to me by Thabit Haddad. Shuba says: Then I met Thabit Haddad and he narrated this hadith to me."
3291,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The diet of a Jew and a Christian will be four thousand dirhams, while the diet of a Magian will be eight hundred dirhams."
3292,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3293,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that considering someone as a partner of Allah does not make someone (a person) immune. The narrator named Afif bin Salem has been misled in quoting this hadith as a hadeeth, it is correct, this hadeeth has been narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as his saying."
3294,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who takes someone as a partner of Allah will not be protected.
3295,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He who associates someone with Allah will not be protected. This hadith has been narrated as marfu', hadith only by a narrator named Ishaq, according to one hadith he turned to it later."
3296,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The blood of the person for whom we are responsible will be (respectable) like our blood. Aban bin Taghlib has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated it with reference to Abu Junob along with his chain of transmission. The narrator named Abu Junob is a weak hadeeth.
3297,"Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He intended to marry a Jewish (maybe the narrator has doubts) with a Christian woman. The narrator of this tradition, Abu Bakr bin Abu Maryam, is weak, while the other narrator, Ali bin Abu Talha, did not find the time of Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik."
3298,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When a Jew was killed with deceit, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered twelve thousand dirhams (as dowry) to be paid in this case."
3299,"Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every contract (dhimmi) whether it is a Magian or someone else, its due date will be fulfilled."
3300,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) has also said the same thing.
3301,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: He found out the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be futile, falling into a well and dying will be futile, falling into a mineral mine and dying, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. A person asked him: O Abu Muhammad, was Abu Salama with him? So he said, If he had been with them, he would have been with them."
3302,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3303,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying will be in vain, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. Al-Zubaidi and Ja'far bin Burqan did not mention Abu Salamah in his chain of transmission."
3304,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Injuring an animal (or the death of a person as a result of it) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and payment of Khums will be required in Rakaz. Ibn Shihab states: The word used in this hadith, al-Jabbar, means his blood will be wasted and the word al-Ajma' means animal. Shaykh Abu Bakr Nishapuri says: According to my knowledge, no narrator except Yunus bin Yazid has mentioned that it was transmitted from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah in his chain of transmission."
3305,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By hitting the feet (of an animal) it will die.
3306,"The same tradition has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but the names are not these words."
3307,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: He will burn in the fire and die."
3308,Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal (may Allah have mercy on him) says about this hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Imam Abdul Razzaq (may Allah have mercy on him) that he will burn in the fire and go to die: It has no status and this hadith is not correct.
3309,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: It will be in vain to fall into the fire and die.
3310,"Narrated Hazeel: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It will be useless to fall into a mineral mine and die", and it will be useless to die by falling into a well, it will be useless for a person to die (as a result of being killed by an animal), and it will be useless to die from (beating) the feet (of an animal), and in Raqqas," the payment of Khums will be required.\"""""
3311,"Hazeel narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may God be pleased with him): I believe that he, Marfu', has narrated it as a hadith."
3312,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Injuring an animal (or causing a person to die) will be in vain, dying as a result of being trampled (by an animal) will be in vain, falling into a well and dying will be in vain, falling into a mineral mine and dying will be in vain, and the payment of Khums will be obligatory in Rakaz.”"
3313,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of his father: A camel of Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib entered someone's garden and damaged some things there, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the protection of property (i.e. land and gardens) during the day is the responsibility of their owners, and the protection of animals during the night is the responsibility of their (animal) owners. Wahib and Abu Mas'ud al-Jajj have differed somewhat in the transmission of Muammar, they did not mention it as a transmission of his father."
3314,"Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari camel entered a garden and caused damage, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the owners of the gardens are responsible for their protection during the day, while the owners of the cattle will be responsible for the young animals causing damage at night. Yunus narrates: Shafi'i heard this hadith from Ayyub, but he narrated it on the authority of Zuhri, on the authority of Haram, on the authority of Sayyidna Bara'."
3315,Haram bin Muhaisa narrates on the authority of his father: Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) says: The camel of Sayyidna Bara (RA) entered a garden.
3316,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of Bara bin Azib (may God be pleased with him): He had a she-camel that damaged (someone's garden). After that, he has mentioned the previous hadith regarding the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Faryabi, Ayyub bin Khalid, and other hadith scholars have disagreed in quoting it with reference to Imam Uza'i."
3317,"Haram bin Muhaisah narrates on the authority of Sayyidna Bara bin Azib: When a camel of the family of Sayyidna Bara damaged something, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the protection of fruits (i.e. gardens and produce) during the day is the responsibility of their owners, and the owners of cattle will pay for what the harmful cattle damage at night."
3318,"Haram bin Muhaisa narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, the camel of these people."
3319,Narrated Haram bin Saad bin Muhaisah: The camel of Sayyiduna Bara entered a garden and damaged (the produce) there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was complained about. This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
3320,"Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passing through the people. Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) was inquiring about the place of Qiyam. threw Then a drunken person was brought before Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) and he punished him with forty lashes."
3321,"Ibn Wabara Kalbi narrates: Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) sent me to Sayyidna Umar (RA). He says that when I arrived at the service of Sayyidna Umar (RA), at that time Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA), Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, Sayyidna Ali, Sayyidna Talha (RA) and Sayyidna Zubair (RA) were also present. They were all reclining in the mosque. I said: I have been sent to serve you. They greeted you: Yes, and requested this: People have started drinking too much and they do not pay any attention to its punishment. Sayyiduna Umar said: These men are here before you. Ask them about this. Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that what he (Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He should convey it to his master (sayyedna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him)). The narrator narrates: When a weak person who had committed this crime was brought before Sayyiduna Umar, he used to give him forty lashes."
3322,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3323,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3324,"Sayyidina Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar (RA) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Hunain, a man was brought before the Prophet (PBUH) who had drunk alcohol, and the Prophet (PBUH) told the people to beat him, so the people gathered and beat him with their shoes."
3325,"Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar narrates the following statement from his father: A man was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had been drinking alcohol. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present in Hunain at that time. He threw dirt on his face and ordered his companions to beat him with their shoes and whatever they had in their hands until (after some time) the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Stop now, then he People stopped. This was the method (of punishing drunkards) until the death of Prophet Reem (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). After that, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed forty lashes as punishment for drinking alcohol, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed forty lashes in the early part of his caliphate and started imposing eighty lashes in the last part. Retained the same whips."
3326,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A maidservant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave birth to a child as a result of adultery. When it becomes pure, issuing a limit on it. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Set a limit (on the slaves and maidservants) under your possession. Shu'ba, Israel, Shareek, Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and Abu Waqiyyah have followed in quoting it from Abd al-Ali."
3327,"Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said while giving a sermon: O people! Fear Allah, and if your slaves or maidservants commit adultery, flog them, whether they are free or not, because a slave girl of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed this crime, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to flog her. If I flog her, she will die. I returned to the service of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) and mentioned this to him. I said: O Prophet of Allah, if I beat her, I am afraid she will die."
3328,"Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) making a similar mention of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but it contained these words, so I left the slave girl until she was cured and recovered."
3329,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man's slave girl commits adultery, a man should flog her and verbally call her a brana. (Here the narrator is in doubt as to which word has been used for rope, habul, yazfir)."
3330,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3331,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it he did not state that he had narrated this tradition with reference to his father."
3332,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3333,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3334,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “When a man’s maid commits adultery, he should flog her according to the command of the Book of Allah and verbally call her ‘Branah’. If she does it again, then do the same thing again. Sell it."
3335,This tradition is also narrated along with another document.
3336,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “When a man’s slave-girl commits adultery and is found guilty of adultery, that person should flog her as a limit, but verbally call her ‘Branah’ (the narrator says). The word used in this hadith, Zafir, refers to a rope."
3337,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Walubanqid min shayar, (here the meaning of naqid is also rope)."
3338,"Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “There shall be no cursing between four types of people: a free man, (husband) and a slave girl (there shall be no cursing between the wife and husband), a free woman (wife) and a slave (there shall be no cursing between the husband), a Muslim (husband) and a Jew (wife), and there shall be no cursing between a Muslim (husband) and a Christian (wife). A narrator named Uthman bin Abd al-Rahman is a Waqasi and hadiths are obsolete."
3339,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, “There shall be no cursing between four types of women (and their husbands): a Christian woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a Jewish woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a slave girl who is the wife of a free man, and a free woman who is the wife of a slave. There are Khorasanis named Uthman bin Ata and they are very weak. The narrator named Yazid bin Bazi Ramli has quoted it with reference to Ata, but they are also weak. This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Imam Uza'i and Ibn Juraj on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather on the authority of his grandfather."
3340,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: (and quoted it as his own saying: he did not quote it as a hadith). It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may God be pleased with him) says: There will be no curse between such women and their husbands: a Jewish woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a Christian woman who is the wife of a Muslim, a free woman who is the wife of a slave, and a woman who is the wife of a free person."
3341,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Utaab ibn Asayd (he then narrates the same hadith as before). The narrators of this tradition are Hamad bin Amr, Ammar bin Matar and Zayd bin Rafi'."
3342,"Qabaisa bin Zuhaib narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) scolded a man who had intercourse with one of his slave girls who was the wife of a slave, and the slave did not divorce him. Sayyidna Umar (RA) gave a ruling about a person who first denied having a child (of his own) by a woman while the child was still in the woman's womb, then he confessed, and the child was still in the woman's womb. When the child was born, the man refused it again, so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) ordered that he should be flogged (as Huddaqf) for what he had accused the woman of, and Sayyidna Umar (RA) established the lineage of the child with that woman."
3343,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) says: If a person commits a punishable crime and I impose a limit on him and he dies because of it, I consider that I have to pay his dowry, except for a person who has been permitted to drink alcohol, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prescribe anything (regular) about this."
3344,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), those who drank alcohol were beaten with hands, shoes and sticks, until the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) passed away. Sayyidna Umar also gave forty lashes to those who drank alcohol, until a Sahab from the first emigrants who had drunk alcohol was brought before Sayyidna Umar, who had drunk alcohol, and he was ordered to flog him. So he said: Allah has said this in His Book: \Those who believe and do righteous deeds"," there will be no sin on them for what they eat and drink.\"" (He said) I am among those who believed", did good deeds, became pious and became believers, then became pious and did good (which is mentioned in the Qur'an). I was with the Holy Prophet in the Battle of Badr, the Battle of Uhud, the Battle of Khandaq and all other battles. Sayyiduna Umar said to the other people," \""Why don't you answer what he said?\"" So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said: This verse was revealed as an excuse for the past people as a proof against the hypocrites", because Allah said: O you who believe, indeed, wine and gambling. Al-Sayyidna Ibn Abbas read these two verses in full and said: If these are among the people who believed and did good deeds, then Allah has forbidden them to drink alcohol. Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: You are right. And when delusion spreads, he makes a false accusation of adultery, and the one who falsely accuses of adultery is given the same whipping, so according to the order of Sayyiduna Umar," he was given the same whipping."""
3345,Narrated Sa'ib bin Yazid: He was with Sayyiduna Umar when he flogged the person who smelled of alcohol.
3346,Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) whipped a person and he smelled alcohol from that person.
3347,"Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: A Jewish person passed by a girl who was wearing an ornament, he (took off that ornament and injured the girl) and threw it into a well. He said that such and such a Jew was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he confessed his crime, so he was also killed under the order of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3348,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: A Jew killed a girl by taking away her jewelry, and this Jew stoned her to death. When the girl was brought to the Prophet (PBUH), there was life in her. He nodded his head in response and said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then asked him again whether so-and-so killed you. So he answered with a nod of his head, yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put the head of this Jew between two stones and killed him by crushing it in between."
3349,"The same tradition is narrated along with another document, however, Qatadah has quoted these words in his tradition, this Jew had confessed his crime."
3350,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a Jew injured an Ansari girl by taking off her necklace and threw her into a pit and crushed her head with a stone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that if she (the Jew) should be stoned to death, she should be stoned."
3351,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person committed adultery and was flogged as punishment under the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
3352,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A man committed adultery with a woman, and he was flogged as punishment under the order of the Prophet (SAW)."
3353,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon to the people on Friday. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Sit down.” He sat down, then he stood up for the third time. The person belonging to Banwalith was not married. It was asked, O Messenger of Allah, why don't you flog the woman with whom he has committed a sin? The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \Flog her"," then bring her to me.\"" He replied"," \""Such and such a woman. He mentioned the name of a woman belonging to Banubakar. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this woman and asked her about it. She said: She lied: \""By Allah", I do not even know her, and I am innocent of what she has accused me of," and Allah is witness to what I am saying.\"" because this woman denies that you have committed any sin with her. If you have any proof", I will flog her, and if you have no proof," I will flog her as a punishment for making a false accusation of adultery."""
3354,"Saeed Ibn Musaib narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) performed the Hajj for the last time, after which he did not get the chance to perform Hajj, during that Hajj, a Muslim man was found dead in the residential area of Banu Da'ah. Sayyidna Umar (RA) sent a message to him. So they answered no. Sayyiduna Umar took fifty thousand of them, and made them stand in Hatim, and took this oath from them: (That they should take this oath) By Allah, who is the Lord of this sacred house, the Lord of this sacred city, the Lord of this sacred month, you people did not kill him, and you do not even know about his killer, these people took this oath, when these people took this oath. Then Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said, \Either you pay this person's Dayat Mughlaza in terms of camels", pay a full Dayat in terms of Dirhams and Dinar," and pay one-third of the Dayat (amount of money).\"" So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""No"," I have given a decision about you according to the decision of your Prophet.\"" So these people paid a full diyat according to dinars and chose to pay a third of the diyat (amount). The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Subhbi."""
3355,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams."
3356,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, fixed the diet of a Jew and a Christian at four thousand dirhams and the diet of a Magian at eight hundred dirhams."
3357,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who had become intoxicated due to the consumption of dates, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him."
3358,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the diet of two members of the tribe of Amir to be equal to the diet of a Muslim. Shaykh Abu Bakr says: That is, each of them had the religion of a Muslim, while both of them were dhimmis."
3359,Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the diet of the People of the Book half of the diet of the Muslim. Ibn Wahhib has quoted these words: The diet of a disbeliever is set as half of the diet of a Muslim.
3360,"Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has decreed: The diet of both types of People of the Book (i.e. Jews and Christians) will be as much as the diet of Muslims, (says the narrator) meaning Jews and Christians."
3361,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There will be five types (of camels) in the slaughtering of camels.
3362,This tradition is narrated along with another document. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There will be five types of (camels) in the day of slaughtering (camels).
3363,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3364,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decided to pay one hundred camels as compensation for murder, out of which twenty would be Haqqah and twenty would be Jaza’a, twenty would be women of Lubun, twenty would be women in labor and twenty would be women of Khad. Sahibzada Abu Ubaidah has narrated it with a valid chain of transmission, which cannot be discredited, and this tradition cannot be interpreted. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) was very fearing of his Lord and was very firm in his religion. It cannot be expected of him that he would narrate a hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had given this decision and then issue a fatwa against it. I have not heard anything from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this and I do not know of any tradition regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I will present my opinion in this matter, if it is right, it will be from Allah and His Messenger, and if there is a mistake in it, it will be from me. His companions saw that he was so happy that the fatwa given by him was in accordance with the decision of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. His companions had never seen him so happy. So how can this be true about those who have this attribute and this condition, that they narrate a hadith regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then contradict it (saw fatwa). This is also supported by the tradition which was narrated by Abu Ubaidah, the son of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, and this tradition was narrated by Waqi’, Abdullah bin Wahib and other muhaddiths, with reference to Sufyan Al-Thawri Mansoor, Ibrahim Nakhai, about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with them."
3365,
3366,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision in the case of killing a sin, it will consist of five types of camels, one type, Jazaa, one type of Haqqah, one type of female Lubun, one type of female Mukhad and one type of male, Banulbon. He has mentioned Banulbon instead of Banumkhaud."
3367,"This hadith has been narrated by Ahmad bin Muhammad and other narrators along with their chain of transmission, with reference to Khushf bin Malik, the statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed the payment of five types of camels for the death of a person who commits a sin. Apart from this, these gentlemen did not copy the word and did not copy the sentence explaining these five types."
3368,"Muhammad bin Qasim Zakariya has narrated this tradition on the authority of Hisham bin Yunus, on the authority of Abu Malik Junbi. All these gentlemen have narrated this hadith regarding Hajj. Ismail bin Muhammad Safar has narrated this tradition from Hajjaj on the authority of Saadan bin Nasr on the authority of Abu Muawiya. Abu Bakr Nishapuri has narrated it on the authority of Abu Muawiya on the authority of Muhammad bin Yazid Tafur. Ahmad bin Najda has narrated a tradition similar to that of Hafs on the authority of Hamani and Abu Muawiya on the authority of him. This hadith has been narrated by Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abu Zayda with reference to Hajjaj, then there has been a dispute with him regarding the copying. Sirih bin Yunus adapted Abd al-Rahim and Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad. Abu Hisham Rifa'i has narrated a different tradition from this. He has narrated it in agreement with Abu Mu'awiyah Zarir and those who follow him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed the Dayat (payment of camels) in five parts. As you have seen, there is a difference in this narration regarding the Hajjaj, as you have seen, so there may be a possibility that it is authentically proven from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) prescribed the payment of camels in the day of killing a sin) in five categories, as Abu Muawiya, Hafs, Abu Malik Junbi, Abu Khalid, Ibn Abi Zaida in the narration narrated by Abu Hisham mentioned these five. The description of the types has not been copied, it is agreed upon by all these gentlemen, their number is also high and all of them are trustworthy. Here is also a possibility: the narrator named Hajjaj sometimes explains the five types as his opinion after narrating the hadith of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which gives the listener the illusion that this may also be a part of the hadith of the Prophet, even though those words are not part of the hadith, but are the words of Hajjaj. This possibility is strengthened by the fact that Abdul Wahid bin Ziyad, Abdul Rahim and Yahya bin Saeed Umayyad have disagreed in quoting traditions regarding him, as we have already mentioned the traditions of these gentlemen, that Yahya bin Saeed Umayyad has mentioned twenty Banulbon instead of Bes, Haqqa, while Abdul Wahid and Abdul Rahim have quoted the words of Beis Haqq instead of Banulbon, Allah knows best. One aspect of it is this: Various sayings have been narrated about a group of Companions belonging to the Muhajireen Ansar of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the issue of the deed of murder, and according to our knowledge, none of them mention Binumkhadh in this tradition. As far as the hadith transmitted from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is concerned, it was narrated by Ishaq bin Yahya bin Waleed bin Ubadah on the authority of Sayyidina Ubadah bin Samit (may God be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him). This hadith is transmitted by Ishaq bin Yahya. He has not heard the hadiths from Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit. Amr bin Shoaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Whoever is killed for committing a crime", his death will be one hundred camels, of which thirty will be female, thirty will be male, thirty will be right," and ten will be male."""
3369,"There are two possibilities in this hadith, one aspect is: Amr bin Shuaib did not mention in it that his father heard the hadith from his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may God be pleased with him) (or not). A similar tradition has been narrated about Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) that Ishaq Bin Yahya has narrated regarding Sayyidna Ubadah (RA). Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) say: In the death of a person who commits a crime, there will be thirty righteous, thirty daughters will be Lubun, twenty daughters will be pregnant, and twenty males will be Banu Lubun."
3370,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyidna Uthman and Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA).
3371,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA).
3372,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He says, four kinds of camels (will be paid) in the day of killing Khata: twenty-five, Jiza'a, twenty-five Haqqa, twenty-five Labun daughters, and twenty-five Makhad daughters."
3373,The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and the same is related to Imam Shaabi and Ibrahim Nakhai.
3374,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The death penalty for the murder of a person will be paid in the form of four types of (camels), twenty-five will be Haqqah, twenty-five will be Jazaa, twenty-five daughters will be Laboon, and twenty-five daughters will be Makhad."
3375,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever kills someone intentionally will be entrusted to the guardian of the deceased, and if they want, they can kill him, and if they want, they can receive a dowry, which will be thirty, right, thirty jaza'a, forty caliphs."
3376,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In cases of willful murder, reconciliation and confession, the family will not pay dowry."
3377,"Sha'bi states: The family shall not be responsible for the payment of a slave, murder (of a murderer), reconciliation, (payment determined as) and acknowledgment (of any payment on their part)."
3378,Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Do not charge the family with any part of a person who confesses.
3379,"Narrated by Sayyidna Hazail bin Shahrabeel (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a person who dies falling into a mineral (mine) will be wasted, the blood of a person who warms in a well will be wasted, the blood of a person who dies from being killed by an animal will be wasted, the payment of Khums will be required in Raqqa, and the blood of a person who dies from being kicked by an animal will be wasted. are: This blood shall be in vain."
3380,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3381,Sayyidna Huzail (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The blood of the foot (of the animal) will be wasted. This hadith is transmitted.
3382,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3383,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The blood of the foot (of the animal) will be wasted.\"""""
3384,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: The blood of the person who dies from being killed by an animal will be wasted, the blood of the person who is heated in a well will be wasted, the blood of the person who dies in a mineral (mine) will be wasted."
3385,"Narrated by Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Whoever keeps his animal in the way of the Muslims or in the bazaar", and that animal tramples someone under his hand or foot," then that person will be a guarantor.\"""""
3386,Sayyidah Umm Sulaiman Shafaa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) appointed Sayyiduna Abu Jaham bin Ghanim (RA) to be the custodian of the booty on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain.
3387,"Amir (Shaabi) narrated: A thief was brought to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) who had stolen, and Sayyidna Ali (RA) cut off his hand. For stealing again, he was brought again, and Sayyidna Ali (RA) cut off his foot. It can eat something and absorb it."
3388,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a thief steals, I will cut off his right hand; if he does it again, I will cut off his left foot; if he does it again, I will keep him in prison until he recovers, because I am ashamed to leave him in such a state (after that he mentioned according to the previous hadith)."
3389,"Sayyidina Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) cut off his hand. Katwadiya, he was then accused of theft and was killed under the order of the Holy Prophet."
3390,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3391,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3392,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: When a thief steals, cut off his hand; if he does it again, cut off his foot; if he does it again, cut off his hand; if he does it again, cut off his foot. Khalid bin Salamah has narrated this tradition in the same way, while other narrators have narrated it on the authority of his uncle Harith on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3393,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was present with Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he cut off one of his (thief's) hands and one of his feet (already)."
3394,"Sha'bi narrated: Two men brought a man to Sayyiduna Ali, they both testified about this person that he had stolen. Sayyidna Ali cut off his hand, then those two men brought another person and said: The first time we made a mistake, this is the real thief. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If I had known that you had deliberately cut off the hands of the first person, I would have cut off both of your hands."
3395,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a limit is issued to a thief, he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3396,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a limit is issued to a thief, then he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3397,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When a limit is issued to a thief, then he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3398,"The same hadith has been narrated from Sayyidina Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, with reference to some other isnads, in which there has been a dispute about a narrator and he has been declared anonymous, and the possibility that this hadith may have been transmitted has been indicated."
3399,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A thief was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his hand to be cut off and said that he will not pay the ransom."
3400,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a limit is issued to a thief, he will not be obliged to pay the ransom (for the stolen property)."
3401,"Narrated by Nafi: A person who had one hand and one foot amputated (as a punishment for theft) became a guest of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddique RA. He replied, \Ya'li bin Maniya has cut it as a cruel act.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said to him"," \""I will write to him about it.\"" Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) promised him. Found by the pass", when his research revealed that he had been sold by the same amputee. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said: By Allah, what is more severe (unpleasant) to me than this action of his is that he was praying to Allah (that the thief be caught)," you people cut off his foot (so that he will not be able to do anything with his hand)."""
3402,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrated: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) cut off the foot of the person whose hand was cut off by Ya'li Ibn Umayyah.
3403,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) narrates: A black man came to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) and stayed with him. Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) began to teach him the Qur'an. But he did not agree to this, so Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) sent him along with the receiver, and urged him to take care of (the black person). After some time, the (black) person came and his hand was cut. When Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) saw him, tears flowed from Tawan's eyes. I was responsible for one of his duties (i.e. an animal or something) and he cut off my hand, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) said, \The one who cut off his hand has betrayed more than twenty duties"," by Allah!\"" If you are right", then I will imprison him for that reason. Then Sayyidna Abu Bakr kept him with him and treated him as before. The man stood up at night (during the Nawafil), and when Sayyidna Abu Bakr heard his voice, he prayed," \""O Allah"," punish the one who cut his hand.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""Last night", there was a theft with us. He stood up with a severed hand (black). He turned towards the Qiblah. He raised both his right hand and the severed hand and prayed: O Allah, catch him who has stolen this (or use similar words). Muammar Nai, the narrator, narrated these words: (The black man prayed:) May Allah catch the person who stole from this noble house. The narrator narrates: The day was not even half over, that the goods were found with this person, and Sayyidna Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him," said to him. The foot was amputated."""
3404,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: When Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) heard his voice, he said, \You do not spend the night of a thief.\"""""
3405,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I bear witness that Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) cut off the foot of a person who had stolen for the third time, before having one hand and one foot cut off."
3406,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his hand amputated (for stealing) something worth five dirhams.
3407,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3408,Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Five (fingers i.e. hands) will be cut off for five (theft of an item worth dirhams).
3409,Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Five (fingers i.e. hands) will be cut off for five (theft of an item worth dirhams).
3410,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand for stealing an item worth five dirhams. A narrator named Abu Hilal narrates: Some narrators told me: Ibn Abu Arooba narrated this hadith from Sayyidna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu from Sayyidna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu. Abu Hilal says: If it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Sayyiduna Anas, then it is either transmitted from the Prophet or it will be from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3411,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The hand of a person who cheats, takes bribes, and commits robbery (in public) will not be cut off."
3412,"Abdullah Bin Amr Hazrami narrates: I brought my slave to Sayyiduna Umar Bin Khattab, I said: O Commander of the Faithful, cut off his hand. Sayyidna Umar asked what he has done. I said: He has stolen my wife's mirror, which was worth more than sixty dirhams, then Sayyiduna Umar said: Your servant has stolen your belongings, his hand will not be cut off."
3413,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Breaking the bone of a dead person is as sinful as breaking the bone of a living person.
3414,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Breaking the bone of a dead Muslim is like breaking the bone of a living person.
3415,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking the bone of a living person.
3416,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The hand of a thief will not be cut off for stealing something less than the value of a shield. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa was asked: What is the value of a shield? So he replied: A quarter of a dinar This statement of Sayyida Aisha has been narrated with reference to another chain of transmission: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The theft of a quarter of a dinar or something worth more will be cut off.
3417,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \The thief's hand will be cut off if he steals anything worth a quarter of a dinar or more.\"""""
3418,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a shield or something as valuable as its value will be cut off for theft. Sulaiman bin Yasar says: The hand will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more (stealing something of value).
3419,Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) cut off his hand for stealing a shield worth three dirhams.
3420,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man stole a shield worth five dirhams, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand."
3421,"Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: In the time of the Holy Prophet, the cost of a shield was ten dirhams."
3422,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams. Ata says: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
3423,"Waleed narrates that I was told by a listener from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that the price of a shield used to be ten dirhams in those days."
3424,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
3425,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
3426,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
3427,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
3428,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: For the theft of (at least) ten dirhams, the hand of the thief will be cut off."
3429,"Along with another chain of transmission, it is narrated: The theft of (something of value) less than the value of the shield will not be punished (says the narrator) The value of the shield was ten dirhams."
3430,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: In the time of the Holy Prophet, the cost of a shield was ten dirhams."
3431,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3432,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The hand will not be cut off for anything worth less than ten dirhams.
3433,The same hadith is also narrated along with a chain of transmission. It is chained with reference to a chain of transmission: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his hand cut off for stealing five dirhams (of something of value).
3434,"Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Whoever prays the Isha prayer after performing ablution well and then performs four rak'ahs (Nawafil) in which he performs complete bowing and prostration, and he knows what he is praying in them, he will get the reward of performing these rak'ahs on the night of Qadr. This hadith has been narrated by Ata on the authority of Ayman, on the authority of Sa'i Yatbi. The narrator named Ayman is the one who has narrated this about the Prophet (peace be upon him) (in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him))."
3435,Abdul Wahid bin Ayman has mentioned him regarding his father. Both Ata and Mujahid have narrated hadiths regarding his father:
3436,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about something that is found in a residential area or a common passage, and he said: \You should announce it for a year", if its owner comes, then it is fine," otherwise it will be yours.\"" Al-Mal) is required to be paid. The narrator narrates) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost goat", and he said: Catch it because either you will find it or one of your brothers will find it or the wolf will find it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it alone, its feet and its belly are with it, it will reach water by itself and eat (leaves of) trees. (The narrator says) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the one who stole from the mountain, and he said, “Let him be beaten well, and he shall be punished twice.” He said: If dates are stolen from a drying place, and the value of the stolen goods is equal to a shield, then the hand will be cut off, and if it is less than that," then (the thief) will be beaten and he will be charged."""
3437,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand for stealing a piece of iron worth twenty-one dirhams.
3438,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever treats someone and he is not a physician (and the patient is harmed due to his treatment), then that person will pay the ransom."
3439,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever treats someone and he is not a physician (and the patient suffers loss of life or less due to his treatment), that person will pay the ransom. The same hadith is narrated as Mursal, a hadith with reference to another Sunnah."
3440,Sayyiduna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I met my maternal uncle. I inquired: He said: Are you going? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has sent me to a man who has married his father's wife. The Prophet (peace be upon him) has instructed me to behead him.
3441,Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person to a person who had married his father's wife to behead that person.
3442,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person belonging to the tribe of Islam came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he testified about himself four times that he had an illicit relationship with a woman. He said yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, (in such a way that) your private parts entered into his private parts like a stitch goes into a head-dress or a dowel goes into a well. He said yes. Allah (swt) asked what do you want by this? He replied, I want you to purify me, so he was stoned to death under the order of the Holy Prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men among his Companions talking. One of them said to the other: Look at this man. Allah kept his veil, but he himself did not let him stay and he was stoned like a dog. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Both of them said, O Messenger of Allah, we are here. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Come down here, both of you have to take your share of meat from this dead donkey. They both said, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah forgive you, who will eat its meat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The attack you have made on your brother's honor a little while ago is more serious than eating a dead body. By the One in whose hand is my life"," that person is taking a dip in the rivers of Paradise at that time.\"""""
3443,"Ibad bin Tamim narrates the statement of his uncle, who participated in the Battle of Badr: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a slave girl commits adultery, flog her, if she commits adultery again, flog her, if she commits it again, flog her, and sell her again, even if it is for a rope."
3444,"Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba (RA) narrates: A woman struck her husband with the wood of a tent, and the other woman was pregnant. The narrator narrates that one of the two women belonged to Banul Hiyan, so the Prophet (PBUH) imposed the payment of the dowry of the slain woman on the family of the murdered woman and ordered the payment of the ransom for the child in the womb of the slain woman. He who has neither eaten nor drunk anything, who has not cried (that is, has not been born), such blood goes in vain. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \Are you talking like the villagers?\"" The narrator says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory to pay the dowry."""
3445,"Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: There were two women, one of them killed the other with a wooden marker, so the Prophet (PBUH) imposed the payment of the dowry of the murdered woman on the family of the murdered woman and ordered the payment of the ransom for the child in the womb of the murdered woman. Then a villager said: Shall I pay the ransom? Whoever did not eat or drink did not scream and cry, such blood goes in vain. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \You are talking like a villager. The Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him," made it necessary to pay the ransom for the child in the woman's womb.\"""""
3446,"Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: A man belonging to the Huzail tribe had two wives. One of them killed the child in her stomach by pelting the other with a stone or perhaps with a tent wood. He who did not shout and cry (i.e. was not born), who did not drink anything, did not eat anything, or recited similar words, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Are you talking like the villagers?\"" The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory for the relatives of this woman to pay the ransom."""
3447,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: (In Madinah) Banu Qurayza and Banu Nazir were two clans. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent to Madinah, a man from Banu Nadir killed a man from Banu Qurayzah. Banu Qurayzah said: Hand him over to us, so that we may kill him (as revenge). They said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, is between us and you. This verse was revealed: \When you have to decide", decide between them with justice," the reward of life is life.\"""""
3448,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given this decision regarding the schools: he will have the rate of payment according to the contract of writing, according to the calculation, his duet will be the duet of a free person, and whatever payment remains on him, his duet will be the same as the duet of a slave."
3449,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The extent to which a person is free will be considered as a free person, and the extent to which he is a slave will be considered as a slave."
3450,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, says: Among the Children of Israel, there was a decree of retribution, but there was no decree of death among them, so Allah said to this Ummah: \Retribution has been decreed for you regarding the slain", the free for the free, the free for the slave, the slave for the woman," and whoever is forgiven by his brother.\"" Forgiveness here means that the other person is ready to accept the death penalty in the case of willful murder. That is", it is a reduction compared to the order that was imposed on the people before you," so Allah has given you a reduction in regard to it. You have received this reduction from your Lord."""
3451,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If a person peeps into someone's house without asking permission", and he (the owner of the house) pokes something in the eye of that (peeping) person with a sharp knife," then there will be no retribution or retribution.\"""""
3452,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: For ten dirhams (theft of something of value) the hand will be cut off and no mahr will be less than ten dirhams.
3453,"Mu'awiya bin Qura'ah narrates this statement from his father: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man to a man who had married his father's wife to behead him."
3454,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who apostatizes will be given respite and will not be killed.
3455,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about a woman who apostatizes, she will be kept alive."
3456,Ibn Abi Khaytmah narrates: Yahya bin Mu'in says: Sufyan al-Thawri used to object to Imam Abu Hanifah because of a hadith which Imam Abu Hanifah has narrated from Abu Razin regarding Asim and no one else has narrated it except Imam Abu Hanifah.
3457,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about an apostate woman: She will be imprisoned and not killed.
3458,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When women become apostates, they will not be killed."
3459,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about the apostate woman that she will be kept alive. Abu Asim says: Imam Abu Hanifa narrated this hadith regarding Asim, but I did not note it, I said: This tradition has been narrated to us regarding Sufyan, that is sufficient for us. Abu Asim says: We believe that Sufyan Al-Thawri has conspired with Imam Abu Hanifa in his death, so I have noted it regarding both of them."
3460,"Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In Damiya, payment of a camel is required. In Baa'ah, two camels are required to be paid. In Mutalahma, three camels are required to be paid. One-third payment will be required. When a person loses his mind as a result of killing him, it will be necessary to pay the full dowry. If (as a result of this multiplication) he coughs (with Yahch) and speaks in such a way that he does not understand what he is saying, then in that case the payment of the full dowry will be required. In case of injury to the eyelid, payment of one-fourth of the dayat will be required. In case of wounding the tip of the breast, payment of one-fourth of the doyet will be required."
3461,"Narrated Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala: He heard a member of the Leprosy tribe narrate this, he narrated this with reference to Adi, a member of his tribe: Sayyidna Adi stoned his wife as a result of which the woman died. and you will not inherit it."
3462,"Arwa narrated: When Marwan bin Huqam was the governor of Madinah, a person was brought before him who used to pick up children and sell them in some other place. His hand was cut off under the order of the Holy Prophet. Marwan also ordered the same about the child stealer and that person's hand was also cut off. Abdullah Bin Muhammad is unique in narrating this tradition from Hisham and he has made many mistakes (in narrating traditions) regarding Hisham."
3463,"Saeed Bin Musayyib says: A person was killed in Sana'a (Yemen city), then Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) had seven people killed in exchange for him, and he said, \If all the people living in Sana'a had participated in the killing of that person"," I would have killed all of them instead of that person.\"""""
3464,"Narrated Ubaidullah bin Umayrah: There was a man from Sana'a who used to come (home) before the people every year. One day he returned to his house and found seven men drinking with his maidservant (or wife). They caught him and killed him and threw him into a well. When the next person came and inquired about the first person, they said that he had already left. The person who came) went to relieve himself, and he saw some flies coming from the mill of the well, from which he realized that there was meat in it. He would have killed."
3465,"Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was sleeping on my cloak in the mosque. The cloak was worth thirty dirhams. A man came and took it from under me, (and tried to steal it). I will sell it and borrow its value (i.e. I will receive it later)."
3466,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah Radiyallahu Anhu was sleeping in the mosque and his cloak was under his head. A thief came and took off that cloak. Then this thief was brought to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He confessed the crime, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered his hand to be cut off. will The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Why didn't you think about this before bringing him to me?\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said", recommend to forgive the criminal until the matter reaches the ruler or the judge. When it reaches the ruler and the ruler forgives him," then Allah will not forgive the ruler."""
3467,"Hisham bin Arwah narrates this statement of his father: Sayyiduna Zubair made intercession about a thief, and someone said: First let this case be brought before the judge and then he will make intercession. So Sayyiduna Zubair said: When it reaches the judge, then Allah will curse the one who intercedes and the one to whom intercession (i.e. whoever accepts it) will be cursed, as the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said."
3468,"Farafsa Hanafi narrates: Some people took a thief with them and passed by Sayyidna Zubair (RA). He said: There is nothing wrong with it, until the matter is presented before the judge, when it is presented before the judge, Allah will not forgive him, even if the judge forgives him."
3469,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a person who had stolen his halah (the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), then he said, O Messenger of Allah, consider (that halah on my behalf) as haba (and do not punish him) then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why not?"
3470,"Hussain bin Munzar narrates: I was present with Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and Waleed bin Uqbah was brought before him. Hamran and another person testified against Waleed. Sayyidna Uthman said to Sayyidna Ali: Sayyidna Ali said to Hasan, Sayyidna Hasan said: Let the one who has this responsibility do this. He said: Stop now, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave forty lashes (to the drinker). A narrator named Abdul Aziz has narrated these words in his tradition: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) inflicted eight lashes, each of them is Sunnah (i.e. permissible), but I prefer it (punishment of forty lashes)."
3471,"Narrated by Nafi: A slave of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar ran away, he passed by some of the slaves of Sayyida Aisha, he stole a bag from those slaves, which contained dates, then he rode on the donkey of those slaves and ran away. Saeed said: I will not cut off the hand of a fugitive slave. Then Sayyida Aisha sent a message to (Ibn Umar) that my slaves are also your slaves. That slave was hungry (so he stole a bag of dates)."
3472,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this in his sermon: The \explained\"" wound will be five"," five (camels)."""
3473,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (From a social point of view), let the people of status pass through the gates, but the ruling of the limits is different (the limits will be extended to them)."
3474,Sayyidna Abu Barda bin Nayar (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that more than ten lashes should be inflicted only within the boundaries.
3475,"Ibn Muhairiz narrates: I asked Fazala bin Ubayd: What do you think about hanging a thief's hand around his neck, is it a Sunnah? He replied, \Yes", a thief was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet, upon the command of the Prophet, his hand was cut off, and then upon the command of the Prophet," that hand was hung around his neck.\"""""
3476,Hamza bin Abdullah narrates this statement from his father: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab used to flog (accusation of adultery) as punishment.
3477,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab used to issue a complete ban on (accusing adultery) as tareez.
3478,"Mu'awiya bin Qura narrated: A person said to another person: O son of a woman who smells a man's private parts (i.e. a woman who commits adultery)! So Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) caught him, he said: I have taken this meaning by him."
3479,"Umrah narrates: There was an argument between two men and one of them said: My mother was not an adulteress and my father was not an adulteress. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) consulted the people about this, so they said: This man has praised his father and mother (that they were not adulterers). Apply"
3480,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm to Najran, his letter also contained the following: ``Death for each tooth will be five camels, deat for all fingers will be ten, ten camels, deat for ear will be fifty camels, deat for eye will be fifty camels, deat for feet will be fifty camels, if the nose is cut off from the hump (i.e. the whole nose) then it will be full deat, in mumoma, wound, one-third of the deat of life should be given, and in the deet of Jaifa, one should pay one-third of deat of life."
3481,"Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Yemen, he wrote to him in a letter: \When the nose is cut off from the hump", full deed shall be paid for it, half deed shall be paid for the eye (for loss), half deed shall be paid for the foot, jaifah, one third deed shall be paid for the wound, mamuma, one third deet shall be paid for the wound, Manqla," the wound shall be paid for fifteen camels. Each of them) will have ten camels."""
3482,"Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Five camels will be required to be paid in the case of an \explained\"" wound", Mamoma, one-third of the duet will be required, Manqla, fifteen camels will be required to be paid, fifty camels will be required to be paid in the eye, when the nose is cut off from the hump, full duet will be required, the tooth will be five camels, the foot will be fifty camels," and each of the fingers and toes will be ten camels."""
3483,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, decreed the payment of five camels for wounds, while he decreed the payment of five camels for teeth and the payment of ten camels for each finger."
3484,"Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had decided to pay ten ten camels in his fingers. Shu'ba narrated a hadith from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Masrooq, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, and did not mention the narrator named Hameed. Shuba has mentioned in it that Ghalib heard hadiths from Masrooq."
3485,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \All fingers are equal.\"" A narrator named Shuba narrates: I inquired (of each of them) that ten camels would be ten. He replied yes. Abu Na'im Affan", Muslim and other narrators have narrated it in the same way. Wakiy, Wahib bin Jarir," narrated by Abu Nazr on the authority of Shu'ba."""
3486,Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the fingers (each of them being equal) will be ten camels.
3487,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The fingers of the hand and the toes are equal"," each of them will have the weight of ten camels.\"""""
3488,Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about the fingers (their allowance) would be ten camels.
3489,"Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about the fingers, (their diet) will be ten camels. A narrator named Abu Ash'ath is unique in narrating it and according to me it is not safe to narrate it from Qatadah, Allah knows best."
3490,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: The value of all the fingers, whether of the hands (fingers) or of the feet (the value of the fingers of each of them), will be ten camels or ten camels in terms of gold and silver."
3491,Hajiya bin Adi narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) had cut the hands of these people at the joints and (to stop the flow of blood) had put stains on them.
3492,Narrated Sha'bi: Sayyiduna Ali used to cut off the feet but leave the heel so that the man could support it.
3493,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I testify about Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he cut off the hands and feet of a thief.
3494,Abd al-Rahman bin Qasim narrates the statement of his father: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) intended to cut off (the second) foot (of the thief). One hand and one foot had already been cut off.
3495,"Narrated by Saeed bin Musaib: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a person kills his father, then kill him (as revenge)."
3496,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words added: I mentioned this tradition to Sufyan al-Thawri, and he said: I have heard this hadith from Abu Hazim, Abu Muhammad bin Sa’id also mentioned it in the same way that I did not hear it from Yahan, that this tradition was narrated from Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Mukhrami."
3497,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Injuring an animal will be in vain", the blood of one who falls into a well and dies in vain, the blood of one who dies by being buried in a mineral mine will be wasted, and the blood of one who dies by being kicked (by an animal) will be in vain. In Raqaz," one-fifth will be required to be paid.\"" The narrator has similarly mentioned the beating of the feet (of an animal) but this is an illusion and no one has followed him in the transmission of this word from Shu'ba."""
3498,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of a camel that damages it during the night will pay for it, but the owner of the camel will not pay for the damage that it causes during the day. (If they then cause any harm) then their feet will be cut off."
3499,"Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Abul Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance, (PBUH) saying, “Whoever falsely accuses a slave under his possession of adultery, and he (the slave) is innocent of what he has accused, then Allah will punish the accuser on the Day of Resurrection with as many lashes as possible. is)."
3500,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of Sayyidna Abul Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance, (PBUH) who falsely accuses his slave of adultery and he is acquitted of what he has accused, then Allah will punish the accuser on the Day of Resurrection with the same whipping."
3501,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled about the nose that if it is cut off completely, its deet will be complete (as much as the deet of the whole soul) and if the front part of it is cut off, its deet will be half."
3502,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: (the penalty for cutting off) the forty hands will be one-third of the duet, and if the eye has lost its light but is still in its place, then one-third of the duet will be required."
3503,"The son of Sayyidna Khuzima bin Thabit Ansari narrates this statement of his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whoever commits a punishable crime and is punished"," it will be an atonement for his sin.\"""""
3504,"The son of Sayyidna Khuzima bin Thabit Ansari narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whoever commits a crime and then is punished for that crime"," then it will be expiation for him.\"""""
3505,"It is narrated along with the same document that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever commits an act that Allah has forbidden, and then a limit is issued to that person, then it will be an atonement for the sinner.” A narrator named Osama bin Zayd has followed both of them in narrating it."
3506,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us: Pledge my allegiance on this matter. You will not associate anyone with Allah. You will not steal. You will not commit adultery. You will not kill your children. Whoever among you fulfills this (covenant) will be rewarded by Allah Almighty. Whoever commits one of these crimes and is punished for it, it will be an atonement for him."
3507,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I pledged allegiance to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with a few of my companions. Allah will reward him, and whoever commits one of these crimes, i.e. the limit of it will be extended to him, it will be a cause of purification for him, and whoever Allah hides, his case will be in the hands of Allah."
3508,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) who participated in the Battle of Badr and is one of the Naqba of the Night of Uqbah, narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the previous hadith). However, it contains these words: Whoever commits one of these crimes and is punished for it in this world, it will be expiation for him."
3509,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, “Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, the glory of Allah is greater than that He punishes that person again, and whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah covers it and forgives him, then the glory of Allah is greater than that He punishes him again for what He has already forgiven.”"
3510,"Qasim narrates that Sayyidna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, after cutting off the hand and foot (of a thief) wanted to cut off the other foot (for his third theft), then Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Sunnah is that (now) the hand should be cut off."
3511,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: In the era of Jahiliyya, there were four ways of marriage. One way of marriage was the one that is common among people today. Send a message and have intercourse with her, that person was separated from his wife during that time, and did not have intercourse with her wife until the pregnancy of the woman with whom the woman had intercourse was revealed to the other person, when the pregnancy of the woman was revealed, her real husband would have intercourse with her if he wanted, he did it so that his child would be the sperm of a member of a large family, the name of this marriage is Nikah Istba'ah. It was given. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The third method of marriage was that when some people gathered, their number was less than ten, they all went to a woman and they all had intercourse with her, then she would get pregnant and finally give birth to a child. was I have given birth to a child, O so-and-so! This is your son, if that woman were to name the person whom she wanted, then her child's lineage would be established with that person, that person could no longer deny this child. The fourth method was that many people would go together to a woman. That woman could not stop anyone who came to her. These women used to be prostitutes. They used to have special flags on their doors. There was a symbol of the young man's profession. The person who wanted to go to them would call. would place his child with the person, with whom that child resembled, then people would call that child as that person's son and that person could not deny it."
3512,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that there were four types of marriages during the time of Jahiliyyah (after that she has mentioned according to the previous hadith). In one tradition, these words are added: (The husband would say to his wife) You send a message to such and such a person, then you have intercourse with him. During this time, the husband of this woman would stay away from her and would not have intercourse with the woman until the person with whom the woman had intercourse became pregnant. had gone The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but the names are these words (the husband would say to his wife:) You send a message to such and such a person and get pregnant from him. Muhammad bin Ishaq narrates: It is true (it also contains these words:) When Allah sent Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, He abolished the nikah (various methods of marriage) of the age of ignorance."
3513,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: In the time of Jahiliyyah, a person used to say to another, “You let me have intercourse with your wife, I will let you have intercourse with my wife, and I will give you more (benefits).” So Allah revealed this verse: The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Uyaina bin Hisn al-Fazari, may God bless him and grant him peace, attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present with Sayyida Aisha, may God bless him and grant him peace. At that time, Ayyaena entered without seeking permission. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ayyaena, why did you not take permission? He said, O Messenger of Allah, since I became an adult, I have not asked permission to enter from any member of the dangerous tribe. He also said: Who is this beautiful lady by your side? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Aisha, the mother of all believers. He said: Shall I not replace her and give you a more beautiful woman? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Ayyna! Allah Ta'ala has declared this act as haram. The narrator says) When that person left, Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) inquired, O Messenger of Allah, who was this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was a foolish leader, you have seen his (mental state) yet he is the leader of his people."
3514,"Abu Barda quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father: There is no marriage without a guardian."
3515,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3516,"Abd al-Rahman Hamzani, in his chain of transmission, has quoted it from Israel as Ibn Sinan has quoted it. Muhammad Ibn Mukhlid says: Abd al-Rahman said to Hamzani: Gaya, Shu'ba and Sufyan both narrated it as a muquf, tradition up to Abu Barda, so he said: The tradition narrated by Isra'il regarding Abu Ishaq is more favorite to me than the tradition transmitted by Sufyan and Shu'ba."
3517,Dalaj bin Ahmar has quoted this saying of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi along with his chain of transmission: Israel remembered the traditions of Abu Ishaq in the same way that they remembered Surah Fatiha. Salih says: Israel especially (transcribes) the traditions of Abu Ishaq more safely.
3518,Abu Barda quotes the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari) that there is no marriage without a guardian.
3519,"Abu Saeed says: A marriage is not valid without guardians, witnesses and dower, but the marriage of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) can also take place without them."
3520,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that if a woman marries without the permission of a guardian, her marriage will be invalid, her marriage will be invalid, her marriage will be invalid, if a man has intercourse with her, then because of this act of the man, the woman will receive a dowry."
3521,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A marriage cannot take place without a guardian and two just witnesses. A narrator named 'Adi bin Fazl narrated it as a Marfu' Hadith, while other narrators did not narrate it as a Marfu' Hadith."
3522,"Abu Salama narrates: I asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA): How much did the Prophet (PBUH) respect his wives? So Sayyida Aisha said twelve oqiyah and, Nish. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa inquired, do you know what is meant by Nish, it means half an ounce and (the total amount of dowry) is five hundred dirhams."
3523,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was among us, we used to pay ten ounces of Mahr."
3524,"Sayyidna Hasan Basri says: Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar (RA) married his sister, her husband divorced her, I married you to my (honorable sister) and you divorced her, now you have sent a message of marriage. \When you divorce women", and their period of marriage is completed, do not forbid them to marry (their former) husbands. This hadith is authentic. Imam Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, narrated it from Yunus on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdul Warith, and on the authority of Ahmad bin Abu Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman," on the authority of Yunus."""
3525,"Hasan al-Basri narrates about Allah's saying: So do not forbid these women to marry (their former) husbands, if they agree (to remarry) properly. Hasan al-Basri said: Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar Muzni (may God be pleased with him) told me: This verse was revealed about him. Then you have come with the message of marriage, no! By Allah, you will never be able to get him again, Sayyiduna Muqal says: There was no other defect in this person, and that woman also wanted to marry him again, so Allah revealed this verse. (Narrated by Sayyidna Muaqal, may Allah be pleased with him) I said: O Messenger of Allah, now I will do the same, then I married the woman to this person."
3526,"Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I had a sister, some people approached her for marriage, but I forbade them, then my cousin came to me, he sent a message of marriage to this girl, so I married the girl to him, as long as Allah permitted, they both stayed together, then the person divorced the girl, in which he had room to approach, but the person did not approach, until That the girl's period has passed, after that she also sent a marriage message along with other people, so I said: I did not marry this girl to any of the other people, and I married her to you, but you divorced her, in which there was room for appeal, but you did not appeal, until her period passed, now when her relationship is coming, you also sent a relationship. The verse was revealed (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) this verse was revealed. \When you divorce women and their periods are completed"," do not forbid them from remarrying (their former) husbands.\"" (Narrated by Sayyiduna Muaqal"," may Allah be pleased with him) I expiate my oath and married this girl to this person. The meaning of this narration is close (to each other)."""
3527,"Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (RA) narrates: My sister was the wife of a man, he divorced her until her period passed, then the person sent a message of marriage, so Sayyidna Muqal (RA) got angry at this, he said, he had left the girl even though he could have approached her. \When you divorce women and their periods are completed"," do not forbid them from remarrying.\"""""
3528,"Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman narrates the statement of his paternal aunt Sakina bint Hantala: Imam Hamad al-Baqir (RA) asked for permission to come to me. At that time, my husband's death had not yet passed. He said: \You are aware of my relationship with the Prophet (PBUH) and my relationship with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and my status among the Arabs (I want to marry you). I said: O Abu Ja'far", may God forgive you. is used, and you are giving me a marriage message during my Idda, so Imam Baqir (RA) said, I told you about my relationship with the Prophet (SAW) and with Sayyiduna Ali (RA), when the Prophet (SAW) took Umm Salama (to give her a message of marriage) to him, she was performing the Idda (married after the death of Sayyidna Abu Salama). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," (O Umm Salamah) you know that I am the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one and my position in my nation (you are aware of it)."""
3529,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Four things are necessary in a marriage: the guardian, the husband, (or wife) and the double. The narrator named Abul Hasib Nafi bin Mesra is unknown."
3530,"Narrated by Ikrama bin Khalid: I met some horsemen on the way. One of them, a Saiba woman, entrusted the matter of her marriage to a person who was not her guardian, (to marry her), so that person married her."
3531,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no marriage without valid and just witnesses.\"""""
3532,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no marriage without a guardian and two righteous witnesses.\"""""
3533,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Marriage cannot take place without a guardian and two righteous witnesses. If those guardians disagree", then the one who has no guardian," the ruler of time is his guardian.\"" This tradition is narrated along with some other isnads"," but there are some word differences in it."""
3534,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \There is no marriage without a guardian and two righteous witnesses.\"""""
3535,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \No woman should marry another woman"," no woman can marry herself. A woman who commits adultery marries herself.\"""""
3536,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, \No woman should marry another woman; no woman can marry herself.\"" (The narrator says) We said: We used to say: A woman who marries herself is a fajra (adulteress"," evildoer)."""
3537,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3538,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: We used to say that a woman who marries herself is an adulteress.
3539,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: No woman can marry another woman, no woman can marry herself, an adulterous woman can marry herself without the permission of her guardian."
3540,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman can marry another woman, no woman can marry herself, a prostitute does her own marriage. A narrator named Ibn Sirin narrates: Sometimes Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) used the word Zania for her."
3541,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates as a hadith: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No woman can marry another woman, nor can a woman marry herself."
3542,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, says: A woman can marry only with the permission of her guardian (if she is not a guardian), then she can marry with the permission of a wise person of her family or the ruler of the time."
3543,"Sha'bi narrated: In the matter of marrying (a woman) without a guardian, the most strict among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he used to punish (committing this act)."
3544,Syedna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that marriage does not take place without the permission of a guardian.
3545,"It has been narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He married the daughter of his uncle Sayyidna Uthman Bin Mazoon (RA). Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The father of this girl came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “My daughter dislikes this relationship.” The Prophet (PBUH) instructed Ibn Umar (RA) to divorce her. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, separated from him. The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \Do not marry girls until their opinion is known. If they remain silent (in response)"," it will be their permission.\"" The narrator narrates: Later", Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) married this girl. A narrator named Ibn Abi Wahhab has not heard it from Nafi," he has narrated it from Nafi on the authority of Umar bin Husain."""
3546,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: My uncle, Sayyidna Qudama bin Maz’un (RA) married the daughter of his brother Sayyidna Uthman bin Maz’un (RA) to me. O Messenger of Allah, this is my niece. I am her father's heir. I did not abuse this girl. I married her to a person whose virtues and kinship (to us) you are also aware of. The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \She is a girl"," and a girl is more entitled to her own affairs.\"" got married Shaykh says: Muhammad bin Ishaq did not hear this tradition from Nafi", he heard it from Umar bin Hussain. Ibrahim ibn Sa'd has narrated this tradition in the same way on his account," while Muhammad ibn Salama has followed it on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq as being transmitted from Umar ibn Husain."""
3547,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun (RA) died, he left behind a daughter whose mother was Sayyida Khula bint Hakim. Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun bequeathed it to his brother Sayyidna Qudama bin Mazoun. These two gentlemen were my uncles. Then Sayyidna Mugheera (RA) went to the girl's mother and offered her more wealth, so she inclined towards him. The girl preferred her mother's wishes. The matter of these people was presented to the Prophet (PBUH), then Sayyidna Qudama said, \O Messenger of Allah", this is my niece. My brother had bequeathed her to me. I will marry her to Ibn Umar. I will improve her and our relationship. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “This is a girl, and she cannot be married without her consent.” (Ibn Umar says) “By Allah, she had become the owner (that is, marriage, but because of this decree of the Prophet, peace be upon him), she was separated from me, and her family married her to Sayyidna Mughira bin Shu’bah," may God be pleased with her.”"""
3548,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun left a girl (among the survivors), my uncle Sayyidna Qudama bin Mazoun married her to me, he did not know the girl's will in this regard, he was the boy's uncle, the girl spoke to the Prophet about this, and the Prophet declared her marriage void. If they did, (the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or Sayyidna Qudama) married that girl to him (ie Sayyidna Mugheera)."
3549,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) married his daughter Zainab bint Uthman after the death of Sayyidna Uthman bint Uthman. This marriage was arranged by the girl's uncle Sayyidna Qudama. Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba offered her a large dowry, so the girl's mother said to the girl: \Don't keep (the marriage made by her uncle).\"" Then this girl and her mother told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled this marriage."""
3550,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A girl should be married with her permission.
3551,"Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid (RA) and Sayyidna Majma’ bin Yazid (RA) say: Sayyidna Khuzam (RA) married his daughter, Khunsa, that woman did not like that person, she was a Thaiba (widow or divorcee)."
3552,"It is narrated about Sayyida Khansaa, may Allah be pleased with her, that she was a widow, her father married her to a man from Banuuf, she wanted to marry a woman named Abul Baba bin Abdul Mundhir, her matter was presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed her father to marry her according to her wishes."
3553,"Abu Salama narrates: A woman from the Ansar family of Banu Umar and Bin Awf, whose name was Khunsa bint Khudam, was married to her by her father, she was Thaiba. Married to Munzar, and had Sayyidna Abul Baba's son, Sa'ib."
3554,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The father of Sayyida Khansa bint Khudam (RA) married her (to this husband). She disliked the woman. She came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and mentioned her matter to the Prophet (PBUH), so the Prophet (PBUH) annulled her marriage. Then Sayyidna Abul Baba Bin Abdul Manzar married her, and with her, Sayyidna Abul Baba Sahibzada, Saib, was born, the woman was a Saiba (widow or divorcee)."
3555,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A girl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father, who is the best of fathers, married me to his nephew so that because of me he would be inferior, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this girl the option (to annul the marriage). That the father has no authority about this."
3556,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A girl came to him (after this the hadith is in the next hadith). Narrated by Abdullah bin Burida: A girl came to the service of Sayyida Aisha (RA) and said: \My father has married me to his nephew so that because of me his inferior status will improve. I don't like it. Sayya Aisha said, 'You sit until the Prophet comes. I will present the matter before you.' So, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the girl's father, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the girl the option (of maintaining or annulling the marriage). A narrator named Ibn Junayd narrated these words: He said, O Messenger of Allah," I maintain what he has done."""
3557,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A woman came to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not there. She sat down and waited for the Prophet (peace be upon him). Better yet, my father has not known my will in this matter, so do I have any authority over myself? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Yes","\"" said the woman"," \""I do not want to reject what my father has done"," but I want women to know that they have a choice about themselves or not.\"" Shaykh says: All these hadiths are transmissions"," because the narrator named Ibn Burida did not hear the hadiths from Sayyida Aisha."""
3558,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: A man married one of his virgin daughters, he did not ask the girl's permission, the girl came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) annulled her marriage. A narrator named Abu Bakr has narrated these words, that girl was a virgin (and her marriage) without his permission, she came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet made a separation between them."
3559,Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: A man married his daughter.
3560,"Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him), a man married his virgin daughter. The girl disliked the relationship. Shaykh says: It is correct that this hadith is transmitted and the statement of a narrator named Shoaib is an illusion."
3561,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) (followed by the previous hadith) The narrator narrates this hadith on the authority of Ata, the Messenger, as a hadith, just as it is on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
3562,"Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, separated a woman from her husband, she was a virgin, her father had married her, and the woman did not like this relationship."
3563,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled the marriage of a virgin girl and a pregnant woman. Their father married them both and they did not like (this relationship), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled their marriage. On the authority of Abu Kathir on the authority of Mahajar bin Ikrimah, it is transmitted as a messenger tradition from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
3564,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3565,Muhajar bin Ikramah has narrated a tradition similar to this regarding the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him).
3566,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A girl's father married her, she did not like (this relationship), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the option (to keep or annul the marriage). A narrator named Abu Khorasan narrated that a girl came to the Prophet's service and mentioned that her father had married her without her permission, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the couple. The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Ikrima with reference to another chain of transmission, while other narrators have quoted it as a transmission from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding Ikrimah, and it is correct that it is a transmission."
3567,"Abu Salama narrates: A man from Banu Mundhir married his daughter, the girl did not like (that relationship), she came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the Prophet (peace be upon him) annulled her marriage."
3568,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3569,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: A man married his daughter. The girl did not like the relationship, so the Prophet (PBUH) separated them."
3570,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: A man married his virgin daughter. The girl did not like the relationship. She came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet declared the marriage invalid. This hadith is not proven on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayb, on the authority of Nafi, but it is correct that it is on the authority of Umar Ibn Husayn on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayb, as has already been said."
3571,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) with his daughter, and said, \My daughter is refusing to marry.\"" What is the husband's right over his wife? If there is an abscess in the husband's nose from which pus and material is coming out", and the woman licks it with her tongue, even if she licks it with her tongue, she will not pay the husband's right, so the woman said: By the One who sent the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth," I will not marry."""
3572,"Sumak bin Harb narrates: A person came to the service of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and said: There is a girl, I am her guardian, she has married without my permission, then Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: Our opinion about what this girl has done is that if she has married me, we will uphold her, and if she has married someone who is not her kafou, then we (have the authority to uphold her). or cancel option) will give you."
3573,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A virgin girl should not be married until her permission is obtained, and Saiba has authority over her own person, unless she invites resentment. Ishaq says: I inquired from Jesus: Is the last part of the tradition transmitted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He replied, \No"," the tradition is the same.\"""""
3574,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A female (widow or divorced woman) should not be married until her will is known, and a virgin should not be married until the adhan is taken from her and her adhan is silent."
3575,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said: The Saiba (widow or divorced woman) is more entitled to her affairs, and permission will be taken from a virgin girl, her permission is her silence. Muammar has narrated something different from both of them in his chain of transmission, he has omitted the mention of a person from the chain of transmission, similarly, Mu'mar has narrated something different from both of them in the text of this hadith and has quoted the tradition in other words, but he has been deceived in this, because every narrator who has narrated it with reference to Abdullah bin Fazl and every narrator who has narrated it with Abdullah bin Fazl from Nafi bin Jubeer, all of them have narrated a different tradition from Muammar. And the agreement of all these narrators to narrate different narrations from Muammar is proof that Muammar is delusional about this and Allah knows best."
3576,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A virtuous woman has more rights over her own self than her husband, and permission will be taken from a virgin girl regarding her own self, and her permission will be silent."
3577,Abdullah bin Raja narrated the same tradition (the above-mentioned hadith) through his chain of transmission.
3578,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian has no authority over the daughter-in-law, and her will will be known from the virgin, and her silence will be her confession."
3579,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The guardian has no authority over the daughter-in-law", and his will will be known from the virgin," and her silence will be pleasing to him.\"" Muammar has narrated it in the same way", the tradition that has passed before it is more correct in terms of chain and text, because the narrator named Saleh did not hear it from Nafi bin Jubeer, he heard it from Abdullah bin Fazl. I have heard Shaykh Abu Bakr Neshapuri say that, in my opinion," Muammar has made a mistake in this regard."""
3580,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A virgin girl will be asked about her will, and her silence will be regarded as her consent. Abu Dawud Tayalasi has narrated it in the same way with his authority."
3581,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virtuous woman has more rights about herself than her guardian, and the will of a virgin girl will be known, and her silence will be permitted."
3582,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virtuous woman has more rights over herself than her guardian, and her father will find out her will (about her) from a virgin girl. A narrator named Amr has quoted these words: His permission will be his silence."
3583,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, all its narrators have copied the word, al-Thayb."
3584,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A virtuous woman has more rights about herself than her guardian, and her will will be known from a virgin girl, and if she remains silent, it will be considered her consent.”"
3585,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “A beautiful woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and her will will be known from a virgin girl, and her permission will be her silence.” Shaykh says: There is a possibility that the word virgin girl used in this hadith refers to a virgin orphan girl. Well, Allah knows best. The reason for this is that we have mentioned this in other narrations narrated by Salih bin Qaisan and after him. Ibn Uyynah quoted these words in reference to Ziyad bin Saad: Her father will take permission from a virgin girl, so according to our knowledge, no narrator has mentioned Ibn Uyynah about these words. It may be that he mentioned this hadith based on his memory and his language was wrong, Allah knows best. The same tradition has been narrated from Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Abu Barda, that the will of an orphan girl will be ascertained."
3586,"Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The will of the orphan girl will be ascertained about her self. If she remains silent", then he has given permission, but if she refuses," then she will not be forced.\"" A narrator named Abu Quttan narrates: I asked Yunus"," have you heard this tradition from him? (The narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) Heard from Abu Barda? He replied yes."""
3587,"Abu Burdah narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \The will of an orphan girl will be ascertained; if she remains silent", it will be considered as permission, and if she refuses," she will not be forced.\"" Ibn Fazil", Waqiyyah, Yahya bin Adam, Abdullah bin Dawud," Abu Qutaiba and other narrators have narrated it on the authority of Yunus bin Abu Ishaq."""
3588,"Abu Barda narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The will of an orphan girl will be ascertained about her self, and her permission will be her silence."
3589,"Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that an orphan girl will be asked about her will, and if she agrees, she will be married, and if she does not agree, then she will not be married."
3590,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A female (widow or divorced woman) has more ownership (rights) of her affairs than her guardian, and permission will be sought from a virgin girl regarding her status, and her silence will be her confession."
3591,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to come and marry a woman in return for a souvenir.
3592,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: We asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the dowry of women, and he (PBUH) said that its amount will be whatever the people decide between themselves."
3593,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man marries a woman with a handful of grains (the condition of dowry), then this will be dowry. Nishapuri has quoted this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) in his hadith with reference to Muhammad bin Muslim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man gives two fistfuls of grain (as dowry) to a woman, then that woman will become halal for that person, (that is, that grain will be accepted as dowry in marriage)."
3594,Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: We used to get married in exchange for a handful of grain during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH).
3595,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Whoever fills both fists in marriage has made the marriage lawful.\"" The narrator explains: Here are probably the words for flour", grain, yastu. The narrator named Ibn Sinan has quoted these words which the narrator says in the person Mahr: Here are probably the words for date," satu or flour. At the end of the hadith are these words) so he made it halal."""
3596,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person makes a witness, there will be no harm to him, whether he marries for a small amount of wealth (as dowry) or for a large amount of wealth."
3597,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no sin on a man when he makes a witness, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth as a dowry.”"
3598,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin on a man when he makes a witness, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth (as a dowry)."
3599,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man makes a witness, it will not harm him, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth (as a dowry)."
3600,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \Marry Thayba.\"" The Prophet", may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said this three times. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Whatever the family is pleased with"," even if it is only a branch of the yellow tree.\"""""
3601,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Marry women only in Kufu, let them be married only by saints, and the dowry should not be less than ten dirhams."
3602,Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams.
3603,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the mahr should not be less than ten dirhams.
3604,Shaabi says: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams.
3605,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The dowry should not be less than five dirhams.
3606,It is narrated along with another chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams.
3607,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him): Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says: The dowry will be whatever the husband and wife agree on."
3608,"Urwa narrates about Sayyida Umm Habiba (may God be pleased with her): She was previously the wife of Abdullah bin Jahsh. A narrator named Abd al-Razzaq narrated this: Sayyidah Umm Habiba's first husband was Ubaidullah bin Jahsh, who was a Christian."
3609,"Urwa narrates about Sayyida Umm Habiba, may Allah be pleased with her: She was the wife of Ubaydullah bin Jahsh. Ubaydullah died in Abyssinia, so Najashi married Sayyida Umm Habiba, may God bless him and grant him peace, and paid her four thousand dirhams as a dowry on his behalf, and then, along with Sayyidana Shahrabeel bin Hasnah, may God bless him and grant him peace, she was in the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Madinah). Munora) sent."
3610,Ubaidullah Ashjajai narrates: I said to Sufyan: Dawood has quoted the saying of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Sha'bi that the dowry will not be less than ten dirhams.
3611,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (RA) narrates: We were present with the Prophet (PBUH) and a woman came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and presented herself for marriage. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, \Do you have anything (to pay as dowry)?\"" He said"," \""I have nothing.\"" He said"," \""I don't even have an iron ring", but I will divide my cloak into two parts and give it to him," and I will keep half for myself.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said"," \""No.\"" He said yes", the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Go", in exchange for the Qur'an that comes to you," I have married you to her.\"""""
3612,"The same tradition has been quoted with reference to some other isnads. In it, the narrator named Thauri has quoted these words: I marry you to the Qur'an that comes to you."
3613,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man stood up who was wearing a cloak, which he tied around his neck. He said, O Messenger of Allah, I will marry him. He said, O Messenger of Allah, there is no Prophet. He said to them, sit down. Then the woman came again. She said, O Messenger of Allah, state your opinion about me. The same gentleman stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ask you if you have wealth? He said, O Messenger of Allah, no, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \You sit down!\"" Then the woman came again and said", O Messenger of Allah, tell me your opinion about me. The same gentleman stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ask you if you have wealth? He asked, O Messenger of Allah, not the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said yes, Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah al-Mushun (remembered orally). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""I marry you to her on the condition that you will teach her to read the Qur'an and teach her", and when Allah gives you sustenance," you will give her dowry. So he married this woman on this condition.\"" Narrator named Utbah bin Sakin is unique in narrating this hadith and it is a lost hadith."""
3614,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to a person, \You should marry this woman"," even if it is in exchange for an iron ring.\"""""
3615,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may God be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari married a woman during illness. The people said: This is not permissible and it (inheritance) will be counted as a third share.
3616,"Saeed bin Musayb narrates this statement of an Ansari Sahabi: I married a virgin without seeing her, (after leave) when I came to her she was pregnant. The same hadith is narrated from Safwan bin Salim with reference to another chain of transmission."
3617,"Sayyidna Basra bin Abu Basra Ghafari narrates: He married a virgin girl without seeing her, later he found that girl pregnant, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two husbands and wives."
3618,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Should I not tell you about the rented ox?\"" The people said yes. The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said"," \""He is a person who makes halalah.\"" Then he","3619""",Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Asila means companionship.
3620,"Sayyidna Aiz bin Amr Muzni (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Islam is exalted, it cannot be defeated."
3621,"Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: I sent a marriage message to a woman, the Prophet (PBUH) asked me, have you seen her? I did not say: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at her because in this way love will be born between the two of you. A narrator named Abu Shahab has narrated these words: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sent a marriage message to a woman. The following words are as before."
3622,"Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to marry. He mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and see this woman, because as a result of this, love will develop between you two. The narrator narrates: He did so and then married that woman, after which the narrator mentions their concord. This is correct: This hadith is narrated from Bikramzni on the authority of Thabit."
3623,"Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) (after that, according to the earlier hadith)."
3624,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A man intended to marry an Ansar woman, so the Prophet (PBUH) said: Look at her, because there is something in the eyes of the women of the Ansar."
3625,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the remarriage of his daughter Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with him) with Sayyidna Abul-Aas bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him). This tradition is not proven, the narration narrated by the narrator named Hajjaj cannot be presented as proof."
3626,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) had sent his daughter Sayyida Zainab (RA) to Sayyiduna Abul-Aas bin Rabi (RA) on the basis of her first marriage, but the Prophet (PBUH) did not allow her to marry again."
3627,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates: My sister was the wife of an Ansari. This Ansari married her on the condition of paying a garden (as dowry). There was disagreement between the two of them. They presented their case to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Give her back her garden. This divorces you.\"" Then the woman said"," \""Okay", I can give her more, Prophet," may God bless him and grant him peace.\"" He said"," \""You return his garden and pay him more.\"""""
3628,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said, O Messenger of God, I am not angry with him regarding his morals or religion, but I do not like ungrateful (husband) after becoming a Muslim. He said, O Thabit, take your garden and divorce him."
3629,"Abu Zubair narrates: Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (RA) married Zainab bint Abdullah, Sayyidna Thabit gave her a garden as a dowry, she did not like him. The woman said, \Yes"," I can give more with her.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," \""There is no need to pay more"," just return the garden.\"" The woman said"," \""Okay.\"" The Prophet", peace and blessings of God be upon him, narrates: Sayyidna Thabit, may God be pleased with him," decided to return the garden and divorce the woman."""
3630,"Ata narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, A man should not take from a divorced woman more than what he gave her (as dowry)."
3631,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, obtained a divorce from her husband, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fixed her period of one and a half months."
3632,"Ikrimah narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may God be pleased with her, obtained Khula from her husband, so the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fixed her period as one period."
3633,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, obtained Khula from him, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed this woman to remain in Idda until one period."
3634,Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that he instructed the wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (RA) to perform ``Idah'' until one menstrual period when she obtained divorce from (her husband).
3635,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
3636,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3637,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
3638,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
3639,"Narrated Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Among the signs of the Last Day is this: Shepherds of goats will become rulers of the people, and barefoot, naked bodies, (i.e. scantily clad) hungry people will build buildings higher than each other, and the maid will give birth to her master."
3640,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth, or intercourse with a young girl until she menstruates (i.e. she becomes an adult)."
3641,"Hasan bin Muhammad and Abdullah bin Muhammad narrate this statement of their father: Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), do you not know this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating (the meat of) domesticated donkeys and having fun."
3642,"Ayyas bin Salamah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Salamah bin Akwa, may Allah be pleased with him): On the occasion of the Battle of Uttas, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted to have intercourse with women for three days, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
3643,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade sexual intercourse with women. He said that Allah had made it lawful for the people during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, the number of women was less and then it was made forbidden for the people. Now, if a person commits this act, he will be punished."
3644,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The laws of marriage, divorce, inheritance and inheritance have declared Mutah to be haram (the narrator is in doubt or perhaps these are the words)."
3645,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Mut'ah.
3646,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: He separated the husband and wife."
3647,"Qudama says: I asked Saeed bin Musaib about the marriage of a person in the state of Ihram, and he said that separation will be done between the two husbands and wives."
3648,Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A person in the state of Ihram can neither marry himself nor marry anyone.
3649,Ikramah bin Khalid narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) about a woman with whom a person who is outside Makkah wants to marry and he is going to perform Umrah or Hajj.
3650,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself, nor can he marry anyone, nor can he give the message of marriage."
3651,"Nafi' narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: He may have quoted this as the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
3652,Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said: A person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself nor can he marry anyone.
3653,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram at that time."
3654,"Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, he was not in Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) left, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was not in Ihram."
3655,"Yazid bin Asm narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimuna, he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimuna passed away, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was not in the state of Ihram."
3656,"Sayyida Maimoona bint Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at the place of Saraf, and we were not in the state of Ihram at that time."
3657,"Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, both of them were not in Ihram."
3658,"Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maimuna (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Maimuna (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away, the Prophet (may Allah's prayers and peace be upon him) was not in the state of Ihram."
3659,"Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was not in the state of Ihram, and when Sayyida Maimunah left, he was not in the state of Ihram either. A narrator named Dawood Abu Amr is Dawood Ibn Zubarqan."
3660,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mahmiyah bin Jaz and two people to Sayyidah Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him) to give her the message of marriage. (uncle) entrusted to Sayyidna Abbas (RA) then Sayyidna Abbas (RA) arranged the marriage of Sayyida Maimuna with the Prophet (PBUH).
3661,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in the state of Ihram at that time."
3662,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in a good condition at that time."
3663,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), both of them were not in good health."
3664,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyida Maimunah (RA), he was not in a good condition at that time."
3665,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3666,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) got married (with Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him)) he was not in a state at that time.
3667,Narrated Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa about this saying of Allah: \And if you fear that you will not be able to do justice to the orphan girls," then marry two or four of the women you like.\"" Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa", may Allah be pleased with her, said: O my nephew, this refers to an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth. If that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of this girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay dowry according to justice. Marry the girls or ask the Ansar to give them Mahrad. These people were ordered to marry other women whom they did not like. Narrated ``Urwa: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: After this verse, people asked various questions about it," so Allah revealed this verse: \""People ask you about women: Say: Allah commands you about them", and about the orphan girls that have been recited in the Book," the orphan girls whom you do not pay what they have been appointed for youth and you are interested in marrying them.\"" What Allah has mentioned here", that the verses of the Book of Allah that have been recited before you, refers to the previous verse," in which Allah Almighty said: \""And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with the orphan girls fairly"," then the women you like best.\"" Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: In the second verse", Allah says: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that people were forbidden to marry orphan girls whom they were attracted to by their wealth and beauty: when they paid them according to justice, this was because if such girls had little wealth or less beauty," the guardians should not be attracted to them."""
3668,"Narrated ``Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha (RA) about this saying of Allah: And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with orphan girls justly, marry two or four of the women you like.'' Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) said: O my nephew, this means an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth. If that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of this girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay as dowry according to justice. So the people were forbidden to marry these girls in this way, or else to marry them justly (i.e. according to common custom) and they were ordered to marry other women. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, said: In the second verse, Allah Ta'ala has said: \And you do not take heart in marrying them.\"" That is", a person is not interested in marrying an orphan girl who is brought up under his care, whose wealth and beauty are less, so people were forbidden to marry those orphan girls whose wealth and beauty people are interested in (because otherwise) their interest ends," but if they do away with them according to justice (the ruling will be different)."""
3669,"Narrated Urwa bin Zubair: He asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) about this saying of Allah: And if you fear that you will not be able to deal with orphan girls justly, then marry two, or three or four women whom you like. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O my nephew, this means an orphan girl who was brought up by a person, and that girl was a sharer in his wealth, and if that person was interested in the wealth and beauty of that girl, then the guardian wanted to marry her, so that she would not have to pay the dowry according to justice. Marry these girls, or rather give them Mehrad Akrin justly (i.e. according to common custom). These people were ordered to marry other women. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: Then the people asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Allah revealed this verse. \People ask you about women", then say, Allah commands you about them, and about the orphan girls that have been recited in the Book, to whom you do not pay what is prescribed for a young man," and you are interested in marrying her.\"" Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: In this verse", Allah Ta'ala has explained this command to the people, if someone is beautiful and rich, then people are interested in marrying her, but they do not give her full Mahrada according to the general custom, but if the girl is lacking in terms of beauty and wealth, then they do not marry her, but look for other women. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha: When these people do not feel interested in such girls and they abandon them, then they do not have the right to marry such girls when they feel attracted to them," but if they treat them fairly and pay the dowry in full (then the ruling will be different). Their subject is mutually exclusive."""
3670,"Hisham bin Urwah narrates the statement of Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding his father (Urwah bin Zubair): If you fear that you will not be able to do justice to the orphan girls, then marry those women whom you like. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: It means an orphan girl who was raised by a person, that person was the guardian of that girl, and then married her because of her wealth, but he did not want to keep her with him and did not deal with her fairly even in wealth."
3671,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Avoid marrying four types of people: madness, insanity, leprosy (leprosy) leprosy."
3672,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: If a woman is married to a person fraudulently, and the woman has insanity, leprosy, or leprosy, the woman will receive dowry, because the man has had intercourse with her, and the man will receive the dowry from the guardian of the woman, who married her fraudulently."
3673,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, gave this ruling regarding a woman suffering from insanity, if her husband has sexual relations with her, then separation will be made between the two wives."
3674,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is not permissible to sell four types of women (whether they are concubines) or to marry them (if they are freedmen), a mad woman, a leprosy woman, a leprous woman, and a woman suffering from the disease of genital swelling."
3675,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \Whoever marries a woman who is insane, leprous, fecund, fertile, or has an obstacle in her private life, then that woman is considered his wife. If a man wishes, he should let her live with him," otherwise he should divorce her.\"""""
3676,Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Amr ibn al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Sayyidna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) about the constant fear of harming his wife.
3677,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \No lawful thing becomes unlawful because of something forbidden.\"""""
3678,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who commits a forbidden act with a woman and then marries her daughter, or marries a woman's mother after committing a forbidden act with a woman."
3679,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): No haram thing makes a haram thing haram.
3680,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a person who had committed adultery with a woman and then later wanted to marry the same woman or perhaps her daughter. The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Nothing forbidden does not make something lawful. Haram is established only when marriage has taken place first.\"""""
3681,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was asked about a man who commits a forbidden act: then later they want to marry, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Their act was adultery, but the second act (will be considered marriage)."
3682,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Allah will not have mercy on a person who looks at the private parts of a woman and her daughter. This hadith) is suspended and the narrator named Hamad bin Abu Sulaiman has been declared weak.
3683,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama accepted Islam and had ten wives. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him: He should keep four of them with him, and separate from the rest. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Safwan Bin Umayyah accepted Islam, he had eight wives, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to keep four of them with him and to separate from the rest."
3684,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama (RA) accepted Islam. He had ten wives. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to marry four of them.
3685,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salamah accepted Islam, he had ten wives during the time of Jahiliyyah. These women also accepted Islam with him. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to adopt four of them. A narrator named Ramadi narrates: The people of Basra narrated in the same way."
3686,"Uthman bin Abu Sawid narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this to Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama, when he accepted Islam and he had ten wives at that time, (the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said) Keep four of them with you and separate from the rest."
3687,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3688,Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this to a man belonging to the Thaqeef tribe (following this is according to the previous hadith).
3689,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3690,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: When he accepted Islam, he had eight wives, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take four of them."
3691,"Qays bin Harith Kalbi, about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrates the Hadith: A man belonging to Banwasad accepted Islam, he had eight wives, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, take four of them, so he said: O so-and-so woman, you come, O so-and-so woman, you come, O so-and-so woman, you go, O so-and-so woman, you go."
3692,"A narrator named Mugheera narrates on the authority of one of the descendants of Sayyidna Harith bin Qays Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him: When Sayyidna Harith bin Qays Asdi, may Allah be pleased with him, accepted Islam, he had eight wives, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him to marry four of them."
3693,"A narrator named Mugheera narrates on the authority of Rabi bin Qays: When his great-grandfather Sayyiduna Harith bin Qays Asadi, may Allah be pleased with him, accepted Islam, he had eight wives, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him to marry four of them."
3694,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: When Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salama Al-Thaqafi accepted Islam, he had ten wives at that time, and the Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to keep four of them with him. During the time of Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ghilan bin Salamah divorced these women, so Sayyidna Umar, Radi Allahu Anhu instructed them to approach these women. There are these words in a hadith: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to them: You should approach them, otherwise I will make them the heirs of your property, and I will give an order about your grave. There are these words in a hadith: When they accepted Islam, these women also accepted Islam along with them."
3695,"Dahhak bin Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam, and I have two sisters in marriage, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Divorce one of them whomever you wish."
3696,"Dhahaq ibn Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: When I accepted Islam, I had two sisters in marriage, the Prophet instructed me: I should divorce one of them."
3697,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3698,Daylami (the narrator is doubtful or perhaps Ibn Daylami) narrates: I accepted Islam and I had two sisters in my marriage.
3699,"Dahhak bin Firoz Daylami narrates this statement of his father: When I accepted Islam, I had two sisters in marriage, I inquired about this from the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he instructed me: I should divorce one of them."
3700,"Uza'i was asked about a Harbi man who is the husband of two sisters, and he said, \If it were not for the hadith in which it is narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave authority to the husband in such a case", I would have given this fatwa," that man (will live with the woman to whom he was previously married).\"""""
3701,"Imam Shafi'i says: When a person is a Muslim and his wives are full sisters, then that person can choose one of them whom he wants, then his marriage with that woman will remain intact, his marriage with the other woman will be annulled, it does not make a difference in this regard (before accepting Islam) whether he married them both together or one after the other."
3702,"Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is your opinion about a person who finds a person with his wife, if he kills that woman, then you will kill him. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has given a decision about you and your wife. The narrator narrates: These two husband and wife cursed in the mosque, I was there along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the narrator says. The narrator says that the woman was pregnant, the man denied her pregnancy, then the woman's son was called after his mother, after that it was customary that such a woman became the heir of her child, and that child became the heir of that woman, the Juwala appointed as the inheritance of the son."
3703,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: An Ansari from Banuzriq accused his wife of adultery, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned him back four times, then God revealed the verses regarding the order of cursing, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Where is the questioner? A great order was revealed by Allah, then the man insisted on cursing and the woman also decided that she would remove the punishment from herself. Another person will have children. (The narrator narrates) So this woman gave birth to a black child, which was like a beige (i.e. dark-colored) camel, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this child, and entrusted him to his mother's relatives."
3704,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (RA) narrates: I was present in the case of the one who cursed (husband and wife) in front of the Prophet (PBUH). This man divorced the woman three times in the presence of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet declared them valid. After that, the same Sunnah was practiced among those who cursed that husband and wife were separated and then they could never be together."
3705,"Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Sa'idi (RA) narrates: Awaimar Ajlani said to a member of his tribe: Ask the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who finds another person with his wife. Both of them cursed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them and said that these two can never be together."
3706,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When cursed people (husband and wife) separate from each other, they can never be together again."
3707,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: What he said is in the next hadith) Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) (and both Sayyidna Ibn Masoud may Allah be pleased with him) say: This is the Sunnah of those who curse, that they can never be together."
3708,Sayyidna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud (RA) both say: This is the prevalent Sunnah that cursers can never come together afterwards.
3709,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (RA) narrates: I was present with the Prophet (PBUH) when the Prophet (PBUH) made a curse between Awimar Ajlani and his wife. Come, the order of the Qur'an has been revealed about both of you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed them both about this pregnancy near the pulpit after Asr prayer."
3710,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3711,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) was cursed with regard to pregnancy.
3712,", Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Hilal bin Umayyah accused his wife in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of having illicit relations with Sharik bin Sahma, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Produce evidence"," otherwise you will be subject to false accusations of adultery.\"" The narrator narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say this", you must provide evidence, otherwise the limit of falsely accusing you of adultery will continue. The narrator narrates: Hilal bin Umayyah said: By the One who sent you with the truth," I am telling the truth and Allah will surely send down a decree about me that will not cause me to be bound. \""Those who accuse their wives: this verse is up to the fifth time she will say: Allah's wrath has descended on her. The group of men are truthful.\"" The narrator narrates: After that", the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) summoned them both. Then the woman stood up and she also testified. When she started to use the fifth sentence, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," \""Stop it"," because it (the fifth testimony) will make punishment for her in the Hereafter.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: The woman hesitated", she bowed her head until we thought that she would turn back now, but then she said: I will never disgrace my tribe. A narrator named Hisham narrates, I think my teacher has quoted the same words as a narrator named Muhammad, and if this woman gave birth to a child with gray eyes, a heavy head and strong legs, then he will be the offspring of Sharik bin Sahma, then this woman gave birth to such a child. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the order of the Book of Allah had not come earlier," then my behavior with this woman would have been different."""
3713,Qazi Shareeh narrates: Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me (may Allah guide him) the person in whose hand is the knot of marriage.
3714,"Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman and Abu Salama narrate: Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am (may Allah be pleased with him) married a woman from Banu Nazir, and then divorced her before leaving. Sayyidna Jubayr sent her a full dowry, and said, \I have more right to forgive than that woman (because Allah says). Except if he forgives women or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven.\"" Jubayr bin Mut'am said) I have more right to forgive than this woman."""
3715,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3716,Abu Salamah narrates: Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut’im married a woman and then divorced her before leaving. He recited this verse: Except in the case that he forgives the woman or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven.
3717,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person who has the marriage knot in his hand means the husband.
3718,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The guardian of the marriage knot means the husband."
3719,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about this decree of Allah: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: \Except for the case that he forgives the women.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas", may Allah be pleased with him, says: That is," he forgives the woman or the person in whose hand the knot of marriage is forgiven."""
3720,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This means the husband.
3721,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: This means the husband.
3722,"Muhammad bin Jubayr narrates: His father (Sayyidna Jubayr bin Mut'am, may Allah be pleased with him) married a woman and then divorced her before leaving."
3723,Saeed bin Musayyib says: The person who has the marriage knot in his hand means the husband.
3724,"Qazi Shareeh says: This refers to the husband, that is, if he wants, he should give the woman full mahrada. Ibrahim, Alqamah and Hasan al-Basri say: It means Wali."
3725,"Qubaisa bin Dhu'ib narrates: Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (may God be pleased with him) was asked about two sisters who are owned by someone, then Sayyidna Uthman said: I will neither instruct you nor forbid you because one verse declares them halal and one verse declares them forbidden. The questioner went out and met a companion. A narrator named Muammar has narrated this: I think it was Sayyidna Ali (may God be pleased with him), he inquired about what you had asked Sayyidna Uthman about. The man told about his question and also about his answer, then Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: I will forbid you if I have any (official authority) over you and then you commit it, I will punish you."
3726,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) was asked about this issue, if a mother and a daughter come under the ownership of a person, can one of them have intercourse with the other? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said, I would not like you to associate with them both."
3727,"Narrated ``Urayb: I asked Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) that a slave girl and her mother are in my possession, both of them have given birth to my children. What is your opinion about this? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One verse declares it halal and one verse declares it forbidden. I will not do this, nor will any member of my family do this."
3728,"Narrated Tariq Bin Qays: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may a man have intercourse with both his maidservant and his daughter, while they both belong to him. So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One verse has declared both of them haram and one verse has declared them halal, but I will not do that."
3729,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, When a man marries a beautiful woman, he should stay with her for three days and then start dividing (among the wives)."
3730,"Narrated Anas: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that the virgin will get seven days and the Saiba will get three days, then the man will divide (the time equally between) his wives."
3731,"Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrated: He said to the Prophet (PBUH): He held the foot of the Prophet (PBUH) and (said) you, the Prophet (PBUH) will stay with me today. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Saiba will get three days and the virgin will get seven days."
3732,"Abdul Malik bin Abu Bakr narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with him) in the month of Shawwal, and he departed in the month of Shawwal. Sayyida Umm Salma said, O Messenger of Allah (now), you may stay with me for three days."
3733,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission: Abd al-Malik bin Abu Bakr narrates the following statement of Sayyidah Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, regarding her father: When he left, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: You are not inferior to your husband. But then I will stay with all my wives (with each of them) for seven days, then Sayyida Umm Salma asked you to stay with me for three days. Imam Malik and Ibn Abi Zayb have derived this ruling from him that a virgin will be left for seven days and that with Saiba will be left for three days."
3734,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The text of the hadith is after the next chain of transmission. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a man marries a virgin and the man has a wife from his first wife, that virgin will get three days, and if he marries a female, she will get two days."
3735,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: It often happened that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit all his wives. was
3736,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not have company, only touched."
3737,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When you marry a free woman and your first wife is a slave woman, you should give two days to the free woman and one day to the slave woman."
3738,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the first wife is a concubine and then someone marries a free man, the share of the concubine will be one-third and the share of the free woman will be two-thirds."
3739,Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyya (may Allah be pleased with him) and declared her freedom as his dower.
3740,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) and married her and declared her freedom as her dowry.
3741,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (may Allah be pleased with him) and married her and made her the dowry of her freedom.
3742,Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Sayyida Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and married her and declared her dowry to be her freedom.
3743,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) married Sayyid Safiyyah (RA). Thabit narrates: I inquired whether the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had paid her dowry. So Sayyiduna Anas said that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had paid her her dowry, and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had freed her and married her."
3744,"Qatadah narrates: Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) was asked about a person who frees his slave girl and marries her, so he said: Did the Prophet (PBUH) not free Sayyida Safiyyah bint Hayy (RA) and Sayyida Juwayriyyah Bint Harith (RA) and marry them with their freedom as their dowry?"
3745,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about a person who has intercourse with his wife during her menstruation: He should give one dinar (maybe the narrator has doubts) and half a dinar in charity.
3746,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Whoever has sex with his wife during her menstruation, he should give one dinar (maybe the narrator has doubts) and half a dinar in charity.”"
3747,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever has sex with his wife while her (menstrual) blood is (flowing), one dinar (in charity) will be required on him, and (if) yellow (material is leaking), then half a dinar (in charity) will be required."
3748,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever has sex with his wife when her discharge (of menstruation) is dark red, one dinar is required, and if it is yellow, then half a dinar is required.”"
3749,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered one dinar in charity for a person who has intercourse with a woman during her period, and if a person has intercourse with a woman after she has become pure and before performing ghusl, then he must give half a dinar in charity."
3750,"Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Be modest, indeed, Allah does not shy away from telling the truth."
3751,"It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she had a slave and a maidservant. When Sayyida Ayesha wanted to free them, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free the slave first."
3752,"It is narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she had a slave and a maidservant. Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to free them."
3753,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Berira: If you want to be the wife of this slave, then it is fine, and if you want to separate from him, then (it is your will) Berira separated from him."
3754,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: She (Barirah) was the wife of a slave, when Sayyida Aisha (RA) freed her, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her, \If you wish", remain the wife of this slave, and if you wish," divorce her.\"""""
3755,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: If you agree to be the wife of this slave, take her from her. If you wish, divorce her."
3756,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her (i.e. Sayyida Barirah) authority, her husband was a slave."
3757,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira was the wife of a slave, when she (Sayyida Barira (may Allah be pleased with her) was freed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him authority over her (Barira’s) self."
3758,Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave of Aal Abu Ahmad.
3759,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Berira was freed, her husband was a free man at that time."
3760,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to Berira, \You go"," your private parts have been freed with you.\"""""
3761,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Berira was the wife of a slave, she became free, so the Prophet gave her authority over her."
3762,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave.
3763,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave.
3764,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: She (the narrator says) i.e. Sayyida Barira (may Allah be pleased with her) was given authority, her husband was a slave."
3765,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave.
3766,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her authority. Her husband was a slave.
3767,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave. Sheikh Abu Bakr Neshapuri says: This hadith is poor.
3768,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Barira's husband was a slave.
3769,"Nafi, narrates this statement of Sayyida Safiyyah bint Abu Ubaid (may God be pleased with her) that Barira's husband was a slave."
3770,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given this decision about Barira: She was the wife of a slave.
3771,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a slave.
3772,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Barira's husband was a black slave of Banumaghira. By Allah, I still remember the scene well on the day when Barira was freed."
3773,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: When Berirah was given authority, I saw her husband walking behind her in the streets of Madinah, his tears were flowing down his beard. Allah you are ordering me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No, I am only recommending. The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave authority to this woman and she adopted her own self."
3774,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When Barirah was given authority, her husband was a slave of Banu Mughira."
3775,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Barira if he had intercourse with you (after you were freed), you will not have authority. In the tradition of Ibn Mujahid, there are these words: If he gets close to you, you will not have authority."
3776,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When Barira separated from her husband, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed her Idda as that of a divorced woman (which means three menstrual periods)."
3777,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) freed Barirah from being married and set the conditions for her marriage, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision: the freedman has the right to marry her. (As much as) appointed. Some narrators have quoted these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed her to observe the Iddah."
3778,: Ubaidah says about this verse: \And if you are afraid of fighting among yourselves," send a mediator from the family of the man and a mediator from the family of the woman.\"" (Ubaidah narrates:) A man and a woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and each of them was accompanied by some people. Sayyidna Ali (RA) instructed them to appoint an arbitrator from the man's family and an arbitrator from the woman's family. It is obligatory upon you that if you think that there should be a separation between the two of them"," then you separate them. Then the woman said: I am satisfied with the decision of the Book of Allah regarding the payment that is required of me and the right that I have to get (i.e. I am ready to accept it). You also have to confess what this woman has done."""
3779,"Ubaidah narrates: A man and a woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and there were some people with them. When Sayyidna Ali (RA) appointed the two as arbitrators, he said: Wait now, I will tell you what is required of you. Do you know what is required of you? Sayyiduna Ali (RA) turned to the woman and said: Will you agree with what these two decide? The woman replied, \Yes"," I agree with the decision of Allah's book regarding what is imposed on me and what I get.\"" Then Sayyiduna Ali turned to the man and said"," \""Will you agree with what these two arbitrators decide?\"" He replied no", if they decide to keep both of them together, then I agree, and if they decide to separate, then I will not agree, then Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said to him, you have said wrong: By Allah," you will have to agree in the same way as this woman is agreeing to her."""
3780,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The best charity is that which is given in the world of prosperity (i.e., after giving charity, the person himself is not poor) and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. The narrator narrates: I said, O Messenger of Allah! Who is my guardian? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Your wife who says"," \""Give me something to eat"," otherwise divorce me.\"""""
3781,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A woman will say to her husband: Give me food, otherwise divorce me. The man's slave will say: First, give me food, then take work from me, and the children will say: To whom are you leaving me?"
3782,"Saeed bin Musaib says about a person who is unable to pay the expenses of his wife, he says: If that person is unable to pay the khach, then the husband and wife will be separated."
3783,Saeed bin Musayyib says about a person who is unable to pay his wife's expenses: Separation will be made between these husband and wife.
3784,The same has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira.
3785,"Ishaq bin Bahlul says: He said to Abdullah bin Dawud: If a man does not find a relation of the same family for a girl under his care, should he marry her to a pious person (of a lesser family)? So he replied, Sayyiduna Umar (RA) says: I will allow women from good families to marry only in the same family."
3786,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take righteous places (i.e. righteous wives) for your sperm.
3787,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Get married in Kufu and get them married, take (righteous wives) for your sperm, and avoid Abyssinians, because their outward appearance is not good."
3788,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the best (i.e. good wives) for your sperm and keep it only in Kafu. A narrator named Ashaj has narrated these words: Take the best (i.e. good wives) for your offspring and marry them in Kafu, and marry them (the Kafu)."
3789,Sufyan says: Kafu will be considered according to customs and religion.
3790,"Ishaq bin Bahlwal narrates: I said to Sufyan: If a person is not the girl's peer in terms of position, can a person marry his (sister) to a pious (poor, or family status) person? He replied yes."
3791,"Shaykh Ibn Abi Laili says: Kafu will be considered in religion and position, and Ka'i narrates: I heard Imam Abu Hanifa (RA) saying that Kafu will be considered in religion, position, and wealth."
3792,"Sha'bi narrated: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married (your wives to) Muqdad and Zayd, because the most honorable among you in the sight of Allah is the one whose morals are the best."
3793,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Abu Hind, a slave of Banubaydah, used to follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wants to see a person in whose heart Allah has engraved faith should look at Abu Hind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also said: Marry her (your female relative) and establish a relationship with her."
3794,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: Abu Hind put his heels on the blessed head of the Prophet (PBUH), then the Prophet (PBUH) said: O Banu Biyadha, marry Abu Hind and marry him (to one of your daughters)."
3795,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever wants to see a person whose heart has been enlightened by Allah with faith, let him see Abu Hind. The narrator narrates: That person used to work as a backhoe."
3796,"Sayyidah Zainab bint Jahsh (RA) narrates: Some people from Quraysh sent me a message of marriage, so I sent my sister Hamna bint Jahsh (RA) to the Prophet (SAW) to consult him about it. The Prophet (SAW) said to her: Why does she not marry the man who taught her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet? Did you find out, O Messenger of Allah! Who is that person? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Zayd bin Haritha, then Hamna got angry, he said: O Messenger of Allah, will you marry your cousin with your (freed, former) slave? Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Hamna came to me and told me about this, so I became more angry with her and I used harsher words than her, so Allah revealed this verse: “No believing man or woman (does not have authority) that when Allah and His Messenger give a decision in a matter, they have the authority (to act differently from this decision) in this matter.” Sayyida Zainab (RA) narrates: I sent a message to the Prophet (PBUH) asking him to marry me to whomever he wishes. The Prophet (PBUH) married me to Zayd bin Haritha (RA). Fear Allah. After that he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
3797,Hanzalah bin Abu Sufyan narrates the statement of his mother: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf's sister was the wife of Sayyidna Bilal.
3798,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Samurah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wealth is according to wealth, and charity is piety."
3799,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \It is according to wealth"," and kindness is piety.\"""""
3800,"Sayyiduna Abi Bin Ka'b Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is the ruling of this verse common to a divorced woman and a widow? The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: In which verse? I said: (This verse) And the Idda of pregnant women will end when they give birth to a child. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said yes."
3801,Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: He asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this verse: And the ``Idah of pregnant women will end when they give birth to a child.'' Is it for Yabih? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is for both the triple talaq woman and the widow.
3802,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A woman is married for four reasons: her wealth, her lineage, her piety and her beauty."
3803,"Sayyidina Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A woman is married for three reasons: her wealth, her beauty, and her religion."
3804,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): A man's dignity is his religion, his greatness is his intellect and his virtue is his morals."
3805,"Abdullah bin Baridah quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father: According to the people of the world, the standard of excellence is wealth."
3806,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: The virtue of a man is his religion, his morals, and his essence (goodness) is his intellect."
3807,"Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: Bravery and cowardice are inherent in men, while the same is the case with karma and custom."
3808,"Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: This is my son. My stomach was a vessel for him, my bosom was a shelter for him, my breast was a source of water for him, and now his father wants to separate him from me. would do"
3809,"Amr bin Shu'ayb, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: A woman had a quarrel with her (former) husband about her child, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman has more right to (raise) her children until she (remarries)."
3810,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A woman came to the Prophet's service and said: O Messenger of Allah, my stomach was a vessel for her, my breast was a source of irrigation for her, and my lap was a shelter for her."
3811,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Indeed, a person will be given a grace period of one year."
3812,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3813,Saeed bin Musayb says about a person who cannot have intercourse with his wife: He will be given a grace period of up to one year.
3814,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Such a person will be given respite for one year, if he is able to have intercourse, then it is fine, otherwise the husband and wife will be separated."
3815,"Abu Nu'man narrates: We came to the service of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radiyallahu Anhu to inquire about the person in question, and he said that he will be given a grace period of one year."
3816,Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radiyallahu Anhu says: A one-year respite will be given to a person who is responsible.
3817,Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) says: A one-year grace period will be given to the person concerned and it will be calculated from the day when the woman filed the case. Abd al-Rahman says: Sufyan Thauri and Imam Malik have given this fatwa (the deadline will start from the day on which) the woman filed the case.
3818,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When the door is closed and the veil is pulled down, the payment of dowry becomes obligatory."
3819,"Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventy, it will be necessary to pay dowry on her."
3820,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventy, it becomes obligatory to pay dowry on her."
3821,The same has been narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Ali (RA).
3822,The same is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him).
3823,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventies, it becomes obligatory to pay dowry on him, and it is obligatory on the woman to perform the `iddah, and she gets a share of the inheritance."
3824,"Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks at a woman with her veil removed, the payment of dowry becomes obligatory on him, regardless of whether he has intercourse with her or not."
3825,"Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: Harith bin Haqm married a woman, he closed the door, then he left the room and divorced that woman. In our view, Harith should be confirmed, asked Sayyiduna Zayd, \If this woman becomes pregnant"," will you stone her?\"" Marwan replied no", Sayyiduna Zaid said, In such a situation," the woman's statement will be confirmed."""
3826,"According to Saeed bin Musayb, there is nothing wrong with a person marrying a fifth wife after divorcing his (fourth) wife, whether she (the divorced woman) is pregnant or not."
3827,"Hasan Basri, Saeed bin Musayb, and Khalas bin Amr say: (What they say is in the next hadith) These gentlemen say: When a man divorces his wife and she is pregnant, even if he wishes, he can marry her sister during the Idda period."
3828,"We are informed by Hammad, who narrates on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who narrated this (the above hadith) from his father (Urwa bin Al-Zubayr)."
3829,"Qasim bin Muhammad and Urwa bin Zubair say: A person who has four wives and divorces one of them, he can marry (the fourth) whenever he wants, he will not arrange for the period (of his former wife) to pass."
3830,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A slave can have two marriages (simultaneously), and he can give two divorces."
3831,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to his father (Sayyidna Imam Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him)) with reference to his grandfather (Imam Zain al-Abidin may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said about a person who bought a slave girl, had intercourse with her, and then discovered a defect in the slave girl, he says that the slave girl will remain with that person, and her price will be reduced according to the defect. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If the ruling is similar to that of a Hoji, then that person will return the woman, and along with it he will also pay the ``aqr (compensation paid in the case of a suspected wati), then it will be similar to the ``Ijarah''. (This is the ruling) When he has intercourse with this slave girl, she will be his and her value will be reduced according to the defect."
3832,"Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of his father (Imam Baqir, may God be pleased with him): Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says: When a person buys a slave girl, then has intercourse with her, and after having intercourse with her, finds a fault in her, then he will take back the price (part of the price) according to the fault. This tradition is \Mrsal\""."""
3833,"Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) quoted his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir may Allah have mercy on him) on the authority of Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) as saying of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): (The buyer will not return the defective maidservant), but the decrease in price due to this defect will be returned to him. This tradition is also transmitted."
3834,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If she is a female slave, then the buyer will return half of the Usher (ie, twentieth part of the original price) with her, and if she is a virgin, he will return usher (ie, one-tenth of the original price). The narrator named Amir has not found the time of Sayyiduna Umar."
3835,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man (buyer) has intercourse with a slave girl, then it will become a transaction, but if the buyer develops a defect in her before intercourse with the slave girl, then he has the right to keep her if he wishes, and to return her if he wishes."
3836,"Raja bin Hayyah narrates: Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about Umm-Wald's Iddah, and he said: Do not confuse the religious rules in front of us. This same tradition along with another chain of transmission has been transmitted as a chain of transmission to Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him."
3837,"Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in front of us. The Idah of her (son's mother) will be the same as the Idah of a widow, i.e. four months and ten days."
3838,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of narrators. The narrator named Qubaysa did not listen to the hadiths from Sayyiduna bin As, may Allah be pleased with him."
3839,"Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
3840,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3841,"Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: When the master of Umm Ould Ka died, her Iddah will be four months and ten days, and when she is freed, her Iddah will be three menstrual periods. This hadith is muquf, and this is correct, this hadith is also transmitted, because the narrator named Qubaysa did not hear the hadiths from Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas."
3842,"Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: We will not play with the rules of our religion (i.e. we will not state wrong rules). A free woman is free and a slave girl is a slave girl."
3843,"Sayyidna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, says: The period of the mother's son is the same as the period of a free woman (says a narrator named Abdullah bin Ahmad). Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The period of the mother's son is the same as the period of a free woman."
3844,It was narrated on the authority of Qubaysa bin Dhuwayb that Sayyid Na Amr bin As said: The rite of a son is the rite of a free woman.
3845,"Abu Hasan narrates: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about a slave whose wife is a maidservant and then he gives her two talaqs, then they both become free together, then Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Abbas said: Now if he wants a man, he can give her a message of marriage. The Prophet (PBUH) has given this decision."
3846,"Abu Hasan narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about a slave whose wife is a maidservant, and then he divorces her twice, and she divorces him, and then they both become free, then whether that man can give the message of marriage to this woman."
3847,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “When a slave girl is the wife of a man and that person gives her two divorces, then he buys her, then that slave woman will not be lawful for him until he remarries (a widow or divorcee)."
3848,"Abu Uthman narrates: A woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and said: Her husband has developed insanity, so Sayyidna Umar (RA) ordered her to wait for four years, and then (after four years) Sayyidna Umar (RA) ordered the guardian of the man suffering from insanity to divorce the woman."
3849,"Narrated by Sayyidna Mughirah bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The wife of a missing person will remain his wife until the news (of the missing person's death) reaches her."
3850,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sayyidna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Abd bin Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) presented a case to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the son of the maidservant of Zam’ah. To obtain the son of a slave girl because he is my (illegitimate) child, Abd bin Zamaa said, O Messenger of Allah (that boy is my brother, who is the son of my father's slave and was born in my father's bed. The Prophet saw a clear resemblance to Utbah, but the Prophet said, O Abd Zamaa, you will get this, because the offspring is counted as the owner of the bed, and O Suda). Bint Zam'ah you cover it. Imam Malik, Salih bin Qaisan, Shuaib bin Abu Hamzah, Ibn Jarij, the nephew of Muammar bin Rashid, Yunus bin Sa'd, Sufyan bin Hussain and other narrators have followed it. In the tradition of Malik, Muammar, Laith, Saleh bin Qaisan, Ibn Ishaq and other narrators, there are these words: He did not see Sayyida bint Zam'ah."
3851,"Zayd bin Aslam says about this statement of Allah Ta'ala, Zalik Idni al-Tawlawa: It is better than not having many people who are under your protection."
3852,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed a widow that if she wanted, she could spend her `iddah outside her home. This hadith has been narrated only by Abu Malik Nakhai with authority and this narrator is weak and the narrator named Mahbub is also weak."
3853,"Saeed bin Basheer narrates: He asked Qatadah about Zahar, so Qatadah told me that Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me: Sayyidna Aus bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Zahar with his wife Khawaila bint Thaalba. The verse related to Zahar was revealed. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Sayyiduna Aws, he said, “I do not have the capacity for it.” Feed, they said, I do not even have this position, but if you help me and act with mercy (then I can do that)."
3854,Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a vessel containing fifteen Sa'a (of grain). (The narrator narrates) In this way every poor man got a mud.
3855,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, a man appeared with his wife, then he saw the shine of her leg in the moonlit night, so (he was able to pass Qa Abuna on himself) and had intercourse with her. \Before they have intercourse with each other (expiation must be paid) (the Prophet", peace and blessings be upon him) said," \""Now do not have intercourse with your wife until you have performed expiation."""
3856,Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salama Bin Sakhar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to go to Banuflan and collect a wasaq of dates from them and give them (one wasaq) to sixty poor people.
3857,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about the person who performed Zahaar, if he had intercourse before paying Kaffaar, then it will be necessary for him to pay two Kaffaras."
3858,Qabaisa bin Dhuwaib says: Two expiations will be required on such a person.
3859,"Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (RA) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), he made an appearance with his wife, and then before paying Kaffara, he also had intercourse with her."
3860,"Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the person who makes Zahar, who has intercourse (with a woman) before performing the expiation, his expiation will be the same."
3861,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I am ready to argue with anyone who wants to discuss the issue of not having sex with a slave girl.
3862,Amr bin Shu'ayb narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Zahar does not occur with female slaves.
3863,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Zahar does not occur with a maidservant.
3864,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) was asked about a person who makes Zahar with his four wives, and he said, his expiation will be only one."
3865,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this saying of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA): When a person has four wives and he performs zahar with all of them, he will have to pay only one Kaffarah."
3866,"Aisha bint Talha narrates: I said: If I marry Mus'ab bin Zubair, he will be my father's back (respectable as) to me. Then he inquired about his command, so he was instructed to free a slave, then he married Mus'ab bin Zubair."
3867,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (may Allah be pleased with him) married a daughter of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and a wife of Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who belonged to the Nahshal tribe (i.e. he married a girl and her stepmother).
3868,A narrator named Muhammad narrates: A Companion from Egypt named Habla married a man's wife and had a daughter by that man's second wife. A narrator named Ayyub narrates: Sayyiduna Hasan Basri has called it makruh.
3869,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, says: Khula, separation, has to happen, it is not divorce."
3870,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used medicine to bring together a husband and wife who had previously been divorced and divorced."
3871,"Ata narrates: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she complained about her husband. Al-Walid has quoted a different chain of transmission regarding Ibn Jarih, he has quoted it from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Ata, but its sender is correct."
3872,"Jamhan narrates: During the caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA), Sayyida Umm Bakra Aslamah (RA) obtained Khula from her husband, then Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) said: This will count as a divorce, but if the two of them have decided on something else, then it will be (counted) according to what they have decided."
3873,Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who gets Khula can get Khula in exchange for something worth less than her father.
3874,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A woman's pregnancy cannot remain in her womb for more than two years, even if she changes as much as the shadow of a spinning wheel."
3875,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: A woman's pregnancy cannot remain in her womb for more than two years, even if she is changed as much as spinning wood. A woman named Jamila Bint Saad is the sister of Ubaid Bin Saad."
3876,"A narrator named Abu Sufyan narrates: Some of our elders narrated this: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab and said: O Amir al-Mu’minin, after two years he came to his wife and she was pregnant. Sayyidna Umar R.A. consulted the people about stoning this woman, then Sayyidna Mu’adh bin Jabal R.A. said: O Amir al-Mu’minin, you can punish this woman, but you cannot punish the child in her womb. So you leave her until she gives birth to a child. Sayyiduna Umar left her. She gave birth to a boy whose front teeth protruded outwards, as a result of which the person found out that the child resembled him. He said: By the Lord of the Kaaba! This is my son, then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said: Women have become unable to give birth to a child like Mu'az. If Mu'az had not been there, Umar would have been killed."
3877,"Waleed bin Muslim narrates: I said to Imam Malik: I was told on the authority of Sayyida Aisha that she says that a woman can be pregnant for a maximum of two years, as long as the shadow of a wheel. So Imam Malik said: Subhan Allah, how can a person say this? This is our girl who is the wife of Muhammad bin Ajlan. She is a virtuous woman. Her husband is also a virtuous man. She has given birth to three children in twelve years."
3878,Mubarak bin Mujahid narrates: It is known among us that the wife of Muhammad bin Ajlan used to give birth to children after being pregnant for four years.
3879,"Hashim bin Yahya narrates: Once Malik bin Dinar was sitting, a man came to him and said: O Abu Yahya: Pray for this woman who has been pregnant for four years and is in severe pain. If I am a girl, then change her into a boy, for You can destroy whom You will and retain whom You will, Umm Al-Katab, with You. Then Malik bin Dinar raised his hands, and the people also raised their hands. At the same time, a messenger came to the man and said, 'Go to your wife.'"
3880,Uza'i says: We have a woman who menstruates in the morning and becomes pure in the evening.
3881,"Ubada bin Ibad Mehlabi narrates: There is a woman in our Mahlib tribe who became a grandmother at the age of eighteen, she gave birth to a girl at the age of Nabars, her daughter also gave birth to a daughter at the age of nine, that woman became a grandmother at the age of eighteen."
3882,"Bahria bint Hani bin Qubaysa narrates: I got married to Qaqaa bin Sur, he stayed with me for one night, then my father, who was a villager, submitted a case to the service of Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Messengers of Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him, came and took him with him to Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him, inquired whether you had intercourse with this woman. maintained."
3883,"Bahria bint Hani bin Qubaysa narrates that her father married her to a man who was a Christian. The woman herself married Qaqaa bin Sur. The girl's father came to Sayyidna Ali (RA). subjected me to disgrace, I did not want it, so Qaqa'a said: Do you think that I have secretly married? These people presented their case in front of Sayyidna Ali (RA), then Sayyidna Ali (RA) inquired, have you had intercourse with this woman? He replied yes, then Sayyiduna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) declared it right for this woman to marry herself. The woman named Bahria is unknown."
3884,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a woman's guardian is harmful and she appoints another person as her guardian and he marries that woman, then his marriage will be valid."
3885,"Shaibani narrates: There was a woman in our neighborhood (in the neighborhood or tribe) whose name was Bahria. Her mother married her. Her father was not there at that time. When her father came, he denied the relationship. He presented this matter to Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and Sayyidna Ali (RA) maintained the marriage."
3886,Abu Qais narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave this decision about this.
3887,Hazeel narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a decision accordingly.
3888,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said: O Messenger of Allah! Didn't Allah Ta'ala say: Divorce is done twice, then why is it ordered for the third time? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Allah has also said this). ’’ Then one has to be restrained in a known manner or released with grace."
3889,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I have heard Allah say: There will be two divorces, then where did the order for the third divorce come from? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (Allah has also said this). ” Then one has to stop in a known way, or release with favor (this refers to the third divorce). The narrator has quoted it on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, but it is true that this hadith has been transmitted on the authority of Ismail bin Sami, on the authority of Aburzeen, as a messenger tradition on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
3890,"Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There are four ways of giving divorce, two of them are halal and two are haram. One halal method is: A man divorces a woman when she is in a state of purity (and the person has not had sexual intercourse with her during the period of purity). (One) Haraam method is that a man divorces a woman when she is menstruating (the second Haraam method is) A man divorces a woman in a state of purity when he has had intercourse with her, and he does not know whether there is a child in the womb or not."
3891,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah way of giving divorce is that a man should give a divorce to a woman during every tahr, when it is completed, this is the ``Idah'' that Allah has ordered."
3892,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A person who wants to divorce according to the Sunnah should divorce a woman when she is in a state of purity, and he has not had intercourse with her (he should also make someone witness when he divorces)."
3893,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I divorced my wife, she was in the state of menstruation at that time. Sayyidna Umar (RA) attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and asked him (about this issue). will The Prophet (PBUH) said yes."
3894,Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the previous hadith).
3895,"Salem narrates about his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): He divorced his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was in the state of menstruation at that time. She does not become pure after another menstrual period, then if the group wishes to divorce her without cohabiting with her in a state of purity, this will be a divorce according to the method that Allah has ordered."
3896,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I divorced my wife who was menstruating. Sayyidna Umar mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace be upon him) expressed his displeasure, and said that he should return to this woman, then keep her with him until her next menstruation, which is other than the period in which he divorced her, then if he feels fit, then he should marry her. Divorce at the time when she is free from this next menses and before cohabiting with her, this divorce will be according to the method that Allah has ordered. Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) had given a divorce to this woman, this divorce was considered to be a divorce, then Hazrat Abdullah (RA) had approached this woman, as the Prophet (PBUH) had ordered him to do."
3897,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) expressed his displeasure about it. A narrator named Saleh has narrated these words: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed his displeasure about Sayyiduna Abdullah (after this the narrator mentioned the previous hadith)."
3898,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) says: The Sunnah way of giving divorce is that a man divorces a woman when she is in a state of purity, and (in the midst of this purity) he has not had intercourse with her, or divorces her again when the woman's pregnancy becomes apparent."
3899,"It has been narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, Sayyidna Umar mentioned this issue to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said, Tell him to approach this woman and then divorce her when she is in a state of purity or pregnancy."
3900,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Umar (RA): The Prophet (SAW) was told that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife during her menstruation.
3901,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3902,"Abu Zubair narrates: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar about a person who divorces his wife during her menstruation, then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar said: Do you know Ibn Umar? I replied yes. He said, I had given three divorces to my wife during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). All the narrators of this tradition are Shia. The safe tradition is this: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during her menstruation."
3903,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife during her menses. Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (SAW) and told him about it. The Prophet (SAW) said to him, \Tell Abdullah to approach this woman", and when she has performed ghusl, (i.e. purified)," he should let her stay like this until (the next time).\"" If he menstruates", then when he takes a bath (i.e. cleans himself) from the next menstruation, he should divorce her before having intercourse with her. If he wants to keep her with him, then he should keep her with him. Ubaidullah narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to this woman during her menstruation," but he did it contrary to the Sunnah method."""
3904,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: He divorced his wife and she was in the state of menstruation at that time. Menstruation comes and after that she becomes pure, then if he wants, he should divorce her before having intercourse with her, and if he wants, he should let her stay with him. Saleh bin Kaisan, Musa bin Uqbah, Ismail bin Umayyah, Laith bin Saad, Ibn Abi Zayb, Ibn Jarij, Jabir, Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated this from Sayyidina Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Nafi. Al-Zuhri has narrated the same thing about Salem from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar). Yunus bin Jubir, Sha'bi and Hasan al-Basri have also narrated the same thing."
3905,"Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar and said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id narrates: A man said to Sayyiduna Umar (RA): I divorced my wife when she was menstruating. After that, the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said, \You have disobeyed your Lord and your wife has separated from you.\"" That person said: When Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) separated from his wife", the Prophet (PBUH) did not instruct him to return to his wife. A narrator named Ibn Sa'id narrated these words: When Abdullah bin Umar (RA) separated from his wife during her period (i.e. divorced her), the Prophet (PBUH) told him to return to her. After that, the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar (RA) said to this person: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him (i.e. Ibn Umar RA) to return to his wife because of the divorce that remained (i.e., which Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) still had the power to grant). A narrator named Ibn Sa`id narrated these words: He had appealed on the basis of the divorce, which he still had the right to, and you did not allow the matter to remain, on the basis of which you could appeal to your wife. A narrator named Ibn Muni has quoted these words: There is nothing left for you on the basis of which you can approach your wife. Shaykh Abul Qasim has narrated this to us: This tradition has been narrated by many narrators: but they did not mention these words of Sayyiduna Umar in it, as far as I know," no other narrator has narrated this saying except Saeed bin Abdul Rahman."""
3906,"Abu Ghulab narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, did you count this divorce? Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar said, \Why didn't I count him? Was I humble?\"" Or was he stupid?"""
3907,"Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: Twenty years ago, an authentic narrator narrated this hadith to me: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar divorced his wife three times during her menstruation, so he was ordered to return to her. I considered this tradition to be authentic, he told me this: He asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar about this, then Sayyidna Abdullah told him that he had divorced his wife during her menstruation, so he was ordered to return to that woman. So Syedna Abdullah said why not, was he humble?"
3908,Yunus bin Jubayr narrates: He asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) how many divorces had he given to his wife? Sayyiduna Ibn Umar said:
3909,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar Z divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Sayyidna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this issue, so the Prophet instructed him to approach the woman and keep her until she becomes pure again, then wait until she becomes pure again before having intercourse with her (divorce her). According to this order, women should be divorced."
3910,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife. She was menstruating at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) went to the Prophet (PBUH) and told him about this. The Prophet (PBUH) said that he should go back to this woman and let her remain like that until she becomes pure. Let it be like this, until she becomes pure. When she becomes pure, divorce her before having intercourse with her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is the way that Allah has decreed, women should be divorced accordingly."
3911,Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) gave a divorce to his wife.
3912,"Nafee narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The woman was in the state of menstruation at that time. A narrator named Ibn Abi Zayb has narrated these words in a hadith: It was a divorce (the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace) said, \This is the way that Allah has decreed"," women should be divorced accordingly.\"""""
3913,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam). She was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar asked the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) about this order (after that, he mentioned it according to the previous hadith)."
3914,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife, then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to keep this woman with him until she becomes pure. The narrator did not mention Sayyiduna Umar in this tradition."
3915,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “It will be one (divorce count)."
3916,"Jabir al-Thuq says: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: A person divorces a woman in the state of menstruation, so Sayyidna Ibn Umar said, \Do you know Ibn Umar?\"" He had divorced his menstruating wife. Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said: Tell him to go back to this woman", then when she (next) menstruates, then after that, when she is pure, at that time, he should divorce her if he wishes, and if he wishes," he should keep her with him. What was the divorce count? He replied yes."""
3917,"Salma bin Abu Salama narrates about her father: It was mentioned before him that it is abominable to divorce three times at once, so he said, Hafs bin Amr bin Mughira had divorced Fatimah bint Qays three times with the same word, so we did not find any information that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, objected to him in this regard. Sath) had given three divorces, but no one objected to them either."
3918,"Sha'bi narrated: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar gave one divorce to his wife. The woman was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar inquired from the Prophet (peace be upon him) and told him about it, so he instructed him (i.e. Ibn Umar) to approach the woman and then divorce her again during her period of Idah."
3919,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah ibn Umar (RA) divorced his wife and she was menstruating at that time. Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, ``Abdullah divorced his wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet (PBUH) said, 'Tell her to return, and then when she becomes pure, her menses will come again after that, and when she becomes pure. Time, if he wishes, let him stay with her, and if he wants to divorce her, then he should not associate with her (rather divorce her). This is the way that Allah has ordered."
3920,"Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of Sayyidna Dahhak bin Qays, narrates that she was the wife of a man from Banu Makhzoom, who divorced her three times and went away to participate in a war."
3921,"Salamah bin Abu Salamah narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Auf divorced his wife Tamazar bint Isbah Kalbiyah (her surname is Umm Salamah) three times with one word, so we did not find any information that anyone objected to him in this regard."
3922,Salama bin Abu Salama narrates this statement of her father: Hafs bin Mughirah divorced his wife Fatimah bint Qays three times in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the same word.
3923,"Along with another document, these two events are narrated together."
3924,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates about Sayyidna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him: A man gave his wife a thousand divorces, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, three of them will be enough for you and leave the remaining ninety-eight."
3925,"Narrated Amr bin Murrah: I heard Mahan asking Saeed bin Jubayr about a person who divorces his wife three times, then Saeed said, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas was asked about a person who divorces his wife once, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, Through three divorces your wife will become forbidden to you and the rest will become a burden because you have mocked the verses of Allah."
3926,"Mujahid narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) asked about a person who gives his wife one hundred divorces. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas said: You have disobeyed your Lord and you have separated from your wife. You do not fear Allah, otherwise He would have created a place for you."
3927,"Mujahid narrates: A Qureshi came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and said: O Abu Abbas: I have divorced my wife three times in anger, then Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Abu Abbas cannot make it lawful for you that which has become haram for you. You have disobeyed your Lord and made your wife haram for you. He recited this verse: \And when you want to divorce women"," divorce them\"" means before their Idda when they are in a state of purity and have not had sex with them. A narrator named Sayf has stated this: This (sentence in question) is not part of the recitation"," but an explanation of (the words of the Qur'an)."""
3928,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and said: I have given my wife a thousand divorces. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Because of three divorces, your wife has become forbidden to you, and the remaining divorces have become a sin for you, because you mocked the verses of Allah."
3929,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3930,Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Divorce cannot be granted before marriage," and a man cannot take a vow regarding something he does not own.\"""""
3931,"Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates this statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man cannot divorce, set free, sell, and fulfill a vow to what he does not own."
3932,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man cannot divorce what he does not own, he cannot sell what he does not own, and he cannot free what he does not own."
3933,Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not permissible to free a man who does not own him. The narrator does not mention selling in it.
3934,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever divorces something that he does not own, it will not be divorced, whoever frees something that he does not own, he will not be freed, whoever takes a vow about something that he does not own, his vow will not be valid, and whoever swears about a sin, his oath will not be valid, and whoever breaks it. If he swears about Rahmi, his oath will not be valid."
3935,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Abu Sufyan bin Harb (may Allah be pleased with him) and instructed him: (i.e. the order is this) A man cannot divorce until he marries, and he cannot free what he does not own."
3936,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) sent Abu Sufyan to the city of Najran in Yemen so that he could offer prayers, fight and receive charity there. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised Abu Sufyan to have piety towards Allah, and this instruction states that no one can divorce a person with whom he has not been married, and no one can free him whom he does not own, and there is no status of vows regarding disobedience to God."
3937,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He was asked about a person who says: On the day I marry such and such a woman, she has a divorce."
3938,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A vow is only about that which obeys the command of Allah."
3939,"Sayyiduna Muadh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Divorce can only be granted after marriage, even if the woman has been given a specific name. A narrator named Yazid bin Ayyad is weak."
3940,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious and joking is also considered serious, divorce, marriage, and regression (i.e. return)."
3941,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3942,"Imam Zayd bin Ali (RA) narrates with reference to his ancestors: A person came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother mentioned to me a relative girl that I should marry her, so I said: If I marry this woman, she has three divorces. He said no, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then there is no problem. The narrator narrates that then the man married this woman."
3943,"Ibrahim bin Ubaidullah narrated this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: A man among his elders gave his wife a thousand divorces, and his children came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, O Messenger of God: Our father has given our mother a thousand divorces. will be separated from him due to three divorces which are against the Sunnah and (remaining) ninety-nine divorces will be on his neck as a sin. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him) narrates that our teacher Ibn Abdul Baqi (apart from these two) all the narrators of this tradition are unknown and weak."
3944,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Mu'adh Bin Jabal (RA) narrating that the Prophet (PBUH) said to me: O Mu'adh, whoever divorces one, two or three times as an innovation (i.e. against the Sunnah), We will make his innovation obligatory on him. A narrator named Isma'il bin Abumiya al-Basri is an obsolete hadith."
3945,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person (or about a person) who had divorced his wife, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said, “You people are mocking the verses of Allah. (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words) Playing with the religion of Allah, whoever divorces, We will make three divorces obligatory for him, and that woman will not be lawful for him until he becomes a widow or divorcee after the second marriage. The narrator named Ismail bin Abuamiyyah has a weak hadeeth."
3946,"Habib bin Abu Thabit narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and said: I have given my wife a thousand divorces. Sayyidna Ali said: Three divorces have made it haram for you, and you should divide the remaining divorces among your other wives."
3947,"Saeed bin Jubayr and Mujahid narrate on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: He was asked about a person who divorces his wife by the number of stars, then Sayyidna Ibn Abbas said: This person violated the Sunnah and his wife became forbidden to him."
3948,"Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: A man divorced his wife as many as the number of stars, then Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said about him, This man violated the Sunnah and his wife became forbidden to him."
3949,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \A pregnant woman", a widow," will not get any expenses.\"""""
3950,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \A pregnant woman", a widow," will not get any expenses.\"""""
3951,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a pregnant woman, a widow, that she will not get any expenses."
3952,Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a woman who has been divorced three times will not get housing and expenses.
3953,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to Fatimah (bint Qays) that the woman whose husband has the right to appeal to her will receive the housing and expenses.
3954,"Amir Shaabi narrates: We came to the service of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, and we said to her: Narrate to us the hadith in which the decision of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is mentioned. It is to say that I will not get housing and expenses, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will get housing and expenses. (His brother-in-law) said: Her husband has divorced her three times. Sha'bi narrates: When I came to Kufa, Aswad bin Yazid called me to ask me about this."
3955,"Aswad narrates: When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) found out about the statement of Sayyida Fatima Bint Qays (RA), he said, \We will not impose orders on Muslims because of the statement of a woman.\"""""
3956,"Shaabi narrates: Aswad bin Yazid met me and he said to me: O Shaabi, fear Allah and refrain from quoting the hadith of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays (RA), because Sayyiduna Umar (RA) has given such a woman the right to live and spend. The hadith was narrated to me."
3957,"Narrated Shaabi: I went to the service of Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the decision of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she said: Her husband divorced her. She went to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He did not give the right to spend. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The woman whose husband has the authority to refer (to her) the residence and the expenses are given.\"""""
3958,"This tradition is narrated along with some other isnads, and in the tradition of Majalid, these words are: Housing and expenses are given to the woman whose husband can approach her."
3959,"Aswad narrates: When the statement of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) came to light, he said, \We will not abandon the commandments of the Book of Allah because of the statement of a woman"," perhaps she has forgotten.\"""""
3960,"Abu Ishaq narrates: I was sitting in the big mosque with Aswad bin Yazid. Sha'bi was also present with us. Sha'bi narrated this hadith regarding Sayyida Fatima bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give her the right to live and spend. He said: We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the commandment of the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the statement of a woman, because we do not know that this woman has forgotten (the original matter)."
3961,"Sayyida Fatima bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My husband divorced me three times. Abu Ishaq narrates: When Sha'bi narrated this tradition, Aswad threw stones at him and said: You are the ones who are narrating this tradition or giving a fatwa on the basis of this tradition. We will not abandon the commandment of the Book of Allah because of the statement of a woman (that commandment is this): \Do not drive them out of their homes"," and they should not leave unless they commit a clear evil.\"" This tradition is more authentic than the one before it"," because these words are not proven. A narrator named Yahya has a greater memory and is more authentic than Abu Ahmad Zubayri. The rest is known to Allah."""
3962,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3963,"Abdullah bin Khalil Hazrami narrates: Sayyidah Fatimah bint Qays was mentioned before Sayyiduna Umar bint Khattab, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give her the right to live and spend. A narrator named Hasan bin Amara is obsolete."
3964,"Aswad narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Umar: We will not abandon the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the statement of a woman. Amish narrated this tradition from Aswad regarding Ibrahim and did not quote these words in it, and the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we have noted this tradition before: Amish is a more authentic and a greater Hafiz al-Hadith than Ash'at."
3965,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3966,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife and she was menstruating at that time. The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to go back to her and let her stay like that until she becomes pure. Then when she next menstruates, let her stay like this until she becomes pure. Divorce her first, this is the way that Allah Ta'ala has ordered, according to which women should be divorced. The narrator narrates: When Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar was asked about this, he used to say, If you have given your wife one divorce (then you should return), because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to do so, but if you have divorced this woman three times, then she will remain forbidden to you at that time, until she marries another person (mutlaqah yabih). You have disobeyed Allah in this regard."
3967,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife while she was menstruating. A narrator named Ibn Arfa narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar gave a divorce to his wife, she was menstruating at that time. After that, the two narrators have narrated these words: Sayyiduna Umar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed him (Ibn Umar) to approach this woman, then leave her alone until she next menstruates, then leave her alone until she is purified, then divorce her before having intercourse with her, this is the method that Allah Almighty has mentioned. He has ordered that women should be divorced accordingly. The narrator narrates: When Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was asked about a person who divorced his wife during her menstruation, Sayyidna Ibn Umar would say: If you have mentioned a divorce, then the Prophet (PBUH) has instructed about such a person that he should return to that woman, then let her stay like that until she next menstruates, then let her stay like this until she becomes pure. If you divorce her three times, then you have disobeyed what Allah commanded you about divorcing your wife, and your wife has separated from you without reason."
3968,"Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) divorced his wife during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and the woman was in the state of menstruation at that time. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) asked the Prophet (SAW) about this order, and he said, Tell him to approach this woman (after that, the narrator mentioned the previous hadith). In this hadith there are these words: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said to such a person: If you have divorced your wife once or twice, the Prophet (PBUH) gave me this command."
3969,"Nafi' narrated: When a person asked Abdullah Ibn Umar about the issue of divorcing his wife while she was menstruating, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) would tell him what the Prophet (PBUH) had said, then he would say, \If you have divorced your wife once", the Prophet (PBUH) has ordered me to do this, but if you have divorced three times," then that woman is forbidden to you until she remarries.\"" You have disobeyed the order of your Lord which He had given you regarding divorce."""
3970,"Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates this statement of Sayyida Fatima bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her. She was the wife of Abu Amr bin Hafs bin Mughirah, and she also divorced him for the third time. When she attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he inquired from him about this issue. Marwan did not accept that a divorced woman can leave her house, he did not accept the statement of Sayyida Fatima bint Qais as reliable. Narrated Urwa: Sayyida Aisha also did not accept the statement of Fatima bint Qays."
3971,"Uza'i narrates: I asked Zahri which wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge with you. So they replied, Urwa bin Zubair told me about Sayyida Aisha that this woman's name was bint Jun Kalabiya, when they visited her and got close to her, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: You have taken refuge in a great person, go to your family."
3972,"Suwayd bin Ghafla narrates: A woman named Aisha Khatamiyyah was the wife of Sayyidna Imam Hass bin Ali (RA). When Sayyidna Ali (RA) was martyred and allegiance was given to Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA), this woman said: Amir al-Mu’minin, may you be blessed with the Caliphate. Narrated by the narrator: This woman wrapped her veil, until when her Eid was completed, Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (RA) gave her the rest of her dowry and ten thousand (dirhams or dinars) as a dowry. The woman said: These things are very little compared to the beloved who is parting. Hada, (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) My father (Sayyidna Ali, may God be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me. Be done. (Imam Hasan says:) Then I would turn to him."
3973,"Suwayd Bin Ghalfah narrates that when Sayyidna Ali (RA) passed away, Aisha bint Khalifa Khatamiyyah, who was the wife of Sayyidna Imam Hasan (RA), said to Sayyidna Imam Hassan (RA): Congratulations on becoming the Commander of the Faithful, then Sayyidna Imam Hassan (RA) said to her: You are congratulating me on the martyrdom of Commander of the Faithful (i.e. Sayyidna Ali (RA)), go away, you are divorced. She put her cloth over her face and said: O Allah, my intention was only good (i.e. I did not have this intention). Later Sayyiduna Imam Hasan sent this woman ten thousand dirhams or dinars and the rest of the dowry as a reward. When these things were placed in front of her, she turned and said: All this is very little compared to the beloved who is being separated. A person who divorces his wife three times, such as one divorce in every tahr or one divorce in every month or three divorces at once, then that woman will not be lawful for that person until she marries another person."
3974,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: He divorced his wife once, while the woman was menstruating at that time, then he intended to give the remaining two divorces to this woman during the subsequent purifications. Allah did not command you (to divorce) in this way. You have disobeyed the Sunnah. The Sunnah is that you should first purify her and then give her a divorce in each purification. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed me, so I turned to this woman. He said, O Messenger of Allah, what do you say, if I divorce her three times, will it be permissible for me to approach her? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No (in such a case) she will be divorced from you and (this method of divorce) will be a sin."
3975,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: If a person divorces his wife three times, then she is divorced from him, and that person disobeys his Lord and has violated the Sunnah."
3976,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Three divorces are made through Bariya, Batah, Bain, and Haram, and that woman will not be lawful for a man until she remarries (mutlaqah yawiah)."
3977,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “When a man divorces his wife three times, that woman is not lawful for him until she remarries, and each of them (husband and wife) does not taste the honey of the other party.”"
3978,"Nafi bin Ajir narrates: Sayyidna Ruqana bin Abdazid (RA) divorced his wife, Suhaimah, then he came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given divorce notice to my wife, Suhaimah. By Allah! Did you mean only one divorce? Sayyiduna Rukana (RA) said: By Allah, I intended only one divorce, so the Prophet (PBUH) sent that woman back. Sayyidna Ruqana (RA) gave this woman a second divorce during the caliphate of Sayyidna Umar (RA) and a third divorce during the caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
3979,"Nafi bin Ujair narrates: Sayyidna Ruqana bin Yazid divorced his wife Suhaimah. He told the Prophet about this. He said, O Messenger of Allah, I have divorced my wife Suhaimah. By Allah, I intended to give only one divorce through her. The Prophet asked Sayyiduna Ruqana. By Allah! Did you mean only one divorce? Sayyiduna Rukana (RA) said: By Allah, I meant only one divorce, so the Prophet sent the woman back. Sayyidna Ruqana (RA) gave this woman a second divorce and a third divorce during the Caliphate of Sayyidna Uthman (RA). Imam Dawood says, this hadith is correct."
3980,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
3981,"Abdullah bin Ali, on the authority of his father, narrates this about his grandfather: He divorced his wife during the blessed covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: What did you mean by that? He said: A (divorce) The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: By Allah: He said: By Allah! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \It will be according to your wishes.\"" In this hadith", the narrator named Abu Nasr did not quote the word," Ibn Yazid bin Raqana."""
3982,Abdullah bin Ali narrates: My grandfather Sayyidna Raqana bin Abd Yazid (RA) divorced his wife. He came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have divorced my wife. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What did you mean (by these words)? He said: I meant a divorce. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: By Allah! He said: By Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it will be one (divorce count). Ishaq ibn Israel has narrated a hadith to the contrary (which follows).
3983,"Abdullah bin Ali narrates this about his grandfather Sayyidna Raqana bin Abd Yazid Radiyallahu Anhu: He divorced his wife, then he attended the Prophet's service and mentioned this to him. The Prophet inquired: By Allah! Did you just mean a divorce? He said: By Allah, I meant only one divorce. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it will count as one divorce."
3984,"Sayyidna Muadh Bin Jabal Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Muadhullah, the Almighty has not created anything on earth that is more pleasing to Him than freeing a slave, and Allah has not created anything on the earth that is more displeasing to Him than divorce. The right of exception will not be granted, if a person says to his wife that if Allah wills, you have divorce, then that person will have the right of exception and divorce will not take place."
3985,"This tradition is narrated along with another document. Hameed narrates, Yazid bin Haroon said to me: How great this hadith would have been if its narrator Hameed bin Malik Lakhmi had been known. I said: He is my grandfather. Taweezid said: You have made me happy, you have made me happy. Now this hadith has become (authentic)."
3986,"Narrated by Sayyidna Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Allah has not declared anything as halal, which is more distasteful to him than divorce."
3987,"Sayyiduna Abu Thalaba Khoshni (RA) narrated: My uncle said to me: You work for me so that I may marry my daughter to you. I said: If you marry my daughter to her, she will have three divorces. Then later I felt it appropriate to marry this woman. It can be given only after, so I got married to this woman and then Saad and Saeed were born to me."
3988,"Muhammad bin Ubaid narrates: Udi bin Udi Kundi sent me to Safiyya bint Sheebah to inquire from her about the traditions that she narrates with reference to the lady Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her), so this lady said, Saida Ayesha Siddiqa narrated to me that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ``Etaq (liberation of the slave) by force (by force) does not take place."
3989,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates this saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \This divorce does not take place by force (through) Ataq (freeing the slave)\""."""
3990,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas says: There are four ways of divorce, two of them are halal, and two ways are forbidden. As far as the two halal ways are concerned, that is for a man to divorce his wife while she is pure, without having intercourse with her, or he divorces his wife when she is pregnant and her pregnancy is obvious. Diede, or divorce her after intercourse with her, in which it is not known whether (as a result of this intercourse) pregnancy has been declared or not?"
3991,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained that his master had married him and now he wanted a woman: separate him and his wife. Want to be careful! The authority to grant divorce is to be given to the one who holds the shank.
3992,Narrated by Ikramah: A slave came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) (followed by the previous hadith) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right to divorce belongs to the one who holds the shin. The narrator did not mention (in his chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas.
3993,"Sayyidna Asma bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A slave came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, My master married me first, and now he wants to separate me and my wife."
3994,Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be two divorces (given to a maidservant) and her period of menstruation will be two.
3995,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, Umar bin Shaib is unique in quoting this tradition as a marfu’, hadith. This is a weak narrator."
3996,"Salim states: A person who is a slave and his wife is a free woman, or a man who is free and his wife is a maidservant, whichever of the spouses is mamluk, then the divorce will be reduced due to this mamluk, however, the status of the woman will be considered in Idda."
3997,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A slave (husband) can give two talaqs to a free (wife) and the woman's period will be three Qur'a.
3998,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: When a free woman is the wife of a slave, then the woman can be given two divorces, and her iddat will be three menstruations, and when a slave girl is the wife of a free person, two divorces can be given to her, and her iddtah will be two menstruations as a slave woman."
3999,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) says: When a slave divorces his wife twice, that woman becomes haram for him until she remarries (a widow or divorcee)."
4000,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, says this about a slave girl who is the wife of a free man: She will become a widow through two divorces, and she will perform two periods of Iddah, and when a free woman is the wife of a slave, she will become a widow through two divorces and will perform three periods of Iddah. This hadith has been narrated by other narrators as a muqaf, tradition, and it is true that this tradition has been narrated as a marfu’ hadith with one and a chain."
4001,"Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: I said to the Prophet (PBUH): \And the end of the period of pregnant women is that they give birth.\"" This ruling is for a woman divorced three times? Is it for Yabih? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is for the divorced and also for the widow."""
4002,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The divorce of a slave will be two, and then that woman will not be lawful for him until she marries another (widow) and the maidservant's Idda will be menstruating."
4003,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates this saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \A slave girl can be given two divorces and her Idda will be two menstruations. With another chain of transmission it is narrated that Sayyida Aisha says"," A slave girl can be divorced twice and her Idda will be two menstruations."""
4004,"Abu Asim says: In Basra, there is no more, negative tradition than this tradition narrated by al-Mazahir."
4005,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates: Qasim was asked about the concubines, how many divorces can be given to him? He said that she can be given two divorces and her Idda will be two periods. The narrator narrates: He was asked whether any hadith regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached you. He replied no."
4006,"Zaid bin Aslam narrates: Qasim was asked about the iddah of the maidservant and he said, People say it will be menstruation, we do not know about it (the narrator doubts or perhaps these are the words) We do not find this ruling in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger. Ibn Wahib has quoted the same saying of Qasim and Salim with his chain of command. This ruling is not in the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, but Muslims follow it."
4007,"Ikrimah narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Using the word haram (for a wife) is not divorce, but an oath for which expiation must be paid. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about using the word Haram, this is an oath for which expiation will be paid. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) says that the best example for you is in the life of the Prophet (PBUH). \Why do you declare that which Allah has made lawful for you: \""This verse is even here", Qud Fard Allah Lakum. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid expiation for his oath and he made using the word, haram," an oath."""
4008,
4009,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when a person declares his wife haram for him, this oath will count and that person will pay expiation for the oath. Sayyiduna Ibne Bass (RA) said, \There is an excellent example for you in the life of the Prophet (PBUH)."""
4010,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: If you use the word Haram, you will have to pay Kaffara."
4011,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (SAW) on the authority of Sayyidna Umar (RA).
4012,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Using the word haram is an oath for which expiation will be paid.
4013,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA): Once, the Prophet (PBUH) came to the house of Sayyida Hafsa (RA) along with his mother, Sayyida Mariya Qobtiyya (RA). You have done this to me by leaving your other wives, because \I have no status in your eyes.\"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said"," \""You shall not mention this in front of Aisha. It is forbidden for me (the concubine) to go near her.\"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned (his wives) that you will not visit your wives for a month. The narrator says that after this there is a long hadith."""
4014,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Hafsa (RA) found the Holy Prophet (SAW) with Umm Ibrahim (i.e. Sayyida Mariya Quptiya (RA)) on the special day of Sayyida Ayesha (RA), so she said: I will definitely tell (Sayida Aisha) about this. Sayyida Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) told about this to Sayyida Ayesha, then Allah told His Messenger about it. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been informed by one who has knowledge and information. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with his wives for a month, then Allah revealed this verse. \If both of you repent before Allah (it would be appropriate) because both of your hearts were crooked.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I asked Sayyidna Umar (RA)"," who were those two women who supported each other (regarding this act) of the Prophet (PBUH)? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: Aisha and Hafsa."""
4015,"Ata says: Whoever says to his wife: You are forbidden to me, you are forbidden to divorce, you have a harmful divorce."
4016,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) that a man came to him and said: I have declared my wife forbidden to me. \O Prophet! Why do you make that thing haram, which Allah has made lawful for you? (Then Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said) The most severe expiation will be imposed on you," i.e. freeing a slave."""
4017,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Rafi bin Sinan (RA) that he accepted Islam but his wife refused to accept Islam. They had a little girl who had reached the age of weaning. They both came to the Prophet (PBUH) with their case. Waslam prayed, O Allah, grant her guidance, then the girl turned towards her father, then Sayyidna Rafi' (RA) obtained her."
4018,"It is narrated about Sayyidna Rafi bin Sinan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he accepted Islam, his wife refused to accept Islam, they had a daughter, whose name was Umayra, the woman asked for the child, then Sayyidna Rafi, may Allah be pleased with her, refused. Both of you call this girl, both of them called, the girl started to turn towards her mother, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, O Allah, guide her, then the girl turned to her father, so he got her, and took her with him."
4019,"Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahba came to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas said to him, Present your position (or question) and what is in your mind and what you have collected. Abu Sahba said to him: Do you know? In the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), three divorces were counted as one, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) replied, Yes, during the time of the Prophet (PBUH), during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA), and in the early days of the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (RA), three talaqs were counted as one. Done)."
4020,"Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: O Moaz! Whoever divorces his wife one, two, or three times in an innovation (i.e. against the Sunnah) way, We will make his innovation obligatory on him."
4021,"Narrated by Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: O Mu'adh! Whoever divorces his wife for one time as an innovation, We will make his innovation binding on him."
4022,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Whoever divorces his wife three times while she is menstruating, she will be divorced from him, but this person has disobeyed his Lord and violated the Sunnah."
4023,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4024,Aban Ibn Taghlib narrates: I asked Imam Jafar Sadiq about such a person: who divorces his wife three times. Imam Jafar Sadiq said that woman will be divorced from that person and it will not be lawful for him until she marries another (widow or divorcee). So they answered yes.
4025,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called Khulaa as a divorce.
4026,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit Bin Qays (RA) had taken away her Khul from him, so the Prophet (PBUH) instructed her to perform one period of menstruation."
4027,"Ikramah narrates: Thabit's wife (after her, according to the previous hadith) has mentioned (in her chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him)."
4028,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: In the first two years of the Caliphate of the Holy Prophet (SAW) of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA), three (talaqs) were counted as one. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people have started hastening about what was given to them."
4029,Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): Do you know that during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) during the caliphate of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and in the (initial) three years of the time of Sayyiduna Umar RA (RA) three (divorces) were counted as one. Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) replied yes.
4030,"Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, I am asking you by Allah, do you know this? In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three (talaqs) were counted as one in the early period of the Caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar, so Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said yes."
4031,"Ta'aws narrates: Abu Sahabah asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, I am asking you by Allah, do you know this? In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), three (talaqs) were counted as one in the early period of the Caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Umar, so Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas said yes."
4032,"Ibn Abu Malikah narrates: Abu Jozaa said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: Do you know that three divorces were counted as one in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) (during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr) and in the early period of the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), so he (Ibn Abbas) replied yes."
4033,Ibn Abu Malika narrated: Abu Jozaa said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas: Do you know that three talaqs were counted as one in the time of the Holy Prophet (Sayyiduna Abu Bakr) and in the early days of Sayyiduna Umar?
4034,"Mujahid narrates: One day I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) and a man came to him and said: O Abu Abbas, have I divorced my wife three times? Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: You disobeyed your Lord and your wife became forbidden to you. You do not fear Allah, otherwise He would have made room for you. Allah Ta'ala has said: \O Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! When you divorce women", give them according to their Idda," i.e. give them before their Idda. This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
4035,"Mujahid narrates: A person asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, he said: He has divorced his wife three times, (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
4036,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4037,"Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says about Ela: After four months, it will be suspended (at the man's will) either he turns to it or applies it."
4038,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4039,"Suhail bin Abu Salih narrates this statement of his father: I asked 12 Companions about such a person who commits adultery, and they gave the same answer."
4040,Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: I found ten companions of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with them) all of them say that they are suspended by the will of the one who gives them permission.
4041,Taus narrates that Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) used to question the one who made the request.
4042,"Sayyiduna Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, did not think anything (i.e. divorce does not take place) even if four months pass (the issue of divorce at the will of the man)."
4043,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) and Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) say: When four months have passed, it will be counted as a divorce."
4044,"Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) and Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) say: When four months have passed, it will be counted as a divorce."
4045,"Maimoni narrates: I mentioned to Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal the narration of Ata Khorasani on the authority of Abu Salama, narrated by Sayyiduna Uthman (may God be pleased with him), and he said, \I do not know what it is.\"" Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) has been quoted to the contrary. He was asked: Who copied it? He quoted the opinion of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding taws by Abd or Habib bin Abu Thabit."""
4046,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) says: (in Ela) when four months have passed, it will be considered as a divorce, and the man will have the right to approach her until the woman's period is completed."
4047,"Ayyub narrates: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr: Did Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) used to say: When four months have passed, it will be considered as a free divorce and Idda will not be required on the woman, she can marry (immediately afterwards) if she wants."
4048,"Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, narrated the following saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: When a woman claims that her husband has divorced her, and she also presents a just witness, then the husband will be sworn."
4049,"Narrated Abdullah bin Abu Malikah: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) about a person who divorces his wife without permission and then dies during her ``Idda''. So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) said: Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Auf divorced his wife Tamazar bint Asbagh Kalbi, then Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (RA) died during this woman’s Idda, so Sayyidna Uthman (RA) declared this woman as an heir."
4050,"Ibn Abu Malikah says: I met Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubayr at that time, he was riding a mule from Qaiqaan. I inquired what is your opinion about such a person. He who divorces his wife three times, he said: Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) has appointed such a woman as an heir."
4051,"Talha bin Abdullah narrates: Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) declared Tamazar bint Asbagh as the heir of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), although Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced this woman, he divorced her during his illness."
4052,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates: People found this in the letter of Sayyidna 'Umar (RA) that when someone commits a sin, his guardian should divorce him on his behalf."
4053,Amr bin Shuaib narrates: We have found this in the letter of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr. \When a madman commits adultery with his wife," his guardian should divorce him on his behalf.\"""""
4054,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: When a madman commits adultery with his wife, his guardian will be ordered to divorce him."
4055,"Muhammad bin Makhlad informed us, Sulayman bin Tawbah informed us, Abu Hudhayfah informed us."
4056,"Saeed Bin Musayyib narrates: An Arab slave girl ran away, she reached the Qura Valley, she reached the tribe from whom she ran away, a man from Banu Zara married her, she had many children, then the master of this slave girl came to him, he wanted to take custody of this slave girl and her children. As a ransom, a slave (or yaknes) should be paid, a male slave for a boy and a female slave for a girl, if these are not available, the townspeople will pay 60 dinars or 700 dirhams for a slave, and six duties will be imposed on the villagers."
4057,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says about (declaring) haram, it is an oath for which expiation must be made."
4058,"Saeed bin Musayb, Ata, Taaws, Sulayman bin Yasar, and Saeed bin Jubeer say: (Declaring) forbidden is an oath for which expiation will be paid."
4059,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Acquire the knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people because it is half of knowledge and it is the first thing that will be forgotten and it is the first thing that will be taken away from my ummah.
4060,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that there are three types of knowledge, and what is in addition to that is extra."
4061,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this after the revelation of Surah Nisa and the rules of inheritance were revealed in it.
4062,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: No one can be held captive from the shares of inheritance appointed by Allah. Except for Ibn Lahiyyah, no one has narrated its chain of transmission, he has narrated it on the authority of his brother. Both narrators are weak."
4063,"Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, has said this about (the deceased's) two daughters, mother, father and wife."
4064,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: One religion does not become the heir of another religion and the testimony of people belonging to one religion cannot be accepted against another religion. And the narrator named Umar is Umar bin Rashid who is not authentic.
4065,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No unbeliever can inherit from a Muslim, and no Muslim can inherit from an unbeliever."
4066,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I was standing under the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) at that time, and its saliva was flowing over me. On that occasion, he said, \Allah has determined the right of every rightful owner", therefore, a will cannot be made for an heir. The offspring will be a slave and the adulterer will be deprived. No one will be called by anyone other than his father. Do not attribute it to anyone other than the one who does it. The person who does this will be cursed by Allah continuously. A woman should not spend anything in her husband's house without his permission. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! Not even cereal? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “It is our most important wealth.” After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said," “The thing given as a loan must be returned."""
4067,"These are the words in another hadith, Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I stood under the camel of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4068,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Pay the property according to the obligatory parts of the inheritance, and whatever property is left over, it will belong to the next of kin."
4069,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Divide the property between the obligatory shares, whatever remains after the obligatory shares will belong to a close male relative. Abu Shiba narrated these words: Distribute the inheritance among the Dhu al-Faruz according to the order of the Book of Allah."
4070,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Give the obligatory shares to their sharers, and whoever is left will be taken by a close relative."
4071,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Give the obligatory portion to those who are entitled to it, and whatever remains will be given to a close relative."
4072,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Divide the wealth according to the obligatory parts, and whatever is left will be given to a close male relative."
4073,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Divide the property according to the obligatory parts, and whatever remains will be given to a close relative."
4074,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up and said: People belonging to two religions will not inherit each other. If so, that woman will not inherit anything from that man's property and wealth, and if one of them has killed the other as a sin, then he will inherit the property, but not the property. The narrator of this tradition is Muhammed bin Saeed Ta'ifi Thaqa."
4075,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4076,"It is narrated about Umar bin Abdul Aziz that he did not declare any deceased as the heir of another deceased, he only declared living persons as heirs of the deceased."
4077,"Shaykh Abul Zanad narrates: In the event of Hura, the inheritance of those who were killed was divided, so the living were made heirs of the deceased, and the deceased were not made heirs of each other."
4078,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: A woman named Umm Kulthum and her son Zayd, who was the son of Sayyidna Umar (RA) both died at the same time, but it was not known which of them died first. So they did not become the heirs of Ekad Vasra."
4079,"Ayyas bin Abd has the honor of being a companion (he says) when their house fell on some people, they were made heirs of each other."
4080,"It is narrated that Iyas bin Abd was asked about a house that is going to fall on people and those people die, so he said that those people will inherit each other."
4081,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: No Muslim can inherit from a Christian, except if he (a Christian) is his (Muslim) slave or slave (he will become an heir)."
4082,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) states: A Jew or a Christian cannot inherit from a Muslim, and a Muslim will not inherit from these people, but if he is a Jew or a Christian Muslim's (slave) or his slave (then the ruling will be different)."
4083,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this as the above hadith: (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said) We cannot inherit from the People of the Book and they cannot inherit from us, but a person can inherit from his (people of the Book) slaves or women."
4084,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People belonging to different religions cannot inherit from each other. You have also said this: The woman will inherit from her husband's wealth and his wealth, and the man will also inherit from the wealth of this woman, but if one of them kills the other, if he killed his partner intentionally, then he will not inherit from his property, and he will not inherit in wealth, but if the deceased was killed by mistake, then (on the other hand) he will inherit from his property, but in wealth. He will not inherit anything."
4085,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4086,Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) wrote in a letter to Sayyidna Dahhak Bin Sufyan (RA) that he should make Sayyidna Ashim Al-Adhabi the wife of his heirs.
4087,"It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrates: Zarara bin Majli, or perhaps Haran, said to Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote in a letter to Sayyidna Dahhak bin Sufyan, that he should be declared the heir, after that, according to a previous tradition. This tradition has also been copied by other narrators."
4088,Sayyidna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu says: Sayyidna Ashim was killed as a mistake.
4089,"Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, stood up and inquired whether any of you have any knowledge about whether the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave any decision regarding the inheritance of a woman in the death of a murdered husband. On this matter, Sayyiduna Dahhak bin Sufyan (RA) said, \I have knowledge about this. The Prophet (PBUH) wrote us this letter that we should give Ashim Zababi's wife a share of her husband's dowry.\"""""
4090,"Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: I think that the dowry will be given only to the Asaba relatives, because these are the people who also pay the dowry. After that, the narrator has narrated the hadith according to the previous one, and the names also contain the words that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) gave a decision according to it. A narrator named Ibn Jaraj has quoted these words additionally."
4091,"Saeed bin Musaib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab said that the dowry will be given to the family members and a woman will not inherit anything from her husband's dowry, until Sayyidna Dahhak bin Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) told him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote this letter to me."
4092,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib Radiyallahu Anhu says: According to the duties prescribed by Allah Ta'ala, the inheritance will be divided and the heir will share in it."
4093,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Aswaf, we came to a woman who was the grandmother of Al-Khaz bin Zayd. We stayed with her that day. They are the daughters of Saeed bin Rabi who were martyred with you in the Battle of Uhud. Their uncle has taken over their property and their share of inheritance. The two cannot marry, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Allah will decide about this.\"" Then the verse of Surah Nisa was revealed in which this command is given: \""Allah has decreed about your offspring that the share of one male will be equal to that of two females.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me", call this woman to me and bring her other half as well. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the executor of these girls: You give two-thirds of the inheritance to these girls and one-eighth to their mother," and you will get the remainder."""
4094,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned one-eighth share to his wife, two-thirds share to his two daughters, and the remaining wealth to his brother-in-law."
4095,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Sa’d bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said, “O Messenger of Allah, Sayyidna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred with him (after that, the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith in which these words are mentioned). You will get the baby."
4096,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Sa’d Bin Rabi’ (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah, Sayyidna Sa’d (RA) has passed away. He left two daughters and a brother. He did not answer, then she came to his service and said, O Messenger of Allah, it is the matter of the two daughters of Sayyiduna Sa'd, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Call his brother to Mir.\"" When that person came", the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said," \""Give two-thirds to his daughters and one-eighth to his wife"," and you will get what is left over.\"""""
4097,"Sayyidna Huzail bin Shahrabeel narrates: A man came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari and Salman bin Rabi'ah, and he inquired from them about the inheritance of a daughter, a granddaughter, and a half-sister. They both said: The daughter will get half of the property, and the rest of the wealth will go to her sister. The person who will answer according to our opinion came to Sayyidna Abdullah, asked him about it and told him that both of them had given this answer, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, I will give the decision about this that was given by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, half of the daughter will get, the sixth part will be given to the granddaughter, so that two-thirds will be completed, and the rest of the wealth will be given to her sister."
4098,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4099,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4100,"Huzail bin Shahrabeel narrates: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari was asked about a person who leaves behind a daughter, a granddaughter, and a half-sister. Hazrat Abu Musa said that his daughter will get half of it, and the rest of the property will be given to his sister. I said: Yes, the people asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud about this and told them about the answer of Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud said, “How can I say this when I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying that (in such a situation) the daughter will get half, the granddaughter will get a sixth, thus two-thirds of the shares will be completed and the remainder will be given to the sister-in-law. will be found."
4101,"Imam Jafar Sadiq narrates this statement of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir): Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and her (wife) son Zayd (who was the son of Sayyidna Umar RA) both of them died on the same day. So that woman did not become the heir of this child and that child did not become the heir of this woman, similarly the people of Safin did not become the heirs of each other, in the same way the people who were killed in the incident of Hara did not become the heirs of each other."
4102,"Shaykh Abu Hani Umar bin Bashir says: Sayyidna Aamir (RA) was asked about a child who is neither male nor female, nor does it have any signs of a male, nor does it have any signs of a female, but urine or faeces comes out of his navel."
4103,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Acquire the knowledge of the Qur’an and teach it to the people. Acquire the knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people. Acquire knowledge and teach it to the people, because I will pass away and soon the knowledge will be taken away and temptations will begin to appear. can decide between The same raiyat is also quoted in some other isnads."
4104,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Acquire knowledge and teach it to the people; “Acquire knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people; Couldn't decide between the two.
4105,"Saeed bin Hasan narrates: I said to Sufyan al-Thawri: If you take the position of giving a decision about inheritance, from whom will you seek guidance in this regard? So Sufyan replied: (I will be guided by the rulings) regarding the inheritance of Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit."
4106,"Aswad bin Yazid narrates that Sayyidna Mu'adhbin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, came to us at the time when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had sent him."
4107,Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) gave half of the share to his daughter and gave the remaining property to her.
4108,Aswad bin Yazid Kufi narrates that Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) divided the inheritance of a person in Yemen who left behind a daughter and a sister. Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) gave half to his daughter and half to his sister.
4109,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the slave of Sayyidna Hamza (RA) died, leaving behind a daughter and a daughter of Sayyidna Hamza (RA), so the Prophet (PBUH) gave half a share to the daughter of that slave and also gave half a share to the daughter of Sayyidna Hamza (RA)."
4110,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: My son has passed away, what will I get from his inheritance? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will get a sixth. When he went back, he called him and said: You will get another sixth. When he went back, the Prophet called him and said: You will get another sixth in addition."
4111,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah bin Sahl Hanif (RA) narrates that a person killed another person with a crossbow. This person was only his uncle. Sayyidna Abu Ubaidah Bin Jarrah (RA) wrote a letter about this to Sayyidna Umar (RA). There are mullahs and the person who has no heir, his maternal uncle will become his heir."
4112,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, whoever has no guardian, Allah is his guardian, and whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle will inherit him."
4113,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who has no guardian, Allah is his guardian, and he who has no heir, his maternal uncle will inherit him. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Allah and His Messenger will be the guardians of the person who has no guardian, and the maternal uncle will be the heir of the person who has no heir."
4114,"Shaykh Abu Asim was asked whether this was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he remained silent. So Shazkuni said to him: Tell us a hadith about the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him. So he remained silent."
4115,"This tradition is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, this tradition is \suspended\""."""
4116,"Sayyiduna Muqadam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I am closer to every believer than his life, whoever leaves property, it will be given to his heirs, and whoever leaves debt or children (even if they are not in a happy state), then they will come to me. Who has no heir because he will pay off his debt and fulfill his obligations."
4117,The same tradition and chain of transmission is narrated by Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maad Yakarb (RA).
4118,"This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another document."""
4119,"This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another document."""
4120,"The same hadith is narrated from Sayyida Aisha on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: Allah and His Messenger (are his guardians)."
4121,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever has no heir," his maternal uncle becomes the heir.\"""""
4122,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH): The maternal uncle becomes the heir.
4123,"Alqamah has narrated this about Abdul Malik that when a person has a grandchild and a niece, then the wealth will be divided between them by half. It is true that this is Alqamah's own opinion."
4124,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: You recite the commandment of the will before paying the debt while reciting. But the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the will (of the deceased) is fulfilled, the debt will be paid and siblings from the mother's side will inherit from each other, while siblings from the father's side will not inherit from each other."
4125,"Al-Harith narrates that a case came to Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about two cousins, one of whom was a half-brother on the mother's side. If I were in his place, I would have given him one-sixth and divided the remaining wealth among them (other cousins)."
4126,"Masoud bin Haqm al-Saqfi narrates that a case came to Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with her, which was about a woman who left behind her husband, her mother, maternal siblings, and paternal siblings. Had not made the other a sharer', then Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: The decision we gave at that time was that of that time. Our decision today is what we have given now."
4127,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) made his Companions brothers, then they made each other heirs, until this verse was revealed: \Only (lineal) relatives will inherit each other.\"" After that"," people started to inherit each other according to lineage."""
4128,Sayyiduna Wathila bin Asqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: A woman inherits from three people: from her freed (slave) her children and from her child whom she cursed.
4129,"Sayyidna Wathla bin Asqaa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A woman inherits in three ways: the inheritance of her freed (slave or maidservant) whom she raised (i.e. fostering an abandoned child), her inheritance and the one for whom she cursed."
4130,This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Wasila (RA) along with another chain of transmission.
4131,Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered three grandmothers and grandmothers to pay one-sixth of it.
4132,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates that two grandmothers (namely, Yadadi and Nani) came to Sayyidna Abu Bakr, so Sayyidna Abu Bakr named Nani instead of the grandmother, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl said to them: 'They have participated in the Battle of Badr.' O Caliph Messenger! You have given the inheritance to her so that if she dies, she (the woman) will not be her heir."
4133,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates that a grandmother and a grandmother came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Radi Allahu Anhu). There was a grandmother and a grandmother. So Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Radi Allahu Anhu) ordered to pay the legacy to the grandmother. He did not order for the grandmother. Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, who belonged to Banu Haritha, said to him: O Caliph Messenger! You have ordered to pay it so that if she died, she would not be his heir, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) ordered to pay both of them (the narrator says:) i.e. ordered to pay one-sixth part."
4134,Abdullah bin Baridah narrates from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered the grandmother to pay one-sixth of the share while there was no mother below her.
4135,Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave Nani (Yadadi) a sixth portion.
4136,"Ibrahim bin Yazid narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared three children as heirs, two of them were from the father's side and one was from the mother's side (that is, there were two grandmothers and one was a grandmother)."
4137,"Al-Khaari bin Zayd narrates this about his father Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA): He had inherited three valleys of grandmothers, while they were of the same rank, two of them from the father's side and one from the mother's side."
4138,"It has been narrated about Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) that he named three wadis and grandmothers as heirs, of which two were from the maternal side and one was from the father's side."
4139,Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) that he has given the status of grandfather and father.
4140,"Aqeel bin Khalid narrates: Saeed bin Sulaiman narrated to his father about his grandfather Zayd bin Thabit (RA) that once Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked for permission to enter his house. Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu said: O Commander of the Faithful! If you had sent me a message, 'I would have come to you', then Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: I have come to you on a mission, 'I have come to inquire about the ruling about Dada,' then Sayyidna Zayd (RA) said: 'No! By Allah! What is your opinion about this? So Sayyiduna Umar said: There is no revelation in this matter that we are guilty of any increase or decrease. This is a matter in which you have to give your opinion. If I understand that your opinion is in accordance with my opinion, then I will accept it. Otherwise, there will be no blame on you in this regard. He said: I have come here because you will solve my problem. Then Sayyiduna Umar came to Sayyidna Zayd again at the same time that he had come on the first day and discussed with him about it. Sayyidna Zayd said: I will give you something to write about this. So he wrote it on a piece of palan and explained it with an example. It grows on top of the stem, a branch comes out of it, then another branch comes out of it, that stem conveys the water to this branch, if the first branch is cut, the water will come to this branch, and if the second branch is cut, the water will go to the first branch. He said: I apply what Zayd has said about Dada. The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) was the first grandfather with whom this situation happened. He took all his wealth, that is, he took the property of his grandson and did not take the property of his sisters (i.e. granddaughters)."
4141,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) that he had ruled that in the presence of siblings (of the deceased), the grandfather would also be a sharer, regardless of the number of siblings."
4142,"Yunus bin Yazid narrates that I inquired from Zuhri about the inheritance of a person who is survived by a grandfather and siblings. Zahri said: Saeed bin Musayb, Ubaidullah bin Abdullah and Qubaysa bin Zuayb have stated that Sayyidna Umar (RA) had given this decision: \The grandfather will share with his siblings and the siblings from the father's side"," while one-third of the wealth is better in his favor.\"" It will be given according to the calculation. They also gave this decision. Full-siblings have more rights than co-siblings from the father's side", whether they are male or female. However, if the co-siblings from the father's side are present with the full-siblings, then they will also get their share. If there is anything left after the obligatory share of the sisters," it will be given by the father to the co-brothers under the principle of equal share for one male and two female."""
4143,Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: A murderer will not inherit.
4144,Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The murderer will not get anything (from the inheritance).
4145,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA).
4146,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) that a murderer does not inherit.
4147,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer does not become an heir (of the murdered). Shaykh Abu Abd al-Rahman says: A narrator named Ishaq is an obsolete hadith.
4148,Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer will not inherit anything.
4149,This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Amro bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather.
4150,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
4151,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “There can be no will for an heir.
4152,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The debt will be paid before the will is completed and no bequest will be made for the heir.
4153,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said: A will cannot be made for an heir.
4154,Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this in his sermon on the Day of Sacrifice: A will cannot be made for an heir.
4155,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
4156,"Ata bin Yasarbayan says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Kurqaba on horseback so that he could discuss the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt, then Allah revealed the order that they would not inherit."
4157,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not received anything for him (i.e., I have not received any order to give him an inheritance)."
4158,"Hisham bin Arwah narrates on the authority of his father that Sayyiduna Zubair (RA) narrated that this verse was revealed to us: \And the relatives will inherit each other (this is the order in the Book of Allah).\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made two Muhajirin and an Ansari brothers to each other", so we had no doubt that we would become each other's heirs. That is, if Sayyiduna Ka'b (R.A.) died and he had no heir, I thought that I would become his heir and if I died," he would also become my heir until this verse was revealed."""
4159,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt, and he said, \I do not know about it.\"" Gabriel will come (and tell me about it)", then he said: Where is the person who inquires about the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt? When this person was brought, he said: Gabriel has told me that these two will not get anything (i.e. they will not inherit). This hadith has been narrated only by a narrator named Masada with reference to Muhammad bin Amr," and this narrator is weak."""
4160,This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet along with another chain of transmission.
4161,Sha'bi narrated: Ziyad bin Abu Sufyan said to his companion: Do you know what Sayyiduna Umar (RA) had decided about paternal aunt and paternal aunt? The man replied: No! Tuziad said: I know the best about what Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled in this regard.
4162,"Sayyidna Abu Baksha Anmari (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) conquered Makkah (i.e. attacked it), Sayyidna Zubair (RA) was in charge of the left part, while Sayyidna Muqdad (RA) was in charge of the right part. He removed the balloon and said: I have appointed two parts for the horse and one part for the rider."
4163,"Sayyiduna Abu Raham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I participated in an expedition with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my brother was with me. We had two horses with us, so he gave us six shares."
4164,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned three parts to the rider and his horse: one part was for the man and two parts were for his horse.
4165,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) prescribed two parts for the horse and one part for the rider.
4166,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) assigned two shares for the horse and one share for the rider while dividing.
4167,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4168,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave three parts to a man and his horse: one part belonged to the man and two parts to his horse.
4169,Sayyidna Muqdad Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I participated in the Battle of Badr with the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam).
4170,Sayyidna Muqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me one share and two shares to my horse on the occasion of the Battle of Khyber.
4171,"Sayyidna Muqdad bin Amr (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Badr, the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to his horse and one part to him."
4172,"Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, Sayyidna Talha bin Ubaidullah and Sayyidna Zubair bin Awam (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave parts to a horse and a part to a man."
4173,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4174,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two hundred horses to two hundred horses on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain.
4175,The same hadith is narrated along with another document which says: Every horse had two parts.
4176,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave one part to the horseman and two parts to the horse.
4177,"Bashir bin Umarubi says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave four parts to my horse and one part to me, so I got five parts."
4178,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I participated in a battle with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
4179,"Sayyidna Majma bin Jariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the Battle of Hudaybiyyah. When we returned from there, people started running their camels. Some people asked others: What has happened to these people? We went out and found the Holy Prophet (PBUH) staying at the place of \Kara' Al-Ghumayim\"". When some people who were going towards him gathered there"," the Prophet (PBUH) recited this verse: \""Verily"," We have given you a clear victory.\"" The narrator narrates: So one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Is this a victory? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! Kind of this caste! In whose power is my life! This is victory. Narrator narrates: Then", among those who participated in the Hudaybiyah campaign, the property of the Khyber campaign was divided into eighteen parts. The number of the army was fifteen hundred," of which three were cavalrymen."""
4180,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed two parts for the horseman and one part for the footman. We have mentioned earlier.
4181,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates about the Prophet (PBUH) that he (PBUH) gave two parts to the cavalry and one part to the infantry.
4182,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave two shares to the horseman and one share to the footman. The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, the narrator has a doubt about one word whether that word is horse or horse."
4183,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4184,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the cavalry and one part to the infantry. This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4185,"With another chain of transmission, it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be three parts for the horseman and one part for the footman."
4186,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khyber, his (booty) was divided into eighteen parts."
4187,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair narrates the statement of Sayyidna Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me four shares on the day of the Battle of Badr, two shares were for my horse, one share was for me, and one share was for my mother, who was among the relatives."
4188,"Sayyiduna Zubair bin Al-Awam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave him four parts: two parts were for his horse, one part was for him, and one part was for him, and one part was for his mother, who was among Dhu al-Qurbi."
4189,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates this on the authority of his father. He says: The Prophet (PBUH) gave four shares to Sayyidna Zubair Bin Awam (RA) on the day of the Battle of Khyber. One part was his, one part belonged to Dhu Al-Qurbi, who was Safiya bint Abdul Muttalib (i.e., who was the maternal grandmother of the Prophet (PBUH)) and two parts belonged to his horse (i.e. Sayyidna Zubair (RA))."
4190,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave four parts to Sayyidna Zubair (RA) one part was for his mother because of his qarat, one part was for Sayyidna Zubair (RA) and two parts were for his horse."
4191,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4192,"Muhammad bin Yahya narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, 'He had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Battle of Hunain, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given two parts to his horse and one part to him."
4193,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the horse and one part to the person with the horse.
4194,Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the horse and one part to the rider.
4195,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever puts a horse among two horses and is not sure that it will come out ahead, there is no harm in it, and whoever puts a horse in two horses and is sure that it will come out ahead, it is gambling."
4196,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the Battle of Utas, we found some captive women, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: No one should have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth to her pregnancy, and a woman who is not pregnant should not have intercourse with her until she has menstruated once."
4197,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a slave leaves the kingdom of the polytheists before his master, he will be free, and if he leaves after his master, then he will be returned to the master. Will get back."
4198,"Salim bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever keeps his (former) wealth in the booty before the division of the booty, he will get it, and whoever finds it after the division of the booty, he will not get anything. The narrator named Ishaq is Ishaq bin Abu Farah and it is obsolete."
4199,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: The polytheists acquire the wealth of the Muslims, and then the Muslims prevail over them, then one of us finds his wealth with them, then he will be more entitled to this wealth than any other person. Shaykh Abu Sahl stated that he would be more entitled to receive this wealth in exchange for the price."
4200,"Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The enemy who takes possession of the wealth and then before it is divided (into booty), if the owner of the wealth takes care of the wealth, it will be given to him."
4201,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The wealth that the enemy seizes and then the Muslims get that wealth from him, the original owner of that wealth can take it before it is divided, he will be more entitled to it. One of the narrators of this tradition, Hasan bin Amara, is extinct."
4202,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of Ghazwa Ahad, I was presented before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was fourteen years old at that time. He did not allow me to participate. He did not consider me an adult. The narrator narrates: I told Sayyiduna Umar bin Abdul Aziz about this, so he wrote a letter to his government officials to pay the salary only to a person who has reached the age of fifteen. It was the custom of Sayyidna Umar bin Abdul Aziz that he fixed a salary of one hundred dirhams for a fifteen-year-old boy."
4203,"Sayyiduna Ya'la bin Marah (RA) narrates that I traveled with the Prophet (PBUH) many times, 'I saw you that whenever you passed by the dead body of a person, you did not pass on until you ordered him to be buried, you did not inquire whether it was a Muslim or an infidel."
4204,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Uhud, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered about Sayyidna Hamza (RA) that his dead body was placed in the direction of the Qiblah, then seven takbirs were recited over him, and other martyrs were also gathered around him until the Prophet (PBUH) prayed over him seventy times. They have been desecrated.' So he said: If I had cursed the Quraysh, I would cut thirty of their men to pieces in the same way. So Allah revealed this verse: \If they have punished you"," then you should treat them the same as you have been treated.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Abdul Aziz bin Imran Zaeef."""
4205,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Uhud, Sayyidna Hamza (RA) came to the Prophet (SAW) and his lips, nose, ears, etc. were cut off and mutilated. Then Sayyiduna Hamza was given a shroud as a shroud. When his head was covered, his feet were visible. These words of the hadith have been narrated only by the narrator named Uthman: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer of any martyr other than him. These words are not preserved."
4206,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: 'Azhar (grass) was placed on their feet and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer for any martyr except him."
4207,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The person who was martyred in Uhud was not bathed, he was buried with his blood and his funeral prayer was not performed."
4208,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: I will be a witness to these people on the Day of Resurrection. Then they were buried along with their blood under the order of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). The Prophet (PBUH) did not offer their funeral prayers. This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4209,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the polytheists left those who were killed in the Battle of Uhud and went back, the Prophet (PBUH) saw something that caused him great pain. He would have left the same, 'Until Allah the Exalted would have revived them from the stomachs of beasts and birds,' I will replace them with the likeness of seventy men. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for his cloak and covered Sayyidna Hamzah’s face with it. Sayyidna Hamzah’s feet appeared. The Prophet covered his face and placed grass on his feet. 'Even the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over them seventy times because the number of martyrs of the Battle of Uhud was seventy.' When these people were buried and you were done with it, this verse was revealed: \Invite to the path of your Lord through wisdom and good preaching.\"" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted patiently and did not imitate any person. This hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Ismail bin Ayyash and there is confusion in the traditions he has quoted from narrators other than the Syrians."""
4210,"Al-Khajri bin Zayd narrates this statement of his father (Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him): Earlier, people of every nation used to become heirs to each other, except when a person died blind due to the collapse of a house or a fire, or a war or any other reason."
4211,"Isa bin Harith narrates that the brother of Shareeh bin Harith had a mother-son, she gave birth to a girl, then the girl got married, she gave birth to a boy, then the mother died. It is not, because this woman is Kanwasa. So Maysara bin Yazid rode to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair and told him about what Qazi Shareeh had given a decision. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair wrote a letter to Qazi Shareeh, 'Maysara bin Yazeed has mentioned to me that you recited this verse in such a situation: \Relationships inherit each other in the book of Allah\"" This verse is about relatives and belongs to the time when people used to make an agreement with each other (i.e. they used to say: they used to become brothers) the man used to say: you become my heir and I will become your heir' When this verse was revealed", this practice was abandoned. Then Maysara bin Yazid came to Qazi Shareeh with that letter. After reading it," he refused to withdraw his decision and said: This man freed this mother in her womb (because of the child)."""
4212,"Imam al-Shaabi narrates: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A person who kills by mistake or on purpose does not become an heir (to the slain), Allah knows best."
4213,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: The person who makes a contract of writing in exchange for one suwa qiya and pays everything except ten oqiyah, then that person will be considered a slave. will be)."
4214,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a person who has entered into a contract of writing commits a crime or becomes a sharer in an inheritance, he will have the right to inherit according to the amount of his freed share, and according to the amount of his freed share, the limit will be issued on him."
4215,"Saeed bin Abu Saeed Maqbari narrates this with reference to his father: A woman belonging to Banulith bought me for seven hundred dirhams in the market of Zul Mijaz, then when I came, she entered into a contract with me for forty thousand dirhams. I will not take it like this, but I will take it every month or every year. I took it with me to Sayyiduna Umar and mentioned this in front of him. Sayyiduna Umar said: You deposit it in Baitul-Mal. Then Sayyiduna Umar called this woman and said: Your wealth is deposited in Baitul-Mal. Abu Saeed is free. The narrator narrates: It was sent to him, so he received it."
4216,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The person who has entered into a contract of writing will pay the free man's dowry according to the amount he has become free, and the slave will pay the dowry according to the amount of his slave."
4217,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had given a decision regarding a person who had been killed, that according to the amount he had paid out of the contract of his correspondence, his dues would be the dues of a free person and the remaining payment would be the dues of a slave."
4218,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever has a share in a slave Yakinis and frees his share, then it is obligatory on him to free him from the shares of the remaining owners of the slave Yakinis. It will be valued according to justice and he shall pay for it on behalf of his partners according to the value of the share of the slave. But this is only when the property of the freedman is equal to the value of the shares of his partners."
4219,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever frees his share of a common slave, then the value of that slave will be assessed according to justice, and then that person will pay his other partners, and the slave will be freed by that person if he is prosperous."
4220,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a slave is jointly owned by two men, one of them frees his share. The narrator named Hisham has adapted it and he did not mention that this slave will be made to work. Shuba and Hisham are more hafiz than other opinions in quoting traditions regarding Qatadah. While other narrators have narrated with regard to Qatadah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered labor, I believe that these narrators are delusional because this tradition is different from the tradition narrated by Shu'ba and Hisham."
4221,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same tradition regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that this is the same tradition as narrated by Shu'ba.
4222,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A man freed his share of a slave, and the Prophet (PBUH) justified his freeing and ordered him to pay the remaining value of that slave as ransom. Qatadah says: If a person does not have wealth, then this slave will be made to work, but he will not be subjected to labor in this regard. Shaykh Nishapuri has stated that the best hadith is the one narrated by Hammam and he has clarified the difference between the saying of the Holy Prophet and the saying of Qatadah."
4223,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about a slave that is jointly owned by two men. One of them frees his share. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That part of the slave will be freed and a suitable price will be paid from the property of the person who freed it. He will not be subjected to labor.
4224,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever frees a part of his slave, then the remaining part of that slave should also be freed from that person’s property, if that person has enough wealth, otherwise, the value of that slave will be set according to justice, and then he will be made to work for it.” However, he will not be subjected to hardship."
4225,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, which is about a slave who is jointly owned by some people and one of them frees his share, then the person who freed him must also free the remaining share. And that slave will be considered free by that person. A narrator has also mentioned the maids in this tradition."
4226,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Whoever frees his share in a slave, he will be the guarantor of his freedom."
4227,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that a person came, his name was Salih, and he brought his brother. He said: O Messenger of God! I want to free this brother of mine, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you became the owner of him, then Allah freed him. A narrator Al-Azrami has been declared obsolete by Abdullah bin Mubarak, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, Ibn Mahdi, while a narrator named Abu Nazr Muhammad bin Saib Kalbi is obsolete."
4228,"Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (RA) says: When you buy a slave who has been freed, he will free him without imposing this condition because it is a bond of slavery."
4229,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: If a man's slave-girl gives birth to a child, that slave-girl will be considered free after that person's death."
4230,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When someone's slave girl gives birth to his child, she will be free after that person's death."
4231,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said this: A slave girl who gives birth to a child will be considered free, even if the child is born incomplete."
4232,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A slave girl who gives birth to her master's child is automatically freed after the master's (death).
4233,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the mother of Sayyidna Ibrahim (RA) gave birth to him, the Prophet (PBUH) said that her child has set her free."
4234,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The mother of Ibrahim has been freed by her child.
4235,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyida Mariya (RA) gave birth to (Sayyidna Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet (PBUH), the Prophet (PBUH) said: Her child has given her freedom."
4236,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a slave girl gives birth to her master's child, then when that master dies, she is freed. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyida Mariya Quptiyah (RA) gave birth to Sayyidna Ibrahim (RA), the son of the Prophet (PBUH), the Prophet (PBUH) said: Her child has set her free."
4237,
4238,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4239,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4240,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this.
4241,"Bashir bin Saeed narrates that Khawat bin Jubeer narrated this: A man left a will to her. This person left behind a mother and a free wife. There was a dispute between the woman and the mother of the son, so the free woman sent a message to the mother of the son: You will soon be sold. Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubeer (RA) presented this matter to the Prophet (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said: He said: He cannot be sold. Under the order of the Holy Prophet, he was declared free."
4242,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4243,The same tradition has been narrated by Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubayr (RA) with reference to some other isnads.
4244,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever frees a slave and the slave has any wealth, that wealth will remain with the slave. However, if his master makes an exception, the ruling will be different."
4245,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person frees a slave, his property also remains with him."
4246,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) that he had given a decision that the mother of the son would not be sold, she would not be bequeathed, she would not be inherited, her master would continue to benefit from her as long as he lived, and when that master died, the son would be free."
4247,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of Umm-Wald. He said: They shall not be sold. He will live, he will benefit from them and when he dies, she will be considered independent."
4248,"The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) with reference to another chain of transmission, and it is not narrated as a \marfu'\"" hadith."""
4249,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he forbade the sale of Umm-Wald, “She cannot be given away, “She shall not be divided in inheritance,” Her master will continue to benefit from her during his lifetime, and when the master dies, she will be considered as free."
4250,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade the sale of Umm-Wald. They cannot be sold. They cannot be given away.
4251,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to sell our mothers and children as maidservants and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive at that time.
4252,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) says about Umm-Wald that during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), we used to buy and sell her."
4253,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: We used to sell the mother of the child during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
4254,Saeed bin Musayyib narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) declared the mothers and children of female slaves free.
4255,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): Once he had separated a slave girl from her child, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from doing so and terminated the transaction."
4256,"Sulaiman bin Yasarbayan narrates: Once I was sitting with Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him. A young man from the Ansar came to him and said: I have a cousin of whom I am a guardian. Peace be upon you. Abu Bakr-e-Nami, the narrator, said: This hadith is: \Gharib\""."""
4257,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The children of the concubines will be considered free with their freedom and slaves with their slavery.
4258,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (may peace be upon him), a man freed his slave. There was 'he had allowed that his services could be sold. The narrator of this tradition is Abdul Ghaffar \weak\"" and other narrators have quoted it as a \""Mursal\"" tradition with reference to the narrator named Abu Ja'far."""
4259,Narrator Abu Ja'farnami (probably Imam Baqir) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold the services of a concubine.
4260,"A narrator named Abu Jaafar narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold the services of a slave girl. A narrator named Abu Bakr narrates: This is the only hadith I could find about this, and the narrator named Abu Jaafar is reliable, but his tradition is \Mussal\""."""
4261,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: There is no harm in selling the services of a counselor while he is in need. This hadith is incorrect as it is transmitted with reference to a narrator named Ibn Tarif. The correct tradition is that it was narrated by a narrator named Abdul Malik as a \Mursal\"" tradition from a narrator named Abu Ja'far and this tradition has already passed."""
4262,Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered the sale of mudbar.
4263,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The executor (the decision to free the deceased) will be from one-third of the property.
4264,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A slave cannot be sold, nor can he be given away. This hadith has only been narrated by a narrator named Ubaidah bin Hasan with a chain of transmission and this narrator is weak."
4265,It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA): He considered it abhorrent to sell a Madbar. This tradition is authentic and this tradition is “Muquf”.
4266,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once a person died, he left a slave and left some debt. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his heirs to sell the slave to pay off the debt. So they sold the slave for eight hundred dirhams. Abu Bakranami Muhaddith stated that these words of the hadith: A person died, the narrator made a mistake in this because other narrators have narrated this: (His master himself freed the slave) The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, while paying the price of this slave to his master, said that you should pay off your debt through him. At that time his master was alive."
4267,"It is narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that once she fell ill, one of her nephews mentioned her illness to a person belonging to the Zat tribe who was a doctor, and that person said: The woman you are talking about has been bewitched and this magic was done by one of her maidservants, who had a child in her lap at that time, and the child urinated on the woman's lap. The nieces reported this to Sayyida Ayesha, and Ayesha said, \Bring such and such a slave girl to me.\"" They said about one of their female slaves: \""So these people said that she has a child in her lap.\"" The one who had urinated on Sayya Ayesha's lap. But what was the magic? So he replied: Yes! Sayyida Aisha inquired: Why them? She replied: I wanted you to set me free. So Saida Aisha freed this slave girl as a counselor. Then Saida Aisha said: Now in the name of Allah"," it is necessary for me to say that you will never be free. Who is very rich and sell it to a slave girl. Then Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) bought another slave girl for her price and set her free."""
4268,"It has been narrated about Ibn Sirin, 'He did not think there was anything wrong with a man paying the price of his wife's maidservants himself."
4269,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) or perhaps Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) that he says: There is nothing wrong with a pregnant woman or a lactating woman not fasting for a day or a few days in the month of Ramadan.
4270,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever takes an oath about an oath and thinks that he will fulfill it and then fails to do so, his sin will be on the person who did not allow it to be fulfilled."
4271,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A woman sent her a plate containing dates. Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) ate some dates from it and left some dates. She said: I swear to you that you will eat all of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill it.
4272,"Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that once after the sun had set, Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) thought it appropriate that he should fast, so he fasted."
4273,"Abu Abd al-Rahman narrates: After the sun had set, Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) intended to fast and fasted."
4274,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a person looks into his neighborhood (or someone's house) and another person hits his eye with a stone, there will be no retribution for him."
4275,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I have been given the most concise words, so I complete the matter in short words."
4276,"It is narrated with the same document that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to me: “The Qur’an is very soft, in which there are many aspects, so you should apply it to the situation that is best for you.”"
4277,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: My words cannot abrogate the words of Allah, but the words of Allah can abrogate my words, and one part of Allah's words can abrogate another."
4278,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Like the abrogation of the Qur'an, our hadiths also abrogate each other."
4279,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates that I swear by my father, “He told me that sometimes the Prophet (PBUH) used to say something, and then after some time, he would abrogate it."
4280,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu says: Avoid those who follow your own opinion, because they will be enemies of the Sunnah, they will not be able to remember the hadiths and will explain the commandment through their own opinion, they will be misguided and mislead others as well."
4281,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The children of Israel fell victim to destruction when the children of captive women began to create new things in them.
4282,"Sayyida Umima bint Ruqiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates a similar hadith regarding the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
4283,"Sayyida Umeema bint Ruqiqa, the aunt of Sayyida Fatimah, the daughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates: We pledged allegiance to the Holy Hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
4284,"Sayyida Umima bint Ruqiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance. We said: O Messenger of Allah! We pledge allegiance to Your Holy Hand that we will not associate anyone with Allah, We will not steal, We will not commit adultery, We will not kill our children, We will not falsely accuse anyone on our behalf, And we will not disobey You in any good deed. The Messenger is more merciful towards us than our own selves, O Messenger of Allah! Extend your holy hand so that we may pledge allegiance to you. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not shake hands with women."
4285,"Bakarbin Abdul Aziz narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received some good news, he would go into prostration before Allah."
4286,"Sayyiduna Zubair (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade us to fight on behalf of the polytheists, but we will fight on behalf of the responsible people."
4287,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Allah, the Exalted, said: O son of Adam! There are two characteristics in you which were not in you before, one is that when you overcome your anger, I will increase your wealth in order to purify you, and the other is that when your life is complete, my servants will continue to pray for you."
4288,"Sayyidna Mu'awiyah bin Qura'ah narrates on the authority of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The person whose time of death approaches and he makes a will, according to the order of the Book of Allah, if he has a will, it will become an atonement for what he was not able to pay Zakat."
4289,Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): \Allah has given you one-third of your wealth at the time of your death as a charity, so that you may increase your good deeds," so that it becomes a source of purity in your actions.\"""""
4290,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No one has the right to have any property in his possession in which he has to make a will, and then two nights pass (that he has not written that will), his will should be written with him."
4291,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: No Muslim has the right to have property that he has to make a will and then two nights pass (that he has not made a will), his will should be in writing with him."
4292,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a person that three days should pass in such a way that he has such property that he should bequeath (and he did not make a bequest).
4293,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is a great sin to harm someone (an heir) while making a will.
4294,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A man should write in his will that if I die without changing my will (so it will be).
4295,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if other heirs wish (then the ruling will be different)."
4296,"Sayyidna Amro bin Al-Khajri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A will is not for an heir, but if the other heirs want it (it can be)."
4297,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
4298,"Imam Ja'far Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates with reference to his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be no will for the heir, nor will there be acknowledgment of debt (in the property of the inheritance)."
4299,"Sayyidna Amroo bin Al-Khajri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) while giving a sermon to us in Mina, said this: Allah has determined the share of each one of you in the estate. Therefore, it is not permissible to make a bequest to an heir."
4300,The same is true of the same (past) Hadith with a different Sunad.
4301,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in the house of Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with him) along with some of his other pure wives, all of whom were waiting for food. The narrator said: This was before the decree of hijab was revealed. Sayyida Aisha grabbed it and broke it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it with his hand and mixed it. He sent Sayyida Hafsa (RA) and gave the broken cup to Sayyida Ayesha (RA) as if it had been decided that whoever breaks something will get it and he will be required to pay for it."
4302,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma narrates about the saying of Allah Ta'ala: \And when the Prophet said something in a whisper to one of his wives.\"" He says: Sayyida Hafsa saw the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace). He was present at that time with the mother of Sayyidna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet said: You should not tell Aisha about this. Sayyida Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) went to Sayyidah Hafsa (may God be pleased with her) and she told Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her)"," then Allah informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. That's why you didn't mention this."""
4303,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Earlier people used to write this at the beginning of their wills: This is the will that So-and-so bin So-and-so has made. He testifies that there is no god but Allah. He is one god. He would revive all the people present, then he would exhort his survivors to fear Allah Almighty and work in peace with each other, obey Allah and His Messenger, if they believe, and he is giving them the will that Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) made to his sons: O my sons! Indeed, Allah Ta'ala has chosen a religion for you, so when you die, then become a Muslim."
4304,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: Once I decided to go to Khyber. I attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was in the mosque at that time. I greeted him. Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you go to my lawyer in Khyber, take fifteen wasqs from him. For the family of Muhammad, there are only those dates in Khyber. If he asks you for a sign (i.e. evidence), you should place your hand on his collarbone. After that, he mentioned the entire hadith. Khabarwahid' makes action necessary."
4305,"Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha, Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka’b and Sayyidna Suhail Bin Bayda (RA) were sitting next to Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) drinking wine made from dates and chawhars. Anas! Pour out the wine in your vessel.' He said this when we came to know about this, then Sayyiduna Anas (RA) says that I poured out the wine. Shaykh Abu Abdullah i.e. Ubaidullah bin Abdul Samad says: This indicates that the news makes the action necessary."
4306,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that when poetry was mentioned before the Prophet (PBUH), he said: It is like speech."
4307,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4308,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Poetry is like speech.
4309,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A good poem is like a good speech and a good poem is like a good speech.
4310,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): It is not necessary to pay jizya on a Muslim.
4311,Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evidence must be presented against the claimant and an oath must be taken against the person against whom the claim is made.
4312,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: If people start giving according to their claims, then people will start making claims about the lives and property of others."
4313,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An oath means that which is confirmed by your companion.
4314,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4315,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4316,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4317,"Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Vows are of two types: the one who makes a vow for the sake of Allah, he should fulfill it, and the one who makes a vow related to disobedience to Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation for breaking an oath."
4318,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever makes a vow and does not mention his name, his expiation will be the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever takes a vow related to disobedience to Allah, then his expiation will be the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow and that vow is not in his power (i.e., he cannot fulfill it), then his expiation will be the atonement of breaking an oath. There will be expiation, and whoever makes a vow in the name of Allah Ta'ala that he can fulfill, then he should fulfill it."
4319,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A vow is only about that thing in which the commandment of Allah has been obeyed.
4320,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever makes a vow of disobedience to Allah, the expiation for him will be the same as the expiation for breaking an oath. If he sends a gift to the Kaaba without seeking the pleasure of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath, and whoever donates his wealth to the poor for a purpose that is not for the sake of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath, and the person who is obliged to walk to the house of Allah on foot, and it is for such a reason that he If the purpose is not to seek the pleasure of Allah, then his expiation is the same as the expiation of breaking an oath. Whoever makes a vow to walk to the house of Allah on account of something that the purpose is to seek the pleasure of Allah, then he should ride. If he does not go on foot, when he reaches Mecca, he will fulfill his vow. If the desire is achieved, then he should fear Allah and try to fulfill it until he becomes tired of the vow (i.e. he is unable to fulfill it)."
4321,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever makes a vow that he does not specify, his expiation is that of breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow that he does not have the power to fulfill, then his expiation is the same as expiation for breaking an oath, and whoever makes a vow that he can fulfill, he should fulfill it."
4322,Ibn Harmala narrates that a person asked Saeed bin Musaib a question. He said: I have vowed that I will walk to the House of Allah. So he replied: No! Taksaid said: Nothing is obligatory on you.
4323,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a man named Abu Israel who was standing in the sun. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What is the matter with him? I told him that he made a vow that he would not speak and would not come into the shade and would not sit and would fast. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell him to talk, come into the shade, sit down and fast."
4324,The same is true of the same (past) Hadith with a different Sunad.
4325,The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him).
4326,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by Abu Israel (after that, the narrator narrated the hadith according to the previous hadith)."
4327,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that once while the Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon, he saw a man who was standing in the sun. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired about him, and the people told him that he was Abu Israel. Let him come even in the shade, let him talk, but he should fast."
4328,"Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: There are four types of oaths, two types of oaths must be expiated and two types of oaths are not expiated. A person who takes this oath: By Allah! We will never do that, and then he has to do it. A person who says: By Allah! I will do that, then he does not do that. As for the two types of oaths in which expiation is not granted, they are if a man swears that I did not do that and although he did that, or a man swears that he did this but he did that (there will be no expiation for him)."
4329,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every exception that is incompatible with an oath, then the person who does this will be an oath breaker."
4330,"Sayyidna Amroob bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Sayyidna Abu Zarghafari (RA) came riding the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) on a camel. If you give me salvation while riding a camel, then I will definitely eat its liver and the flesh of its hump. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have given him a great reward."
4331,"Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that his freed maid intended to separate Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) and his wife. He said one day: If she does this, she will be a Jew. his He asked Sayyida Aisha, Sayyida Abdullah bin Umar, Sayyida Abdullah bin Abbas, Sayyida Hafsa and Sayyida Umm Salma about this, and they all said to him: Do you want to become like Harut and Marut? Then all of them instructed him to make expiation of his oath and leave the pursuit of both of them."
4332,"Narrated Abu Rafi': My freed slave girl said: I will make a separation between you and your wife. If I can do this, all her property will be in the name of the Kaaba and she will be a Jew, a Christian or a Magi on that day. If she cannot separate between you and your wife. Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I attended the service of Umm al-Mu'minin, Sayyida Umm Salama (may God be pleased with him), and I said: My freed slave girl wants to create a separation between me and my wife. Sayyida Umm Salama (may God be pleased with her) said: Go to your slave girl and tell her that it is not permissible for you to do this. He said, 'He came' until he came to the door and said: Here are Harut and Marut. This maid said: I have given all my property to the treasure of the Kaaba. He said: I said: I will be a Jew on that day or a Christian or a Magian on that day (if I did not separate between them) then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said: If you accept Judaism, you will be killed. He said: Make expiation for your oath and do not cause separation between this person and his wife."
4333,"Qasim narrates: A woman came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with her. She vowed that she would slaughter her son, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered her to make expiation, and one of the people present said: Subhan Allah! Atonement will be given for the disobedience of Allah Ta'ala. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: Yes! Allah Ta'ala has made Zahar and ordered expiation for it too (Tazahar is also a disobedience to Allah, but expiation is given for it)."
4334,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The type of expiation is to give one mudd of wheat to every poor person.
4335,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every poor person will be given a helping of wheat along with curry.
4336,Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) says about the type of expiation that one mud of wheat will be given to a poor person.
4337,"Ata narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu saying in a Masjid: One of three things will be given a “mad” in expiation for breaking an oath, in expiation for zahar and in ransom for feeding the poor."
4338,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Every poor person will be given a \muad\"" of wheat"," along with curry."""
4339,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When an old person is unable to keep fast, he will feed one meal for one day."
4340,"Amro bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When a woman claims to divorce her husband and she presents a just witness about it, her husband will be sworn in. If he swears, the testimony of that witness will be invalidated, and if he refuses to swear, then his refusal will be considered as the substitute of the other witness, and his divorce will be recognized."
4341,"Amir al-Shaabi narrates: Two Christian people living in \Daquqa\"" became witnesses to the will of a Muslim. This Muslim had left with the people about whom the will was made. They had doubts about it. We did not get any price in return for it and we did not hide any testimony in the name of Allah Ta'ala. If we do that"," we will be sinful. Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: This is a decision that has not been made before today after the departure of the Prophet (PBUH)."""
4342,"Adi bin Adi narrates the statement of his father: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case. The case was about a piece of land. One of them said: This is my land and the other said: It is mine. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about this that the person who has land will take an oath. When he was ready to take the oath, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If that person takes an oath to seize the property of a Muslim, when he appears in the court of Allah, Allah will be angry with him."
4343,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4344,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (PBUH) granted safety to all but four people. They were Abdul Uzza bin Khatl, Muqis bin Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad and Umm Sarah. As for Abdul Uzza, he was killed. He was hiding in the curtains of the Kaaba."
4345,"Musab bin Saeed narrates this statement of his father: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to all the people except four men and two women. He said: They (six persons) must be killed, even though you find them hidden in the curtains of the Kaaba: Ikrama bin Abu Jahl, Abdullah bin Khatl, Muqis bin Sababah, Abdullah bin Saad."
4346,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4347,"Umar ibn Uthman narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are four people whom I will not allow anywhere in the \Hal\"" and the \""Haram\""."""
4348,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Tamim Dari and Udi bin Bada used to go to Makkah for trade. At the same time, a man belonging to the Banusham tribe was going. He died in a place where no Muslim lived. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him to take an oath: And he said: \Swear by the name of Allah and say that you have not hidden anything from this and you have no knowledge of it.\"" After that", the bowl was found in Makkah," and the person from whom it was found said that I had bought it from Adi bin Bada and Tamim. The heirs obtained that cup and this verse was revealed about them:"""
4349,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Tamim Dari and Adi used to come to Makkah. Once a young man from the Banusham tribe was going with them. He died in a place where no Muslim was present. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore to them both in the name of Allah that we have not hidden anything and we are not aware of such a thing. Then later that vessel was found in Makkah, so these people said: We bought it from Adi and Tamim. The testimony should be more truthful than the other two (i.e. it is true) and if we do anything wrong, then we will be counted among the wrongdoers. Then these people obtained this vessel. This verse was revealed about these people:"
4350,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a Jewish man and a Jewish woman were brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Both of them had committed adultery. The Jews said: We used to do this when they were in our possession, but when our possession ended, it is no longer in our power. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to them: Bring to me two of your greatest scholars. They brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the two sons of Surya. It is said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I ask you both by the name of Allah, who revealed the Torah to Sayyiduna Musa, what punishment have you found for these two (criminals) in the Torah? So they both said: The person who is with a woman will be punished. The person who is seen on a woman's stomach will be punished. But when four men will testify that they saw this person insert his private parts inside the woman, the way the inner stitches of the head are inserted (then they will be stoned). The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Bring witnesses! Then the four men testified, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned them both."
4351,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has narrated this: Allah has forgiven my ummah for the sins committed through omission and compulsion.
4352,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: May Allah Ta'ala do it or do it deliberately (Tawa will not be punishable).
4353,Sayyidna Wasthla bin Asqa' and Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA) narrate that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The Yamin is not required on the person who is forced to do so.
4354,"Abu Zubayr states that he asked Sayyiduna Jabir, may God be pleased with him: What do you think that sanctity is proved once through reza'at? He replied: Yes!"
4355,"Mujahideen narrates that Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with them) say: Rizaat, whether it is small or large, proves sanctity."
4356,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the next hadith), while Sayyida Aisha also narrated this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) The words of one of them are: \Sucking once or twice does not prove haram\""."""
4357,"Sayyida Aisha has also narrated this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The words of one of them are: \Sucking once or twice does not prove haram\""."""
4358,"Abu Musa Hilali narrates the statement of his father that once a man was traveling, his wife gave birth to a child, but the woman's milk did not flow, so the man was afraid of the woman, so he began to suck the woman's breast, due to which the milk reached his throat. It has become haram for you. Then he came to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him. He asked him about this, and he told him that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is the feeding that proves haram that produces meat and causes bones to grow (i.e., that which is at a young age)."
4359,Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Drinking Yadu Martaba (one sip) once does not prove Haram.
4360,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Sucking once or twice does not prove sanctity. Ibrahim narrates that I mentioned this tradition to Saeed bin Musayb, and he said: When even a drop of milk reaches the stomach of a child while it is still small, then it becomes haraam for it. While the narrator named Uthman has quoted these words that sanctity is proved only by the one who irrigates the bowels with milk, he did not quote any other words."
4361,"The sons of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrate: Once a man was traveling with his wife. This woman gave birth to a child and the child could not suck milk. The husband of that woman began to suck her milk until he felt the taste of the milk in his throat. The person came to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radi Allahu Anhu, then Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Masud Radi Allahu Anhu came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash’ari Radi Allahu Anhu and said: He has given this fatwa, while the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this: Breastfeeding is what strengthens the bone and produces the flesh."
4362,"Abu Atiyyah narrates: A man came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) and said: My wife had a swelling in her breast. I sucked it and a little milk went down my throat, so Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) scolded him severely. He replied: Yes! Narrated by Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) and he scolded me severely about this. So Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) and said: Is this person a milk drinker? Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) said: As long as there are such great scholars among you, you people do not ask me any problem: Do it."
4363,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: After two years have passed, adoption is not valid."
4364,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only the breastfeeding that takes place within two years is valid."
4365,"Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the case of a minor, breastfeeding is only done within two years."
4366,"Sayyidah Umm Fazl (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about sucking a sip, does it prove sanctity? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! Abu Hamdanami the narrator has quoted these words; A person from Banu Umar said: O Allah?? The prophet! Does sucking once prove haram? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!"
4367,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sucking once or twice does not prove sanctity; sanctity is proven by one who irrigates the bowels.
4368,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A woman came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and she said: \So-and-so has married.\"" While I have breast-fed both of them"," the Prophet (PBUH) asked: \""Did you breast-feed them?\"" So the woman replied: I breastfed this girl when she was six and a half years old and I breastfed the child when he was three years old. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and tell her to live happily with her wife"," because breastfeeding after the age of breastfeeding does not prove the order of breastfeeding."""
4369,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Harith narrates: I married a woman. A black woman came to us and said: I have breastfed you both. (The narrator says:) I attended the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: I have married the daughter of so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from me. I came in front of him from the other side and I said: She is lying. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What can happen now? While he has stated that he has nursed both of you, you separate this woman (i.e. your wife) from you."
4370,"Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I had married the daughter of Abu Ahab and a black woman came and said: I have breastfed you both (husband and wife). When asked for the third time, he said: What can happen now? While this has been stated, the narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped this gentleman from establishing a relationship with this woman."
4371,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, which contains these words: I married the daughter of Abu Ahab."
4372,Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A black woman came and she stated that I had breastfed them both (husband and wife). Sayyidna Uqbah's wife was the daughter of Abu Ahab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from her.
4373,"Sayyidna Uqbah bin Harith (RA) narrates that I married a woman, a black woman came to her, she asked me something, but I delayed in giving it to her, so she said: You confirm this to me. By Allah! I have breast-fed both of you husband and wife. The narrator says: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I mentioned this to him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Separate your wife from yourself. There is no good in her for you."
4374,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: My uncle Aflah bin Abul Qais asked permission to enter my house after the decree of hijab was revealed, so I did not give him permission. I was breastfed by a woman, I was not breastfed by a man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should have given him permission because he is your uncle."
4375,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) narrates that Abul Qays's brother Aflah came and asked for permission to enter. He was the foster brother of Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her). This was after the revelation of the Hijab. (to come in) allowed.
4376,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: First, this verse was revealed in which stoning was ordered, and the verse was revealed in which it was ordered that feeding an older child ten times proves breastfeeding."
4377,"Amro bin Dinar narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about any issue of nursing, and he said: According to my knowledge, Allah Almighty has declared the foster sister to be haram. Abdallah bin Zubair was very happy with his decision."
4378,"Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) was asked about a person who has a wife and a concubine, 'one of them gives birth to a child and the other gives birth to a girl', so would it be permissible for the child to marry the girl of that concubine? So he replied: No! Because sperm is one."
4379,"Sayyida Zainab bint Abu Salama (RA) narrates: Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) breastfed me, so (Syida Asma’s husband) Sayyida Zubair (RA) used to come to me even when I was combing her hair. I have brothers. After that, shortly before the incident of Jarrah, Abdullah bin Zubair (who was my foster brother) asked for my daughter's relationship for his son Hamza, Hamza and Musab, both of whom were the sons of such and such a woman. I am your brother and the children of Sayyida Asmaa (RA) are your brothers. But the children of Sayyidna Zubair who are from children other than Sayyida Asmaa (RA) are not your brothers and sisters. Does not prove."
4380,Sayyida Umm Fazl (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that drinking one or two sips does not prove Haram.
4381,"Sayyida Umm Fazl (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present in my house. I have a wife, and I married another woman after that, so my first wife said, 'She has breastfed my wife', who had breastfed her once, maybe twice, and had given her a yadug lip (the narrator has doubts about this), then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Filling one yadug lip (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these words are: drinking a yadug twice) does not prove haram."
4382,Sayyidah Umm Fazl (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Drinking a single lip balm does not prove haram. A narrator named Qatadah has quoted these words: By sucking once or twice (it does not prove sanctity).
4383,Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sucking twice does not prove haram.
4384,"Sayyida Aisha (RA) says: In the Qur'an, the command to suck ten specified times was first revealed. Sayyida Aisha (RA) meant that the breast-feeding which proves its sanctity must be sucked ten times. After that, the command of five specified times was revealed."
4385,Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates: I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who accepts Islam at the hands of another person. The Prophet (PBUH) said: That person will be considered closer to him in life and death than all other people.
4386,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever accepts Islam on someone else's hand, then that other person will be the owner of the previous one's wealth."
4387,"Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates that I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about a person who accepts Islam at the hands of another person, and he said: He will be closer to him in life and death than all other people."
4388,Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He asked a person (after that the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith).
4389,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a fallen object, and he said: It is not permissible to use a fallen object. Whoever picks it up will announce it for a year. If its owner comes, he will return it. Will decide about."
4390,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: Allah Almighty has completed four things: creation, habit and behavior, sustenance and life."
4391,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A camel named Uzba was owned by a person from Banu Uqeel. This person was taken prisoner. Along with this person, his camel Uzba was also taken prisoner. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him. You people have arrested me on the basis of the case and for what reason have you arrested Azba while I am a Muslim? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you are saying this, then you are the master of your own affairs (i.e. free) and you will be fully prosperous. Then the man was released in exchange for the ransom of two men. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put the camel of ``Uzba to ride because she used to travel fast. Once some polytheists robbed a part of Medina at night and captured a Muslim woman. She made a sound. She came to Uzba, but she did not make a sound. It was a camel carrying a great command. That woman rode that camel and came to Madinah. She made a vow that if Allah grants her salvation, she will sacrifice this camel. Peace be upon him is a camel. The narrator narrates: Then this woman was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was told about her vow, so he said: You have repaid a lot."
4392,"Ata states: The sanctity of breast-feeding is the same as the sanctity of breast-feeding. Once, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, found out that Abdullah bin Zubair narrates with reference to Sayyida Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that he said this about breastfeeding: Sucking milk less than seven times does not prove haram, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah's command, Sayyida Aisha. Better than the saying of the Prophet (may Allah be pleased with him) is what Allah has said: \And your foster sisters.\"" Allah Ta'ala did not say that the reza'at of one time or two times."""
4393,Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Haram is not proven by breastfeeding less than five times.
4394,"Amro bin Dinar narrates: A person asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: Does it prove sanctity through breastfeeding once or twice? So he said: I understand that a foster sister is forbidden. Then a person said: Amir al-Mu'minin has stated this (this person meant Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him) that it is not forbidden by fostering one time."
4395,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4396,"Sayyidna Abu Taalba al-Khushai (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Allah has prescribed some duties, ‘You shall not waste them’, He has made certain things forbidden, you shall not commit them, and He has set certain limits, ‘You shall not transgress them,’ He has not mentioned anything about certain things without forgetting them, so you should not try to do them.”"
4397,Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave any gold or silver (after Wasal) except a piece of land which he declared as charity and a white mule.
4398,"Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left only his weapons, his white mule and a piece of land in Turkey, which he declared as charity."
4399,"Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) did not leave any dinar or dirham or any slave or any female slave (in Turkey), only his white mule on which he used to ride, his weapons and a piece of land which he gave (as charity) in the name of Allah. A narrator named Qutiba once quoted these words: You called it charity."
4400,Sayyiduna Amro bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) who was the brother of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the brother of his wife Ms.
4401,"Sayyidna Amroob bin Harith (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) passed away, he left only his white mule, his weapons and a piece of land in Turkey, which he declared as charity."
4402,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the first charity given in Islam was done by Sayyidna Umar (RA). Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! You advise me what should I do about it? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Keep this land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah.
4403,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found a piece of land in Khyber. I have never found a more desirable piece of land. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to him, \If you wish"," give it (the fruit) in charity and keep the original land.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave it (the fruit) as a charity for his close relatives", the poor and travelers, and there is no sin on the person who oversees it, if he himself is from it. Eats or gives food to one of his friends," provided that he is a hoarder."""
4404,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Sayyidna Umar (RA) found a land in Khyber called Samagh. He inquired about it from the Prophet (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \Keep this land with you and donate its fruits in charity.\"""""
4405,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) for permission to donate his land in Shamgh, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Give it as a charity in such a way that you distribute its fruits and keep the land with you"," which cannot be sold or inherited.\"""""
4406,Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): Sayyidna Umar (RA) consulted the Holy Prophet (SAW) about giving his land in Samg in Sadaqah. There are these words in a hadith: You should give it in charity in such a way that its fruits are divided and the original land remains with you so that it cannot be sold or inherited.
4407,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked the Prophet (SAW) for permission to give the land in Shamgh as charity, and the Prophet (SAW) said: Leave the land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
4408,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Umar (RA) that I inquired from the Holy Prophet (PBUH) about my land in Shamgh, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, “Leave the land with you and donate its fruits in charity.”"
4409,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar narrates that he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have made a vow that I will give my property in charity, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the land with you and give its fruits in charity."
4410,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) found a piece of land in Khyber. He came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said, \I have found such a land that no better land has been found before"," so what do you order me about it?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish"," let that land remain with you and give its fruits in charity. He properly eats from it 'or gives it to a friend' but the condition is that he is not a hoarder."""
4411,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) found land in Khyber. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He said: O Messenger of Allah! I have not found any wealth that is better for me, so what do you guide me? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \If you wish to dedicate the land in the name of Allah", the original land will remain with you and you give charity from its fruits. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave it as charity to the poor, close relatives, slaves, travelers and guests," and there is no sin on its caretaker if he eats from it properly or feeds it to a friend\"" while he is not a hoarder. The narrators have disagreed about one word of this tradition."""
4412,"This same hadith is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: So Sayyiduna Umar gave him charity in such a way that the original land cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, it cannot be divided into inheritance. The narrator then quotes these words at the end: \Let that person be the possessor of wealth.\"""""
4413,"Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) found a piece of land in Khyber. I have found land in Khyber, I have never found a better land than this. What do you order me about it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, let the earth remain with you and give its fruits in charity. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him charity in such a way that the original land could not be sold, given away, or inherited, and its fruit was a charity for the poor, close relatives, slaves, Mujahideen, travelers and guests, and the person who was in charge of it would have no sin if he himself ate from it properly or fed it to one of his friends while he was collecting wealth."
4414,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) narrated that I found a piece of land in Khyber, so I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found the best land. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want, give it as charity and let the original land remain with you. There would be no sin if he ate some of it himself or fed it to a friend while he was a hoarder. Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu made this will to Sayyida Hafsa Radiyallahu Anhu and then to the older people belonging to the descendants of Sayyidna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu. These words of the hadith are from the narrator Abu Mas'udani, but other narrators have some differences in quoting it."
4415,"This tradition is narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: the original land cannot be sold, it will not be divided by inheritance."
4416,"The same hadith is also narrated along with another document, however, it contains these words: So they let the original land remain with them in such a way that it should not be sold, not bequeathed, not be inherited, and its fruits should be given as charity to the poor, close relatives, slaves, the needy, travelers and guests."
4417,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the Prophet (PBUH) and said: I have found land in Khyber. In my opinion, I have never found a better land than this. What do you order me about this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want to continue, let the land remain with you and give its fruits in charity. There is no sin on him if he properly eats some of it himself or feeds it to a friend while he is a hoarder."
4418,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (R.A.) said that I found land in Khyber. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found a land that I like more than this and there is no land that is more refined than that. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar gave this land as charity in such a way that it cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, its fruits will be for the poor, close relatives, slaves, guests, travelers, and there will be no sin on the person who takes care of it."
4419,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA): I found a piece of land in Khyber which was the best for me. I have found land in Khyber, which has been the most abundant for me. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you want to keep the land with you and donate its fruits in charity, then Sayyiduna Umar gave it as charity in such a way that it could not be sold, it could not be given away, it would not be inherited. And he who is in charge of it will not be guilty of any sin if he properly eats some of it or properly gives it to a friend while he is a hoarder. Here the narrators have disagreed about one word of the tradition."
4420,"On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, a similar narration has been narrated from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
4421,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when this verse was revealed: \You people cannot attain goodness until you spend what you like.\"" So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have a garden in such and such a place. It is a charity for Allah Ta'ala. If I could have given it in secret"," I would not have announced it."""
4422,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) named him Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka’b and Sayyidna Hasan Bin Thabit (RA), because these two gentlemen were closer to Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) than I was."
4423,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
4424,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when this verse was revealed: \You cannot attain goodness until you spend on what you like.\"" So Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Our Lord has asked us for our wealth. I am making you my witness that I dedicate my land in Birha to the name of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it to your close relatives. So Sayyiduna Abu Talha (RA) divided that land between Sayyidna Hasan Bin Thabit and Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA)."""
4425,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! According to me, the best wealth is the land whose yield is one hundred wasaqs, which you gave me in Khaybar. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Keep the original land with you and give its fruits in charity. The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (RA) wrote this text: This is from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab\ which is about the land of \""Shamgh\"" and about the one hundred wasaqs that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me which are in Khaybar. I will keep the original of it and give its fruit in charity. \""What will be given to the close relatives", orphans, poor travelers and the overseer," then the overseer himself can eat from it and can also feed one of his friends.\"" But there will be no sin", but this land cannot be sold, cannot be given away, cannot be divided into inheritance, as long as heaven and earth are established. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) gave this will to his daughter Sayyida Hafsa (RA), then if she passed away," this will would be transferred to another person of opinion from the family of Sayyidna Hafsa (RA)."""
4426,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab (RA) intended to donate his land which was in Shamgh. This was mentioned to the Prophet (PBUH) and he said: \Keep the original land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah.\"""""
4427,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found a land which is excellent. I want to give it as charity. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should give it as charity in such a way that the original land cannot be sold, not bequeathed, not shared as an inheritance, and its fruits are spent (in the way of Allah). The narrator says: So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave him charity in the same way, and he wrote in the writing of his charity that it can be given in the way of Allah (i.e. to the Mujahideen) to guests, to travelers, to the poor and to the close relatives of the person who will be the caretaker of this land."
4428,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) said to the Prophet (SAW): I received a hundred shares in Khyber.
4429,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) He became the owner of a hundred shares in Khyber, he also acquired some more land by purchase, then he came to the service of the Prophet (SAW) and said: I have found such a land that has never been found before. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep the original and give its fruits in the way of Allah."
4430,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said in the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) 'After that, it is according to the previous hadith."
4431,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) attended the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have found such a land that I have never found such a land. (The narrator says:) Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, received one hundred shares. He says: I bought one hundred shares from its owners in Khyber through it (i.e. I bought this much land). I want to get close to Allah through it."
4432,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that I asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the land in Shamgh.
4433,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! I have got land in Shamgh. I dislike that it should be sold after me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep it and give its fruits in the way of Allah.
4434,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) found land in Khyber. He came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW). He said: I have found land in Khaybar. I have never found any land that is better than this land. The narrator narrates: So Sayyiduna Umar kept the original land and gave its produce as charity, in such a way that this land cannot be sold, it cannot be given away, it cannot be inherited, its produce will be distributed among the poor, close relatives, guests, Mujahideen and travelers. be"
4435,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Umar (RA) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and received one hundred plots of land in Khyber. He bought land and gathered them together. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the original land with you and give its fruits in the way of Allah.
4436,"The judge al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Jarīr narrated to us, Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr ibn Abī al-Jahm narrated to us, al-Sarī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us. And it was read to Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Shawārib, in my presence, and I heard it being said to him: \Did you hear ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd?\"" He said: \""I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs say: 'I heard Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrate from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān.'\"" And Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿdān narrated to us", Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated, from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān al-Saʿdī. And ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to me, Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated, from Ḥuṣayn," who narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn Jāwān al-Māzinī said: \""I heard al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays.\"" And Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Aṣbahānī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us", Abū Masʿūd narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Abū ʿAwwānah narrated, Ḥuṣayn informed me, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Abū ʿAwwānah narrated to us, Ḥuṣayn narrated, from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān. And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated, from al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān," who said: \""I heard my father narrate from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān", from ʿAmr ibn Jāwān," a man from Banī Tamīm. That was because I said to him: 'What do you think about the withdrawal (iʿtizāl) of al-Aḥnaf—what was it?' He said: 'I heard al-Aḥnaf say—while I was performing Ḥajj—we were at our encampment unloading our saddles when a messenger came to us and said: \""The people have gathered in the mosque.\"" I went and found the people assembling", and among them were a group of men seated. There was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, al-Zubayr, Ṭalḥah, and Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. When I stood over them," it was announced: \""ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān has come to al-Madīnah.\"" He came wearing a yellow cloak. I said to my companion: \""Stay as you are until I see what he has brought.\"" ʿUthmān said: \""Is ʿAlī here? Is al-Zubayr here? Is Ṭalḥah here? Is Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ here?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah", besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Whoever purchases the mirbad of Banī So-and-so, Allah will forgive him'? So I purchased it, and I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'I have purchased the mirbad of Banī So-and-so.' He said: 'Make it part of our mosque," and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah", besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Whoever purchases the well of Rūmah, Allah will forgive him'? So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'I have purchased the well of Rūmah.' He said: 'Make it a watering place for the Muslims," and its reward is for you.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I adjure you by Allah", besides whom there is no deity—do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Whoever equips the Army of Hardship (jaysh al-ʿUsrah)," Allah will forgive him'? So I equipped them to the point that they lacked neither a hobble nor a bridle.'\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: 'O Allah", bear witness! O Allah, bear witness! O Allah," bear witness!'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Muʿtamir", from his father," from Ḥuṣayn. Ibn Idrīs said in his narration: \""Whoever purchases the mirbad of Banī So-and-so", Allah will forgive him,"\"" so I purchased it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand. He also said regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for such-and-such","\"" then I came to him. He said: \""Make it a watering place for the Muslims"," and its reward is for you.\"" ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim said in his narration regarding the story of the mirbad: \""I purchased it for such-and-such", then I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: 'I have purchased the mirbad of Banī So-and-so to expand the mosque of the Muslims.' He said: 'Yes," and its reward is incumbent upon you.'\"" He said regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand\""—the doubt being from Ḥuṣayn. Abū Dāwūd said", from Abū ʿAwwānah," regarding the story of the mirbad: \""I purchased it for twenty-odd thousand or thereabouts.\"" The remainder of their wordings are close in meaning"," and the import is the same. In the ḥadīth of Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal regarding the well of Rūmah: \""I purchased it for such-and-such.\"""""
4437,"Samama bin Hazan Qashiri narrated that I was at the house of Sayyidna Uthman RA at that time, when Sayyidna Uthman RA looked at the people and said: I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah, do you know that when the Prophet SAW came to Madinah, at that time there was only a well of fresh water, then the Prophet SAW said: Who By purchasing Bayrumah, he will devote it to the Muslims. In return, he will get Paradise. So I bought it from my property and gave all Muslims equal rights to it, and today you people are preventing me from drinking water from that well, and I have to drink sea water. These people replied: Allah knows that it is so. I am asking if you people know that I provided equipment for the Tabuk campaign from my personal wealth. The people replied: Allah knows that it is so. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani said: I ask you by Allah and Islam that you know that the mosque had become small. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy the land of such and such people for the expansion of the mosque? \He will get Paradise in return"," so I bought him out of my wealth and made an addition to the mosque through him.\"" Today"," you people are preventing me from praying two rak'ahs in the same mosque. They said: \""Allah knows that it is so.\"" Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you people by the name of Allah Almighty and Islam", do you know that the Prophet (PBUH) was on Mount Sabir in Makkah, along with him were Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar and I too. There is a Prophet, a Siddique and two martyrs. The people said: Allah knows that it is like this. Then Sayyiduna Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, and said: You people, be witnesses about me! By the Lord Kaaba! I am a martyr," he said this three times. Here the words of tradition are similar to each other."""
4438,"This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: I ask you people by the name of Allah, do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married his second daughter to me after the death of one of his daughters? He was pleased with me and was happy with me."
4439,"Tamma bin Hazun Qashiri narrates that I was at the house of Sayyidna Uthman (RA) when Sayyidna Uthman (RA) was martyred. Sayyidna 'Uthman (RA) peeked through the wall of this house and said: Bring your two companions before me, who are the root of the mischief. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, the mosque was too crowded for worshipers, so he said: Who will dedicate this land from his wealth to the Muslims? He will find a better place in Paradise than this. So I bought it from my wealth and dedicated it to the Muslims. The people said: Allah knows that it is so. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: Now you people are preventing me from offering two rakat prayers from this mosque. I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah. That's how it is."
4440,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: Where are the two people who incited you against me? Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you people by the name of Allah, do you know that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, there was no sweet well there, there was only Birrumah? So he will be more beautiful than him in heaven, so I bought him from my wealth and today you people are preventing me from drinking water from that well."
4441,"A narrator named Musa bin Hakim narrates that Ibn Amir wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and by that time these people had surrounded him. They kept looking and I extended the letter towards them. They read it and then they turned towards the mosque and saw Sayyiduna Talha (RA) sitting in the eastern direction of the mosque. They called out: O Talha! Sayyiduna Talha replied: I am present! Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: I swear to you in the name of Allah, do you know that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Who will buy this piece of land and expand the mosque through it? He said: You people are in a state of peace in this mosque and I am in a state of fear. Then Syedna Uthman Ghani said: O Talha! He said: I am present! Then Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: I swear to you in the name of Allah, do you know that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will buy the well of Rumah and dedicate it to the Muslims? He will get this something in exchange for it. So I bought it from my wealth. He said: 'Allah knows that it is so.' Talha! He said: I am present! So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask you by the name of Allah, do you know that I provided one hundred camels for the Tabuk campaign? Sayyidna Talha (RA) replied: Allah knows that it is so. After that, Sayyidna Talha (RA) said: O Allah! According to my knowledge, Syedna Uthman (RA) is oppressed."
4442,"Sayyidna Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates that when Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) was surrounded in his house, he looked at the people and swore to them. He said: Do you people know that I was with the Prophet (PBUH) on Mount Hara? The narrator says that the people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: Do you people know that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will add a house to the mosque? So I bought a house and expanded the mosque through it, so the people confirmed his statement. Do you know that the water of Ruma well was sold only to travelers? I bought this well and dedicated it in the name of Allah. People replied: Yes! The people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: I ask you people by swearing in the name of Allah! Do you people know that I had provided equipment for the battle of Tabuk and I had spent so much money on it, so the people also confirmed this? Then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have lived among you for so long, but you have shown haste about me that I should take off the khilaat that Allah has made me wear, by Allah! It will never happen."
4443,"Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman narrates that Sayyiduna Uthman looked out from his house and saw that it was besieged at that time and said: By the name of Allah, I ask you people, who was there at that time? When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Mount Hara and the mountain began to move, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with his foot and said: O Hara! Be still. Above you is a Prophet, a Siddique and a martyr. I was also with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that time, so some people testified to this (that this is true). Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, said: The person who was with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time when he took the pledge of allegiance, I ask him in the name of Allah that when the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to the polytheists. So he said that this is my hand and this is Uthman's hand. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the oath of allegiance on my behalf. Some people also confirmed this to him. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I ask this person through Allah, who was present at the time when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Who will buy this house and add it to the mosque? So I bought this house from my wealth and expanded this mosque through it. Some people confirmed this to him. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani said: I ask this person in the name of Allah who was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time when he was preparing for the Tabuk campaign. So I provided half of the army with equipment from my own wealth.' Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, said: I ask this person in the name of Allah, who was present when the water of Rumah was sold only to travelers, so I bought it from my property and dedicated it to travelers (and to all Muslims). Some people also confirmed this."
4444,This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads.
4445,"This tradition is also narrated along with some other isnads. However, it contains these words: When Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani was surrounded in his house, some people gathered around his house. Sayyidna Uthman looked at him."
4446,"Abu Abdul Rahman Salmi narrates that when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) was besieged, he looked at the people from the roof of his house and said: I am reminding you people of Allah. Do you not know that when the Hara began to move, the Prophet (PBUH) said: O Hara! Stay in your place! There is a Prophet, a Siddiq and a Martyr above you. People replied: Yes! So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) said: I am reminding you of Allah. Do you know that when the Prophet (PBUH) started providing supplies for the Tabuk campaign, he said: Who will spend such a thing that will be accepted? So the people were in need at that time. I ask if you people do not know that the water from the Ruma well could be drunk only for a price, so I dedicated it to every wealthy, poor and traveler by purchasing it, so these people replied: Yes! After that Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) counted some other things as well."
4447,"Abu Abd al-Rahman Salmi narrates that when Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) was besieged, he looked at the people and said: I am asking you in the name of Allah, and I am only asking the companions of the Prophet (PBUH) that do you not know that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever digs a well in Rumah (i.e. dedicates it) ga) He will get Jannah, so I dug it. Do you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever provides supplies for the battle of Tabuk, he will receive Paradise. will"
4448,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: Allah Almighty has finished with four things: the creation of man, his morals, his sustenance and his death. It is no longer possible for a person to acquire anything."
4449,"Basheer bin Muhammad narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gave his garden as charity. That is what we used to live on. We have no wealth other than this. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Sayyiduna Abdullah and said: Allah has accepted your charity and returned it to your parents."
4450,"Basheer bin Muhammad narrates that his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA) gave his wealth in charity. He had no wealth other than this, so the Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Abdullah (RA): Allah has accepted your charity from you. In quoting the words here, the narrator has quoted some different words (and the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said:) and returned it to your parents."
4451,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd (RA) gave his wealth in charity and the parents of Tawan attended the service of the Prophet (PBUH) after that, the narrator has mentioned it according to the previous hadith."
4452,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of Allah! This garden of mine is a charity. It is in the name of Allah and His Messenger. So his parents came to the service of the Holy Prophet. They said: O Messenger of Allah! We passed away in this garden, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that garden to both of them. This hadith is \transmitted\"". The reason for this is that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd (RA) died during the reign of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA)."""
4453,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: This is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, may God be pleased with him, who was shown the way to call the call to prayer in a dream, and then he attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
4454,"Amro bin Salim narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd, who was taught how to call the call to prayer in a dream, gave a garden of his in charity. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned that garden to his parents, then when these parents died, the heirs of Tawan got it."
4455,Amro bin Salim narrates that Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zaid (RA) gave his garden as charity. He came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). He said: I dedicate this garden of mine to the Prophet (PBUH).
4456,"Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man named Abdullah bin So-and-so (the narrator named Shaaban has been forgotten here) came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! My everything is in charity except my horse and my weapons. The narrator narrates: He also had some land. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took possession of it and assigned it as afaz (i.e. as a financial aid to various people). We don't have anything other than this. We people go round and round about things. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took this garden and handed it over to them both. What I gave in charity and what you returned to my parents, then both of them passed away: O Messenger of Allah! What I gave in charity and what you gave back to my parents, now that they have both passed away, is this halal for me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! You eat with pleasure."
4457,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas (may God be pleased with him): You decide between them. He said: O Messenger of Allah! In your presence? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! He said: How should I decide? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you do ijtihad and make a correct decision, you will get ten rewards, and if you make a mistake after doing ijtihad, you will get one reward."
4458,"This is narrated along with the hadith and the chain of transmission, but in it the word \goodness\"" has been used instead of reward."""
4459,"Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their case, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O Uqbah! Get up and decide between them. I said: O Messenger of Allah! You are more entitled to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you used ijtihad while deciding between them and made a correct decision, you will get ten rewards, and if you made a mistake while making ijtihad, you will get one reward."
4460,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that when a person performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision, he receives ten rewards, and when a person performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a mistake, he receives rewards."
4461,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever wants to be a judge is slaughtered without a knife.\"""""
4462,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The person who is made a Qazi is as if he had been slaughtered without a knife.
4463,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The person who was made a judge was slaughtered without a knife.
4464,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person who makes a decision performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision, he gets rewards, and when he makes a wrong decision while making ijtihad, he gets a reward. \When a Qazi performs ijtihad while making a decision and makes a correct decision", he gets rewards and when he makes a mistake while making a decision," he gets a reward.\"""""
4465,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Whoever is a ruler who makes decisions between people, when he is resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, an angel will take him with a mace and take him to the edge of Hellfire and make him stumble. The distance will be forty years. A narrator named Masrooq narrates: If I make righteous decisions for one day, that is more preferable to me than fighting for a hundred years in the cause of Allah."
4466,"Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever is tempted to judge between people, he should act justly between people in his behavior, in his gestures, in the way he sits (act justly in all respects)."
4467,"Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who is tempted to decide between people should not raise his voice in front of any of the two sides of the case, until he raises his voice in front of the other side as well (i.e. treat both equally)."
4468,Sayyidah Umm Salamah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever is tempted to decide between Muslims," should not decide between two parties in anger.\"""""
4469,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Bakra that he wrote in a letter to his son who was a judge in Sajistan: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No judge should judge between two men in a state of anger and should not give two judgments in one case.
4470,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A person who makes a decision should make a decision when he is full and has eaten (that is, he should not make a decision in a state of restlessness and indecisiveness or mental disorder)."
4471,"Abul Malih al-Hazli narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) wrote a letter to Sayyidna Musa Ash'ari (RA) in which it was written: (Amaafad!) Qada is a duty that is very important and a method that should be maintained. When the evidence comes before you, if the right is clear, then you enforce it, and it is of no use to speak about a right that cannot be enforced. You sit on an equal level with people. It will be obligatory on him who denies it. It is permissible to make peace between Muslims, except for such a peace that makes the forbidden thing lawful and the lawful thing declared forbidden. It is ``to act with understanding'' to act with understanding' about the thing that you are confused about in your mind' and no ruling from the Book or the Sunnah has reached you about it', so in such a case, put other cases like it in front of you and hypothesize the rulings and give preference to that which is more pleasing to Allah Almighty and is more similar to the truth, according to your opinion. The person who has claimed, if he asks for time to present the evidence, give him time to present the evidence, and if the evidence is presented, give a decision according to his right, if not, then give a decision against that person. This is because this situation has become clear even for a blind person and is more eloquent in terms of excuses. Every Muslim is just. They are related to each other. It is that he bears false witness, or whoever is thought to be (giving false witness) because of his lineage because of his guardianship, then take care of him. This is because Allah is the guardian of the inner things, but the punishment will be removed from you on the basis of evidence. Allah will make the reward obligatory. This thing will become a treasure for you in the hereafter. This is because the person whose intention is right in the matter between Allah and the servant, even if that thing is against the person himself, Allah will protect that person from harm in relation to the people, and whoever is adorned with regard to the people, but Allah's knowledge about it will be different, then Allah will disgrace that person. So you want to get wages from someone else instead of Allah Ta'ala? While Allah Ta'ala also gives immediate sustenance and also gives the treasures of His mercy and peace be upon you."
4472,"It is narrated about Saeed bin Abu Barda that once he took out a letter of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and said: This is the letter of Sayyidna Umar (RA) then a narrator named Sufyan read this letter in front of me in which it was written: But later! Justice is a duty that is necessary and a method that should be maintained. You should understand that when a case comes before you, it does not help you to talk about the right. It is necessary to present evidence and the person who refuses will take an oath. It is permissible to make peace between Muslims, except for a peace that makes a forbidden thing lawful or a lawful thing forbidden. Nothing can invalidate and return to the truth. It is better than a person to continue on falsehood which causes confusion in your mind. To try to understand it in relation to that which has not reached you in terms of the Qur'an and the Sunnah. I came, you give time to the person claiming to present his evidence during this time, if he did, then it is fine, otherwise, to decide against him, because now this situation will become more common for the blind person and will be more eloquent regarding the excuse. All Muslims are just. They are related to each other. Allah Ta’ala is the guardian of the inner things, but based on evidence, you will be removed from Samzak and yes, avoiding disturbing people, persecuting them, and avoiding opposition about the truth from such a place. As a result, Allah Ta’ala will make the reward obligatory. This thing will become a treasure for you in the Hereafter. This is because between Allah Ta’ala and a servant whose intention is right, even if that thing is against him, Allah Ta’ala. He will protect him from harm in relation to people, and whoever has good knowledge about people, but his knowledge about Allah will be different. Allah will disgrace that person. So you should get rewards from someone else instead of Allah. This does not happen in the presence of Allah, Allah disgraces this person."
4473,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that there will come to you traditions that are different from each other, so whoever comes to him with traditions that are in agreement with the Book of Allah, they will be from me."
4474,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If you are told a hadith about me that you understand, and you do not deny it, then you remain silent and confirm it."
4475,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words added: The reason for this is that I will say that which is known and which is not \denied\"" and I will not say that which is \""denied\"" and is not known."""
4476,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: After me, there will be some people who will narrate traditions about me, so you should present those traditions on the Qur'an and accept those that are in accordance with the Qur'an, and do not accept those that are not in accordance with the Qur'an. (Imam Dar al-Qati says:) The tradition is illusory. The correct one is that it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a “Mursal” tradition with reference to Asim, with reference to Imam Zayd, with reference to Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him."
4477,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a case regarding a camel, and one of them said: This camel has given birth to a child with me."
4478,"Abu Qais, who is the slave of Sayyiduna Amro bin Al-Aas, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has decreed that when a judge performs ijtihaad while giving a decision and makes a mistake about it, he will receive a reward."
4479,Another hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him).
4480,"Sayyiduna Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a judge performs ijtihad while giving a decision and gives a wrong decision, he will be rewarded for it, and if he gives a correct decision while giving a decision, he will be punished."
4481,
4482,"Al-Qamah Bin Wail narrates this on the authority of his father: A man from Hadramout and a man from Qandah came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Hadrami said: O Messenger of God! This person has taken possession of my land. That land belonged to my father. This person said: That land is mine and I have it. I cultivate it. This person has no right in this land. So he said no! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Then this other party will take an oath. This Hazrami inquired: O Messenger of Allah! It wouldn't care what oath it was taking? Because he does not avoid committing sins. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the situation for you. Then this person took an oath. When he left, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he has taken an oath on another person's property for the purpose of consuming it as an act of injustice, then when he appears in the court of Allah, Allah will turn away from him."
4483,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that two men claimed ownership of an animal, neither of them had any evidence, so the Prophet (PBUH) ordered them both to take an oath and take part in it."
4484,"The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it has these words added: \They both agree or do it in a state of compulsion.\"""""
4485,Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) gave a decision in favor of a person through a witness and taking an oath.
4486,"Imam Jafar bin Sadiq (RA) narrates on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath from a person who sought the truth and had a witness with him."
4487,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a decision through the testimony of a person and the swearing of a rightful person. The narrator says that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) also gave such a decision in Iraq.
4488,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said this: Regarding the truth, Allah and His Messenger have ruled in favor of two witnesses: \Whoever brings two witnesses will receive his right.\"""""
4489,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a verdict by taking an oath with a witness.
4490,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) returned the oath of a person who sought the truth.
4491,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The person against whom a claim has been made will be more entitled to take an oath, but if that person refuses to take an oath, then the person making the claim will take an oath and receive this right."
4492,"Sayyidna Hasan Basri narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A person who is called to the court of a Muslim (judge) and does not go there, then that person will be a tyrant, he will have no right."
4493,Rabi'ah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding the son of Sayyidna Sa'd bin Ubada: We have found this in the writings of Sa'd bin Ubada: \The Holy Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him," gave a decision by taking an oath with a witness.\"""""
4494,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave a verdict by taking an oath with a witness. Some narrators have disagreed in narrating it.
4495,"Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH), Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Sayyidna Umar), Sayyidna Uthman (RA) used to take an oath from the claimant and give judgments."
4496,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Aamir (RA) narrates that I agreed to see Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA), Sayyidna Umar (RA) and Sayyidna Uthman (RA)."
4497,Adi al-Kindi narrates that two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a case. One of them said: This land is mine. It is my property.
4498,"Amro bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates from his grandfather that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: He who takes up the profession of wisdom and does not know about it, if any person is harmed as a result of his treatment, he will pay a ransom."
4499,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The person who adopts wisdom even though he is not known for wisdom, and as a result of it someone dies or suffers less damage, then that person will pay the ransom."
4500,Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who becomes a doctor and is not well-known in this profession will pay a ransom.
4501,Amro bin Shu'ayb narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The claimant has the greater right to present evidence.
4502,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4503,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the wife of a man who had given birth to that man's two children, that woman used to hurt the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He put the crucible until the hoe crossed her body (and the woman died), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You people, be witnesses! This woman's blood has been wasted."
4504,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4505,"This is what was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, however, it contains these words: This person said: The other day this woman started cursing you and insulted you, so I killed her. Imam Dar al-Qati has stated that this proves this Sunnah: \When giving a decision"," the ruler can make the people witness about himself.\"""""
4506,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that all cities are the cities of Allah, all the servants are the servants of Allah, whoever settles a barren land will get it, and no one can occupy it as an injustice."
4507,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is obligatory for the person who claims to present evidence and for the one who denies it to swear an oath.
4508,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that it is necessary for a person who makes a claim to present evidence and for a person who denies it, it is necessary to swear an oath."
4509,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: Evidence must be presented against the claimant, and an oath must be taken against the person against whom the claim is made."
4510,Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the person who makes a claim must be presented with evidence and the person against whom the claim is made must only swear an oath.
4511,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) has said that the person against whom a claim has been made will have the right to only take an oath, but if evidence is presented (then the ruling will be different)."
4512,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the claimant to produce a double witness and instructed the person against whom the claim was made to take an oath.
4513,"Sayyiduna Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that a person who receives something from his brother without proof, then the person against whom there is a case, must take an oath."
4514,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The testimony of a villager will not be valid against a person living in a city.
4515,Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the testimony of a villager against a citizen will not be accepted.
4516,"Muhammad bin Abu Bakr narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, with reference to his father, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr As-Sadiq (may Allah be pleased with him), saying: The inheritance is divided which can be divided."
4517,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates on the authority of his father in the same way, in which it is narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the inheritance that can be divided."
4518,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: An Ansari was found dead near the well of the Jews in Khyber. They mentioned this to the Prophet (PBUH). The Prophet (PBUH) sent a message to these people to take 50 people, each of whom swore by name that I did not kill him, nor do I know anything about the murderer. He said: He has given the same ruling as was in the Shari'ah of Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him)."
4519,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A space of up to 25 cubits is protected around a well in the forest, and a space of up to 50 cubits around a well in a village is protected, a space of up to three hundred cubits is protected around a spring flowing in an open place, while a space of six hundred cubits is protected around a spring flowing near a farm."
4520,"Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal narrates that he requested the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to give him a piece of land called \Malh Shaza\"" at the location of \""Ma'rib\""; the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave that place to him. I had reached this place in the time of Jahiliyyah. It was a place where the water had no name and no sign. The person who reached there used to occupy it. The example of this was flowing water. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took back that place from Sayyidna Abayd bin Hamal. Sadaqah from the side will be counted but its example is like flowing water", whoever reaches for it will get it. Narrator named Farrukh has stated that the place is still the same today, the person who reaches there gets it," then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Sayyiduna Abayd bin Hamal at the place of \""Jarf\"" which means \""Jarf\""."""
4521,"Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal (RA) narrates that I said to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH): I asked him for a place called \Malh\"" and he gave it to me. Do you know which place you gave him? You gave him running water"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took that place back from him."""
4522,"Sayyidna Safwan bin Ya'ila narrates this statement of his father: I participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I consider this to be my greatest good deed. I had a laborer with me. He had a fight with a man. She has forgotten. When the other person pulled his hand, the front teeth of the chewing person broke. This case was presented in the presence of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he declared these teeth useless and he said: \Would this person had let his hand remain in your mouth so that you would have chewed his hand.\"" (The narrator says: I think this is an example in the tradition) You chew like a cow."""
4523,"Sufyan bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his two aunts, Sayyidna Ya'ila and Sayyidna Salama, that we participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him. There was a man living in Makkah with us. He used to come to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him to give him his diet. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person goes to his brother and bites him like a bull and then he comes to demand about it. You will not get any right. The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him."
4524,"This same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, it contains these words that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not have any marriage, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him like that."
4525,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The partner has the right to intercede and intercession is made in everything."
4526,Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to intercede in his immediate place.
4527,"Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyidna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) made a deal with Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him), or perhaps Sayyidna Abu Rafi' (may God be pleased with him) made a deal with Sayyidna Sa'd (may God be pleased with him). Sayyidna Abu Rafi' said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: \The neighbor has more right to intercede in his neighborhood.\"" If I had not heard this"," I would not have given you this place."""
4528,"Amro bin Sharid narrates: I and Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) came to Sayyidna Sa’d. Sayyidna Abu Rafi’ (RA) said: “You should buy my share in my house.” Sayyidna Sa’d said: “I don’t want to buy it.” Then someone suggested that you buy it from him. Allahu Anhu said: I will give it to him in exchange for five thousand dirhams, and I will have to pay it immediately, then Sayyiduna Saad said to him: I cannot pay you more. Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' said: If I had not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \The neighbor has more right to buy the land in his neighborhood\"""," then I would not have left five thousand dirhams and sold it for four dirhams."""
4529,"Sharid bin Suwayd narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The partner has more right to intercede, even if he obtains it or leaves it."
4530,"Amro bin Sharid narrates the statement of his father that he sold another part of his house. Another partner was with him, so this partner said to him: I have more right to buy it than anyone else."
4531,"Amro bin Sharid narrates the statement of his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to his \Saqb\"". Asked them what is meant by \""Saqb\""? So they replied: The neighborhood (in the place)."""
4532,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has ruled that anything that is jointly owned by two people can be interceded in and cannot be divided, whether it is land or a garden, it is not permissible for a man to sell it unless he obtains the permission of his partner. In one hadith it is said that if a person sells such a place and does not inform his partner, then the partner will be more entitled to the place. In this hadith, the words \distributed\"" have been narrated only by the narrator named Abdullah bin Idris"," and he is Sahib Thaqa and Hafiz."""
4533,"Amro bin Sharid narrates that Sayyidna Sa'd, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a deal with Sayyidna Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, in the house of Sayyidna Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: I will not pay you more than four dirhams. Karta) \Saqab\"" means to be close to a place."""
4534,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever creates something new in our religion that has nothing to do with it, that thing will be rejected."
4535,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever does something about his wealth that is not permitted in the Book of Allah, that deed will be rejected."
4536,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does something that is not according to our command, then that work will be rejected."
4537,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates that the person who does such a good deed \about which we do not have a command\"" will be rejected."""
4538,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Any work that does not have our command will be rejected.\"""""
4539,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No harm will be done to anyone."
4540,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A neighbor has the right to put a beam on his neighbor's wall, even if the other neighbor dislikes it, and the way for people to pass is seven cubits."
4541,Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: No one will be harmed if one does not harm oneself.
4542,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: No harm will be done to anyone, and no one should forbid his neighbor from throwing his beam on his wall."
4543,"Qasim bin Muhammad states that when a guilty person makes a claim against a good person, about whom people think that person is lying, even if there is no issue between them, then the oath will not be taken from that good person."
4544,Haritha bin Zafar narrates that a house was jointly owned by two brothers. They both erected a fence in the middle. Then they both died. Both of them left behind children. The children of each of them claimed that the fence of the land belonged to us and not to the other. Allah sent him to judge them. He calculated the wall as to whose land it meets and gave a decision in favor of the concerned person. They came back and told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have given a right decision.
4545,Nimran al-Haritha narrates that his father narrated that some people came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a house that was common between the young men. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) to decide between them. Sayyiduna Huzaifah (RA) decided in favor of the one whose ropes were tied. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have given the right decision. The narrator suspects that perhaps these are the words (that you have given a good decision).
4546,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a person becomes bankrupt and the person who sells his goods is found with him, then that person who sells will be more entitled to that thing than other creditors."
4547,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever sells an item, and the person who bought it becomes bankrupt, and that person finds his item with him,” then he (the seller) will be more entitled to that item."
4548,"Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A person who is declared bankrupt and has property belonging to another person and has not received any value for that property, then he will collect the debt along with other debts."
4549,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If a seller of goods finds his goods with a person who has been declared bankrupt, and the first person has not received anything from the second person, the goods will be found by the seller. But if this other person has paid some of the price of the goods, then the amount that was left, the seller will be treated like other creditors in this respect."
4550,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): After that, it is according to the previous hadith."
4551,The sons of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) narrate their father's statement that the Prophet (PBUH) had prevented Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) from disposing of his wealth 'due to the payment of a debt which was obligatory on the young man' and had sold this property.
4552,"Hisham bin Urwa narrates this statement that Abdullah bin Jafar came to Sayyiduna Zubair and said: I have bought such and such things for so much. Said: Ja'far's son has bought such and such thing for so much. When I tried to prevent him from disposing of it, Sayyidna Zubair (RA) said: I am also a sharer with him in this deal. So Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: How can I prevent someone from disposing of a deal in which Sayyidna Zubair (RA) is a partner? The narrator of this tradition, Yaqoob, i.e. Qazi Abu Yusuf, says: I am of the opinion that in such a case the person concerned can be restrained from disposing of it. But if a thing has been bought or sold by a person before it is disposed of, then if it is in a valid condition, I will declare it valid. will Qazi Abu Yusuf says: Imam Abu Hanifa did not prevent us from possession, nor has he issued a fatwa about the prohibition of possession."
4553,Makhool narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who is right has a hand and a tongue.
4554,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: If a person dies and he has to pay a debt and he has to recover a debt from someone, it is his responsibility to pay it immediately and the debt he has to take will be collected at the appointed time."
4555,"Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has established the right of \intercession\"" for something that has not been divided", that has been divided and the limits have been determined, and if the paths have separated," then there will be no intercession in it."""
4556,Sayyiduna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) maintained the testimony of the midwife (present at the time of the child's birth).
4557,Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) maintained the testimony of the midwife (present at the time of the child's birth).
4558,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The testimony of the midwife regarding the birth of the child will be accepted.
4559,Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace be upon him) accepted the testimony of one man and two women in marriage.
4560,It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he made it obligatory to pay twelve dirhams (on the husband).
4561,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that a man freed six slaves at the time of his death. This man had no property except these slaves.
4562,Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person belonging to the Ansar died. He left behind six slaves in Turka. (i.e. freed duku and allowed four to remain slaves).
4563,"Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Dhi Allah Anhu narrates that a man freed six slaves, he had no wealth except these slaves, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about this, he became very angry about it, then he divided them and gave them one-third (i.e. freed two slaves)."
4564,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Hind bint Utbah, who was the wife of Abu Sufyan, came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said: O Messenger of Allah! Abu Sufyan is a miserly man 'they don't give me enough money for me or my children' so I have to take it out on their ignorance 'will I be guilty of this? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should acquire as much as is sufficient for you and your children."
4565,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: This is the “sanctuary” of Allah, the Most High, which Allah made honorable on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He has placed these two mountains here. The thorn shall not be broken, the prey here shall not be driven away, the grass here shall not be cut, the fallen thing here shall not be picked up, but may be picked up to declare. Sayyidna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! The people living in Makkah cannot live without using Azkhar, goldsmiths also use it and it is also used in homes. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The order of Azkhar is different (i.e. it is permissible to cut it)."
4566,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid Jahni (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about gold or silver that had fallen, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: Remember the mark of the thread tied on the mouth of this (bag) and announce it for a year. If it comes, you will pay it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel. Let it remain there. Its stomach and its feet are with it. It will reach its own water and eat leaves. Until its owner feeds it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about the (lost) goat."
4567,"Amro bin Shuaib narrated his grandfather's story regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel and he said: Its belly and its feet are with it. He will go to the wolf, so you catch him."
4568,"Sayyidna Hibban bin Abu Jubla narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every person has more right to his wealth than his parents, his children and all other people."
4569,"Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid (RA) narrates that a person came to the Prophet (PBUH) and asked: What do you say about the lost camel? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, his face turned red, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your connection with him? His feet and his stomach are with him, he will reach water by himself and eat leaves from trees until his owner comes to him. He said: Then what do you say about the lost goat? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You catch her, because either you will find her, or one of your brothers will find her, or the wolf will find her."
4570,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas (RA) narrates that a person belonging to the Muzaina tribe came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! If someone breaks the rope, what do you say about it? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In this and similar (other things), the hand will not be cut off for stealing an animal. Will there be an order? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For stealing something like this, whipping will be done. For stealing a fruit from a tree, hands will not be cut off. Therefore, if the fruit stolen from there is equal to the value of the shield, then the hand will be cut off, but if it is not worth that much, then the hand will not be cut off. Or get something dropped? So what will be the ruling about it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should keep announcing it throughout the year. If its owner comes, pay it. Otherwise, use it. Whenever its owner comes to you, you shall pay it. If something is found in an uninhabited town or at the end of the road, it is the order to pay one-fifth of the treasure that comes out of it. The person asked: If a lost goat is found, what is your order about it? He said: You will find it, or one of your brothers will find it, or a wolf will find it. Therefore, he was asked about it as his brother's lost thing. The man said: What is your opinion about the lost camel? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He does not care. Its belly and its feet are with it. It will eat itself and drink water until its owner reaches it."
4571,Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: A will cannot be made for a murderer.
4572,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A murderer does not inherit.
4573,Amro bin Shuaib narrates this statement from his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer does not get anything from his inheritance.
4574,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said that the murderer gets something (that is, he does not get anything from the inheritance). A similar tradition has been narrated by other people."
4575,A similar tradition is transmitted by other people.
4576,"Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) appointed his slave to be the overseer of the pasture. Be gentle with the Muslims, avoid the curse of the oppressed, because it is answered, you are a little sheep, let the owner of the goats enter the pasture, but do not let the animals of Uthman bin Affan and Abd al-Rahman bin Auf enter. They will come and say: O Commander of the Faithful! (Help us!) Shall I give them up? Providing water and mercury to these people is easier for me than providing dinars and dirhams, by Allah! These people think that we have violated them even though this is their territory, about which they used to fight with each other in the age of ignorance. And while living in the same area, they have accepted Islam, by this caste! In whose power is my life! If I did not want to provide wealth to the Mujahideen in the way of Allah, then I would not have prevented people from entering a place the size of a pillow (i.e. I would not have declared it a public pasture)."
4577,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Saab bin Jathama (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: Pasture belongs only to Allah and His Messenger.
4578,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather about his father that Sayyiduna Bilal, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had the tithe of his land with him. Sufyan bin Wahhib wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Umar and asked him about it, and Sayyiduna Umar said: He will pay you what he used to pay the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), i.e. one-twentieth of the produce of this place."
4579,Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pasture is only for Allah and His Messenger.
4580,"Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates that once she was sitting with the Prophet (PBUH) two men came to serve him, and there was a dispute between them regarding inheritance, which was about some things that had become old. If he finds something, he will get a piece of hell, which he will bring around his neck on the Day of Judgment. The narrator says that both of them started crying. One of them said: The right that I was demanding is actually the right of my companion. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: No! Both of you go and examine it and take its portion, then each of you shall make it lawful for your partner."
4581,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: He said: Whoever among you I give judgment on the basis of evidence according to my opinion, and he will get a fair share as oppression."
4582,Sayyidah Umm Salma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and there was a veil between me and the people.
4583,"Sayyida Zainab bint Abu Salama (RA) narrates that Sayyid Umm Salama told her about the Prophet (PBUH) that he heard the sound of some people arguing at the door of his room. If I give a verdict in favor of a Muslim, then it will be a piece of Hell."
4584,"Sayyidah Zainab bint Umm Salama (RA) narrates this tradition on the authority of her mother that the Prophet (PBUH) said: You people come to me with a case, one of you may be faster than the other in presenting his argument. Do it because I would have cut a piece of hell for him. One hadith has these words: Now it is his will to obtain it or to give it up."
4585,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once came to me and he was very happy. He said: O Ayesha! Do you know that Majzamd Laji came to me, he saw Usamah and Zayd (they were both sleeping) with a cloak covering their parts, but their feet were visible, so he said: These two are father and son."
4586,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me once. He said: Do you know that Majzamd Laji looked at Osama bin Zayd who was lying with his father, and he said: These two are father and son."
4587,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once a physicologist came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also there, Sayyida Usama bin Zayd and Zayd bin Haritha were both lying down. The person said: These are the feet of the father and son. Narrated Ibrahim bin Saadnami: Sayyidna Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu was the owner of red and white color while Sayyidna Osama was like night (black)."
4588,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her, he was very happy and his face was shining with happiness. He said: Have you heard? What Majizzumdulji said about Zayd and Osama: He saw only their feet and said: These feet belong to the father and the son."
4589,"Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Zubayr narrates that Zam'ah had a slave girl with whom he used to have intercourse. This slave girl says that another person had intercourse with her. Meanwhile, Zam'ah died and she became pregnant. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As far as the inheritance is concerned, he will get it, but as far as your affairs are concerned, you should hide from him because he is not your brother."
4590,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sa'd and Abd bin Zam'ah sat next to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to argue. My brother Utbah gave me this will. He said: When you go to Makkah, you should see the son of the slave girl of Zamaa and take him in your arms because he is my son. Abd bin Zamaa said: O Messenger of Allah! He is the son of my father's maidservant and my brother, who was born on my father's bed. When the Prophet saw the clear resemblance of this child with Atba, he said: O Abd bin Zamaa! You will get it because the child belongs to the one who sleeps. You cover this boy."
4591,"Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas and Abd bin Zam'ah brought a case about the son of the maidservant of Zam'ah. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah! This is the son of my brother Utbah bin Abi Waqqas. My brother made a promise to me about him that this is his son. You should liken him to Qutiba. Abd bin Zamaa said: This is my brother who was born on my father's floor by his maidservant. The narrator says; The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likened it to Qutbiyah, which is clearly similar to Qutbiyah. He said that you will get a child because a child gets a bedridden person and an adulterer gets deprivation. The narrator says: After that, the child never saw Sayyida Saudah."
4592,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4593,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) narrates that Qutiba bin Abi Waqqas made a promise to her brother Zayd bin Abi Waqqas that the daughter of the concubine Zam’ah is from me. And said: This is my brother. This is the son of my father's maidservant, who was born in my father's bed. These two came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is my nephew, about whom my brother made a promise to me. Abd bin Zam'ah said: This is my brother, the son of my father's maidservant, who was born on my father's bed. You will get it. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child will be considered as an infidel and the adulterer will be deprived. The reason for this was that the Prophet (PBUH) had seen its similarity with Utba. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: This boy never saw Sayyida Soudah (may Allah be pleased with him) until he died."
4594,"Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us: my uncle narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uzzayz narrated to us: Salamah narrated to us: from Aqil. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Salih, and Ibn Ishaq. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Hani and Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Shu'ayb narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: [Layth?] narrated to us. And Abu Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Daqiqiyy narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us. All of them narrated from Ibn Shihab. And Layth said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us: from Urwah: from Aisha: from the Prophet ﷺ, to the same effect."
4595,"A narrator named Muhammad narrates that there was a disagreement between Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab and Sayyidna Mu'azbin Afraa about something. These two men appointed Sayyidna Abi bin Ka'b as an arbiter. Sayyidna Umar narrated the whole incident to them. This payment is obligatory on you. So Sayyiduna Umar took an oath and said: Because of my oath, I am absolved from him. Take this thing, it is yours."
4596,"Hasan bin Thumamah narrates that once Sayyidna Huzaifah (RA) recognized his camel which had been stolen. He went to the Muslim judge with a case about it. According to the court decision, Sayyidna Huzaifah (RA) had to take an oath. So he announced the compensation of his oath: I give you ten dirhams. He refused. He said: I give you twenty dirhams. He refused. He said: I give you thirty dirhams. He refused. He said: I will give you forty dirhams. When he refused, Sayyiduna Huzaifa said: Leave my camel. Then he swore that it was his camel, which he had neither sold nor given to anyone."
4597,"Muhammad Bin Jubayr narrates his father's statement that he had paid ten thousand dirhams in exchange for his oath, and then he said: By the Lord of this mosque! And by the Lord of this grave! If I had been truthful in swearing in my oath, but this is something that I have given ransom in exchange for my oath."
4598,"It is narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered forty dirhams for a hunting dog, one goat for a goat guard dog, and ordered a large pot of grain for a field guard dog, while he ordered a large clay pot for a house guard dog. Therefore, it is necessary that while receiving this compensation, he should reduce it."
4599,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever builds a building on the land of another person and builds it with his permission, then he will be required to pay the price, and whoever builds a building there without the owner's permission, then this building will be demolished."
4600,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected the testimony of a cheating man, a cheating woman, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a house servant."
4601,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a man who betrays, a woman who betrays, a man who is severely punished, a woman who is severely punished, who has a grudge against his brother will not be accepted."
4602,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a man who betrays, a woman who betrays, a man who is severely punished, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a servant of the house against his family is not valid."
4603,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said while giving a sermon: Remember that the testimony of a cheating man, a cheating woman, a person who has a grudge against his brother, and a person who has been violated is not valid."
4604,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The unfaithful man, the unfaithful woman, the person on whom the limit has been issued, and the person who bears testimony against his brother while bearing a grudge against him, their testimony is not valid."
4605,"Shaabi states that Qazi Shareeh used to accept the testimony of a person belonging to a religion against a person belonging to the same religion. He did not accept the testimony of a Jew against a Christian or a Christian against a Jew, but the problem of Muslims was different because he accepted the testimony of any Muslim against all other religions."
4606,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am leaving two things between you, you will not go astray after they are (joined): the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, these two will not be separated until they reach me at the reservoir."
4607,"Sayyidna Ka’b bin Asim Ash’ari (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: “Allah has given me refuge in three things regarding my Ummah: They will not remain hungry, they will not agree on misguidance, and they will not perish."
4608,Sayyidna Abaid bin Hamal (RA) narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! What do I pick from the yellow tree? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That which the camel's feet could not reach.
4609,"Marwan Jafar says that my father told me that once in Kufa, there was a dispute between Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba and Musqila bin Habira. I have more right to say that he is closer than me. Musqala said to them: The reason for this is that I left Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) among the emigrants and the Ansar and the great people of Iraq and joined Sayyidna Muawiya (RA) and used to wield the sword with him, and he appointed me as governor, so I freed Banusamah bin Lui for him. And they were rejoicing with their wives and playing with their children. Your tongue was long. You were miserly. Oh Masqala! These are the things you are talking about today. As far as you are concerned about leaving Sayyiduna Ali, you have done it. You have not done this out of love for the people of Syria, but you have done it because of your hatred for the people of Iraq. As far as you saying that you have freed Banusama bin Lui, a trusted companion of Sayyiduna Ali, trusting in you, has freed him. By Allah! You did not associate yourselves with them, nor did you free them from your wealth. As for my staying in Taif, the reason for this is that Allah has afflicted me with the trial of the family, which He has not afflicted you with."
4610,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wine of Umm al-Khabayth is (the root of all evils).” Whoever drinks it, Allah will not accept his prayers for 40 days."
4611,"Sayyidna Zayd bin Khalid (RA) narrates, 'I heard the Prophet (PBUH) say this during his sermon in Tabuk: \Wine is a combination of sins.\"""""
4612,Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Alcohol is the root of evil and the greatest sin. Whoever drinks it, he can attack the honor of his mother, his grandmother," his aunt.\"""""
4613,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Wine is the root of all evils.\"""""
4614,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu saying this on the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When the order of sanctity of wine was revealed", it was made from five things: grapes, wheat, barley," dates and honey.\"""""
4615,"Sa'ib bin Yazid narrates: Once Sayyiduna Umar (RA) came to the people. He said: \I smelled alcohol from such and such a person.\"" I asked him what it was. So he said: He has taken talapia. I am inquiring about alcohol. If he becomes intoxicated"," I will flog him. Then Sayyiduna Umar r.a."""
4616,"Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates (this saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a valid hadith: \Every intoxicant is forbidden", and every intoxicant is khamr. Whoever drinks alcohol in this world and dies while drinking it regularly," he will not drink it in the Hereafter.\"""""
4617,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4618,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4619,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4620,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicating things should be forbidden and all intoxicating things are forbidden.\"""""
4621,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicants should be forbidden and all intoxicants are forbidden.\"""""
4622,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All things that are intoxicating should be curdled and anything that is intoxicating is forbidden.\"""""
4623,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Every intoxicating thing is forbidden"," and every intoxicating thing should be bowed down.\"""""
4624,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every intoxicating substance is Haraam and every wine is Haraam.\"""""
4625,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicants should be bowed down and all intoxicants are prohibited.\"""""
4626,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \All intoxicating things should be forbidden and all intoxicating things are forbidden.\"""""
4627,"Narrated by Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Let every intoxicating thing be bent and intoxicating is forbidden.\"""""
4628,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every intoxicating thing is Haram and every intoxicating thing is forbidden.\"""""
4629,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Let every one of you be humble.\"""""
4630,"Narrated by Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Every intoxicating thing is forbidden", and whatever intoxicates in large quantities," even a small amount of it is forbidden.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""I do not declare intoxicants as halal.\"""""
4631,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, \every intoxicating thing is forbidden", and a small amount of anything that intoxicates is forbidden," and even a sip of any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
4632,Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Anything that intoxicates is forbidden.”
4633,Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: This is the sip that will intoxicate you.
4634,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Any intoxicant is forbidden.\"" This means a drink that intoxicates you."""
4635,"This hadith was mentioned before Sufyan bin Abdul Malik on the authority of Sayyidna Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: This is the sip that will intoxicate you. Abdullah bin Mubarak said: This is a false tradition."
4636,"The tradition that is narrated with reference to Hamad, \Intoxicating food is forbidden"," it means the cup that causes intoxication\"" is correct"," it is the opinion of Ibrahim Nakhai."""
4637,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about \Ba'ta\"" (a certain type of alcohol)"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
4638,"Sayyida Aisha Sidiqah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about \Ba'ta\"" (a certain type of alcohol)"," and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \""Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.\"""""
4639,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about “bata” (the narrator says: Taba means the sleep of honey), then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Any drink that intoxicates is forbidden.”"
4640,"Aamir bin Saad quotes the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father: \I forbid you even a small amount of anything that intoxicates you in excess.\"""""
4641,"Aamir bin Saad quotes the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father: \I forbid you even a small amount of anything that intoxicates you in excess.\"""""
4642,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I prepared sleep in a daba (a special vessel for making wine) in order to present it as a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that day when he was fasting, when it was time to break the fast, I picked it up and brought it to his service. He inquired: O Abu Huraira! what is it I said: O Messenger of Allah! My parents are a sacrifice to you. This is Nabeez, which I have prepared for you. I knew that you would fast today, so I want you to use it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Bring it near me. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, examined it, he was excited. He said: Hit it against this wall, because he who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day will drink it."
4643,Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Khumrangur, date, raisin, wheat," barley and corn are prepared and I forbid you from anything that is intoxicating.\"""""
4644,"Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: I heard Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying from the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \And then! O people! When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed", it was made from five things: grapes, honey, dates, wheat, and barley; everything that covers the intellect (i.e. produces intoxication) was curdled. O people! I wished for three things that the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would explain to us about them: Dada (part of k and ast)," kalala and usury (some forms of usury).\"""""
4645,"Narrated Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar: I heard Sayyiduna Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying from the pulpit of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \Afterwards! O people! When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed", it was made from five things: grapes, wheat, barley," dates and honey.\"""""
4646,"Imam Shaabi narrates: I heard Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer Radiyallahu Anhu describing this minbar (the narrator says:) i.e. from the pulpit of Kufa, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed", wine is made from dates, kushmush, wheat, barley," and honey.\"""""
4647,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer Radi Allahu Anhu cites this as a \marfu'\"" hadith that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is made from five things: wheat", dates, raisins and honey," and everything that veils the intellect is called 'Khamr'."""
4648,"Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Dates make wine, Raisins make wine, Wheat makes wine, and honey makes wine."
4649,"The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of narrators on the authority of Sayyidna Numan bin Basheer (RA), however, there has been an illusion in quoting the narrator."
4650,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Remember that wine is made from grapes, raisins, dates, wheat and barley."
4651,"Sayyidna Nu'man bin Bashir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Wheat makes wine, which makes wine, raisins make wine, dates make wine, and honey makes wine, and I forbid you anything intoxicating."
4652,"Abdullah bin Abu Hazil narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah took an oath and stated that when the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, under the order of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the pots for making alcohol were broken and the dates and raisins (which were used for alcohol) were discarded."
4653,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Anything that produces intoxication in large quantities is prohibited even in small quantities.\"""""
4654,"Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubayr Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “Anything that causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
4655,Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden and anything that produces intoxication in large quantities is also forbidden in small quantities.
4656,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: A portion (i.e. a cup) of something that causes intoxication, even a small amount (i.e. a small amount) of it is forbidden."
4657,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \Even a sip of it is forbidden.\"""""
4658,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \One cup of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.\"""""
4659,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.
4660,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whatever causes intoxicants," its awqiyyah is forbidden.\"""""
4661,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.
4662,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden. This hadith is \suspended\""."""
4663,"Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.\"""""
4664,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.
4665,Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even a single sip of anything that causes intoxication is forbidden.
4666,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: Alcohol and intoxicating drinks have been forbidden. This tradition has been narrated along with some other isnads. \Intoxicants are prohibited.\"" While some narrators have quoted these words: \""Anything that produces intoxication in large quantities"," even a small quantity of it is forbidden.\"" Some narrators have also narrated the fatwa of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding intoxicants (which is as follows)."""
4667,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
4668,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden."
4669,"One of the descendants of Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the statement of a member of his family, that he asked Sayyida Ayesha, may Allah be pleased with her, about Nabeez. She said: O my son! Allah Ta'ala has not declared the khamrakwas haram because of its name, but has made it haram because of its consequences."
4670,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father: Some people came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God! We do Zatiyar and drink it in the morning and evening. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink it, but (remember) every intoxicant is forbidden. He said: O Messenger of Allah! We break (the rush of intoxication) through water. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whatever causes intoxication in large quantities"," even a small amount of it is forbidden.\"""""
4671,"Amro bin Shoaib, regarding his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather that some people came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said: O Messenger of God! We make nabi zatiar and drink it with food. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink it, but avoid anything intoxicating. He repeated what he said, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden you to consume even a small amount of that which causes intoxication in large quantities."
4672,"Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates: My father and I came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib, may God be pleased with him. He fed us dinner, then he gave us a drink."
4673,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when I mentioned a few pots in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a villager said: There is nothing wrong with the pots."
4674,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (may God bless him and grant him peace) said to the delegation of the tribe of Abdul Qais: You people, do not drink from muqeer, muqeer, daba hantam, and Mazada (all these are different vessels for preparing alcohol)."
4675,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a person goes to his Muslim brother and feeds him, then a person should eat and not ask him for anything."
4676,"Sayyiduna Abu Burda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You people should drink (ordinary drink) in a \muzfat\"" (special vessel) but not drink intoxicating drink. In one hadith there are these words: Thou shalt not drink intoxicating drink."""
4677,"Ibn Burida narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father: I forbade you from certain vessels, so drink from whatever vessels you want, but do not drink intoxicants."
4678,"Ibn Buridah quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, regarding his father, that we had previously forbidden you to drink in certain vessels, 'You drink in whatever vessel you want', but do not drink anything intoxicating."
4679,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once we camped with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Wadi Batha (after that the narrator has narrated the entire hadith, which has these words:). \I forbade you to visit the graves. Now visit them because they will remind you of the hereafter. I forbade you to use the meat of the sacrifice for more than three days"," so now you should eat it and store it."""
4680,"Zaid bin Aslam narrates that I used to recite Nabi zatiaar for Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) in the morning, which he used to drink in the evening, and in the evening, the Nabi used to recite zatiaar, which he used to drink in the morning, but he did not allow him to get excited."
4681,"Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says, \I am a fast drinker who digests the meat of camels in our stomachs.\"""""
4682,"Saeed Bin Musayyib narrates that the Nabi was sent to Sayyiduna Umar (R.A) on the occasion when he was supposed to come, but he came late."
4683,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that the people of Thaqeef tribe humiliated the Prophet and came to Sayyiduna Umar (RA), then Sayyiduna Umar (RA) found that she had become hot, so he called for water and mixed it thirty times."
4684,"Umar bin Maimon narrates that I performed Hajj twice with Sayyiduna Umar, I heard him say: We pray to the Prophet so that the meat in our stomachs does not torment us (i.e. it is properly digested)."
4685,A narrator named Saeed narrates that once a villager drank the Prophet from the vessel of Sayyiduna Umar (RA).
4686,"Uthman ibn Abul-Aas narrates that Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by the vessel of a man of the Thaqif tribe, and he said: \This nabeez"," let me have it. It was brought to his service.\"" Sayyiduna Umar", may Allah be pleased with him," took it and said that it was sharp."""
4687,"Utbah bin Farq says that once I came to Sayyiduna Umar's service with a plate of sweetmeats. I placed them in front of him. All Muslims are blessed with this thing. I said: No! This thing is only available to rich people. Sayyiduna Umar said: You take it, I don't need it. The narrator narrates: Meanwhile, they asked for food in my presence, so fat meat and hard bread were brought to them. Then he let him stay for a little while. Then he gave me water and drank it himself. Then he said: O Utba! We cook camel meat every day and feed its good sirin meat to guests or common Muslims and eat the neck meat that does not rot, which you have seen just now, after that the Prophet eats it so that the meat is digested in our stomach."
4688,"Abdullah bin Mubarak narrates that Abdullah bin Umar Umari asked Imam Abu Hanifa (RA) about the drink, and he told us that people have narrated this hadith to us regarding your father, that he said: If you are worried about it, then increase its strength through water."
4689,It is narrated about Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) that he had given a complete whipping to a person whose mouth had been sprinkled with alcohol.
4690,"Sha'bi states that a person drank Nabeez from the vessel of Sayyidna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) - this is about the place of Safin - He became intoxicated, then Sayyidna Ali (Radi Allahu Anhu) reprimanded him."
4691,"Amir narrates that a villager drank Nabeez from an old musket and became intoxicated, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stopped him. This is a messenger and these two narrations are not proven."
4692,"Sayyidna Maald bin Abu Wada' Sahmi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once on a hot summer day, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House of Allah. He asked some people of Quraysh for water to drink. So one of them sent from his house, a maid came, she had a vessel, in which there was a Nabi Dhimm made of raisins. Even if it was covered by a piece of wood, when he brought the vessel near you, you felt a sharp smell from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it. The person said: O Messenger of Allah! If it is forbidden, then don't drink it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for this vessel again and did the same thing with it. The person said the same again. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a bucket of Zamzam and put it in the vessel and said: \When your drink becomes strong"," do this with it.\"""""
4693,"Sayyidna Matal bin Abu Wada'a narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after circumambulating the House of Allah: Give me something to drink! So the Prophet of Raisin was humiliated in your service. You gave him something to drink and then returned him. I said: O Prophet of Allah! Is it forbidden? By Allah! It is a drink, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. They asked him this question again, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent again. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it forbidden? By Allah! This is the special drink of the people of Makkah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring it back to me! Then he ordered the people to add water to it, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to drink it sip by sip."
4694,"Malik bin Thaqafi narrates that I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) about the smell of Teznabeez, and he said: Once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in a gathering. It was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his blessed face to it and smelled it. Then he brought the face back and returned it. When the person had left Batha, the person came back and asked: Is it haram or halal? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his head close to it and felt its bitterness and added water to it, then drank it. This hadith has been narrated in the same way, however, it has been authentically narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): \Anything that causes intoxication in large quantities"," even a small quantity of it is forbidden.\"" This tradition has been passed before."""
4695,Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt thirsty near the Kaaba. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mixed that water in it and drank it. A person said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it forbidden? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!
4696,"Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt thirsty, he was circumambulating the Kaaba at that time, so Prophet Zakam Shakiza was brought to his service. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not accept him. Is it forbidden? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: No! You come to me with a bucket of zam-zam. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mixed that water with it and drank it, and then he started circumambulating."
4697,"Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I remember about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a vessel was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present. Is it forbidden? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of this vessel, then he called for a bucket of zam-zam and mixed that water in it, then he drank this drink, then he said: When your Prophet becomes zatiz, end his fastness with water."
4698,Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about Nabeez: Is it halal or haram? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is lawful.
4699,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the following about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A person was brought (to him) who had become intoxicated due to drinking Nabeez of dates, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged him."
4700,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: A person was brought to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) who had become intoxicated due to drinking Nabeez, so the Prophet (PBUH) flogged him."
4701,Sulaiman Taymi says: There is no harm in drinking Nabeez.
4702,Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought some wine for the orphans under my care. The Prophet (PBUH) repeated this three times.
4703,"Alqamah bin Wail narrates the statement of his father: A man named Suwayd bin Tariq asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about alcohol, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from drinking this wine. The man said: I prepare it for medicine."
4704,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wine: Should it be made into vinegar? So he said: No!
4705,Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that there was an orphan boy under the care of Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) Sayyidna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) bought wine for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No!
4706,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that Sayyidna Abu Talha (RA) told me this: He had some property of the orphans, and he used it to buy alcohol. Then the order of sanctity of alcohol was revealed. I have bought wine through him. This is before the revelation of the order of wine. So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed me to break the vessel and pour out the wine. I attended your service three times."
4707,"Sayyidah Umm Salma (RA) narrates: We had a goat that was sick. The Prophet (PBUH) inquired: What happened to your goat? We told him that it was epilepsy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not benefit from its skin? We said: He is dead. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its tanning makes it halal, just as a head made of wine is halal."
4708,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that one day we were participating in a battle, 'We felt hungry,' until we distributed another two dates.' Then we reached the seashore. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Do you have any part of it? Nafi' narrated that when those people came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him about it, the Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: Do you have any share of it? People answered: Yes! The people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you have any part of it? People answered: Yes! People offered it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he ate it."
4709,"It has been narrated about Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Huraira that he asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): Shall I skin the fish that floats on the water (after death)? Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The fish that swims in the water is dead.\"""""
4710,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (RA) who is an old man, narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: Allah has slaughtered the fish in the sea for the children of Adam."
4711,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every animal in the sea has been declared pure by Allah for the children of Adam.
4712,"Amro bin Dinar says that I have come to know (that is, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:) Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for the children of Adam."
4713,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): “Eat the animal that the sea appears and throws out, but do not eat the one that you find dead (the narrator doubts these words here) that floats on the water."
4714,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “When the animal swims on the water, do not eat it, and when the water recedes, then eat it, and what is found on the shore, eat it too.” The narrators have differed in quoting the authenticity of this tradition."
4715,"Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Eat what the sea takes out or what it brings up, and do not eat what dies in the sea and floats in the water."
4716,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that eat the fish that the sea throws out or that appears, and do not eat the fish that you find floating on the water."
4717,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Eat what the sea throws out or abandons it and retreats or hunts it, and do not eat what dies in it and then floats on the water."
4718,"This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another document."""
4719,Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Sadiq (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for you.
4720,Sayyiduna Shareeh (may God be pleased with him) who was a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for the children of Adam.
4721,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) that he said: A fish floating on water (i.e. a dead fish) is lawful for a person who wants to eat it.
4722,It has been narrated with the same authority that he said: (After death) the fish that floats on the water is halal.
4723,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) saying: Allah has slaughtered everything in the sea for you, so eat them all because they have been slaughtered."
4724,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) that he ate fish that floated on the water.
4725,Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says that Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) said: All kinds of fish are slaughtered.
4726,Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: Every kind of fish is slaughtered and every kind of grasshopper is slaughtered.
4727,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that Allah Ta'ala has said: \For you the game of the sea and its food has been made lawful for you. It is Zadrah for you and for those who travel.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: What is meant by his food is what he throws out."""
4728,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about this decree of Allah Ta'ala: \The hunting of the sea and its food have been made lawful for you.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Hunting means something that is hunted"," and eating means something that is thrown out into the sea."""
4729,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub that he was going on a sea voyage with some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him. They found a dead fish floating on the water. When people asked him about it, he asked: Is it clean? There has been no change in it (i.e. the flowers have not started coming)? People answered: Yes! (Pure is) So Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Radiyallahu Anhu said: Eat it and take my share from it (i.e. keep it). The reason for this was that he was fasting at that time."
4730,Jablah bin Atiya narrates that some of the companions of Sayyiduna Abu Talha (radiyallahu anhu) found a fish floating on the water (after his death).
4731,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb of an animal is considered as slaughtering it, whether its hair has come out or not. A narrator named Ubaidullah has stated this: But if he comes out of the mother's womb, then he will be ordered to be slaughtered until blood comes out of his womb."
4732,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two kinds of blood have been made lawful for us and two kinds of dead bodies have been made lawful. Dead (things) are fish and locusts.
4733,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the baby in the belly of an animal, which comes out dead, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Eat it if you wish.\"""""
4734,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat the baby that comes out of the womb of the mother (female animal). Narrator Abu Sudnami has narrated that eat the baby in the camel's stomach.
4735,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates this about the Prophet (PBUH): He (PBUH) was asked about a she-camel that has a baby in its belly, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: When you slaughter it, mention the name of Allah, then slaughtering the mother of the baby in that womb will be counted as slaughtering the baby."
4736,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that we asked the Prophet (PBUH) 'We said: If a person slaughters a camel or a cow or a goat and finds a child in its belly, should he eat it or throw it away? So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you want, eat as much as you like, because slaughtering his mother will be counted as slaughtering him."
4737,Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb of an animal is considered as slaughtering it.
4738,"Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the following as a \marfu'\"" hadith: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb is considered as slaughtering her."""
4739,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): As for the child in the womb of an animal, slaughtering its mother is considered slaughtering."
4740,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb (of an animal) is considered as slaughtering it. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Slaughtering the mother of a child in the womb (of an animal) is considered as slaughtering it.
4741,"Abu Salamah and Sulaiman bin Yasarbayan say that they have come to know the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that whoever wants to delay can offer sacrifice until the end of the month."
4742,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: Whoever has the capacity and still does not offer sacrifice, then he should not come to our mosque. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed two horned bulls, one of which he slaughtered on behalf of himself and his family, and the other he slaughtered on behalf of those members of his Ummah who could not."
4743,Saeed bin Al-Masayyib narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) that he used to say: \Whoever has ease (financial ability) but does not offer sacrifice," then he should not enter our mosque.\"""""
4744,"On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Hurairah (may God be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed two goats, both of which had crooked horns and acorns on the back."
4745,"Sayyidah Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the first ten days of Dhul-Julj begin and a person wants to make a sacrifice, he should not cut his hair and nails."
4746,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: The order of sacrifice has abolished every sacrifice that preceded it.
4747,"Abolished every previous ablution, the fasting of Ramadan has abrogated every fast, the ablution of Janabat has abrogated every ablution, and Zakat has abrogated every charity."
4748,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zakat has canceled every charity in the Qur’an, Ramadan fasting has canceled every fast, Ghusl Janabat has canceled every bath, and Eid sacrifice has canceled every sacrifice."
4749,"Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have been commanded that the day of Eid al-Adha is the Eid that Allah has appointed for this Ummah. Can I slaughter an animal if I have given it? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! However, if you trim your nails, trim your moustache, clean your pubic hair, then your sacrifice will be complete in the presence of Allah."
4750,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \I have been ordered to sacrifice," but it is not obligatory.\"""""
4751,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Sacrifice has been made obligatory on me, but it has not been made obligatory on you people. I have been ordered to offer the Eid-ul-Adha prayer," but you have not been ordered to do it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
4752,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whatever you spend silver (i.e. money) on," the most excellent thing in it is to sacrifice on the day of Eid al-Adha.\"""""
4753,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of a camel that eats filth and drinking its milk. \Only goods can be loaded on it.\"" People will not slaughter it until it has eaten fodder for forty days."""
4754,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet sent Badil bin Warqa Al-Khuza’i (may Allah be pleased with him) on a camel to announce in the paths of semen that the throat and lips will be slaughtered and do not hasten to take life and the days of semen are days of eating and drinking and spending time with wives.
4755,Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! Can I sacrifice by taking a loan? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! It is a debt that will be repaid.
4756,Nafi bin Jubayr narrates the statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Tashriq are the days of slaughter for all (i.e. sacrifices can be made during these days).
4757,This tradition is also narrated along with another document.
4758,Sayyidna Jabir bin Mut'im narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the days of Tashreeq are the days of slaughter (i.e. they can be sacrificed).
4759,"Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed a horned ram and then prayed: \O Allah! This is on behalf of me and on behalf of every member of my Ummah who could not sacrifice.\"""""
4760,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Eid-ul-Adha prayer. When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and finished the sermon, he came down from his pulpit. Harass is towards the person who cannot perform the sacrifice."
4761,"Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He slaughtered two black sheep, one of them was from his Ummah and the other was from him and his family."
4762,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever has the capacity and still does not offer sacrifice, should not come to our Eidgah."
4763,"Asim bin Kalib narrates this statement of a person belonging to the Ansar: We attended a funeral with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We came to the grave. Q: So-and-so lady has invited you and your companions. The Prophet (PBUH) went to this lady. When all the people were seated and the food was brought, the Prophet (PBUH) extended his blessed hand towards her. The people also extended their hands and the Prophet (PBUH) started eating. Meanwhile, he stopped his hand. The narrator says: We were sitting in the place where children sit with their fathers. saw that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had vomited what he had eaten, so all those people hit their children's hands and dropped the herbs in their hands. I sent someone to Baqi' to look for my goat, but he could not find that goat. I found out that my neighbor had also bought a goat. So I sent a message to him, but he refused. We could not get it. Then this goat was sent by the man's wife, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Feed it to the prisoners."
4764,"Asim bin Kalib narrates the statement of a man from the tribe of Muzaina regarding his father: A woman belonging to the Quraysh prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and invited him and his companions. It is said that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had started eating, when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a morsel, then he put it away from her and said: I have felt the taste of this goat's meat as if it had been slaughtered without the permission of its owner. The woman said: O Messenger of Allah! It belongs to my brother and my brother loves me the most. If there was a better goat, it would not have been difficult for us to slaughter it."
4765,"Asim bin Kalib narrates with reference to his father that an Ansari narrated this hadith to me: When I was a young child, I went with my father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). After that, he mentioned the previous hadith, which reads as follows: This woman said: I sent a message to my brother Amir bin Abu Waqqas because a goat was bought from Baqi', but my brother was not there, so his wife took this goat. sent me"
4766,"Abdul Wahid bin Ziyad states that I inquired from Imam Abu Hanifa: Where did you get the issue that a person disposes of another's wealth without his permission, then he will give the profit as charity? So Imam Abu Hanifah said: I obtained it from the hadith narrated by Asim bin Kalib."
4767,"Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maad Yakarb (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared certain things haram on the day of the Battle of Khyber. will make it forbidden (the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:). \Whatever the Messenger of Allah has forbidden is like that which Allah has forbidden.\"""""
4768,"Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maadikarb (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given the Book and that which is similar to it (i.e. the Sunnah has been given). We will declare it haram. (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Yarawi said:). It is not like 'eating any sharp-toothed beast or eating a donkey' it is not permissible to pick up the fallen thing of a contracted person' but if it is something that is not needed, then the ruling will be different."
4769,"Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of horses, mules, donkeys, sharp-toothed beasts (maybe these words are the words:) on the day of the Battle of Khyber."
4770,"Sayyiduna Khalid bin Waleed, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of horses, mules, donkeys, and sharp-toothed beasts on the day of the Battle of Khyber."
4771,"This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but this tradition is weak because Waqidi has stated that Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) accepted Islam after the conquest of Khyber."
4772,"Yahya bin Muqadam narrates that he heard his grandfather narrating: Once I and ten people of my tribe, perhaps a little more than that, had not eaten for twenty-two days. They had blinded the horse to be slaughtered. So they would do evil, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the property of Dhimmis, the meat of donkeys, horses and mules to be haram. Then Sayyidna Qald (RA) ordered these people to give them two grains of grain and one aid and said that when we encounter any campaign, we will inform them."
4773,"Sayyidna Khalid bin Waleed (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade domesticated donkeys, horses and mules. The narrator says: His chain of transmission is not authentic because Sayyiduna Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam after the Battle of Khyber."
4774,"Majzat bin Zahir narrates the statement of his father: who had pledged allegiance to the Holy Prophet under the tree, he narrates that once he was afflicted with an illness, the Holy Prophet sent him a message to use donkey milk and broth (as medicine), but he did not like this food (yadwa)."
4775,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we used to eat the meat of horses. The narrator says that we inquired: And of mules? He replied: Not that.
4776,Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that those people used to eat horse meat during the time of the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator states: A narrator named Ata has narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of mules and donkeys.
4777,Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once we were traveling with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we ate horse meat and drank (mare's) milk.
4778,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Khyber, we ate the meat of horses, mules and donkeys, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of mules and donkeys, but he did not forbid us to eat the meat of horses."
4779,"Sayyiduna Jajar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to feed us the meat of horses, but he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the meat of donkeys."
4780,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Khyber, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of domestic donkeys, but he allowed us to eat the meat of horses."
4781,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to eat the meat of horses, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to eat the meat of donkeys."
4782,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade eating the meat of pet donkeys.
4783,Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we slaughtered a horse and ate its meat.
4784,"Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (RA) narrates that we had a horse during the time of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and it started to die, so we slaughtered it and ate its meat."
4785,Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we kept a horse and we (slaughtered) it and ate its meat.
4786,Sayyida Asmaa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we slaughtered a horse.
4787,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade eating cat meat and using its value.
4788,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that a rabbit was served in the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was asleep at that time, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held its back for me. When I woke up, the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave it to me to eat."
4789,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that grunts in ghee or fat, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it is ghee, then throw away the ghee around it, and if it is in the form of an obstacle, then use it for another purpose, but do not eat it."
4790,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about a rat that grunts in ghee and olive oil, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: Use it for something else. Do not eat it. This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another chain of transmission."""
4791,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if there is thunder in olive oil in the chuhaghi, then you should profit from it, but do not eat it."
4792,"Sayyidna Abu Waqid Laithi (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) came to Madinah, people used to cut the humps of camels and the meat of the tusks and eat them."
4793,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The part of a live animal that is cut off will be considered dead.
4794,"Imam Muhammad bin Hasan Shaibani narrates the following statement of Abd al-Rahman bin Laila regarding Imam Abu Hanifa: I went to a farmer with Sayyidna Hudhaifa, may Allah be pleased with him, and he brought food to us, and we ate it. Then Sayyiduna Huzaifa (RA) said: We came to him last year too, and he brought me a drink in the same vessel. I told him that the Prophet (PBUH) forbade us to eat or drink in gold or silver vessels, or to wear silk clothes (the Prophet (PBUH) said:). \These two things are for the polytheists in this world"," but they will be for us in the Hereafter.\"""""
4795,"This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying these words: \Do not drink from gold and silver vessels and do not eat from them.\"""""
4796,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Huzaifa that once he asked for water to drink and a farmer brought water to him in a silver vessel. Sayyidna Huzaifa caught it and threw it away and then said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) forbade us to drink or eat from gold or silver vessels, and he also prohibited us from wearing silk and jewelry and from sitting on them. What is forbidden?"
4797,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father that a person attended the service of the Holy Prophet, his name was Abu Thaalba, he said: O Messenger of Allah! I have some trained dogs 'you tell me about hunting through them! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your dogs are trained, then eat the prey they catch for you, regardless of whether they get a chance to slaughter it or not. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if he himself eats some of it (yet you can eat it), this person said: O Messenger of Allah! You tell me about my bow! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat whatever your bow (i.e. arrow) shoots. He asked: Whether it was slaughtered or not. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he hides from you, then until he is lost, until you find no other mark in him than your arrow (then you can eat him). This person said: O Messenger of Allah! You tell me about the potions of the Magi when we use them under compulsion? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You can wash them and then eat in them."
4798,"Shaabi narrates that Sayyidna Udi bin Hatim asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: I shoot my arrow, but I reach the target after one day. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you capture the prey and there is no mark or scratch on it other than your arrow, then you should eat it. (Here the narrator is in doubt about a word) This is because you do not know whether you have hunted it or someone else has hunted it. Likewise, when you release your dog and it catches the prey and you reach the prey, then you should slaughter it. Killed and even ate some of it, then you should not eat the prey (the narrator has doubts about a word here). The reason is that this animal has kept that prey for itself. Eat! Because you don't know whether your dog has killed him or another dog has killed him."
4799,"Sayyidina Adi bin Hatim (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about hunting, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: When you start to shoot your arrow, take the name of Allah over it. If you find the prey in such a state that it is dead, then eat it."
4800,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: (The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)) forbade the slaughter of a Magian, the prey of his dog or the prey of his bird."
4801,"Sayyidna Abu Tha'laba Hashani (RA) narrates that I said: O Messenger of Allah! We live together with the idolaters. We do not have separate pots and pans. The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If possible, try to avoid them. But if there is no space, wash it with water. Water will purify it, then cook (food) in it."
4802,"Sayyiduna Abu Thalaba Khoshni (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that when you throw your fish and it is absent from you for three days, then you reach it, then eat it, while it does not smell bad."
4803,Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! What is your ruling about a person who forgets to recite the name of Bismillah while slaughtering? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The name of Allah is present on the tongue of every Muslim. My narrator has disagreed about one word here.
4804,Ibrahim says about a Muslim who forgets to recite Bismillah while slaughtering. Ibrahim says: There is nothing wrong with that.
4805,"With another chain of transmission, it is narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) that he did not think there was anything wrong with it."
4806,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: When a Muslim slaughters an animal and does not mention the name of Allah on it, he can eat it because the word Muslim also contains a name of Allah."
4807,Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There is no harm in eating the bread cooked by a Magi.
4808,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: His name alone is sufficient for a Muslim. If he forgets to recite Bismillah, he should eat it after reciting Tabsmillah and mentioning the name of Allah."
4809,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that some people said: O Messenger of Allah! Some people slaughter meat and bring it to us. We do not know at that time whether they mentioned the name of Allah while slaughtering it or not. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You eat it while mentioning the name of Allah.\"""""
4810,"Al-Khajri ibn Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he attended the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him), then he was returning from the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and he passed by some people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Did you recite this Surah (Fatihah)? He said: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then accept it, by my life! Whoever eats something with false breath (it will be wrong), you have eaten it with true breath."
4811,"Al-Khajri bin Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then according to the previous hadith, in which there are these words: You should eat it with the name of Allah, because whoever eats it with false breath, he is doing wrong."
4812,This tradition is narrated along with another document.
4813,"Al-Khajri ibn Salat narrates the statement of his uncle that he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then according to the previous hadith, however, it has these words that he said: You people will pay us for it. So I said: I will ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about this first."
4814,"Dahhak bin Muzahim narrates: I Hasan bin Abul Hasan, Makhool, Amro bin Dinar and Taus gathered in \Masjid Khaif\"" these people began to argue loudly", these people began to argue about tazeez, on this Taus said: who was the favorite person of all: you should be quiet! I am narrating to you the hadith that I heard on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Darda, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Allah has made certain things obligatory upon you, so do not waste them, and He has set certain limits for you, do not transgress them. Do not oblige him, because it is a mercy from your Lord, accept it! (After that," Taus said:) We say what our Lord and our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: All things are in the hands of Allah Almighty. He orders everything. He will also reward everything. At this all the people stood up and these people liked (i.e. adopted) the saying of the Taos."""
4815,The hadiths that have been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are mentioned here (this is an addition to the original book). 4729 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses and the one who reached the limit first was declared successful.
4816,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (pbuh) used to train horses and compete between them.
4817,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ran from \Hafiyyah\"" to \""Taniya Al-Wadaa\"" among trained horses and ran from \""Tanayyah Al-Wadaa\"" to Masjid Banuzriq among untrained horses."""
4818,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet used to train horses.
4819,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a race between trained horses from Thaniya al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. My horse took me and climbed the wall. A narrator named Sufyan has stated that there is a distance of five or six miles from Saniya Al-Wada to Hafiyyah, while the distance from Saniya Al-Wada to Masjid Banuzariq is up to one mile. A narrator named Abu Mas'ud has narrated these words in his tradition: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conducted a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was also among those who participated in this race."
4820,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) conducted a competition between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I was also among those riders, I went ahead of the people and my horse took me to Masjid Banuzreeq."
4821,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I went ahead and was close enough that my horse would have taken me and climbed the wall of the mosque, which was very small."
4822,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet made a competition between trained horses from Hafiyyah to Saniyyah al-Wada, while he made a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was also among those who won this competition."
4823,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a competition between horses. I was also riding one of them.
4824,"Abul Baid al-Mazah bin Zubayd Bayan says that I made a competition between the horses of the pilgrims. Hakim bin Ayyub was the governor of Basra in those days. When we reached the race field and the horses came there, we thought that if we went to Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about it, did those people also run in the same way during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him, then it would be appropriate. Ibn Malik (R.A.) appeared in his service. He was in his palace. We said: O Sayyidna Anas! Did you people used to fight horses during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he replied: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered his horse in the competition, whose name was \Sanjah\"""," and it came first."""
4825,"The same hadith has been narrated by Ibn Mubashir along with another chain of transmission from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (RA), which is similar to the tradition narrated by Yazid."
4826,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that whenever the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) Qaswa joined the race, it used to go ahead. Saeed bin Musaib narrates that once a person came and his camel overtook the Qaswa. The people were very sorry that a camel overtook the camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4827,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could win a race with the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) in a race, it always went ahead."
4828,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could get ahead of Qaswa. Once a villager brought a young camel. He fought with Qaswa and he got ahead of him. This caused a lot of trouble for the Muslims. He said: O Messenger of Allah! A person has gone beyond the Quswa', so he said: In this world, whomever Allah gives high, He sometimes lowers him."
4829,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that Qaswa was the camel of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. “Whatever race she participated in, she would lead the way. Words are:) when wanting to see someone high."
4830,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a villager fought with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
4831,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said this: There is no reality of Jalab, Janab and Shaghar in Islam, and the person who practices any of them has nothing to do with us."
4832,"Basramzni quotes his grandfather's statement regarding his father saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. Narrator Ibn Abawais stated that Jalab means that a man pulls a horse from behind in order to overtake him, and Janab means that he creates an obstacle in front of another horse so that it does not win."
4833,"Abu Ubaidnami, the narrator, has quoted these words in the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. The narrator says: Jalab occurs only in two things, one is in horse racing, and this is the way that a man rides on the back of a horse and pulls the horse. It is forbidden to buy its fruits and receive its charity. Rather, it is ordered that he should go to people and collect charity from them. Run and win, because that horse will be less tired than a horse with a rider on it."
4834,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that there is no reality of ``Atira'' and ``Fa'ar'' in Islam, and there is no reality of ``Jilb'' and ``Janb'' either. The narrator says: Atirah is the animal that was slaughtered by the people of the dangerous tribe in the age of ignorance."
4835,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever enters his horse among other horses in such a way that he is not sure that it will get ahead of him, then there is no harm."
4836,"A narrator named Hasan has narrated this tradition about Sayyidna Ali (RA) that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ali (RA): I am appointing you as a horse-runner. I am entrusting you with the responsibility of those who join the race, which the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has entrusted to me. So when you reach Maitan (Abu Abd al-Rahman says: This means the place from where the race was to start), form a line of horses and announce three times: Someone is going to fix the bridle, someone is going to lift the boy, someone is going to put (the end of the bridle) on the horse's head (i.e. if it is not If no one gives you an answer, then say Allahu Akbar three times and leave him, then Allah will help him for the sake of whomever He wills from among His creatures. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) would come to the last mark of the race, he would draw a line and make two men stand face to face on both sides of this line. Declaring and if you doubt about it, you would declare them both successful and when you declare the two equal, then make the last limit which is the smaller of the two."
4837,"Dahhak bin Muzahim narrates: I Hasan bin Abul Hasan, Makhool, Amro bin Dinar and Taus gathered in \Masjid Khaif\"" these people began to argue loudly", these people began to argue about tazeez, on this Taus said: who was the favorite person of all: you should be quiet! I am narrating to you the hadith that I heard on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Darda, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: Allah has made certain things obligatory upon you, so do not waste them, and He has set certain limits for you, do not transgress them. Do not oblige him, because it is a mercy from your Lord, accept it! (After that," Taus said:) We say what our Lord and our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: All things are in the hands of Allah Almighty. He orders everything. He will also reward everything. At this all the people stood up and these people liked (i.e. adopted) the saying of the Taos."""
4838,The hadiths that have been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are mentioned here (this is an addition to the original book). 4729 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses and the one who reached the limit first was declared successful.
4839,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (pbuh) used to train horses and compete between them.
4840,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ran from \Hafiyyah\"" to \""Taniya Al-Wadaa\"" among trained horses and ran from \""Tanayyah Al-Wadaa\"" to Masjid Banuzriq among untrained horses."""
4841,Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet used to train horses.
4842,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a race between trained horses from Thaniya al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. My horse took me and climbed the wall. A narrator named Sufyan has stated that there is a distance of five or six miles from Saniya Al-Wada to Hafiyyah, while the distance from Saniya Al-Wada to Masjid Banuzariq is up to one mile. A narrator named Abu Mas'ud has narrated these words in his tradition: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conducted a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was also among those who participated in this race."
4843,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) conducted a competition between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I was also among those riders, I went ahead of the people and my horse took me to Masjid Banuzreeq."
4844,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a race between horses. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I went ahead and was close enough that my horse would have taken me and climbed the wall of the mosque, which was very small."
4845,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet made a competition between trained horses from Hafiyyah to Saniyyah al-Wada, while he made a competition between untrained horses from Saniyyah al-Wada to Masjid Banuzreeq. The narrator narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was also among those who won this competition."
4846,Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a competition between horses. I was also riding one of them.
4847,"Abul Baid al-Mazah bin Zubayd Bayan says that I made a competition between the horses of the pilgrims. Hakim bin Ayyub was the governor of Basra in those days. When we reached the race field and the horses came there, we thought that if we went to Sayyidna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him about it, did those people also run in the same way during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him, then it would be appropriate. Ibn Malik (R.A.) appeared in his service. He was in his palace. We said: O Sayyidna Anas! Did you people used to fight horses during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he replied: Yes! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had entered his horse in the competition, whose name was \Sanjah\"""," and it came first."""
4848,"The same hadith has been narrated by Ibn Mubashir along with another chain of transmission from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Anas (RA), which is similar to the tradition narrated by Yazid."
4849,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that whenever the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) Qaswa joined the race, it used to go ahead. Saeed bin Musaib narrates that once a person came and his camel overtook the Qaswa. The people were very sorry that a camel overtook the camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4850,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could win a race with the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) in a race, it always went ahead."
4851,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that no one could get ahead of Qaswa. Once a villager brought a young camel. He fought with Qaswa and he got ahead of him. This caused a lot of trouble for the Muslims. He said: O Messenger of Allah! A person has gone beyond the Quswa', so he said: In this world, whomever Allah gives high, He sometimes lowers him."
4852,"Saeed bin Musayyib narrates that Qaswa was the camel of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. “Whatever race she participated in, she would lead the way. Words are:) when wanting to see someone high."
4853,Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a villager fought with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).
4854,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) has said this: There is no reality of Jalab, Janab and Shaghar in Islam, and the person who practices any of them has nothing to do with us."
4855,"Basramzni quotes his grandfather's statement regarding his father saying that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. Narrator Ibn Abawais stated that Jalab means that a man pulls a horse from behind in order to overtake him, and Janab means that he creates an obstacle in front of another horse so that it does not win."
4856,"Abu Ubaidnami, the narrator, has quoted these words in the hadith of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no truth in Jalab and Janab. The narrator says: Jalab occurs only in two things, one is in horse racing, and this is the way that a man rides on the back of a horse and pulls the horse. It is forbidden to buy its fruits and receive its charity. Rather, it is ordered that he should go to people and collect charity from them. Run and win, because that horse will be less tired than a horse with a rider on it."
4857,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) that there is no reality of ``Atira'' and ``Fa'ar'' in Islam, and there is no reality of ``Jilb'' and ``Janb'' either. The narrator says: Atirah is the animal that was slaughtered by the people of the dangerous tribe in the age of ignorance."
4858,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever enters his horse among other horses in such a way that he is not sure that it will get ahead of him, then there is no harm."
4859,"A narrator named Hasan has narrated this tradition about Sayyidna Ali (RA) that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to Sayyidna Ali (RA): I am appointing you as a horse-runner. I am entrusting you with the responsibility of those who join the race, which the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, has entrusted to me. So when you reach Maitan (Abu Abd al-Rahman says: This means the place from where the race was to start), form a line of horses and announce three times: Someone is going to fix the bridle, someone is going to lift the boy, someone is going to put (the end of the bridle) on the horse's head (i.e. if it is not If no one gives you an answer, then say Allahu Akbar three times and leave him, then Allah will help him for the sake of whomever He wills from among His creatures. When Sayyiduna Ali (RA) would come to the last mark of the race, he would draw a line and make two men stand face to face on both sides of this line. Declaring and if you doubt about it, you would declare them both successful and when you declare the two equal, then make the last limit which is the smaller of the two."
